UNWIND [{tmdbId:"14435", properties:{bornIn:"Salt Lake City, Utah, USA", imdbId:"0841501", born:date('1876-02-16'), name:"Mack Swain", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMack Swain (born Moroni Swain, February 16, 1876 – August 25, 1935) was an early American film actor, who appeared in many of Mack Sennett's comedies at Keystone Studios, including the Keystone Cops series.  He also appeared in major features by Charlie Chaplin. \n\nIn the early 1900s Swain had his own stock theater company, which performed in the western and midwestern United States...", died:date('1935-08-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yoxashVRv3PBTiispOboUjIZJy2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14435"}}, {tmdbId:"14437", properties:{bornIn:"Stonefort, Illinois, United States", imdbId:"0615306", born:date('1874-09-08'), name:"Tom Murray", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nTom Murray (September 8, 1874 – August 27, 1935) was an American film actor.  He appeared in thirteen films between 1922 and 1931.  Born in Stonefort, Illinois and died in Hollywood, California of a heart attack. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Tom Murray (actor), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1935-08-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/p80JeuEZeSrRpfmIYH47ARG47C4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14437"}}, {tmdbId:"14438", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0074788", born:date('1868-02-22'), name:"Henry Bergman", bio:"Henry Bergman (February 23, 1868 – October 22, 1946) was an American actor of stage and film, known for his long association with Charlie Chaplin.  Born in San Francisco, California, he acted in live theater, appearing in Henrietta in 1888 at the Hollis Street Theater in Boston and in the touring production of The Senator in 1892 and 1893.  He made his Broadway debut in 1899.  He made his first film appearance was with The L-KO Kompany in 1914 at the age of forty-six...", died:date('1946-10-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1vIoHPX8faMuMQJtKrqqrZpGgPQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14438"}}, {tmdbId:"34746", properties:{bornIn:"Parsons, Kansas, USA", imdbId:"0686032", born:date('1894-01-03'), name:"Zasu Pitts", bio:"Zasu Pitts was an American actress who starred in many silent dramas and comedies, transitioning successfully to mostly comedy films with the advent of sound films.  She may be best known for her performance in Erich von Stroheim's epic silent film Greed. \n\nBased on her performance, von Stroheim labeled Pitts \"the greatest dramatic actress\"...", died:date('1963-06-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8QdLqPfgbdzR2VJ8GjduBIJhYwP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34746"}}, {tmdbId:"9097", properties:{bornIn:"Spennymoor, Durham, England, UK", imdbId:"0332998", born:date('1877-01-04'), name:"Gibson Gowland", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGibson Gowland (4 January 1877 Spennymoor, Durham, England, UK – 9 September 1951 London, England, UK) was an English film actor. \n\nGowland came to the United States from England, by way of Canada, in 1913 where he met Beatrice Bird, also from England, whom he married.  They moved to Hollywood, working as bit players.  In 1916, his son, actor and photographer Peter Gowland, was born...", died:date('1951-09-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tmla3xqOEoXEwL8oczKqNFtD3bH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9097"}}, {tmdbId:"32138", properties:{bornIn:"Copenhagen, Denmark", imdbId:"0380965", born:date('1886-07-12'), name:"Jean Hersholt", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJean Pierre Hersholt (12 July 1886 – 2 June 1956) was a Danish-born actor who lived in the United States, where he was a leading film and radio talent, best known for his 17 years starring on radio in Dr.  Christian and for playing Shirley Temple's grandfather in Heidi.  Asked how to pronounce his name, he told The Literary Digest, \"In English, her'sholt; in Danish, hairs'hult. \" Of his total credits, 75 were silent films and 65 were sound films...", died:date('1956-06-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9R1oslAoQmjq1sv0wf9oD1WGe5N.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32138"}}, {tmdbId:"35504", properties:{bornIn:"Santa Ana, California, USA ", imdbId:"0298202", born:date('1885-06-17'), name:"Dale Fuller", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDale Fuller (June 17, 1885 – October 14, 1948) was an American actress of the silent era.  She appeared in 67 films between 1915 and 1935.  She was born in Santa Ana, California and died in Los Angeles County, California...", died:date('1948-10-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7lcEEJj7yigfUWxiE6bTMLpxkdO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/35504"}}, {tmdbId:"95624", properties:{bornIn:"Santa Monica, California, USA", imdbId:"0000073", born:date('1928-04-23'), name:"Shirley Temple", bio:"Shirley Temple was easily the most popular and famous child star of all time.  She got her start in the movies at the age of three and soon progressed to super stardom.  Shirley could do it all: act, sing and dance and all at the age of five! Fans loved her as she was bright, bouncy and cheerful in her films and they ultimately bought millions of dollars worth of products that had her likeness on them...", died:date('2014-02-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7GcYKxdt4eRsv9yboVI9zlAKdJd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95624"}}, {tmdbId:"17753", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0000859", born:date('1878-04-28'), name:"Lionel Barrymore", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLionel Barrymore (born Lionel Herbert Blythe; April 28, 1878 – November 15, 1954) was an American actor of stage, screen and radio as well as a film director.  He won an Academy Award for Best Actor for his performance in A Free Soul (1931), and remains best known to modern audiences for the role of villainous Mr.  Potter in Frank Capra's 1946 film It's a Wonderful Life...", died:date('1954-11-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4vPzIVCzB21IlWX86VtFuHwMv3v.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/17753"}}, {tmdbId:"117073", properties:{bornIn:"Cincinnati, Ohio, U.S.", imdbId:"0892867", born:date('1913-10-18'), name:"Evelyn Venable", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEvelyn Venable (October 18, 1913 – November 15, 1993) was an American actress.  In addition to starring in several films in the 1930s and 1940s, she is notable as the voice and model for the Blue Fairy in the Walt Disney's Pinocchio. \n\nFor her work in motion pictures, Venable has a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame at 1500 Vine Street...", died:date('1993-11-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/n5IvAVQitXYvph1Hj5y2jCZ4BiT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/117073"}}, {tmdbId:"133470", properties:{imdbId:"0517099", born:date('1903-10-20'), name:"John Lodge", died:date('1985-10-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zN02wJwWyhZid9UanZCTG14MLzX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/133470"}}, {tmdbId:"29258", properties:{bornIn:"Midland, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0522281", born:date('1898-09-10'), name:"Bessie Love", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Bessie Love (September 10, 1898 – April 26, 1986) was an American motion picture actress who achieved prominence mainly in the silent films and early talkies.   With a small frame and delicate features, she played innocent young girls, flappers, and wholesome leading ladies.  In addition to her acting career, she wrote the screenplay for the 1919 movie A Yankee Princess...", died:date('1986-04-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hBz2aeYgPru5xBCLiGc8KmS2cMw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29258"}}, {tmdbId:"29259", properties:{bornIn:"Worcester, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0832011", born:date('1879-11-15'), name:"Lewis Stone", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLewis Shepard Stone (November 15, 1879 – September 12, 1953) was an American actor known for his role as Judge James Hardy in Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer's Andy Hardy film series and as an MGM contract player. \n\nBorn in Worcester, Massachusetts to Bertrand Stone and Philena Heald Ball, Lewis Stone's hair turned gray prematurely (reportedly by age 20).  Lewis served in the United States Army in the Spanish–American War, then returned to a career as a writer...", died:date('1953-09-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nxK5PexEFccYJxBGBTWju4TBAqT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29259"}}, {tmdbId:"29261", properties:{bornIn:"Bisbee, Arizona, USA", imdbId:"0400763", born:date('1897-10-21'), name:"Lloyd Hughes", bio:"Lloyd Hughes (October 21, 1897 – June 6, 1958) was an American actor of both the silent and sound film eras...", died:date('1958-06-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/a3bHZyiVkHLP1DjNkyrxcghcb2f.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29261"}}, {tmdbId:"14484", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0679907", born:date('1902-07-16'), name:"Mary Philbin", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMary Loretta Philbin (July 16, 1902 – May 7, 1993) was an American film actress of the silent film era, who is best known for playing the roles of Christine Daaé in the 1925 film The Phantom of the Opera opposite Lon Chaney, and as Dea in The Man Who Laughs.  Both roles cast her as the beauty in Beauty and the Beast type stories...", died:date('1993-05-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1Leb5fBpbSTKlyEDNIumadczb8D.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14484"}}, {tmdbId:"14485", properties:{bornIn:"Rochester, New York, USA", imdbId:"0449908", born:date('1894-06-16'), name:"Norman Kerry", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nNorman Kerry (born Norman Hussey Kaiser, June 16, 1894 – January 12, 1956) was an American actor whose career in the motion picture industry spanned over twenty-five years beginning in 1916 and peaking during the silent era of the 1920s...", died:date('1956-01-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7M4hNqyLcor0Z4T9TMVWZsVBEQH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14485"}}, {tmdbId:"14486", properties:{bornIn:"Trapzon [Trebizond], Turkey", imdbId:"0136886", born:date('1884-12-30'), name:"Arthur Edmund Carewe", died:date('1937-04-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/etzgPT4aqxI4HfMpG8Z8waqIiSS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14486"}}, {tmdbId:"99377", properties:{bornIn:"Lincolnshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0055797", born:date('1880-08-11'), name:"T. Roy Barnes", died:date('1937-03-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yrlTOlD9Ve3xp1dbFGjQbslxzC5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/99377"}}, {tmdbId:"144011", properties:{imdbId:"0245536", name:"Ruth Dwyer", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/144011"}}, {tmdbId:"85425", properties:{bornIn:"Durango City, Durango, Mexico", imdbId:"0003895", born:date('1899-02-06'), name:"Ramon Novarro", bio:"Mexico native Ramon Novarro (born Jose Ramon Gil Samaniego) was a Hollywood film and television actor.  He was a major star and matinee idol of 1920s Silent through early 1930s \"talkies\" cinema...", died:date('1968-10-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9jhYW0DAfLQpKaZ0kbS4dZSYVIy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85425"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"50837", properties:{bornIn:"Baltimore, Maryland, USA", imdbId:"0124279", born:date('1883-01-10'), name:"Francis X. Bushman", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nFrancis Xavier Bushman (January 10, 1883 – August 23, 1966) was an American actor, film director, and screenwriter.  His matinee idol career started in 1911 in the silent film His Friend's Wife, but it did not survive the silent screen era.  Bushman, like many of his contemporaries, broke into the film business via the stage...", died:date('1966-08-23'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/50837"}}, {tmdbId:"14287", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0564219", born:date('1899-09-08'), name:"May McAvoy", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMay McAvoy (September 8, 1899 – April 26, 1984) was an American actress who worked mainly during the silent film era.  Some of her major roles are Laura Pennington in The Enchanted Cottage, Esther in Ben-Hur: A Tale of the Christ, and Mary Dale in The Jazz Singer. \n\nMcAvoy appeared in her first film, entitled Hate, in 1917.  After appearing in more than three dozen films, she co-starred with Ramón Novarro and Francis X...", died:date('1984-04-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mEToUYwMXd1ujIauMaPUaISWLX9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14287"}}, {tmdbId:"108101", properties:{bornIn:"Trenton, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0111503", born:date('1906-11-17'), name:"Betty Bronson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia:\n\nBetty Bronson (November 17, 1906 – October 19, 1971) was an American television and film actress who began her career during the silent film era.  She was a famous actress in silent and sound films. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Betty Bronson, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1971-10-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/isRDEuw8ITGTuzXf9a23Z9VBsmI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/108101"}}, {tmdbId:"34744", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0235521", born:date('1903-05-14'), name:"Billie Dove", bio:"Billie Dove (born Bertha Bohny) was an American star actress of 1920s Silent cinema and of the first few years of the 'talkies' era.  She retired from show business in 1932...", died:date('1997-12-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/27wZv6AD5vqrGVAwBTGUVt1u9ch.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34744"}}, {tmdbId:"29603", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0683114", born:date('1884-02-02'), name:"Tempe Pigott", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nTempe Pigott (2 February 1884 – 6 October 1962) was an English silent and sound screen, as well as stage, character actress.  Her film appearances were numerous.  She is remembered mainly for playing the mother of Gibson Gowland in Greed (1925) and the landlady Mrs.  Hawkins in Dr.  Jekyll and Mr.  Hyde (1931).  She was born in London, England and died in Woodland Hills, California, USA...", died:date('1962-10-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bRPwCTNKlWZfNZc3kMjxp8oQAOw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29603"}}, {tmdbId:"29952", properties:{bornIn:"Bathurst - New Brunswick - Canada", imdbId:"0208659", born:date('1875-06-12'), name:"Sam De Grasse", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nSamuel Alfred De Grasse (June 12, 1875 – November 29, 1953)\n\nwas a Canadian actor.  He was born in Bathurst, New Brunswick, he trained to be\n\na dentist. \n\nHe married Annie McDonnell in 1904.  Their daughter,\n\nClementine Bell, was born in 1906.  Annie died in 1909, probably in childbirth\n\nwith another daughter, Olive...", died:date('1953-11-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qiMJezjBhoygL6UDnGxF1wfqBm1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29952"}}, {tmdbId:"66790", properties:{bornIn:"Stockholm, Stockholms län, Sweden", imdbId:"0252473", born:date('1939-07-28'), name:"Gösta Ekman", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nHans Gösta Gustaf Ekman (born July 28, 1939 in Stockholm) was a Swedish actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Gösta Ekman, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2017-04-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3B8Q7a7O56Mt865LQzdmjUUp0Zi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/66790"}}, {tmdbId:"48938", properties:{bornIn:"Frankfurt am Main, Germany", imdbId:"0394806", born:date('1903-04-25'), name:"Camilla Horn", bio:"The daughter of a railroad official, Camilla Horn was educated in Germany and Switzerland.  She initially trained as a dressmaker and received her first job experience in a fashion salon in Erfurt.  This was merely a stepping stone for a performing career which began with dance lessons in Berlin and subsequent acting studies under Lucie Höflich.  The lithe, blond and strikingly beautiful Camilla soon appeared in cabaret revues staged by Rudolf Nelson...", died:date('1996-08-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nFqE1c0T2sDy7noZ4J0xeFTuldp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/48938"}}, {tmdbId:"48062", properties:{bornIn:"Vienna, Austria-Hungary [now Austria]", imdbId:"0723801", born:date('1873-11-01'), name:"Frida Richard", died:date('1946-09-12'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/48062"}}, {tmdbId:"29999", properties:{bornIn:"Columbus, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0062828", born:date('1889-03-29'), name:"Warner Baxter", bio:"Warner Leroy Baxter (March 29, 1889 – May 7, 1951) was an American film actor from the 1910s to the 1940s.  Baxter became known for his role as The Cisco Kid in the 1928 film In Old Arizona for which he won the Academy Award for Best Actor at the 2nd Academy Awards.  He frequently played womanizing, charismatic Latin bandit types in westerns, and played The Cisco Kid or a similar character throughout the 1930s, but had a range of other roles throughout his career...", died:date('1951-05-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/i77UjwZQW4ZXnIBcbqHj3fNhhYj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29999"}}, {tmdbId:"148836", properties:{bornIn:"Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0933773", born:date('1894-06-28'), name:"Lois Wilson", died:date('1988-03-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uAWHCbZuaI6S0zApa1y5aqC7dCb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/148836"}}, {tmdbId:"27733", properties:{bornIn:"Lynn, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0358076", born:date('1899-09-09'), name:"Neil Hamilton", bio:"Neil Hamilton (born James Neil Hamilton; September 9, 1899 - September 24, 1984) was an American screen, stage, and television actor.  During the 1920s and 1930s he was a popular leading man in films.  Today he is perhaps best known for his portrayal of Commissioner Gordon on the Batman television series of the 1960s...", died:date('1984-09-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vnSGmbMtpu6maoelN3bKnA8aE79.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27733"}}, {tmdbId:"14434", properties:{bornIn:"St. Joseph, Missouri, U.S.", imdbId:"0354913", born:date('1905-06-24'), name:"Georgia Hale", bio:"In 1922, Georgia won a beauty contest and went to New York to get a job in the theater.  Unsuccessful, she left New York for Hollywood where she worked as a bit player in a few movies.  Georgia's first break came when she was hired for the film The Salvation Hunters (1925).  It was from this picture that Charlie Chaplin hired her to play the Georgia, the dance-hall girl who wins Charlie's heart, in The Gold Rush (1925)...", died:date('1985-06-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8EB0OKtzCr7cQ6bVeDsmtyZ9iNy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14434"}}, {tmdbId:"27911", properties:{bornIn:"Wigan, Lancashire, England, UK", imdbId:"0042083", born:date('1870-09-02'), name:"Marie Ault", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMarie Ault (2 September 1870 – 9 May 1951) was a British character actress of stage and film. \n\nShe was a star in many British films of the silent era, but is most remembered for her role as Daisy Bunting's mother in The Lodger: A Story of the London Fog (1927) directed by Alfred Hitchcock.  Other notable film work includes the role of Rummy Mitchens in the film of Bernard Shaw's Major Barbara (1941)...", died:date('1951-05-09'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27911"}}, {tmdbId:"27912", properties:{bornIn:"Wandsworth, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0156241", born:date('1881-11-21'), name:"Arthur Chesney", bio:"Arthur Chesney (born Arthur Kellaway) was a British film and stage actor.  His older brother was screen actor Edmund Gwenn (born Edmund Kellaway)...", died:date('1949-08-27'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27912"}}, {tmdbId:"27914", properties:{bornIn:"Bristol, England, UK", imdbId:"0444602", born:date('1887-08-08'), name:"Malcolm Keen", bio:"Malcolm Keen was a British stage, film, and television actor...", died:date('1970-01-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kH1sBRZZKh5vBGBzciKGbg4FC4k.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27914"}}, {tmdbId:"74", properties:{bornIn:"Hannover, Germany", imdbId:"0297054", born:date('1902-03-21'), name:"Gustav Fröhlich", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGustav Fröhlich (21 March 1902 – 22 December 1987) was a German actor and film director.  He landed secondary roles in a number of films and plays before landing his breakthrough role of Freder Fredersen in Fritz Lang's 1927 film Metropolis.  He remained a popular film star in Germany until the 1950s...", died:date('1987-12-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kqUdWJcrdDIbTi8YvLtok5EmYxQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74"}}, {tmdbId:"78", properties:{bornIn:"Bayreuth, Germany", imdbId:"0003248", born:date('1891-05-13'), name:"Fritz Rasp", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nFritz Heinrich Rasp (13 May 1891; Bayreuth – 30 November 1976; Gräfelfing) was a German film actor who appeared in 104 films between 1916 and 1976. \n\nHis most notable film roles were J. J.  Peachum in The Threepenny Opera (1931), as Meinert in Diary of a Lost Girl (1929), and as \"Der Schmale\" (\"The Thin Man\") in Fritz Lang's Metropolis (1927)...", died:date('1976-11-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7vE2alehNfoL4CKqkNkhkTFBHVc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78"}}, {tmdbId:"121001", properties:{bornIn:"Göteborg, Sweden", imdbId:"0361319", born:date('1886-07-26'), name:"Lars Hanson", bio:"Lars Hanson was a Swedish film and stage actor, internationally most remembered for his starring motion picture roles during the Silent film era.  In major Hollywood movies 1926-1928...", died:date('1965-04-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/r4SGQ8QnV1S0swQ16ukOlnVwWgr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/121001"}}, {tmdbId:"29978", properties:{bornIn:"Copenhagen, Denmark", imdbId:"0199322", born:date('1886-10-12'), name:"Karl Dane", died:date('1934-04-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cc3BzJF5qQf8hnVVwF38DxmEZJ2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29978"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"116367", properties:{bornIn:"Castellaneta, Puglia, Italy", imdbId:"0884388", born:date('1895-05-06'), name:"Rudolph Valentino", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRudolph Valentino (May 6, 1895 – August 23, 1926) was an Italian actor, and early pop icon.  A sex symbol of the 1920s, Valentino was known as the \"Latin Lover\".  He starred in several well known silent films including The Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse, The Sheik, Blood and Sand, The Eagle and Son of the Sheik. \n\nHis sudden death at age 31 caused mass hysteria among his female fans, propelling him into icon status...", died:date('1926-08-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eX4g6CfvtqS5lCjua25JItO7puT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/116367"}}, {tmdbId:"932465", properties:{bornIn:"Nagydorog, Austria-Hungary [now Hungary]", imdbId:"0126566", born:date('1901-01-09'), name:"Vilma Bánky", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nVilma Bánky (January 9, 1901 – March 18, 1991) was a Hungarian-born American silent film actress, although the early part of her acting career began in Budapest, spreading to France, Austria, and Germany.  Banky was best known for her roles in The Eagle and The Son of the Sheik with Rudolph Valentino and several romantic teamings with Ronald Colman. \n\nShe was hailed as \"The Hungarian Rhapsody\" and was an immediate hit with American audiences...", died:date('1991-03-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/Wo9GwClcpFDAvlL57kUQTwWAKG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/932465"}}, {tmdbId:"262394", properties:{bornIn:"Alexandria, Virginia, USA", imdbId:"0269493", born:date('1860-08-25'), name:"George Fawcett", bio:"George Fawcett was an American stage and screen actor as well as a three-time (in 1920 and 1921) film director.  His screen acting career spanned the years 1915 to 1931...", died:date('1939-06-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pZBmcj6XkdBkNKvUIovZMNqg8qU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/262394"}}, {tmdbId:"92907", properties:{bornIn:"Portsmouth, Hampshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0002311", born:date('1880-03-15'), name:"Montagu Love", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMontagu Love (15 March 1880 – 17 May 1943), also known as Montague Love, was an English screen, stage and vaudeville actor. \n\nBorn Harry Montague Love in Portsmouth, Hampshire, he was the son of Harry Love (b.  1852) and Fanny Louisa Love, née Poad (b.  1856); his father was listed as accountant on the 1881 English Census...", died:date('1943-05-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/y6thiSUw8nJShbN6fEXNp8yrxGx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/92907"}}, {tmdbId:"2797", properties:{bornIn:"Posen", imdbId:"0902438", born:date('1847-10-02'), name:"Paul von Hindenburg", bio:"Paul Ludwig Hans Anton von Beneckendorff und von Hindenburg, dit Paul von Hindenburg, né le 2 octobre 1847 à Posen (aujourd'hui en Pologne) et décédé le 2 août 1934 au manoir de Neudeck en Prusse-Occidentale1, fut un militaire, nommé maréchal, et homme d'État allemand qui, du fait de son prestige et de sa longévité, joua un rôle important dans l'Histoire allemande...", died:date('1934-08-02'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2797"}}, {tmdbId:"141304", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0180465", born:date('1897-01-17'), name:"Anne Cornwall", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAnne Cornwall (January 17, 1897 – March 2, 1980), was an American actress.  She performed for forty years in many early silent film productions starting in 1918, and later in talkies, until 1959.  She was first married to writer/director Charles Maigne, then later to Los Angeles Engineer Ellis Wing Taylor.  Taylor fathered her only child, Peter. \n\nIn 1925, Anne was one of the WAMPAS Baby Stars...", died:date('1980-03-02'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/141304"}}, {tmdbId:"143818", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0104238", born:date('1904-09-14'), name:"Flora Bramley", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nFlora Bramley (1909 – 23 June 1993) was an English-born American actress and comedian. \n\nBorn in London, Bramley started out on stage in musical revues, and in June 1926, while visiting relatives in Hollywood, was signed by United Artists.  Her first film (for Film Booking Offices of America), The Dude Cowboy (1926) was followed by three more films, all for United Artists...", died:date('1993-06-23'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/143818"}}, {tmdbId:"80545", properties:{bornIn:"Peoria, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0329467", born:date('1902-12-01'), name:"Harold Goodwin", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nHarold Goodwin (December 1, 1902 – July 12, 1987) was an American film actor who performed in over 225 films. \n\nBorn in Peoria, Illinois, Goodwin began his film career while still in his teens in the 1915 film short Mike's Elopement.  One of his most popular roles of the silent era was that of Ted Brown in the 1927 Buster Keaton comedy College...", died:date('1987-07-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/y3RGWvME7g4QrpJQok6WqBQ1aKZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80545"}}, {tmdbId:"14417", properties:{imdbId:"0533045", born:date('1902-04-08'), name:"Marion Mack", died:date('1989-05-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wya8hfPbEM6syBOqtTgXfjUWvJa.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14417"}}, {tmdbId:"14419", properties:{bornIn:"Tucson, Arizona, USA", imdbId:"0147070", born:date('1883-09-19'), name:"Glen Cavender", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGlen Cavender (September 19, 1883 – February 9, 1962) was an American film actor.  He appeared in 259 films between 1914 and 1949. \n\nThe Spanish–American War soldier was born in Tucson, Arizona, and died in Hollywood, California.  He started his acting career in vaudeville shows.  Cavender belonged to the original Keystone Cops and was a regular in numerous Mack Sennett comedies.  He also worked as a director for three Mack Sennett films between 1914 and 1916...", died:date('1962-02-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mkCWTmyWtInbtNiSkBaUU20DgXz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14419"}}, {tmdbId:"14420", properties:{bornIn:"Waldron, Arkansas, USA", imdbId:"0267650", born:date('1882-01-08'), name:"Jim Farley", died:date('1947-10-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fNM5KM1PeDxGIkHffFqXB09i7HW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14420"}}, {tmdbId:"97996", properties:{bornIn:"Chattanooga, Tennessee, USA", imdbId:"0417012", born:date('1882-06-03'), name:"Walter James", bio:"Walter James was an American stage and screen actor...", died:date('1946-06-27'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/97996"}}, {tmdbId:"141140", properties:{bornIn:"Wapanucka, Oklahoma, USA", imdbId:"0932381", born:date('1890-01-05'), name:"Leo Willis", died:date('1952-04-10'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/141140"}}, {tmdbId:"143356", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0226387", born:date('1889-11-26'), name:"Albert Dieudonné", bio:"Albert Dieudonné  was a French actor,screenwriter, film director and novelist. \n\nDieudonné was born in Paris, France, and made his acting debut in silent film in 1908 for The Assassination of the Duke of Guise, with musical score by Camille Saint-Saëns.  In 1924, he directed the film drama Catherine, in which he also appeared as a major character.  Jean Renoir acted as his assistant director on the film...", died:date('1976-03-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1VMqCKPC5KgbziBCWfIZYuoES5D.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/143356"}}, {tmdbId:"1693168", properties:{name:"Vladimir Roudenko", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1693168"}}, {tmdbId:"150860", properties:{imdbId:"0885965", name:"Edmond Van Daële", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/UyMRqHMEtS4L8ohmMHH5cmw0L2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/150860"}}, {tmdbId:"1693169", properties:{name:"Alexandre Koubitzky", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1693169"}}, {tmdbId:"9087", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0639563", born:date('1899-04-19'), name:"George O'Brien", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nGeorge O'Brien (April 19, 1899 – September 4, 1985) was an American actor, popular during the silent film era and into the talkie era of the 1930s, best known today as the lead actor in F.  W.  Murnau's 1927 film Sunrise: A Song of Two Humans...", died:date('1985-09-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fc960YdabhS8yjLRf4IxETSN4Hu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9087"}}, {tmdbId:"9088", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0310980", born:date('1906-10-06'), name:"Janet Gaynor", bio:"Janet Gaynor (October 6, 1906 – September 14, 1984) was an American actress and painter. \n\nOne of the most popular actresses of the silent film era, in 1928 Gaynor became the first winner of the Academy Award for Best Actress for her performances in three films: Seventh Heaven (1927), Sunrise: A Song of Two Humans (1927) and Street Angel (1928).  This was the only occasion on which an actress has won for multiple roles.  This rule would be changed three years later by AMPAS...", died:date('1984-09-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kwyClWei18GOssMPbrs4RL61izG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9088"}}, {tmdbId:"9089", properties:{bornIn:"Salt Lake City, Utah, USA", imdbId:"0515272", born:date('1895-11-25'), name:"Margaret Livingston", bio:"Margaret (born Marguerite) Livingston was an American screen actress, in films from 1916 to 1934, most notably during the Silent era...", died:date('1984-12-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gkLkBJMDjm3AFo8CUmMZDgAKMGD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9089"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"9090", properties:{bornIn:"Copenhagen, Denmark", imdbId:"0743017", born:date('1877-12-27'), name:"Bodil Rosing", died:date('1941-12-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zNhUo6xA1AAjtshFInTabGct4O9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9090"}}, {tmdbId:"102499", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001966", born:date('1905-07-29'), name:"Clara Bow", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nClara Gordon Bow (July 29, 1905 – September 27, 1965) was an American actress who rose to stardom in silent films during the 1920s and successfully made the transition to \"talkies\" after 1927.  Her appearance as a plucky shopgirl in the film It brought her global fame and the nickname \"The It Girl\".  Bow came to personify the Roaring Twenties and is described as its leading sex symbol...", died:date('1965-09-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gt3m6XcULHedwr3fT8Oaxfwl1QF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/102499"}}, {tmdbId:"102500", properties:{bornIn:"Olathe, Kansas, USA", imdbId:"0736777", born:date('1904-08-13'), name:"Charles 'Buddy' Rogers", bio:"Charles \"Buddy\" Rogers (1904—1999), nicknamed America's Boyfriend, was an American film actor and musician. \n\nHe was the husband of Silent screen star Mary Pickford for more than forty years until her death...", died:date('1999-04-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xWAatpaqEQF5y0HKuYaSbhDuBQO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/102500"}}, {tmdbId:"29760", properties:{bornIn:"St. Paul, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0035159", born:date('1899-09-01'), name:"Richard Arlen", bio:"Richard Arlen (born Sylvanus Richard Mattimore) was an American film and television actor.  He served as a pilot in the Royal Canadian Flying Corps during World War I.  After the war, he went to the oilfields of Texas and Oklahoma and found work as a tool boy.  He was thereafter a messenger and sporting editor of a newspaper before going to Los Angeles to act in films, but no producer wanted him...", died:date('1976-03-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bsWai47uXHIEInGmobbVpQRTzhJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29760"}}, {tmdbId:"13904", properties:{bornIn:"Cherryvale, Kansas, USA", imdbId:"0000315", born:date('1906-11-14'), name:"Louise Brooks", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMary Louise Brooks (November 14, 1906 – August 8, 1985), generally known by her stage name Louise Brooks, was an American dancer, model, showgirl and silent film actress, noted for popularizing the bobbed haircut.  She is best known for the films Pandora's Box (1929), Diary of a Lost Girl (1929), and Prix de Beauté (Miss Europe) (1930).  She starred in 17 silent films and, late in life, authored a memoir, Lulu in Hollywood...", died:date('1985-08-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/z5SZ8JIMJxdJC0L3uwz0aSzvQfH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13904"}}, {tmdbId:"13905", properties:{bornIn:"Vienna - Austria", imdbId:"0466776", born:date('1892-05-12'), name:"Fritz Kortner", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.  Fritz Kortner (12 May 1892 – 22 July 1970) was an Austrian-born stage and film actor and theatre director. \n\nKortner was born in Vienna as Fritz Nathan Kohn.  He studied at the Vienna Academy of Music and Dramatic Art.  After graduating, he joined Max Reinhardt in Berlin in 1911 and then Leopold Jessner in 1916.  Also in that year he made his first appearance in a silent film.  He became one of Germany's best known character actors...", died:date('1970-07-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aah9CtF4RTjPWgFHdICT5Yftpcx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13905"}}, {tmdbId:"13906", properties:{bornIn:"Prague, Bohemia, Austria-Hungary [now Czech Republic]", imdbId:"0496473", born:date('1899-11-06'), name:"Francis Lederer", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nFrancis Lederer (November 6, 1899 – May 25, 2000) was a Czech-born film and stage actor with a successful career, first in Europe, then in the United States.  His original name was František Lederer.   Lederer's first American movies were Man of Two Worlds (1934), Romance in Manhattan (1934), with Ginger Rogers, The Gay Deception (1935), with Frances Dee, and One Rainy Afternoon (1936)...", died:date('2000-05-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7heriGOapJPNxxpWxN0ahg9u1HV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13906"}}, {tmdbId:"13907", properties:{bornIn:"Vienna, Austria-Hungary (now Austria)", imdbId:"0324501", born:date('1862-04-10'), name:"Carl Goetz", died:date('1932-08-15'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13907"}}, {tmdbId:"122974", properties:{bornIn:"Colorado Springs, Colorado, USA", imdbId:"0206496", born:date('1908-04-24'), name:"Marceline Day", bio:"Marceline Day (born Marceline Newlin) was an American screen actress who achieved stardom in the mid 1920s, appearing opposite such diverse stars as Harry Langdon, John Barrymore, Ramon Novarro, Lon Chaney, and Buster Keaton.  Her career faltered in the early 1930s and she was soon reduced to appearing in low-budget thrillers and action pictures.  Day retired in the mid 1930s.  She died in 2000...", died:date('2000-02-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nUgZ88hv2zvjJPvmVca7CxgXeGA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/122974"}}, {tmdbId:"80546", properties:{bornIn:"Melbourne, Victoria, Australia", imdbId:"0102718", born:date('1877-12-18'), name:"Sidney Bracey", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nSidney Bracey (18 December 1877 – 5 August 1942) was an Australian-born American actor.  After a stage career in Australia, on Broadway and in Britain, he appeared in 321 films between 1909 and 1942. \n\nBracey was born in Melbourne, Victoria, with the name Sidney Bracy, later changing the spelling of his last name.  He was the son of Welsh tenor Henry Bracy and English actress Clara T.  Bracy.  His aunt was actress and dancer Lydia Thompson...", died:date('1942-08-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zwWZ51P10q6fAydhoQk2tkOR8ei.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80546"}}, {tmdbId:"13855", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0305087", born:date('1887-03-11'), name:"Al Ernest Garcia", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAl Ernest Garcia (11 March 1887 – 4 September 1938) was an American actor, best known for his long association with Charlie Chaplin.  He acted with Chaplin in six films between 1921 and 1936, cast mostly in clinical or villainous supporting roles.  Garcia portrayed the brutal circus director in The Circus (1928), the snobbish butler of the millionaire in City Lights (1931), and the factory owner in Modern Times (1936)...", died:date('1938-09-04'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13855"}}, {tmdbId:"147962", properties:{bornIn:"Kankakee, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0448224", born:date('1908-09-07'), name:"Merna Kennedy", bio:"Merna Kennedy (September 7, 1908 - December 20, 1944) was an American actress of the late silent era...", died:date('1944-12-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fRnKwgnclUQ1m1OwWkTtGMPRkrH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/147962"}}, {tmdbId:"147963", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0188357", born:date('1893-07-02'), name:"Harry Crocker", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nHarry Crocker (July 2, 1893 - May 23, 1958) was an American film star of the 1920s and who starred in Charlie Chaplin's The Circus in 1928.  He was a Los Angeles Examiner newsman. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Harry Crocker, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1958-05-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zU1gFnjgJpBO1Blek4s7FI9iHBj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/147963"}}, {tmdbId:"120701", properties:{bornIn:"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands", imdbId:"0204639", born:date('1889-11-07'), name:"George Davis", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nGeorge Davis (7 November 1889 – 19 April 1965) was a Dutch-born American actor.  He appeared in more than 260 films between 1916 and 1963.  He was born in Amsterdam and died in Los Angeles, California...", died:date('1965-04-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bYZ6eVY8RTYZHuWORH2mKrtQ5RK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/120701"}}, {tmdbId:"11589", properties:{bornIn:"Pantin, Seine [now Seine-Saint-Denis], France ", imdbId:"0266029", born:date('1892-07-21'), name:"Maria Falconetti", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nRenée Jeanne Falconetti (July 21, 1892 – December 12, 1946), sometimes credited as Maria Falconetti, Marie Falconetti, Renée Maria Falconetti, or, simply, Falconetti, was a French stage and film actress, notable for her role as Joan of Arc in Carl Theodor Dreyer's 1928 silent film, La Passion de Jeanne d'Arc. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article  Renée Jeanne Falconetti, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1946-12-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gt2p4FrgveCD5qb0uhYH67MIUd5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11589"}}, {tmdbId:"11590", properties:{bornIn:"Bourg-en-Bresse, France", imdbId:"0798564", born:date('1851-06-17'), name:"Eugene Silvain", died:date('1930-08-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pTe6VvXg6UeYklsdwuALsoaHlax.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11590"}}, {tmdbId:"11591", properties:{bornIn:"Paris - France", imdbId:"0075551", born:date('1890-01-13'), name:"André Berley", died:date('1936-11-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ckoUscLgTslbUzj293t6mWxCQt9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11591"}}, {tmdbId:"11586", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0776914", born:date('1866-08-04'), name:"Maurice Schutz", died:date('1955-03-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rAgFu1nz3AUnlupU39fY3WKAoPY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11586"}}, {tmdbId:"120811", properties:{bornIn:"Lancashire, England, UK", imdbId:"0570297", born:date('1873-09-01'), name:"Tom McGuire", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nTom McGuire (1 September 1873 – 6 May 1954) was an English stage and film actor.  He appeared in about 175 films between 1919 and 1949.  He was born in Lancashire, England and died in Hollywood, California...", died:date('1954-05-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vsEHvdahFS06ZkkfLosU3k9C6ex.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/120811"}}, {tmdbId:"98034", properties:{bornIn:"Edinburgh, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0868458", born:date('1878-06-26'), name:"Ernest Torrence", bio:"He was the man you loved to hiss.  This towering (6' 4\"), highly imposing  character star with cold, hollow, beady eyes and a huge, protruding  snout would go on to become one of the silent screen's finest arch  villains.  Born Ernest Thayson Torrence-Thompson on June 26, 1878, in  Edinburgh, Scotland, he was, unlikely enough, an exceptional pianist and  operatic baritone...", died:date('1933-05-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/h616zkF9v9dyNkmMspe54sTsFTn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/98034"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"1444312", properties:{name:"Tom Lewis", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1444312"}}, {tmdbId:"7380", properties:{imdbId:"0648565", born:date('1902-05-15'), name:"Anny Ondra", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAnny Ondra (May 15 1903 – February 28 1987) was a Czech film actress.  She was born Anna Sophie Ondráková in Tarnów, Galicia, Austria–Hungary, now Poland, and died in Hollenstedt near Harburg, Germany. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Anny Ondra, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1987-02-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qj3Qgd6tldsGwYUe125TD4iIQZh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7380"}}, {tmdbId:"7381", properties:{bornIn:"Dublin, Ireland", imdbId:"0021329", born:date('1879-10-31'), name:"Sara Allgood", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nSara Allgood (October 15, 1879 – September 13, 1950) was an Irish actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Sara Allgood, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1950-09-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hgnPW9s348IuRTP6cMryYQZIEWs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7381"}}, {tmdbId:"7382", properties:{imdbId:"0665715", born:date('1874-07-31'), name:"Charles Paton", died:date('1970-04-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/o4bThCQndsD9wMzL5D1K7KkFfKV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7382"}}, {tmdbId:"7383", properties:{bornIn:"West Indies", imdbId:"0519274", born:date('1900-11-11'), name:"John Longden", bio:"John Longden was a West Indian-born English screen, stage, and television actor.  He appeared in dozens of films from 1926 to 1964, including five (Blackmail, Juno and the Paycock, The Skin Game, Young and Innocent, Jamaica Inn) directed by Alfred Hitchcock.  Longden appeared in numerous television series...", died:date('1971-05-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9LkSpBSZbC9RcQiTmoi0Yw3X0Xy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7383"}}, {tmdbId:"1516030", properties:{imdbId:"0454558", name:"Charles King", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1516030"}}, {tmdbId:"98012", properties:{bornIn:"Flushing, New York, USA", imdbId:"0656105", born:date('1910-08-04'), name:"Anita Page", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAnita Page (August 4, 1910 – September 6, 2008), born Anita Evelyn Pomares, was an American film actress who reached stardom in the last years of the silent film era.  She became a highly popular young star, reportedly receiving the most fan mail of anyone on the MGM lot.  Page was referred to as \"a blond, blue-eyed Latin\" and \"the girl with the most beautiful face in Hollywood\" in the 1920s.  She retired from acting in 1936 at the age of 23...", died:date('2008-09-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mZUSOcjuP7YVtNQvUDrWljcd0aP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/98012"}}, {tmdbId:"1042437", properties:{bornIn:"Bialystok, Grodno Province, Russian Empire (now Poland)", imdbId:"0442227", born:date('1897-09-05'), name:"Mikhail Kaufman", died:date('1980-11-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/o2EH1WP2Qu271ToI63okSZwCzTF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1042437"}}, {tmdbId:"30014", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0555688", born:date('1901-02-25'), name:"Zeppo Marx", bio:"Herbert Manfred \"Zeppo\" Marx (February 25, 1901 – November 30, 1979) was an American film star, theatrical agent and businessman.  He was the youngest of the five Marx Brothers.  He appeared in the first five Marx Brothers films, but then left the act to start his second career as a theatrical agent. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Zeppo Marx, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list  of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1979-11-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xHuDj6pCGhQTDVpP8QBKV7dFNM7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30014"}}, {tmdbId:"10798", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000050", born:date('1890-10-02'), name:"Groucho Marx", bio:"Julius Henry \"Groucho\" Marx (October 2, 1890 – August 19, 1977) was an American comedian and film star famed as a master of wit.  His rapid-fire delivery of innuendo-laden patter earned him many admirers. He made 13 feature films with his siblings the Marx Brothers, of whom he was the third-born.  He also had a successful solo career, most notably as the host of the radio and television game show You Bet Your Life...", died:date('1977-08-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mIoLM0MlEAP71ZwU8YeW8VpK268.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10798"}}, {tmdbId:"10800", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0555617", born:date('1888-11-23'), name:"Harpo Marx", bio:"Arthur Adolph \"Harpo\" Marx (November 23, 1888 – September 28, 1964) was an American comedian and film star.  He was the second oldest of the Marx Brothers.  His comic style was influenced by clown and pantomime traditions.  He wore a curly reddish wig, and never spoke during performances (he blew a horn or whistled to communicate).  Marx frequently used props such as a walking stick with a built-in bulb horn, and he played the harp in most of his films...", died:date('1964-09-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oD5kj8uHtCi1KLm7uanUICUtDP7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10800"}}, {tmdbId:"587954", properties:{bornIn:"Milaca, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0071602", born:date('1891-04-22'), name:"Belle Bennett", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nBelle Bennett (April 22, 1891 – November 4, 1932) was a stage and screen actress who started her professional career in vaudeville.  She was born in Milaca, Minnesota. \n\nBennett was working as a film actress by 1913, and was cast in numerous one-reel shorts by small East Coast film companies.  She appeared in minor motion pictures like the western film A Ticket to Red Horse Gulch (Mutual, 1914)...", died:date('1932-11-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oYyIWd9goKe9Jql9wOZArQohg1P.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/587954"}}, {tmdbId:"120536", properties:{imdbId:"0720885", born:date('1904-04-18'), name:"Dorothy Revier", died:date('1993-11-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8qa37zMOkCZrTeWUXgGQ7DVkVm3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/120536"}}, {tmdbId:"29953", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0507849", born:date('1873-06-10'), name:"Vera Lewis", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nVera Lewis (June 10, 1873 – February 8, 1956) was an American film and stage actress, beginning in the silent film era.  She appeared in 183 films between 1915 and 1947.  She was married to actor Ralph Lewis. \n\nShe was born in Manhattan, where she began acting in stage productions.  Her film career started in 1915 with the film Hypocrites, which starred Myrtle Stedman and Courtenay Foote...", died:date('1956-02-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/q8kMDxClpiT543Ktt5I4gUZ3LkE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29953"}}, {tmdbId:"8993", properties:{bornIn:"Perigueux, Dordogne, Aquitaine, France", imdbId:"0546540", born:date('1903-08-25'), name:"Simone Mareuil", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nSimone Mareuil (25 August 1903 – 24 October 1954) was a French actress best known for appearing in the surrealist film Un chien andalou. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Simone Mareuil, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1954-10-24'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8993"}}, {tmdbId:"8992", properties:{bornIn:"Harbin, Manchuria", imdbId:"0060715", born:date('1907-06-23'), name:"Pierre Batcheff", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nPierre Batcheff (23 June 1907 – 13 April 1932) was a French actor, whose original name was Piotr Bacev (from Russia), born in Harbin, Manchuria.  His best-known film was Un chien andalou (1929) by Luis Buñuel and Salvador Dali.  He was married to French film editor Denise Piazza...", died:date('1932-04-13'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8992"}}, {tmdbId:"2010", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0938464", born:date('1880-03-27'), name:"Louis Wolheim", bio:"It was Lionel Barrymore who gave Louis Wolheim his start as an actor.  Wolheim had had his face more or less smashed in and his nose nicely fractured while playing on a scrub Cornell football team.  Later as a Cornell Instructor he found life none too easy.  He had worked off and on as an extra in the Wharton studio but never received much attention.  Barrymore had only to look at him once to realize that Wolheim's face was his fortune...", died:date('1931-02-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/unc3IbI5KSZDVRS7o7x6aS8T26e.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2010"}}, {tmdbId:"2007", properties:{bornIn:"Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0000817", born:date('1908-12-28'), name:"Lew Ayres", bio:"Lew Ayres was born in Minneapolis, Minnesota and raised in San Diego,  California.  A college dropout, he was found by a talent scout in the  Coconut Grove nightclub in Los Angeles and entered Hollywood as a bit  player.  He was leading man to Greta Garbo in The Kiss (1929), but it was the role of Paul Baumer in All Quiet on the Western Front  (1930) that was his big break.  He was profoundly affected by the  anti-war message of that film, and when, in 1942, the popular star of Young Dr...", died:date('1996-12-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rXT2hHyiQV3Ufb8tHD2iyoCabPC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2007"}}, {tmdbId:"2009", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0942046", born:date('1887-02-13'), name:"John Wray", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJohn Wray (13 February 1887 - 5 April 1940) was an American character actor of stage and screen...", died:date('1940-04-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oNX9BXP9Eu16EvEwgoBp8tzmvJp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2009"}}, {tmdbId:"2008", properties:{bornIn:"Tottenham, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0524803", born:date('1865-08-08'), name:"Arnold Lucy", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nArnold Lucy was a British actor claimed to have performed on the fabled west-end stage over 1,200 times before making his early film debut in the early 1910s during the Golden Era of the Hollywood system.  Though probably best known for his role as the professor in All Quiet on the Western Front...", died:date('1945-12-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jtIFDhtIzckMcbfHpSbU50tIw5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2008"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"10799", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0555597", born:date('1887-03-22'), name:"Chico Marx", bio:"Leonard \"Chico\" Marx (March 22, 1887 – October 11, 1961) was an American comedian and film star as part of the Marx Brothers.  His persona in the act was that of a dim-witted con artist, seemingly of rural Italian origin, who wore shabby clothes, and sported a curly-haired wig and Tyrolean hat. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Chico Marx, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1961-10-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4DSVzN5yokNp7Y8AVK5UedqxB1c.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10799"}}, {tmdbId:"2896", properties:{bornIn:"Berlin, Germany", imdbId:"0000017", born:date('1901-12-27'), name:"Marlene Dietrich", bio:"Marlene Dietrich was a German actress and singer. \n\nDietrich remained popular throughout her long career by continually re-inventing herself.  In 1920s Berlin, she acted on the stage and in silent films.  Her performance as Lola-Lola in The Blue Angel, directed by Josef von Sternberg, brought her international fame and a contract with Paramount Pictures in the US...", died:date('1992-05-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gQFppqFeUdJDfKsp4Lh2G7UDd0R.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2896"}}, {tmdbId:"2897", properties:{bornIn:"Berlin, Germany", imdbId:"0314777", born:date('1897-05-11'), name:"Kurt Gerron", died:date('1944-10-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1dannHvwMGKxqITWP6VNoR3nwIC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2897"}}, {tmdbId:"2898", properties:{bornIn:"Berlin, Germany", imdbId:"0884665", born:date('1876-01-25'), name:"Rosa Valetti", died:date('1937-12-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6FkyTtJRJJIkHQbU5G6HLnqOtms.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2898"}}, {tmdbId:"13566", properties:{bornIn:"Bucharest, Romania", imdbId:"0000064", born:date('1893-12-12'), name:"Edward G. Robinson", bio:"Edward G.  Robinson (born Emanuel Goldenberg; December 12, 1893 – January 26, 1973) was a Romanian-born American actor.  Although he played a wide range of characters, he is best remembered for his roles as a gangster, most notably in his star-making film Little Caesar. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Edward G.  Robinson, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1973-01-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sI3vtDTeGcV0uhumtZmYmfcOBav.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13566"}}, {tmdbId:"51762", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001195", born:date('1909-12-09'), name:"Douglas Fairbanks Jr.", bio:"Although he appeared in approximately 100 movies or television shows, Douglas Fairbanks Jr.  never really intended to take up acting as a career.  However, the environment he was born into and the circumstances naturally led him to be a thespian. \n\nThe son of future silent era swashbuckling idol Douglas Fairbanks (born Douglas Elton Thomas Ullman) and Beth Sully - the daughter of a very wealthy cotton mogul - was born in 1909 and soon proved a gifted boy...", died:date('2000-05-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jjb8iJ0d419dVP2VTYzjy38FxXV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/51762"}}, {tmdbId:"29315", properties:{bornIn:"Enid, Oklahoma, USA", imdbId:"0268225", born:date('1904-06-30'), name:"Glenda Farrell", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGlenda Farrell (June 30, 1904 – May 1, 1971) was an American actress of film, television, and theater.  She is best known for her role as Torchy Blane in the Warner Bros.  Torchy Blane film series and the Academy Award-nominated films Little Caesar (1931), I Am a Fugitive from a Chain Gang (1932), and Lady for a Day (1933).  With a career spanning more than 50 years, Farrell appeared in over 100 films and television series, as well as numerous Broadway plays...", died:date('1971-05-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xZVRc0gR5BdJ7J1TwusxTtgxD6o.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29315"}}, {tmdbId:"128159", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0171873", born:date('1902-02-12'), name:"William Collier Jr.", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nWilliam Collier Jr.  (born Charles F.  Gall Jr. , February 12, 1902 – February 5, 1987) was an American film and stage actor who appeared in 89 films. \n\nWilliam Collier (nicknamed \"Buster\") was born in New York City.  When his parents divorced, his mother, the actress Paula Marr, remarried the actor William Collier Sr.  who adopted Charles (the two did share a resemblance) and gave the boy the new name William Collier Jr...", died:date('1987-02-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2cIBLXuJOCnfi5S3DA4svDXtibj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/128159"}}, {tmdbId:"2435", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0003339", born:date('1890-05-23'), name:"Herbert Marshall", bio:"Herbert Brough Falcon Marshall (23 May 1890 – 22 January 1966) was an English stage, screen and radio actor who, despite losing a leg during the First World War, starred in many popular and well-regarded Hollywood films in the 1930s and 1940s.  After a successful theatrical career in the United Kingdom and North America, he became an in-demand Hollywood leading man, frequently appearing in romantic melodramas and occasional comedies.  In his later years, he turned to character acting...", died:date('1966-01-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/r2DrJ6dxBNSjCtP7PRNBsYjbNI2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2435"}}, {tmdbId:"32926", properties:{bornIn:"London,  England", imdbId:"0054689", born:date('1905-11-26'), name:"Norah Baring", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nNorah Baring (26 November 1905 – 8 February 1985), born Norah Minnie Baker, was an English film actress most famous for portraying \"Diana Baring\" in the Alfred Hitchcock thriller Murder! (1930).  She is also known for playing the female lead in Anthony Asquith's silent thriller A Cottage on Dartmoor (1929).  Originally she studied art before succumbing to the footlights and soon became well known to London theatre goers...", died:date('1985-02-08'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32926"}}, {tmdbId:"553482", properties:{imdbId:"0042496", born:date('1907-04-14'), name:"Phyllis Konstam", died:date('1976-08-20'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/553482"}}, {tmdbId:"33267", properties:{bornIn:"Harrogate, Yorkshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0152361", born:date('1901-10-13'), name:"Edward Chapman", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEdward Chapman (13 October 1901 - 9 August 1977) was an English actor who starred in many films and television programmes, but is chiefly remembered as \"Mr.  Wilfred Grimsdale\", the officious superior and comic foil to Norman Wisdom's character of Pitkin in many of his films from the late 1950s and 1960s. \n\nChapman was born in Harrogate, Yorkshire, England...", died:date('1977-08-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ozanx4gVXZoEvCAzMtRwG3A5hNF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33267"}}, {tmdbId:"11543", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0595321", born:date('1887-12-30'), name:"Gaston Modot", died:date('1970-02-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2iYNh1NPS21O3Cq5sWzHlOUOFv3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11543"}}, {tmdbId:"33023", properties:{bornIn:"Berlin, Germany", imdbId:"0529227", born:date('1908-05-18'), name:"Lya Lys", died:date('1986-06-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/y17WtVmp9s4r5qDrDv3D3xm7H1r.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33023"}}, {tmdbId:"1830629", properties:{name:"Caridad de Laberdesque", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1830629"}}, {tmdbId:"45201", properties:{bornIn:"Brühl, Germany", imdbId:"0259722", born:date('1891-04-02'), name:"Max Ernst", died:date('1976-04-01'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/45201"}}, {tmdbId:"88671", properties:{bornIn:"St. Paul, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0228715", born:date('1893-07-18'), name:"Richard Dix", bio:"Richard Dix was a major leading man at RKO Radio Pictures from 1929  through 1943.  He was born Ernest Carlton Brimmer July 18, 1893, in St.   Paul, Minnesota.  There he was educated, and at the desires of his  father, studied to be a surgeon.  His obvious acting talent in his school  dramatic club led him to leading roles in most of the school plays.  At  6' 0\" and 180 pounds, Dix excelled in sports, especially football and  baseball...", died:date('1949-09-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6ULd271XEtP6nTy11VStE7gq9ae.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88671"}}, {tmdbId:"77158", properties:{bornIn:"Louisville, Kentucky, USA", imdbId:"0002050", born:date('1898-12-20'), name:"Irene Dunne", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nIrene Dunne (born Irene Marie Dunn, December 20, 1898 – September 4, 1990) was an American film actress and singer of the 1930s, 1940s and early 1950s.  Dunne was nominated five times for the Academy Award for Best Actress, for her performances in Cimarron (1931), Theodora Goes Wild (1936), The Awful Truth (1937), Love Affair (1939) and I Remember Mama (1948).  In 1985, Dunne was given Kennedy Center Honors for her services to the arts...", died:date('1990-09-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ddzluiSppzKAfUd4g5iAxIDfsav.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77158"}}, {tmdbId:"128966", properties:{bornIn:"Wilmington, Delaware, USA", imdbId:"0852347", born:date('1894-05-20'), name:"Estelle Taylor", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEstelle Taylor (May 20, 1894—April 15, 1958) was an American Hollywood actress whose career was most prominent during the silent film era of the 1920s. \n\nBorn Ida Estelle Taylor in Wilmington, Delaware, the daughter of Harry D Taylor and Ida LaBertha (Barrett) Taylor, Estelle married three times during her lifetime...", died:date('1958-04-15'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/128966"}}, {tmdbId:"129038", properties:{bornIn:"Oakland, California, USA", imdbId:"0642042", born:date('1874-10-08'), name:"Nance O'Neil", bio:"Nance O'Neil, born Gertrude Lamson, was an American stage and screen actress.  When she decided to become an actress, her religious father, George Lamson, an auctioneer, denounced his daughter in church for going on the stage and asked the congregation to pray for her.  O'Neil's first performance in a professional production was in the role of a nun in Sarah at the Alcazar Theatre in San Francisco on October 16, 1893...", died:date('1965-02-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wXolbmlbecvQq7CinMpIrZpE7KU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/129038"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"13852", properties:{bornIn:" Carthage, Illinois", imdbId:"0156039", born:date('1908-04-12'), name:"Virginia Cherrill", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nVirginia Cherrill (April 12, 1908 - November 14, 1996) was an American actress best known for her role as the blind flower girl in Charlie Chaplin's City Lights (1931).  She married an English earl in the 1940s, and is also known as Virginia Child-Villiers, Countess of Jersey.  Virginia Cherrill was born on a farm in rural Carthage, Illinois, to James E.  and Blanche (née Wilcox) Cherrill...", died:date('1996-11-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/d2Mrbpgi9XYPrtGCFKoYYOwmEE6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13852"}}, {tmdbId:"13853", properties:{bornIn:"Vermont, United States", imdbId:"0497265", born:date('1888-03-12'), name:"Florence Lee", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nFlorence Lee (March 12, 1888 – September 1, 1962) was an American actress of the silent era.  She appeared in 99 films between 1911 and 1931.  She was born in Jamaica, Vermont and died in Hollywood, California at the age of 74. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article  Florence Lee licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1962-09-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/u2L68ykx3etqVpdI9MvHSy8yvvJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13853"}}, {tmdbId:"13854", properties:{bornIn:"New Haven, Connecticut, USA", imdbId:"0616729", born:date('1882-09-05'), name:"Harry Myers", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nHarry C.  Myers (5 September 1882 – 25 December 1938), sometimes credited as Henry Myers, was an American film actor and director.  He was born in New Haven, Connecticut, and died in Hollywood, California from pneumonia.  He was married to the actress Rosemary Theby. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Harry C.  Myers   licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1938-12-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pAr30tmTYCD58KmDdpkzthSI13W.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13854"}}, {tmdbId:"1547", properties:{bornIn:"Lugos, Kingdom of Hungary, Austria-Hungary [now Lugoj, Timis County, Romania]", imdbId:"0000509", born:date('1882-10-20'), name:"Bela Lugosi", bio:"Bela Lugosi (born Bela Ferenc Dezso Blasko) was a Hungarian stage, screen, and television actor.  He is best remembered for his iconic portrayal of Count Dracula in the classic 1931 Dracula film...", died:date('1956-08-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nG5R612STBg6RB7HJ6Aa3He50uD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1547"}}, {tmdbId:"1548", properties:{bornIn:"Charleston, South Carolina, USA", imdbId:"0151377", born:date('1906-02-01'), name:"Helen Chandler", bio:"Helen Chandler was an American stage and screen actress.  She is today best remembered for her portrayal of Mina in the 1931 classic horror film Dracula...", died:date('1965-04-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ofOzVWvIBIURFXwTKpt3Y3EVmhO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1548"}}, {tmdbId:"2125", properties:{bornIn:"Halifax, Nova Scotia, Canada", imdbId:"0543115", born:date('1900-04-30'), name:"David Manners", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDavid Joseph Manners (born Rauff de Ryther Duan _[some other sources spell Daun]_ Acklom, April 30, 1900 – December 23, 1998) was a Canadian-American actor who played John Harker in Todd Browning's 1931 horror classic Dracula.  The following year he portrayed the archaeologist Frank Whemple in another pre-Code thriller by Universal Pictures, The Mummy.  Manners abandoned his film career in 1936, and his theatrical career seventeen years later...", died:date('1998-12-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pPZvYbYlTYC97yMBDJ4ywMjQ4u1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2125"}}, {tmdbId:"1549", properties:{bornIn:"Salina, Kansas, USA", imdbId:"0296859", born:date('1899-02-22'), name:"Dwight Frye", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDwight Iliff Frye (February 22, 1899 – November 7, 1943) was an American stage and screen actor, noted for his appearances in the classic horror films Dracula, Frankenstein and Bride of Frankenstein. \n\nFrye was born in Salina, Kansas...", died:date('1943-11-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/i08HYM8ddyK82fynl7WZy6HFLBI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1549"}}, {tmdbId:"37675", properties:{bornIn:"Gröbming, Austria-Hungary", imdbId:"0286993", born:date('1884-10-30'), name:"Rudolf Forster", died:date('1968-10-25'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/37675"}}, {tmdbId:"222228", properties:{bornIn:"München, Germany", imdbId:"0624552", born:date('1900-11-02'), name:"Carola Neher", bio:"Carola Neher was a German stage and screen actress and singer.  In 1926, she went to Berlin to work with Bertolt Brecht, who wrote the role of Polly Peachum in \"The Threepenny Opera\" for her.  While in Berlin, she practiced boxing with Turkish trainer and prizefighter Sabri Mahir at his studio, which opened to women, including Vicki Baum and Marlene Dietrich, in the 1920s.  Carola Neher positioned herself as a \"New Woman\", challenging traditional gender categories...", died:date('1942-06-26'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/222228"}}, {tmdbId:"4344", properties:{bornIn:"Hamburg, Germany", imdbId:"0778306", born:date('1886-11-07'), name:"Reinhold Schünzel", died:date('1954-11-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jT61usHhQHPiWAFluozzjD2ZHvZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4344"}}, {tmdbId:"2923", properties:{bornIn:"Saint-Malo, Brittany, France", imdbId:"0166972", born:date('1900-01-20'), name:"Colin Clive", bio:"Colin Clive was born to a British colonel and his wife in St.  Malo, France on 20 January 1900.  His schooling was at the Convent of the Holy Cross, Boscombe, and Stonyhurst College, in preparation for entering Sandhurst, the British royal military academy.  Unfortunately, a riding accident shattered the young man's knee and disqualified him for military service.  Clive entered the Royal Academy of Dramatic Arts, making his debut in 1919 as 'Claude' in The Eclipse...", died:date('1937-06-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/msElGi0wyZ3BfUcnyi5UXAQzy00.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2923"}}, {tmdbId:"29814", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0164883", born:date('1910-08-16'), name:"Mae Clarke", bio:"Mae Clarke (born Violet Mary Klotz in 1910) was an American stage, screen, and television actress.  She is best known for being the recipient of Jimmy Cagney's half grapefruit in 'The Public Enemy' and for her role in 'Frankenstein'...", died:date('1992-04-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9u2HttpMOejKjrF61eOdjE9uw8c.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29814"}}, {tmdbId:"29815", properties:{bornIn:"Greenville, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0092900", born:date('1895-10-28'), name:"John Boles", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJohn Boles (October 28, 1895 – February 27, 1969) was an American singer and actor best known for playing Victor Moritz in the 1931 film Frankenstein.   He started out in Hollywood in silent movies, but became a huge star with the advent of talkies.  After the war, Boles moved to New York to study music.  He quickly became well known for his talents and was selected to replace the leading man in the 1923 Broadway musical Little Jesse James...", died:date('1969-02-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/q9738FvgVVOowYHp3UCWcTuTNcA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29815"}}, {tmdbId:"2922", properties:{bornIn:"Camberwell, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0000472", born:date('1887-11-23'), name:"Boris Karloff", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBoris Karloff (23 November 1887 – 2 February 1969), whose real name was William Henry Pratt, was an English-born actor who emigrated to Canada in 1909. \n\nKarloff is best remembered for his roles in horror films and his portrayal of Frankenstein's monster in Frankenstein (1931), Bride of Frankenstein (1935), and Son of Frankenstein (1939)...", died:date('1969-02-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fVi0QkiziavXB8HnWk5NzRcnCO1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2922"}}, {tmdbId:"55336", properties:{bornIn:"Rio de Janeiro, Brazil", imdbId:"0107539", born:date('1911-01-18'), name:"Olga Breno", died:date('2000-10-11'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55336"}}, {tmdbId:"55337", properties:{imdbId:"0721169", name:"Tatiana Rey", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55337"}}, {tmdbId:"55338", properties:{imdbId:"0774231", name:"Raul Schnoor", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55338"}}, {tmdbId:"55339", properties:{imdbId:"0670083", name:"Brutus Pedreira", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55339"}}, {tmdbId:"2094", properties:{bornIn:"Rózsahegy (now Ružomberok), Austria-Hungary (now Slovakia)", imdbId:"0000048", born:date('1904-06-26'), name:"Peter Lorre", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPeter Lorre (26 June 1904 – 23 March 1964) was an Austrian-American actor frequently typecast as a sinister foreigner. \n\nHe caused an international sensation in 1931 with his portrayal of a serial killer who preys on little girls in the German film M.  Later he became a popular featured player in Hollywood crime films and mysteries, notably alongside Humphrey Bogart and Sydney Greenstreet, and as the star of the successful Mr.  Moto detective series...", died:date('1964-03-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/elyPDRDyCFGsdyXjxqlS4cdtN8A.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2094"}}, {tmdbId:"12322", properties:{bornIn:"Biel/Bienne, Switzerland Switzerland", imdbId:"0927145", born:date('1894-12-15'), name:"Ellen Widmann", died:date('1985-10-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lYbFnXdGCgyHh2pVnELQVmLgKKu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12322"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"12323", properties:{bornIn:"Berlin - Germany", imdbId:"0484737", born:date('1922-11-23'), name:"Inge Landgut", bio:"Inge Landgut war eine deutsche Schauspielerin und Synchronsprecherin. \n\nDie Tochter des Kraftfahrers Wilhelm Landgut und seiner Ehefrau Gertrud stand bereits im Alter von drei Jahren vor der Kamera und wirkte als Kinderdarstellerin in knapp 30 Stummfilmen sowie frühen Tonfilmen mit.  Hervorzuheben sind dabei ihre Auftritte als Pony Hütchen in der ersten Verfilmung von Emil und die Detektive nach Erich Kästner und als Opfer des Kindermörders in Fritz Langs M...", died:date('1986-05-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zNzk5bvChgVx4tAKpuCJPX5xxMO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12323"}}, {tmdbId:"12324", properties:{bornIn:"Osterode am Harz", imdbId:"0921532", born:date('1893-09-30'), name:"Otto Wernicke", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nOtto Karl Robert Wernicke (30 September 1893, Osterode am Harz – 7 November 1965) was a German actor.  He was best known for his role as police inspector Karl Lohmann in the two Fritz Lang films M and The Testament of Dr.  Mabuse.  He was the first one to portray Captain Smith in the first \"official\" Titanic film. \n\nWernicke was married to a Jewish woman.  Only due to a special permit was he allowed to continue his work in Nazi Germany...", died:date('1965-11-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2jz2sXMeO5LM1DSJs3zeAkNtjj2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12324"}}, {tmdbId:"83476", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0007220", born:date('1900-09-19'), name:"Ricardo Cortez", bio:"Ricardo Cortez (September 19, 1900 – April 28, 1977) was an American film actor who began his career during the silent film era. \n\nBorn Jacob Krantz in New York City into a Jewish family, he worked on Wall Street in a broker's office and as a boxer before his looks got him into the film business.  Hollywood executives changed his name to Cortez to appeal to film-goers as a \"Latin lover\" to compete with such highly popular actors of the era as Rudolph Valentino, Ramon Novarro and Antonio Moreno...", died:date('1977-04-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7Q6drcz0brLbgu3zuJuL1naemdu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83476"}}, {tmdbId:"100243", properties:{bornIn:"Dublin, Ireland, UK [now Republic of Ireland]", imdbId:"0226502", born:date('1879-06-09'), name:"Dudley Digges", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDudley Digges (June 9, 1879 – October 24, 1947) was an Irish character actor on stage and in motion pictures. \n\nHe was born in Dublin.  He went to America with a group of Irish players in 1904 and became successful both as an actor and producer.  For a time he was stage manager to Charles Frohman and George Arliss.  He went to Hollywood in 1930...", died:date('1947-10-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1VCZYSSO7JTrwMLeI1NBp4d7o2x.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100243"}}, {tmdbId:"13963", properties:{bornIn:"Covington, Kentucky, USA", imdbId:"0580916", born:date('1903-12-10'), name:"Una Merkel", bio:"Southerner Una Merkel was a popular American stage, screen, and television actress.  In movies, while often cast as the female lead, she more typically appeared in prominent supporting roles...", died:date('1986-01-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hBDjQyU2xJ9vELw0H63igS7ugSD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13963"}}, {tmdbId:"5788", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000010", born:date('1899-07-17'), name:"James Cagney", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJames Francis Cagney, Jr.  (July 17, 1899 – March 30, 1986) was an American film actor.  Although he won acclaim and major awards for a wide variety of roles, he is best remembered for playing \"tough guys\".  In 1999, the American Film Institute ranked him eighth among the Greatest Male Stars of All Time. \n\nIn his first performing role, Cagney danced dressed as a woman in the chorus line of the 1919 revue Every Sailor...", died:date('1986-03-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kcFPx9Xq63AUZ83zMoqqs8Zjrcj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5788"}}, {tmdbId:"82315", properties:{bornIn:"Kansas City, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0001318", born:date('1911-03-03'), name:"Jean Harlow", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJean Harlow (March 3, 1911 – June 7, 1937) was an American film actress and sex symbol of the 1930s.  Known as the \"Blonde Bombshell\" and the \"Platinum Blonde\" (due to her platinum blonde hair), Harlow was ranked one of the greatest movie stars of all time by the American Film Institute...", died:date('1937-06-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bZGHQeMeD6oXqi3373IPYrSB761.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82315"}}, {tmdbId:"82316", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0940589", born:date('1903-07-05'), name:"Edward Woods", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEdward Woods (July 5, 1903, Los Angeles -- October 8, 1989, Salt Lake City) was an American actor best known for his lead role in The Public Enemy opposite James Cagney...", died:date('1989-10-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/m2146RHFqYIDqoLI75vSKIg8zsF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82316"}}, {tmdbId:"13568", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000951", born:date('1906-08-30'), name:"Joan Blondell", bio:"Rose Joan Blondell (August 30, 1906 – December 25, 1979) was an American actress. \n\nAfter winning a beauty pageant, Blondell embarked upon a film career.  Establishing herself as a sexy wisecracking blonde, she was a pre-Code staple of Warner Brothers and appeared in more than 100 movies and television productions.  She was most active in films during the 1930s, and during this time she co-starred with Glenda Farrell in nine films, in which the duo portrayed gold-diggers...", died:date('1979-12-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/s2jdLZ53csCtTtDebKYno7xECPG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13568"}}, {tmdbId:"14582", properties:{imdbId:"0558038", name:"Matahi", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14582"}}, {tmdbId:"14583", properties:{bornIn:"Tahiti, French Polynesia", imdbId:"0156617", born:date('1912-01-01'), name:"Anne Chevalier", died:date('1977-01-01'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14583"}}, {tmdbId:"14584", properties:{imdbId:"0051447", name:"Bill Bambridge", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14584"}}, {tmdbId:"14585", properties:{imdbId:"0386979", name:"Hitu", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14585"}}, {tmdbId:"117802", properties:{imdbId:"0545384", born:date('1898-08-28'), name:"Henri Marchand", died:date('1959-05-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/epDF1A2LcQCGLY4ZKKO2sdoxtYl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/117802"}}, {tmdbId:"117803", properties:{bornIn:"Vitry-sur-Seine, Val-de-Marne, France", imdbId:"0179690", born:date('1898-12-09'), name:"Raymond Cordy", died:date('1956-04-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/d2A3UUlSoemwnMN5D8VzCPLfltV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/117803"}}, {tmdbId:"117804", properties:{imdbId:"0289840", name:"Rolla France", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fBphMzuDc27GJ0J6Y2ruUSQwlsx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/117804"}}, {tmdbId:"117805", properties:{bornIn:"Marseille, Bouches du Rhône, France", imdbId:"0647378", born:date('1876-02-09'), name:"Paul Ollivier", died:date('1948-06-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rAg9cXJZ4AMI6jHZPozYgbXoUWd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/117805"}}, {tmdbId:"47439", properties:{bornIn:"Washington, District of Columbia, USA", imdbId:"0371040", born:date('1900-10-10'), name:"Helen Hayes", bio:"Helen Hayes was an American actress whose career spanned almost 70 years.  She eventually garnered the nickname \"First Lady of the American Theatre\" and was one of twelve people who have won an Emmy, a Grammy, an Oscar and a Tony Award.  Hayes also received the Presidential Medal of Freedom, America's highest civilian honor, from President Ronald Reagan in 1986.  In 1988 she was awarded the National Medal of Arts...", died:date('1993-03-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/i1mqaJOQG9TBVBZjn8No70GeGhE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/47439"}}, {tmdbId:"4068", properties:{bornIn:"Helena, Montana, USA", imdbId:"0000011", born:date('1901-05-07'), name:"Gary Cooper", bio:"Gary Cooper was an American film actor known for his natural, authentic, and understated acting style and screen performances.  His career spanned thirty-six years, from 1925 to 1961, and included leading roles in eighty-four feature films.  He was a major movie star from the end of the silent film era through to the end of the golden age of Classical Hollywood.  His screen persona appealed strongly to both men and women, and his range of performances included roles in most major movie genres...", died:date('1961-05-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/67svKX2KuFwwBvrijIb7bBtBgIM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4068"}}, {tmdbId:"14563", properties:{bornIn:"Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0579663", born:date('1890-02-18'), name:"Adolphe Menjou", bio:"Adolphe Menjou was an American actor, his screen career spanning both silent films (with credited roles from 1916 onward) and talkies.  Among the many well-known films Menjou had prominent roles in are The Sheik, A Woman of Paris, Morocco, A Farewell to Arms, A Star is Born, Stage Door, Paths of Glory, and Pollyanna.  Menjou was nominated for a Best Lead Actor Academy Award for 1931's The Front Page...", died:date('1963-10-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/88FfjxT3cFDIbCIK0UmwyjEF6tU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14563"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"48960", properties:{bornIn:"New London, Connecticut, USA", imdbId:"0680102", born:date('1901-01-23'), name:"Mary Philips", bio:"Mary Philips was an American stage, screen, and television actress...", died:date('1975-04-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/seFakubSAT4uEsd3N9uUjxvrfm4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/48960"}}, {tmdbId:"35849", properties:{bornIn:"Bolton, Lancashire, England, UK ", imdbId:"0285922", born:date('1898-02-12'), name:"Wallace Ford", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nWallace Ford (12 February 1898 – 11 June 1966) was an English movie and television actor who, with his friendly appearance and stocky build later in life, appeared in a number of movie westerns and B-movies. \n\nBorn Samuel Jones Grundy in Bolton, Lancashire, England, he spent his childhood in a Dr.  Barnardo's home.  At an early age he was adopted by a farmer from Manitoba, Canada, where he was ill treated...", died:date('1966-06-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7Dlj58KmYEerbvzqZ03Cc7xvMYh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/35849"}}, {tmdbId:"1507", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0404885", born:date('1905-05-01'), name:"Leila Hyams", bio:"Leila Hyams (May 1, 1905 – December 4, 1977) was an American model, vaudeville and film actress, who came from a show business family.  Her relatively short film career began in the 1920s during the era of silent films and ended in 1936.  Although her career only lasted around twelve years, the blonde blue-eyed ingenue appeared in more than 50 film roles and remained a press favorite, with numerous magazine covers...", died:date('1977-12-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yNgnTnK8OVBIgFvud4mzY3PMn5Z.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1507"}}, {tmdbId:"1508", properties:{bornIn:"Moscow, Russian Empire [now Russia]", imdbId:"0045754", born:date('1893-08-19'), name:"Olga Baclanova", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nÓlga Vladímirovna Baclanova (19 August 1893 – 6 September 1974) was a Russian-born actress and operatic singer, who achieved prominence during the silent film era and was often billed under her last name only, as Baclanova, similarly to the surname-only nomenclature assigned to fellow countryman Nazimova...", died:date('1974-09-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9TewBEtr4CvKMc5cUi12mI0q2h.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1508"}}, {tmdbId:"1509", properties:{bornIn:"Grange, Mississippi, USA", imdbId:"0040374", born:date('1895-01-20'), name:"Roscoe Ates", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nRoscoe Ates (January 20, 1895 – March 1, 1962) was an American vaudeville performer, actor of stage and screen, comedian and musician who primarily was featured in western films and television.  He was best known as western character Soapy Jones...", died:date('1962-03-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rZ2Oq45XeKNwz913Jo4DJBzW0b4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1509"}}, {tmdbId:"19549", properties:{bornIn:"Stockholm, Stockholms län, Sweden", imdbId:"0001256", born:date('1905-09-18'), name:"Greta Garbo", bio:"Greta Garbo was a Swedish-American film actress during the 1920s and 1930s.  Garbo was nominated three times for the Academy Award for Best Actress and received an Academy Honorary Award in 1954 for her \"luminous and unforgettable screen performances...", died:date('1990-04-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/erOWor1CMGwQUAjosN760gde7hj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19549"}}, {tmdbId:"29578", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0000858", born:date('1882-02-15'), name:"John Barrymore", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJohn Sidney Blyth Barrymore (February 15, 1882 – May 29, 1942) was an acclaimed American actor.  He first gained fame as a handsome stage actor in light comedy, then high drama and culminating in groundbreaking portrayals in Shakespearean plays Hamlet and Richard III.  His success continued with motion pictures in various genres in both the silent and sound eras...", died:date('1942-05-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rteTiRqFoINZvf3qoXk6nHE7ekk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29578"}}, {tmdbId:"31550", properties:{bornIn:"San Antonio, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0001076", born:date('1904-03-23'), name:"Joan Crawford", bio:"Born Lucille Fay LeSueur in San Antonio, Texas, but christened Joan Crawford by Hollywood, she exemplified the 1920s carefree \"flapper\" era to a 'T'.  Her beauty and vivacity catapulted her to stardom in the late 1920s in the hugely popular silent film Our Dancing Daughters.  Ever since that point, the resilient actress with the ever expressive eyes, the famous over-painted lips and the will of steel created for herself one of the most legendary and enduring Hollywood personae of all time...", died:date('1977-05-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/AtEGacmejG86ug8tKTxFd7JbJJO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31550"}}, {tmdbId:"13352", properties:{bornIn:"Lemberg, Galicia, Austria-Hungary", imdbId:"0612847", born:date('1895-09-22'), name:"Paul Muni", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPaul Muni (born Meshilem Meier Weisenfreund, September 22, 1895 – August 25, 1967) was an Austrian-Hungarian-born American stage and film actor.  During the 1930s, he was considered the most prestigious actor at Warner Brothers studios, and one of the rare actors who was given the privilege of choosing which parts he wanted...", died:date('1967-08-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4ZWtvroJFsfjpQ8H7PhEVeBqRy3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13352"}}, {tmdbId:"99349", properties:{bornIn:"Beaumont, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0899091", born:date('1907-09-17'), name:"Helen Vinson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nHelen Vinson (September 17, 1907 – October 7, 1999) was an American film actress, who appeared in 40 films between 1932 and 1945. \n\nVinson's screen career often featured her in roles in which she played the part of the other woman or (pre-Code) loose women with active romantic lives.  Her first film role was Jewel Robbery (1932), which starred William Powell and Kay Francis...", died:date('1999-10-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8hoGY2a62SHP5A1FovtCRTWphY1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/99349"}}, {tmdbId:"104800", properties:{bornIn:"Temple, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0290271", born:date('1906-08-31'), name:"Noel Francis", bio:"Noel Francis was born in Temple, Texas in 1906.  By age 20 she was appearing in the Ziegfeld Follies, working opposite the comedy team of Wheeler and Woolsey.  Eventually Fox scouts noticed her and in 1929 she was signed to a Hollywood contract.  Because of her Follies background, Fox intended to develop Noel as a musical and dance star.  Unfortunately, musicals were on the wane at the time (they did rebound) and her contract was dropped...", died:date('1959-10-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6ThFI6XzI32Xe7CtK4buhGmqCL7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/104800"}}, {tmdbId:"78828", properties:{bornIn:"Deutschbentschek, Austria-Hungary [now Romania]", imdbId:"0423685", born:date('1904-07-14'), name:"Zita Johann", bio:"Zita Johann (born Elisabeth Johann) was a stage and screen actress best known for her dual role as Helen Grosvenor / Princess Ankhesenamón in the 1932 film The Mummy.  Born in what is today part of Romania, Johann immigrated to the United States with her family in 1911...", died:date('1993-09-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3IowlVJPxpQgHjdrTuGMxUqyAib.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78828"}}, {tmdbId:"78829", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn [now in New York City], New York, USA", imdbId:"0126365", born:date('1872-04-03'), name:"Arthur Byron", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nArthur William Byron (April 3, 1872 – July 16, 1943) was an American actor, the son of actors Kate Crehan and Oliver Doud Byron.  He played a mixture of British and American roles in films.  He was a nephew of the stage actress Ada Rehan, his maternal aunt. \n\nByron started his theatrical career at the age of 17 with his father's dramatic company.  In 1939 he celebrated his 50 years in show business...", died:date('1943-07-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/v3D12CCPQbyzxFiX2ZwbRvv7DHJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78829"}}, {tmdbId:"77669", properties:{imdbId:"0513325", name:"Leon M. Lion", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eHYga4nBTh93oUyUVBGyMPMDnq2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77669"}}, {tmdbId:"77670", properties:{bornIn:"Lincoln, Lincolnshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0340514", born:date('1907-03-06'), name:"Anne Grey", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nAnne Grey (6 March 1907 – 3 April 1987) was an English actress, who appeared in 44 films between 1928 and 1939, including some Hollywood films during the late 1930s. \n\nShe was educated at Lausanne and King's College London.  She originally intended a literary career, and to become a journalist but went on stage instead.  Her first film experience in 1925 was in a crowd scene in The Constant Nymph but she got second lead in her next picture just two months later...", died:date('1987-04-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wWtvH3LtQLNvgk0vLgAPkAPwqGi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77670"}}, {tmdbId:"30709", properties:{bornIn:"Edinburgh, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0835738", born:date('1898-07-18'), name:"John Stuart", died:date('1979-10-17'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30709"}}, {tmdbId:"7384", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0130740", born:date('1888-04-11'), name:"Donald Calthrop", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDonald Esme Clayton Calthrop (11 April 1888 – 15 July 1940) was an English stage and film actor. \n\nCalthrop made his first stage appearance at eighteen years of age.  His first film was The Gay Lord Quex released in 1917.  He starred as the title character in the successful musical The Boy in the same year.  He then appeared in 63 films between 1916 and 1940, including five films directed by Alfred Hitchcock...", died:date('1940-07-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eTSdS6mPjClbRXwWezEB3397nAP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7384"}}, {tmdbId:"34745", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0002051", born:date('1893-02-10'), name:"Jimmy Durante", bio:"Comedian, composer, actor, singer and songwriter (\"Inka Dinka Doo\")  Jimmy Durante was educated in New York public schools.  He began his  career as a Coney Island pianist, and organized a five-piece band in  1916.  He opened the Club Durant with Eddie Jackson and Lou Clayton,  with whom he later formed a comedy trio for vaudeville and on  television.  He appeared in the Broadway musicals \"Show Girl\", \"The New  Yorkers\", \"Strike Me Pink\", \"Jumbo\", \"Red Hot and Blue\", and \"Stars in  Your Eyes\"...", died:date('1980-01-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lYZ7X60QrRe6CxmWaJJAisHz7p3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34745"}}, {tmdbId:"148513", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0602959", born:date('1883-06-28'), name:"Polly Moran", died:date('1952-01-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hvhMZo9CNtBNOwm1CVO5e2HthG0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/148513"}}, {tmdbId:"148512", properties:{bornIn:"Whiting, Indiana, USA", imdbId:"0700723", born:date('1896-08-07'), name:"Irene Purcell", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nIrene Mary Purcell (August 7, 1896 – July 9, 1972) was an American film and stage actress, who appeared mostly in comedies, and later married Herbert Fisk Johnson Jr. , the wealthy grandson of the founder of S.  C.  Johnson & Son...", died:date('1972-07-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/f1d0cQIIVMbuesA2ydj9xBlVY3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/148512"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"33973", properties:{bornIn:"Boston, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0397300", born:date('1899-01-03'), name:"Fred Howard", died:date('1960-04-21'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33973"}}, {tmdbId:"229958", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0376698", born:date('1893-11-02'), name:"Ben Hendricks Jr.", died:date('1938-08-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gpNJtZQ78NvXRmYoErCPuotQJ7y.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/229958"}}, {tmdbId:"87697", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0307326", born:date('1905-07-18'), name:"William Gargan", bio:"William Gargan, born William Dennis Gargan July 17, 1905 in Brooklyn, New York, USA and died February 17, 1979 aged 73 on a flight between New York and San Diego. \n\nHe was an American motion picture, television and radio actor.  Gargan played character roles in many Hollywood productions, including two appearances as detective Ellery Queen, but was best known for his role as Detective Martin Kane in the 1949-51 radio-television series, Martin Kane, Private Eye, sponsored by U. S.  Tobacco...", died:date('1979-02-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/55wJFlLmqeSGKVV91KuqNgSeZT9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/87697"}}, {tmdbId:"232955", properties:{imdbId:"0789865", name:"Mary Shaw", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/232955"}}, {tmdbId:"11492", properties:{bornIn:"Cadiz, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0000022", born:date('1901-02-01'), name:"Clark Gable", bio:"William Clark Gable (February 1, 1901 – November 16, 1960) was an American film actor.  In 1999, the American Film Institute named Gable seventh among the greatest male stars of all time. \n\nGable's most famous role was Rhett Butler in the 1939 Civil War epic film Gone with the Wind, in which he starred with Vivien Leigh...", died:date('1960-11-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qD6WJzydym7n7fCeL9PGnHe1aEV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11492"}}, {tmdbId:"117419", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0713270", born:date('1908-08-13'), name:"Gene Raymond", bio:"Gene Raymond, born Raymond Guion, was an American film, television, and stage actor of the 1930s and 1940s.  In addition to acting, Raymond was also a composer, writer, director, producer, and decorated military pilot. \n\nHis screen debut was in Personal Maid (1931).  Another early appearance was in the multi-director If I Had a Million with W.  C.  Fields and Charles Laughton...", died:date('1998-05-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kCY8h8lNlh9GtQ0MtC32omMAj9k.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/117419"}}, {tmdbId:"13992", properties:{bornIn:"Quincy, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0000802", born:date('1906-05-03'), name:"Mary Astor", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMary Astor (May 3, 1906 - September 25, 1987) was an American actress.  Most remembered for her role as Brigid O'Shaughnessy in The Maltese Falcon (1941) with Humphrey Bogart, Astor began her long motion picture career as a teenager in the silent movies of the early 1920s.  She eventually made a successful transition to talkies, but almost saw her career destroyed due to public scandal in the mid-1930s...", died:date('1987-09-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/njNeTQorH4omB41znMZEgAJsXop.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13992"}}, {tmdbId:"114768", properties:{bornIn:"Streatham Hill, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0447597", born:date('1897-05-28'), name:"Henry Kendall", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nHenry Kendall, (28 May 1897 – 9 June 1962) was an English stage and film actor, theatre director and an immaculately stylish revue artiste. \n\nKendall was born in London in 1897 and educated at the City of London School.  He made his first appearance on the stage in September 1914 at the Lyceum Theatre, playing a 'super' in Tommy Atkins...", died:date('1962-06-09'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/114768"}}, {tmdbId:"115153", properties:{bornIn:"Detroit, Michigan, Stati Uniti", imdbId:"0058039", born:date('1903-11-05'), name:"Joan Barry", died:date('1989-04-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ytLF5h5CPeWA9VcfP9RFwEXVgIl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/115153"}}, {tmdbId:"27929", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0549385", born:date('1883-11-25'), name:"Percy Marmont", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nPercy Marmont (25 November 1883 – 3 March 1977) was an English film actor.  Marmont appeared in more than 80 films between 1916 and 1968.  He is best remembered today for playing the title character in Lord Jim (1925), the first film version of Joseph Conrad's novel, and for playing one of Clara Bow's love interests in the Paramount Pictures film Mantrap (1926)...", died:date('1977-03-03'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27929"}}, {tmdbId:"222671", properties:{bornIn:"Pirmasens, Germany", imdbId:"0023894", born:date('1907-03-10'), name:"Betty Amann", died:date('1990-08-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ggAZUi7OV019dysiER3UTVxFk35.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/222671"}}, {tmdbId:"13353", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0245304", born:date('1911-08-02'), name:"Ann Dvorak", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAnn Dvorak (born Anna McKim) was an American stage and film actress.  Asked how to pronounce her adopted surname, she told The Literary Digest: \"My fake name is properly pronounced vor'shack.  The D remains silent...", died:date('1979-12-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/w7AIhoCgeruXUzz9UCVWHA3Ztx0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13353"}}, {tmdbId:"13354", properties:{bornIn:"Ottumwa, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0605904", born:date('1909-12-12'), name:"Karen Morley", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nKaren Morley (December 12, 1909 – March 8, 2003) was an American film actress. After working at the Pasadena Playhouse, she came to the attention of the director Clarence Brown when he was looking for an actress to stand-in for Greta Garbo in screen tests...", died:date('2003-03-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/akdCM0dAmHDBYycLuUQqpyLMmk0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13354"}}, {tmdbId:"32004", properties:{bornIn:"Wien, Austria", imdbId:"0226158", born:date('1899-12-30'), name:"Gustav Diessl", died:date('1948-03-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1vYIlFuRYohcwE3GFoyqqo7u0XA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32004"}}, {tmdbId:"26600", properties:{bornIn:"Leipzig, Germany", imdbId:"0771869", born:date('1906-04-17'), name:"Rudolf Schündler", died:date('1988-12-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cGQbR4f9cLRld2j8CWPXP2c2g4k.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/26600"}}, {tmdbId:"2433", properties:{bornIn:"Savannah, Georgia, USA", imdbId:"0394244", born:date('1902-10-18'), name:"Miriam Hopkins", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nEllen Miriam Hopkins (October 18, 1902 – October 9, 1972) was an American actress known for her versatility.  She first signed with Paramount Pictures in 1930, working with Ernst Lubitsch and Joel McCrea, among many others.  Her long-running feud with Bette Davis was publicized for effect.  Later she became a pioneer of TV drama.  Hopkins was a distinguished Hollywood hostess, who moved in intellectual and creative circles...", died:date('1972-10-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2ET5s4fwU1lWwbJ73FJw0xQGgdr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2433"}}, {tmdbId:"2434", properties:{bornIn:"Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, USA", imdbId:"0290215", born:date('1905-01-13'), name:"Kay Francis", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nKay Francis (January 13, 1905 – August 26, 1968) was an American stage and film actress.  After a brief period on Broadway in the late 1920s, she moved to film and achieved her greatest success between 1930 and 1936, when she was the number one female star at the Warner Brothers studio, and the highest paid American film actress...", died:date('1968-08-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4H1R7ICS3xHDBi9dg0EkSuvPTqp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2434"}}, {tmdbId:"2436", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA ", imdbId:"0749476", born:date('1886-02-08'), name:"Charles Ruggles", bio:"Charles Ruggles had one of the longest careers in Hollywood, lasting more than 60 years and encompassing more than 100 films.  He made his film debut in 1914 in The Patchwork Girl of Oz (1914) and worked steadily after that.  He was memorably paired with Mary Boland in a series of comedies in the early 1930s, and was one of the standouts in the all-star comedy If I Had a Million (1932), as a harried, much-put-upon man who finally goes berserk in a china shop...", died:date('1970-12-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yokW91qtcCJvWoqxC3ODumu8yVV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2436"}}, {tmdbId:"213511", properties:{bornIn:" Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0756870", born:date('1902-06-10'), name:"Tatsuo Saitô", bio:"Tatsuo Saitō (斎藤 達雄, Saitō Tatsuo, 10 June 1902 – 2 March 1968) was a Japanese film actor.  He appeared in more than one hundred films from 1925 to 1967...", died:date('1968-03-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gFue2IdqAXQLm9GkeiDDOmoBAQx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/213511"}}, {tmdbId:"142474", properties:{bornIn:"Yokohama, Japan", imdbId:"0031832", born:date('1923-10-07'), name:"Tomio Aoki", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nTomio Aoki (October 7, 1923 in Yokohama, Japan – January 24, 2004 in Setagaya, Tokyo, Japan) aka Tokkan Kozō was a Japanese film actor. \n\nAoki became famous as a child actor after debuting at the age of six in silent films directed by Yasujirō Ozu.  His leading role in Ozu's 1929 short comedy Tokkan kozo gave Aoki his nickname.  I Was Born, But. . ...", died:date('2004-01-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4DXHn4MgfZgf72wNvG7uYhe1Ld9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/142474"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"145253", properties:{bornIn:"Chūō, Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0948989", born:date('1901-06-21'), name:"Mitsuko Yoshikawa", bio:"Mitsuko Yoshikawa (吉川 満子) (June 21, 1901 – August 8, 1991) was a Japanese actress.  She debuted during the silent film era in 1926 and made her last film in 1984, which was Juzo Itami's The Funeral...", died:date('1991-08-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qp9Nx3nzlIYy6Lrhv1fapNLxUpL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/145253"}}, {tmdbId:"1092896", properties:{bornIn:"Hakodate, Hokkaido, Japan", imdbId:"0837424", born:date('1924-01-03'), name:"Hideo Sugawara", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xJPGRBjBDaxKDfsTWoDYGE77vY1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1092896"}}, {tmdbId:"96470", properties:{bornIn:"Hillsboro, Texas, U.S", imdbId:"0068705", born:date('1899-06-30'), name:"Madge Bellamy", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMadge Bellamy (June 30, 1899 – January 24, 1990) was an American film actress who was a popular leading lady in the 1920s and early 1930s.  Her career declined in the sound era, and ended following a romantic scandal in the 1940s. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Madge Bellamy, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1990-01-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2hXkzJFw2M5sy2Aa0YvqJUQsRDk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96470"}}, {tmdbId:"34758", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0147248", born:date('1868-03-29'), name:"Joseph Cawthorn", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJoseph Cawthorn (March 29, 1868, New York City, New York – January 21, 1949, Beverly Hills, California) was an American stage and film comic actor.   Cawthorn started out in show business as a child, debuting at Robinson's Music Hall in his hometown of New York in 1872.  He appeared in minstrel shows and vaudeville as a \"Dutch\" comic, employing a thick German dialect.  He later worked in British music halls and American touring companies...", died:date('1949-01-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7qZSva6ZbWenUPli0knUphbRKpZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34758"}}, {tmdbId:"96471", properties:{bornIn:"Worcester, Massachusetts, US", imdbId:"0292537", born:date('1891-06-29'), name:"Robert Frazer", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRobert W.  Frazer born Robert William Browne on 29 June 1891 in Worcester, Massachusetts, US was an American actor that appeared in some 224 shorts and films from the 1910s until his death on 17 August 1944, aged 53 in Los Angeles, California, US due to leukemia.  In 1912 he played the title role in the 1912 silent film version of Robin Hood and a year later he played Jesus Christ in Thus Saith the Lord...", died:date('1944-08-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tyiZdwKcMkROcZhqI7LtBBR7X8n.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96471"}}, {tmdbId:"134268", properties:{bornIn:"Georgetown, British Guiana [now Guyana]", imdbId:"0042552", born:date('1884-06-12'), name:"William Austin", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nWilliam Austin  (12 June 1884 – 15 June 1975) was a British character actor who was born on a sugar plantation in Georgetown in British Guiana (now Guyana).  On the death of his father he was brought to England to complete his education.  He later filled a business post in Shanghai and on being sent to San Francisco by the company he worked for, he decided to stay in America and take up acting on the stage and later in films...", died:date('1975-06-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iesu5SUtuUhtyiHUwBDBQl9AJKW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/134268"}}, {tmdbId:"89610", properties:{bornIn:"Cobourg, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0237597", born:date('1868-11-09'), name:"Marie Dressler", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMarie Dressler (born Leila Marie Koerber, November 9, 1868 – July 28, 1934) was a Canadian-American stage and screen actress, comedian, and early silent film and Depression-era film star.  Successful on stage in vaudeville and comic operas, she was also successful in film. \n\nLeaving home at the age of 14, Dressler built a career on stage in traveling theatre troupes, where she learned to appreciate her talent in making people laugh...", died:date('1934-07-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/x7pzugeAYtTVzoeRisXv9TJgkBg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89610"}}, {tmdbId:"20364", properties:{bornIn:"Ballinasloe, County Galway, Ireland", imdbId:"0107575", born:date('1904-03-15'), name:"George Brent", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGeorge Brent (born George Patrick [or George Brendan] Nolan, 15 March 1904 – 26 May 1979) was an Irish-American stage, film, and television actor. \n\nBrent was born in Ballinasloe, County Galway in 1904 to John J.  and Mary (née McGuinness) Nolan.  His mother was a native of Clonfad, Moore, County Roscommon. \n\nBrent made his first film, Under Suspicion, in 1930...", died:date('1979-05-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/831vetUvPxlDCd6yJitdnH1YeyX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20364"}}, {tmdbId:"30001", properties:{bornIn:"Dartmouth, Nova Scotia, Canada", imdbId:"0444528", born:date('1910-08-25'), name:"Ruby Keeler", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRuby Keeler, born Ethel Hilda Keeler, (August 25, 1910 – February 28, 1993) was an actress, singer, and dancer most famous for her on-screen coupling with Dick Powell in a string of successful early musicals at Warner Brothers, particularly 42nd Street (1933).  From 1928 to 1940, she was married to legendary singer Al Jolson.  She retired from show business in the 1940s but made a widely publicized comeback on Broadway in 1971...", died:date('1993-02-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5CmcKWPEaGgxMb8SgOtybECboj6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30001"}}, {tmdbId:"103616", properties:{bornIn:"Bushwick, Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0922213", born:date('1893-08-17'), name:"Mae West", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMae West (born Mary Jane West; August 17, 1893 – November 22, 1980) was an American actress, playwright, screenwriter and sex symbol whose entertainment career spanned seven decades.  Known for her bawdy double entendres, West made a name for herself in vaudeville and on the stage in New York before moving to Hollywood to become a comedienne, actress and writer in the motion picture industry...", died:date('1980-11-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fG3xtgjmTm5tXbNb6NSugtbhEyC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/103616"}}, {tmdbId:"2638", properties:{bornIn:"Horfield, Bristol, England, UK", imdbId:"0000026", born:date('1904-01-18'), name:"Cary Grant", bio:"Cary Grant (born Archibald Alec Leach; January 18, 1904 – November 29, 1986) was an English-born American actor, known as one of classic Hollywood's definitive leading men.  He was known for his transatlantic accent, debonair demeanor, light-hearted approach to acting, and sense of comic timing. \n\nGrant was born in Horfield, Bristol.  He became attracted to theater at a young age and began performing with a troupe known as \"The Penders\" at age six...", died:date('1986-11-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/moeJxPpEIF0abbjXYDPknDKLn44.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2638"}}, {tmdbId:"10610", properties:{bornIn:"Samara, Russian Empire [now Russia]", imdbId:"0711855", born:date('1897-04-20'), name:"Gregory Ratoff", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGregory Ratoff (20 April 1897 — 14 December 1960) was a Russian-born American film director, actor and producer.  His most famous role as an actor was as producer Max Fabian who feuds with star Margo Channing (Bette Davis) in All About Eve (1950). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Gregory Ratoff, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1960-12-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/u7uLiwMka8ipsZU5YE3jxe3HVcH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10610"}}, {tmdbId:"30211", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0036427", born:date('1890-02-18'), name:"Edward Arnold", bio:"Edward Arnold was born as Gunther Edward Arnold Schneider in 1890, on the Lower East Side of New York City, the son of German immigrants, Elizabeth (Ohse) and Carl Schneider.  Arnold began his acting career on the New York stage and became a film actor in 1916...", died:date('1956-04-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/acDcznSuVWTpPHtR6LJ3fJKT3c3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30211"}}, {tmdbId:"4113", properties:{bornIn:"Clapham, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0001647", born:date('1889-11-10'), name:"Claude Rains", bio:"Claude Rains (10 November 1889 – 30 May 1967) was an English stage and film actor whose career spanned 47 years; he later held American citizenship.  He was known for many roles in Hollywood  films, among them the title role in The Invisible Man (1933), a corrupt senator in Mr.  Smith Goes to Washington  (1939), and, perhaps his most famous performance, Captain Renault in Casablanca (1942). \n\nRains was born William Claude Rains in Camberwell, London on November 10, 1889...", died:date('1967-05-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/l8di3lovLqcJQ8gbHKJltQk5KvD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4113"}}, {tmdbId:"8535", properties:{bornIn:"Santa Monica, California, USA", imdbId:"0001784", born:date('1910-07-04'), name:"Gloria Stuart", bio:"Gloria Stuart (1910–2010) was an American actress, activist, painter, bonsai artist and fine printer. \n\nShe is best known for The Invisible Man and her Academy Award nominated role in Titanic.  She is the oldest person to be nominated for a competitive Oscar, at the age of 87...", died:date('2010-09-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9aG7UUX3PWIGGf1KRY5TsBSoNz9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8535"}}, {tmdbId:"66789", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0364203", born:date('1886-03-27'), name:"William Harrigan", bio:"William Harrigan was an American stage, screen, and television actor...", died:date('1966-02-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aV4dPO2hIi82t9Z8LtjHnc0oKFI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/66789"}}, {tmdbId:"7666", properties:{bornIn:"Berwick-upon-Tweed, Northumberland, England", imdbId:"0871287", born:date('1874-03-05'), name:"Henry Travers", bio:"British-born Henry Travers was a veteran of the English stage before  emigrating to the U. S.  in 1917.  He gained more stage experience there on  Broadway working with the Theatre Guild, and began his long film career  with Reunion in Vienna (1933).  Travers' kindly, grandfatherly demeanor became familiar to filmgoers over the next 25 years, especially in films like High Sierra (1941), where he played Joan Leslie's kindly but slyly observant uncle, and the generous Mr.  Bogardus in The Bells of St...", died:date('1965-10-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7qsZdxnngfOqXVaJOodfzeH6OGx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7666"}}, {tmdbId:"3242", properties:{bornIn:"Cardston, Alberta, Canada", imdbId:"0942039", born:date('1907-09-15'), name:"Fay Wray", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nFay Wray (born Vina Fay Wray; September 15, 1907 – August 8, 2004) was a Canadian-American actress.  Through an acting career that spanned 57 years, Wray attained international stardom as an actress in horror film roles, leading to many considering her as the first \"scream queen\". \n\nAfter appearing in minor film roles, Wray gained media attention being selected as one of the \"WAMPAS Baby Stars\"...", died:date('2004-08-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dfpwqfEulBX06hOrX56fLhGSWAz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3242"}}, {tmdbId:"3243", properties:{bornIn:"Saginaw, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0035877", born:date('1890-11-20'), name:"Robert Armstrong", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRobert Armstrong (November 20, 1890 – April 20, 1973) was an American film actor best remembered for his role as Carl Denham in the 1933 version of King Kong by RKO Pictures.  He uttered the famous exit quote, \"'Twas beauty killed the beast,\" at the film's end.  Months later, he starred as Carl Denham again in the sequel, Son of Kong, released the same year...", died:date('1973-04-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/s0wEwEJwkuPVLYeHC8CyXkUDrHy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3243"}}, {tmdbId:"3244", properties:{bornIn:"Carlsbad, New Mexico, U.S.", imdbId:"0127677", born:date('1904-04-20'), name:"Bruce Cabot", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Bruce Cabot (April 20, 1904 – May 3, 1972) was an American film actor.  Tall and athletic looking, he is best remembered as Jack Driscoll in King Kong (1933).  He is also well known for his roles in films such as the original Last of the Mohicans, Fritz Lang's Fury and the classic western Dodge City. \n\nThe character of \"Bruce Baxter\" in the 2005 remake of King Kong was based on Cabot...", died:date('1972-05-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nmeSnJ57IqExS4PRNmidJUXEwXy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3244"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"3245", properties:{bornIn:"München, Germany", imdbId:"0717046", born:date('1875-12-02'), name:"Frank Reicher", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nFrank Reicher (December 2, 1875 – January 19, 1965) was a German-born American stage and film actor, director and producer.  He is best known for playing Captain Englehorn in the 1933 film King Kong. \n\nReicher made his Broadway debut the year he came to America playing Lord Tarquin in Harrison Fiske's production of Becky Sharp, a comedy by Langdon Mitchell based on William Makepeace Thackeray’s Vanity Fair...", died:date('1965-01-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7Zg7zOlqe0m1TwijInbLEhE9BNI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3245"}}, {tmdbId:"6598", properties:{bornIn:"Hartford, Connecticut, USA", imdbId:"0000031", born:date('1907-05-12'), name:"Katharine Hepburn", bio:"Katharine Houghton Hepburn (May 12, 1907 – June 29, 2003) was an American actress of film, stage, and television.  Raised in Connecticut by wealthy parents, Hepburn turned to acting after graduation.  Favorable reviews of her work on stage in 1932 brought her to the notice of Hollywood.  After a few early film successes, including her first Academy Award, for Morning Glory, Hepburn endured a string of flops, which led to her being voted \"box office poison\"...", died:date('2003-06-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hzBSOe6bburyMeeCqD9kR9tRfdD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6598"}}, {tmdbId:"7639", properties:{bornIn:"Palisades, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0000910", born:date('1910-02-27'), name:"Joan Bennett", bio:"Joan Geraldine Bennett (February 27, 1910 – December 7, 1990) was an American stage, film and television actress.  Besides acting on the stage, Bennett appeared in more than 70 motion pictures from the era of silent movies well into the sound era.  She is possibly best-remembered for her film noir femme fatale roles in director Fritz Lang's movies such as The Woman in the Window (1944) and Scarlet Street (1945)...", died:date('1990-12-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sHsRIRoLqv8IhpKXu3xJaaJA92J.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7639"}}, {tmdbId:"2092", properties:{bornIn:"Budapest, Austria-Hungary [now Hungary]", imdbId:"0510134", born:date('1894-05-26'), name:"Paul Lukas", bio:"Paul Lukas (originally named Pál Lukács) was a Hungarian born stage, screen, radio, and television actor, in Hollywood from 1927...", died:date('1971-08-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uPN8hpMtacoFylb0Ez9j800bilZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2092"}}, {tmdbId:"82412", properties:{bornIn:"Malden, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0646829", born:date('1883-11-09'), name:"Edna May Oliver", bio:"​ She was born Edna May Nutter, a child of solid New England stock, on 9th November 1883 in Malden, Massachusetts.  The daughter of Ida May and Charles Edward Nutter, Edna was a descendant of the 6th American president John Quincy Adams.  Miss Oliver took an early interest in the stage, and she would quit school at the age of 14 to pursue her ambitions in the theater. \n\nDespite abandoning traditional schooling, Edna continued to study the performing arts, including speech and piano...", died:date('1942-11-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/acKhlaTO3FSxmn4DdWn2BF3lnCp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82412"}}, {tmdbId:"3609", properties:{bornIn:"Withington, Manchester, England, UK", imdbId:"0232196", born:date('1905-03-18'), name:"Robert Donat", bio:"Robert Donat (born Friedrich Robert Donat) was a star English film and stage actor.  He is best remembered for his roles in The 39 Steps (1935) and Goodbye, Mr.  Chips (1939), the latter which earned him a Best Actor Academy Award...", died:date('1958-06-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ayjbCULHaEEUdBLHeJmMX66wiJx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3609"}}, {tmdbId:"47677", properties:{bornIn:"Liverpool, England, UK", imdbId:"0245579", born:date('1874-02-03'), name:"Franklin Dyall", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nFranklin Dyall (3 February 1874, Liverpool – 8 May 1950, Worthing, Sussex) was an English actor. \n\nHe appeared in 26 films between 1916 and 1948.  He was the father of actor Valentine Dyall. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Franklin Dyall, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1950-05-08'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/47677"}}, {tmdbId:"19329", properties:{bornIn:"Wolverhampton, England", imdbId:"0541766", born:date('1888-05-14'), name:"Miles Mander", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nMiles Mander (May 14, 1888 – February 8, 1946), born Lionel Henry Mander (and sometimes credited as Luther Miles), was a well-known and versatile English character actor of the early Hollywood cinema, also a film director and producer, and a playwright and novelist. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Miles Mander,  licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1946-02-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/i3BY2sLJZ964AJgiw83gZYLyGjt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19329"}}, {tmdbId:"98045", properties:{bornIn:"Logan, Utah, USA", imdbId:"0318105", born:date('1897-07-10'), name:"John Gilbert", bio:"American actor John Gilbert (born John Cecil Pringle) was one of the biggest stars of the Silent films era.  His career subsequently significantly waned during the first years of the sound era...", died:date('1936-01-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xq2XDFsg4yzRiwix9Hk3Z2fymcl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/98045"}}, {tmdbId:"84230", properties:{bornIn:"Boston, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0445246", born:date('1899-02-27'), name:"Ian Keith", bio:"Ian Keith (born Keith Macaulay Ross) was an American stage, screen, and television actor...", died:date('1960-03-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zzHfJYGhhsTeN2OoLgXolvJPRyh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/84230"}}, {tmdbId:"89107", properties:{bornIn:"Fordstown Crossroads, County Meath, Ireland", imdbId:"0601698", born:date('1886-12-12'), name:"Owen Moore", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nOwen Moore (December 12, 1886 - June 9, 1939) was an actor in American films, appearing in more than 279 movies spanning from 1908 to 1937...", died:date('1939-06-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9Oe7l13NoYrdgM5nZcWiK6pHW7L.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89107"}}, {tmdbId:"29273", properties:{bornIn:"Juarez, Chihuahua, Mexico", imdbId:"0738042", born:date('1905-12-11'), name:"Gilbert Roland", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGilbert Roland (born Luis Antonio Dámaso de Alonso, December 11, 1905 – May 15, 1994) was a Mexican-born American film and television actor whose career spanned seven decades from the 1920s until the 1980s.  He was twice nominated for the Golden Globe Award in 1952 and 1964, and inducted into the Hollywood Walk of Fame in 1960. \n\nRoland was born in Ciudad Juárez, Chihuahua, Mexico...", died:date('1994-05-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lKqHWWnAhRXncCzGaR97YVXRBgq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29273"}}, {tmdbId:"33776", properties:{bornIn:"Wappingers Falls, New York, USA", imdbId:"0611804", born:date('1887-10-07'), name:"Jack Mulhall", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJack Mulhall, born John Joseph Francis Mulhall, (October 7, 1887 in Wappingers Falls, New York – June 1, 1979 in Woodland Hills, Los Angeles, California) was a movie actor since the silent film era and appeared in over 430 films.  Reputedly, he was one of a number of male models(Fredric March &amp; Reed Howes were two others) for the Arrow Collar Man in the Arrow collar ads illustrated by J.  C.  Leyendecker for the Cluett Peabody shirt company...", died:date('1979-06-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eCvm0iQ5al56zCtfK762fMWZ2s2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33776"}}, {tmdbId:"90333", properties:{bornIn:"Red Oak, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0369058", born:date('1887-07-07'), name:"Raymond Hatton", died:date('1971-10-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qahw4i1eLSgKOjdU5LM89m6QF0J.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/90333"}}, {tmdbId:"149017", properties:{bornIn:"Warroad, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0856077", born:date('1910-03-05'), name:"Sheila Terry", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nSheila Terry (March 5, 1910 – January 19, 1957) was an American film actress.  She was born Kay Clark in Warroad, Minnesota.   Terry first studied dramatics at Dickson-Kenwin academy, a school affiliated with London's Royal Academy.  Later she moved to New York, where she continued her studies and appeared in a number of plays...", died:date('1957-01-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/Nstq8erLO3ozLS3sAuhzoAvQBp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/149017"}}, {tmdbId:"149018", properties:{bornIn:" Seattle, Washington, USA", imdbId:"0419880", born:date('1926-03-25'), name:"Shirley Jean Rickert", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nShirley Jean Rickert (March 25, 1926 – February 6, 2009) was an American child actress who was briefly the \"blonde girl\" for the Our Gang series in 1931, during the Hal Roach talkie period.   At 18 months of age, Rickert won a local baby beauty contest, which emboldened her mother to move the family to Hollywood.  She made her screen debut at the age of four in the short How's My Baby (1930), soon followed by her Our Gang debut, Helping Grandma in 1931...", died:date('2009-02-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gjf9W4RlYa4mToxYt3gOEKE1OLi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/149018"}}, {tmdbId:"88655", properties:{imdbId:"0734340", born:date('1890-10-06'), name:"Jack Rockwell", died:date('1947-11-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/m1srtIUdzZyFUkLBqBGHo4MGxrM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88655"}}, {tmdbId:"12748", properties:{bornIn:"Geneva, Switzerland", imdbId:"0800302", born:date('1895-04-09'), name:"Michel Simon", bio:"Michel Simon (9 April 1895, Geneva, Switzerland – 30 May 1975, Bry-sur-Marne, France), was a Swiss actor.  The actor François Simon is his son. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Michel Simon, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1975-05-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pXrTn4i457RxXJ85djxF7KCmUfu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12748"}}, {tmdbId:"11545", properties:{bornIn:"Stettin, Pomerania, Germany [now Szczecin, Zachodniopomorskie, Poland]", imdbId:"0663077", born:date('1908-09-04'), name:"Dita Parlo", bio:"Dita Parlo, born either Grethe Gerda Kornstädt or Gerda Olga Justine Kornstädt, was a German film actress...", died:date('1971-12-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xB7jUhS8EWFlhtbx2OBmWT5jeY9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11545"}}, {tmdbId:"11550", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0202120", born:date('1904-08-18'), name:"Jean Dasté", died:date('1994-10-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hNas1gkLtQS7ZRTXXEvPIatUM7H.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11550"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"142918", properties:{imdbId:"0546621", name:"Gilles Margaritis", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iFmjjsy3RcKAcmHEpXjKBXky9pU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/142918"}}, {tmdbId:"94333", properties:{imdbId:"0439852", name:"Virginia Karns", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94333"}}, {tmdbId:"94105", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0377766", born:date('1914-03-03'), name:"Charlotte Henry", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nCharlotte Henry (March 3, 1914 – April 11, 1980) was an American actress, who starred in the Frank Buck serial Jungle Menace...", died:date('1980-04-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kTKiREs37qd8GUlNI4Koiupwy6W.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94105"}}, {tmdbId:"94331", properties:{imdbId:"0460901", name:"Felix Knight", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94331"}}, {tmdbId:"94332", properties:{imdbId:"0731095", born:date('1861-03-16'), name:"Florence Roberts", died:date('1940-06-06'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94332"}}, {tmdbId:"131618", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0007223", born:date('1901-11-02'), name:"James Dunn", bio:"James Dunn worked on the stage, in vaudeville and as an extra in silent movies before he was signed by Fox in 1931.  His first movie with Fox was 1931's Sob Sister (1931).  While at Fox, he appeared with Shirley Temple in her first three features: Baby Take a Bow (1934), Stand Up and Cheer! (1934) and Bright Eyes (1934).  Dunn's screen character was usually the boy next door or the nice guy...", died:date('1967-09-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6hYThYlAxY9w0CHnluxl16gEwwo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/131618"}}, {tmdbId:"14965", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0872456", born:date('1910-03-08'), name:"Claire Trevor", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nClaire Trevor (March 8, 1910 – April 8, 2000) was an Academy Award-winning American actress.  She was nicknamed the \"Queen of Film Noir\" because of her many appearances in \"bad girl” roles in film noir and other black-and-white thrillers.  She appeared in over 60 films. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Claire Trevor, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2000-04-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9XHXzn7NM3GnYwZn6YsmjbsSqIF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14965"}}, {tmdbId:"34348", properties:{bornIn:"St. Paul, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0003062", born:date('1889-10-03'), name:"Alan Dinehart", died:date('1944-07-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fpUvPuJP4PbT8zcxGxuVCDN1f8J.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34348"}}, {tmdbId:"82349", properties:{bornIn:" Denver, Colorado, USA", imdbId:"0084098", born:date('1914-08-30'), name:"Julie Bishop", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nJulie Bishop (August 30, 1914 – August 30, 2001) was an American film and television actress.  She appeared in over 80 films between 1923 and 1957. \n\nBishop was born Jacqueline Wells and used her birth name professionally through 1941.  She also appeared on stage (and in one film) as Diane Duval.  She was a child actress, beginning her career in 1923...", died:date('2001-08-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2IbSP5DeNv8GOKG5niBFworYCeu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82349"}}, {tmdbId:"8515", properties:{bornIn:"Palmyra, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0002034", born:date('1879-10-15'), name:"Jane Darwell", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJane Darwell (October 15, 1879 – August 13, 1967) was an American film and stage actress.  With appearances in over 100 major motion pictures, Darwell is perhaps best-remembered for her portrayal of the matriarch and leader of the Joad family in the film adaptation of The Grapes of Wrath, for which she received the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress, and her role as the Bird Woman in Mary Poppins...", died:date('1967-08-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xWTsj5z2N94OOnimMmUYewQXOIi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8515"}}, {tmdbId:"143670", properties:{imdbId:"0020703", born:date('1911-02-08'), name:"Judith Allen", died:date('1996-10-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/asYURcGcgsVcN0HpFaBj1BrIWZ9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/143670"}}, {tmdbId:"30181", properties:{bornIn:"Omaha, Nebraska, USA", imdbId:"0000001", born:date('1899-05-10'), name:"Fred Astaire", bio:"Fred Astaire (May 10, 1899 – June 22, 1987) was an American dancer, singer, actor and choreographer.  He is widely regarded as the most influential dancer in the history of film.  Born as Frederick Austerlitz in Omaha, Nebraska, on May 10, 1899, to Johanna (Geilus) and Fritz, a brewer, he entered show business at age 5.  He was successful in vaudeville and on Broadway as well as in London's West End together with his sister Adele, a partnership that lasted 27 years...", died:date('1987-06-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zdYM70m1EhhHaOJaN6TmrZDExoS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30181"}}, {tmdbId:"30003", properties:{bornIn:"Independence, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0001677", born:date('1911-07-16'), name:"Ginger Rogers", bio:"Ginger Rogers (July 16, 1911 – April 25, 1995) was an American actress, dancer, and singer who appeared in film, and on stage, radio, and television throughout much of the twentieth century. \n\nDuring her long career, she made a total of 73 films and is noted for her role as Fred Astaire's partner in a series of ten musical films.  She achieved great success in a variety of film roles and won the Academy Award for Best Actress for her performance in Kitty Foyle...", died:date('1995-04-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ah4nyaNUOMZwmGbDOAtN8S8J6ap.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30003"}}, {tmdbId:"125841", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0103567", born:date('1892-11-02'), name:"Alice Brady", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAlice Brady (November 2, 1892 – October 28, 1939) was an American actress who began her career in the silent film era and survived the transition into talkies.  She worked up until six months before her death from cancer in 1939.  Her films include My Man Godfrey (1936), in which she played the flighty mother of Carole Lombard's character, and In Old Chicago (1938) for which she won the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress...", died:date('1939-10-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pp6XGg2Xeik10oiGXq4rn8UKmb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/125841"}}, {tmdbId:"2437", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0002143", born:date('1886-03-18'), name:"Edward Everett Horton", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nEdward Everett Horton Jr.  (March 18, 1886 – September 29, 1970) was an American character actor.  He had a long career in film, theater, radio, television, and voice work for animated cartoons.   Horton began his stage career in 1906, singing and dancing and playing small parts in vaudeville and in Broadway productions.  In 1919, he moved to Los Angeles, California, where he began acting in Hollywood films...", died:date('1970-09-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/t6G79n8HHlMyKYygro3RWisMxlC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2437"}}, {tmdbId:"30155", properties:{bornIn:"Saint-Mandé, Val-de-Marne, France", imdbId:"0001055", born:date('1903-09-13'), name:"Claudette Colbert", bio:"Claudette Colbert was born in Saint-Mandé, Val-de-Marne, France on September 13, 1903 and was brought to the United States as a child three years later.  Born Emilie 'Lily' Claudette Chauchoin, she went to high school in New York.  She was studying at the Art Students League when, in 1923, she took the name Claudette Colbert for her first Broadway role in \"The Wild Westcotts\".  Her most noteworthy stage vehicle was the \"The Barker\" in 1927...", died:date('1996-07-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lgiSXDYAe7Oo4bIRx71G1RIZdT0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30155"}}, {tmdbId:"30156", properties:{bornIn:"Cincinnati, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0175369", born:date('1887-04-08'), name:"Walter Connolly", bio:"The name may have been forgotten, especially today (seven decades later), but the portly, apoplectic, exasperated figure on the 1930s screen wasn't.  While his film career, save a couple of silents, lasted a paltry seven years (1932-1939), character actor Walter Connolly certainly ran the distance.  While some film historians complain that a number of his performances were annoying or overbaked, he was for the most part applauded for his zesty contributions to a number of comedy classics...", died:date('1940-05-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1C2pNVYcULNgoG8wCWMtr4WrXMp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30156"}}, {tmdbId:"30157", properties:{bornIn:"San Bernardino, California, USA", imdbId:"0439850", born:date('1891-09-07'), name:"Roscoe Karns", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRoscoe Karns (September 7, 1891 – February 6, 1970) was an American actor who appeared in nearly 150 films between 1915 and 1964.  He specialized in cynical, wise-cracking (and often tipsy) characters, and his rapid-fire delivery enlivened many comedies and crime thrillers in the 1930s and 1940s.   Though he appeared in numerous silent films, such as Wings and Beggars of Life, his career didn't really take off until sound arrived...", died:date('1970-02-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uglIhGytbfyGhppGxn1ed1wQpw0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30157"}}, {tmdbId:"20502", properties:{bornIn:"West Derby, Liverpool, England, UK", imdbId:"0052203", born:date('1890-06-09'), name:"Leslie Banks", bio:"Leslie Banks, CBE (9 June 1890 – 21 April 1952) was an English theatre and cinema actor, director and producer, now best remembered playing gruff, menacing characters in black and white movies of the 1930s and 1940s. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Leslie Banks, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1952-04-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ydC9247DfVfbem0IjZtZLtDgRq6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20502"}}, {tmdbId:"88569", properties:{bornIn:"Hove, East Sussex, England, UK", imdbId:"0078923", born:date('1900-03-03'), name:"Edna Best", died:date('1974-09-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5fFLQFt7uISZIsxIIjAQZ5KBSTN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88569"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"54036", properties:{bornIn:"Hampstead, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0903687", born:date('1899-12-15'), name:"Frank Vosper", died:date('1937-03-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/z7kf7Bcvo3oJtmT9RF0fhc9GxOX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54036"}}, {tmdbId:"104728", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0263004", born:date('1909-07-01'), name:"Madge Evans", bio:"Lovely Madge Evans was the perennial nice girl in films of the 1930's.   By then, she had been in front of the camera for many years, starting  with Fairy Soap commercials at the age of two (she sat on a bar of soap  holding a bunch of violets with the tag line reading \"have you a little  fairy in your home?\").  'Baby Madge' also lent her name to a children's  hat company...", died:date('1981-04-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fmZdMlyCRANCaEShFvAF2mt5W2J.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/104728"}}, {tmdbId:"1465942", properties:{imdbId:"0296436", name:"Sylvia Froos", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qGX7sH1ycqHWxJSZiBvQrgQY2Y.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1465942"}}, {tmdbId:"41516", properties:{bornIn:"Boyle, County Roscommon, Ireland", imdbId:"0001577", born:date('1911-05-17'), name:"Maureen O'Sullivan", bio:"Maureen Paula O'Sullivan was born in County Roscommon, Ireland, on May 17, 1911.  The future mother of Mia Farrow was a schooldays classmate of Vivien Leigh at the Convent of the Sacred Heart at Roehampton in London.  Even as a schoolgirl, Maureen desired an acting career; she studied hard and read widely.  When the opportunity to be an actress came along, it almost dropped in her lap.  The director Frank Borzage was in Dublin filming “Song o’ My Heart” (1930) when Maureen, then 18, met him...", died:date('1998-06-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zWovLel1yHMSpWpoAUbfhs7uw9j.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41516"}}, {tmdbId:"96064", properties:{bornIn:"Chislehurst, Kent [now in Bromley, London], England, UK", imdbId:"0146905", born:date('1888-12-08'), name:"Paul Cavanagh", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nPaul Cavanagh (8 December 1888 – 15 March 1964) was an English film actor.  He appeared in more than 100 films between 1928 and 1959. \n\nCavanagh was born in Chislehurst, Kent, and attended the Royal Grammar School, Newcastle upon Tyne, and Emmanuel College, Cambridge.  Cavanagh studied law in England, earning a master of arts degree at Cambridge...", died:date('1964-03-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/opbXZoEJjKVA2xKrd7fDQyMqhq9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96064"}}, {tmdbId:"3371", properties:{bornIn:"County Cork, Ireland", imdbId:"0367516", born:date('1884-06-27'), name:"Forrester Harvey", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nForrester Harvey (27 June 1884 – 14 December 1945) was an Irish film actor. \n\nFrom 1922 until his death year Harvey appeared in more than 115 films.  He was credited for about two-thirds of his film appearances, but some of his roles were uncredited.  The burly actor with a mustache mostly played comic supporting roles, often as an innkeeper.  His best-known role was Beamish in the first two Tarzan films starring Johnny Weissmuller...", died:date('1945-12-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7HOryiAAEFef1JPD7FpGlaSDCn5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3371"}}, {tmdbId:"32428", properties:{bornIn:"Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0001635", born:date('1892-07-28'), name:"William Powell", bio:"William Horatio Powell (July 29, 1892 – March 5, 1984) was an American actor.  A major star at Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer, he was paired with Myrna Loy in 14 films, including the Thin Man series based on the Nick and Nora Charles characters created by Dashiell Hammett.  Powell was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Actor three times: for The Thin Man (1934), My Man Godfrey (1936), and Life with Father (1947)...", died:date('1984-03-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/p9RKEHo2m3VPoYPejwFkI7PwqZY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32428"}}, {tmdbId:"13577", properties:{bornIn:"Radersburg, Montana, USA", imdbId:"0001485", born:date('1905-08-02'), name:"Myrna Loy", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMyrna Loy (August 2, 1905 – December 14, 1993) was an American actress.  Trained as a dancer, she devoted herself fully to an acting career following a few minor roles in silent films.  Originally typecast in exotic roles, often as a vamp or a woman of Asian descent, her career prospects improved following her portrayal of Nora Charles in The Thin Man (1934)...", died:date('1993-12-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xbNyKENYwyx6u4OR087SbEkmOo9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13577"}}, {tmdbId:"32430", properties:{bornIn:"Davenport, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0671738", born:date('1895-08-09'), name:"Nat Pendleton", bio:"Nathaniel Greene 'Nat' Pendleton was an American former Olympic wrestler turned actor. \n\nTwo-time Eastern Intercollegiate Wrestling Association (EIWA) champion (1914-1915) in the 175-lb.  class at Columbia University, Pendleton graduated Class of 1916.  He wrestled for the United States at the 1920 Olympic Games in Antwerp, Belgium, earning a silver medal, losing only one match due to a controversial point decision...", died:date('1967-10-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jnNinNqn2FfdulCzk5ycnBFDWUm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32430"}}, {tmdbId:"10279", properties:{bornIn:"Braunau am Inn, Austria", imdbId:"0386944", born:date('1889-04-20'), name:"Adolf Hitler", bio:"Adolf Hitler (20 April 1889 – 30 April 1945) was an Austrian-born German politician and the leader of the National Socialist German Workers Party (German: Nationalsozialistische Deutsche Arbeiterpartei, abbreviated NSDAP), commonly known as the Nazi Party.  He was Chancellor of Germany from 1933 to 1945, and served as head of state as Führer und Reichskanzler from 1934 to 1945...", died:date('1945-04-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8nLLFbGFjwbvcBXFRczD9sSJCoU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10279"}}, {tmdbId:"1090805", properties:{imdbId:"0023907", name:"Max Amann", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1090805"}}, {tmdbId:"1090806", properties:{bornIn:"Halberstadt-Germany", imdbId:"0097006", born:date('1900-06-17'), name:"Martin Bormann", died:date('1945-05-02'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1090806"}}, {tmdbId:"2491", properties:{bornIn:"Fort Wayne, Indiana, USA", imdbId:"0001479", born:date('1908-10-06'), name:"Carole Lombard", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nCarole Lombard (born Jane Alice Peters, October 6, 1908 – January 16, 1942) was an American film actress.  She was particularly noted for her energetic, often off-beat roles in the screwball comedies of the 1930s.  She was the highest-paid star in Hollywood in the late 1930s.  She was the third wife of actor Clark Gable. \n\nLombard was born into a wealthy family in Fort Wayne, Indiana, but was raised in Los Angeles by her single mother...", died:date('1942-01-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7crNXh8KXwIYhEFHf0KtkOneCmj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2491"}}, {tmdbId:"3610", properties:{bornIn:"West Bromwich, West Midlands, England, UK", imdbId:"0140914", born:date('1906-02-26'), name:"Madeleine Carroll", bio:"Edith Madeleine Carroll (26 February 1906 - 2 October 1987) was an English actress, popular both in Britain and America in the 1930s and 1940s.  At the peak of her success she was the highest-paid actress in the world, earning a then staggering $250,000 in 1938.  Carroll is remembered for her role in Alfred Hitchcock's The 39 Steps...", died:date('1987-10-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/toL1pA9nWiH8IhZ2Ywyk8trIePB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3610"}}, {tmdbId:"3611", properties:{bornIn:"Berlin, Germany", imdbId:"0543169", born:date('1899-04-30'), name:"Lucie Mannheim", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Lucie Mannheim (30 April 1899 – 28 July 1976) was a German singer and actress. \n\nMannheim was born in Berlin–Köpenick where she studied drama and quickly became a popular figure appearing on stage in plays and musicals.  Among other roles, she played Nora in Ibsen's A Doll's House, Marie in Büchner's Woyzeck, and Juliet in Shakespeare's Romeo and Juliet...", died:date('1976-07-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zhyrXGO5h2KcS9cUs8PDAyvkvtK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3611"}}, {tmdbId:"3612", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0853607", born:date('1884-10-12'), name:"Godfrey Tearle", bio:"Sir Godfrey Tearle was an American-born actor who portrayed the quintessential Englishman on stage and in films in both England and the United States...", died:date('1953-06-08'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3612"}}, {tmdbId:"2924", properties:{bornIn:"Larne, Northern Ireland", imdbId:"0387753", born:date('1917-04-14'), name:"Valerie Hobson", bio:"Valerie Hobson (14 April 1917 – 13 November 1998) was a British actress who appeared in a number of British films during the 1940s and 1950s.  She was born Babette Valerie Louise Hobson in Larne, County Antrim, Ireland. \n\nShe appeared as Baroness Frankenstein in Bride of Frankenstein (1935) with Boris Karloff and Colin Clive, taking over the role from Mae Clarke, who had played it in the original Frankenstein (1931)...", died:date('1998-11-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1sfD32ahPZwDIcWUIlx4tFG8fnr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2924"}}, {tmdbId:"2925", properties:{bornIn:"Chelsea, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0857658", born:date('1879-01-15'), name:"Ernest Thesiger", bio:"Ernest Thesiger, CBE, was an English stage and screen actor.  He is best known for his distinctive performance as Dr.  Septimus Pretorius in James Whale's 1935 film The Bride of Frankenstein...", died:date('1961-01-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ueiMQiDkGGDCq0nDkdxu27HaM1B.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2925"}}, {tmdbId:"8724", properties:{bornIn:"Hobart, Tasmania, Australia", imdbId:"0001224", born:date('1909-06-20'), name:"Errol Flynn", bio:"Errol Leslie Thomson Flynn (June 20, 1909 - October 14, 1959) was an Australian-American actor and writer.  He is popularly remembered as a charismatic romantic hero in the eight films he starred in with Olivia de Havilland.  With Flynn and de Havilland's on-screen chemistry, they're widely regarded as one of Classic Hollywood’s greatest partnerships.  Flynn’s most iconic role came as Robin Hood in \"The Adventures of Robin Hood\" (1938). \n\nAfter signing with Warner Bros...", died:date('1959-10-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uh4gFoEKJpMAq4JQTwVzpVVl455.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8724"}}, {tmdbId:"8725", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0000014", born:date('1916-07-01'), name:"Olivia de Havilland", bio:"Dame Olivia Mary de Havilland DBE (July 1, 1916 - July 25, 2020) was a British-American actress, whose career spanned from 1935 to 1988.  She appeared in 49 feature films, and was one of the leading movie stars during the golden age of Classical Hollywood.  She is best known for her early screen performances in The Adventures of Robin Hood (1938) and Gone with the Wind (1939), and her later award-winning performances in To Each His Own (1946), The Snake Pit (1948), and The Heiress (1949)...", died:date('2020-07-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9xlzpDzb1dhj3z0ODMz0ig6PUQf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8725"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"2495", properties:{bornIn:"Croydon, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0041172", born:date('1885-03-01'), name:"Lionel Atwill", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLionel Atwill (1 March 1885 – 22 April 1946) was an English stage and film actor born in Croydon, London, England. \n\nHe studied architecture before his stage debut at the Garrick Theatre, London in 1904.  He become a star in Broadway theatre by 1918, and made his screen debut in 1919.  He acted on the stage in Australia but was most famous for his U. S.  horror roles in the 1930s...", died:date('1946-04-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nsUWekQKPpINTNSu4AEHprsFf4z.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2495"}}, {tmdbId:"8727", properties:{bornIn:"Johannesburg, South African Republic", imdbId:"0001651", born:date('1892-06-13'), name:"Basil Rathbone", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSir Basil Rathbone, KBE, MC, Kt (13 June 1892, Johannesburg – 21 July 1967, New York City) was a South African actor.  He rose to prominence in England as a Shakespearean stage actor and went on to appear in over 70 films, primarily costume dramas, swashbucklers, and, occasionally, horror films...", died:date('1967-07-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vHdw4YuybYJqISjZoLQtC2Hm3L0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8727"}}, {tmdbId:"2777", properties:{bornIn:"Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, USA", imdbId:"0399955", born:date('1916-03-06'), name:"Rochelle Hudson", bio:"Rochelle Hudson (March 6, 1916 — January 17, 1972) was an American film actress from the 1930s through the 1960s.  Hudson was a WAMPAS Baby Star in 1931. \n\nThe Oklahoma City-born actress began her career as a teenager.  She signed a contract with RKO Pictures on November 22, 1930, when she was 17 years old...", died:date('1972-01-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vZ97bWPZ2npdLDTJmLsblfxSCos.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2777"}}, {tmdbId:"93910", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0392442", born:date('1888-05-31'), name:"Jack Holt", bio:"Jack Holt (born Charles John Holt, Jr. ) was an American film actor.  He was a leading man of Silent and sound films and known for his many roles in Westerns...", died:date('1951-01-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pMEdSfiMTUwHNjBUMIthslka7YD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/93910"}}, {tmdbId:"72059", properties:{bornIn:"Niagara Falls, New York, USA", imdbId:"0867144", born:date('1905-02-27'), name:"Franchot Tone", bio:"Franchot Tone (February 27, 1905 – September 18, 1968) was an American stage, film, and television actor, star of Mutiny on the Bounty (1935) and many other films through the 1960s.  In the early 1960s Tone appeared in character roles on TV dramas like Bonanza, Wagon Train, The Twilight Zone, and The Alfred Hitchcock Hour...", died:date('1968-09-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5B8lpIuX1huJOGkaF2m3XdJ5Krt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/72059"}}, {tmdbId:"72060", properties:{bornIn:"St Helens, Lancashire, UK", imdbId:"0612743", born:date('1898-08-21'), name:"Herbert Mundin", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nHerbert Mundin (21 August 1898 – 5 March 1939) was an English-born Hollywood character actor.  He was frequently typecast in films as an older cheeky eccentric, a type helped by his jowled features and cheerful disposition. \n\nHe was born Herbert Thomas Mundin in St Helens, then in Lancashire (now part of Merseyside).  His father was a nomadic, Primitive Methodist home missionary...", died:date('1939-03-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7OGFOd1Kfc8XyGhd4BhRvhgrl9z.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/72060"}}, {tmdbId:"121019", properties:{bornIn:"New Orleans, Louisiana, USA", imdbId:"0137634", born:date('1910-09-03'), name:"Kitty Carlisle", bio:"Kitty Carlisle (September 3, 1910 – April 17, 2007) was an American singer, actress and spokeswoman for the arts.  She is best remembered as a regular panelist on the television game show To Tell the Truth.  She served 20 years on the New York State Council on the Arts.  In 1991, she received the National Medal of Arts from President George H.  W.  Bush...", died:date('2007-04-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wlcASy2DWuLo88ZNDo27ZWwuM8V.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/121019"}}, {tmdbId:"1170215", properties:{imdbId:"0024743", name:"Rosemary Ames", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2hkXHUgvBxKVxieD3T2RQqYpXaY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1170215"}}, {tmdbId:"20501", properties:{bornIn:"South Pasadena, California, USA", imdbId:"0566948", born:date('1905-11-05'), name:"Joel McCrea", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJoel Albert McCrea (November 5, 1905 – October 20, 1990) was an American actor whose career spanned almost five decades and appearances in more than 90 films...", died:date('1990-10-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/d2Txihsl4A1V1Cozmj2kBAd8Odn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20501"}}, {tmdbId:"34119", properties:{bornIn:"Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0847939", born:date('1902-02-08'), name:"Lyle Talbot", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLyle Talbot (born Lisle Henderson, February 8, 1902 – March 2, 1996) was an American actor on stage and screen, known for his career in film from 1931 to 1960 and for his appearances on television in the 1950s and 1960s.  He played Ozzie Nelson's friend and neighbor, Joe Randolph, for ten years in the ABC situation comedy The Adventures of Ozzie and Harriet.  He began his movie career under contract with Warner Brothers in the early days of sound film...", died:date('1996-03-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nIXEoog89UHwHY1s5Fq7VLLK8b3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34119"}}, {tmdbId:"32923", properties:{bornIn:"King's Norton, Worcestershire, England, UK", imdbId:"0000731", born:date('1902-05-02'), name:"Brian Aherne", bio:"English born Brian Aherne (born William Brian de Lacy Aherne) was a stage, screen, and television actor successful in America...", died:date('1986-02-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/23soV7PVvFVrEm6TLm7bH4nrM6s.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32923"}}, {tmdbId:"22600", properties:{bornIn:"Wandsworth, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0350324", born:date('1877-09-26'), name:"Edmund Gwenn", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nEdmund Gwenn (born Edmund John Kellaway, 26 September 1877– 6 September 1959) was an English actor.  On film, he is perhaps best remembered for his role as Kris Kringle in the Christmas film Miracle on 34th Street (1947), for which he won the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor and the corresponding Golden Globe Award.  He received a second Golden Globe and another Academy Award nomination for the comedy film Mister 880 (1950)...", died:date('1959-09-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9xUiHCycn0WsxqiqFjq2fI40FpQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/22600"}}, {tmdbId:"30183", properties:{bornIn:"El Reno, Oklahoma Territory, USA", imdbId:"0722424", born:date('1906-02-10'), name:"Erik Rhodes", bio:"Erik Rhodes (born Ernest Sharpe; February 10, 1906 - February 17, 1990) was an American stage, film, and television actor best remembered for his comedic performances as delightful hyperactive Italian gentlemen in the classic Fred Astaire and Ginger Rogers Hollywood musicals The Gay Divorcee (1934) and Top Hat (1935).  With a good baritone voice, he was successful, both prior to and subsequent his film career, in Broadway musicals...", died:date('1990-02-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2k5KPCobo7LgqToW8EGbLSJfrRF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30183"}}, {tmdbId:"854", properties:{bornIn:"Indiana, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0000071", born:date('1908-05-20'), name:"James Stewart", bio:"James Maitland \"Jimmy\" Stewart was an American film and stage actor, known for his distinctive voice and his everyman persona.  Over the course of his career, he starred in many films widely considered classics and was nominated for five Academy Awards, winning one in competition and receiving one Lifetime Achievement award.  He was a major MGM contract star...", died:date('1997-07-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aBLtt0Sl4AZVNclzFrXzbndRzux.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/854"}}, {tmdbId:"32924", properties:{bornIn:"Venice, Italy", imdbId:"0484748", born:date('1904-12-06'), name:"Elissa Landi", bio:"Elissa Landi (December 6, 1904 – October 21, 1948) was an Italian born actress who was popular in Hollywood films of the 1920s and 1930s.  Rumoured to be a descendant of Emperor Franz Joseph of Austria, she was noted for her aristocratic bearing. \n\nBorn Elisabeth Marie Christine Kühnelt in Venice, Landi was raised in Austria and educated in England. \n\nHer first ambition was to be a writer, and she wrote her first novel at the age of twenty...", died:date('1948-10-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iiQCnsCZ2cj3RusFfZ8NkA32Li8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32924"}}, {tmdbId:"30002", properties:{bornIn:"El Paso, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0452128", born:date('1882-03-06'), name:"Guy Kibbee", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGuy Bridges Kibbee (March 6, 1882 – May 24, 1956) was an American stage and film actor. \n\nBorn in El Paso, Texas, Kibbee began his entertainment career on Mississippi riverboats and eventually became a successful Broadway actor.  In the 1930s, Kibbee moved to California and became part of what became known as \"Warner Bros. ' stock company\", contracted actors who cycled through different productions in supporting roles...", died:date('1956-05-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/imDHdLuaQC2b0kEO37JLjbtyR4h.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30002"}}, {tmdbId:"2016", properties:{bornIn:"Albuquerque, New Mexico, USA", imdbId:"0838843", born:date('1892-07-10'), name:"Slim Summerville", bio:"Slim Summerville (born George Joseph Somerville) was a comedic American screen actor who began his career during the Silent era...", died:date('1946-01-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nhQ6CUbtWjmocr2UOBME43RAcR0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2016"}}, {tmdbId:"1935", properties:{bornIn:"Belleville, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0001171", born:date('1908-04-02'), name:"Buddy Ebsen", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nChristian Ludolf \"Buddy\" Ebsen Jr.  (April 2, 1908 – July 6, 2003) was an American actor and dancer, whose career spanned seven decades, including the role of Jed Clampett in the CBS television sitcom The Beverly Hillbillies (1962–1971) and the title character in the television detective drama Barnaby Jones (1973–1980), also on CBS. [3] The SAG-AFTRA records also show him as Frank \"Buddy\" Ebsen...", died:date('2003-07-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xBscNtDuEAUld96AlFEUPKM8TG9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1935"}}, {tmdbId:"9067", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0604656", born:date('1890-06-01'), name:"Frank Morgan", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nFrank Morgan (June 1, 1890 – September 18, 1949) was an American actor.  He was best known for his portrayal of the title character in the film The Wizard of Oz...", died:date('1949-09-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vSCvrwFacSTPxxUFf94s3vTH5kA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9067"}}, {tmdbId:"26029", properties:{imdbId:"0448836", born:date('1908-12-03'), name:"Robert Kent", died:date('1955-05-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nLqggn5bX0YW1thl0EofjbUHYOx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/26029"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"108986", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0922818", born:date('1875-03-28'), name:"Helen Westley", died:date('1942-12-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7cqZn76oOLV5IbgLCHL2I36pSH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/108986"}}, {tmdbId:"19020", properties:{bornIn:"Toronto, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0404158", born:date('1883-04-05'), name:"Walter Huston", bio:"Walter Huston was a Canadian-born American actor.  He was the father of actor and director John Huston and the grandfather of actress Anjelica Huston and actor Danny Huston. \n\nBorn Walter Houghston in Toronto, Ontario to an Ulster-Scottish father and a Scottish Canadian mother, he began his Broadway career in 1924.  Once talkies began in Hollywood, he achieved fame in character roles.  His first major role was in 1929's The Virginian with Gary Cooper...", died:date('1950-04-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zbuPnuQ6v15k8Zk4LmnXMtWeAfd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19020"}}, {tmdbId:"130385", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0154183", born:date('1892-12-24'), name:"Ruth Chatterton", bio:"Ruth Chatterton (December 24, 1892 – November 24, 1961) was an American stage, film, and television actress.  She was at her most popular in the early to mid-1930s, and in the same era gained prominence as an aviator, one of the few female pilots in the United States at the time.  In the late 1930s, Chatterton retired from film acting but continued her career on the stage.  She had several TV roles beginning in the late 1940s and became a successful novelist in the 1950s...", died:date('1961-11-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/h0EDXB5ZhK2VeWvsTcrsv8sTewx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/130385"}}, {tmdbId:"1009", properties:{bornIn:"Orange County, Virginia, USA", imdbId:"0000068", born:date('1898-01-23'), name:"Randolph Scott", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRandolph Scott (January 23, 1898 – March 2, 1987) was an American film actor whose career spanned from 1928 to 1962. \n\nAs a leading man for all but the first three years of his cinematic career, Scott appeared in a variety of genres, including social dramas, crime dramas, comedies, musicals (albeit in non-singing and non-dancing roles), adventure tales, war films, and even a few horror and fantasy films...", died:date('1987-03-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qM2DNQ7kI9oZqAYfhzgKaGURCnm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1009"}}, {tmdbId:"108702", properties:{bornIn:"Des Moines, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0384948", born:date('1909-07-18'), name:"Harriet Hilliard", bio:"Harriet Nelson will always have a secure place alongside Barbara Billingsley and Jane Wyatt in the \"TV's Golden Age Mom Hall of Fame. \" For fourteen years, she, husband Ozzie Nelson, and their two boys, David Nelson and Ricky Nelson,  were the quintessential role models of the '50s ideal nuclear family.   Harriet, the daughter of actors, was practically born in a trunk.  She  made her debut amid the footlights at age 6 weeks with her parents.  The  Iowa beauty attended St...", died:date('1994-10-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oB1VglXBvN1DbkYitqa02dB8KS0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/108702"}}, {tmdbId:"528", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0796662", born:date('1910-08-09'), name:"Sylvia Sidney", bio:"Sylvia Sidney (born Sophia Kosow, August 8, 1910 – July 1, 1999) was an American stage, screen and film actress whose career spanned over 70 years.  She rose to prominence in dozens of leading roles in the 1930s.  She later gained attention for her role as Juno, a case worker in the afterlife, in Tim Burton's film Beetlejuice, for which she won a Saturn Award as Best Supporting Actress...", died:date('1999-07-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mnTIQavldzHDgPFOmL4BSDFkM8q.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/528"}}, {tmdbId:"12147", properties:{bornIn:"Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA", imdbId:"0000075", born:date('1900-04-05'), name:"Spencer Tracy", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nSpencer Bonaventure Tracy (April 5, 1900 – June 10, 1967) was an American actor, noted for his natural style and versatility.  One of the major stars of Hollywood's Golden Age, Tracy won two Academy Awards for Best Actor from nine nominations, sharing the record for nominations in that category with Laurence Olivier...", died:date('1967-06-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9HmmAYhUyQ3tG1ZqnqQwPNePZEM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12147"}}, {tmdbId:"77114", properties:{bornIn:"St. Paul, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0008496", born:date('1898-06-06'), name:"Walter Abel", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nWalter Abel (June 6, 1898 – March 26, 1987) was an American stage and film character actor.  His eyes were brown and his (adult) height was five foot ten inches. \n\nAbel was born in St.  Paul, Minnesota, the son of Christine (née Becker) and Richard Michael Abel.  Abel graduated from the American Academy of Dramatic Arts where he had studied in 1917 and joined a touring company.  He made his Broadway debut in Forbidden in 1919...", died:date('1987-03-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cTKeEvBvfHZnpkTVDLNPgbjQE8L.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77114"}}, {tmdbId:"1099453", properties:{name:"Nino Martini", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vD0AV32dNYr1JLyAsXxOImzd7om.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1099453"}}, {tmdbId:"78850", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0140504", born:date('1880-08-06'), name:"Leo Carrillo", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLeo Carrillo (August 6, 1880 – September 10, 1961) was an American actor, vaudevillian, political cartoonist, and conservationist.  He was best known for playing Pancho in the popular Western television series The Cisco Kid (1950–1956) and in several films...", died:date('1961-09-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mQKgQ8Gfry1imZLDHs9w8BUsUrL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78850"}}, {tmdbId:"32435", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0399346", born:date('1909-12-05'), name:"Harold Huber", bio:"Harold Huber (born Harold Joseph Huberman) was an American stage, screen, and television actor...", died:date('1959-09-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/46XRvEpn9ADtLp1OXXeIHMSZxHc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32435"}}, {tmdbId:"125482", properties:{bornIn:"Düsseldorf, Prussia, German Empire", imdbId:"0707023", born:date('1910-01-12'), name:"Luise Rainer", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLuise Rainer (/ˈraɪnər/; January 12, 1910 – December 30, 2014) was a German-American film actress.  She was the first actor to win more than one Academy Award; at the time of her death she was the longest-lived Oscar recipient. \n\nHer training began in Germany from the age of 16 by leading stage director Max Reinhardt.  After a few years, she became recognized as a \"distinguished Berlin stage actress\", acting with Reinhardt's Vienna theater ensemble...", died:date('2014-12-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zSAhb0OAi1IIO4QnuHCgt01STJG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/125482"}}, {tmdbId:"80567", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0000861", born:date('1924-03-28'), name:"Freddie Bartholomew", bio:"Freddie Bartholomew was an English-American child actor.   One of the most famous child actors of all time, he became very popular in 1930s Hollywood films.  His most famous starring roles are in Captains Courageous and Little Lord Fauntleroy. \n\nHe was born in London and for the title role of David Copperfield, he emigrated to the United States in 1934, living there the rest of his life.  He became an American citizen in 1943 following World War II military service...", died:date('1992-01-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1B0mx3uPr2j7gi6Cu8fIkqw0AkW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80567"}}, {tmdbId:"14515", properties:{bornIn:"Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0182537", born:date('1903-09-17'), name:"Dolores Costello", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDolores Costello (September 17, 1903 – March 1, 1979) was an American film actress who achieved her greatest success during the era of silent movies.  She was nicknamed \"The Goddess of the Silent Screen\"...", died:date('1979-03-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/e7qj9piLfzWTVpz0Z3KGY9O0r9v.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14515"}}, {tmdbId:"2438", properties:{bornIn:" London, England, UK", imdbId:"0807580", born:date('1863-07-21'), name:"C. Aubrey Smith", bio:"C.  Aubrey Smith (Sir Charles Aubrey Smith, CBE) was an English born stage and screen actor, prominent in Hollywood films starting from the beginning of the sound era...", died:date('1948-12-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bmkvivg9TJJhbc2ZxQ1xJfq0mWt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2438"}}, {tmdbId:"14027", properties:{bornIn:"Whitestone Landing, Long Island, New York, USA", imdbId:"0002104", born:date('1910-06-03'), name:"Paulette Goddard", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPaulette Goddard (June 3, 1910 – April 23, 1990) was an American film and theatre actress.  A former child fashion model and in several Broadway productions as Ziegfeld Girl, she was a major star of the Paramount Studio in the 1940s.  She was married to several notable men, including Charlie Chaplin, Burgess Meredith, and Erich Maria Remarque...", died:date('1990-04-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7fMtXuVbJMbsFB4U3CsgDdivizP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14027"}}, {tmdbId:"30194", properties:{bornIn:"Osage, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0761866", born:date('1894-02-26'), name:"Tiny Sandford", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nStanley J.  \"Tiny\" Sandford (February 26, 1894 – October 29, 1961) was a tall, burly actor who is best remembered for his roles in Laurel and Hardy and Charlie Chaplin films.  He was usually cast as a comic heavy, and often played policemen, doormen, prizefighters, or bullies. \n\nSandford was born in Osage, Iowa.  After working in stock theater he began acting in movies around 1910...", died:date('1961-10-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kTIvxCBa3Z168aIZoFKvuPIAQYb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30194"}}, {tmdbId:"30210", properties:{bornIn:"Plattsburgh, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000795", born:date('1900-10-17'), name:"Jean Arthur", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Jean Arthur (October 17, 1900 – June 19, 1991) was an American actress and a major film star of the 1930s and 1940s.  She remains arguably the epitome of the female screwball comedy actress.  As James Harvey wrote in his recounting of the era, \"No one was more closely identified with the screwball comedy than Jean Arthur...", died:date('1991-06-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jtLHDKcrm3jIpu0jjTWmi2Ls2og.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30210"}}, {tmdbId:"13555", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0051628", born:date('1882-09-30'), name:"George Bancroft", bio:"George Bancroft was an American screen actor of the 1920s and 1930s...", died:date('1956-10-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6aDCnMFJANk1NPn84Vs5ks0Qp9y.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13555"}}, {tmdbId:"4969", properties:{bornIn:"The Bronx, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0822034", born:date('1908-01-11'), name:"Lionel Stander", bio:"Lionel Stander was an American stage, screen, radio, and television actor...", died:date('1994-11-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/t2KrtknCJd5zsXWmMH089z5ePbT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4969"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"98574", properties:{bornIn:"Birmingham, Alabama, USA", imdbId:"0665850", born:date('1911-06-20'), name:"Gail Patrick", bio:"​Gail Patrick (born Margaret LaVelle Fitzpatrick, June 20, 1911 - July 6, 1980) was an American film actress. \n\nShe appeared in 62 movies between 1932 and 1948.  Some of these roles are in My Favorite Wife, Dangerous to Know, and in My Man Godfrey.  Patrick retired from acting in films in 1948 and later became a producer of Perry Mason...", died:date('1980-07-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nrlF5DlPY9dEQcZ5aPdab88ECWY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/98574"}}, {tmdbId:"3380", properties:{bornIn:"Lowell, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0000012", born:date('1908-04-05'), name:"Bette Davis", bio:"Ruth Elizabeth \"Bette\" Davis (April 5, 1908 – October 6, 1989) was an American actress of film, television and theater.  Noted for her willingness to play unsympathetic characters, she was highly regarded for her performances in a range of film genres; from contemporary crime melodramas to historical and period films and occasional comedies, though her greatest successes were her roles in romantic dramas...", died:date('1989-10-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iu6k5EluDgM7OT4X8WaqXCBWK61.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3380"}}, {tmdbId:"81167", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0864931", born:date('1899-11-29'), name:"Genevieve Tobin", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGenevieve Tobin (November 29, 1899 – July 21, 1995) was an American actress. \n\nThe daughter of a vaudeville performer, Tobin made her film debut in 1910 in Uncle Tom's Cabin as Eva.  She appeared in a few films as a child, and formed a double act with her sister Vivian.  Their brother, George, also had a brief acting career.  Following her education in Paris and New York, Tobin concentrated on a stage career in New York...", died:date('1995-07-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xndEM5JDTK2ahhzNKWaLkhh5He0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81167"}}, {tmdbId:"81168", properties:{bornIn:"Flemington, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0285264", born:date('1910-06-18'), name:"Dick Foran", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJohn Nicholas 'Dick' Foran (June 18, 1910 – August 10, 1979) was an American actor, known for his performances in western musicals and for playing supporting roles in dramatic pictures. \n\nForan was still billed as Nick Foran when he signed a contract with Fox in 1934.  In 1935, Foran, who stood 6-foot-2 and had red hair, was hired by Warner Bros.  as a supporting actor, changing his first name to Dick...", died:date('1979-08-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/f2zaSQQw8mGR4Uo0khpr1Jf64rX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81168"}}, {tmdbId:"94928", properties:{bornIn:" New York City, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0269647", born:date('1915-05-05'), name:"Alice Faye", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAlice Faye (May 5, 1915 – May 9, 1998) was an American actress and singer, called by The New York Times \"one of the few movie stars to walk away from stardom at the peak of her career\". \n\nShe is often associated with the Academy Award–winning standard \"You'll Never Know\", which she introduced in the 1943 musical film Hello, Frisco, Hello...", died:date('1998-05-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/g1Hd3MmFahWoIQVQZw9qtxWfIsF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94928"}}, {tmdbId:"9070", properties:{bornIn:"Boston, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0355095", born:date('1897-08-10'), name:"Jack Haley", died:date('1979-06-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9KSDR9ABg1pPLN8ZJMF3HxemlNH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9070"}}, {tmdbId:"29661", properties:{bornIn:"Vienna, Austria-Hungary [now Austria]", imdbId:"0393028", born:date('1898-08-12'), name:"Oskar Homolka", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nOskar Homolka (August 12, 1898 – January 27, 1978) was an Austrian film and theatre actor.  Homolka's strong accent, stocky appearance, bushy eyebrows and Slavic-sounding name led many to believe he was Eastern European or Russian, but he was born in Vienna, Austria-Hungary. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Oskar Homolka, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1978-01-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oh0kTpM8ZAPJgX4GzjzUIZa9LE0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29661"}}, {tmdbId:"102885", properties:{bornIn:"London, England", imdbId:"0856469", born:date('1919-02-17'), name:"Desmond Tester", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDesmond Tester (17 February 1919 – 31 December 2002) was an English and Australian film actor and television actor, host and executive.  He was born in London, England.  Among his most notable roles was that of the ill-fated boy Stevie in the Alfred Hitchcock film Sabotage (1936). \n\nTester made his first stage appearance at the age of 12, receiving positive reviews from London critics.  He was known more as a child actor in film in his native England...", died:date('2002-12-31'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/102885"}}, {tmdbId:"29127", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0517058", born:date('1898-01-03'), name:"John Loder", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJohn Loder (3 January 1898 — 26 December 1988) was a British-American actor.  He was born William John Muir Lowe in London.  His father was General W.  H.  M.  Lowe, the British officer to whom Patrick Pearse, the leader of the Irish 1916 Rising in Dublin, surrendered.  Both General Lowe and his son were present at the surrender of Pearse...", died:date('1988-12-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/i2RHR5Xs8CsegAfHdDDLS1wlv2u.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29127"}}, {tmdbId:"14868", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0001870", born:date('1907-02-22'), name:"Robert Young", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRobert George Young  (February 22, 1907 – July 21, 1998) was an American television, film, and radio actor, best known for his leading roles as Jim Anderson, the father of Father Knows Best (NBC and then CBS) and as physician Marcus Welby in Marcus Welby, M. D.  (ABC). \n\nYoung appeared in over 100 films between 1931 and 1952...", died:date('1998-07-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zsUCL3cmKSyOE2xSjXDT8v7SOYi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14868"}}, {tmdbId:"8728", properties:{bornIn:"Winfield, Kansas, USA", imdbId:"0657874", born:date('1889-07-08'), name:"Eugene Pallette", bio:"Eugene William Pallette (July 8, 1889 – September 3, 1954) was an American actor.  He appeared in over 240 silent era and sound era motion pictures between 1913 and 1946...", died:date('1954-09-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/k4MvMvY3DMSXNfXJEWiTaBi9Ir4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8728"}}, {tmdbId:"125364", properties:{bornIn:"Hammonton, New Jersey, United States", imdbId:"0602005", born:date('1876-02-24'), name:"Victor Moore", bio:"Victor Moore was born on February 24, 1876 in Hammonton, New Jersey, USA as Victor Frederick Moore.  He was an actor, known for Swing Time (1936), Make Way for Tomorrow (1937) and The Seven Year Itch (1955).  He was married to Shirley Paige and Emma Littlefield.  He died on July 24, 1962 in East Islip, Long Island, New York, USA. \n\nMoore and his first wife were a vaudeville team for several decades before her death...", died:date('1962-07-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qDoKZ77Pmq1RebbJiQHEmwpUyia.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/125364"}}, {tmdbId:"30185", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0110813", born:date('1891-08-11'), name:"Helen Broderick", bio:"Helen Broderick (August 11, 1891 - September 25, 1959) was a wonderfully funny character comedienne with vaudeville and stage experience, a close friend of Jeanne Eagels.   The story goes, that at the age of 14 she ran away from home, because  her mother, who appeared in operatic comedy, was totally obsessed by the  theatre...", died:date('1959-09-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ivLLiHElyLFtRlYxj46f4Rc91Li.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30185"}}, {tmdbId:"118630", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0795044", born:date('1915-06-29'), name:"Dorothy Short", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDorothy Short (1915 - 1963) was an American film actress mainly in low-budget westerns and serials in the 1930s and 1940s. \n\nA native of Philadelphia, she married actor Dave O'Brien in 1936, the same year they appeared together in the low-budget exploitation cheapie Reefer Madness, which in modern times has become a well-known cult film.  She also appeared in another anti-marijuana film Assassin of Youth in 1937...", died:date('1963-06-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8ebNyRnsa2Ts2P1X4TxWHJF4SZh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/118630"}}, {tmdbId:"118631", properties:{imdbId:"0185924", born:date('1914-12-07'), name:"Kenneth Craig", died:date('1994-07-12'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/118631"}}, {tmdbId:"118632", properties:{bornIn:"Oskaloosa, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0587178", born:date('1907-08-01'), name:"Lillian Miles", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLillian Miles, (1907 - 1972) was an American actress in several films in the 1930s.  Aside from singing and performing in the celebrated 'Continental' musical number in The Gay Divorcee (1934), starring Fred Astaire and Ginger Rogers, Ms.  Miles film career was brief, unremarkable and confined to low-budget 'B' pictures...", died:date('1972-02-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/urveKLgpGWSkbkXhxpBTaVRotbl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/118632"}}, {tmdbId:"118633", properties:{bornIn:"Big Spring, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0639495", born:date('1912-05-31'), name:"Dave O'Brien", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDave O'Brien (born David Poole Fronabarger, May 31, 1912 – November 8, 1969) was an American film actor, director, and writer. \n\nO'Brien was best known to movie audiences in the 1940s as the hero of the Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer comedy short film series Pete Smith Specialties narrated by Pete Smith.  O'Brien wrote and directed many of these subjects under the name David Barclay.  He also appeared in many low-budget Westerns, often billed as Tex O'Brien...", died:date('1969-11-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/y8gqfJFqLkqTvAPkLKsnaDKK5q2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/118633"}}, {tmdbId:"1208", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0000897", born:date('1904-06-17'), name:"Ralph Bellamy", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRalph Rexford Bellamy (June 17, 1904 – November 29, 1991) was an American actor whose career spanned 62 years on stage, screen and television.  During his career, he played leading roles as well as supporting roles, garnering acclaim and awards, including an Academy Award nomination for Best Supporting Actor for The Awful Truth (1937). \n\nHis film career began with The Secret Six (1931) starring Wallace Beery and featuring Jean Harlow and Clark Gable...", died:date('1991-11-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vOWBfOx8ixLjRyAJfMkUwaKUeRs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1208"}}, {tmdbId:"77159", properties:{bornIn:"Cairo, Egypt", imdbId:"0195422", born:date('1908-08-10'), name:"Alexander D'Arcy", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAlexander D'Arcy, ( 10 August 1908 – 20 April 1996) was an Egyptian actor with an international film repertoire. \n\nBorn Alexander Sarruf in Cairo, Egypt, D'Arcy, variously credited as Alexandre D'Arcy, Alex D'Arcy, Alexandre Darcy and Alex d'Arcy appeared in some 45 films, mostly as a suave gentleman or smooth rogue.  His first film appearance was in 1927 in The Garden of Allah, before appearing in Alfred Hitchcock's Champagne (1928)...", died:date('1996-04-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pHYCv2MYqUEWfM6pRIbZHSQ5CDR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77159"}}, {tmdbId:"80625", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York", imdbId:"0122675", born:date('1896-01-20'), name:"George Burns", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGeorge Burns (January 20, 1896 – March 9, 1996), born Nathan Birnbaum, was an American comedian, actor, and writer. \n\nHis career spanned vaudeville, film, radio, and television, with and without his wife, Gracie Allen.  His arched eyebrow and cigar smoke punctuation became familiar trademarks for over three quarters of a century...", died:date('1996-03-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5YnwfZGvoRkftMmo4xx6xyMBCg5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80625"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"109896", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California.", imdbId:"0020555", born:date('1895-07-26'), name:"Gracie Allen", bio:"Grace Ethel Cecile Rosalie Allen (July 26, 1895 – August 27, 1964) was an American comedian who became internationally famous as the zany partner and comic foil of husband George Burns, her straight man.   Description above from the Wikipedia article Gracie Allen, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1964-08-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/29wnBIgMcu1lDlafcHs5pjfNUSa.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/109896"}}, {tmdbId:"3360", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0000021", born:date('1917-10-22'), name:"Joan Fontaine", bio:"Born Joan de Beauvoir de Havilland on October 22, 1917, in Tokyo, Japan, in what was known as the International Settlement.  Her father was a British patent attorney with a lucrative practice in Japan, but due to Joan and older sister Olivia de Havilland's recurring ailments the family moved to California in the hopes of improving their health.  Mrs.  de Havilland and the two girls settled in Saratoga while their father went back to his practice in Japan...", died:date('2013-12-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zwbyeuUkfNwq97L3Xlb2YIFhig.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3360"}}, {tmdbId:"10802", properties:{bornIn:"Old Forge, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0427452", born:date('1907-10-14'), name:"Allan Jones", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nAllan Jones (14 October 1907–27 June 1992) was an American actor and singer.  For many years he was married to actress Irene Hervey; their son is American pop singer Jack Jones. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Allan Jones  licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1992-06-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ekFLEoK1U29wAAQjrKecpp1XNVe.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10802"}}, {tmdbId:"125483", properties:{bornIn:"Vienna, Austro-Hungarian Empire", imdbId:"0521300", born:date('1903-11-15'), name:"Tilly Losch", bio:"Ottilie Ethel Leopoldine \"Tilly\" Losch, Countess of Carnarvon was an Austrian-born dancer, choreographer, actress and painter.  She studied ballet from childhood at the Vienna Opera, making her debut in 1913 in Louis Frappart's 1885 Wiener Walzer.  Her film debut was in  Richard Boleslawski \"The Garden of Allah\" (1936)...", died:date('1975-12-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xImi4NxeWVXVlPkyh1PHxiy0ng.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/125483"}}, {tmdbId:"11544", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0300064", born:date('1904-05-16'), name:"Jean Gabin", bio:"Jean Gabin (17 May 1904 – 15 November 1976) was a major French actor and war hero...", died:date('1976-11-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pmFuOVTQvYdgmN7cYOuyJHPfMRt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11544"}}, {tmdbId:"11546", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0294382", born:date('1897-04-04'), name:"Pierre Fresnay", bio:"Pierre Fresnay (4 April 1897 - 9 January 1975) was a French stage and film actor...", died:date('1975-01-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ukt3W6FiJpFrWxR3CuLS2cgVpkH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11546"}}, {tmdbId:"5831", properties:{bornIn:"Brighton, England, UK", imdbId:"0871546", born:date('1894-07-23'), name:"Arthur Treacher", bio:"Born Arthur Veary Treacher in Brighton, East Sussex, England, he was the son of a lawyer.  He established a stage career after returning from World War I, and by 1928, he had come to America as part of a musical-comedy revue called Great Temptations.  When his film career began in the early 1930s, Treacher was Hollywood's idea of the perfect butler, and he headlined as the famous butler Jeeves in Thank You, Jeeves! (1936) and Step Lively, Jeeves! (1937)--based on the P. G.  Wodehouse character...", died:date('1975-12-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oPhvOmBTJxFqRQfkEyyPuKJM5Bu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5831"}}, {tmdbId:"10922", properties:{bornIn:"Cincinnati, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0000061", born:date('1914-05-05'), name:"Tyrone Power", bio:"One of the great romantic swashbuckling stars of the mid-twentieth  century, and the third Tyrone Power of four in a famed acting dynasty  reaching back to the eighteenth century.  His great-grandfather was the  first Tyrone Power (1795-1841), a famed Irish comedian.  His father,  known to historians as Tyrone Power Sr. ,  but to his contemporaries as either Tyrone Power or Tyrone Power the  Younger, was a huge star in the theater (and later in films) in both  classical and modern roles...", died:date('1958-11-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6eVz28D9V080Oqzj1DRCctfUGcu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10922"}}, {tmdbId:"18156", properties:{bornIn:"Kenosha, Wisconsin, USA", imdbId:"0000747", born:date('1908-05-31'), name:"Don Ameche", bio:"Don Ameche was a versatile and popular American film actor in the 1930s and '40s, usually as the dapper, mustached leading man.  He was also popular as a radio master of ceremonies during this time.  As his film popularity waned in the 1950s, he continued working in theater and some TV.  His film career surged in a comeback in the 1980s with fine work as an aging millionaire in Trading Places (1983) and a rejuvenated oldster in Cocoon (1985).  Don Ameche was an Academy Award winning American actor...", died:date('1993-12-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bcuX5Rx1G6iqiupBuEr6JyEgyhR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18156"}}, {tmdbId:"98568", properties:{bornIn:"Princeton, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0732079", born:date('1898-04-09'), name:"Paul Robeson", bio:"Paul Robeson (April 9, 1898 - January 23, 1976) was an American concert bass-baritone, athlete,  actor and political activist.   Born in Princeton, New Jersey he was educated at Rutgers College and Columbia University Law School.  After briefly practising as a lawyer he left the trade due to racism and instead pursued his acting and singing career...", died:date('1976-01-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9Mu2bol7MeJeFjeWc38UQ74DZKO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/98568"}}, {tmdbId:"99461", properties:{bornIn:"Lye, Worcestershire, England, UK", imdbId:"0362567", born:date('1893-02-19'), name:"Cedric Hardwicke", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSir Cedric Webster Hardwicke (19 February 1893 – 6 August 1964) was a noted English stage and film actor whose career spanned nearly fifty years.  Hardwicke's theatre work included notable performances in productions of the plays of William Shakespeare and George Bernard Shaw, and his film work included leading roles in a number of adapted literary classics...", died:date('1964-08-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4nKaHppmOSS958pXNuGiYQYT6b0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/99461"}}, {tmdbId:"14685", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0950019", born:date('1887-11-11'), name:"Roland Young", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRoland Young (11 November 1887 – 5 June 1953) was an English actor. \n\nYoung made his first stage appearance in London's West End in Find the Woman in 1908, and in 1912 he made his Broadway debut in Hindle Wakes.  He appeared in two comedies written for him by Clare Kummer, Good Gracious Annabelle! (1916) and A Successful Calamity (1917) before he served with the United States Army during World War I...", died:date('1953-06-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nejnPh8IICfhtYDX7R5C0Qb3yKM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14685"}}, {tmdbId:"88460", properties:{bornIn:"Igtham, Kent, England, UK", imdbId:"0496819", born:date('1913-01-02'), name:"Anna Lee", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nAnna Lee, MBE (2 January 1913 – 14 May 2004), born Joan Boniface Winnifrith, was an English actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Anna Lee, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2004-05-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xAwrTwcbxTpOcZhcrdCtdfRzDys.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88460"}}, {tmdbId:"25173", properties:{bornIn:"Litchfield, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0814216", born:date('1899-02-15'), name:"Gale Sondergaard", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGale Sondergaard (February 15, 1899 – August 14, 1985) was an American actress. \n\nSondergaard began her acting career in theatre, and progressed to films in 1936.  She was the first recipient of the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress for her film debut in Anthony Adverse (1936).  She played supporting roles in various films during the late 1930s and early 1940s, including The Cat and the Canary (1939), The Mark of Zorro (1940) and The Letter (1940)...", died:date('1985-08-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xl1Xgn4c4wx9I9z47e3AVVw3emr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25173"}}, {tmdbId:"24820", properties:{bornIn:"Vienna, Austria", imdbId:"0771584", born:date('1896-03-22'), name:"Joseph Schildkraut", bio:"Joseph Schildkraut was an Austrian born stage, screen, and television actor...", died:date('1964-01-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/74UNeM6FKCWhgoqwadOhRE8fAZs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24820"}}, {tmdbId:"100779", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0390192", born:date('1903-09-05'), name:"Gloria Holden", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nGloria Anna Holden (September 5, 1903 – March 22, 1991) was an English-born American film actress, best known for her 1936 role as Dracula's Daughter in the film of the same title...", died:date('1991-03-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cuyP722J6jgs1cltb2KzmyZ5Pcr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100779"}}, {tmdbId:"29522", properties:{bornIn:" Richmond, Surrey, England, UK", imdbId:"0172903", born:date('1891-02-09'), name:"Ronald Colman", bio:"British leading man of primarily American films, one of the great stars of the Golden Age.  Raised in Ealing, the son of a successful silk merchant, he attended boarding school in Sussex, where he first discovered amateur theatre.  He intended to attend Cambridge and become an engineer, but his father's death cost him the financial support necessary.  He joined the London Scottish Regionals and at the outbreak of World War I was sent to France...", died:date('1958-05-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eYzmXamTV6CpqwxZqTEJSBRNlb0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29522"}}, {tmdbId:"2021", properties:{bornIn:"Campgaw, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0943553", born:date('1910-08-12'), name:"Jane Wyatt", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nJane Wyatt (August 12, 1910 – October 20, 2006) was an American actress best known for her role as the housewife and mother on the NBC and CBS television comedy series, Father Knows Best, and as Amanda Grayson, the human mother of Spock on the science fiction television series Star Trek.  Wyatt was a three-time Emmy Award-winner. \n\nJane Waddington Wyatt was born on August 12, 1910 in Mahwah, New Jersey, but raised in Manhattan.  Her father, Christopher Billopp Wyatt, Jr...", died:date('2006-10-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/blYpLJKupFFi6QKqfMWJvN2hkpn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2021"}}, {tmdbId:"102687", properties:{bornIn:"Cleveland, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0397397", born:date('1913-04-14'), name:"John Howard", bio:"John Howard (born John Richard Cox Jr. ) was an American screen and television actor.  He made his movie debut in a bit part in Paramount's One Hour Late (1934) before moving up the Hollywood ladder to featured parts and ultimately landing his own series, the Bulldog Drummond mysteries.  Decades later, when offers of work began to slow down, Howard went into teaching...", died:date('1995-02-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1R9cb9oCVnAbuvFLZggPEg9Rzuy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/102687"}}, {tmdbId:"13576", properties:{bornIn:"Racine, Wisconsin, USA", imdbId:"0545298", born:date('1897-08-31'), name:"Fredric March", bio:"Fredric March (born Ernest Frederick McIntyre Bickel; August 31, 1897 – April 14, 1975) was an American actor, regarded as \"one of Hollywood's most celebrated, versatile stars of the 1930s and '40s. \" He won the Academy Award for Best Actor for Dr.  Jekyll and Mr.  Hyde (1931) and The Best Years of Our Lives (1946), as well as the Tony Award for Best Actor in a Play for Years Ago (1947) and Long Day's Journey into Night (1956)...", died:date('1975-04-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3QzMI2O7NP2j45XBCoBl7o1KogN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13576"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"83474", properties:{bornIn:"Athens, Wisconsin, USA", imdbId:"0935415", born:date('1884-05-26'), name:"Charles Winninger", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nCharles Winninger (May 26, 1884 – January 27, 1969) was an American stage and film actor, most often cast in comedies or musicals, but equally at home in dramas...", died:date('1969-01-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oAMKXg214DACXg5jLQyA57Rj0ji.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83474"}}, {tmdbId:"94937", properties:{bornIn:"Reims, Marne, France", imdbId:"0300388", born:date('1887-01-13'), name:"Gabriel Gabrio", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGabriel Gabrio (13 January 1887 – 31 October 1946) was a French stage and film actor whose career began in cinema in the silent film era of the 1920s and spanned more than two decades...", died:date('1946-10-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2H55al1OCSlY5EaaJKISs0Sel2y.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94937"}}, {tmdbId:"94938", properties:{bornIn:"Sens, Yonne, France", imdbId:"0264692", born:date('1884-04-04'), name:"Saturnin Fabre", bio:"Saturnin Fabre, born April 4, 1884 in Sens (Yonne) and died October 24, 1961 in Montgeron (Essonne), is a French actor. \n\nHis paternal family was from the south of France (Var and Bouches-du-Rhône).  He lived in Deuil-la-Barre.  He won a first prize at the Conservatoire and played dramas, boulevard comedies and operettas as well, setting himself up as the \"thundering\", out of phase phrasing, of French cinema...", died:date('1961-10-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cxpVmAdqLqGkrlGBpJlOdpIvxra.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94938"}}, {tmdbId:"94939", properties:{bornIn:"Marseilles, France", imdbId:"0153457", born:date('1887-06-01'), name:"Fernand Charpin", died:date('1944-11-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/til2Tyu3BWeZ3ObIkp0cYKuCjqQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94939"}}, {tmdbId:"30184", properties:{bornIn:"Finchley, Middlesex, England, UK", imdbId:"0089314", born:date('1887-12-23'), name:"Eric Blore", bio:"Eric Blore (23 December 1887 - 2 March 1959) was an English actor...", died:date('1959-03-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8FqfAtUoP5ZmId498VCKWs3UuT7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30184"}}, {tmdbId:"5457", properties:{bornIn:"Syracuse, New York, USA", imdbId:"0041165", born:date('1878-05-02'), name:"Roy Atwell", died:date('1962-02-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/huVgxMlWdN6VvIzfiMLEZi4Zlbu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5457"}}, {tmdbId:"5458", properties:{imdbId:"0118081", name:"Stuart Buchanan", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5458"}}, {tmdbId:"5460", properties:{bornIn:"Bridgeport, Connecticut, U.S.A.", imdbId:"0143314", born:date('1916-05-16'), name:"Adriana Caselotti", died:date('1997-01-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7nOCtRQnfH6RQ39IZBDffIadgR7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5460"}}, {tmdbId:"13816", properties:{bornIn:"Melbourne, Victoria, Australia", imdbId:"0733480", born:date('1858-04-19'), name:"May Robson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMay Robson (19 April 1858 - 20 October 1942) was an actress and playwright.  A major stage actress of the late 19th and early 20th century, Robson is best known today for the dozens of 1930s motion pictures she appeared in when she was well into her seventies, usually playing cross old ladies with hearts of gold...", died:date('1942-10-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3j6dLrmRF5eXZtE256ojJRTNNq6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13816"}}, {tmdbId:"14974", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001766", born:date('1907-07-16'), name:"Barbara Stanwyck", bio:"Barbara Stanwyck (July 16, 1907 – January 20, 1990) was an American actress.  A film and television star, she was known during her 60-year career as a consummate and versatile professional with a strong screen presence and was a favorite of directors including Cecil B.  DeMille, Fritz Lang and Frank Capra.  After a short stint as a stage actress, she made 85 films in 38 years in Hollywood, before turning to television...", died:date('1990-01-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/y9BX4FNoFBjP2HPcs8rlzqXjJbu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14974"}}, {tmdbId:"19327", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0794297", born:date('1918-04-17'), name:"Anne Shirley", bio:"Anne Shirley (born Dawn Evelyeen Paris) was an American child, teen, and young adult screen actress.  She retired at age 26.  Initially appearing in films under the name Dawn O'Day, she changed her name to Anne Shirley (the name of the title character she portrayed) upon the success of the 1934 film Anne of Green Gables...", died:date('1993-07-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gzfeLyzAvQkdaMFpxhYFvWLpzEo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19327"}}, {tmdbId:"7642", properties:{bornIn:"St. Louis, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0641966", born:date('1910-07-17'), name:"Barbara O'Neil", died:date('1980-09-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/i0OOcgkuMVemnKmqwb7WY8kTDGu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7642"}}, {tmdbId:"89731", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000909", born:date('1904-10-22'), name:"Constance Bennett", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nConstance Campbell Bennett (October 22, 1904 – July 24, 1965) was an American actress. \n\nShe started off with a spell in a convent but decided to go into the family business.  Independent, cultured, ironic and outspoken, Constance, the first Bennett sister to enter motion pictures, appeared in New York-produced silent movies before a meeting with Samuel Goldwyn led to her Hollywood debut in Cytherea (1924)...", died:date('1965-07-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hi8BAIa1Ng0b48MJ20t7JdcMEY8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89731"}}, {tmdbId:"9071", properties:{bornIn:"Washington, District of Columbia, USA", imdbId:"0000992", born:date('1884-08-07'), name:"Billie Burke", bio:"Mary William Ethelbert Appleton \"Billie\" Burke (August 7, 1884 – May 14, 1970) was an American actress.  She is primarily known to modern audiences as Glinda the Good Witch of the North in the musical film The Wizard of Oz.  She was nominated for an Academy Award for her performance as Emily Kilbourne in Merrily We Live. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Billie Burke,  licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1970-05-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ysobf0jqoOP6r7AriTUHxxK7QeC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9071"}}, {tmdbId:"30495", properties:{bornIn:"Stepney, East London, England, UK", imdbId:"0572142", born:date('1886-12-09'), name:"Victor McLaglen", bio:"Victor McLaglen was a British-American film actor.  He was known as a character actor, particularly in Westerns, and made seven films with John Ford and John Wayne.  McLaglen won the Academy Award for Best Actor in 1935 for his role in The Informer...", died:date('1959-11-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vYj8mVtT8CgQOHH8eRNMl7pA7F1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30495"}}, {tmdbId:"227034", properties:{bornIn:"Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0485806", born:date('1917-05-05'), name:"June Lang", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJune Lang (born Winifred June Vlasek, May 5, 1917 – May 16, 2005) was an American film actress.   Born in Minneapolis, Minnesota, the daughter of Edith and Clarence Vlasek, Lang originally trained as a dancer in \"kiddie revues\" and went to Hollywood at the urging of her mother.   She made her film debut in 1931 and caught the eye of Darryl F.  Zanuck at 20th Century Fox, gradually securing second lead roles in mostly B movies...", died:date('2005-05-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tRcnZ2Ed1krFt9Vpy6iG97aYn0j.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/227034"}}, {tmdbId:"4958", properties:{bornIn:"Grand Island, Nebraska, USA", imdbId:"0000020", born:date('1905-05-16'), name:"Henry Fonda", bio:"Henry Jaynes Fonda (May 16, 1905 – August 12, 1982) was an American actor who had a career that spanned five decades in Hollywood.  Fonda cultivated a strong, appealing screen image in several films now considered to be classics, earning one Academy Award for Best Actor on two nominations. \n\nFonda made his mark early as a Broadway actor and made his Hollywood film debut in 1935...", died:date('1982-08-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6wXWsqSXF3wCsGcwVqiszy6RX9X.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4958"}}, {tmdbId:"14451", properties:{bornIn:"Columbia, South Carolina, USA", imdbId:"0533692", born:date('1902-12-25'), name:"Barton MacLane", bio:"Barton MacLane graduated from Wesleyan University, where he displayed a notable aptitude for sports, in particular football and basketball.  Not surprisingly, his physical prowess led to an early role in The Quarterback (1926) with Richard Dix.  MacLane once commented that, as an actor, he needed to have the physical strength to tear the bad guys \"from limb to limb\", if necessary...", died:date('1969-01-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hcxJh7J38sQIp1X0cQbQY4SbK0F.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14451"}}, {tmdbId:"80238", properties:{imdbId:"0228863", born:date('1896-07-14'), name:"Jean Dixon", bio:"Connecticut-born Jean Dixon had an auspicious theatre debut:  on a Parisian stage with Sarah Bernhardt while still a student at a  French university.  Upon her return to the U. S.  in 1921, she made her Broadway debut, and thereafter appeared in many stage productions, on Broadway  and across the country, before Hollywood called her in 1929.  She most  often appeared as the streetwise, smart-mouthed friend of the leading  lady...", died:date('1981-02-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vVCyYX7paMvtaU9oXcXCCOs8Hjt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80238"}}, {tmdbId:"3155", properties:{bornIn:"Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA", imdbId:"0002285", born:date('1899-11-11'), name:"Pat O'Brien", bio:"Pat O’Brien (born William Joseph Patrick O'Brien) was an American stage, screen, radio, and television actor.  He was a star during the first several years of his film career, the height of his popularity being during the 1930s and 1940s...", died:date('1983-10-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tVi4a98SiPWjRPunpLlLMK78iCq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3155"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"4110", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000007", born:date('1899-12-25'), name:"Humphrey Bogart", bio:"Humphrey DeForest Bogart (December 25, 1899 – January 14, 1957) was an American actor.  He is widely regarded as a cultural icon.  The American Film Institute ranked Bogart as the greatest male star in the history of American cinema. \n\nAfter trying various jobs, Bogart began acting in 1921 and became a regular in Broadway productions in the 1920s and 1930s.  When the stock market crash of 1929 reduced the demand for plays, Bogart turned to film...", died:date('1957-01-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dXGs7F5ezehcofe6j7Kz7wIhmV6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4110"}}, {tmdbId:"80994", properties:{bornIn:"Denton, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0792130", born:date('1915-02-21'), name:"Ann Sheridan", bio:"Ann Sheridan was an American film actress...", died:date('1967-01-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pAPqHCSn5Qmtr7QFbCJ2NwCUBBr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80994"}}, {tmdbId:"13819", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0146185", born:date('1889-02-04'), name:"Walter Catlett", died:date('1960-11-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nVTm1BgX8ipp15WrjeCKVU0MeKN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13819"}}, {tmdbId:"5832", properties:{bornIn:"Wheathampstead, Hertfordshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0654239", born:date('1887-08-05'), name:"Reginald Owen", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJohn Reginald Owen (5 August 1887 – 5 November 1972) was an English character actor.  He was known for his many roles in British and American films and later in television programmes.   The son of Joseph and Frances Owen, Reginald Owen studied at Sir Herbert Tree's Royal Academy of Dramatic Art and made his professional debut in 1905...", died:date('1972-11-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eurF2C1e5GwG1EE8vdAf9IOFttK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5832"}}, {tmdbId:"30234", properties:{bornIn:"London, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0516876", born:date('1891-07-18'), name:"Gene Lockhart", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nEdwin Eugene Lockhart (July 18, 1891 – March 31, 1957) was a Canadian-American character actor, singer, and playwright.  He also wrote the lyrics to a number of popular songs.  He became a United States citizen in 1939. \n\nBorn in London, Ontario, the son of John Coats Lockhart and Ellen Mary (née Delaney) Lockhart, he made his professional debut at the age of six when he appeared with the Kilties Band of Canada...", died:date('1957-03-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8lSQRefIA5kNylZOF7anexkDxqQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30234"}}, {tmdbId:"34182", properties:{bornIn:"Southsea, Hampshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0516883", born:date('1894-08-09'), name:"Kathleen Lockhart", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nKathleen Lockhart  (August 9, 1894 — February 18, 1978) was an English-born stage actress. \n\nShe was born Kathleen Arthur in Southsea, Hampshire in England.  An actress and musician, Kathleen got her start on the stage in England and then immigrated to the United States in 1924, upon her marriage to Canadian-born actor Gene Lockhart.  She continued to appear on stage and in Hollywood films for almost forty years...", died:date('1978-02-17'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34182"}}, {tmdbId:"81933", properties:{bornIn:"West Ham, Essex, Greater London, England, UK", imdbId:"0452953", born:date('1926-11-25'), name:"Terry Kilburn", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nTerence E.  Kilburn (born 25 November 1926), known for his acting work prior to 1953 as Terry Kilburn, is an English-American actor.  Born in London, he moved to Hollywood in the U. S.  at the age of 10, and is best known for his roles as a child actor, in films such as A Christmas Carol (1938) and Goodbye, Mr.  Chips (1939) in the late 1930s and the early 1940s. \n\nKilburn was born in West Ham, Essex, in Greater London in 1926, to working-class parents...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kp8eIhg3QPkIeeVUPSsA7tqrvcD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81933"}}, {tmdbId:"80234", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0634260", born:date('1916-07-14'), name:"Doris Nolan", died:date('1998-07-29'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80234"}}, {tmdbId:"20365", properties:{bornIn:"Dubuque, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0512267", born:date('1910-09-19'), name:"Margaret Lindsay", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMargaret Lindsay (born Margaret Kies; September 19, 1910 – May 9, 1981) was an American film actress.  Her time as a Warner Bros.  contract player during the 1930s was particularly productive.  She was noted for her supporting work in successful films of the 1930s and 1940s such as Jezebel (1938) and Scarlet Street (1945) and her leading roles in lower-budgeted B movie films such as the Ellery Queen series at Columbia in the early 1940s...", died:date('1981-05-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yIs7hUnLh2xasSWS7lHbIYtlXI4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20365"}}, {tmdbId:"218442", properties:{bornIn:"Saint Paul, Minnesota, U.S.", imdbId:"0204843", born:date('1907-06-29'), name:"Joan Davis", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJoan Davis (June 29, 1907 – May 22, 1961) was an American comedic actress whose career spanned vaudeville, film, radio and television.  Remembered best for the 1950s television comedy, I Married Joan, Davis had a successful earlier career as a B-movie actress and a leading star of 1940s radio comedy. \n\nBorn as Madonna Josephine Davis in Saint Paul, Minnesota, Davis was a performer since childhood.  She appeared with her husband Si Wills in vaudeville...", died:date('1961-05-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4xujDxiROtPDOjVkcxzLTrXkeO9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/218442"}}, {tmdbId:"1231648", properties:{bornIn:"Onset Bay, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0268190", born:date('1900-08-09'), name:"Charles Farrell", bio:"Popular Hollywood leading man of late silents and early talkies.  He is best remembered for his teaming with Janet Gaynor in 12 screen romances between 1927 and 1934.  He retired from films in the early 1940s, but TV audiences of the 1950s would see him as Gale Storm's widower dad in the popular television series My Little Margie (1952)...", died:date('1990-05-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5fhrR7vCYtlyJQxnhNPscwFxfgT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1231648"}}, {tmdbId:"229632", properties:{bornIn:"Fresno - California - USA", imdbId:"0240358", born:date('1914-03-06'), name:"Amanda Duff", bio:"Amanda Duff was born on March 6, 1914 in Fresno, California.  She was an actress, known for The Devil Commands (1941), Just Around the Corner (1938) and Mr.  Moto in Danger Island (1939).  She was married to Philip Dunne.  She died on April 6, 2006 in San Francisco, California. \n\nAfter abandoning her acting career, she turned to photography in the 1940s...", died:date('2006-04-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9F7IpiOXJYTOaYCXdISN5ObPPS6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/229632"}}, {tmdbId:"14298", properties:{bornIn:"Karachi, British India", imdbId:"0516994", born:date('1916-09-15'), name:"Margaret Lockwood", bio:"Margaret Lockwood, CBE (15 September 1916 – 15 July 1990) was an English actress, notable for her performance in the 1945 Gainsborough movie, The Wicked Lady. \n\nMargaret Mary Lockwood Day was born in Karachi, British India (now Karachi, Pakistan), to an English administrator of a railway company and his Scottish wife.  Lockwood's family returned to the United Kingdom when she was a child, along with her brother...", died:date('1990-07-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hJfWWVKiH7eiV7E1H5SXHA3SkfG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14298"}}, {tmdbId:"7640", properties:{bornIn:"Bristol, Gloucestershire, England", imdbId:"0714878", born:date('1908-03-20'), name:"Michael Redgrave", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nSir Michael Scudamore Redgrave, CBE (20 March 1908 – 21 March 1985) was an English stage and film actor, director, manager and author. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Michael Redgrave, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1985-03-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cgEKItL4uwcpX4SXzXCStsqlVgP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7640"}}, {tmdbId:"14299", properties:{bornIn:"Liverpool, Merseyside, England, UK", imdbId:"0926599", born:date('1865-06-19'), name:"Dame May Whitty", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDame Mary Louise Webster, DBE (19 June 1865 – 29 May 1948), known professionally as May Whitty and later, for her charity work, Dame May Whitty, was an English stage and film actress.  She was one of the first two women entertainers to become a Dame.  The British actors union Equity was established in her home.  After a successful career she moved over to Hollywood films at the age of 72.  She went to live in America, where she won awards for her film roles...", died:date('1948-05-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/w469bqojhlsp5YeChbMLDy4gkLH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14299"}}, {tmdbId:"103366", properties:{bornIn:"New Haven, Connecticut, USA", imdbId:"0614278", born:date('1902-07-04'), name:"George Murphy", bio:"George Murphy was an American dancer and stage, screen, and television actor, as well as a United States Senator.  Murphy was a song-and-dance leading man in many big-budget Hollywood musicals from 1930 to 1952.  He was the president of the Screen Actors Guild from 1944 to 1946, and was awarded an honorary Oscar in 1951.  Murphy served from 1965 to 1971 as U. S.  Senator from California, the first notable U. S...", died:date('1992-05-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cWFvUd0cE1EYHu6GKQf3ju1ZTbA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/103366"}}, {tmdbId:"120758", properties:{bornIn:"Boise, Idaho, USA", imdbId:"0112198", born:date('1915-07-18'), name:"Phyllis Brooks", bio:"Phyllis Brooks was an American actress and model.  Brooks was born Phyllis Seiler in Boise, Idaho on July 18, 1915.  She began her career in films at age 20, and had been known as the \"Ipana Toothpaste Girl\" due to her work as a model.  Brooks, who had about 30 performances in films, was a B-movie leading lady during the 1930s and 1940s, with roles in such films as In Old Chicago (1937), Little Miss Broadway (1938), and the Shanghai Gesture (1941)...", died:date('1995-08-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qBiCziLTqc5HGgGsZApQzSRu6pI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/120758"}}, {tmdbId:"13325", properties:{bornIn:"Bramhall, Cheshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0384908", born:date('1912-08-15'), name:"Wendy Hiller", died:date('2003-05-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/psF8n2DRp0UCsmUBnRKwu6YmMoA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13325"}}, {tmdbId:"106154", properties:{bornIn:"Bradford, Yorkshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0493347", born:date('1900-01-14'), name:"Wilfrid Lawson", died:date('1966-10-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ylLCOBNvc5g3AkRLBXfSY4KgoEr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/106154"}}, {tmdbId:"90644", properties:{imdbId:"0517919", born:date('1890-07-28'), name:"Marie Lohr", bio:"Marie Lohr was an Australian film and stage actress...", died:date('1975-01-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/a5EeAv67WWWSpekY36AZ5jMMoao.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/90644"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"40174", properties:{bornIn:"Jamestown, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000840", born:date('1911-08-06'), name:"Lucille Ball", bio:"Lucille Désirée Ball  (August 6, 1911 – April 26, 1989) was an American comedian, film, television, stage and radio actress, model, film and television executive, and star of the sitcoms I Love Lucy, The Lucy–Desi Comedy Hour, The Lucy Show, Here's Lucy and Life With Lucy...", died:date('1989-04-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gcJ5Qwg9lcadvdCxC22AjFuJC4A.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/40174"}}, {tmdbId:"19967", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0340706", born:date('1917-03-22'), name:"Virginia Grey", bio:"Virginia Grey (March 22, 1917 – July 31, 2004) was an American actress. \n\nShe was born in Los Angeles, California, the daughter of director Ray Grey.  One of her early babysitters was Gloria Swanson.  Grey debuted at the age of ten in the silent film Uncle Tom's Cabin (1927) as Little Eva.  She continued acting for a few more years, but then left movies in order to finish her education...", died:date('2004-07-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ftyCI3XPJoGS75m3DFXOgOpw58z.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19967"}}, {tmdbId:"4071", properties:{bornIn:"Toledo, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0472603", born:date('1885-09-06'), name:"Otto Kruger", bio:"Otto Kruger (1885–1974) was an American actor who began his career in 1915.  His career was most prolific during the 1930s and 1940s...", died:date('1974-09-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nGSvwcSyD0645Vuv1xTJbzA21aq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4071"}}, {tmdbId:"550529", properties:{imdbId:"0048653", born:date('1912-09-30'), name:"Kenny Baker", died:date('1985-08-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mTiwquvDVV3ulBih9YTVnP3net0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/550529"}}, {tmdbId:"30226", properties:{bornIn:" Greystones, County Wicklow, Ireland", imdbId:"0280242", born:date('1913-11-24'), name:"Geraldine Fitzgerald", bio:"Geraldine Fitzgerald, Lady Lindsay-Hogg was an Irish-American actress and a member of the American Theatre Hall of Fame.  She was born south of Dublin, the daughter of Edith Catherine and Edward Martin FitzGerald. \n\nShe studied painting at the Dublin School of Art.  Inspired by her aunt,  and began her acting career in at Dublin's Gate Theatre.  After two seasons in Dublin, she moved to London, where she found success in films The Mill on the Floss, The Turn of the Tide, and Cafe Mascot...", died:date('2005-07-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ybUphD37eQrjd9PN4eIHSkmdxTs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30226"}}, {tmdbId:"39801", properties:{bornIn:"St. Petersburg, Russian Empire [now Russia]", imdbId:"0041681", born:date('1905-11-17'), name:"Mischa Auer", bio:"Mischa Auer was a Russian-born American stage, screen, and television actor, in films from 1928...", died:date('1967-03-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7mCfBcUq6FedSlD9lT6AWR3bIou.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/39801"}}, {tmdbId:"88935", properties:{bornIn:"Wien, Austria", imdbId:"0906932", born:date('1896-11-19'), name:"Anton Walbrook", bio:"Adolf Anton Wilhelm Wohlbrück (19 November 1896 – 9 August 1967) was an Austrian actor who settled in the United Kingdom under the name Anton Walbrook...", died:date('1967-08-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jA1iCJeDFuQ39uChf1uDdrFRWGN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88935"}}, {tmdbId:"117499", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0944087", born:date('1906-01-17'), name:"Diana Wynyard", bio:"Diana Wynyard, CBE  (16 January 1906 – 13 May 1964), whose birth name was Dorothy Isobel Cox, was an English stage and film actress...", died:date('1964-05-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vhDP6VEkcyuFhsLz4Rc7W8HQnnJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/117499"}}, {tmdbId:"106626", properties:{bornIn:"Liverpool, England, UK", imdbId:"0678693", born:date('1891-01-01'), name:"Frank Pettingell", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nFrank Pettingell (1 January 1891 – 17 February 1966) was an English actor. \n\nPettingell was born in Liverpool, and educated at Manchester University.  During the First World War he served with the King's Liverpool Regiment. \n\nHe appeared in such films as the original 1940 Gaslight (as the former detective who solves the case), Kipps (1941 - as Old Kipps), and Becket (1964 - as the Duke of York)...", died:date('1966-02-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wKdzspi5CETjZIJClGYWWuFcVAU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/106626"}}, {tmdbId:"153422", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0179451", born:date('1915-05-21'), name:"Cathleen Cordell", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nCathleen Cordell (May 21, 1915 – August 19, 1997) was an American film and television actress. \n\nCordell was born in Brooklyn, New York.  Cordell moved to England and then France, in order to begin her childhood education.  She died on August 19, 1997, in Cedars-Sinai Medical Center, Los Angeles, California, she was 82.  Apparently, according to the Internet Movie Database, Cordell's cause of death was emphysema.  Her burial is unknown...", died:date('1997-08-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iHE9QmxiUwFg5ltl1vkGadvjUSy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/153422"}}, {tmdbId:"3383", properties:{bornIn:"Elizabeth, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0593775", born:date('1892-07-11'), name:"Thomas Mitchell", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nThomas Mitchell (July 11, 1892 – December 17, 1962) was an American actor, playwright and screenwriter.  Among his most famous roles in a long career are those of Gerald O'Hara, the father of Scarlett O'Hara in Gone with the Wind, the drunken Doc Boone in John Ford's Stagecoach, and Uncle Billy in It's a Wonderful Life.  Mitchell was the first person to win an Oscar, an Emmy, and a Tony Award...", died:date('1962-12-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uOhcftGVj7tPrCKBYHYtYPlQKUP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3383"}}, {tmdbId:"10538", properties:{bornIn:"Darjeeling, Bengal Presidency, British India [now West Bengal, India]", imdbId:"0000046", born:date('1913-11-05'), name:"Vivien Leigh", bio:"Vivien Leigh (born Vivian Mary Hartley, and also known as Lady Olivier after 1947; 5 November 1913 – 8 July 1967) was an English stage and film actress.  She won two Academy Awards for Best Actress, for her iconic performances as Scarlett O'Hara in Gone with the Wind (1939) and Blanche DuBois in the film version of A Streetcar Named Desire (1951), a role she had also played on stage in London's West End in 1949...", died:date('1967-07-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6BqI3L41hwAwZM9ppTIBrwGT6jy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10538"}}, {tmdbId:"11494", properties:{bornIn:"Port Arthur, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0450810", born:date('1916-11-21'), name:"Evelyn Keyes", bio:"Evelyn Louise Keyes  was an American film actress.  A chorus girl by age 18, Keyes came out to Hollywood and was introduced to Cecil B.  DeMille, who in her own words, “signed me to a personal contract without even making a test”.  After a handful of B-movies at Paramount Pictures, she landed the role in Gone with the Wind, of Scarlett O'Hara's sister, Suellen.  She was later interviewed for the 1988 documentary The Making of a Legend: Gone with the Wind. \n\nColumbia Pictures signed her to a contract...", died:date('2008-07-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/efzYiYB72V8NoWTs8wItkyVjDQi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11494"}}, {tmdbId:"93805", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0002093", born:date('1904-09-29'), name:"Greer Garson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nGreer Garson, CBE (September 29, 1904 – April 6, 1996) was a British-born actress who was very popular during World War II, being listed by the Motion Picture Herald as one of America's top ten box office draws in 1942, 1943, 1944, 1945, and 1946.  As one of MGM's major stars of the 1940s, Garson received seven Academy Award nominations, winning the Best Actress award for Mrs.  Miniver (1942)...", died:date('1996-04-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oQatKGqoTuf5k2L4b5KrCIoeKhQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/93805"}}, {tmdbId:"11859", properties:{bornIn:"The Watts Naval Training College, North Elmham, Norfolk, England, UK", imdbId:"0590055", born:date('1908-02-22'), name:"John Mills", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nSir John Mills, CBE (born Lewis Ernest Watts Mills, 22 February 1908 – 23 April 2005) was an English actor who appeared in more than 120 films in a career spanning seven decades.  On screen, he often played people who are not at all exceptional, but become heroes because of their common sense, generosity and good judgement...", died:date('2005-04-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jMqhI1NeTwgdKsrj9vMshk1r5hP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11859"}}, {tmdbId:"1238764", properties:{bornIn:"India", imdbId:"0236756", born:date('1900-02-04'), name:"Jessica Dragonette", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Jessica Dragonette (February 14, 1900-March 18, 1980) was a singer who became popular on American radio and was active in the World War II effort.   Description above from the Wikipedia article Jessica Dragonette, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1980-03-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ssBYIqnkCei0SBhWfdCG9hZFYvD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1238764"}}, {tmdbId:"143466", properties:{bornIn:"Seattle, Washington, USA", imdbId:"0743595", born:date('1906-01-19'), name:"Lanny Ross", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLanny Ross (January 19, 1906 - April 25, 1988) was an American singer, pianist and songwriter. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Lanny Ross, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1988-04-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qA7d93HY7h2n7ocDFbkCxQNSJn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/143466"}}, {tmdbId:"10024", properties:{bornIn:" New York City, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0415488", born:date('1891-03-10'), name:"Sam Jaffe", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nSam Jaffe (March 10, 1891 – March 24, 1984) was an American actor, teacher, musician and engineer.  In 1951, he was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor for his performance in The Asphalt Jungle (1950) and appeared in other classic films such as Ben-Hur (1959) and The Day the Earth Stood Still (1951).  He may be best remembered for playing the title role in Gunga Din (1939), and the High Lama in Lost Horizon (1937)...", died:date('1984-03-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pvWsxtku6Ki4zKJPUz3K2StJmwB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10024"}}, {tmdbId:"32128", properties:{bornIn:"Plymouth, Devon, England, UK", imdbId:"0338901", born:date('1918-08-25'), name:"Richard Greene", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Richard Marius Joseph Greene (25 August 1918 – 1 June 1985) was a noted English film and television actor.  A matinee idol who appeared in more than 40 films, he was perhaps best known for the lead role in the long-running British TV series The Adventures of Robin Hood, which ran for 143 episodes from 1955 to 1960. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Richard Greene, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1985-06-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sjYM6UaGCwPJS3XbGNpB1paTebz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32128"}}, {tmdbId:"106089", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0057412", born:date('1912-04-18'), name:"Wendy Barrie", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nWendy Barrie (18 April 1912 – 2 February 1978) was a British actress who worked in British and American films. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Wendy Barrie, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1978-02-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1xhRhiU95SS6y79v7YBlSN3JuFy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/106089"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"3363", properties:{bornIn:"Ensenada, Baja California, Mexico", imdbId:"0115558", born:date('1895-02-04'), name:"Nigel Bruce", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nWilliam Nigel Ernle Bruce (4 February 1895 – 8 October 1953), best known as Nigel Bruce, was a British character actor on stage and screen.   He was best known for his portrayal of Doctor Watson in a series of films and in the radio series The New Adventures of Sherlock Holmes (starring Basil Rathbone as Sherlock Holmes).  Bruce is also remembered for his roles in the Alfred Hitchcock films Rebecca and Suspicion...", died:date('1953-10-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sUXVAHPZbBHKGYKTbLKbBCVwSCy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3363"}}, {tmdbId:"70035", properties:{bornIn:"Ranelagh, County Dublin, Ireland", imdbId:"0000058", born:date('1920-08-17'), name:"Maureen O'Hara", bio:"Maureen O'Hara was an Irish film actress and singer.  She was noted for playing fiercely passionate heroines with a highly sensible attitude.  She often worked with director John Ford and longtime friend John Wayne...", died:date('2015-10-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yGNh18kBF7afOdjTcEP2zFCxzCH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70035"}}, {tmdbId:"552407", properties:{imdbId:"0388166", born:date('1865-12-19'), name:"Horace Hodges", died:date('1951-07-06'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/552407"}}, {tmdbId:"552408", properties:{bornIn:"Dundee, Tayside, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0677961", born:date('1895-07-16'), name:"Hay Petrie", died:date('1948-07-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pJnBDNUr3JjcmjW4ObOjb3L7Nrr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/552408"}}, {tmdbId:"34442", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0521937", born:date('1915-01-09'), name:"Anita Louise", bio:"Anita Louise (born January 9, 1915) was an American actress. \n\nShe made her acting debut on Broadway at the age of six, and within a year was appearing regularly in Hollywood films.  By her late teens she was being cast in leading and supporting roles in major productions.   As her stature in Hollywood grew, she was named as a WAMPAS Baby Star...", died:date('1970-04-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3kPCTRG7ZLIEX5Zs9zbxFAaGPJT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34442"}}, {tmdbId:"8731", properties:{bornIn:"Cape Town, South Africa", imdbId:"0402842", born:date('1900-06-13'), name:"Ian Hunter", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Ian Hunter (13 June 1900 – 22 September 1975) was a British character actor. \n\nAmong dozens of film roles, his best-remembered appearances include That Certain Woman (1937) with Bette Davis, The Adventures of Robin Hood (1938, as King Richard the Lionheart), The Little Princess (1939, as Captain Reginald Crewe) and Dr.  Jekyll and Mr.  Hyde (1941, as Dr.  Lanyon)...", died:date('1975-09-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yiSGJGTyww5YQwi9PYS96nefkOw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8731"}}, {tmdbId:"11169", properties:{bornIn:"Macon, Georgia, USA", imdbId:"0002013", born:date('1877-06-19'), name:"Charles Coburn", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nCharles Douville Coburn (June 19, 1877 – August 30, 1961) was an American film and theatre actor.  Best known for his work in comedies, Coburn received the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor for 1943's The More the Merrier...", died:date('1961-08-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cx8DLZsUrannzYwcl8MNiCRm0hy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11169"}}, {tmdbId:"83260", properties:{bornIn:"Quebec City, Quebec, Canada", imdbId:"0914778", born:date('1879-05-27'), name:"Lucile Watson", bio:"Canadian born Lucile Watson was a stage, screen, and television actress in America...", died:date('1962-06-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wNBcS1nGUNvKta1jHrnoSdxDUUZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83260"}}, {tmdbId:"19550", properties:{bornIn:"Macon, Georgia, USA", imdbId:"0002048", born:date('1901-04-05'), name:"Melvyn Douglas", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMelvyn Douglas (born Melvyn Edouard Hesselberg, April 5, 1901 – August 4, 1981) was an American actor.  Douglas came to prominence in the 1930s as a suave leading man, perhaps best typified by his performance in the 1939 romantic comedy Ninotchka with Greta Garbo...", died:date('1981-08-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4WuaoFCSdffenrKeCJAIX0MmyJt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19550"}}, {tmdbId:"116185", properties:{bornIn:"Washington, District of Columbia, USA", imdbId:"0163257", born:date('1893-10-15'), name:"Ina Claire", died:date('1985-02-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uQXZ0Blms7JDX1HqGlqsGEXxi0d.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/116185"}}, {tmdbId:"16523", properties:{bornIn:"Cleveland, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0580565", born:date('1907-11-16'), name:"Burgess Meredith", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nOliver Burgess Meredith (November 16, 1907 – September 9, 1997), known professionally as Burgess Meredith, was an American actor in theatre, film, and television, who also worked as a director.  Active for more than six decades, Meredith has been called \"a virtuosic actor\" who was \"one of the most accomplished actors of the century. \" Meredith won several Emmys and was nominated for Academy Awards...", died:date('1997-09-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pTMJmozZqCY0VY7UiMDlM3upuZu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16523"}}, {tmdbId:"13785", properties:{bornIn:"Boston, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0275897", born:date('1913-02-08'), name:"Betty Field", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBetty Field (February 8, 1913 – September 13, 1973) was an American film and stage actress.  Through her father, she was a direct descendant of the Pilgrims John Alden and Priscilla Mullins. \n\nBorn in Boston, Massachusetts to George Field and Katharine Lynch, Field began her acting career on the London stage in Howard Lindsay's farce, She Loves Me Not...", died:date('1973-09-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zwKYuyKC45hn1UpMCaYif7KMNHV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13785"}}, {tmdbId:"4072", properties:{bornIn:"Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, USA", imdbId:"0001033", born:date('1906-02-10'), name:"Lon Chaney Jr.", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLon Chaney, Jr.  (February 10, 1906 – July 12, 1973), born Creighton Tull Chaney, was an American character actor.  He was best known for his roles in monster movies and as the son of famous silent film actor, Lon Chaney.  He is notable for playing Larry Talbot in The Wolf Man movies. \n\nOriginally credited in films as Creighton Chaney, he was first credited as \"Lon Chaney, Jr. \" in 1935.  Chaney had English, French and Irish ancestry...", died:date('1973-07-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4DHZ2jXQFbTuslsaOmrmrJ9HMMd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4072"}}, {tmdbId:"30527", properties:{bornIn:"Cambridge, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0001948", born:date('1891-01-01'), name:"Charles Bickford", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nCharles Bickford (January 1, 1891 – November 9, 1967) was an American actor best known for his supporting roles.   He was nominated three times for the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor, for The Song of Bernadette (1943), The Farmer's Daughter (1947), and Johnny Belinda (1948).  Other notable roles include Whirlpool (1948), A Star is Born (1954) and The Big Country (1958)...", died:date('1967-11-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xsasX7nazQWV3FtVR35vZeaIhsU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30527"}}, {tmdbId:"13789", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001932", born:date('1895-05-09'), name:"Richard Barthelmess", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.  \n\nRichard Semler \"Dick\" Barthelmess (May 9, 1895 – August 17, 1963) was an Oscar-nominated silent film star. \n\nBarthelmess was educated at Hudson River Military Academy at Nyack and Trinity College at Hartford, Connecticut.  His father died when he was a baby and his mother, Caroline Harris , was a stage actress, so he worked in theatres in his early days, between schooling, doing \"walk-ons\".  This led to acting in college, doing amateur productions...", died:date('1963-08-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6VvXDC26fUA97dVDTNziBdgoifP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13789"}}, {tmdbId:"33741", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000028", born:date('1918-10-17'), name:"Rita Hayworth", bio:"Rita Hayworth (October 17, 1918 – May 14, 1987) was an American film actress and dancer who attained fame during the 1940s as one of the era's top stars.  She appeared in 61 films over 37 years and is listed as one of the American Film Institute's Greatest Stars of All Time. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Rita Hayworth, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1987-05-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iFgp3nBPnbtmE1ZLog33fOLH1LF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33741"}}, {tmdbId:"11534", properties:{bornIn:"Görz, Istria, Austria-Hungary, now Gorizia, Italy", imdbId:"0339669", born:date('1901-02-03'), name:"Nora Gregor", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nNora Gregor (3 February 1901 – 20 January 1949) was a stage and film actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Nora Gregor, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1949-01-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7hOjInnf0E4G2Ohwz7QPvdamMcj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11534"}}, {tmdbId:"11535", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, Ile-de-France, France", imdbId:"0239513", born:date('1910-10-08'), name:"Paulette Dubost", bio:"Paulette Dubost (October 8, 1910 - September 21, 2011) was a French actress who began her career at the age of 7 at the Paris Opera.  She appeared in over 250 films and worked with such directors as Jean Renoir, Jacques Tourneur, Marcel Carné, Julien Duvivier, Preston Sturges and Max Ophüls.  One of her most famous roles was as Lisette in Renoir's La Règle du jeu. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Paulette Dubost, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2011-09-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4BYuOUfXSiWmGKB0THmvp9CDJfV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11535"}}, {tmdbId:"9744", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, Ile-de-France, France", imdbId:"0664186", born:date('1917-10-07'), name:"Mila Parély", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMila Parély is a French actress best known for the roles of Belle's sister in Jean Cocteau's La Belle et la Bête and as Geneviève in La Règle du jeu.  She gave up acting in the late 1950s in order to take care of her race-car driving husband, who had been injured in an accident. \n\nShe also worked with such notable directors as Max Ophüls, Robert Bresson, Fritz Lang and G. W.  Pabst.  She returned to acting briefly in the late 1980s...", died:date('2012-01-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yB8FTPTQnfzBCY5cBFHK18DfOSH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9744"}}, {tmdbId:"11537", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, Ile-de-France, France", imdbId:"0847851", born:date('1883-05-06'), name:"Odette Talazac", bio:"Odette Talazac was the daughter of tenor Jean-Alexandre Talazac and his wife, the soprano Hélène Fauvelle.  She began her career singing in music halls before turning to the theater and cinema.  She was married in 1900 in Chatou to jeweler Georges Aucoc.   She died on March 29, 1948 in Paris...", died:date('1948-03-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tm3f7ix1HiY2xCowmDPCXe0yl9h.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11537"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"14966", properties:{bornIn:"Flagstaff, Arizona, USA", imdbId:"0222596", born:date('1905-10-07'), name:"Andy Devine", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAndrew Vabre \"Andy\" Devine (October 7, 1905 – February 18, 1977) was an American character actor known for his distinctive raspy, crackly voice and roles in Western films. \n\nHe is probably best remembered for his role as Cookie, the sidekick of Roy Rogers in ten feature films.  He also appeared alongside John Wayne in films like Stagecoach (1939), The Man Who Shot Liberty Valance, and How the West Was Won (both 1962)...", died:date('1977-02-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2U0KIVdWCbNMFLhCnpB5568eMrU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14966"}}, {tmdbId:"8516", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001017", born:date('1906-02-05'), name:"John Carradine", bio:"John Carradine (1906–1988) was an American actor, best known for his roles in horror films, Westerns, and Shakespearean theatre. \n\nCarradine's first film credit was Tol'able David.  By 1933, he was being credited as John Peter Richmond.  He adopted the stage name \"John Carradine\" in 1935, and legally took the name as his own two years later. \n\nBy 1936, Carradine had become a member of John Ford's stock company and appeared in The Prisoner of Shark Island...", died:date('1988-11-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cUlQO0vGGFoF3VZjzok8U276exY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8516"}}, {tmdbId:"235632", properties:{imdbId:"0725844", name:"Martin Good Rider", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mHSEW7eFlSjljuj5zijflxXO81t.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/235632"}}, {tmdbId:"94936", properties:{bornIn:"Freidorf, Austria-Hungary [now Timisoara, Timis County, Romania]", imdbId:"0919321", born:date('1904-06-02'), name:"Johnny Weissmuller", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJohnny Weissmuller (born Johann Peter Weißmüller; June 2, 1904 – January 20, 1984) was an Austro-Hungarian-born American swimmer and actor.  Weissmuller was one of the world's best swimmers in the 1920s, winning five Olympic gold medals and one bronze medal.  He won fifty-two US National Championships and set sixty-seven world records.  After his swimming career, he became the sixth actor to portray Tarzan in films, a role he played in twelve motion pictures...", died:date('1984-01-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vDLtAiCXw12vqnK9LhVzBA9uUsb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94936"}}, {tmdbId:"101740", properties:{bornIn:"Pasadena, California, USA", imdbId:"0790788", born:date('1931-04-11'), name:"Johnny Sheffield", bio:"Johnny Sheffield (born John Matthew Sheffield Cassan) was an American child, teen, and young-adult actor, his screen career lasting from 1938 to 1955. \n\nIn 1938, Sheffield became a child star after he was cast in the juvenile lead of a West Coast production of the highly successful Broadway play On Borrowed Time, which starred Dudley Digges and featured Victor Moore as Gramps.  Sheffield played the role of Pud, a long role for a child...", died:date('2010-10-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lBpyntAmFpp1Wf9OpCnlk6qLCJu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101740"}}, {tmdbId:"81970", properties:{bornIn:"Manhattan, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0002092", born:date('1913-03-04'), name:"John Garfield", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJohn Garfield (born Jacob Julius Garfinkle, March 4, 1913 – May 21, 1952) was an American actor who played brooding, rebellious, working-class characters.  He grew up in poverty in Depression-era New York City.  In the early 1930s, he became a member of the Group Theater.  In 1937, he moved to Hollywood, eventually becoming one of Warner Bros. ' stars.  Called to testify before the U. S...", died:date('1952-05-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/f0OMA5i7YCYuHrmgy13BypChCg3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81970"}}, {tmdbId:"9066", properties:{bornIn:"Grand Rapids, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0000023", born:date('1922-06-10'), name:"Judy Garland", bio:"Judy Garland (1922–1969) was an American actress and singer.   After appearing in vaudeville with her sisters, Garland was signed to Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer.  There she made more than two dozen films, including nine with Mickey Rooney and The Wizard of Oz.  After fifteen years, Garland was released from the studio but gained renewed success through concert appearances and later a return to acting...", died:date('1969-06-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mfsGFy3JemDL85XcMYuo5RBNR6R.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9066"}}, {tmdbId:"9068", properties:{bornIn:"Boston, Massachusetts, U.S", imdbId:"0001961", born:date('1904-01-10'), name:"Ray Bolger", bio:"Ray Bolger began his career in vaudeville.  He was half of a team called \"Sanford and Bolger\" and also did numerous Broadway shows on his own.  He, like Gene Kelly, was a song-and-dance man as well as an actor.  He was signed to a contract with MGM in 1936 and his first role was as himself in The Great Ziegfeld (1936).  This was soon followed by a role opposite Eleanor Powell in Rosalie (1937)...", died:date('1987-01-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/43GZ1i6m905Q0r0qe99lgUUPX5O.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9068"}}, {tmdbId:"9069", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, United States", imdbId:"0481618", born:date('1895-08-13'), name:"Bert Lahr", bio:"Bert Lahr (born Irving Lahrheim; August 13, 1895 – December 4, 1967) was an American actor and comedian.  Lahr is remembered today for his roles as the Cowardly Lion and the farmworker Zeke in the 1939 movie The Wizard of Oz, but was also well-known for work in burlesque, vaudeville, and on Broadway. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Bert Lahr, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1967-12-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3yAOM7NNlxxbIAErFgoPEBJEB9T.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9069"}}, {tmdbId:"88867", properties:{bornIn:"Montreal, Quebec, Canada", imdbId:"0790454", born:date('1902-08-10'), name:"Norma Shearer", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEdith Norma Shearer (August 10, 1902 – June 12, 1983) was a Canadian-American actress.  Shearer was one of the most popular actresses in North America from the mid-1920s through the 1930s.  Her early films cast her as the girl next door, but for most of the Pre-Code film era, beginning with the 1930 film The Divorcee, for which she won an Oscar for Best Actress, she played sexually liberated women in sophisticated contemporary comedies...", died:date('1983-06-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5ID9vKsFSTVlNPmfB6vMewOffUW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88867"}}, {tmdbId:"30233", properties:{bornIn:"Waterbury, Connecticut, USA", imdbId:"0751426", born:date('1907-06-04'), name:"Rosalind Russell", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRosalind Russell (June 4, 1907 – November 28, 1976) was an American actress of stage and screen, perhaps best known for her role as a fast-talking newspaper reporter in the Howard Hawks screwball comedy His Girl Friday, as well as the role of Mame Dennis in the film Auntie Mame.  She won all 5 Golden Globes for which she was nominated, and was tied with Meryl Streep for wins until 2007 when Streep was awarded a sixth...", died:date('1976-11-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hDkFFfVgrC36RnW2MxBbMbMpwdQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30233"}}, {tmdbId:"88870", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0092683", born:date('1880-01-28'), name:"Mary Boland", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMary Boland (January 28, 1882 – June 23, 1965) was an American stage and film actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Mary Boland, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1965-06-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mqQFCk1l04bnqs5prmrDkupVy8B.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88870"}}, {tmdbId:"30225", properties:{bornIn:"Bombay, Bombay Presidency, British India [now Mumbai, Maharashtra, India]", imdbId:"0643353", born:date('1911-02-19'), name:"Merle Oberon", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMerle Oberon (18 February 1911  – 23 November 1979) was an Indian-born British actress. \n\nShe began her film career in British films, and a prominent role, as Anne Boleyn in The Private Life of Henry VIII (1933), brought her attention.  Leading roles in such films as The Scarlet Pimpernel (1934) advanced her career, and she travelled to the United States to make films for Samuel Goldwyn...", died:date('1979-11-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uRc4TzGXojrivskCw37609FcK0i.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30225"}}, {tmdbId:"14261", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0000057", born:date('1910-03-01'), name:"David Niven", bio:"James David Graham Niven (1 March 1910 – 29 July 1983), known as David Niven, was a British actor and novelist, best known for his roles as Phileas Fogg in Around the World in 80 Days and Sir Charles Lytton, a. k. a.  \"the Phantom\", in The Pink Panther.  He was awarded the 1958 Academy Award for Best Actor in Separate Tables...", died:date('1983-07-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ioW2DU6T2HPvTdqUSaLLQmGPb38.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14261"}}, {tmdbId:"30126", properties:{bornIn:"South Shields, (which was then in County Durham), England", imdbId:"0733460", born:date('1902-03-28'), name:"Flora Robson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDame Flora McKenzie Robson, DBE (28 March 1902 – 7 July 1984) was an English actress and star of the theatrical stage and cinema, particularly renowned for her performances in plays demanding dramatic and emotional intensity.  Her range extended from queens to murderesses...", died:date('1984-07-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yLiY0Sk7IMg5O2rUFW70Kpc2DXi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30126"}}, {tmdbId:"13954", properties:{bornIn:"Darby, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0001211", born:date('1880-01-29'), name:"W.C. Fields", died:date('1946-12-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nDkOOGRuLt0bndmtskgY5c993wX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13954"}}, {tmdbId:"13962", properties:{imdbId:"0936755", born:date('1890-01-05'), name:"Cora Witherspoon", died:date('1957-11-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nJ4gg8qKwz61ocOrIW7OOe3u8Rg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13962"}}, {tmdbId:"13964", properties:{imdbId:"0215822", name:"Evelyn Del Rio", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rNVaLuP4vuoJLNqL0AW6FYkuaiZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13964"}}, {tmdbId:"233471", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0831439", born:date('1882-04-18'), name:"Leopold Stokowski", bio:"Leopold Anthony Stokowski (18 April 1882 – 13 September 1977) was an English conductor of Jewish-Polish and Irish descent.  One of the leading and influential conductors of the early and mid-20th Century, he is best known for his long association with the Philadelphia Orchestra and for appearing in the film Fantasia.  He was especially noted for his free-hand conducting style that spurned the traditional baton and for obtaining a characteristically sumptuous sound from the orchestras he directed...", died:date('1977-09-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yQfjAXLKUMwWPwijDBsbs0zIPIS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/233471"}}, {tmdbId:"565402", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0852252", born:date('1885-12-22'), name:"Deems Taylor", died:date('1966-07-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2xyj2fd3jTeqZnzhCQqkOXqqRkm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/565402"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"41245", properties:{bornIn:"Roosevelt, Utah, USA", imdbId:"0206478", born:date('1920-10-13'), name:"Laraine Day", bio:"Laraine Day, born La Raine Johnson, was a major movie star of the 1940s and '50s.  Raised in Utah as part of a prominent Mormon family, she came to Hollywood as a young woman, and made her film debut with an uncredited role in Stella Dallas.  Before she was famous she also played the birth-mother of Tarzan and Jane's adopted son \"Boy\" in Tarzan Finds a Son.  Her break came in 1939, with the wildly popular \"Dr Kildare\" sequels...", died:date('2007-11-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rprHvH9QWqHlFPDfNy0N9RGtvqy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41245"}}, {tmdbId:"3361", properties:{bornIn:"St. Petersburg, Russian Empire [now Russia]", imdbId:"0001695", born:date('1906-07-03'), name:"George Sanders", died:date('1972-04-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vzLXpwttlcYt24YMGbg7KrScb45.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3361"}}, {tmdbId:"103671", properties:{bornIn:"\tNew Orleans, Louisiana, USA", imdbId:"0140865", born:date('1906-07-17'), name:"John Carroll", bio:"John Carroll (July 17, 1906 – April 24, 1979) was an American actor and singer.  He was born Julian Lafaye in New Orleans, Louisiana.   Carroll performed in several small roles in films under his original name until 1935, when he first used the name John Carroll in Hi, Gaucho! He appeared in several Western films in the 1930s, including the role of Zorro in Zorro Rides Again in 1937.  He was the male lead in the Marx Brothers' Western comedy Go West in 1940...", died:date('1979-04-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/b6mIYfSaIuNQfUfivqPhBlXWz3z.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/103671"}}, {tmdbId:"8517", properties:{bornIn:"Xenia, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0335788", born:date('1869-12-20'), name:"Charley Grapewin", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nCharles Ellsworth Grapewin (December 20, 1869 – February 2, 1956) was an American vaudeville performer, writer and a stage and silent and sound actor, and comedian who was best known for portraying Aunt Em's husband, Uncle Henry in Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer's The Wizard of Oz (1939) as well as Grandpa Joad in The Grapes of Wrath (1940) and Jeeter Lester in Tobacco Road (1941)...", died:date('1956-02-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uPBFR5aayuPJOlSVBAOMSsLdan4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8517"}}, {tmdbId:"14028", properties:{bornIn:"Sedalia, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0642988", born:date('1903-11-12'), name:"Jack Oakie", bio:"Jack Oakie (November 12, 1903 – January 23, 1978) was an American actor, starring mostly in films, but also working on stage, radio and television...", died:date('1978-01-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9oWdEicbTjfpfiCtvvYuxi0UseU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14028"}}, {tmdbId:"14029", properties:{bornIn:"Londra, Regno Unito", imdbId:"0306786", born:date('1903-02-27'), name:"Reginald Gardiner", bio:"Reginald Gardiner (27 February 1903 - 7 July 1980) was an English-born actor in film and television and a graduate of the Royal Academy of Dramatic Arts in Britain.  He made his film debut in 1926 in the silent film The Lodger, by Alfred Hitchcock.  Moving to Hollywood, he was cast in numerous roles, often as a British butler.  One of his most famous roles was that of Schultz in Charlie Chaplin's The Great Dictator...", died:date('1980-07-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/A24zNUDwHQrb9HUhu670r6X9xdo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14029"}}, {tmdbId:"10924", properties:{bornIn:"Barnes, Surrey, UK", imdbId:"0199787", born:date('1894-03-05'), name:"Henry Daniell", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nCharles Henry Daniell (5 March 1894 – 31 October 1963) was an English actor who had a long and prestigious career on stage as well as in films.  He is perhaps best known for his villainous roles in films like The Great Dictator, The Philadelphia Story and The Sea Hawk.  Daniell was given few opportunities to play a 'good guy', including a supporting part as Franz Liszt in the biographical film Song of Love (1947).  His last name is sometimes spelled \"Daniel\"...", died:date('1963-10-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8eODn1AnmZZ2OYAQfPVxY7lbQbx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10924"}}, {tmdbId:"82382", properties:{bornIn:"Selby, Yorkshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0827263", born:date('1889-04-14'), name:"James Stephenson", bio:"British stage actor James Stephenson made his film debut quite late in life, at the age of 49, in 1937, making four pictures that year.  Warner Bros.  got a glimpse of this distinguished gent and signed him to a contract where he indulged himself in urbane villainy...", died:date('1941-07-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cVJ8AT4lHXBjtyyP5WN91Hmnawx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82382"}}, {tmdbId:"82383", properties:{bornIn:"Edinburgh, Midlothian, Scotland", imdbId:"0408586", born:date('1901-06-29'), name:"Frieda Inescort", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nFrieda Inescort (born Frieda Wrightman, 29 June 1901 – 26 February 1976) was a Scottish-born actress best known for creating the role of Sorel Bliss in Noël Coward's play Hay Fever on Broadway.  She also played the shingled lady in John Galsworthy's 1927 Broadway production Escape. \n\nInescort's acting debut came in The Truth About Blayds (1922), which was presented at the Booth Theatre on Broadway...", died:date('1976-02-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/frPg59773VRgXQKNeAGjEzJlQRD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82383"}}, {tmdbId:"30289", properties:{bornIn:"Dallas, Texas, U.S", imdbId:"0001105", born:date('1923-10-16'), name:"Linda Darnell", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLinda Darnell  (October 16, 1923 – April 10, 1965) was an American film actress.  Darnell was a model as a child, and progressed to theater and film acting as an adolescent.  At the encouragement of her mother, she made her first film in 1939, and appeared in supporting roles in big budget films for 20th Century Fox throughout the 1940s...", died:date('1965-04-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tZ7egse2JFKBIzYhqVoiG9jfAxY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30289"}}, {tmdbId:"102363", properties:{bornIn:"Clinton, Iowa, U.S.", imdbId:"0602955", born:date('1918-10-23'), name:"Peggy Moran", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.  \n\n \n\nPeggy Moran (October 23, 1918 – October 24, 2002) was an American film actress who appeared in films between 1938 and 1943. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Peggy Moran , licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2002-10-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3g7vMfcY9yQpcAlf2TlF0nr5ih6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/102363"}}, {tmdbId:"16761", properties:{imdbId:"0161862", born:date('1889-08-30'), name:"Eduardo Ciannelli", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nEduardo Ciannelli, sometimes credited as Edward Ciannelli, (30 August 1889 - 8 October 1969), was an Italian baritone and character actor with a long career in American films, mostly playing gangsters and criminals. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Eduardo Ciannelli, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1969-10-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eiDBc4v8xrRhkaIpXEu9ZNViAiB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16761"}}, {tmdbId:"33747", properties:{bornIn:"Saqqajja Square, Rabat, Malta", imdbId:"0130407", born:date('1897-08-04'), name:"Joseph Calleia", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJoseph Calleia (August 4, 1897 – October 31, 1975), was a Maltese born American singer, composer, and actor, both on Broadway and in film.  Calleia played opposite some Hollywood greats, including John Wayne, William Holden, Errol Flynn, Rita Hayworth, Mae West, Bette Davis, Jane Russell, Mario Lanza, Charlton Heston, Dean Martin and Jerry Lewis, Orson Welles, Tyrone Power, Alan Ladd and Anthony Quinn...", died:date('1975-10-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/h4PyptE7clC6RNpKSUyLG4YZEJK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33747"}}, {tmdbId:"8252", properties:{bornIn:"O'Fallon, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0000034", born:date('1918-04-17'), name:"William Holden", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia William Holden (April 17, 1918 – November 12, 1981) was an American actor.  Holden won the Academy Award for Best Actor in 1953 and the Emmy Award for Best Actor in 1974.  One of the biggest box office draws of the 1950s, he was named one of the \"Top 10 Stars of the Year\" six times (1954–1958, 1961) and appeared on the American Film Institute's AFI's 100 Years…100 Stars list as #25...", died:date('1981-11-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1xYhynSYtesFbXpwRtz05y7znS6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8252"}}, {tmdbId:"10022", properties:{bornIn:"Jamesport, Missouri, U.S.", imdbId:"0779549", born:date('1912-09-22'), name:"Martha Scott", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMartha Ellen Scott (September 22, 1912 – May 28, 2003) was an American actress best known for her roles as mother of the lead character in numerous films and television shows. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Martha Scott, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2003-05-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/z48gWmIbNkVANSkxViuX2dkKf6o.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10022"}}, {tmdbId:"20366", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0047810", born:date('1891-12-07'), name:"Fay Bainter", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nFay Okell Bainter (December 7, 1893 – April 16, 1968) was an American film and stage actress.  She won the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress for Jezebel (1938) and has a star on the Hollywood Walk of Fame.   MGM persuaded her to try films and her movie debut was in This Side of Heaven (February 1934), the same year she appeared in Dodsworth on Broadway and in the film It Happened One Day (July 1934)...", died:date('1968-04-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tPUbXDb4xLAsZ5OUf91FaAijyNk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20366"}}, {tmdbId:"17755", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0094135", born:date('1889-05-03'), name:"Beulah Bondi", bio:"Beulah Bondi (born Beulah Bondy; May 3, 1889 - January 11, 1981) was an American stage, screen, and television actress.  She was twice nominated for a Best Supporting Actress Academy Award.  For a guest appearance on the television series The Waltons she won an Emmy Award...", died:date('1981-01-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eMBdRplrMZfv7xC5FjzfOiOOb3E.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/17755"}}, {tmdbId:"14683", properties:{bornIn:"Providence, Rhode Island, USA", imdbId:"0404046", born:date('1911-10-30'), name:"Ruth Hussey", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRuth Carol Hussey (October 30, 1911 – April 19, 2005) was an American actress best known for her Academy Award-nominated role as photographer Elizabeth Imbrie in The Philadelphia Story. \n\nAfter working as an actress in summer stock, she returned to Providence and worked as a radio fashion commentator on a local station.  She wrote the ad copy for a Providence clothing store and read it on the radio each afternoon...", died:date('2005-04-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1O1PXsuZelrq7OD2pI2UJQJdqRU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14683"}}, {tmdbId:"33923", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0000305", born:date('1908-05-30'), name:"Mel Blanc", bio:"Mel Blanc (May 30, 1908 – July 10, 1989) was an American voice actor and comedian. \n\nAlthough he began his nearly six-decade-long career performing in radio commercials, Blanc is best remembered for his work with Warner Bros.  during the \"Golden Age of American animation\" (and later for Hanna-Barbera television productions) as the voice of such well-known characters as Bugs Bunny, Daffy Duck, Porky Pig, Sylvester the Cat, Tweety Bird, Foghorn Leghorn, Yosemite Sam, Wile E...", died:date('1989-07-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sicAwqCq5PLCj12KlGWFKJLr1Zv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33923"}}, {tmdbId:"67369", properties:{bornIn:"Cincinnati, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0110893", born:date('1904-05-29'), name:"Don Brodie", bio:"Don Brodie was an American stage, screen, and television actor...", died:date('2001-01-08'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67369"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"5463", properties:{bornIn:"Monrovia, California, USA", imdbId:"0201428", born:date('1910-11-07'), name:"Marion Darlington", died:date('1991-03-17'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5463"}}, {tmdbId:"95013", properties:{bornIn:"Sydney, New South Wales, Australia", imdbId:"0039049", born:date('1904-08-12'), name:"Edward Ashley", bio:"Edward Montague Hussey Cooper was an actor descended from an English family but born in Australia.   Known by his professional name Edward Ashley (to avoid confusion with a fellow actor Edward Cooper), Cooper performed in 60 films for Metro Goldwyn Mayer including Pride and Prejudice, in which he played George Wickham.   He made a number of films in the United Kingdom before moving to California in 1940, where his first big role was as George Wickham in Pride and Prejudice...", died:date('2000-05-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qdmt0eSJyoVj1REpnm45ilgjgE4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95013"}}, {tmdbId:"939983", properties:{imdbId:"0483672", born:date('1911-03-16'), name:"Marten Lamont", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dlVtcwESFo9S4ze4gQ0oxMHGTkT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/939983"}}, {tmdbId:"2617002", properties:{name:"E.E. Clive", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/coIEofQiaMTV7wSH1KrqnurHOAM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2617002"}}, {tmdbId:"98964", properties:{imdbId:"0939864", name:"Marjorie Wood", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eA9uQJb62wDJ4TdK6MPmluxOcHL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/98964"}}, {tmdbId:"3362", properties:{bornIn:"Adelaide, South Australia, Australia", imdbId:"0000752", born:date('1897-02-10'), name:"Judith Anderson", bio:"Dame Judith Anderson was born Frances Margaret Anderson on February 10, 1897 in Adelaide, South Australia.  She began her acting career in Australia before moving to New York in 1918.  There she established herself as one of the greatest theatrical actresses and was a major star on Broadway throughout the 1930s, 1940s and 1950s.  Her notable stage works included the role of Lady Macbeth, which she played first in the 1920s, and gave an Emmy Award-winning television performance in Macbeth (1960)...", died:date('1992-01-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1ObiPNEpP1ohD8opYkCInERp2w4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3362"}}, {tmdbId:"24937", properties:{bornIn:"Tacoma, Washington, USA", imdbId:"0001078", born:date('1903-05-03'), name:"Bing Crosby", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nHarry Lillis \"Bing\" Crosby Jr.  (May 3, 1903 – October 14, 1977) was an American singer, comedian and actor.  The first multimedia star, Crosby was a leader in record sales, radio ratings, and motion picture grosses from 1931 to 1954.  His early career coincided with recording innovations that allowed him to develop an intimate singing style that influenced many male singers who followed him, including Perry Como, Frank Sinatra, Dick Haymes, and Dean Martin...", died:date('1977-10-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ydxPEeNPr0vaKZmEZXVNvhav3LB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24937"}}, {tmdbId:"83400", properties:{bornIn:"New Orleans, Louisiana, U.S.", imdbId:"0483787", born:date('1914-12-10'), name:"Dorothy Lamour", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDorothy Lamour (December 10, 1914 – September 22, 1996) was an American film actress.  She is best-remembered for appearing in the Road to. . .  movies, a series of successful comedies co-starring Bob Hope and Bing Crosby. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Dorothy Lamour, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1996-09-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3ZKsWOxec9knAonFzIGDrzC0y1g.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83400"}}, {tmdbId:"82388", properties:{bornIn:"Eltham, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0001362", born:date('1903-05-29'), name:"Bob Hope", bio:"Bob Hope (1903 – 2003) was a British-born American comedian and actor who appeared in vaudeville, on Broadway, and in radio, television and movies. \n\nHe was also noted for his work with the US Armed Forces and his numerous USO shows entertaining American military personnel.  Throughout his career, he was honored for his humanitarian work.  In 1996, the U. S.  Congress honored Bob Hope by declaring him the \"first and only honorary veteran of the U. S.  armed forces...", died:date('2003-07-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mrXRDCgz5Y7YGe8ussvW2ObEqs8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82388"}}, {tmdbId:"2669", properties:{bornIn:"Toronto, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0557339", born:date('1896-08-30'), name:"Raymond Massey", bio:"Raymond Massey was a prominent Canadian/American stage and screen actor...", died:date('1983-07-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nngqXbUPI5dtT10tDJxDAl0f8Pr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2669"}}, {tmdbId:"18802", properties:{bornIn:"Tampico, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0001654", born:date('1911-02-06'), name:"Ronald Reagan", bio:"Ronald Reagan (1911–2004) was the 40th President of the United States (1981–1989), the 33rd Governor of California (1967–1975) and prior to that an actor. \n\nUpon his college graduation, Reagan first moved to Iowa to work as a radio broadcaster and then in 1937 to Los Angeles, California.  He began a career as an actor appearing in over fifty movie productions.  Some of his most notable roles are in Knute Rockne, All American and Kings Row...", died:date('2004-06-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hz4anVIrSgqFn2ECgviJSqcl6mK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18802"}}, {tmdbId:"14869", properties:{bornIn:"Norfolk, Virginia, USA", imdbId:"0837925", born:date('1909-05-16'), name:"Margaret Sullavan", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMargaret Brooke Sullavan (May 16, 1909 – January 1, 1960; studio publicity incorrectly reported her year of birth as 1911) was an American stage and film actress.  Sullavan started her career on the stage in 1929.  In 1933 she caught the attention of movie director John M.  Stahl and had her debut on the screen that same year in Only Yesterday. \n\nMargaret Sullavan preferred working on the stage and did only 16 movies...", died:date('1960-01-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8DAArOiIWxsCNmFQJVof2btqEEK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14869"}}, {tmdbId:"3152", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0706368", born:date('1895-09-26'), name:"George Raft", bio:"George Raft (born George Ranft; September 26, 1901 – November 24, 1980) was an American film actor and dancer identified with portrayals of gangsters in crime melodramas of the 1930s and 1940s.  A stylish leading man in dozens of movies, today Raft is mostly known for his gangster roles in the original Scarface (1932), Each Dawn I Die (1939), and Billy Wilder's 1959 comedy Some Like It Hot, as a dancer in Bolero (1934), and a truck driver in They Drive by Night (1940)...", died:date('1980-11-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fuKfrJHsCW3dvCPN8M0BjZ4DdPk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3152"}}, {tmdbId:"83477", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0276065", born:date('1917-11-04'), name:"Virginia Field", died:date('1992-01-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aaQp52i6bvivilPOv7wqELd0SVG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83477"}}, {tmdbId:"94803", properties:{bornIn:" San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0553149", born:date('1913-12-25'), name:"Tony Martin", bio:"Alvin Morris, known professionally as Tony Martin, was an American actor and popular singer.  His career spanned over seven decades, and he scored dozens of hits between the late-1930s and mid-1950s with songs such as \"Walk Hand in Hand\", \"Stranger in Paradise\" and \"I Get Ideas\".  He was married to actress and dancer Cyd Charisse for 60 years, from 1948 until her death in 2008. \n\nIn his grammar school glee club, he became an instrumentalist and singer...", died:date('2012-07-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qKsFTry1dp8So4EZagXBT58Rkx7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94803"}}, {tmdbId:"7664", properties:{bornIn:"Petersburg, Virginia, USA", imdbId:"0001072", born:date('1905-05-15'), name:"Joseph Cotten", bio:"Joseph Cheshire Cotten (May 15, 1905 – February 6, 1994) was an American actor of stage and film.  Cotten achieved prominence on Broadway, starring in the original productions of The Philadelphia Story and Sabrina Fair.  He is associated with Orson Welles, leading to appearances in Citizen Kane (1941), The Magnificent Ambersons (1942), Journey into Fear (1943), for which Cotten was also credited with the screenplay, and The Third Man (1949)...", died:date('1994-02-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/djfCB0jPOgmq3w7RD3BMLzWsAu8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7664"}}, {tmdbId:"11029", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0173827", born:date('1913-08-24'), name:"Dorothy Comingore", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMary Louise Comingore, best known professionally as Dorothy Comingore (August 24, 1913 – December 30, 1971), was an American film actress.  She is best known for starring as Susan Alexander Kane in Citizen Kane (1941), the critically acclaimed debut film of Orson Welles.  In earlier films she was credited as Linda Winters, and she had appeared on the stage as Kay Winters.  Her career ended when she was caught up in the Hollywood blacklist...", died:date('1971-12-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oZCewbT89apDCvHvMHxYs9n8Llc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11029"}}, {tmdbId:"11025", properties:{bornIn:"Clinton, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0001547", born:date('1900-12-06'), name:"Agnes Moorehead", bio:"Agnes Robertson Moorehead (December 6, 1900 – April 30, 1974) was an American actress.  Although she began with the Mercury Theatre, appeared in more than seventy films beginning with Citizen Kane and on dozens of television shows during a career that spanned more than thirty years, Moorehead is most widely known to modern audiences for her role as the witch Endora in the series Bewitched...", died:date('1974-04-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kckvDNzGhillNhWtasYePSFJEKs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11025"}}, {tmdbId:"11026", properties:{bornIn:"Saint Joseph, Missouri, U.S.", imdbId:"0913095", born:date('1915-06-29'), name:"Ruth Warrick", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDame Ruth Elizabeth Warrick (June 29, 1916 – January 15, 2005), DM, was a long-time American singer, Hollywood Golden-Age actress and political activist, best known for her role as Phoebe Tyler on All My Children, which she played regularly from 1970 until her death in 2005. \n\nShe celebrated her 80th birthday by attending a special screening of Citizen Kane to a packed, standing-room-only audience, to which she spoke afterward...", died:date('2005-01-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tcSwLMrFZDfak0kcGGXIcR0MBeO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11026"}}, {tmdbId:"4111", properties:{bornIn:"Stockholm, Sweden", imdbId:"0000006", born:date('1915-08-29'), name:"Ingrid Bergman", bio:"Ingrid Bergman (29 August 1915 – 29 August 1982) was a Swedish actress who starred in a variety of European and American films.  She won three Academy Awards, two Emmy Awards, and the Tony Award for Best Actress.  She is ranked as the fourth greatest female star of American cinema of all time by the American Film Institute...", died:date('1982-08-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/x6LOGUWNHH3pRO8gOup68xPJL46.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4111"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"29623", properties:{bornIn:"Wallace, Idaho, USA", imdbId:"0001805", born:date('1921-02-08'), name:"Lana Turner", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLana Turner (February 8, 1921 – June 29, 1995) was an American actress.  Discovered and signed to a film contract by MGM at the age of sixteen, Turner first attracted attention in They Won't Forget (1937).  She played  featured roles, often as the ingenue, in such films as Love Finds Andy Hardy (1938)...", died:date('1995-06-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fidHU5kJmjAjWATXCdj44DGpjNU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29623"}}, {tmdbId:"535025", properties:{bornIn:"Indianapolis, Indiana[", imdbId:"0059934", born:date('1904-02-16'), name:"James Baskett", bio:"James Baskett was born on February 16, 1904 in Indianapolis, Indiana.  He was an actor, known for Song of the South (1946), Policy Man (1938) and Gone Harlem (1938).  He was married to Margaret.  He died on July 9, 1948 in Los Angeles, California...", died:date('1948-07-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vYYM7vog8eE1kLoNkwyDc6GTq6C.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/535025"}}, {tmdbId:"9084", properties:{bornIn:"Frankfurt am Main, Germany", imdbId:"0082884", born:date('1889-03-30'), name:"Herman Bing", bio:"Herman Bing was a German born character actor and voice actor...", died:date('1947-01-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/c5iPC1oUMmFMXsM8qjYeYOs6P75.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9084"}}, {tmdbId:"31771", properties:{bornIn:"Lancaster, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0088285", born:date('1894-09-24'), name:"Billy Bletcher", bio:"The diminutive (5 feet 2 inches/1. 57 meters) Bletcher appeared on-screen in films and later television from the 1910s to the 1970s, including appearances in several Our Gang and Three Stooges comedies. Bletcher was also famous as a voice actor.  Uncharacteristically for someone of his size, his voice was a deep and strong-sounding baritone...", died:date('1979-01-05'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31771"}}, {tmdbId:"32437", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0112395", born:date('1895-02-27'), name:"Edward Brophy", bio:"Edward Brophy was an American character actor, voice artist, and comedian.  Small of build, balding, and raucous-voiced, he frequently portrayed dumb cops and gangsters, both serious and comic. \n\nHe is best remembered for his roles in the Falcon film series and for voicing Timothy Q.  Mouse in Dumbo. \n\nHis screen debut was in Yes or No.  He appeared in The Champ, Freaks, The Thin Man, The Thin Man Goes Home (1944).  He also made several appearances in the films of director John Ford...", died:date('1960-05-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gxAnTjS7tnVOFdhUjkWYcsdXhWm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32437"}}, {tmdbId:"1003178", properties:{imdbId:"0313582", name:"Richard George", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1003178"}}, {tmdbId:"96994", properties:{bornIn:"Halifax, Yorkshire", imdbId:"0692439", born:date('1901-07-13'), name:"Eric Portman", bio:"Eric Portman (13 July 1901, Akroydon, Halifax, West Riding of Yorkshire - 7 December 1969, St Veep, Cornwall) was a distinguished English stage and film actor.  He is probably best remembered for his roles in several films for Michael Powell and Emeric Pressburger during the 1940s. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Eric Portman , licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1969-12-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/37W0YteueUf1Y6xUlJj0zmftcHB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96994"}}, {tmdbId:"115376", properties:{bornIn:"Montréal, Québec, Canada", imdbId:"0522577", born:date('1900-04-13'), name:"Raymond Lovell", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Raymond Lovell (13 April 1900 - 1 October 1953) was a Canadian-born film actor who performed in British produced films.  He mainly played supporting roles, and was often seen as slightly pompous characters.  After a short marriage to Tamara Desni which ended in a divorce, Lovell found love with Margot Ruddock, an actress, singer and poet and they had a daughter, Simone Lovell...", died:date('1953-10-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8kjIm2fcEKjU41wOKQy0FEiczy8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/115376"}}, {tmdbId:"93163", properties:{bornIn:"Dublin, Ireland", imdbId:"0532277", born:date('1913-03-29'), name:"Niall MacGinnis", bio:"Niall MacGinnis was an Irish actor who made around 80 screen appearances...", died:date('1977-01-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zjkPWbcoJibyn5Rwknm0XRuJYeY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/93163"}}, {tmdbId:"83253", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0193232", born:date('1909-07-24'), name:"Alan Curtis", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAlan Curtis (July 24, 1909 - February 2, 1953) was an American film actor appearing in over 50 films. \n\nBorn Harry Ueberroth in Chicago, Illinois, he began his career as a model before becoming an actor, appearing in local newspaper ads.  His looks did not go unnoticed in Hollywood...", died:date('1953-02-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3EK6qYoGejw6ctRzlSx0BAEC0VW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83253"}}, {tmdbId:"11128", properties:{bornIn:"Worcester, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0447913", born:date('1914-02-17'), name:"Arthur Kennedy", bio:"John Arthur Kennedy (February 17, 1914 – January 5, 1990) was an American stage and film actor known for his versatility in supporting film roles and his ability to create \"an exceptional honesty and naturalness on stage\", especially in the original casts of Arthur Miller plays on Broadway.  He won the 1949 Tony Award for Best Featured Actor in a Play for Miller's Death of a Salesman...", died:date('1990-01-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kFAsXBARq2MhWLW7FzGxqtubZlZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11128"}}, {tmdbId:"12308", properties:{bornIn:"Saint John, New Brunswick, Canada", imdbId:"0682074", born:date('1897-09-23'), name:"Walter Pidgeon", bio:"Walter Davis Pidgeon (September 23, 1897 – September 25, 1984) was a Canadian actor who lived most of his adult life in the United States.  He starred in many motion pictures, including Mrs.  Miniver, The Bad and the Beautiful, Forbidden Planet, Advise and Consent and Funny Girl...", died:date('1984-09-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6qSsi9m4eYD4QxLhei08DjpW3Ck.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12308"}}, {tmdbId:"18803", properties:{bornIn:"Walters, Oklahoma, USA", imdbId:"0001336", born:date('1910-12-13'), name:"Van Heflin", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEmmett Evan \"Van\" Heflin, Jr.  (December 13, 1910 – July 23, 1971) was an American film and theatre actor.  He played mostly character parts over the course of his film career, but during the 1940s had a string of roles as a leading man.  He won the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor for his performance in Johnny Eager (1942). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Van Heflin, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1971-07-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kbAT9HlIHYPRLEdeGYRD2HGblk6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18803"}}, {tmdbId:"7663", properties:{bornIn:"Manhattan, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0942863", born:date('1918-10-27'), name:"Teresa Wright", bio:"Teresa Wright (October 27, 1918 – March 6, 2005) was an American actress. \n\nHer first Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress nomination came in 1941 for her debut work in The Little Foxes.  She received the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress in 1942 for her performance in Mrs.  Miniver.  That same year, she received an Academy Award for Best Actress nomination for her performance in Pride of the Yankees opposite Gary Cooper...", died:date('2005-03-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1J7IOy7S8krsTK22agsFLm2dYXU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7663"}}, {tmdbId:"67685", properties:{bornIn:"Albert Lea, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0137999", born:date('1912-04-30'), name:"Richard Carlson", bio:"Richard Dutoit Carlson (April 29, 1912 – November 25, 1977) was an American actor, television and film director, and screenwriter...", died:date('1977-11-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sN3qLfctzChKjOLDuleWJEbugO0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67685"}}, {tmdbId:"14450", properties:{bornIn:"Patten, Maine, U.S.", imdbId:"0313438", born:date('1900-09-13'), name:"Gladys George", bio:"Gladys George was an American actress. \n\nGeorge went on the stage at the age of 3 and toured the United States, appearing with her parents.  She starred on stage in the 1920s, although she had made several films in the early part of that decade.  She starred in Personal Appearance, a comedy by Lawrence Riley.  This role was reprised by Mae West in the classic film, Go West, Young Man, which West adapted from the play...", died:date('1954-12-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uvRwnNvXitEF7IW4diA26Y7IJcv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14450"}}, {tmdbId:"93123", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0941253", born:date('1888-08-17'), name:"Monty Woolley", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMonty Woolley (August 17, 1888 – May 6, 1963) was an American stage, film, radio, and television actor.  At the age of 50, he achieved a measure of stardom for his best-known role in the stage play and 1942 film The Man Who Came to Dinner.  His distinctive white beard was his trademark...", died:date('1963-05-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/a6eZUY568tOA9UfE0Fdgz9iaXSo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/93123"}}, {tmdbId:"84634", properties:{imdbId:"0871432", born:date('1913-04-17'), name:"Richard Travis", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRichard Travis (born William Benton Justice, April 17, 1913 – July 11, 1989) was an American actor in films and television. \n\nThe son of William Justice and Ella Justice, née Spain, he was born in Carlsbad, New Mexico and grew up in Paragould, Arkansas.  His father owned and operated a marble yard in Paragould. \n\nTravis began his Hollywood career in 1930s action films...", died:date('1989-07-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yrTujfazJzokubJk7jhMpXBjkpD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/84634"}}, {tmdbId:"4302", properties:{bornIn:"Lynn, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0000974", born:date('1894-07-25'), name:"Walter Brennan", bio:"In many ways the most successful and familiar character actor of  American sound films and the only actor to date to win three Oscars for  Best Supporting Actor, Walter Brennan attended college in Cambridge,  Massachusetts, studying engineering.  While in school he became  interested in acting and performed in school plays.  He worked some in  vaudeville and also in various jobs such as clerking in a bank and as a  lumberjack...", died:date('1974-09-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wgY4WHuM65nZ5Dg5Cwl9GcCCruc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4302"}}, {tmdbId:"2672", properties:{bornIn:"Carman, Manitoba, Canada", imdbId:"0007217", born:date('1910-10-27'), name:"Jack Carson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJohn Elmer \"Jack\" Carson (October 27, 1910 – January 2, 1963) was a Canadian-born, American film actor, with a film career spanning the 1930s, 1940s, and 1950s.  Though he was primarily used in supporting roles for comic relief, his work in films such as Mildred Pierce (1945) and Cat on a Hot Tin Roof (1958) displayed his mastery of \"straight\" dramatic actor roles as well...", died:date('1963-01-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/r1HIeyZoJ67iD0uGKQGRgWqfnc6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2672"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"101991", properties:{bornIn:"Buffalo, New York, USA", imdbId:"0419849", born:date('1926-04-14'), name:"Gloria Jean", bio:"Gloria Jean (born Gloria Jean Schoonover,) was an American actress and singer who starred or co-starred in  films from 1939-1959, and made numerous radio, television, stage, and nightclub appearances.  She is probably best rememberedfor her appearance with W. C.  Fields in the film Never Give a Sucker an Even Break...", died:date('2018-08-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8vbHXGIkxwX1nPudch8blbyhNyk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101991"}}, {tmdbId:"100769", properties:{imdbId:"0259816", born:date('1881-07-03'), name:"Leon Errol", died:date('1951-10-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/seoOrNsz48L4pIoKy6BpKUbY5OQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100769"}}, {tmdbId:"101992", properties:{imdbId:"0501886", born:date('1930-12-14'), name:"Billy Lenhart", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101992"}}, {tmdbId:"30512", properties:{bornIn:"Humansville, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0118000", born:date('1903-03-20'), name:"Edgar Buchanan", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEdgar Buchanan (March 20, 1903 – April 4, 1979) was an American actor with a long career in both film and television, most familiar today as Uncle Joe Carson from the Petticoat Junction, Green Acres and Beverly Hillbillies television sitcoms of the 1960s.  As Uncle Joe, he took over as proprietor of the Shady Rest Hotel following the death of Bea Benaderet, who had played Kate Bradley...", died:date('1979-04-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zKcqHZrqVsS0N4kdnqaD8vdOINI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30512"}}, {tmdbId:"30269", properties:{bornIn:"Detroit, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0504125", born:date('1925-01-26'), name:"Joan Leslie", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJoan Leslie (born Joan Agnes Theresa Sadie Brodel; January 26, 1925 – October 12, 2015) was an American actress, dancer, and vaudevillian who, during the Hollywood Golden Age, appeared in such films as High Sierra, Sergeant York, and Yankee Doodle Dandy. \n\nJoan Agnes Theresa Sadie Brodel was born on January 26, 1925, in Highland Park, Michigan, the youngest child of John and Agnes Brodel...", died:date('2015-10-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vft5HULa1wnW1dQEWd197XBchs0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30269"}}, {tmdbId:"30272", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, U.S", imdbId:"0864869", born:date('1901-07-14'), name:"George Tobias", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGeorge Tobias (July 14, 1901 – February 27, 1980) was an American character actor. \n\nBorn to a Jewish family in New York, he began his acting career at the Pasadena Playhouse in Pasadena, California.  He then spent several years in theater groups before moving on to Broadway and, eventually, Hollywood...", died:date('1980-02-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8zOQk7ardIOtrYJn4ddGqHyVwqq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30272"}}, {tmdbId:"10411", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0625167", born:date('1917-04-16'), name:"Barry Nelson", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nBarry Nelson (April 16, 1917 – April 7, 2007) was an American actor, noted as the first actor to portray Ian Fleming's secret agent James Bond...", died:date('2007-04-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mPJX312FaIfJXTochCs3g26YcFd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10411"}}, {tmdbId:"17752", properties:{bornIn:"Denison, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0001656", born:date('1921-01-27'), name:"Donna Reed", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDonna Reed (born Donna Belle Mullenger; January 27, 1921 – January 14, 1986) was an American film and television actress and producer.  Her career spanned more than 40 years, with performances in more than 40 films.  She is well known for her role as Mary Hatch Bailey in Frank Capra's 1946 film It's a Wonderful Life.  In 1953 she received the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress for her performance as Lorene Burke in the war drama From Here to Eternity...", died:date('1986-01-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/l5Djv58sAIA5ODWI4FwYGp8CrkU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/17752"}}, {tmdbId:"79245", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000043", born:date('1919-11-14'), name:"Veronica Lake", bio:"Veronica Lake (November 14, 1922 – July 7, 1973) was an American film actress and pin-up model.  She received both popular and critical acclaim, most notably for her role in Sullivan's Travels and her femme fatale roles in film noir with Alan Ladd during the 1940s, and was well-known for her peek-a-boo hairstyle.  Her success did not last; she had a string of broken marriages and long struggles with mental illness and alcoholism until she died of hepatitis...", died:date('1973-07-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hTbDKSKiCj8fUNTaOJdUPWwvBHh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/79245"}}, {tmdbId:"33007", properties:{bornIn:"Sacramento, California, USA", imdbId:"0913094", born:date('1878-10-09'), name:"Robert Warwick", bio:"Robert Warwick (born Robert Taylor Bien) was an American stage, screen, and television actor.  He appeared in over 200 films during the 1914 through 1959 span of years.  Warwick's television career (which began in 1949) continued to 1962...", died:date('1964-06-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yuyAwJFZu4ibocJ5LGGCedKpIJZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33007"}}, {tmdbId:"21510", properties:{bornIn:"St. Paul, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0218131", born:date('1892-02-27'), name:"William Demarest", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Carl William Demarest (February 27, 1892 – December 27, 1983) was an American character actor, known for playing Uncle Charley in My Three Sons.  A veteran of World War I, Demarest became a prolific film and television actor, appearing in over 140 films, beginning in 1926 and ending in the 1970s.  He frequently played crusty but good-hearted roles...", died:date('1983-12-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vWaJnQ9OuRIw2sI515PA80HD9xj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21510"}}, {tmdbId:"76974", properties:{bornIn:"Aitkin, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0929925", born:date('1894-12-02'), name:"Warren William", bio:"Warren William (born Warren William Krech; 2 December 1894 - 24 September 1948) was an American stage, screen, and radio actor, popular as a film leading man during the early 1930s, and later nicknamed the \"King of Pre-Code\".  He is best remembered for portraying amoral businessmen, lawyers, and other heartless types...", died:date('1948-09-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9ujhjRcVijJOvcGdxcHyJP8Upik.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/76974"}}, {tmdbId:"89670", properties:{bornIn:"Ulverston, Lancashire, England, UK", imdbId:"0491048", born:date('1890-06-16'), name:"Stan Laurel", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nStan Laurel (born Arthur Stanley Jefferson, 16 June 1890 – 23 February 1965) was an English comic actor, writer, and film director who was part of the comedy duo Laurel and Hardy.  He appeared with his comedy partner Oliver Hardy in 107 short films, feature films, and cameo roles...", died:date('1965-02-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eT15ERUT5T3CVyf2a9JD1VAzC6q.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89670"}}, {tmdbId:"78057", properties:{bornIn:"Harlem, Georgia, USA", imdbId:"0001316", born:date('1892-01-18'), name:"Oliver Hardy", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nOliver Norvell Hardy (born Norvell Hardy, January 18, 1892 – August 7, 1957) was an American comic actor and one half of Laurel and Hardy, the double act that began in the era of silent films and lasted from 1927 to 1951.  He appeared with his comedy partner Stan Laurel in 107 short films, feature films, and cameo roles.  He was credited with his first film, Outwitting Dad, in 1914.  In some of his early works, he was billed as \"Babe Hardy\"...", died:date('1957-08-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/byzeG5z2HRMajhI7ML2zbcSyuvv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78057"}}, {tmdbId:"132838", properties:{bornIn:"Copenhagen, Denmark", imdbId:"0200580", born:date('1883-10-03'), name:"Dante", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDante was born Harry August Jansen in Copenhagen, Denmark in 1883.   Jansen's first glimpses of magic were a distance from his home in New York, in Chicago, where, from the galleries of the McVicker's Theatre, he saw the Great Herrmann, rival and later friend of Harry Kellar.  Several illusions were pioneered during Jansen's early career, including \"Sawing a woman in half\" and several of the illusions of his soon to be successors Thurston and Kellar...", died:date('1955-06-15'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/132838"}}, {tmdbId:"120712", properties:{bornIn:"Topeka, Kansas, U.S.", imdbId:"0752846", born:date('1921-06-08'), name:"Sheila Ryan", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nSheila Ryan, (June 8, 1921 – November 4, 1975) was an American actress who starred in over 60 movies. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Sheila Ryan, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1975-11-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9PwiqHQKUPfQScOuUAp0b28eiXh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/120712"}}, {tmdbId:"31702", properties:{bornIn:"Charleroi, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0017013", born:date('1903-12-16'), name:"Hardie Albright", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nHardie Hunter Albright (born Hardie Hunter Albrecht; December 16, 1903 – December 7, 1975) was an American actor.  He was the child of traveling vaudeville performers and made his stage debut in one of his parents' acts at the age of seven.  His Broadway debut came in 1926. \n\nAlbright was playing the juvenile lead on the stage in The Greeks when a scout from the Fox Company saw him.  He was given a contract and headed for Hollywood...", died:date('1975-12-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qGL5I64xIbXW77eW2lGhatmS78q.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31702"}}, {tmdbId:"31703", properties:{imdbId:"0018755", name:"Stan Alexander", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bMQ0GfAXYobGYAWvM198JxkBxgN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31703"}}, {tmdbId:"31704", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California", imdbId:"0066951", born:date('1934-07-04'), name:"Peter Behn", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPeter Behn  (b.  July 4, 1934) is an American voice actor.  He is best known for providing the voice of the young Thumper in the film Bambi...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/y5jHtmdYNmw7zpfyZj94z2ZVg1s.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31704"}}, {tmdbId:"103781", properties:{bornIn:"Marseille, Bouches-du-Rhône, Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur, France", imdbId:"0800386", born:date('1910-04-23'), name:"Simone Simon", bio:"French screen actress Simone Simon's film career spanned the years 1931-1973.  She is best remembered, regarding her English language roles, for the Hollywood films The Devil and Daniel Webster [originally titled All That Money Can Buy] (1941), Cat People (1942), and The Curse of the Cat People (1944).  Simon died in Paris in 2005...", died:date('2005-02-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oo0bjmSaITHbqhAeGObHlCr5mTX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/103781"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"51764", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0808949", born:date('1907-03-19'), name:"Kent Smith", bio:"Kent Smith (born Frank Kent Smith) was an American stage, screen, and television actor. \n\nSmith's early acting experience started in 1925 when he was one of the founders of the famed Harvard \"University Players\", which later included Henry Fonda, James Stewart, Joshua Logan and Margaret Sullavan in Falmouth, Massachusetts.  Smith's stock experience also included productions with the Maryland Theatre in Baltimore.  His professional acting debut was in 1929 in Blind Window in Baltimore, Mayland...", died:date('1985-04-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2GHATvR422EaWU7BkSoj9kbgzt0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/51764"}}, {tmdbId:"48962", properties:{bornIn:"St. Petersburg, Russian Empire [now Russia]", imdbId:"0007218", born:date('1904-09-15'), name:"Tom Conway", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nTom Conway (born Thomas Charles Sanders, 15 September 1904 – 22 April 1967) was a British film, television and radio actor remembered for playing private detectives (including The Falcon, Sherlock Holmes, Bulldog Drummond, and The Saint) and psychiatrists.  He is perhaps best known for playing \"The Falcon\" in ten of the series' entries, taking over for his younger brother, George Sanders, in The Falcon's Brother (1942), in which they both starred...", died:date('1967-04-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4o97uF07BLM6BZ62TGELfUhjq8J.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/48962"}}, {tmdbId:"30114", properties:{bornIn:"Youngstown, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0709905", born:date('1915-10-30'), name:"Jane Randolph", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJane Randolph, born Jane Roemer (October 30, 1915 – May 4, 2009), was an American film actress.  She was born in Youngstown, Ohio and died in Gstaad, Switzerland. \n\nAfter growing up in Kokomo, Indiana, she moved to Hollywood in 1939 in an attempt to start a movie career.  She was eventually picked up by Warner Bros.  and appeared in bit movie roles in 1941...", died:date('2009-05-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cqxm2GndX2gmNllF9RcHsAGWGOH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30114"}}, {tmdbId:"82348", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0446769", born:date('1899-08-09'), name:"Paul Kelly", bio:"Paul Michael Kelly was an American child actor who later as an adult became a stage, film, and television actor...", died:date('1956-11-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6QyN1xPDHiKJ5NxGsw0e8KGeYoi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82348"}}, {tmdbId:"41755", properties:{bornIn:"Portadown, County Armagh, Ireland [now in Northern Ireland], UK", imdbId:"0002046", born:date('1901-02-09'), name:"Brian Donlevy", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nBrian Donlevy  (February 9, 1901 – April 5, 1972) was an Ulster-born American film actor, noted for playing tough guys from the 1930s to the 1960s.  He usually appeared in supporting roles.  Among his best known films are Beau Geste (1939) and The Great McGinty (1940).  For his role as Sergeant Markoff in Beau Geste he was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor...", died:date('1972-04-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/y5GkswX7U1srCMXWJfrGcTokD2s.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41755"}}, {tmdbId:"30510", properties:{bornIn:"Hot Springs, Arkansas USA", imdbId:"0000042", born:date('1913-09-03'), name:"Alan Ladd", bio:"Alan Walbridge Ladd was an American actor and film and television producer.  Ladd found success in film the 1940s and early 1950s, particularly in Westerns and film noirs where he was often paired with Veronica Lake, as she was one of the few Hollywood actresses shorter than he.  His popularity diminished in the late 1950s, though he continued to appear in popular films until his death from cerebral edema in January 1964...", died:date('1964-01-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tAMVLKk0A73RBIvib7QBntutKI8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30510"}}, {tmdbId:"14870", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0335748", born:date('1923-02-02'), name:"Bonita Granville", bio:"Daughter of Bernard 'Bunny' Granville and Rosina Timponi, Bonita Granville was born into an acting family on 2 Febuary 1923, in New York, New York.  It's not surprising that she herself became a child actor, first on the stage and, at the age of 9, debuting in movies in Westward Passage (1932).  She was regularly cast as a naughty little girl, as in These Three (1936) where she played Mary, an obnoxious girl spreading lies about her teachers...", died:date('1988-10-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yHFzyrwDEFnDYY8QzbeBa6tN9SW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14870"}}, {tmdbId:"33022", properties:{bornIn:"Prentice, Wisconsin, USA", imdbId:"0604605", born:date('1908-12-20'), name:"Dennis Morgan", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDennis Morgan (born Earl Stanley Morner, December 20, 1908 – September 7, 1994) was an American actor-singer.  He used the acting pseudonym Richard Stanley before adopting the name under which he gained his greatest fame. \n\nMorgan started working at MGM as Stanley Morner.   His best roles were in Mama Steps Out (1937) and Song of the City (1937), but he mostly did small parts.  Morgan signed with Paramount billed as Richard Stanley...", died:date('1994-09-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lRNp0iYnLhP8A12ZYvTLeOxCwFt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33022"}}, {tmdbId:"87545", properties:{bornIn:"Buhl, Idaho, USA", imdbId:"0721851", born:date('1917-08-12'), name:"Marjorie Reynolds", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMarjorie Reynolds (née Goodspeed; August 12, 1917 – February 1, 1997) was an American film/television actress and dancer, who appeared in more than fifty films. \n\nPerhaps Reynolds' best-known film was Holiday Inn (1942), which introduced the classic song \"White Christmas\".  She performed the song both as a duet with Bing Crosby and later in a solo performance, although her singing was dubbed by Martha Mears.  The movie also showcased her dancing ability...", died:date('1997-02-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kwSKPhNoyqnn5zcqjk8Jq4elPH9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/87545"}}, {tmdbId:"131001", properties:{bornIn:"Charlotte, North Carolina, USA", imdbId:"0197713", born:date('1917-07-01'), name:"Virginia Dale", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nVirginia Dale was an American film actress, who was born Virginia Paxton, in Charlotte, North Carolina.  She appeared in a number of movies in the 1930s and 1940s, including Holiday Inn, and became particularly associated with musicals.   While working as one of the dancing Paxton Sisters in New York City, she was discovered by Darryl F.  Zanuck who signed her to a contract with 20th Century Fox...", died:date('1994-10-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4AGWHKbVrTEd95i3vhsPZfNlHhY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/131001"}}, {tmdbId:"71784", properties:{bornIn:"Karapur, Mysore, Kingdom of Mysore, British India", imdbId:"0754942", born:date('1924-01-27'), name:"Sabu", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nSabu Dastagir (27 January 1924 – 2 December 1963) was a film actor of Indian origin—although he later took American citizenship.  He was normally credited only by his first name, Sabu, and is primarily known for his work in film during the 1940s in Britain and America. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Sabu Dastagir licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1963-12-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4tBtK9Hi4Plns5AP7sjixaWJZat.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71784"}}, {tmdbId:"4119", properties:{bornIn:"Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada", imdbId:"0702798", born:date('1899-12-08'), name:"John Qualen", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJohn Qualen (born Johan Mandt Kvalen, December 8, 1899 – September 12, 1987) was a Canadian-American character actor of Norwegian heritage who specialized in Scandinavian roles. \n\nQualen was born in Vancouver, British Columbia, the son of immigrants from Norway; his father was a Lutheran minister and changed the family's original surname, \"Kvalen\", to \"Qualen\" – though some sources give Oleson, later Oleson Kvalen as Qualen's earlier surnames...", died:date('1987-09-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hBwBXICncxwdTVWRxw5OuGFDeB4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4119"}}, {tmdbId:"89691", properties:{bornIn:"Linguaglossa, Sicily, Italy", imdbId:"0700084", born:date('1892-03-09'), name:"Frank Puglia", bio:"Francesco Giuseppe \"Frank\" Puglia (9 March 1892 – 25 October 1975) was an Italian-American film actor.  He had small, but memorable roles in films including Casablanca (a Moroccan rug merchant), Now, Voyager and The Jungle Book...", died:date('1975-10-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/r1wLNTEnjKEQGrfUB5qzf8RpiCn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89691"}}, {tmdbId:"7125", properties:{bornIn:"Joplin, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0191950", born:date('1910-06-10'), name:"Robert Cummings", bio:"Effective light comedian of '30s and '40s films and '50s and '60s TV series, Robert Cummings was renowned for his eternally youthful looks (which he attributed to a strict vitamin and health-food diet).  He was educated at Carnegie Tech and the American Academy of Dramatic Arts.  Deciding that Broadway producers would be more interested in an upper-crust Englishman than a kid from Joplin, Missouri, Cummings passed himself off as Blade Stanhope Conway, British actor.  The ploy was successful...", died:date('1990-12-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/opnAIsyGG8Tgnr0KyrmHJxkFSxX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7125"}}, {tmdbId:"10606", properties:{bornIn:"Michigan City, Indiana, USA", imdbId:"0000879", born:date('1923-05-07'), name:"Anne Baxter", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAnne Baxter (May 7, 1923 – December 12, 1985) was an American actress, star of Hollywood films, Broadway productions, and television series.  She won an Academy Award and a Golden Globe, and was nominated for an Emmy. \n\nIn 1947, Baxter won the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress for her role as Sophie MacDonald in The Razor's Edge (1946).  In 1951, she received an Academy Award nomination for Best Actress for the title role in All About Eve (1950)...", died:date('1985-12-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mUMKB7ZGzHJ38LpDWnA4VheIGBB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10606"}}, {tmdbId:"14517", properties:{bornIn:"Beverly Hills, California, USA", imdbId:"0392529", born:date('1919-02-05'), name:"Tim Holt", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Tim Holt (February 5, 1918 – February 15, 1973) was an American film actor, perhaps best-known for co-starring in the 1948 film The Treasure of the Sierra Madre. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Tim Holt, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1973-02-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1p5tgRKkoCOXph5ezQnI4uNl4qO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14517"}}, {tmdbId:"7124", properties:{bornIn:"Neath, Glamorgan, Wales, UK", imdbId:"0001537", born:date('1907-01-04'), name:"Ray Milland", bio:"Ray Milland (born Reginald Alfred John Truscott-Jones or Alfred Reginald Jones; 3 January 1907 – 10 March 1986) was a Welsh actor and director.  He is best remembered for his Academy Award–winning portrayal of an alcoholic writer in The Lost Weekend (1945), as well as for his performances in Dial M for Murder (1954) and Love Story (1970)...", died:date('1986-03-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zB7jGIBc6dc3fMqCpXlCDZxQrll.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7124"}}, {tmdbId:"85358", properties:{bornIn:"Worcester, Massachusetts, United States", imdbId:"0426089", born:date('1913-08-13'), name:"Rita Johnson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Rita Johnson (August 13, 1912 – October 31, 1965) was an American actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Rita Johnson, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1965-10-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dMWhm0NpzS1IZPFU9qvrNtrXtQz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85358"}}, {tmdbId:"94433", properties:{bornIn:"Worcester, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0070361", born:date('1889-09-15'), name:"Robert Benchley", bio:"Robert Benchley (September 15, 1889 - November 21, 1945) was an American humorist, a newspaper columnist and an actor...", died:date('1945-11-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/48IbSHrFzcuFBROisAXlKrae7qo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94433"}}, {tmdbId:"33230", properties:{bornIn:"East Chicago, Indiana, USA", imdbId:"0399192", born:date('1914-04-14'), name:"John Hubbard", bio:"John Hubbard (April 14, 1914 – November 6, 1988) was an American television and film actor...", died:date('1988-11-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1wLeZETqU950FkJfYYSAy7AXynz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33230"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"123121", properties:{imdbId:"0461618", born:date('1917-12-14'), name:"Elyse Knox", died:date('2012-02-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4TVDi2XIBFqYtXmOA4WB2WBQsaw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/123121"}}, {tmdbId:"3366", properties:{bornIn:"Chiswick, England, UK", imdbId:"0178066", born:date('1888-12-18'), name:"Gladys Cooper", bio:"Dame Gladys Constance Cooper, DBE (18 December 1888 – 17 November 1971) was an English actress whose career spanned seven decades on stage, in films and on television. \n\nBeginning on the stage as a teenager in Edwardian musical comedy and pantomime, she was starring in dramatic roles and silent films by World War I.  She also became a manager of the Playhouse Theatre from 1917 to 1933, where she played many roles.  Beginning in the early 1920s, Cooper was winning praise in plays by W...", died:date('1971-11-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tfR1RBgPnoAnj7GEjUpYVy5CRRQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3366"}}, {tmdbId:"83452", properties:{bornIn:"Island Pond, Vermont, USA", imdbId:"0884964", born:date('1901-07-28'), name:"Rudy Vallee", bio:"Rudy Vallee started his career as a saxophone player and singer and  later became a band leader.  In the 1920s and early 30s he had a hit  radio program, The Fleishmann's Yeast Hour (where he was hated by his  cast and crew due to his explosive ego-driven personality).  In the early  1930's he was ranked with the likes of Bing Crosby and the tragic Russ Columbo  in the Hit Parade...", died:date('1986-07-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/HtYql5Q8SAfRohzCg3RYswzJIj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83452"}}, {tmdbId:"88960", properties:{bornIn:"Baltimore, Maryland, USA", imdbId:"0751899", born:date('1895-02-06'), name:"Babe Ruth", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGeorge Herman Ruth, Jr.  (February 6, 1895 – August 16, 1948), best known as \"Babe\" Ruth and nicknamed \"the Bambino\" and \"the Sultan of Swat\", was an American Major League baseball player from 1914–1935.  Ruth originally broke into the major leagues with the Boston Red Sox as a starting pitcher, but after he was sold to the New York Yankees in 1919, he converted to a full-time right fielder and subsequently became one of the league's most prolific hitters...", died:date('1948-08-16'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88960"}}, {tmdbId:"33031", properties:{bornIn:"Scheveningen, 's-Gravenhage, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands", imdbId:"0233856", born:date('1901-09-30'), name:"Philip Dorn", bio:"Fritts van Dongen (30 September 1901 – 9 May 1975), born Hein van der Niet and sometimes billed as Philip Dorn, was a Dutch actor who had a career in Hollywood. \n\nDorn was born in Scheveningen, The Hague, South Holland and made his stage debut at age 14 in Dutch productions.  By the 1930s, he was a popular matinee idol and was acting in films...", died:date('1975-05-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/czlpwal7fFnDlQXakDG58gIJKcD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33031"}}, {tmdbId:"84635", properties:{bornIn:"Spokane, Washington, USA", imdbId:"0676688", born:date('1921-07-03'), name:"Susan Peters", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nSusan Peters (born Suzanne Carnahan; July 3, 1921 – October 23, 1952) was an American film, stage, and television actress who appeared in over twenty films over the course of her decade-long career. \n\nIn 1942, the year she signed a contract with Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer (MGM), Peters had a featured role in the Mervyn LeRoy-directed drama Random Harvest...", died:date('1952-10-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oLtK6ykSJoo18MDUgKemfHySS5z.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/84635"}}, {tmdbId:"5401", properties:{bornIn:"Chihuahua, Mexico", imdbId:"0000063", born:date('1915-04-21'), name:"Anthony Quinn", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAnthony Quinn (April 21, 1915 – June 3, 2001) was a Mexican-American actor, as well as a painter and writer.  He starred in numerous critically acclaimed and commercially successful films, including Zorba the Greek, Lawrence of Arabia, The Guns of Navarone, The Message , \" Lion of the Desert\" and Federico Fellini's La strada.  He won the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor twice; for Viva Zapata! in 1952 and Lust for Life in 1956...", died:date('2001-06-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kHMcKl4bzyc43XL1spo79G37jnO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5401"}}, {tmdbId:"2670", properties:{bornIn:"Indianola, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0485509", born:date('1915-06-12'), name:"Priscilla Lane", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nPriscilla Lane (born Priscilla Mullican, June 12, 1915 – April 4, 1995) was an American actress, and the youngest of the Lane Sisters of singers and actresses.  She is best remembered for her roles in the films The Roaring Twenties (1939) co-starring with James Cagney and Humphrey Bogart; Saboteur (1942), an Alfred Hitchcock film in which she plays the heroine, and Arsenic and Old Lace (1944), in which she portrays Cary Grant's fiancée and bride...", died:date('1995-04-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yZaydqhhBySCTQOE4lVU9S07P4k.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2670"}}, {tmdbId:"12156", properties:{bornIn:"East Cleveland, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0062667", born:date('1908-11-19'), name:"Alan Baxter", died:date('1976-05-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4xnz5LWDxvMeSSj2y0cz8q0NA3q.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12156"}}, {tmdbId:"5344", properties:{bornIn:"Fairfield, Connecticut, USA", imdbId:"0000212", born:date('1961-11-19'), name:"Meg Ryan", bio:"Meg Ryan (born Margaret Mary Emily Anne Hyra; November 19, 1961) is an American actress and producer.  She had lead roles in six films, When Harry Met Sally. . . , Sleepless in Seattle, French Kiss, City of Angels, Addicted to Love and You've Got Mail whose total gross was over $870 million worldwide.  In 1995, critic Richard Corliss called her \"the current soul of romantic comedy. \" She had leads in several romantic comedies, including When Harry Met Sally. . ...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bGDMgSAl0Kw0Po1eKujXRNaivGj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5344"}}, {tmdbId:"6968", properties:{bornIn:"Sydney, New South Wales, Australia", imdbId:"0413168", born:date('1968-10-12'), name:"Hugh Jackman", bio:"Hugh Michael Jackman (born 12 October 1968) is an Australian actor and producer who is involved in film, musical theatre, and television.  Jackman has won international recognition for his roles in major films, notably as action/superhero, period and romance characters. \n\nHe is known for his role as Wolverine in the X-Men series, as well as for his leads in Kate & Leopold, Van Helsing, The Prestige, and Australia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bKkbbFMTyQ2EvheAy4SbxbjkjtB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6968"}}, {tmdbId:"33654", properties:{bornIn:"Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0005227", born:date('1974-05-07'), name:"Breckin Meyer", bio:"Breckin Erin Meyer (born May 7, 1974) is an American actor, comedian, writer, producer, and drummer...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7V3hXjmSJXApsuu2aGkEgFFAy03.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33654"}}, {tmdbId:"40202", properties:{bornIn:"Newton Highlands, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0696481", born:date('1918-06-08'), name:"Robert Preston", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRobert Preston (June 8, 1918 – March 21, 1987) was an American stage and film actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Robert Preston (actor), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1987-03-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/geEkOOrrqYXZ6NEj62drfAR8kM0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/40202"}}, {tmdbId:"80726", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0187284", born:date('1913-07-28'), name:"Laird Cregar", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nLaird Cregar (July 28, 1913 – December 9, 1944) was an American film actor. \n\nSamuel Laird Cregar was the youngest of six sons of Edward Matthews Cregar, a cricketer and member of a team called the Gentlemen of Philadelphia.  They toured internationally in the late 1890s and early 1900s.  Laird's mother was the former Elizabeth Smith...", died:date('1944-12-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/x0RC52ecsUWwmnXiC03gjpwQtjJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80726"}}, {tmdbId:"2492", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, United States", imdbId:"0000912", born:date('1894-02-14'), name:"Jack Benny", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Jack Benny (February 14, 1894 – December 26, 1974) was an American comedian, vaudevillian, and actor for radio, television, and film.  Widely recognized as one of the leading American entertainers of the 20th century, Benny played the role of the comic penny-pinching miser, insisting on remaining 39 years old on stage despite his actual age, and often playing the violin badly...", died:date('1974-12-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nHhy8tF4WjGWvAfv0tM2pyl4D6R.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2492"}}, {tmdbId:"2493", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0821041", born:date('1919-01-13'), name:"Robert Stack", bio:"Robert Langford Modini Stack was a multilingual American actor and television host.  In addition to acting in more than 40 films, he also appeared on the television series The Untouchables and later served as the host of Unsolved Mysteries. \n\nBorn in Los Angeles, California, Stack spent his early childhood growing up in Europe.   Becoming fluent in French and Italian at an early age, and he did not learn English until returning to Los Angeles...", died:date('2003-05-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/f1MchlCMVc4LDWEALsodZHPkbIu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2493"}}, {tmdbId:"2494", properties:{bornIn:"Eydtkuhnen, East Prussia, Germany [now Chernyshevskoe, Russia]", imdbId:"0107795", born:date('1892-03-02'), name:"Felix Bressart", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Felix Bressart (March 2, 1892 – March 17, 1949) was a German-American actor of stage and screen. \n\nFelix Bressart (pronounced \"BRESS-ert\") was born in East Prussia, Germany (now part of Russia) and was already a very experienced stage actor when he had his film debut in 1928.  He started off as a supporting actor, e. g.  as the Bailiff in the box-office hit Die Drei von der Tankstelle (1930), but had soon established himself in leading roles of minor movies...", died:date('1949-03-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/x3NDEBpQavuhcV2yFNgm3JK0d5J.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2494"}}, {tmdbId:"30270", properties:{bornIn:"Winthrop, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0926636", born:date('1906-06-04'), name:"Richard Whorf", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Richard Whorf (June 4, 1906 – December 14, 1966) was an American actor, author, director, and designer. \n\nRichard was born in Winthrop, Massachusetts to Harry and Sarah (Lee) Whorf.  Richards's older brother was the well-known American linguist, Benjamin Lee Whorf.  Whorf began his acting career on the Boston stage as a teenager then moving to Broadway when he was 21...", died:date('1966-12-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ljBgWIw0yfARaykmyK6YBKTwBn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30270"}}, {tmdbId:"98570", properties:{bornIn:"Chester, Pennsylvania, U.S.", imdbId:"0914083", born:date('1896-10-31'), name:"Ethel Waters", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEthel Waters (October 31, 1896 – September 1, 1977) was an American blues, jazz and gospel vocalist and actress.  She frequently performed jazz, big band, and pop music, on the Broadway stage and in concerts, although she began her career in the 1920s singing blues...", died:date('1977-09-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6FqqQX50zyoNEotbEUjAvWb0XST.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/98570"}}, {tmdbId:"98571", properties:{bornIn:"Oakland, California, USA", imdbId:"0026655", born:date('1905-09-18'), name:"Eddie 'Rochester' Anderson", bio:"Eddie \"Rochester\" Anderson (1905–1977)  was an American comic actor who became famous playing Rochester, the valet to Jack Benny's eponymous title character on the long-running radio and television series The Jack Benny Program...", died:date('1977-02-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/95DoyaHU01D2kR6AmiFe5axoUK2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/98571"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"92900", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, United States", imdbId:"0395043", born:date('1917-06-30'), name:"Lena Horne", bio:"Lena Horne was (1917-2010) was a singer, dancer, actress, and civil rights activist. \n\nHorne joined the chorus of the Cotton Club at the age of sixteen and became a nightclub performer before moving to Hollywood, where she had small parts in numerous movies, and more substantial parts in the films Cabin in the Sky and Stormy Weather. \n\nDue to the Red Scare and her left-leaning political views, Horne found herself blacklisted and unable to get work in Hollywood...", died:date('2010-05-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mDTgjiRVc0nPALapCSDrlEVvutY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/92900"}}, {tmdbId:"82280", properties:{bornIn:" New Orleans, Louisiana, USA", imdbId:"0001918", born:date('1901-08-04'), name:"Louis Armstrong", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLouis Daniel Armstrong  (August 4, 1901 – July 6, 1971), nicknamed Satchmo or Pops, was an American jazz trumpeter and singer from New Orleans, Louisiana. \n\nComing to prominence in the 1920s as an \"inventive\" cornet and trumpet player, Armstrong was a foundational influence in jazz, shifting the music's focus from collective improvisation to solo performance...", died:date('1971-07-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5CVEC0suCGkLGFoBhYa2RNQHgmJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82280"}}, {tmdbId:"8729", properties:{bornIn:"Washington, District of Columbia, USA", imdbId:"0002118", born:date('1892-02-10'), name:"Alan Hale", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAlan Hale Sr.  (born Rufus Edward Mackahan; February 10, 1892 – January 22, 1950) was an American movie actor and director, most widely remembered for his many supporting character roles, in particular as a frequent sidekick of Errol Flynn, as well as films supporting Lon Chaney, Wallace Beery, Douglas Fairbanks, James Cagney, Clark Gable, Cary Grant, Humphrey Bogart and Ronald Reagan, among dozens of others...", died:date('1950-01-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/e90MwAMkxjDqr3wOnOhDAjvylW5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8729"}}, {tmdbId:"2673", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0725891", born:date('1909-09-06'), name:"John Ridgely", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJohn Ridgely (born John Huntington Rea, September 6, 1909 – January 18, 1968) was an American film character actor with over 175 film credits. \n\nHe appeared in the 1946 Humphrey Bogart film The Big Sleep as blackmailing gangster Eddie Mars and had a memorable role as a suffering heart patient in the film noir Nora Prentiss (1947).  He appeared in a large number of other Warner Bros.  films in the 1930s and 1940s...", died:date('1968-01-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tIekNLaW3MrnD9Xh6e3pW9bJZ64.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2673"}}, {tmdbId:"30719", properties:{bornIn:"Tiflis, Russian Empire [now Tbilisi, Republic of Georgia]", imdbId:"0848667", born:date('1899-10-29'), name:"Akim Tamiroff", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAkim Mikhailovich Tamiroff  (Russian: Аким Михайлович Тамиров; 29 October 1899 – 17 September 1972), Tiflis, Russian Empire (now Tbilisi, Georgia) was an Armenian actor.  He won the first Golden Globe Award for Best Supporting Actor.  He was born of Armenian ethnicity, trained at the Moscow Art Theatre drama school.  He arrived in the US in 1923 on a tour with a troupe of actors and decided to stay...", died:date('1972-09-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uX8oQDIA0N33McsTduwf5qsFdGA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30719"}}, {tmdbId:"99171", properties:{bornIn:"Mérida, Yucatán, Mexico", imdbId:"0194742", born:date('1908-05-08'), name:"Arturo de Córdova", bio:"Arturo de Córdova (born Arturo García Rodríguez; 8 May 1908 – 3 November 1973) was a Mexican film actor.  He made over one hundred films in all. \n\nArturo García Rodríguez was born in Mérida, Yucatán.  Most of Córdova's films were made in Mexico and he became a major motion picture actor in Latin America and Spain winning three Silver Ariel's and received four other nominations...", died:date('1973-11-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4bNiOCwHQ9GKS2m3a7lPUmelVRH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/99171"}}, {tmdbId:"30143", properties:{bornIn:"Budapest, Hungary", imdbId:"0557314", born:date('1910-06-16'), name:"Ilona Massey", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Ilona Massey (born Ilona Hajmássy; June 16, 1910 – August 20, 1974 ) was a film, stage and radio performer. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Ilona Massey, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1974-08-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wy12tcIH6c5fYMf1EsqivgYeT0j.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30143"}}, {tmdbId:"8726", properties:{bornIn:"Horsforth, Yorkshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0461549", born:date('1911-11-11'), name:"Patric Knowles", bio:"Reginald Lawrence Knowles (11 November 1911 – 23 December 1995) was an English film actor who renamed himself Patric Knowles, a name which reflects his Irish descent.  He appeared in films of the 1930s through the 1970s.  He made his film debut in 1933, and played either first or second film leads throughout his career. \n\nIn his first American film, Give Me Your Heart (1936), released in Great Britain as Sweet Aloes, Knowles was cast as a titled Englishman of means...", died:date('1995-12-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4X3rTHSrPXO4iZ6o0ibcQNV2AIW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8726"}}, {tmdbId:"33004", properties:{bornIn:"Pitman, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0288003", born:date('1900-08-24'), name:"Preston Foster", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPreston Foster (August 24, 1900 – July 14, 1970) was an American stage and film actor, and singer.  Foster entered films in 1929 after appearing as a Broadway stage actor.  He was appearing in Broadway plays as late as October 1931 when he acted in a play titled Two Seconds starring Edward J.  Pawley...", died:date('1970-07-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/l46SNs5QMJCK4WhCc8hByfQI1Y3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33004"}}, {tmdbId:"19411", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0634313", born:date('1902-08-11'), name:"Lloyd Nolan", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLloyd Benedict Nolan (August 11, 1902 – September 27, 1985) was an American film and television actor.   Among his many roles, Nolan is remembered for originating the role of private investigator Michael Shayne in a series of 1940s B movies. \n\nNolan was born in San Francisco, California, the son of Margaret and James Nolan, who was a shoe manufacturer of Irish descent...", died:date('1985-09-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6Gd5iklRjRv8kX74NDbIlha7LAS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19411"}}, {tmdbId:"79246", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, United States", imdbId:"0000904", born:date('1906-01-14'), name:"William Bendix", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nWilliam Bendix (January 14, 1906 – December 14, 1964) was an American film, radio, and television actor, best remembered in movies for the title role in the movie The Babe Ruth Story and for portraying clumsily earnest aircraft plant worker Chester A.  Riley in radio and television's The Life of Riley.  He also received an Academy Award nomination as Best Supporting Actor for Wake Island (1942)...", died:date('1964-12-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ayUpuZeOU9XickmaoN01iHVloUP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/79246"}}, {tmdbId:"3090", properties:{bornIn:"Jersey City, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0002017", born:date('1910-03-24'), name:"Richard Conte", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRichard Conte (March 24, 1910 – April 15, 1975) was an American actor.  He appeared in numerous films from the 1940s through 1970s, including I'll Cry Tomorrow and The Godfather...", died:date('1975-04-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pTTzNets0bgWAqx18D7by0hWUea.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3090"}}, {tmdbId:"20124", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000074", born:date('1920-11-19'), name:"Gene Tierney", bio:"Gene Eliza Tierney was an American film and stage actress.  Acclaimed as one of the great beauties of her day, she is best-remembered for her performance in the title role of Laura (1944) and her Academy Award-nominated performance for Best Actress in Leave Her to Heaven (1945).   Other notable roles include Martha Strable Van Cleve in Heaven Can Wait (1943), Isabel Bradley Maturin in The Razor's Edge (1946), Lucy Muir in The Ghost and Mrs...", died:date('1991-11-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/x18cwuOj3gMioswH46I8VsEEYi3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20124"}}, {tmdbId:"13996", properties:{bornIn:"Acton, Indiana, USA", imdbId:"0537685", born:date('1890-02-24'), name:"Marjorie Main", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMarjorie Main (born Mary Tomlinson, February 24, 1890 – April 10, 1975) was an American actress, best known as a Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer contract player and for her role as Ma Kettle in a series of ten Ma and Pa Kettle movies. \n\nMain worked in vaudeville on the Orpheum circuit and in Chautauqua presentations, and debuted on Broadway in 1916.  Her first film was A House Divided in 1931...", died:date('1975-04-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hP0EbMfwCi7GmwnRrNToCzbcWD4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13996"}}, {tmdbId:"97037", properties:{bornIn:"Guthrie Center, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0255199", born:date('1910-05-04'), name:"James Ellison", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJames Ellison (May 4, 1910 - December 23, 1993) was an American actor, born James Ellison Smith in Guthrie Center, Iowa, son of Edward James Smith and Ona Mary Ellis. \n\nEllison appeared in nearly seventy films between 1932 and 1962. \n\nEllison worked for a time in a film laboratory and while there was offered a screen test.  He developed it himself and when he saw it, decided it was not satisfactory so he would not show it to the director...", died:date('1993-12-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zGo5aW6P0SBaPd73XqpDqBpL34J.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/97037"}}, {tmdbId:"95117", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0214168", born:date('1909-11-26'), name:"Frances Dee", bio:"Frances Marion Dee (November 26, 1909 – March 6, 2004) was an American screen and television actress.  She starred opposite Maurice Chevalier in the early talkie musical Playboy of Paris (1930).  She starred in the film An American Tragedy (1931) in a role later recreated by Elizabeth Taylor in the 1951 re-titled remake A Place in the Sun.  She also had a prominent role in the classic 1943 Val Lewton psychological horror film I Walked With a Zombie.  Dee was the wife of Hollywood star Joel McCrea...", died:date('2004-03-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fu9Iorb3U4vfMyR3m4KEttc4YTN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95117"}}, {tmdbId:"97039", properties:{bornIn:"Roxbury, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0057121", born:date('1907-01-19'), name:"Edith Barrett", bio:"Edith Barrett was an American screen actress...", died:date('1977-02-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rwLezxZVA2bGInIVVJIBZUdgN6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/97039"}}, {tmdbId:"7505", properties:{bornIn:"Herne Hill, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0001522", born:date('1928-09-17'), name:"Roddy McDowall", bio:"Roderick Andrew Anthony Jude McDowall (17 September 1928 – 3 October 1998) was an English-American actor, director, and photographer.  He is best known for portraying Cornelius and Caesar in the original Planet of the Apes film series, as well as Galen in the spin-off television series...", died:date('1998-10-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/662lMePzVeUicNvQPXpfq2ezEfN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7505"}}, {tmdbId:"146551", properties:{bornIn:"Glasgow, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0571129", born:date('1911-04-08'), name:"James McKechnie", died:date('1962-05-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lk7fmaFgNDKKVI7vf2m2Hgk4BUR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/146551"}}, {tmdbId:"558443", properties:{imdbId:"0544623", name:"Neville Mapp", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/558443"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"1107072", properties:{bornIn:"Wandsworth, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0391644", born:date('1886-09-22'), name:"Vincent Holman", died:date('1962-04-07'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1107072"}}, {tmdbId:"83907", properties:{bornIn:"Barry, Wales, UK", imdbId:"0515193", born:date('1906-06-25'), name:"Roger Livesey", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRoger Livesey (25 June 1906 – 4 February 1976) was a British stage and film actor.  He is most often remembered for the three Powell &amp; Pressburger films in which he starred: The Life and Death of Colonel Blimp, I Know Where I'm Going! and A Matter of Life and Death.  Tall and broad with a mop of chestnut hair, Livesey used his highly distinctive husky voice, gentle manner and athletic physique to create many notable roles in his theatre and film work...", died:date('1976-02-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3broshB7x5kIKM7MkvM7dCYIwMO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83907"}}, {tmdbId:"78847", properties:{bornIn:"Providence, Rhode Island, U.S.", imdbId:"0248904", born:date('1901-06-29'), name:"Nelson Eddy", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nNelson Ackerman Eddy (June 29, 1901 - March 6, 1967) was an American singer and movie star who appeared in 19 musical films during the 1930s and 1940s, as well as in opera and on the concert stage, radio, television, and in nightclubs.  A classically trained baritone, he is best remembered for the eight films in which he costarred with soprano Jeanette MacDonald...", died:date('1967-03-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vhY2XZrKHZCwLGWRq2RqCcax23.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78847"}}, {tmdbId:"78848", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois", imdbId:"0288078", born:date('1924-12-06'), name:"Susanna Foster", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSuzanne DeLee Flanders Larson (known professionally as Susanna Foster) (6 December 1924 – 17 January 2009) was an American film actress best known for her leading role as Christine in the 1943 film version of The Phantom of the Opera. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Susanna Foster, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2009-01-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/otC0elawgBbiMfBbO6Fj5VMDBtQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78848"}}, {tmdbId:"78849", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0057422", born:date('1907-03-04'), name:"Edgar Barrier", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEdgar Barrier (March 4, 1907 - June 20, 1964) was an American actor who appeared on radio, stage, and screen.  In the 1930s he was a member of Orson Welles' Mercury Theatre and played Simon Templar on The Saint radio show. \n\nBarrier was born in New York City and died in Hollywood, California. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Edgar Barrier, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1964-06-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xz8KWxBtfczccMkGv0dOd8VOrg6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78849"}}, {tmdbId:"30303", properties:{bornIn:"Tacoma, Washington, USA", imdbId:"0071636", born:date('1906-05-19'), name:"Bruce Bennett", bio:"Bruce Bennett (born Harold Herman Brix) was an American actor and Olympic silver medalist shot putter.   His first career was as an athlete.   At the University of Washington, where he majored in economics, he played football (tackle) in the 1926 Rose Bowl and was a track-and-field star.  Two years later, he won the Silver medal for the shot put in the 1928 Olympic Games...", died:date('2007-02-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/70GxHSRcIsgSsTVl0hzjxLEA4s7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30303"}}, {tmdbId:"30686", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0619798", born:date('1896-01-21'), name:"J. Carrol Naish", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJoseph Patrick Carrol Naish (January 21, 1896 – January 24, 1973) was an American character actor born in New York City, New York.  Naish did many film roles, but they were eclipsed when he found fame in the title role of radio's Life with Luigi (1948–1953), which surpassed Bob Hope in the 1950 ratings. \n\nNaish appeared on stage for several years before he began his film career.  He began as a member of Gus Edwards's vaudeville troupe of child performers...", died:date('1973-01-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xtYBFzDJQJM5KzSHDMx86l8uAvl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30686"}}, {tmdbId:"2177", properties:{bornIn:"San Leandro, California, USA", imdbId:"0000978", born:date('1913-01-15'), name:"Lloyd Bridges", bio:"Lloyd Bridges (1913–1998) was an American actor who starred in a number of television series and appeared in more than 150 feature films.  Bridges is best known for his role on Sea Hunt.  He is the father of actors Beau Bridges and Jeff Bridges...", died:date('1998-03-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3dUJhLyaOl32mOU9HBpgTniLNJc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2177"}}, {tmdbId:"566738", properties:{bornIn:"Kansas City - Missouri - USA", imdbId:"0793195", born:date('1904-05-18'), name:"Fred Shields", bio:"In Kansas City, Shields owned a theatre group, The Playmakers,  and performed in stage plays.  He also worked as a newscaster for WDAF  radio.  In 1929, he announced the plane flight of Germany's Graf Zeppelin  over the U. S.  In 1930, he came to Hollywood, CA, with Ger, his wife,  Karena, and daughter, Evelyn.  He was employed as the Station Manager for  KTM Los Angeles.  In 1939, he was President of the American Federation  of Radio Artists...", died:date('1974-06-30'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/566738"}}, {tmdbId:"77619", properties:{imdbId:"0647057", name:"José Oliveira", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77619"}}, {tmdbId:"86824", properties:{bornIn:"Houston, Texas", imdbId:"0112046", born:date('1915-12-23'), name:"Jean Brooks", bio:"Fluent in Spanish, Jean Brooks began professionally by singing with Enric Madriguera and Orchestra in New York.  She had a small role in the New York City-filmed The Crime of Doctor Crespi (1935) and the second lead in a Broadway play, \"Name Your Poison\" (1938), with Lenore Ulric, all under her real name of Jeanne Kelly.  She was signed by an independent film production company that had gone under by the time she got to Hollywood...", died:date('1963-11-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9vv1Y6iLwCz5Ro7fUMrKSOwZUts.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/86824"}}, {tmdbId:"33277", properties:{bornIn:"Shoshone, Wyoming, USA", imdbId:"0422436", born:date('1907-07-19'), name:"Isabel Jewell", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nIsabel Jewell (July 19, 1907 – April 5, 1972) was an American actress most active in the 1930s and early 1940s.  Some of her most famous films were Ceiling Zero, Marked Woman, A Tale of Two Cities, and Gone With the Wind.   After years in theater stock companies, including an 87-week stint in Lincoln, Nebraska, she hit the big time after getting a part on Broadway in Up Pops the Devil (1930)...", died:date('1972-04-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/a7DL3IbUiV2x8eiDCkijIi1m1qo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33277"}}, {tmdbId:"10539", properties:{bornIn:"Detroit, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0001375", born:date('1922-11-12'), name:"Kim Hunter", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nKim Hunter (November 12, 1922 – September 11, 2002) was an American film, theatre, and television actress.  She won both an Academy Award and a Golden Globe Award, each as Best Supporting Actress, for her performance as Stella Kowalski in the 1951 film A Streetcar Named Desire.  Decades later she received a Daytime Emmy Award for her work on the long running soap The Edge of Night...", died:date('2002-09-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/knu87rUxQVZ65Plp6BgoyasAHOT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10539"}}, {tmdbId:"7665", properties:{bornIn:"Sioux City, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0136994", born:date('1913-03-15'), name:"Macdonald Carey", bio:"Edward Macdonald Carey (March 15, 1913 – March 21, 1994) was an American actor, best known for his role as the patriarch Dr.  Tom Horton on NBC's soap opera Days of our Lives.  For almost three decades, he was the show's central cast member...", died:date('1994-03-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/o9lTQsuzEGimjjMGISKjppT4CxA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7665"}}, {tmdbId:"94217", properties:{imdbId:"0656745", born:date('1910-12-02'), name:"Robert Paige", bio:"Robert Paige (born John Arthur Page December 2, 1911 in Indianapolis, Indiana, died Dec 21,1987) was a TV star and Universal Pictures leading man who made 65 films in his lifetime and was the only actor ever allowed to sing on film with Deanna Durbin (in 1944's Can't Help Singing).  He was a graduate of West Point and was related to Admiral David Beatty, hero of the World War I Battle of Jutland.   Paige began his screen career in 1934...", died:date('1987-12-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aiUfDDefiY9e2YByAJRMVhwYqCs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94217"}}, {tmdbId:"95312", properties:{imdbId:"0020145", born:date('1920-07-03'), name:"Louise Allbritton", died:date('1979-02-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7nakrHwm5FKdFo2fXdYSDmXIotQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95312"}}, {tmdbId:"30133", properties:{bornIn:"Valparaíso, Chile", imdbId:"0030166", born:date('1918-08-17'), name:"Evelyn Ankers", bio:"Evelyn Felisa Ankers  was an American actress best known for playing roles in American horror films during the 1940s...", died:date('1985-08-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/p0KMOycio9FSF4PZeEo9bcAGsnh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30133"}}, {tmdbId:"107684", properties:{bornIn:"Boston, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0186600", born:date('1875-08-24'), name:"Frank Craven", died:date('1945-09-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sGHy6jQelr4EjXpqapwzE7HkMur.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/107684"}}, {tmdbId:"39554", properties:{bornIn:"Tulsa - Oklahoma - USA", imdbId:"0428354", born:date('1919-03-02'), name:"Jennifer Jones", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPhylis Lee Isley (March 2, 1919 – December 17, 2009), better known by her stage name Jennifer Jones, was an American actress.  A five-time Academy Award nominee, Jones won the Academy Award for Best Actress for her performance in The Song of Bernadette (1943)...", died:date('2009-12-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qig8grCaqapFoCfc4qJKx77s5Ow.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/39554"}}, {tmdbId:"1905", properties:{bornIn:"St. Louis, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0001637", born:date('1911-05-27'), name:"Vincent Price", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nVincent Leonard Price, Jr.  (May 27, 1911 – October 25, 1993) was an American actor, well known for his distinctive voice and performances in horror films.  His career spanned other genres, including film noir, drama, mystery, thriller, and comedy.  He appeared on stage, television, radio, and in over one hundred films.  He has two stars on the Hollywood Walk of Fame: one for motion pictures, and one for television...", died:date('1993-10-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1B5qC9TdVc20e6pA5zpFsuoCXUg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1905"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"5248", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0002011", born:date('1911-12-08'), name:"Lee J. Cobb", bio:"Lee J.  Cobb (December 8, 1911 - February 11, 1976) ) was an American actor best known for his performance in 12 Angry Men (1957), his Academy Award-nominated performance in On the Waterfront, and one of his last films, The Exorcist (1973).  He also played the role of Willy Loman in the original Broadway production of Arthur Miller's 1949 play Death of a Salesman under the direction of Elia Kazan...", died:date('1976-02-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yxMxBvM0PZwu7YXQamG0kFwt9DZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5248"}}, {tmdbId:"240072", properties:{bornIn:"Richmond - Virginia - USA", imdbId:"0732408", born:date('1878-05-25'), name:"Bill Robinson", bio:"According to one jazz dance source, Bill 'Bojangles' Robinson was the chief instigator for getting tap dance \"up on its toes. \" Early forms of tap, including the familiar \"buck and wing\", contained a flat-footed style, while Robinson performed on the balls of his feet with a shuffle-tap style that allowed him more improvisation.  It obviously got him noticed and it certainly made him a legend...", died:date('1949-11-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/icJ0rUzDLMVXPMDlBVzL2RSfBkO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/240072"}}, {tmdbId:"1584484", properties:{name:"Katherine Dunham and Her Troupe", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1584484"}}, {tmdbId:"142900", properties:{imdbId:"0028249", name:"Kirsten Andreasen", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/142900"}}, {tmdbId:"142901", properties:{imdbId:"0073899", name:"Sigurd Berg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/142901"}}, {tmdbId:"142903", properties:{imdbId:"0392306", name:"Harald Holst", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/142903"}}, {tmdbId:"142902", properties:{imdbId:"0406029", name:"Albert Høeberg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/142902"}}, {tmdbId:"34498", properties:{bornIn:"Syracuse, New York, USA", imdbId:"0141466", born:date('1936-06-16'), name:"Ann Carter", bio:"Ann Carter was an American child screen actress during the 1940s.  She is perhaps best remembered for her portrayal of misunderstood little Amy Reed in the 1944 film The Curse of the Cat People...", died:date('2014-01-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xCBpBSPQBtztSLdEAaI7vw3ZaKc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34498"}}, {tmdbId:"4091", properties:{bornIn:"Kankakee, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0534045", born:date('1908-08-30'), name:"Fred MacMurray", bio:"Born to Maleta Martin and Frederick MacMurray (concert violinist).  Fred sang and played in orchestras to earn tuition.  He was educated at Carroll College, Wis.  Fred played with a Chicago orchestra for more than a year.  Then he joined an orchestra in Hollywood where he played, did some recording and played extra roles.  He then joined a comedy stage band, California Collegians, and went to New York.  There he joined \"Three's A Crowd\" revue on Broadway and on the road...", died:date('1991-11-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lxxixlFMNH0JuA9K0K3mJmigYcc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4091"}}, {tmdbId:"14975", properties:{bornIn:"Cincinnati, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0356004", born:date('1888-09-19'), name:"Porter Hall", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nClifford Porter Hall (September 19, 1888 – October 6, 1953) was an American character actor known for appearing in a number of films in the 1930s and 1940s.  Hall played movie villains or comedic incompetent characters.   Hall was born in Cincinnati, Ohio and began his career touring as a stage actor with roles in productions of The Great Gatsby and Naked in 1926.  Hall made his film debut in the 1931 drama Secrets of a Secretary...", died:date('1953-10-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8VObqTCOljxeyfVWaIthtEbw4lm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14975"}}, {tmdbId:"30124", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001333", born:date('1917-06-30'), name:"Susan Hayward", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nSusan Hayward (June 30, 1917 – March 14, 1975) was an American actress. \n\nAfter working as a fashion model in New York, Hayward travelled to Hollywood in 1937 when open auditions were held for the leading role in Gone With the Wind (1939).  Although she was not selected, she secured a film contract, and played several small supporting roles over the next few years...", died:date('1975-03-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nIp5HCQHTvnD0zppdPM0ff3QBM0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30124"}}, {tmdbId:"88462", properties:{bornIn:"Fort Madison, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0641454", born:date('1908-03-29'), name:"Dennis O'Keefe", bio:"Dennis O'Keefe (March 29, 1908 – August 31, 1968) was an American actor.   He was the son of Irish vaudevillians working in the United States.  As a small child he joined his parents' act and later wrote skits for the stage. \n\nO'Keefe started in films as an extra in the early 1930s.  After a small but impressive role in Saratoga, Clark Gable recommended O'Keefe to Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer, which signed him to a contract in 1937...", died:date('1968-08-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/h6FJdct42dMtl0fSeuQt2r1s0kL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88462"}}, {tmdbId:"34285", properties:{bornIn:"Burlington, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0292433", born:date('1887-02-26'), name:"William Frawley", bio:"William Frawley was born in Burlington, Iowa.  As a boy he sang at St.  Paul's Catholic Church and played at the Burlington Opera House.  His first job was as a stenographer for the Union Pacific Railroad.  He did vaudeville with his brother Paul, then joined pianist Franz Rath in an act they took to San Francisco in 1910.  Four years later he formed a light comedy act with his new wife Edna Louise Broedt, \"Frawley and Louise\", touring the Orpheum and Keith circuits until they divorced in 1927...", died:date('1966-03-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mPCnAsN2GbBoLl34nrviZ4aCCe1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34285"}}, {tmdbId:"29519", properties:{bornIn:"Figeac, Lot, Midi-Pyrénées, France", imdbId:"0000964", born:date('1899-08-28'), name:"Charles Boyer", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nCharles Boyer (28 August 1899 – 26 August 1978) was a French actor who appeared in more than 80 films between 1920 and 1976.  After receiving an education in drama, Boyer started on the stage, but he found success in movies during the 1930s.  His memorable performances were among the era's most highly praised romantic dramas, Algiers (1938) and Love Affair (1939).  Another famous role was in the 1944 mystery-thriller Gaslight...", died:date('1978-08-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/egJji1E0AOw4curkRQBQ0R3vZJK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29519"}}, {tmdbId:"13578", properties:{bornIn:"Covington County, Mississippi, USA", imdbId:"0000763", born:date('1909-01-01'), name:"Dana Andrews", bio:"President of the Screen Actors Guild from 1963 to 1965, Dana Andrews was one of the first to speak out against the degradation of the acting profession, particularly actresses doing nude scenes just to get a role.  Probably the first actor to do a public service announcement about alcoholism (in 1972 for the U. S.  Department of Transportation), he was a member of the National Council on Alcoholism and did public speaking tours...", died:date('1992-12-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gTZaqIS441ejTsQmfZff6SHvWja.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13578"}}, {tmdbId:"13820", properties:{bornIn:"Dublin, Ireland", imdbId:"0280178", born:date('1888-03-10'), name:"Barry Fitzgerald", bio:"Brother of actor Arthur Shields, with whom he performed in several films, most notably John Ford's The Quiet Man (1952).  One of the very few character actors ever to achieve star status. \n\nFitzgerald was the only player ever nominated for the Academy Award for both Best Actor and Best Supporting Actor in the same year for the same role.  The recognition was for Going My Way (1944)...", died:date('1961-01-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/z8opHNghuygzMWsVOpG1Ln3ahmG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13820"}}, {tmdbId:"74875", properties:{bornIn:"Homestead, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0570451", born:date('1898-05-23'), name:"Frank McHugh", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nFrancis Curray \"Frank\" McHugh (May 23, 1898 – September 11, 1981) was an American film and television actor. \n\nBorn in Homestead, Pennsylvania, McHugh came from a theatrical family.  His parents ran a stock theatre company and as a young child he performed on stage.  His brother Matt and sister Kitty performed an act with him by the time he was ten years old, but the family quit the stage around 1930...", died:date('1981-09-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yxr2eRkScZWPQOtm2vzz38hALHD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74875"}}, {tmdbId:"7172", properties:{bornIn:"Barnwell, South Carolina, USA", imdbId:"0113768", born:date('1933-04-03'), name:"James Brown", bio:"James Brown (May 3, 1933 - December 25, 2006) was an American singer and songwriter, eventually referred to as \"The Godfather of Soul\"(GFOS).  Brown started singing in gospel groups and worked his way on up.  He has been recognized as one of the most iconic figures in the 20th century popular music and was renowned for his vocals and feverish dancing.  He was also called \"the hardest-working man in show business\"...", died:date('2006-12-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/q9Q3c7HsZEEqrwNIY9yDgsJ74uE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7172"}}, {tmdbId:"115457", properties:{bornIn:"Astoria, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0102787", born:date('1915-02-07'), name:"Eddie Bracken", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Edward Vincent \"Eddie\" Bracken  was an American actor.   Bracken became a Hollywood comedy legend with lead performances in the films Hail the Conquering Hero and The Miracle of Morgan's Creek both in 1944, both of which have been preserved by the National Film Registry.   During this era, he also had success on Broadway, with performances in plays like Too Many Girls...", died:date('2002-11-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iHAR0dzXbYw2pS2WkOmJGOd7QXG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/115457"}}, {tmdbId:"78052", properties:{bornIn:"Snoqualmie Falls, Washington State, USA", imdbId:"0707048", born:date('1920-08-06'), name:"Ella Raines", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nElla Wallace Raines (August 6, 1920 – May 30, 1988) was an American film and television actress...", died:date('1988-05-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6nSd8pqGWQEsFm5cAg19jBsgIEr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78052"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"89673", properties:{bornIn:"Plymouth, Indiana, USA", imdbId:"0906940", born:date('1887-09-09'), name:"Raymond Walburn", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.    \n\nRaymond Walburn (September 9, 1887 – July 26, 1969) was an American character actor who appeared in dozens of Hollywood comedies and an occasional dramatic role during the 1930s and 1940s. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Raymond Walburn, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1969-07-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/l2Nkf9zmVsP6NpcOid01HTzpEDm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89673"}}, {tmdbId:"85345", properties:{bornIn:"Corsham, Wiltshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0043875", born:date('1889-02-21'), name:"Felix Aylmer", died:date('1979-09-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/f7eu6BVjWMb5qOy4yX6DNef5qvj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85345"}}, {tmdbId:"81463", properties:{bornIn:"Mount Gambier, South Australia, Australia", imdbId:"0375818", born:date('1909-04-09'), name:"Robert Helpmann", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Sir Robert Helpmann CBE (9 April 1909 – 28 September 1986) was an Australian dancer, actor, theatre director and choreographer. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Robert Helpmann, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1986-09-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/37yiR16LB5HFTXtJ9kF16Nc3Igm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81463"}}, {tmdbId:"1057660", properties:{imdbId:"0339512", name:"Vernon Greeves", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1057660"}}, {tmdbId:"13991", properties:{bornIn:"San Diego, California, USA", imdbId:"0639684", born:date('1937-01-15'), name:"Margaret O'Brien", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMargaret O'Brien (born January 15, 1937) is an American film and stage actress.  Although her film career as a leading character was brief, she was one of the most popular child actors in cinema history.  In her later career, she appeared on stage and in supporting film roles. \n\nShe was born Angela Maxine O'Brien; (she later changed her name to Margaret following the success of the film Journey for Margaret, in which she played the title role)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iLzh8P6N7qKWpVltgBOB7ItBfCu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13991"}}, {tmdbId:"34210", properties:{bornIn:"Canton, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0307750", born:date('1932-02-03'), name:"Peggy Ann Garner", bio:"Peggy Ann Garner (February 3, 1932 – October 16, 1984) was an American actress.  As a child actress, Garner had her first film role in 1938.  She won the Academy Juvenile Award for her work in A Tree Grows in Brooklyn...", died:date('1984-10-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uHbsLjq3rqLFw9NyND7HIEBqunX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34210"}}, {tmdbId:"20125", properties:{bornIn:"Indianapolis, Indiana, USA", imdbId:"0916067", born:date('1889-11-19'), name:"Clifton Webb", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nClifton Webb (November 19, 1889 – October 13, 1966) was an American actor, dancer, and singer known for his Oscar-nominated roles in such films as Laura, The Razor's Edge, and Sitting Pretty.  In the theatrical world he was known for his appearances in the plays of Noël Coward, notably Blithe Spirit...", died:date('1966-10-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wD7udcxwvikYPlZSjGSXB1NAB4M.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20125"}}, {tmdbId:"93895", properties:{bornIn:"Huntsville, Alabama, U.S.", imdbId:"0000845", born:date('1902-01-31'), name:"Tallulah Bankhead", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nTallulah Brockman Bankhead (January 31, 1902 – December 12, 1968) was an American actress, talk-show host, and bon vivant. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Tallulah Bankhead, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1968-12-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dYSYUUb09TTvIiAbqnc58K53m2T.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/93895"}}, {tmdbId:"37884", properties:{bornIn:"Vienna, Austria", imdbId:"0805790", born:date('1902-05-03'), name:"Walter Slezak", bio:"Walter Slezak (3 May 1902 – 21 April 1983) was a portly Austrian character actor who appeared in numerous Hollywood films.   Slezak often portrayed villains or thugs, most notably the German U-boat captain in Alfred Hitchcock's 1944 Lifeboat, but occasionally he got to play lighter roles, as in 1962's The Wonderful World of the Brothers Grimm...", died:date('1983-04-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8RPITP47AOYYsvNRsrSB9bGnF5l.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/37884"}}, {tmdbId:"93896", properties:{bornIn:"Birmingham, Alabama, USA", imdbId:"0027156", born:date('1918-04-03'), name:"Mary Anderson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMary Bebe Anderson (April 3, 1918 – April 6, 2014) was an American actress, who appeared in 31 films and 22 television productions between 1939 and 1965.  She was best known for her small supporting role in the film Gone With the Wind as well as one of the main characters in Alfred Hitchcock's 1944 film Lifeboat...", died:date('2014-04-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/f1WzqnpBUektFZH5LiMVbiTb892.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/93896"}}, {tmdbId:"13993", properties:{bornIn:"Amsterdam, New York, USA", imdbId:"0107082", born:date('1917-02-21'), name:"Lucille Bremer", bio:"Lucille Bremer (1917–1996) was an American film actress and dancer. \n\nBremer was born in Amsterdam, New York and began her career as a Rockette at Radio City Music Hall in New York City, aged 16.  Bremer, along with fellow stars Vera-Ellen and June Allyson, appeared as a Pony Girl in the Broadway musical Panama Hattie in 1940.   She made her screen debut in Meet Me in St.  Louis, and followed this with Yolanda and the Thief, and a featured dance performance in Ziegfeld Follies...", died:date('1996-04-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mgMryylfPrKqre4sNlpSVKqDo5J.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13993"}}, {tmdbId:"87546", properties:{bornIn:"Wien, Austria", imdbId:"0260722", born:date('1902-06-14'), name:"Carl Esmond", died:date('2004-12-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5pxXV4VKrYvVC1KONvnv0C2e80R.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/87546"}}, {tmdbId:"8241", properties:{bornIn:"Astoria, New York, USA", imdbId:"0111702", born:date('1914-09-08'), name:"Hillary Brooke", bio:"Hillary Brooke (born Beatrice Sofia Mathilda Peterson) was an American screen and television actress best known for her work in Abbott and Costello and Sherlock Holmes films...", died:date('1999-05-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2R5hSW5KO1yCkLHj5MVe5dXlSSb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8241"}}, {tmdbId:"11028", properties:{bornIn:"Manchester, England, UK", imdbId:"0183459", born:date('1903-10-01'), name:"George Coulouris", bio:"George Coulouris was a British stage, film and television actor...", died:date('1989-04-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/paUT7zrlV6o5Tc7f6axUoIz5ArR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11028"}}, {tmdbId:"30416", properties:{bornIn:"Dubrovnik, Yugoslavia", imdbId:"0168658", born:date('1918-11-11'), name:"Peter Coe", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Percy Newbold \"Peter\" Coe (1919 – 9 August 2008) was the father and athletics coach to Sebastian Coe. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Peter Coe, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1993-06-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jSP2jlwRETcHKQcRfggAKWOYgtD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30416"}}, {tmdbId:"101481", properties:{bornIn:"Stanton, Iowa, U.S.", imdbId:"0160417", born:date('1920-03-05'), name:"Virginia Christine", bio:"Virginia Christine Ricketts was an American stage and screen film actress.  She began training for a theatrical career with actor/ director Fritz Feld whom she married in 1940.  In 1942, she made her stage debut in the Los Angeles production of \"Hedda Gabler\".   While performing in the play, she was spotted by an agent from Warner Bros.  who signed her to a film contract with the studio.  Virginia Christie appeared in more than 170 feature films and TV-productions...", died:date('1996-07-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/82bTZIPSZpNmuO3H431yQHDDrHP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101481"}}, {tmdbId:"130061", properties:{imdbId:"0362323", name:"Kay Harding", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rtSmQjgBBa3W8BZoY1vLo708blU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/130061"}}, {tmdbId:"34117", properties:{bornIn:"Kansas City, Missouri, USA ", imdbId:"0523225", born:date('1913-10-17'), name:"Robert Lowery", died:date('1971-12-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/y1oCtAjBrUz8AdypxLiOR2D3CDf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34117"}}, {tmdbId:"103347", properties:{imdbId:"0024738", born:date('1919-03-30'), name:"Ramsay Ames", died:date('1998-03-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uetDpsAIVRZl2VQiVxWV4VDzjEM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/103347"}}, {tmdbId:"1937", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001682", born:date('1920-09-23'), name:"Mickey Rooney", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMickey Rooney (born Joseph Yule Jr. ; September 23, 1920 – April 6, 2014) was an American actor, vaudevillian, comedian, producer, and radio personality.  In a career spanning nine decades and continuing until shortly before his death, he appeared in more than 300 films and was among the last surviving stars of the silent film era...", died:date('2014-04-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eYuayEC3xhXQf3Z1Cy6AVMEcgZb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1937"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"3635", properties:{bornIn:"Hampstead, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0000072", born:date('1932-02-27'), name:"Elizabeth Taylor", bio:"Dame Elizabeth Rosemond \"Liz\" Taylor, DBE (February 27, 1932 – March 23, 2011) was a British-American actress.  From her early years as a child star with MGM, she became one of the great screen actresses of Hollywood's Golden Age.  As one of the world's most famous film stars, Taylor was recognized for her acting ability and for her glamorous lifestyle, beauty and distinctive violet eyes...", died:date('2011-03-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1GXYcfIxJdLhrfM312daOEcfwUb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3635"}}, {tmdbId:"7641", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0720843", born:date('1903-06-25'), name:"Anne Revere", bio:"​Anne Revere was an American stage, screen, and television actress...", died:date('1990-12-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lsGPYDdTqBk6rRICswxOaXXPaNm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7641"}}, {tmdbId:"120306", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0002038", born:date('1925-07-23'), name:"Gloria DeHaven", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGloria Mildred DeHaven (born July 23, 1925) is an American actress, singer and a former contract star for Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer.   \n\nEarly life and career\n\nDeHaven was born in Los Angeles, California, the daughter of actor-director, Carter DeHaven, and actress, Flora Parker DeHaven, both former vaudeville performers. \n\nShe began her career as a child actor with a bit part in Charlie Chaplin's Modern Times (1936).  She was signed to a contract with MGM...", died:date('2016-07-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jdoS7iWTklH2j5Zcb2w10qzr8VM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/120306"}}, {tmdbId:"7570", properties:{bornIn:"The Bronx, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000002", born:date('1924-09-16'), name:"Lauren Bacall", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLauren Bacall (born Betty Joan Perske; September 16, 1924 – August 12, 2014) was an American actress known for her distinctive husky voice and sultry looks.  She began her career as a model...", died:date('2014-08-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iCOzbSzCSUC6D9EcyXtVb2FRNu0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7570"}}, {tmdbId:"95965", properties:{bornIn:"Stockton, California, U.S.", imdbId:"0602834", born:date('1924-01-27'), name:"Dolores Moran", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDolores Moran (January 27, 1924 – February 5, 1982) was an American film actress and model. \n\nMoran's brief career as a film actress began in 1942 with some uncredited roles in such films as Yankee Doodle Dandy.  By 1943 she had become a popular pin-up girl and appeared on the cover of such magazines as Yank.  She was given supporting roles in films such as Old Acquaintance (1943) with Bette Davis and Warner Bros...", died:date('1982-02-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/b8xXAxWUGQ9FARGoWYwIOj9RFlu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95965"}}, {tmdbId:"80467", properties:{imdbId:"0804224", name:"Cornelia Otis Skinner", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wOYRIFNIUhDJ1Q1rFNEMnhInuU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80467"}}, {tmdbId:"81291", properties:{bornIn:"Hamilton, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0107631", born:date('1882-12-12'), name:"Edmund Breon", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nEdmund Breon (12 December 1882 – 24 June 1953) was a Scottish film and stage actor.  He appeared in 131 films between 1907 and 1952. \n\nBorn Iver Edmund de Breon MacLaverty in Hamilton, South Lanarkshire, he began in John Hare's touring company and later played on the West End stage and in Glasgow, gaining prominence.  According to his grandson, Breon \"started out at the turn of the century doing silent pictures in France...", died:date('1953-06-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uR49CwS2gV2DtNGzrwo0juPBFNt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81291"}}, {tmdbId:"4347", properties:{bornIn:"Hoboken, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0000069", born:date('1915-12-12'), name:"Frank Sinatra", bio:"Francis Albert \"Frank\" Sinatra ( December 12, 1915 – May 14, 1998) was an American singer and actor.  Beginning his musical career in the swing era with Harry James and Tommy Dorsey, Sinatra became a successful solo artist in the early to mid-1940s, being the idol of the \"bobby soxers\". \n\nHis professional career had stalled by the 1950s, but it was reborn in 1954 after he won the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor (for his performance in From Here to Eternity)...", died:date('1998-05-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/w9Wl6FznONDn5O880ScJo79AOMU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4347"}}, {tmdbId:"82407", properties:{bornIn:"Winston-Salem - North Carolina - USA", imdbId:"0337113", born:date('1922-02-09'), name:"Kathryn Grayson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nKathryn Grayson  (February 9, 1922 – February 17, 2010) was an American actress and operatic soprano singer.  From the age of twelve, Grayson trained as an opera singer.  She was under contract to MGM by the early 1940s, soon establishing a career principally through her work in musicals...", died:date('2010-02-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ezysNRuMuiHSovFEFzkVNGZ7SoI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82407"}}, {tmdbId:"129512", properties:{imdbId:"0411826", born:date('1895-11-28'), name:"José Iturbi", bio:"Temperamental, volatile Spanish-born pianist and conductor whose life and career were varied and often controversial.  Born in Valencia, he was a child prodigy, giving piano recitals by the age of seven and supplementing the family income by playing for up to 14 hours daily at a silent cinema theatre.  He was an honours graduate from the Conservatoire de Musique in Paris, and, by the age of 24, occupied Franz Liszt's former post as leader of the piano department of the Geneva Conservatory...", died:date('1980-06-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tp7gBFjksQnW0iO6RGmuuNcFNbz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/129512"}}, {tmdbId:"39799", properties:{bornIn:"Johannesburg, South Africa", imdbId:"0371775", born:date('1909-03-20'), name:"Louis Hayward", bio:"Louis Hayward (1909–1985) was a British actor born in South Africa...", died:date('1985-02-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9ZSgjyfnwO2eJVVEAgAUyGdvJbc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/39799"}}, {tmdbId:"14577", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0041138", born:date('1911-04-22'), name:"Edith Atwater", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEdith Atwater (April 22, 1911 – March 14, 1986) was an American stage, film and television actress. \n\nBorn in Chicago, Illinois, Atwater made her Broadway debut in 1933.  In 1939 she starred in The Man Who Came to Dinner. \n\nOn screen she appeared in such films as The Body Snatcher, Sweet Smell of Success, and Strait-Jacket.  Her television work included roles on The Rockford Files and Knots Landing. \n\nAtwater was married to actor Hugh Marlowe in 1941...", died:date('1986-03-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/g6K6pHXE5TBySJuUZurreteIALH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14577"}}, {tmdbId:"12725", properties:{bornIn:"Richmond, Surrey, England, UK", imdbId:"0424743", born:date('1908-12-18'), name:"Celia Johnson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nDame Celia Elizabeth Johnson DBE (18 December 1908 – 25 April 1982) was a British actress. \n\nShe began her stage acting career in 1928, and subsequently achieved success in West End and Broadway productions.  She also appeared in several films, including the romantic drama Brief Encounter (1945), for which she received a nomination for the Academy Award for Best Actress...", died:date('1982-04-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/stVwzdFNs6qPSF5ZfBhyFqxuevl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12725"}}, {tmdbId:"12726", properties:{bornIn:"Cliftonville, Kent, England, UK", imdbId:"0002145", born:date('1913-09-29'), name:"Trevor Howard", bio:"Howard was born in Cliftonville, Kent, England, the son of Mabel Grey (Wallace) and Arthur John Howard.  He was educated at Clifton College (to which he left in his will a substantial legacy for a drama scholarship) and at the Royal Academy of Dramatic Art (RADA), acting on the London stage for several years before World War II.  His first paid work was in the play Revolt in a Reformatory (1934), before he left RADA in 1935 to take small roles...", died:date('1988-01-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jnt4bc6P433sUZNThxxUaDTK9NB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12726"}}, {tmdbId:"12727", properties:{bornIn:"Manor Park, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0391361", born:date('1890-10-01'), name:"Stanley Holloway", bio:"Stanley Augustus Holloway, OBE (1 October 1890 – 30 January 1982) was an English stage and film actor, comedian, singer, poet and monologist.  He was famous for his comic and character roles on stage and screen, especially that of Alfred P.  Doolittle in My Fair Lady.  He was also renowned for his recordings of comic monologues and songs, which he performed throughout most of his 70-year career. \n\nBorn in London, in his early years Holloway pursued a career as a clerk...", died:date('1982-01-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7ifTxk7gUmxTxQByIDrjbVOBAJi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12727"}}, {tmdbId:"12728", properties:{bornIn:" London, England, UK", imdbId:"0136983", born:date('1898-03-30'), name:"Joyce Carey", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nJoyce Carey, OBE (30 March 1898 – 28 February 1993) was a British actress, best known for her long professional and personal relationship with Noël Coward.  Her stage career lasted from 1916 until 1984, and she was performing on television in her nineties.  Though never a star, she was a familiar face both on stage and screen.  In addition to light comedy, she had a large repertory of Shakespearean roles...", died:date('1993-02-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nHgwq5a5wtxDTw1GmgmChWXrUE3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12728"}}, {tmdbId:"12499", properties:{bornIn:"Salt Lake City, Utah, USA", imdbId:"0908153", born:date('1918-10-13'), name:"Robert Walker", bio:"Robert Walker (October 13, 1918 - August 28, 1951) was an American film actor.  He is probably best known for his role as Bruno Anthony in Alfred Hitchcock's 1951 thriller Strangers on a Train...", died:date('1951-08-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4CpjkhPwZiV993CaM9u91G1QBz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12499"}}, {tmdbId:"30537", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0322299", born:date('1882-05-23'), name:"James Gleason", bio:"James Gleason was born in New York City to William Gleason and Mina Crolius, who were both in the theatre.  He was married to Lucile Gleason (born Lucile Webster), and had a son, Russell Gleason.   As a young man James fought in the Spanish-American War.  After the war  he joined the stock company at the Liberty Theater in Oakland,  California, which his parents were running.  James and his wife then  moved to Portland, Oregon, where they played in stock at the Baker  Theater...", died:date('1959-04-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/24sn7JhD5O5NlNjtnZxRINjM1Hw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30537"}}, {tmdbId:"4966", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0943978", born:date('1916-07-27'), name:"Keenan Wynn", bio:"Keenan Wynn (1916 – 1986) was an American character actor.  His bristling mustache and expressive face were his stock in trade, and though he rarely had a lead role, he got prominent billing in most of his movie and TV parts...", died:date('1986-10-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/z6Krk3fIoW6O9EhZTWb2EFJtzp2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4966"}}, {tmdbId:"85993", properties:{bornIn:"Evanston, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0623684", born:date('1914-01-28'), name:"Tom Neal", bio:"​From Wikipedia\n\nThomas Carroll Neal Jr.  (January 28, 1914 – August 7, 1972) was an American actor and boxer best known for appearing in the critically lauded film Detour (1945), for having a tryst with actress Barbara Payton, and for later committing manslaughter...", died:date('1972-08-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/43Cfyjj3TXmNFjBcQtdQTZDCgOn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85993"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"34330", properties:{bornIn:"Columbia, South Carolina, USA", imdbId:"0767243", born:date('1921-02-19'), name:"Ann Savage", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAnn Savage (February 19, 1921 – December 25, 2008) was an American film and television actress.  She is best-remembered as the cigarette-puffing femme fatale in the critically acclaimed film noir Detour (1945), and starred in more than twenty B movies between 1943 and 1946...", died:date('2008-12-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fyleNTYHJjk1v4Qh0RRG9H92k4b.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34330"}}, {tmdbId:"85994", properties:{imdbId:"0236873", born:date('1918-01-30'), name:"Claudia Drake", died:date('1997-10-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7E0gHwOgVfLAl5V06Rvm8wcDA9N.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85994"}}, {tmdbId:"85995", properties:{imdbId:"0531705", born:date('1908-05-07'), name:"Edmund MacDonald", died:date('1951-09-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9zoueJEgi6GxsxYNWWzrc0MFdoj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85995"}}, {tmdbId:"64838", properties:{bornIn:"St. Louis, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0002107", born:date('1916-12-18'), name:"Betty Grable", bio:"Betty Grable (1916–1973) was an American actress. \n\nGrable was enrolled in Clark's Dancing School at the age of three.  At age 13, Grable and her mother set out for Hollywood with the hopes of stardom.  There she landed several minor parts in films such as Whoopee!, New Movietone Follies of 1930, Happy Days and Let's Go Places. \n\nIn 1932, she signed with RKO Radio Pictures.  The bit parts continued for the next three years until Grable was cast in By Your Leave...", died:date('1973-07-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vy2jMXXaT7MX5Uso5Fcpb8707Ab.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/64838"}}, {tmdbId:"70820", properties:{bornIn:"Roanoke, Virginia, USA", imdbId:"0668361", born:date('1912-05-28'), name:"John Payne", bio:"John Payne was an American stage, screen, and television actor.  He is best remembered as a singer in 20th Century Fox musical films and for his roles in Miracle on 34th Street (1947) and the television series The Restless Gun (1957-1959)...", died:date('1989-12-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2PRAP6XPLMQFK5eeJ63A7g0jvw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70820"}}, {tmdbId:"226642", properties:{bornIn:"Rock Island, Illinois, U.S.", imdbId:"0369792", born:date('1926-06-10'), name:"June Haver", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nJune Haver (June 10, 1926 – July 4, 2005), was an American film actress.  She is most well-known as a popular star of 20th Century-Fox musicals in the late 1940s, most notably The Dolly Sisters, with Betty Grable.  She is also often linked to her second husband, actor Fred MacMurray. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article June Haver, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2005-07-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8JkiObmDAbLjd9Gu6IWEbCCQqUR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/226642"}}, {tmdbId:"94110", properties:{bornIn:"Budapest, Austria – Hungary (now Budapest, Hungary)", imdbId:"0757064", born:date('1884-02-02'), name:"S.Z. Sakall", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSzőke Szakáll  (February 2, 1883 – February 12, 1955), known as S. Z.  Sakall, was a Hungarian film character actor.  He was in many films including In the Good Old Summertime, Lullaby of Broadway, Christmas in Connecticut and Casablanca in which he played Carl, the head waiter. \n\nChubby-jowled Sakall played numerous supporting roles in Hollywood musicals and comedies in the 1940s and 1950s...", died:date('1955-02-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4GwNU8pQnmXd4a3032aAbBGOwlG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94110"}}, {tmdbId:"25154", properties:{bornIn:"Courbevoie, Seine, France", imdbId:"0001916", born:date('1898-05-15'), name:"Arletty", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nArletty (15 May 1898 – 24 July 1992) was a French actress, singer, and fashion model. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Arletty, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1992-07-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iI4wBjZgg6AneXXMUfWF9Gxf27v.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25154"}}, {tmdbId:"25155", properties:{bornIn:"Le Vésinet, Yvelines, Île-de-France, France", imdbId:"0056761", born:date('1910-09-08'), name:"Jean-Louis Barrault", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJean-Louis Barrault (8 September 1910, Le Vésinet, Yvelines – 22 January 1994) was a French actor, director and mime artist, training that served him well when he portrayed the 19th-century mime Jean-Gaspard Deburau (Baptiste Debureau) in Marcel Carné's 1945 film Les Enfants du Paradis (Children of Paradise). \n\nJean-Louis Barrault studied with Charles Dullin in whose troupe he acted from 1933 to 1935...", died:date('1994-01-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/i7ctsNqijuw4cOevV5jXYO9GrFt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25155"}}, {tmdbId:"24476", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0105482", born:date('1905-12-22'), name:"Pierre Brasseur", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPierre Brasseur, born Pierre-Albert Espinasse (22 December 1905, Paris – 16 August 1972, Bruneck, Italy) was a French actor. \n\nHe was the son of actor Georges Espinasse and actress Germaine Brasseur while the latter was married to Albert Brasseur.  His grandfather, Jules Brasseur, was an actor as well.  The family tradition of using the name Brasseur was continued by his son Claude and his grandson Alexandre...", died:date('1972-08-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/y9moezayXgiGbJWa9V1tFuljjc8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24476"}}, {tmdbId:"25159", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0719749", born:date('1885-03-21'), name:"Pierre Renoir", died:date('1952-03-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1cyQDcUyJuBrbdFWkBqrZjo0DwJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25159"}}, {tmdbId:"590274", properties:{imdbId:"0138791", born:date('1887-11-21'), name:"George Carney", died:date('1947-12-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lx9b7kOZ4q3orkDofJICWp01HBn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/590274"}}, {tmdbId:"85936", properties:{imdbId:"0399648", born:date('1897-02-20'), name:"Walter Hudd", died:date('1963-01-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/peR5wePzaafbSOu3c6cwgcQGrc0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85936"}}, {tmdbId:"2549829", properties:{name:"Duncan MacKechnie", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2549829"}}, {tmdbId:"35320", properties:{bornIn:"Prievidza, Hungary", imdbId:"0664273", born:date('1912-10-13'), name:"Cornel Wilde", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nCornel Wilde (October 13, 1912 – October 16, 1989) was a Hungarian-American actor and film director. \n\nWilde's acting career began in 1935, when he made his debut on Broadway.  In 1936 he began making small, uncredited appearances in films.  By the 1940s, he had signed a contract with 20th Century Fox, and by the mid-1940s, he was a major leading man.  He was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Actor for his performance in 1945's A Song to Remember...", died:date('1989-10-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mZb4WB8j0DLSBSwmUSIs8ex5b8S.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/35320"}}, {tmdbId:"82170", properties:{bornIn:"Barstow, California, United States", imdbId:"0002022", born:date('1925-05-25'), name:"Jeanne Crain", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nJeanne Elizabeth Crain (May 25, 1925 – December 14, 2003) was an American actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jeanne Crain, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2003-12-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hCq0tzgeEIJRKrosxiEQrQidlcW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82170"}}, {tmdbId:"20391", properties:{bornIn:"St. Joseph, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0943837", born:date('1917-01-05'), name:"Jane Wyman", bio:"Jane Wyman (born Sarah Jane Mayfield; January 5, 1917 – September 10, 2007) was an American singer, dancer, and character actress of film and television.  She began her film career in the 1930s, and was a prolific performer for two decades.  She received an Academy Award for Best Actress for her performance in Johnny Belinda (1948), and later achieved success during the 1980s for her leading role in the television series Falcon Crest. \n\nWyman was the first wife of Ronald Reagan...", died:date('2007-09-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/e7mRq5fOsVZ2dnTFfuQScDDs2ON.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20391"}}, {tmdbId:"101490", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0856062", born:date('1909-03-07'), name:"Phillip Terry", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nPhillip Terry (born Frederick Henry Kormann, March 7, 1909 – February 23, 1993) was an American actor. \n\nTerry was born in San Francisco, California, the only child of German Americans, Frederick Andrew Kormann (1883–1948) and Ida Ruth Voll (1883–1954).   He attended Stanford University, where he became interested in theatre.  After a brief stay in New York, he went to London, in 1933, where he attended the Royal Academy of Dramatic Art...", died:date('1993-02-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dlUADvosLtvOFGzv2g5Bv2aoxjk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101490"}}, {tmdbId:"79247", properties:{bornIn:"Cleveland, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0196247", born:date('1909-05-04'), name:"Howard Da Silva", bio:"Howard Da Silva (born Howard Silverblatt) was an American stage, screen, and television actor...", died:date('1986-02-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1wtPeAsAg3jkuqYof1JUCTmS4zm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/79247"}}, {tmdbId:"31551", properties:{bornIn:"Austin, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0779923", born:date('1914-02-21'), name:"Zachary Scott", bio:"Zachary Scott (21 February 1914 – 3 October 1965) was an American actor, most notable for his roles as villains and \"mystery men\"...", died:date('1965-10-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xpaQEamAxrDU0yrbol8MERwcIJt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31551"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"860", properties:{bornIn:"Mill Valley, California, U.S.", imdbId:"0000781", born:date('1908-04-30'), name:"Eve Arden", bio:"Eve was born just north of San Francisco in Mill Valley and was interested in show business from an early age.  At 16, she made her stage debut after quitting school to joined a stock company.  After appearing in minor roles in two films under her real name, Eunice Quedens, she found that the stage offered her the same minor roles.  By the mid 30s, one of these minor roles would attract notice as a comedy sketch in the stage play \"Ziegfeld Folies\"...", died:date('1990-11-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/chvptc4if2kfcmTd1JuCchxDIJJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/860"}}, {tmdbId:"80620", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0368836", born:date('1917-12-07'), name:"Hurd Hatfield", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nWilliam Rukard Hurd Hatfield was an American actor,  best known for often playing characters of handsome, narcissistic young men, most notably Dorian Gray in the film The Picture of Dorian Gray.  Hatfield was born in New York City to William Henry Hatfield, who died in 1954, an attorney who served as deputy attorney general for New York, and his wife, Adele (née McGuire)...", died:date('1998-12-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4RuN7DdY3Ne6xUdUylsGVtxk7k3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80620"}}, {tmdbId:"14730", properties:{bornIn:"Regent's Park, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0001450", born:date('1925-10-16'), name:"Angela Lansbury", bio:"Dame Angela Brigid Lansbury DBE (born October 16, 1925) is a British-American actress and singer who has appeared in theater, television, and film roles.  Her career has spanned almost eight decades, much of it in the United States.  Her work has received international attention.  Her first film appearance was in the 1944 film Gaslight as a conniving maid, for which she received an Academy Award nomination...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fMAigMOfERlIAOUVlStRjq2COD6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14730"}}, {tmdbId:"64212", properties:{bornIn:"White Plains, New York, USA", imdbId:"0002053", born:date('1907-01-23'), name:"Dan Duryea", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDan Duryea (January 23, 1907, in White Plains, New York – June 7, 1968, in Hollywood, California) was an American actor of film, stage and television.  Duryea graduated from Cornell University in 1928.  While at Cornell, Duryea was elected into the Sphinx Head Society.  He made his name on Broadway in the play Dead End, followed by The Little Foxes, in which he played the dishonest and not particularly bright weakling Leo Hubbard...", died:date('1968-06-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tfX2o7EBXRbJhCrVKnSfvfPSG0K.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/64212"}}, {tmdbId:"4353", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0492444", born:date('1923-09-07'), name:"Peter Lawford", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPeter Sydney Vaughn Aylen (7 September 1923 – 24 December 1984), better known as Peter Lawford, was an English-American actor.  He was a member of the \"Rat Pack\", and brother-in-law to President John F.  Kennedy, perhaps more noted in later years for his off-screen activities as a celebrity than for his acting...", died:date('1984-12-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lmD2YbX6NrqCHrMdrTTCkAh3Ry0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4353"}}, {tmdbId:"13997", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001478", born:date('1925-06-25'), name:"June Lockhart", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJune Lockhart (born June 25, 1925) is an American actress, primarily in 1950s and 1960s television, but with memorable performances on stage and in film too.  She is remembered as the mother in two TV series, Lassie and Lost in Space.  She also portrayed Dr.  Janet Craig on the hit CBS television sitcom Petticoat Junction (1968-70). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article June Lockhart , licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/p7EdyUnOc3uOj3mvSmgKFEhVsR6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13997"}}, {tmdbId:"13026", properties:{bornIn:"Leiden, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands", imdbId:"0001225", born:date('1924-04-21'), name:"Nina Foch", bio:"Nina Foch (born Nina Consuelo Maud Fock; April 20, 1924 – December 5, 2008) was a Dutch American actress.  After signing a contract with Columbia Pictures at age 19, Foch became a regular in the studio's horror pictures and films noir before establishing herself as a leading lady in the mid-1940s through the 1950s, often playing roles as cool, aloof sophisticates.  Her career spanned six decades, consisting of over 50 feature films and over 100 television appearances...", died:date('2008-12-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7G1PlnCSzRHa9DTQcN0zO1y7sM3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13026"}}, {tmdbId:"8487", properties:{bornIn:"La Jolla, California, USA", imdbId:"0000060", born:date('1916-04-05'), name:"Gregory Peck", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nEldred Gregory Peck (April 5, 1916 – June 12, 2003) was an American actor who was one of the most popular film stars from the 1940s to the 1960s.  Peck continued to play major film roles until the late 1980s.  His performance as Atticus Finch in the 1962 film To Kill a Mockingbird earned him the Academy Award for Best Actor...", died:date('2003-06-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ycs6o0UoohQ7nV7A6VWaTkoIkCQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8487"}}, {tmdbId:"35193", properties:{bornIn:"St. Petersburg, Russian Empire", imdbId:"0155011", born:date('1891-08-29'), name:"Michael Chekhov", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Michael Chekhov (29 August 1891 – 30 September 1955) was a Russian-American actor, director, author, and theatre practitioner.  His acting technique has been used by actors such as Clint Eastwood, Marilyn Monroe, Yul Brynner, and Robert Stack.  Constantin Stanislavski referred to him as his most brilliant student.  He was a nephew of the playwright Anton Chekhov...", died:date('1955-09-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fBrtV58lCCowEKpxfS0Vf8CPXKx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/35193"}}, {tmdbId:"2642", properties:{bornIn:"Weedon Bec, Northamptonshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0001991", born:date('1886-10-25'), name:"Leo G. Carroll", bio:"Leo G.  Carroll was an English-born stage, screen, and television actor.  He is best known for his roles in six Alfred Hitchcock films - Rebecca, Suspicion, Spellbound, The Paradine Case, Strangers on a Train, and North by Northwest - and the television series Topper, Going My Way, and The Man from U. N. C. L. E...", died:date('1972-10-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9Xr1695IaBwQcTsYHRBuH0KwPYW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2642"}}, {tmdbId:"152713", properties:{bornIn:"Buenos Aires, Argentina", imdbId:"0371376", born:date('1918-09-13'), name:"Dick Haymes", bio:"Arguably one of the best singers of the twentieth century, Dick Haymes  was born in Argentina to a Scots/Irish father and Irish mother, but  brought to the U. S.  as an infant.  Dick inherited his vocal gift from his  mother who made ends meet during the Depression as a singer and voice  teacher.  A music gig in 1931 caught the eye of a local band leader and  soon Dick was moving up, but it was slow-going...", died:date('1980-03-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qUdlck1Avp6IncUgdOcwBiBeCe2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/152713"}}, {tmdbId:"41748", properties:{bornIn:"Newark, New Jersey, USA ", imdbId:"0086176", born:date('1921-11-22'), name:"Vivian Blaine", bio:"Vivian Blaine (1921–1995) was an American actress and singer best known for originating the role of Miss Adelaide in the musical theater production Guys and Dolls...", died:date('1995-12-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yKc6ymn8uzhflDRIIzUtlPXOTW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41748"}}, {tmdbId:"119300", properties:{imdbId:"0592058", born:date('1915-04-20'), name:"Aurora Miranda", bio:"Born sixteen years after her sister -- entertainer Carmen Miranda.   Aurora is probably best known for appearing in the Disney film The Three Caballeros and in the classic film noir Phantom Lady.   Her career in movies was short-lived due to her leaving the business to raise a family...", died:date('2005-12-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vuJuI1mxdhve815sOla3nJf2B17.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/119300"}}, {tmdbId:"119301", properties:{bornIn:"Mexico City, Mexico.", imdbId:"0596663", born:date('1920-01-01'), name:"Carmen Molina", bio:"Carmen Molina was born in 1920.  She was a mexican actress, singer, and dancer...", died:date('1998-01-01'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/119301"}}, {tmdbId:"119302", properties:{imdbId:"0527741", name:"Dora Luz", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/119302"}}, {tmdbId:"34759", properties:{bornIn:"Cedartown, Georgia, USA", imdbId:"0001359", born:date('1905-01-04'), name:"Sterling Holloway", bio:"Sterling Price Holloway, Jr.  was an American character actor who appeared in 150 films and television programs.  He was also a voice actor for The Walt Disney Company.  He was well-known for his distinctive tenor voice, and is perhaps best remembered as the voice of Walt Disney's Winnie the Pooh...", died:date('1992-11-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qZt4J4yj645Ted9C38DzwQiQZYc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34759"}}, {tmdbId:"34421", properties:{imdbId:"0879000", born:date('1917-02-06'), name:"George Tyne", died:date('2008-03-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/x4TpIf1oA2EFk4inF85As8wDN5o.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34421"}}, {tmdbId:"89091", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0828668", born:date('1902-03-29'), name:"Onslow Stevens", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nOnslow Stevens (March 29, 1902 – January 5, 1977) was an American stage, television and film actor. \n\nStevens became involved in performing in 1926 at the Pasadena Community Playhouse, where his entire family worked as performers, directors and teachers. \n\nHis Broadway debut came in Stage Door (1936).  He starred over 80 films, at first as the lead actor, but mostly in character roles later in his career...", died:date('1977-01-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8RvAGGEr5GtZwEWeKHRWJgVCow6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89091"}}, {tmdbId:"35321", properties:{bornIn:"Huyton, Lancashire, England, UK", imdbId:"0001322", born:date('1908-03-05'), name:"Rex Harrison", bio:"Sir Reginald “Rex” Carey Harrison (5 March 1908 – 2 June 1990) was an English actor of stage and screen.  Harrison won both an Academy Award and a Tony Award...", died:date('1990-06-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hy8cyCpmV0iRSl4Thby01anz4FY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/35321"}}, {tmdbId:"85737", properties:{bornIn:"Mankato, Minnesota", imdbId:"0396633", born:date('1889-05-07'), name:"Billy House", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBilly House (May 7, 1889 – September 23, 1961) was an US vaudevillian, Broadway performer and feature film actor.  After devoting most of his career to live performance, he moved to Hollywood where he became a supporting actor during the 1940s and 1950s.  According to Orson Welles, the name \"Billy House\" was likely an invention for use in burlesque theatres...", died:date('1961-09-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/a65kGjTWTFWC4N5qTZBkdDJcp0E.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85737"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"100074", properties:{bornIn:"Edinburgh, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0292219", born:date('1913-03-15'), name:"Richard Fraser", bio:"Early life\n\nAfter graduating from Sedbergh School as Richard Mackie Simpson, Richard's mother Margaret Kyd Mackie divorced and his name was shortened to Richard Mackie.  After attending Cambridge University, Richard Mackie studied acting at the Royal Academy of Dramatic Art.  Having Spent time as a London stage actor, Richard emigrated to the USA and in New York married Louise Christine Sheldon, the couple then moved to Hollywood before the Second World War...", died:date('1972-01-19'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100074"}}, {tmdbId:"9741", properties:{bornIn:"Cherbourg, Manche, France", imdbId:"0544786", born:date('1913-12-11'), name:"Jean Marais", bio:"Jean-Alfred Villain-Marais (11 December 1913 – 8 November 1998), was a French actor and director. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jean Marais, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1998-11-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/68SthRQ494vF0GzXTpXflTCY8LP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9741"}}, {tmdbId:"9742", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0196816", born:date('1914-07-31'), name:"Josette Day", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJosette Day (July 31, 1914 - June 27, 1978) was a French film actress. \n\nBorn in Paris, she began her career as an actress in 1919 at the age of five.  Day was married in 1941 to famous French studio head Marcel Pagnol, who she met in January 1939. \n\nIn 1946, she played her best-known role, alongside Jean Marais, as Belle in director Jean Cocteau's famous take on the classic French fairytale Beauty and the Beast...", died:date('1978-06-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qT3NV4okYlFOT8k2C6YZ7NkVdbj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9742"}}, {tmdbId:"9745", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, Ile-de-France, France", imdbId:"0314590", born:date('1909-06-10'), name:"Nane Germon", died:date('2001-03-06'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9745"}}, {tmdbId:"13975", properties:{bornIn:"Ann Arbor, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0896015", born:date('1925-05-28'), name:"Martha Vickers", bio:"Martha Vickers (born Martha MacVicar) was an American film and television actress...", died:date('1971-11-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/V9BW15Ka9tDUtBCf4lqJcG19b4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13975"}}, {tmdbId:"38231", properties:{bornIn:"Harrods, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0898687", born:date('1920-07-17'), name:"June Vincent", died:date('2008-11-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zo7NC08Tw9EtVBvu1Q46EThTQ5S.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/38231"}}, {tmdbId:"85895", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0002024", born:date('1911-12-09'), name:"Broderick Crawford", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.  Broderick Crawford (December 9, 1911 – April 26, 1986) was an Academy Award-winning American stage, film, radio and TV actor, often cast in tough-guy roles and best known for his starring role in the television series \"Highway Patrol. \"\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Broderick Crawford, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1986-04-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ayyZGl7LJa9d6QC62oEoqUYFr0n.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85895"}}, {tmdbId:"19022", properties:{bornIn:"Seattle, Washington, USA", imdbId:"0191870", born:date('1910-05-15'), name:"Constance Cummings", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nConstance Cummings, CBE (May 15, 1910 – November 23, 2005) was an American-born British actress, known for her work on both screen and stage. \n\nBorn Constance Halverstadt in Seattle, Washington to Dallas Halverstadt and Kate Cummings, she began as a stage actress, landing her first role on Broadway by the age of 18.  While appearing on Broadway, she was discovered by Sam Goldwyn, who brought her to Hollywood in 1931...", died:date('2005-11-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nfGnC9P3FTrK0YKmFtg4n3vMxvC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19022"}}, {tmdbId:"87858", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0358723", born:date('1909-02-18'), name:"Kay Hammond", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Dorothy Katherine Standing (18 February 1909 - 4 May 1980), better known under the stage name Kay Hammond, was an English stage and film actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Kay Hammond, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1980-05-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5Tmqy8R2Ao4wUm826W17ioRPaZe.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/87858"}}, {tmdbId:"11127", properties:{bornIn:"Balham, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0751983", born:date('1892-05-11'), name:"Margaret Rutherford", bio:"Dame Margaret Taylor Rutherford DBE (11 May 1892 – 22 May 1972) was an English character actress, who first came to prominence following World War II in the film adaptations of Noel Coward's Blithe Spirit, and Oscar Wilde's The Importance of Being Earnest.  She is best-known for her 1960s performances as Miss Marple in several films based loosely on Agatha Christie's novels...", died:date('1972-05-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fRoihdvOhIqFWjLPS0DCfdwmjLA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11127"}}, {tmdbId:"3381", properties:{bornIn:" Quebec City, Quebec, Canada ", imdbId:"0001229", born:date('1916-05-01'), name:"Glenn Ford", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGlenn Ford (May 1, 1916 – August 30, 2006) was a Canadian-born American actor from Hollywood's Golden Era with a career that spanned seven decades.  Despite his versatility, Ford was best known for playing ordinary men in unusual circumstances. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Glenn Ford, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2006-08-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8POh9BUezZCXWJOVjP5ie8sw2EG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3381"}}, {tmdbId:"14564", properties:{bornIn:"Providence, Rhode Island, USA", imdbId:"0534317", born:date('1899-08-29'), name:"George Macready", bio:"George Peabody Macready, Jr.  (August 29, 1899 – July 2, 1973) was an American stage, film, and television actor often cast in roles as polished villains. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article George Macready, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1973-07-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eP74tyPu3qMVApVN7kSwJfGXBF8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14564"}}, {tmdbId:"29655", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0312890", born:date('1905-08-09'), name:"Leo Genn", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLeo John Genn (9 August 1905 – 26 January 1978) was a British stage and film actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Leo Genn, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1978-01-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qN8a2Esr843C5UeJgPRQwRVM96X.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29655"}}, {tmdbId:"47657", properties:{bornIn:"Weston-Super-Mare, Somerset, England, UK", imdbId:"0250038", born:date('1882-09-18'), name:"Henry Edwards", died:date('1952-11-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/AgdhycpBbTJHMIfQ6KwujHxYR5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/47657"}}, {tmdbId:"104302", properties:{bornIn:"Bromyard, England, UK", imdbId:"0010580", born:date('1896-12-31'), name:"Ronald Adam", died:date('1979-03-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mD8zf8SdsreKNW6lN2hmtG1hBRA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/104302"}}, {tmdbId:"85437", properties:{bornIn:"Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, U.S.", imdbId:"0388303", born:date('1914-04-16'), name:"John Hodiak", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJohn Hodiak (April 16, 1914 – October 19, 1955) was an American actor who worked in radio and film. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article John Hodiak, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1955-10-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6usASE7IWXyS4eVy5ZINbCnknSo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85437"}}, {tmdbId:"25787", properties:{bornIn:"Grabtown, North Carolina, USA", imdbId:"0001257", born:date('1922-12-24'), name:"Ava Gardner", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAva Lavinia Gardner (December 24, 1922 – January 25, 1990) was an American actress. \n\nShe was signed to a contract by MGM Studios in 1941 and appeared in small roles until she drew attention with her performance in The Killers (1946).  She became one of Hollywood's leading actresses, considered one of the most beautiful women of her day.  She was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Actress for her work in Mogambo (1953)...", died:date('1990-01-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nVA3wB8xnV7GdHKSIEk7AeN2FtI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25787"}}, {tmdbId:"8254", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0639529", born:date('1915-09-10'), name:"Edmond O'Brien", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEdmond O'Brien (September 10, 1915 – May 9, 1985) was an Academy Award-winning American film actor who is perhaps best remembered for his role in D. O. A.  (1950).  His many memorable films included The Killers, White Heat, The Man Who Shot Liberty Valance and The Wild Bunch. \n\nHe also co-starred with Richard Rust in the NBC legal drama Sam Benedict, which aired during the 1962-1963 television season...", died:date('1985-05-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6qHu8P9ZEJ8zm7TCCvZmyrBx83T.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8254"}}, {tmdbId:"2755", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0215260", born:date('1905-12-20'), name:"Albert Dekker", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAlbert Dekker (December 20, 1905 – May 5, 1968) was an American character actor and politician best known for his roles in Dr.  Cyclops, The Killers, Kiss Me Deadly, and The Wild Bunch.  He is sometimes credited as Albert Van Dekker or Albert van Dekker. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Albert Dekker, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1968-05-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pgvLnzm4NuJQZiSRVhpQDz8QUYT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2755"}}, {tmdbId:"137829", properties:{bornIn:"Winchester, Tennessee, USA", imdbId:"0794918", born:date('1916-02-29'), name:"Dinah Shore", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDinah Shore (born Frances Rose Shore; February 29, 1916 – February 24, 1994) was an American singer, actress, and television personality.  She was most popular during the Big Band era of the 1940s and 1950s. \n\nAfter failing singing auditions for the bands of Benny Goodman and both Jimmy Dorsey and his brother Tommy Dorsey, Shore struck out on her own to become the first singer of her era to achieve huge solo success...", died:date('1994-02-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zNCOXEgX6qsOisgwiTOU5vpCdWv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/137829"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"82408", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago - Illinois - USA", imdbId:"0329015", born:date('1909-05-30'), name:"Benny Goodman", bio:"The King of Swing! Famed clarinetist, composer (\"Stompin' at the Savoy\")  and conductor, educated at the Lewis Institute in Chicago and a student  of Schillinger and Schoepp.  He was a clarinetist with the orchestras of  Bix Beiderbecke, Jules Herbuveaux, Arnold Johnson and Ben Pollack,  and also played in Broadway theater orchestras...", died:date('1986-06-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7fOfiNRNe677BMhnGTZLvJ6fErd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82408"}}, {tmdbId:"30290", properties:{bornIn:"Louisville, Kentucky, USA", imdbId:"0001514", born:date('1913-01-29'), name:"Victor Mature", bio:"Victor John Mature was an American stage, film and television actor. \n\nIn July 1942 Mature attempted to enlist in the U. S.  Navy but was rejected for color blindness.  He enlisted in the U. S.  Coast Guard after taking a different eye test the same day.  He was assigned to the USCGC Storis (WMEC-38), which was doing Greenland patrol work.  After 14 months aboard the Storis, Mature was promoted to the rate of Chief Boatswain's Mate.  In 1944 he did a series of War Bond tours and acted in morale shows...", died:date('1999-08-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aQpiinWT3QJQzLi7mWbW45kXXPz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30290"}}, {tmdbId:"30291", properties:{bornIn:"Port Jefferson, Long Island, New York, USA", imdbId:"0236157", born:date('1926-03-03'), name:"Cathy Downs", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nCathy Downs (March 3, 1924 – December 8, 1976) was an American film actress. \n\nBorn in Port Jefferson, New York, Downs began her film career with a small role in The Dolly Sisters (1945) and the following year played the title role in My Darling Clementine.  Following the success of the latter, Downs was cast in a prison drama For You I Die (1947), an Abbott &amp; Costello comedy The Noose Hangs High, and several western films...", died:date('1976-12-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2Af6o8FuDE3igTZuLM6XGl5bE14.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30291"}}, {tmdbId:"4343", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn [now in New York City], New York, USA", imdbId:"0129894", born:date('1895-02-19'), name:"Louis Calhern", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nCarl Henry Vogt (February 19, 1895 – May 12, 1956), known professionally as Louis Calhern, was an American stage and screen actor.  For portraying Oliver Wendell Holmes in the film The Magnificent Yankee (1950), he was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Actor.   Calhern began working in silent films for director Lois Weber in the early 1920s; the most notable being The Blot in 1921...", died:date('1956-05-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/80l4tBYFQ08GLFk9wjilThyM8H.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4343"}}, {tmdbId:"54929", properties:{imdbId:"0768578", name:"Carmela Sazio", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54929"}}, {tmdbId:"54930", properties:{imdbId:"0887449", name:"Robert Van Loon", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54930"}}, {tmdbId:"54931", properties:{imdbId:"0256457", name:"Benjamin Emanuel", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54931"}}, {tmdbId:"54932", properties:{imdbId:"0132797", name:"Raymond Campbell", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54932"}}, {tmdbId:"30228", properties:{bornIn:"Cape Town, South Africa", imdbId:"0445523", born:date('1890-08-22'), name:"Cecil Kellaway", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nCecil Lauriston Kellaway (22 August 1890 – 28 February 1973) was a South African-born character actor. \n\nCecil Kellaway spent many years as an actor, author, and director in the Australian film industry until he tried his luck in Hollywood in the 1930s.  Finding he could get only gangster bit parts, he got discouraged and returned to Australia.  Then William Wyler called and offered him a part in Wuthering Heights (1939)...", died:date('1973-02-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rGVj5ODGkAxEllJt2JZTtO7doIj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30228"}}, {tmdbId:"7668", properties:{bornIn:"London, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0002025", born:date('1911-07-19'), name:"Hume Cronyn", bio:"Hume Blake Cronyn, Jr. , OC (July 18, 1911 – June 15, 2003) was a Canadian actor of stage and screen, who enjoyed a long career, often appearing professionally alongside Jessica Tandy, his wife of over fifty years...", died:date('2003-06-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2Tdh3cbagprrV0wN6q96u8wTTNJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7668"}}, {tmdbId:"4420", properties:{bornIn:"Rome, Lazio, Italy", imdbId:"0264762", born:date('1905-11-01'), name:"Aldo Fabrizi", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAldo Fabrizi (November 1, 1905, Rome, Italy – April 2, 1990, Rome, Italy) was an Italian actor and cinema and theatre director...", died:date('1990-04-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kiepVXPAObnzcUqTuuvHfak0vBM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4420"}}, {tmdbId:"4421", properties:{bornIn:"Rome, Italy", imdbId:"0536167", born:date('1908-03-07'), name:"Anna Magnani", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAnna Magnani (pronounced: mahn-YANEE; 7 March 1908 – 26 September 1973) was an Italian stage and film actress.  She won the Academy Award for Best Actress, along with four other international awards, for her portrayal of a Sicilian widow in The Rose Tattoo. \n\nBorn in Rome to an Egyptian father and an Italian mother, she worked her way through Rome's Academy of Dramatic Art by singing at night clubs...", died:date('1973-09-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ygpE4VtT0TtrF2mfceJBT8u2Nhh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4421"}}, {tmdbId:"4422", properties:{bornIn:" London, England, UK", imdbId:"0656496", born:date('1907-01-15'), name:"Marcello Pagliero", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMarcello Pagliero (15 January 1907 – 18 October 1980) was an Italian film director, actor, and screenwriter. \n\nPagliero was born in London and died in Paris.  He is perhaps best known for his performance in the Roberto Rossellini film Rome, Open City (1945). \n\nHe moved to France in 1947, and continued to work in film until 1960 and in French television after that...", died:date('1980-10-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lXAv4nx1KkvZFohYn7fi5SFZRVO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4422"}}, {tmdbId:"4423", properties:{imdbId:"0030383", name:"Vito Annichiarico", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/s4yAkoTsZbOziTFbzmBSTN7GV9G.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4423"}}, {tmdbId:"50997", properties:{bornIn:"Cedar Rapids, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0237985", born:date('1937-03-03'), name:"Bobby Driscoll", bio:"Bobby Driscoll was an American child and young-adult actor whose substantial career included work on the screen, television, stage, and radio.  The 1949 films So Dear to My Heart and The Window earned him an Academy Award as the year's outstanding juvenile actor.  His career and life eventually gradually went into decline.  In late 1961, addicted to drugs (having begun using when 17), he was sentenced to prison.  In 1965, a year after his parole expired, he relocated to New York City...", died:date('1968-03-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9wObiIeS3eRzWotKPpp7M4MfHPZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/50997"}}, {tmdbId:"137831", properties:{bornIn:"Long Beach, California, USA", imdbId:"0666087", born:date('1938-07-06'), name:"Luana Patten", died:date('1996-05-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/p7rNFi5qTidBvUiIYoeCmcxSftN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/137831"}}, {tmdbId:"24815", properties:{bornIn:"Omaha, Nebraska, USA", imdbId:"0570192", born:date('1916-06-14'), name:"Dorothy McGuire", bio:"Dorothy Hackett McGuire (June 14, 1916 – September 13, 2001) was an American actress from the 1940s to 1990.  Some of her movies include: Gentleman's Agreement (nominated for the Best Actress Academy Award for this film), The Enchanted Cottage, A Tree Grows in Brooklyn, and Old Yeller (as the mother).  She passed away in 2001 at the age of 85...", died:date('2001-09-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ilzwbgMD8rHZ1wNKI4Roi4GNrGi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24815"}}, {tmdbId:"97777", properties:{bornIn:" Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0000856", born:date('1879-08-15'), name:"Ethel Barrymore", bio:"Ethel Barrymore was the second of three children seemingly destined for  the actor's life of their parents Maurice and Georgiana.  Maurice  Barrymore had emigrated from England in 1875, and after graduating from  Cambridge in law had shocked his family by becoming an actor.  Georgiana  Drew of Philadelphia acted in her parents' stage company.  The two met  and married as members of Augustin Daly's  company in New York...", died:date('1959-06-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2YrpVZCBUHUSuNJbtTOp4TgAsa2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/97777"}}, {tmdbId:"83796", properties:{bornIn:"Scranton, Pennsylvania, U.S.", imdbId:"0779507", born:date('1922-09-29'), name:"Lizabeth Scott", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLizabeth Virginia Scott (September 29, 1922 – January 31, 2015) was an American film actress, known for her \"smoky voice\" and \"the most beautiful face of film noir during the 1940s and 1950s...", died:date('2015-01-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/79FcLzTM156S9nDm2dU1Lh5QPIN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83796"}}, {tmdbId:"2090", properties:{bornIn:"Amsterdam, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000018", born:date('1916-12-09'), name:"Kirk Douglas", bio:"Kirk Douglas (born Issur Danielovitch; December 9, 1916 – February 5, 2020) was an American actor, producer, director and author.  He grew up as Izzy Demsky and legally changed his name to Kirk Douglas before entering the United States Navy during World War II.  During his career, Douglas appeared in more than 90 movies and was known for his explosive acting style...", died:date('2020-02-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tsuLHw2TD8EtvIAEgYQu9l2kQkC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2090"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"85848", properties:{bornIn:"Salt Lake City, Utah, USA", imdbId:"0949835", born:date('1913-01-06'), name:"Loretta Young", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nLoretta Young (January 6, 1913 – August 12, 2000) was an American actress.  Starting as a child actress, she had a long and varied career in film from 1917 to 1953.  She won the 1948 best actress Academy Award for her role in the 1947 film The Farmer's Daughter, and received an Oscar nomination for her role in Come to the Stable, in 1950...", died:date('2000-08-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oPImBlHIgWeKeYBkfGbAaRtYyaQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85848"}}, {tmdbId:"105007", properties:{bornIn:"Rehutia, Manickpur, India", imdbId:"0580882", born:date('1886-11-02'), name:"Philip Merivale", bio:"Philip Merivale was born on November 2, 1886 in Rehutia, Manickpur, India.  He was an actor and writer, known for The Stranger (1946), Mr.  & Mrs.  Smith (1941) and Sister Kenny (1946).  He was married to Gladys Cooper and Viva Birkett.  He died on March 12, 1946 in Los Angeles, California, USA...", died:date('1946-03-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yj7rYzBcz2sLRsMIUIklF4JnOcP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/105007"}}, {tmdbId:"70036", properties:{imdbId:"0418741", born:date('1934-09-27'), name:"Claude Jarman Jr.", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qRPUgk3FP6Agm5RhCLz09zSbFF8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70036"}}, {tmdbId:"14001", properties:{bornIn:"Seagoville, Texas, U.S.", imdbId:"0932629", born:date('1902-07-18'), name:"Chill Wills", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nChill Theodore Wills (July 18, 1902 – December 15, 1978) was an American film actor, and a singer in the Avalon Boys Quartet. \n\nHe was a performer from early childhood, forming and leading the Avalon Boys singing group in the 1930s.  After appearing in a few westerns he disbanded the group in 1938, and struck out on a solo acting career. \n\nOne of his more memorable roles was that of the distinctive voice of Francis the Mule in a series of popular films...", died:date('1978-12-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/AuPtl5YaRlHzGYPdCZHIKqdFyJG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14001"}}, {tmdbId:"80469", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0751149", born:date('1924-09-21'), name:"Gail Russell", bio:"Gail Russell was an American screen and television actress who is probably best remembered for her role as Stella Meredith in the 1944 film The Uninvited...", died:date('1961-08-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7l30nC4KPBJl6IcIJ5nW0dWEWbP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80469"}}, {tmdbId:"30212", properties:{bornIn:"The Bronx, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0002503", born:date('1878-01-16'), name:"Harry Carey", bio:"Born in New York City to a Judge of Special Sessions who was also  president of a sewing machine company.  Grew up on City Island, New York.   Attended Hamilton Military Academy and turned down an appointment to  West Point to attend New York University, where his law school  classmates included future New York City mayor James J.  Walker...", died:date('1947-09-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/anb733JSA0OPnYEnWRFdztKuncw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30212"}}, {tmdbId:"20141", properties:{bornIn:"Helensburgh, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0000039", born:date('1921-09-30'), name:"Deborah Kerr", bio:"Born Deborah Jane Kerr-Trimmer in Scotland in 1921, she was the daughter of a soldier who had been gassed in World War I.  A shy, insecure child, she found an outlet for expressing her feelings in acting.  Her aunt, a radio star, got her some stage work when she was a teenager, and she came to the attention of British film producer Gabriel Pascal, who cast her in his film of George Bernard Shaw's \"Major Barbara\" (Major Barbara (1941)) and Love on the Dole (1941)...", died:date('2007-10-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8yQXQlSOlHMZ9rLf9DP6YbWHjS0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20141"}}, {tmdbId:"101514", properties:{imdbId:"0481966", born:date('1917-02-13'), name:"Jenny Laird", died:date('2001-10-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zEPHtONOCHPM7LqcAkc503lBihz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101514"}}, {tmdbId:"40947", properties:{bornIn:"Camberley, Surrey, England, UK", imdbId:"0299093", born:date('1912-03-04'), name:"Judith Furse", bio:"Judith Furse (4 March 1912 - 29 August 1974) was an English actress...", died:date('1974-08-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/e054LhwQ9wPKXDU4dFYb2l3BwtK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/40947"}}, {tmdbId:"27932", properties:{bornIn:"Posen, Germany", imdbId:"0658339", born:date('1914-05-24'), name:"Lilli Palmer", bio:"Lilli Palmer  was a German actress and writer.  She won the Volpi Cup, the Deutscher Filmpreis three times, and was nominated twice for a Golden Globe Award...", died:date('1986-01-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1geMK7mL8vQ71riZuMEI3ZEbkcY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27932"}}, {tmdbId:"81971", properties:{bornIn:"Città del Capo, Sudafrica", imdbId:"0112014", born:date('1924-09-08'), name:"Hazel Brooks", died:date('2002-09-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3I2OshPLLaDQjpnHT9cGgmfSNJS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81971"}}, {tmdbId:"8253", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0752813", born:date('1909-11-11'), name:"Robert Ryan", bio:"Robert Bushnell Ryan (November 11, 1909 – July 11, 1973) was an American  actor who often played hardened cops and ruthless villains. \n\nRyan was born in Chicago, Illinois, the first child of Timothy Ryan and his wife Mabel Bushnell Ryan.   He graduated from Dartmouth College in 1932, having held the school's heavyweight boxing title all four years of his attendance.  After graduation, the 6'4\" Ryan found employment as a stoker on a ship, a WPA worker, and a ranch hand in Montana...", died:date('1973-07-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/l0dFzaqeGvvZSXB7B6Yo0CDNxHP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8253"}}, {tmdbId:"77081", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0002108", born:date('1923-11-28'), name:"Gloria Grahame", bio:"Gloria Grahame (November 28, 1923 – October 5, 1981) was an American actress. \n\nGrahame began her acting career in theatre, and in 1944 she made her first film for MGM.  Despite a featured role in It's a Wonderful Life (1946), MGM did not believe she had the potential for major success, and sold her contract to RKO Studios...", died:date('1981-10-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2kVTJO8TVF5zHkKrbJi2IPcZe2p.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77081"}}, {tmdbId:"31977", properties:{bornIn:"St. Louis, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0138885", born:date('1897-09-05'), name:"Morris Carnovsky", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMorris Carnovsky (September 5, 1897 – September 1, 1992) was an American stage and film actor born in St.  Louis, Missouri.  He worked briefly in the Yiddish theatre before attending Washington University in St.  Louis.  Opting for a mainstream acting career, he appeared in dozens of Broadway shows. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Morris Carnovsky, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1992-09-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2I2o2LrjnY37ptKSQwOvFFG1zkL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31977"}}, {tmdbId:"86402", properties:{bornIn:"St. Louis, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0133802", born:date('1899-04-18'), name:"Charles Cane", died:date('1973-11-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vc5xFe2MJuK1lzDNBZtsqNxVVJP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/86402"}}, {tmdbId:"93902", properties:{bornIn:"Stockholm, Sweden", imdbId:"0368516", born:date('1915-08-15'), name:"Signe Hasso", bio:"Signe Hasso was a Swedish-born American actress, writer and composer...", died:date('2002-06-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5n1w9tknGAg4wvtziRe6Li5LWqv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/93902"}}, {tmdbId:"7632", properties:{bornIn:"St. Louis, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0001859", born:date('1920-08-18'), name:"Shelley Winters", bio:"Shelley Winters (born Shirley Schrift; August 18, 1920 – January 14, 2006) was an American actress whose career spanned almost six decades.  She appeared in numerous films, and won Academy Awards for The Diary of Anne Frank (1959) and A Patch of Blue (1965), and received nominations for A Place in the Sun (1951) and The Poseidon Adventure (1972)...", died:date('2006-01-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5jFYpqDBIkXfJ9AepHE4QPHUJJC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7632"}}, {tmdbId:"101879", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0001944", born:date('1903-02-16'), name:"Edgar Bergen", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nEdgar John Bergen (born Edgar John Berggren, February 16, 1903 – September 30, 1978) was an American actor, comedian and radio performer, best known for his proficiency in ventriloquism and his characters Charlie McCarthy and Mortimer Snerd.  He was the father of actress Candice Bergen...", died:date('1978-09-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hk4RCdmNGStJUkgnm2nZ8BfMH4r.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101879"}}, {tmdbId:"10607", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0002141", born:date('1917-04-29'), name:"Celeste Holm", died:date('2012-07-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gZmCGQayug4ZHPEopj7RxGvLKmF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10607"}}, {tmdbId:"53627", properties:{imdbId:"0595531", name:"Edmund Moeschke", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6GxJvsWVl3XgyHOLHLzH22VcEbz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53627"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"53628", properties:{bornIn:"Hamburg, Germany", imdbId:"0686035", born:date('1883-10-05'), name:"Ernst Pittschau", died:date('1951-06-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/e7M7OYrA9dqTPaWCVr81H8bIvZM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53628"}}, {tmdbId:"53629", properties:{imdbId:"0386085", name:"Ingetraud Hinze", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nw3QvbCXDosk8M5JJDVO2MvR31.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53629"}}, {tmdbId:"52109", properties:{bornIn:"Berlin, Germany", imdbId:"0473223", born:date('1917-04-01'), name:"Franz-Otto Krüger", died:date('1988-03-17'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/52109"}}, {tmdbId:"3336", properties:{bornIn:"Staplehurst, Nebraska, U.S.", imdbId:"0336531", born:date('1922-10-23'), name:"Coleen Gray", bio:"Coleen Gray (born Doris Bernice Jensen; October 23, 1922 – August 3, 2015) was born in Staplehurst, Nebraska.  After graduating from high school she studied dramatics at Hamline University, graduating with a Bachelor of Arts degree, she then decided to see America and traveled to California, stopping off at La Jolla where she worked as a waitress.  After several weeks there, she moved to L. A.  and enrolled in a drama school...", died:date('2015-08-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9DLWFJofnWiXlzIBVweDRRPed90.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3336"}}, {tmdbId:"12149", properties:{bornIn:"Sunrise Township, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0001847", born:date('1914-12-26'), name:"Richard Widmark", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRichard Widmark (December 26, 1914 – March 24, 2008) was an American actor of films, stage, radio and television. \n\nHe was nominated for an Academy Award for his role as the villainous Tommy Udo in his debut film, Kiss of Death.  Early in his career Widmark specialized in similar villainous or anti-hero roles in films noir, but he later branched out into more heroic leading and support roles in westerns, mainstream dramas and horror films, among others...", died:date('2008-03-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tKtQMe37U9GTFOzSh0Qx5QSDK0E.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12149"}}, {tmdbId:"106569", properties:{bornIn:"Montréal, Québec, Canada", imdbId:"0180900", born:date('1907-04-19'), name:"Mady Correll", bio:"Mady Correll was born on April 19, 1907 in Montréal, Québec, Canada.  She was an actress, known for A Girl, a Guy, and a Gob (1941), Texas Masquerade (1944) and Monsieur Verdoux (1947).  She was married to Warren Ashe.  She died on December 18, 1981 in Los Angeles, California, USA...", died:date('1981-12-18'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/106569"}}, {tmdbId:"106570", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0734467", born:date('1941-05-06'), name:"Allison Roddan", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iQgXQtwOhr9E0uykZgNV3z4XfbO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/106570"}}, {tmdbId:"60063", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0507673", born:date('1909-03-16'), name:"Robert Lewis", bio:"Robert Lewis (1909 – 1997) was an American actor, director, teacher, author and founder of the Actors Studio in New York in 1947. \n\nIn addition to his accomplishments on Broadway and in Hollywood, Lewis' greatest and longest lasting contribution to American theater may be the role he played as one of the foremost acting and directing teachers of his day...", died:date('1997-11-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gXfuaw24fX4ckXdGlX8jLKSjwRY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/60063"}}, {tmdbId:"83475", properties:{bornIn:"Worcester, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0907785", born:date('1920-07-17'), name:"Helen Walker", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nHelen Walker (born July 17, 1920 – March 10, 1968) was an American movie actress of the 1940s and 1950s. \n\nShe was born in Worcester, Massachusetts and made her film debut in 1942.  After a promising start in Hollywood, Walker was involved in a 1946 car wreck.  A hitchhiker was killed, and Walker and two others were seriously injured, for which she was charged with drunk and reckless driving.  She made a comeback, but her career never fully recovered...", died:date('1968-03-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jXLKPyAHN7YmkQIpnbQkmmCkyLM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83475"}}, {tmdbId:"2091", properties:{bornIn:"Huddersfield, Yorkshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0000051", born:date('1909-05-15'), name:"James Mason", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJames Neville Mason (15 May 1909 – 27 July 1984) was an English actor who attained stardom in both British and American films.  Mason remained a powerful figure in the industry throughout his career and was nominated for three Academy Awards as well as three Golden Globes (winning once). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article James Mason, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1984-07-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ivmJl4jLgYoxI93EPgBehund505.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2091"}}, {tmdbId:"29520", properties:{bornIn:"Shaftesbury, Dorset, England", imdbId:"0628579", born:date('1905-06-01'), name:"Robert Newton", bio:"Robert Newton was an English stage and film actor.  Along with Errol Flynn, Newton was one of the most popular actors among the male juvenile audience of the 1940s and early 1950s, especially with British boys.  He was cited as a role model by actor Tony Hancock and drummer Keith Moon...", died:date('1956-03-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aIqHUa2cQO5G5UfObOxDfXrcCHE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29520"}}, {tmdbId:"4973", properties:{bornIn:"Durban, Natal, South Africa", imdbId:"0159258", born:date('1910-11-26'), name:"Cyril Cusack", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nCyril James Cusack (26 November 1910 – 7 October 1993) was an Irish actor, who appeared in more than 90 films. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Cyril Cusack, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1993-10-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aQiVDfLChtFpTo4BTxyoz1X74lI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4973"}}, {tmdbId:"131447", properties:{bornIn:"Dublin, Ireland", imdbId:"0431922", name:"F.J. McCormick", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nF.  J.  McCormick (real name Peter Judge) (1889 in Skerries, Ireland – 1947 in Dublin, Ireland) was an Irish actor who came to fame as part of Dublin's Abbey Theatre.  He was also in four films; most famously Carol Reed's Odd Man Out (1947), in which he played the opportunistic Shell.  He died in 1947 of a brain tumor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article F.  J.  McCormick, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1947-04-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6mb46WtiDNxNjRZRIfiPy16yhaI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/131447"}}, {tmdbId:"10159", properties:{bornIn:"Washington, D.C., United States", imdbId:"0339452", born:date('1924-09-09'), name:"Jane Greer", bio:"Jane Greer was a film and television actress who was perhaps best known for her role as femme fatale Kathie Moffat in the 1947 film noir Out of the Past. \n\nA beauty-contest winner and professional model from her teens, Greer began her show-business career as a big-band singer.  She sang in Washington, DC, with the orchestra of Enric Madriguera.  She \"sang phonetically in Spanish\" with the group...", died:date('2001-08-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eqnPmly09oLsaRdzShzXuOtiF3P.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10159"}}, {tmdbId:"10160", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0281766", born:date('1923-08-10'), name:"Rhonda Fleming", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRhonda Fleming (born Marilyn Louis, Hollywood, California, August 10, 1923) is an American film and television actress. \n\nShe acted in more than forty films, mostly in the 1940s and 1950s, and became renowned as one of the most glamorous actresses of her day.  She was nicknamed the \"Queen of Technicolor\" because her fair complexion and flaming red hair photographed exceptionally well in Technicolor...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7V3he6CbG8kwEWmnww4Ex1spA2V.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10160"}}, {tmdbId:"100784", properties:{bornIn:"Hartford, Cheshire, England", imdbId:"0002897", born:date('1909-01-24'), name:"Ann Todd", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDorothy Anne Todd (24 January 1907, Hartford, Cheshire – 6 May 1993, London) was an English actress and producer. \n\nShe was born in Hartford, Cheshire and was educated at St.  Winifrid's School, Eastbourne.  She became a popular actress from appearing in such films as Perfect Strangers (1945) (as a nurse) and The Seventh Veil (1945) (as a troubled concert pianist)...", died:date('1993-05-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dljzNAQi385qDQ8aVH2FEWtBjJv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100784"}}, {tmdbId:"97182", properties:{bornIn:"Battle Creek, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0002149", born:date('1921-02-26'), name:"Betty Hutton", bio:"Betty Hutton (February 26, 1921 – March 11, 2007) was an American stage, film, and television actress, comedienne and singer...", died:date('2007-03-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/p0U4UFN75rlV6jl7W2QG6aqFMfl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/97182"}}, {tmdbId:"95313", properties:{bornIn:"Rochester, New York, USA", imdbId:"0526184", born:date('1911-02-07'), name:"John Lund", bio:"John Lund (6 February 1911 - 10 May 1992) was an American film actor who is probably best remembered for his role in the film A Foreign Affair (1948), directed by Billy Wilder...", died:date('1992-05-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hWSxn2X6Cs1S40P9tN3S7CVeUMB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95313"}}, {tmdbId:"110135", properties:{imdbId:"0212461", born:date('1907-02-18'), name:"Billy De Wolfe", died:date('1974-03-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9MTgNNz688CFeK3BB78RrDuFcAC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/110135"}}, {tmdbId:"86641", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0111997", born:date('1925-10-29'), name:"Geraldine Brooks", died:date('1977-06-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qLb4QcPRlDxkFyQsWzmAfhy9i5C.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/86641"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"109345", properties:{bornIn:"Crozon, France", imdbId:"0431212", born:date('1887-12-24'), name:"Louis Jouvet", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLouis Jouvet (24 December 1887 - 16 August 1951) was a renowned French actor, director, and theatre director. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Louis Jouvet, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1951-08-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/x38oBn5ccdG8IA2b4TGf66x2OGR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/109345"}}, {tmdbId:"34615", properties:{bornIn:"Amiens, Somme, Picardie, France", imdbId:"0719135", born:date('1911-03-19'), name:"Simone Renant", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSimone Renant (19 March 1911 – 29 March 2004) was a French film actress.  She appeared in 43 films between 1934 and 1983.  She was born in Amiens, France and died in Garches, France. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Simone Renant, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2004-03-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uCFsiPGebOk3DhL61XXE6ejbnkn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34615"}}, {tmdbId:"24379", properties:{bornIn:"Buenos Aires, Argentina", imdbId:"0088396", born:date('1916-01-11'), name:"Bernard Blier", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nBernard Blier (11 January 1916 – 29 March 1989) was a French character actor.  His rotund features and premature baldness allowed him to often play cuckolded husbands in his early career.  He proved to be one of France's most versatile and sought-after character actors, performing interchangeably in comedies and dramas.  He often worked in Italian films, particularly in the last decade of his life...", died:date('1989-03-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4lnE5NCisXPNQ6dnO6ewaIcEyiG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24379"}}, {tmdbId:"11188", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, Ile-de-France, France", imdbId:"0216177", born:date('1917-12-31'), name:"Suzy Delair", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSuzy Delair, born Suzanne Pierrette Declair (31 December 1917 - 15 March 2020) was a vivacious French entertainer who starred in many different films.  Her real name is Suzanne Pierrette Delaire. \n\nShe acted in films directed by Henri-Georges Clouzot, Jean Dréville, Jean Grémillon, Marcel L'Herbier, Christian-Jaque, Marcel Carné, Luchino Visconti, René Clément and Gérard Oury.  She is also famous in France as singer (\"Avec son Tra-la-la\")...", died:date('2020-03-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/AlLLqEaBmvpkcSUQBi9OcT5SAfP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11188"}}, {tmdbId:"38232", properties:{bornIn:"Kansas, USA", imdbId:"0064604", born:date('1909-02-16'), name:"Hugh Beaumont", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nEugene Hugh Beaumont (February 16, 1909 – May 14, 1982) was an American actor and television director.  He was also licensed to preach by the Methodist church.  Beaumont is best known for his portrayal of Ward Cleaver on the 1957-1963 television series Leave It to Beaver.  He had earlier played the role of the private detective Michael Shayne in a series of films in the 1940s...", died:date('1982-05-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/evE8f3kyy5NPN8Zijm16wxU9tSr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/38232"}}, {tmdbId:"70668", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001414", born:date('1911-01-18'), name:"Danny Kaye", bio:"Danny Kaye (born David Daniel Kaminsky; January 18, 1911 – March 3, 1987) was a celebrated American actor, singer, dancer, and comedian.  His best known performances featured physical comedy, idiosyncratic pantomimes, and rapid-fire nonsense songs. \n\nKaye starred in 17 movies, notably The Kid from Brooklyn (1946), The Secret Life of Walter Mitty (1947), The Inspector General (1949), Hans Christian Andersen (1952), and — perhaps his most accomplished performance — The Court Jester (1956)...", died:date('1987-03-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/atyzQdwbpX8zitXCInOBKjJbyp2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70668"}}, {tmdbId:"13579", properties:{bornIn:"St. Louis, Missouri, U.S.", imdbId:"0562920", born:date('1920-11-30'), name:"Virginia Mayo", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nVirginia Mayo (November 30, 1920 – January 17, 2005) was an American film actress.  After a short career in vaudeville, Mayo progressed to films and during the 1940s established herself as a supporting player in such films as The Best Years of Our Lives (1946) and White Heat (1949).  She worked extensively during the 1950s, but after this her appearances were fewer.  She worked occasionally until her final performance in 1997...", died:date('2005-01-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rlE1fh3KEzxxtBiP1gv4B2elzxW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13579"}}, {tmdbId:"923", properties:{bornIn:"North Hollywood, Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0001777", born:date('1936-03-05'), name:"Dean Stockwell", bio:"Dean Stockwell (born March 5, 1936) is an American actor of film and television, active for over 70 years.  He played Rear Admiral Albert \"Al\" Calavicci in the NBC television series Quantum Leap and in the Sci Fi Channel revival of Battlestar Galactica as Brother Cavil. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Dean Stockwell, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gdHo8LNElMf1XxoRYgi0UUzbJuB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/923"}}, {tmdbId:"94778", properties:{imdbId:"0574971", name:"Mary Meade", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94778"}}, {tmdbId:"15620", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0753086", born:date('1916-01-05'), name:"Alfred Ryder", died:date('1995-04-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bAZhNIshbrhbwykjwJnBcemmBjS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15620"}}, {tmdbId:"94097", properties:{imdbId:"0146542", born:date('1922-06-01'), name:"Joan Caulfield", bio:"Beatrice Joan Caulfield (June 1, 1922 – June 18, 1991) was an American actress and former fashion model.  After being discovered by Broadway producers, she began a stage career in 1943 that eventually led to signing as an actress with Paramount Pictures. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Monica Bellucci, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1991-06-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wmhKgpufRz55021mjAZcOxSIczr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94097"}}, {tmdbId:"19413", properties:{bornIn:"Joliet, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0869429", born:date('1917-12-21'), name:"Audrey Totter", bio:"Audrey Mary Totter (December 20, 1917 – December 12, 2013) is an American actress and former MGM contract star of Austrian-Slovene and Swedish descent.  Most references cite December 20, 1918 as her date of birth, although Intelius indicates the year was 1917. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Audrey Totter, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2013-12-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bMrbgF8AneUck5P1o1yZIVZ57uP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19413"}}, {tmdbId:"30111", properties:{bornIn:"Asbury Park, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0007941", born:date('1895-10-02'), name:"Bud Abbott", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nWilliam Alexander \"Bud\" Abbott (c.  1897 – April 24, 1974) was an American actor, producer and comedian. [1] He is best remembered as the straight man of the comedy team of Abbott and Costello, with Lou Costello...", died:date('1974-04-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wNL70NGLpZ0a3IwQ4mlieBIC8GQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30111"}}, {tmdbId:"29642", properties:{bornIn:"Paterson, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0182579", born:date('1906-03-06'), name:"Lou Costello", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLouis Francis Costello (March 6, 1906 – March 3, 1959) was an American actor and comedian best known as half of the comedy team of Abbott and Costello, with Bud Abbott.  Costello was famous for his bumbling, chubby, clean-cut image that has appealed to many Americans over the decades, and for his shouted line of \"HEEEEYYY ABBOTT!!...", died:date('1959-03-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3LgR3ZEcgJPRr91uvMsYfvVpDcB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29642"}}, {tmdbId:"15008", properties:{bornIn:"Houston, Texas, USA ", imdbId:"0587900", born:date('1923-04-12'), name:"Ann Miller", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJohnnie Lucille Collier (April 12, 1923 – January 22, 2004), known professionally as Ann Miller, was an American dancer, singer and actress.  She is best remembered for her work in the Classical Hollywood musical films of the 1940s and 1950s. \n\nAt age 13 in 1936, Miller became a showgirl at the Bal Tabarin.  She was hired as a dancer in the \"Black Cat Club\" in San Francisco (she reportedly told them she was 18)...", died:date('2004-01-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3IWXjk5Qc4RYBdPEQdQsyo20ymh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15008"}}, {tmdbId:"12689", properties:{bornIn:"Tivoli Road, Cheltenham, Gloucestershire, England, UK", imdbId:"0724732", born:date('1902-12-19'), name:"Ralph Richardson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSir Ralph David Richardson (19 December 1902 – 10 October 1983) was an English actor, one of a group of theatrical knights of the mid-20th century who, though more closely associated with the stage, also appeared in several classic films. \n\nRichardson first became known for his work on stage in the 1930s.  In the 1940s, together with Laurence Olivier, he ran the Old Vic company...", died:date('1983-10-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/meAOwvd6XIxvBXVXV7kuTOnCkqw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12689"}}, {tmdbId:"35254", properties:{bornIn:"Neuilly-sur-Seine, Seine [now Hauts-de-Seine], France", imdbId:"0006807", born:date('1920-02-29'), name:"Michèle Morgan", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMichèle Morgan (born 29 February 1920) is a French film actress, who was a leading lady for three decades. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Michèle Morgan, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2016-12-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yXPWF4sqVIsZbcS6iePquycsXoB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/35254"}}, {tmdbId:"87745", properties:{bornIn:"Hornsea, Yorkshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0237520", born:date('1909-05-05'), name:"Sonia Dresdel", bio:"Sonia Dresdel (5 May 1909 - 18 January 1976) was an English actress, whose career ran between the 1940s and 1970s. \n\nShe was born Lois Obee in Hornsea, East Riding of Yorkshire, England and was educated at Aberdeen High School for Girls. \n\nHer leading role in the 1947 film While I Live gained her a great deal of acclaim.  In the film she plays Julia Trevelyan, a spinster living in a lonely cliff top house in Cornwall and haunted by the death of her sister 25 years earlier...", died:date('1976-01-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vmpl8AMgVYjCqQzU8RRXgmFTRGa.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/87745"}}, {tmdbId:"87746", properties:{bornIn:"Villers-sur-Mer, Calvados, France", imdbId:"0377501", born:date('1939-06-26'), name:"Bobby Henrey", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Bobby Henrey (later Robert Henrey) was a child actor immortalised in two books written by his mother, the memoirist, Madeleine Henrey.  He starred in two films, The Fallen Idol (1948) and The Wonder Kid (1951).  In later life he moved to the United States and worked as a chaplain in Greenwich, Connecticut. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Bobby Henrey, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/87746"}}, {tmdbId:"18646", properties:{bornIn:"New York, City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0327089", born:date('1905-07-10'), name:"Thomas Gomez", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nThomas Gomez (July 10, 1905 – June 18, 1971) was an American actor. \n\nBorn Sabino Tomas Gomez in New York City, Gomez began his acting career in theater during the 1920s and was a student of the actor Walter Hampden.  He made his first film Sherlock Holmes and the Voice of Terror in 1942 and by the end of his career had appeared in sixty films...", died:date('1971-06-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/B8xqQSXSFUjlXydqMN2w6WdFiV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18646"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"3340", properties:{bornIn:"Marysvale, Utah, USA", imdbId:"0934798", born:date('1919-12-11'), name:"Marie Windsor", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMarie Windsor (born Emily Marie Bertelsen; December 11, 1919 – December 10, 2000) was an actress known as \"The Queen of the Bs\" because she appeared in so many B-movies and film noirs. \n\nAfter working for several years as a telephone operator, a stage and radio actress, and a bit and extra player in films, Windsor began playing feature parts on the big screen in 1947. \n\nHer first film contract, with Warner Bros...", died:date('2000-12-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nIGCLyRym5UUpo2CAZauojkCEJ0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3340"}}, {tmdbId:"96137", properties:{imdbId:"0150166", born:date('1911-08-02'), name:"Howland Chamberlain", died:date('1984-09-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ceIpblKuZ0jGPLZv1MkZK3qVv31.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96137"}}, {tmdbId:"3673", properties:{bornIn:"Dumfries, Dumfriesshire, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0491406", born:date('1897-03-25'), name:"John Laurie", bio:"John Laurie was a noted Scottish stage, screen, and television actor...", died:date('1980-06-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4mmgq0Mq8ycabV7BWwduAGMd265.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3673"}}, {tmdbId:"56875", properties:{bornIn:"East Sheen, Surrey, England", imdbId:"0460874", born:date('1906-05-04'), name:"Esmond Knight", bio:"Esmond Penington Knight (4 May 1906 – 23 February 1987) was an English actor. \n\nHe was an accomplished actor with a career spanning over half a century.  For much of his career Esmond Knight was virtually blind.  He had been badly injured in 1941 whilst on active service on board HMS Prince of Wales when she fought the Bismarck at the Battle of the Denmark Strait, and remained totally blind for two years, though he later regained some sight in his right eye...", died:date('1987-02-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ka4eJaGtMlghVQnVcQOFSFEb2uA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56875"}}, {tmdbId:"14371", properties:{bornIn:"Ainsdale, Southport, Lancashire, England", imdbId:"0703033", born:date('1913-09-07'), name:"Anthony Quayle", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSir John Anthony Quayle, CBE (7 September 1913 – 20 October 1989) was an English actor and director. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Anthony Quayle, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1989-10-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6hTRCasvtV0tjwba4HM7qg906NN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14371"}}, {tmdbId:"5403", properties:{bornIn:"Zanesville, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0000865", born:date('1914-08-13'), name:"Richard Basehart", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJohn Richard Basehart (August 31, 1914 – September 17, 1984) was an American actor.  He starred in the 1960s television science fiction drama Voyage to the Bottom of the Sea, in the role of Admiral Harriman Nelson. \n\nOne of his most notable film roles was the acrobat known as \"the Fool\" in the acclaimed Italian film La strada directed by Federico Fellini...", died:date('1984-09-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rlk0wF1UbQH7DPGmkXKd1tMzDWo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5403"}}, {tmdbId:"14847", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York", imdbId:"0103722", born:date('1924-09-13'), name:"Scott Brady", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nScott Brady (September 13, 1924 – April 16, 1985) was an American film and television actor.  Born as Gerard Kenneth Tierney, he was the younger brother of fellow actor Lawrence Tierney.  Brady served in the Navy during World War II, where he was a boxing champ.  After being discharged, he supported himself as a lumberjack, and began taking acting classes; he began his film career soon afterward...", died:date('1985-04-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/IfanKuKH88XKccqig6A3nanVKj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14847"}}, {tmdbId:"19400", properties:{imdbId:"0731507", born:date('1906-03-19'), name:"Roy Roberts", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRoy Roberts (born Roy Barnes Jones, March 19, 1906 – May 28, 1975) was an American character actor.  Over his more than 40-year career, he appeared in more than nine hundred productions on stage and screen...", died:date('1975-05-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nsbNzLtRwlLAyk88EJ3E7gngaCI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19400"}}, {tmdbId:"13786", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000946", born:date('1909-10-25'), name:"Whit Bissell", bio:"Whit Bissell (born Whitner Nutting Bissell) was an American character actor.  His career in film and television spanned the years 1940 to 1984...", died:date('1996-03-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/utFxx3j5J4zg7YMZ5Y0Bp4RBBFO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13786"}}, {tmdbId:"42416", properties:{bornIn:"Rome", imdbId:"0536009", born:date('1909-08-28'), name:"Lamberto Maggiorani", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nLamberto Maggiorani (28 August 1909; Rome – 22 April 1983; Rome) was an Italian actor notable for his portrayal of Antonio Ricci in Ladri di Biciclette (\"Bicycle Thieves\").  He was a factory worker (he worked as a turner) and non-professional actor at the time he was cast in this film.  After he became famous by his performance in Ladri di Biciclette, he also found himself being unemployed and this forced him to become a full-time actor...", died:date('1983-04-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qp3oZcD8UwTGRg1GiMMOyWLwSaX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/42416"}}, {tmdbId:"42417", properties:{bornIn:"Rome, Lazio, Italy", imdbId:"0821543", born:date('1939-11-15'), name:"Enzo Staiola", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nEnzo Staiola (born 15 November 1939) is an Italian actor best known for playing, at the age of seven, the role of Bruno Ricci, the son of protagonist Antonio Ricci in Vittorio De Sica's neorealist 1948 film Bicycle Thieves.  He appeared in several other films (including the American-produced The Barefoot Contessa in 1954, which starred Humphrey Bogart) before becoming a math teacher in adulthood...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/k64j9HlXiHIn0DJOUX9Uk8MCtAw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/42417"}}, {tmdbId:"42419", properties:{bornIn:"Rome, Italy", imdbId:"0136794", born:date('1927-05-06'), name:"Lianella Carell", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nLianella Carell (6 May 1927 – 22 December 2000) was an Italian film actress and screenwriter.  She appeared in 18 films between 1948 and 1958.  She is perhaps best known for playing Maria Ricci, the wife of the main protagonist in the 1948 Vittorio De Sica film Bicycle Thieves, which was also her acting debut. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article  Lianella Carell, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2000-12-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dbLf4dnEpapogvOYoe6Mm5rbWbG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/42419"}}, {tmdbId:"944148", properties:{bornIn:" Rome, Italy", imdbId:"0759031", born:date('1902-06-02'), name:"Gino Saltamerenda", bio:"Gino Saltamerenda was born on June 2, 1902 in Rome, Lazio, Italy as Luigi Saltamerenda.  He was an actor, known for Bicycle Thieves (1948), The Affairs of Messalina (1951) and Campane a martello (1949).  He died on September 25, 1951 in Rome...", died:date('1951-09-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xGSWaSgVYBTC2meKANoZp9JrM9S.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/944148"}}, {tmdbId:"11027", properties:{bornIn:"Manhattan, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0806041", born:date('1909-10-01'), name:"Everett Sloane", bio:"Everett Sloane (October 1, 1909 – August 6, 1965) was an American stage, film and television actor, songwriter, and theatre director. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Everett Sloane , licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1965-08-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/d3XQhnUWh1eLjh1uLaWEbIxGgey.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11027"}}, {tmdbId:"33742", properties:{imdbId:"0026011", born:date('1889-09-01'), name:"Glenn Anders", died:date('1981-10-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nNhlqPw7m4Px0bdFDzwKzu96Jmt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33742"}}, {tmdbId:"10508", properties:{bornIn:"Marseille, Bouches-du-Rhône, France", imdbId:"0431139", born:date('1921-06-20'), name:"Louis Jourdan", bio:"Louis Jourdan (born Louis Robert Gendre; 19 June 1921 – 14 February 2015) was a French film and television actor.  He was known for his suave roles in several Hollywood films, including Alfred Hitchcock's The Paradine Case (1947), Letter from an Unknown Woman (1948), Gigi (1958), The Best of Everything (1959), The V. I. P. s (1963) and Octopussy (1983).  He played Dracula in the 1977 BBC television production Count Dracula...", died:date('2015-02-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xCrLoRd1MR0puY386BRnPWAWTQ6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10508"}}, {tmdbId:"14357", properties:{bornIn:"Vienna, Austria-Hungary (now Austria)", imdbId:"0160130", born:date('1892-01-19'), name:"Mady Christians", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMarguerita Maria \"Mady\" Christians (January 19, 1892 – October 28, 1951) was an Austrian actress and naturalized US citizen who had a successful acting career in theatre and film in the United States until she was blacklisted during the McCarthy period.   She was born on January 19, 1892 to Rudolph Christians, a well-known German actor, and his wife, Bertha...", died:date('1951-10-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/c9sCssop7SESa6OxOGXY2P3JuSS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14357"}}, {tmdbId:"14358", properties:{imdbId:"0431169", born:date('1895-08-08'), name:"Marcel Journet", died:date('1973-02-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/942hs3rAnvZ4FVaasnEhXIBpW59.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14358"}}, {tmdbId:"3364", properties:{bornIn:"Richmond, Surrey, England, UK", imdbId:"0219666", born:date('1891-11-20'), name:"Reginald Denny", bio:"Reginald Denny (born Reginald Leigh Dugmore) was an English stage, screen, and television actor, as well as an aviator and unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV) pioneer...", died:date('1967-06-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/Jw7vvd8DrVS0RQiDMcnWU0Cr2D.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3364"}}, {tmdbId:"67616", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0203791", born:date('1939-03-09'), name:"John Howard Davies", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJohn Howard Davies  (born Paddington, London; 9 March 1939) is a British television director and producer and former child actor.  Davies was the son of the scriptwriter Jack Davies.  His credits as a child actor include the title role in David Lean's Oliver Twist (1948), The Rocking Horse Winner (1949), Tom Brown's Schooldays (1951) and a few episodes of the television series William Tell (1958)...", died:date('2011-08-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9wlkDHzZE6y5nGBeLO92wAFb4mR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67616"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"12248", properties:{bornIn:"Marylebone, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0000027", born:date('1914-04-02'), name:"Alec Guinness", bio:"Sir Alec Guinness, CH, CBE (2 April 1914 – 5 August 2000) was an English actor.  He was featured in several of the Ealing Comedies, including Kind Hearts and Coronets in which he played eight different characters.  He later won the Academy Award for Best Actor for his role as Colonel Nicholson in The Bridge on the River Kwai.  His is known for playing Obi-Wan Kenobi in the original Star Wars trilogy...", died:date('2000-08-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dddx1VI6l1Ge8SQEJz7rI8OSmkv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12248"}}, {tmdbId:"67615", properties:{bornIn:"Chelsea, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0909727", born:date('1911-11-15'), name:"Kay Walsh", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nKay Walsh  (born Kathleen Walsh, 15 November 1911,Chelsea, London, England; died 16 April 2005, Chelsea, London) was an English actress and dancer.  She grew up in Pimlico, brought up by her grandmother.  She began her career as a dancer in West End music halls.  Walsh made her film debut in How's Chances? (1934) in a small part, and had a larger role in another 1934 film, Get Your Man.  She continued to act in \"quota quickies\" films for several years...", died:date('2005-04-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2xjVvJoFczhz7aYRzre1rK2z434.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67615"}}, {tmdbId:"11165", properties:{bornIn:"Bemidji, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0000066", born:date('1921-06-21'), name:"Jane Russell", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJane Russell (June 21, 1921 – February 28, 2011) was an American film actress and was one of Hollywood's leading sex symbols in the 1940s and 1950s. \n\nRussell moved from the Midwest to California, where she had her first film role in 1943 with The Outlaw.  In 1947, Russell delved into music before returning to films.  After starring in multiple films in the 1950s, Russell again returned to music while completing several other films in the 1960s...", died:date('2011-02-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gjNlwyqY4zihLN5tD5nv0ATCB7n.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11165"}}, {tmdbId:"34509", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0012441", born:date('1912-05-29'), name:"Iris Adrian", bio:"Iris Adrian (born Iris Adrian Hostetter) was an American screen and stage actress and dancer, as well as television actress...", died:date('1994-09-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3EmN2KpUPy1AfB5QNQkF79HKBwO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34509"}}, {tmdbId:"1215925", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0402554", born:date('1917-10-17'), name:"Marsha Hunt", bio:"Marsha Hunt (born Marcia Virginia Hunt; October 17, 1917) is an American retired actress, model, and activist, with a career spanning over 70 years.  She was blacklisted by Hollywood film studio executives in the 1950s during McCarthyism. \n\nAlthough initially reluctant to pursue a film career, in June 1935, at age 17, Hunt signed a seven-year contract with Paramount Pictures...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/j3puYHooaHgKqafAWWrc0OxZyJW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1215925"}}, {tmdbId:"12151", properties:{bornIn:"Omaha, Nebraska, USA", imdbId:"0001050", born:date('1920-10-17'), name:"Montgomery Clift", bio:"Edward Montgomery Clift (October 17, 1920 – July 23, 1966) was an American actor.  The New York Times’ obituary noted his portrayal of \"moody, sensitive young men\". \n\nHe invariably played outsiders, often \"victim-heroes\" - examples include the social climber in George Stevens' A Place in the Sun, the anguished Catholic priest in Hitchcock's I Confess, the doomed regular soldier Robert E...", died:date('1966-07-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sWF3K2JvLWiA8WJ108sBMVV07UA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12151"}}, {tmdbId:"30296", properties:{bornIn:"Logan, West Virginia, USA", imdbId:"0238445", born:date('1922-01-31'), name:"Joanne Dru", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.  \n\nJoanne Dru (January 31, 1922 – September 10, 1996)  was an American film and television actress, known for such films as Red River and All the King's Men. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Joanne Dru, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1996-09-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/avhJYMT8DHUU6gEQZv4N6iH3xzC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30296"}}, {tmdbId:"14504", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0197982", born:date('1918-05-26'), name:"John Dall", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJohn Dall (May 26, 1918 – January 15, 1971) was an American actor. \n\nPrimarily a stage actor, he is best remembered today for two film roles; the cool-minded intellectual killer in Alfred Hitchcock's film Rope, and the trigger-happy lead in the 1950 noir Gun Crazy. \n\nHe first came to fame as the young prodigy who comes alive under the tutelage of Bette Davis in The Corn Is Green, for which he was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor...", died:date('1971-01-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1Auqr14buK15CFhECOWG3TBlUi7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14504"}}, {tmdbId:"12497", properties:{bornIn:"San Jose, California, USA", imdbId:"0335048", born:date('1925-07-01'), name:"Farley Granger", bio:"Farley Earle Granger Jr.  (July 1, 1925 – March 27, 2011) was an American actor, best known for his two collaborations with director Alfred Hitchcock: Rope in 1948 and Strangers on a Train in 1951...", died:date('2011-03-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4Tqi22qSxBdeWGDAOVvfa8pDX8E.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12497"}}, {tmdbId:"17662", properties:{imdbId:"0263330", born:date('1896-04-28'), name:"Edith Evanson", died:date('1980-11-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cCQQcs7TPz4IvSyZXG4kd1nHqmY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/17662"}}, {tmdbId:"17661", properties:{bornIn:"Charleston, West Virginia, United States", imdbId:"0225255", born:date('1920-11-20'), name:"Douglas Dick", bio:"Douglas Dick (born November 20, 1920) is a retired American actor...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uO9sPjZJ1aSo6a8bYfvIjqEuJEP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/17661"}}, {tmdbId:"87390", properties:{bornIn:"Cleveland, Ohio, U.S.", imdbId:"0828594", born:date('1916-12-13'), name:"Mark Stevens", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nMark Stevens (December 13, 1916 – September 15, 1994) was an American actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Mark Stevens (actor), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1994-09-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iMHKYBtro1owqhVfwvkXoAEusBe.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/87390"}}, {tmdbId:"87749", properties:{bornIn:"Sydney, New South Wales, Australia", imdbId:"0723954", born:date('1917-12-13'), name:"Ann Richards", bio:"Ann Richards was an Australian actress who, as Shirley Ann Richards (her full original name), achieved notability in Australian films, then moved to Hollywood to pursue an American screen career...", died:date('2006-08-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oHFWyWQpw8zQttNvXRSQ1MRap3X.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/87749"}}, {tmdbId:"7683", properties:{bornIn:"Dracut, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0179819", born:date('1914-03-20'), name:"Wendell Corey", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nWendell Reid Corey was an American actor and politician.  He began his acting career on the stage, doing a number of productions in summer stock.  His Broadway debut was in Comes the Revelation (1942).  After appearing in a number of supporting roles, he scored his first hit as a cynical newspaperman in Elmer Rice's comedy Dream Girl (1945)...", died:date('1968-11-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eA8sjsZzDz0MywoxfbdRs9Ejwnu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7683"}}, {tmdbId:"10023", properties:{bornIn:"Siluria, Alabama, USA", imdbId:"0640732", born:date('1923-07-06'), name:"Cathy O'Donnell", bio:"Cathy O'Donnell (July 6, 1923 – April 11, 1970) was an American actress, best known for her many roles in film-noir movies. \n\nWhile under contract with Samuel Goldwyn, O'Donnell made her debut in an uncredited role as a nightclub extra in Wonder Man (1945).  Her first major role in The Best Years of Our Lives (1946), playing Wilma Cameron, the high-school sweetheart of double amputatee Homer Parrish, played by real-life World War II veteran/amputee Harold Russell...", died:date('1970-04-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xPqSCE8w7oSYv2A74YO9jXQVVTi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10023"}}, {tmdbId:"3338", properties:{bornIn:"Little Rock, Arkansas, USA", imdbId:"0282435", born:date('1899-03-06'), name:"Jay C. Flippen", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJay C.  Flippen  (born March 6, 1899, Little Rock, Arkansas – February 3, 1971, Los Angeles, California) is an American character actor who often played police officers or weary criminals in many movies of the 1940s/'50s. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jay C...", died:date('1971-02-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uKdC4woip1qC3Uj1Lw1Y91d4twu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3338"}}, {tmdbId:"85485", properties:{bornIn:"Carnegie, Oklahoma, USA", imdbId:"0492631", born:date('1930-02-24'), name:"Barbara Lawrence", died:date('2013-11-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/llGi5r9qH6asOTE9iiwR5IM95Ox.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85485"}}, {tmdbId:"70985", properties:{bornIn:"St. Cloud, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0949574", born:date('1913-11-04'), name:"Gig Young", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGig Young (November 4, 1913 - October 19, 1978) was an American film, stage, and television actor, who developed a passion for the theatre while appearing in high school plays.  After graduating from high school he worked as a used car salesman and studied acting at night at Phil Hayden Theatre school. \n\nHe moved to Hollywood when a friend offered him a ride if he would pay for half the gas...", died:date('1978-10-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xyyQcTxjxj92eF2erciNQNZunTO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70985"}}, {tmdbId:"34315", properties:{bornIn:"Highland Park, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0544711", born:date('1923-04-28'), name:"Adele Mara", bio:" From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAdele Mara (April 28, 1923 – May 7, 2010), born Adelaide Delgado, was an American actress, singer and dancer who appeared in films during the 1940s and 1950s.  During the 1940s, the blond actress was also a popular pinup girl. \n\n One of her early roles was as a receptionist in the Three Stooges film I Can Hardly Wait...", died:date('2010-05-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jegIpLctU7RvYyrwdnG1sfYXmc6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34315"}}, {tmdbId:"7453", properties:{bornIn:"Ikuno, Hyogo, Japan", imdbId:"0793766", born:date('1905-03-12'), name:"Takashi Shimura", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nTakashi Shimura (志村 喬 Shimura Takashi,  March 12, 1905 – February 11, 1982) was a Japanese actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Takashi Shimura, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1982-02-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ydyAm2vyBbEPZRICIMqqjDm0NM9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7453"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"7450", properties:{bornIn:"Tsingtao, China (now Qingdao, Shandong, China)", imdbId:"0001536", born:date('1920-04-01'), name:"Toshirô Mifune", bio:"Toshirō Mifune (三船 敏郎 Mifune Toshirō, April 1, 1920 – December 24, 1997) was a Japanese actor who appeared in almost 170 feature films.  He is best known for his 16-film collaboration with filmmaker Akira Kurosawa, from 1948 to 1965, in works such as Rashomon, Seven Samurai, Throne of Blood, and Yojimbo.  He is also popular for portraying Musashi Miyamoto in Hiroshi Inagaki's Samurai Trilogy...", died:date('1997-12-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2GU6d2jm2J644FmYxxl4sbq52Bl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7450"}}, {tmdbId:"118176", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0945468", born:date('1902-09-15'), name:"Reizaburô Yamamoto", died:date('1964-09-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2UcHnjsXa3ZCVqPDuixLc3EtJdO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/118176"}}, {tmdbId:"108025", properties:{bornIn:"Shimonoseki, Yamaguchi, Japan", imdbId:"0463152", born:date('1918-01-31'), name:"Michiyo Kogure", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nMichiyo Kogure (Kogure Michiyo?) (31 January 1918 – 13 June 1990) was a Japanese film actress.  She appeared in 89 films between 1939 and 1984.  She is perhaps best known for her starring role as the headstrong housewife who begins to tire of her dull, earnest husband in The Flavor of Green Tea over Rice (1952). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Michiyo Kogure, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1990-06-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5OsLOgxYrwiqGmnLvRXkfuuNgsi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/108025"}}, {tmdbId:"85651", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0391062", born:date('1921-06-21'), name:"Judy Holliday", bio:"Judy Holliday was born Judith Tuvim in New York City on June 21, 1921.   Her mother, a piano teacher, was attending a play when she went into  labor and made it to the hospital just in time.  Judy was an only child.   By the age of four, her mother had her enrolled in ballet school which  fostered a life-long interest in show business.  Two years later her  parents divorced.  In high school, Judy began to develop an interest in  theater.  She appeared in several high school plays...", died:date('1965-06-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/frERdNO8QNlTkl8C4St1gWcIt89.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85651"}}, {tmdbId:"43819", properties:{bornIn:"Owensboro, Kentucky, USA", imdbId:"0263885", born:date('1909-04-29'), name:"Tom Ewell", bio:"Tom Ewell (born Samuel Yewell Tompkins) was an American stage, screen, and television actor...", died:date('1994-09-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9sAvaHpPULsMKu3LTPYfv089c36.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/43819"}}, {tmdbId:"22602", properties:{imdbId:"0641729", born:date('1904-03-15'), name:"J. Pat O'Malley", died:date('1985-02-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jk7mm6Q9S0w6gRspM9VIXwMvG4r.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/22602"}}, {tmdbId:"85862", properties:{bornIn:"Bainbridge, Ohio", imdbId:"0064197", born:date('1903-06-10'), name:"Clyde Beatty", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nClyde Beatty (June 10, 1903 – July 19, 1965) joined the circus as a cage cleaner as a teen and became famous as a lion tamer and animal trainer.  He also became a circus impresario who owned his own show that later merged with the Cole Bros.  Circus to form the Clyde Beatty-Cole Bros.  Circus. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Clyde Beatty, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1965-07-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hgtAbiWjxos0OveK9zsVEdzf55d.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85862"}}, {tmdbId:"85863", properties:{bornIn:"Gainesville, Texas, U.S.", imdbId:"0118353", born:date('1888-03-17'), name:"Frank Buck", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nFrank Howard Buck (March 17, 1884 – March 25, 1950) was a hunter and \"collector of wild animals,\" as well as a movie actor, director, writer and producer.  He is known for his book Bring 'Em Back Alive and his 1930s and 40s jungle adventure movies including: Wild Cargo, Jungle Cavalcade, Jacare, Killer of the Amazon, many of which included staged \"fights to the death\" between formidable beasts...", died:date('1950-03-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7s1wHTfL7p6gRze5szeaJy8ZBfm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85863"}}, {tmdbId:"33135", properties:{bornIn:"Tachibana, Kumamoto Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0753479", born:date('1904-05-13'), name:"Chishû Ryû", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nChishu Ryu (May 13, 1904 in Kumamoto, Japan – March 16, 1993 in Yokohama, Japan) was a famous Japanese film actor, a favourite of the director Yasujiro Ozu.  From 1928 to 1992 he appeared in at least 155 films, including Ozu's Tokyo Story (1953) and Yoshitaro Nomura's Castle of Sand (1974)...", died:date('1993-03-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/md0GCQUr0ktyjigmnFhRRhIE1tK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33135"}}, {tmdbId:"95504", properties:{bornIn:"Yokohama, Kanagawa, Japan", imdbId:"0361697", born:date('1920-06-17'), name:"Setsuko Hara", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSetsuko Hara (June 17, 1920 – September 5, 2015) was a Japanese actress who appeared in six of Yasujirō Ozu's films, most notably as Noriko in the 'Noriko Trilogy': Late Spring (1949), Early Summer (1951) and Tokyo Story (1953).  Her other films for Ozu were Tokyo Twilight (1957), Late Autumn (1960) and finally The End of Summer in 1961. \n\nShe was born  Masae Aida in Yokohama, Kanagawa prefecture...", died:date('2015-09-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zaiy9COvjUVGV6q9x7ptuZeuTCa.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95504"}}, {tmdbId:"131012", properties:{bornIn:"Hiroshima City, Japan", imdbId:"0875366", born:date('1922-10-14'), name:"Yumeji Tsukioka", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nYumeji Tsukioka (月丘 夢路, Tsukioka Yumeji, 14 October 1922 – 3 May 2017) was a Japanese film actress.  She has appeared in over 150 films between 1940 and 1994.  She starred in the film The Temptress and the Monk, which was entered into the 8th Berlin International Film Festival.  Her husband was the director Umetsugu Inoue. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Yumeji Tsukioka, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2017-05-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xlpCLoNSwAjw2H7O73VCcooHIp1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/131012"}}, {tmdbId:"131013", properties:{bornIn:"Hiroshima, Japan", imdbId:"0837503", born:date('1909-01-07'), name:"Haruko Sugimura", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nHaruko Sugimura (杉村 春子 Sugimura Haruko, January 6, 1909 – April 4, 1997) was a Japanese stage and film actress, best known for her appearances in the movies of Yasujiro Ozu and Mikio Naruse from the late 1940s to the early 1960s.  In the West, her most famous role was that of Shige, the elderly couple's hairdresser daughter in Ozu's Tokyo Story (1953)...", died:date('1997-04-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/g4ro32UO0Aob9QtLAVAXI9oOKZT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/131013"}}, {tmdbId:"37446", properties:{bornIn:"Newport, Rhode Island, USA", imdbId:"0004496", born:date('1916-08-25'), name:"Van Johnson", bio:"Van Johnson (1916–2008) was an American film, television theatre and radio actor, singer, and dancer.  He was a major star at Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer during and after World War II...", died:date('2008-12-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/A6vw5kbdmyXDz1ddQOocJmg9TSc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/37446"}}, {tmdbId:"1793", properties:{bornIn:"Mexico City - Mexico", imdbId:"0001544", born:date('1920-11-25'), name:"Ricardo Montalban", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRicardo Gonzalo Pedro Montalbán y Merino, KSG ( November 25, 1920 – January 14, 2009) was a Mexican radio, television, theatre and film actor.  He had a career spanning seven decades (motion pictures from 1943 to 2006) and multiple notable roles.  During the mid-1970s, Montalbán was most notable as the spokesman in automobile advertisements for the Chrysler Cordoba, in which he famously extolled the \"soft Corinthian leather\" used for its interior...", died:date('2009-01-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/c0ShoobuOTen4mvVfCQFqrXXpkp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1793"}}, {tmdbId:"41240", properties:{bornIn:"Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada", imdbId:"0001119", born:date('1922-09-01'), name:"Yvonne De Carlo", bio:"Yvonne De Carlo (September 1, 1922 – January 8, 2007) was a Canadian-born American actress of film and television.  During her six-decade career, her most frequent appearances in film came in the 1940s and 1950s and included her best-known film roles, such as of Anna Marie in Salome Where She Danced (1945); Anna in Criss Cross (1949); Sephora the wife of Moses in The Ten Commandments (1956), starring Charlton Heston; and Amantha Starr in Band of Angels (1957) with Clark Gable...", died:date('2007-01-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kXFPHMtGwWHzRCOp88TW85mDwY5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41240"}}, {tmdbId:"37448", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0573640", born:date('1911-07-29'), name:"Stephen McNally", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nStephen McNally (born Horace Vincent McNally, July 29, 1911 – June 4, 1994) was an American actor remembered mostly for his appearances in many Westerns and action films.  He often played hard-hearted characters or villains.  He was an attorney in the late 1930s before pursuing his passion for acting.  He was a one time president of the Catholic Actors Guild...", died:date('1994-06-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/e0wwYKZtdye8D2JAfKHWlLM0Ebj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/37448"}}, {tmdbId:"114287", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0856583", born:date('1921-06-21'), name:"Joan Tetzel", bio:"Aside from her movie career, Joan Tetzel was well known as a Broadway and London stage actress.  She played nurse Ratchett in the Broadway\n\n edition of \"One Flew Over The Cuckoo's Nest. \" During the early \n\nseventies, she appeared in the London play, \"How The Other Half Loves. \" \n\nDuring this period, she had a running part in the TV series \n\n\"Policewoman. \" As a noted stage actress, her picture appeared on the \n\nfront cover of Life Magazine on February 14, 1948...", died:date('1977-10-31'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/114287"}}, {tmdbId:"110938", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0551031", born:date('1930-06-08'), name:"Marion Marshall", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nBeoAv7HiAhwIs6sgHp1wII2kJj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/110938"}}, {tmdbId:"109407", properties:{bornIn:"Iola, Kansas, USA", imdbId:"0835836", born:date('1924-10-12'), name:"Randy Stuart", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRandy Stuart, born as Elizabeth Shaubell (October 24, 1924 – July 20, 1996), was an American actress in film and television...", died:date('1996-07-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7hzDV4VwBYJZ4D1L6crc2kLcspc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/109407"}}, {tmdbId:"10611", properties:{bornIn:" Denver, Colorado, USA", imdbId:"0060845", born:date('1925-08-06'), name:"Barbara Bates", died:date('1969-03-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tYdngwN8JzCBJH0ircz8CKCwdg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10611"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"2926", properties:{bornIn:"Lewisham, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0006471", born:date('1902-10-28'), name:"Elsa Lanchester", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nElsa Sullivan Lanchester  (28 October 1902 – 26 December 1986) was an English-American character actress with a long career in theatre, film and television. \n\nLanchester studied dance as a child and after the First World War began performing in theatre and cabaret, where she established her career over the following decade.  She met the actor Charles Laughton in 1927, and they were married two years later...", died:date('1986-12-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aQUGJvs6Y3zBRGIWoLIZ1IG1Px6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2926"}}, {tmdbId:"30766", properties:{bornIn:"Twyford, Berkshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0696866", born:date('1915-06-23'), name:"Dennis Price", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDennis Price (23 June 1915 – 6 October 1973) was an English actor, remembered for his suave screen roles, particularly Louis Mazzini in Kind Hearts and Coronets, and for his portrayal of the omniscient valet Jeeves in 1960s television adaptations of P.  G.  Wodehouse's stories...", died:date('1973-10-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ax3BdKRYdmbGtY8a6RBj8bxk6Qd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30766"}}, {tmdbId:"45466", properties:{bornIn:"Chelsea, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0339343", born:date('1921-03-04'), name:"Joan Greenwood", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJoan Greenwood (4 March 1921 – 27 February 1987) was an English actress.  Born in Chelsea, she studied at the Royal Academy of Dramatic Art.  Her husky voice, coupled with her slow, precise elocution, was her trademark.  Perhaps her most famous role was Gwendolen in The Importance of Being Earnest (1952)...", died:date('1987-02-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dQw8PW2f7XpVntyFFKoj28RBeXW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/45466"}}, {tmdbId:"87685", properties:{bornIn:"Valley City, North Dakota USA", imdbId:"0815433", born:date('1909-01-22'), name:"Ann Sothern", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAnn Sothern (born Harriette Arlene Lake; January 22, 1909 – March 15, 2001) was an American actress who worked on stage, radio, film, and television, in a career that spanned nearly six decades.  Sothern began her career in the late 1920s in bit parts in films.  In 1930, she made her Broadway stage debut and soon worked her way up to starring roles.  In 1939, MGM cast her as Maisie Ravier, a brash yet lovable Brooklyn showgirl...", died:date('2001-03-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sPSFce7FL8ifU93HnRwaY4DtASx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/87685"}}, {tmdbId:"33716", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles - California - USA", imdbId:"0601930", born:date('1929-01-07'), name:"Terry Moore", bio:"Born Helen Luella Koford on January 7, 1929, the Los Angeles, California native worked as a model before she made her film debut at age 11 in 20th Century Fox's Maryland (1940).  Throughout the 1940s, she worked under a variety of names (her own, Judy Ford and January Ford) before settling on Terry Moore in 1948...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/znkj4uTUkNpJucQcW4z4juqf6b6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33716"}}, {tmdbId:"8258", properties:{bornIn:"Foraker, Shidler, Oklahoma, USA", imdbId:"0424565", born:date('1918-06-13'), name:"Ben Johnson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nBen \"Son\" Johnson, Jr.  (June 13, 1918 – April 8, 1996) was an American motion picture actor who was mainly cast in Westerns.  He was also a rodeo cowboy, stuntman, and rancher. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Ben Johnson (actor) , licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1996-04-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/VJYWJAOLcLE1WyG1v8W2h7TahA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8258"}}, {tmdbId:"2609193", properties:{imdbId:"5935170", name:"Mr. Joseph Young", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/o1Hmb7YVfEvRPSVpLgvGCHYyGUB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2609193"}}, {tmdbId:"106159", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0043396", born:date('1933-07-17'), name:"Keiko Awaji", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nKeiko Awaji (1933) is a Japanese film actress. \n\nNotable highlights of her career were an appearance in Akira Kurosawa's Stray Dog, and a role as Kimiko in The Bridges at Toko-Ri, where she appeared alongside William Holden and Mickey Rooney. \n\nHer first husband was Filipino musician and actor Rodrigo \"Bimbo\" Danao; they had two children together.  Their eldest is actor Etsuo Shima...", died:date('2014-01-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oswdrJiFWHbBVnjpYhodzeTsIDc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/106159"}}, {tmdbId:"106160", properties:{bornIn:" Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0594542", born:date('1894-04-08'), name:"Eiko Miyoshi", died:date('1963-07-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/914W9oYJMWI7rlm1oEzbyMEdXb4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/106160"}}, {tmdbId:"109614", properties:{bornIn:"St. Joseph, Missouri, U.S.", imdbId:"0308081", born:date('1919-05-23'), name:"Betty Garrett", bio:"A sunny singer, dancer and comic actress, Betty Garrett starred in several Hollywood musicals and stage roles.  She was at the top of her game when the Communist scare in the 1950s brought her career to a screeching, ugly halt.  She and her husband Larry Parks, an Oscar-nominated actor, were summoned by the House UnAmerican Activities Committee and questioned about their involvement. \n\nAs the drama played out, a very pregnant Garrett was never called to testify, but her husband was...", died:date('2011-02-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kyUVKNJtXq4azGyqJkgK3XZkNAU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/109614"}}, {tmdbId:"103071", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, U.S.", imdbId:"0000730", born:date('1921-01-31'), name:"John Agar", bio:"John G.  Agar (January 31, 1921 – April 7, 2002) was an American actor.  He starred alongside John Wayne in the films Sands of Iwo Jima and She Wore a Yellow Ribbon, but was later relegated to B movies, such as Tarantula, The Mole People, The Brain from Planet Arous, Flesh and the Spur, and Hand of Death.  He also starred with Lucille Ball in the 1951 movie The Magic Carpet. \n\nAgar was born in Chicago, Illinois, the son of Lillian (née Rogers) and John Agar, Sr. , a meat packer (see Agar Hams)...", died:date('2002-04-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zIFQzZaSUzsRGh0EdaLeFr1bJHW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/103071"}}, {tmdbId:"2753", properties:{bornIn:"Hunt City, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0412322", born:date('1909-06-14'), name:"Burl Ives", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBurl Icle Ivanhoe Ives (June 14, 1909 – April 14, 1995) was an American singer and actor of stage, screen, radio and television. \n\nIves began as an itinerant singer and banjoist, and launched his own radio show, The Wayfaring Stranger, which popularized traditional folk songs.  In 1942 he appeared in Irving Berlin's This Is the Army, and then became a major star of CBS radio...", died:date('1995-04-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eyx3PKEsmThQmrtTCpheiUeynCz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2753"}}, {tmdbId:"35190", properties:{imdbId:"0899887", name:"Mario Vitale", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ilyaKzrkssetdp8XOIi4jQPrMhV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/35190"}}, {tmdbId:"110205", properties:{imdbId:"0149027", born:date('1907-10-30'), name:"Renzo Cesana", died:date('1970-11-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2YtSiM0f3rgFcexWLud5fX3ViJ7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/110205"}}, {tmdbId:"224455", properties:{imdbId:"0819374", name:"Mario Sponzo", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/224455"}}, {tmdbId:"129520", properties:{bornIn:"Inglewood, California, USA", imdbId:"0930565", born:date('1921-08-08'), name:"Esther Williams", bio:"Esther Jane Williams (August 8, 1921 – June 6, 2013) was an American competitive swimmer and MGM movie star. \n\nWilliams set multiple national and regional swimming records in her late teens as part of the Los Angeles Athletic Club swim team.  Unable to compete in the 1940 Summer Olympics because of the outbreak of World War II, Williams joined Billy Rose's Aquacade, where she took on the role vacated by Eleanor Holm after the show's move from New York City to San Francisco...", died:date('2013-06-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mqLhC3OWVmCzT64vZk5rufuVlR3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/129520"}}, {tmdbId:"15385", properties:{bornIn:"Pola, Istria, Italy [now Pula, Istria, Croatia]", imdbId:"0885098", born:date('1921-05-31'), name:"Alida Valli", bio:"Alida Valli (31 May 1921 – 22 April 2006), sometimes simply credited as Valli, was an Italian actress who appeared in more than 100 films, including Mario Soldati's Piccolo mondo antico, Alfred Hitchcock's The Paradine Case, Ayn Rand's We the Living, Carol Reed's The Third Man, Michelangelo Antonioni's Il Grido, Luchino Visconti's Senso, and Dario Argento's Suspiria...", died:date('2006-04-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ze8OiV87TYR4PmyuNIobl02ODjo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15385"}}, {tmdbId:"10609", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0549280", born:date('1911-01-30'), name:"Hugh Marlowe", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Hugh Marlowe (January 30, 1911 – May 2, 1982) was an American film, television, stage and radio actor. \n\nMarlowe was born Hugh Herbert Hipple in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, and began his stage career in the 1930s at the Pasadena Playhouse in California.  Marlowe was usually a secondary lead or supporting actor in the films he appeared in. \n\nHis films included Meet Me in St...", died:date('1982-05-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5GyNiSiS9RQduMt0JlFn8jCnKb2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10609"}}, {tmdbId:"10608", properties:{bornIn:"Hartford, Connecticut, USA", imdbId:"0581282", born:date('1915-08-02'), name:"Gary Merrill", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGary Fred Merrill (August 2, 1915 – March 5, 1990) was an American film and television character actor whose credits included more than fifty feature films, a half-dozen mostly short-lived TV series, and dozens of television guest appearances. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Gary Merrill, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1990-03-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sMmRlBwu1lS8qJW6t9iRNn8qBxA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10608"}}, {tmdbId:"13297", properties:{imdbId:"0593612", born:date('1903-08-14'), name:"Millard Mitchell", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMillard Mitchell (August 14, 1903 – October 13, 1953) was an American character actor whose credits include roughly thirty feature films and two television appearances. \n\nBorn in Havana, Cuba, Mitchell appeared as a bit player in eight films between 1931 and 1936.  He returned to film work in 1942 after a six-year absence.  Between 1942 and 1953, Mitchell was a successful supporting actor...", died:date('1953-10-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7o0uEdJOQzuC4CIj3PBrGtO2fo7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13297"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"20392", properties:{bornIn:"Leigh-on-Sea, Essex, England, UK", imdbId:"0928697", born:date('1912-07-23'), name:"Michael Wilding", died:date('1979-07-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9xPmDXGKqzdUUHopFog7pVG8Lat.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20392"}}, {tmdbId:"80255", properties:{bornIn:"Barnt Green, Worcestershire, England, U.K.", imdbId:"0500364", born:date('1922-02-26'), name:"Margaret Leighton", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMargaret Leighton (26 February 1922 – 13 January 1976) was an English actress.  She had an exquisite sense of grandeur and refinement.  She created the role of Hannah Jelkes in Tennessee Williams' The Night of the Iguana. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Margaret Leighton, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1976-01-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vL6rYdIC1Eg7kiyiIMVqDxJeCk5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80255"}}, {tmdbId:"78791", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0943618", born:date('1881-10-26'), name:"Margaret Wycherly", bio:"English born Margaret Wycherly was, in England, a stage actress, and, in America, a stage, film, and television actress...", died:date('1956-06-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/deOr31wqp3iKvGxm8M2XXgQbcAT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78791"}}, {tmdbId:"3088", properties:{bornIn:"Upper Montclair, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0001330", born:date('1916-03-26'), name:"Sterling Hayden", bio:"Sterling Walter Hayden, born Sterling Relyea Walter, was an American actor and author.  He didn't really harbor any aspirations of being an actor, dropped out of high school at the age of 16 and hired on as mate on a schooner.  He was a ship's captain at 22, and in need of cash to buy his own boat, established himself as a model in New York, discovered by Paramount Studios talent scouts and offered a contract...", died:date('1986-05-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/twzaqv1ymkWYKHFF3kbvwaTIrFO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3088"}}, {tmdbId:"13296", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0353405", born:date('1923-08-03'), name:"Jean Hagen", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJean Hagen (born Jean Shirley Verhagen, August 3, 1923 – August 29, 1977) was an American actress best known for her role as Lina Lamont in Singin' in the Rain (1952), for which she was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress.  Hagen was also nominated three times for an Emmy Award for Best Supporting Actress in a Comedy Series for her role as Margaret Williams (1953–56) on the television series Make Room For Daddy...", died:date('1977-08-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8DVERsEW1C2B9vhqjsASLidonQB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13296"}}, {tmdbId:"6577", properties:{bornIn:"White Plains, New York, USA", imdbId:"0926235", born:date('1921-10-01'), name:"James Whitmore", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJames Allen Whitmore Jr.  (October 1, 1921 – February 6, 2009) was an American film, theatre, and television actor.  During his career, Whitmore won three of the four EGOT honors; - a Tony, a Grammy, and an Emmy.  Whitmore also won a Golden Globe and was nominated for two Academy Awards.   Following World War II, Whitmore appeared on Broadway in the role of the sergeant in Command Decision...", died:date('2009-02-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kjEaGEeZaSFPL5siFi1MA9Q6Tmh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6577"}}, {tmdbId:"4299", properties:{bornIn:"Steubenville, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0001509", born:date('1917-06-07'), name:"Dean Martin", bio:"Dean Martin was an American singer, film actor, television star and comedian. \n\nMartin's hit singles included Memories Are Made of This, That's Amore, Everybody Loves Somebody, Mambo Italiano, Sway, Volare and Ain't That a Kick in the Head. \n\nNicknamed the King of Cool, he was one of the members of the Rat Pack and a major star in concert stage/night clubs, recordings, motion pictures, and television...", died:date('1995-12-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yykP81aQ5wLAJsggLFjFIKC4Kwv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4299"}}, {tmdbId:"50762", properties:{bornIn:"Hartford, Connecticut, U.S.", imdbId:"0446037", born:date('1922-04-26'), name:"Mike Kellin", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMike Kellin (April 26, 1922 – August 26, 1983) was an American actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Mike Kellin, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1983-08-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fe17vLfGXhbuLkyNQN7miebxWKu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/50762"}}, {tmdbId:"120035", properties:{bornIn:"Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0242190", born:date('1900-12-19'), name:"Jimmie Dundee", bio:"Jimmie Dundee was born on December 19, 1900 in Missouri, USA as James Reed Dundee.  He is known for his work on At War with the Army (1950), Sullivan's Travels (1941) and Hail the Conquering Hero (1944).  He died on November 20, 1953 in Woodland Hills, Los Angeles, California, USA...", died:date('1953-11-20'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/120035"}}, {tmdbId:"5792", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, U.S.", imdbId:"0820643", born:date('1905-10-09'), name:"Howard St. John", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nHoward St.  John (October 9, 1905 – March 13, 1974) was a Chicago-born character actor who specialized in unsympathetic roles.  His work spanned Broadway, film and television.  He is probably best remembered for his bombastic General Bullmoose, which he played in the stage and screen versions of the 1956 musical Li'l Abner. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Howard St.  John, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1974-03-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5HkEPH9C4JTzR0mQjDKzqbmrpQe.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5792"}}, {tmdbId:"133730", properties:{bornIn:"Kansas City, Missouri, U.S.", born:date('1926-08-29'), name:"Betty Lynn", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nElizabeth Ann Theresa \"Betty\" Lynn (born August 29, 1926) is a former American actress.  She is best known for her role as Thelma Lou, Deputy Barney Fife's girlfriend, on The Andy Griffith Show. \n\nBetty Lynn was born in Kansas City, Missouri, Her mother, Elizabeth Ann Lynn, was \"an accomplished mezzo-soprano\" who taught Betty to sing and started her in the Kansas City Conservatory of Music when she was 5 years old...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pjVWMB5fxt7zm1c5Vno9ZWt8Du9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/133730"}}, {tmdbId:"68652", properties:{bornIn:"Portsmouth, New Hampshire, USA", imdbId:"0940627", born:date('1929-05-05'), name:"Ilene Woods", died:date('2010-07-01'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/68652"}}, {tmdbId:"67289", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0041598", born:date('1905-11-19'), name:"Eleanor Audley", bio:"Eleanor Audley (November 19, 1905 – November 25, 1991) was an American actress who was a familiar radio and animation voice, in addition to her TV and film roles.  She is best remembered on television as Eunice Douglas on Green Acres and, for many, for providing Disney animated features with their most outstanding and memorable villainess voices, most notably two of the most sinister Disney villainesses, Lady Tremaine and Maleficent...", died:date('1991-11-25'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67289"}}, {tmdbId:"67290", properties:{bornIn:"Salinas, California, USA", imdbId:"0271658", born:date('1890-07-20'), name:"Verna Felton", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nVerna Felton (July 20, 1890 – December 14, 1966) was an American character actress who was best-known for providing many female voices in numerous Disney animated films, as well as voicing Fred Flintstone's mother-in-law Pearl Slaghoople for Hanna-Barbera.  Her film appearances during the 1940s included If I Had My Way (1940), Girls of the Big House (1945) and The Fuller Brush Man (1948)...", died:date('1966-12-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ffqjAUeXx85LrS571Ex0zys7si7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67290"}}, {tmdbId:"68653", properties:{bornIn:"Bonners Ferry, Idaho, USA", imdbId:"0238855", born:date('1892-08-31'), name:"Claire Du Brey", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nClaire Du Brey (born Clara Violet Dubrey, August 31, 1892 – August 1, 1993) was an American actress.  She appeared in more than 200 films between 1916 and 1959.  Her name is sometimes rendered as Claire Du Bray or as Claire Dubrey. \n\nDu Brey's screen career began with Universal Studios and she played at one time or another with almost all the larger companies...", died:date('1993-08-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oW7EUQCD1noYuvIH0umuhQisp5s.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/68653"}}, {tmdbId:"34516", properties:{bornIn:"Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA", imdbId:"0110219", born:date('1923-03-19'), name:"Pamela Britton", died:date('1974-06-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/d809jd9tfHLE95kDK30lhqDwKLK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34516"}}, {tmdbId:"55821", properties:{bornIn:"New York City - New York - USA", imdbId:"0012204", born:date('1903-05-04'), name:"Luther Adler", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   He was an American actor best known for his work in theatre, but who also worked in film and television.  He also directed plays on Broadway.   Adler was born Lutha Adler on May 4, 1903 in New York City.  He was one of six children born to Russian Jewish actors Sara and Jacob P.  Adler.  His father was considered to be one of the founders of the Yiddish theater in America...", died:date('1984-12-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4wWnZCULWIxJKh3F2JbgG65B9EV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55821"}}, {tmdbId:"83987", properties:{bornIn:"Santa Cruz, California, United States", imdbId:"0307500", born:date('1926-10-17'), name:"Beverly Garland", bio:"Beverly Garland (1926–2008) was an American film and television actress, businesswoman, and hotel owner. \n\nGarland gained prominence with her role on My Three Sons.  In the 1980s, she co-starred as Kate Jackson's widowed mother on Scarecrow and Mrs.  King.  She also had a recurring role as on 7th Heaven...", died:date('2008-12-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tDeQON5mwWgoQtIESVSy8uBBZln.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83987"}}, {tmdbId:"86001", properties:{bornIn:"Prestatyn, North Wales", imdbId:"0192033", born:date('1925-12-18'), name:"Peggy Cummins", bio:"Peggy Cummins was a Welsh-born Irish actress, best known for her performance in Joseph H.  Lewis's Gun Crazy, playing a trigger-happy femme fatale, who robs banks with her lover, played by John Dall...", died:date('2017-12-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/r8od7pVjh9w4Y1mIobqTfFRvsJc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/86001"}}, {tmdbId:"85988", properties:{bornIn:"San Antonio, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0471854", born:date('1912-10-16'), name:"Berry Kroeger", bio:"Berry Kroeger was an American film, television and stage actor. \n\nBorn in San Antonio, Texas, Kroeger got his acting start on radio as an announcer on Suspense and as an actor, playing for a time The Falcon in the radio series.  Kroeger was a regular as Sam Williams on the radio daytime drama Young Doctor Malone.  He was discovered by filmmaker William Wellman while performing on Broadway and began appearing in films in 1948 with his role in The Iron Curtain...", died:date('1991-01-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/egarsq9nJe61ligHIhOsrCSnd9d.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85988"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"2667", properties:{bornIn:"Newtonville, Massachusetts, U.S.", imdbId:"0401449", born:date('1877-01-03'), name:"Josephine Hull", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.  Josephine Hull (born January 3, reportedly 1886, but probably 1883  – died March 12, 1957) was an American actress.  She had a successful 50-year career on stage while taking some of her better known roles to film.  She won the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress for Harvey, a role she also created on the Broadway stage. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Josephine Hull, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1957-03-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sairV7DdvAzdnDMlSJ013szsaOC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2667"}}, {tmdbId:"70492", properties:{bornIn:"Columbia, Mississippi, USA", imdbId:"0235627", born:date('1928-03-18'), name:"Peggy Dow", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qilNLNko3Uh1AFd2pPZFbtLk3Bm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70492"}}, {tmdbId:"15978", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0236866", born:date('1917-10-02'), name:"Charles Drake", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nCharles Drake (October 2, 1917 – September 10, 1994) was an American actor. Drake was born as Charles Ruppert in New York City.  He graduated from Nichols College and became a salesman.  In 1939, he turned to acting and signed a contract with Warner Brothers.  He wasn't immediately successful.  World War II interrupted his career; soon after his military service was complete, Drake returned to Hollywood in 1945, his contract with Warner Brothers ended...", died:date('1994-09-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8MbNiIMYrJ7UgKseAmBbw2sXH1M.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15978"}}, {tmdbId:"81179", properties:{bornIn:"Bronx, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0522481", born:date('1912-03-28'), name:"Frank Lovejoy", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nFrank Lovejoy (March 28, 1912 – October 2, 1962) was an American actor in radio, film, and television.  He was born Frank Lovejoy Jr.  in Bronx, New York, but grew up in New Jersey.  His father, Frank Lovejoy Sr. , was a furniture salesman from Maine.  His mother, Nora, was born in Massachusetts to Irish immigrant parents. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Frank Lovejoy, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1962-10-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/54lyen5kzZ7xehjCVR6dJxe3qRo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81179"}}, {tmdbId:"81180", properties:{bornIn:"Lansing, Michigan, U.S.", imdbId:"0717203", born:date('1893-08-14'), name:"Carl Benton Reid", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nCarl Benton Reid (August 14, 1893 – March 16, 1973) was an American actor.  He achieved fame on the Broadway stage in 1939 as Oscar Hubbard, one of Regina Giddens's (Tallulah Bankhead) greedy, devious brothers in the play The Little Foxes, and made his film debut reprising his role opposite Bette Davis in the 1941 film version...", died:date('1973-03-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/A2iV2g3pbCCej5h3myvrT4MMgEH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81180"}}, {tmdbId:"33484", properties:{bornIn:"Bletchley, Buckinghamshire, England, UK. [now Milton Keynes, Buckinghamshire, England, UK]", imdbId:"0001888", born:date('1909-11-09'), name:"Robert Douglas", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRobert Douglas (9 November 1909 - 11 January 1999) was born as Robert Douglas Finlayson in Fenny Stratford, Buckinghamshire.  He was a successful stage and film actor, a television director and producer. \n\nHe studied at RADA and made his screen debut at Bournemouth in 1927.  A year later he made his first appearance on stage in Many Waters at the Ambassadors Theatre and went into films the following year...", died:date('1999-01-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kx6sACi2ceMcGAnZ4rgCmu6qTVk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33484"}}, {tmdbId:"41235", properties:{bornIn:"Santa Monica, California, U.S.", imdbId:"0001289", born:date('1913-05-06'), name:"Stewart Granger", bio:"Stewart Granger (6 May 1913 – 16 August 1993), born James Lablache Stewart, was an English-American film actor, mainly associated with heroic and romantic leading roles.  He was a popular leading man from the 1940s to the 1960s. \n\nStewart attended Epsom College but left after deciding not to pursue a medical degree.  He decided to try acting and attended Webber-Douglas School of Dramatic Art, London...", died:date('1993-08-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pZ7YT97vHeeEzo6iwHrr7cnXGmO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41235"}}, {tmdbId:"94198", properties:{bornIn:"Brno, Moravia, Austria-Hungary", imdbId:"0351947", born:date('1901-02-18'), name:"Hugo Haas", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nHugo Haas (18 February 1901 – 1 December 1968) was a Czech film actor, director and writer.  He appeared in over 60 films between 1926 and 1962, as well as directing 20 films between 1933 and 1962. He was born in Brno, Moravia (now in the Czech Republic), and died in Vienna, Austria from complications of asthma.  His brother Pavel Haas (1899–1944) was a noted composer...", died:date('1968-12-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6pYX2tC71bRwM6uhtyJsvnCgM92.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94198"}}, {tmdbId:"8634", properties:{bornIn:"Santa Monica, California, USA", imdbId:"0916131", born:date('1920-04-02'), name:"Jack Webb", bio:"John Randolph 'Jack' Webb, also known by the pen name John Randolph, was an American actor, television producer, director, and screenwriter, who is most famous for his role as Sergeant Joe Friday in the radio and television series Dragnet.  He was also the founder of his own production company, Mark VII Limited. \n\nBorn in Santa Monica, California, Webb grew up in the Bunker Hill section of Los Angeles as the child of a single mother after his father left home before he was born...", died:date('1982-12-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rUeuDfNK9yhsXklXwONbt2X4w2M.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8634"}}, {tmdbId:"14306", properties:{bornIn:"Karachi, British India", imdbId:"0936727", born:date('1917-03-12'), name:"Googie Withers", bio:"Georgette Lizette \"Googie\" Withers CBE, AO was a British entertainer who had a lengthy career in theatre, film, and television...", died:date('2011-07-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dKuUvJtKMbw4i0cODvXn8wRgxuI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14306"}}, {tmdbId:"111578", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, U.S.", imdbId:"0007222", born:date('1907-04-11'), name:"Paul Douglas", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nPaul Douglas (April 11, 1907 – September 11, 1959) was an American actor. \n\nBorn in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania as Paul Douglas Fleischer, Douglas began his career as a stage actor.  He made his Broadway debut in 1936 as the Radio Announcer in Doty Hobart and Tom McKnight's Double Dummy at the John Golden Theatre.  In 1946 he won both a Theatre World Award and a Clarence Derwent Award for his portrayal of Herry Brock in Garson Kanin's Born Yesterday...", died:date('1959-09-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/k7hV301icnwPaBUl1LITgbZqMbR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/111578"}}, {tmdbId:"5730", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000895", born:date('1922-10-31'), name:"Barbara Bel Geddes", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nBarbara Bel Geddes (October 31, 1922 – August 8, 2005) was an American actress, artist and children's author.  She is best known for her role in the television drama series Dallas as matriarch Eleanor \"Miss Ellie\" Ewing.  Bel Geddes also starred in the original Broadway production of Cat On A Hot Tin Roof in the role of Maggie, and also appeared in Alfred Hitchcock's Vertigo (1958)...", died:date('2005-08-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xia6FCoc50eVYjp2b9ipHJbNtxF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5730"}}, {tmdbId:"3785", properties:{bornIn:"Lattimer Mines, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0001588", born:date('1919-02-18'), name:"Jack Palance", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nVolodymyr Palahniuk (February 18, 1919 – November 10, 2006), known professionally as Jack Palance, was an American film actor.  During half a century of film and television appearances he was nominated for three Academy Awards, all as Best Actor in a Supporting Role, winning in 1991 for his role in City Slickers...", died:date('2006-11-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hbM3yUIjxdfMdYOT5OdGo4katIW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3785"}}, {tmdbId:"7451", properties:{bornIn:"Osaka, Osaka Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0477553", born:date('1924-03-25'), name:"Machiko Kyô", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMachiko Kyō (Japanese: 京 マチ子 Hepburn: Kyō Machiko, March 25, 1924 – May 12, 2019) was a Japanese actress whose film work occurred primarily during the 1950s.  She rose to extraordinary domestic praise in Japan for her work in two of the greatest Japanese films of the 20th century, Akira Kurosawa's Rashōmon and Kenji Mizoguchi's Ugetsu. \n\nMachiko trained to be a dancer before entering films in 1949...", died:date('2019-05-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rWpsDPm87CQ3ekRuvDAqHBLf18a.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7451"}}, {tmdbId:"7452", properties:{bornIn:"Sapporo, Hokkaido, Japan", imdbId:"0605270", born:date('1911-01-13'), name:"Masayuki Mori", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMasayuki Mori  (森 雅之 Mori Masayuki, January 13, 1911 – October 7, 1973) Born in Sapporo, Hokkaido prefecture) was a Japanese actor, the son of Takeo Arishima, a Japanese novelist active during the late Meiji and Taishō periods.  Mori appeared in many of Akira Kurosawa 's films such as Rashomon and The Idiot.  He also starred in pictures by Kenji Mizoguchi (Ugetsu), Mikio Naruse (Floating Clouds) and other prominent directors...", died:date('1973-10-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hX7gD4gUcymXJrgwcMtw8VCqimY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7452"}}, {tmdbId:"89684", properties:{bornIn:"Copenhagen, Denmark", imdbId:"0535169", born:date('1914-01-14'), name:"Osa Massen", bio:"Osa Massen (January 13, 1914 - January 2, 2006) was a Danish actress who went on to become a successful movie actress in Hollywood.  She became a naturalized citizen of the United States in 1941...", died:date('2006-01-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4BgadnWxF1YLytcakN7b42HKwiE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89684"}}, {tmdbId:"35194", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0256305", born:date('1905-05-20'), name:"John Emery", died:date('1964-11-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kuzWbz3ACuW8UeD5CX90uSjMdYn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/35194"}}, {tmdbId:"30297", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000890", born:date('1913-08-10'), name:"Noah Beery Jr.", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nNoah Lindsey Beery (August 10, 1913 – November 1, 1994), known professionally as Noah Beery, Jr.  or just Noah Beery, was an American actor specializing in warm, friendly character parts similar to the ones played by his uncle Wallace Beery, although Noah Beery, Jr. , unlike his uncle, seldom broke away from playing supporting roles. \n\nHis father, Noah Nicholas Beery (known professionally as Noah Beery or Noah Beery, Sr...", died:date('1994-11-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vRzZSIsnfDZOLhi8QN5As9vtizc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30297"}}, {tmdbId:"20393", properties:{bornIn:"Dublin, Ireland", imdbId:"0865262", born:date('1919-06-11'), name:"Richard Todd", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRichard Todd OBE (11 June 1919 – 3 December 2009) was an Irish-born British stage and film actor and soldier. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Richard Todd, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2009-12-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oSOgN8DF1J6OFE6vXAEa8ms9ilt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20393"}}, {tmdbId:"8629", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0841797", born:date('1899-03-27'), name:"Gloria Swanson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGloria Swanson (March 27, 1899 – April 4, 1983) was an American actress.  She was one of the most prominent stars during the silent film era as both an actress and a fashion icon, especially under the direction of Cecil B.  DeMille, made dozens of silents and was nominated for the first Acadamy Award in the Best Actress catagory.  In 1929, Swanson successfully transitioned to talkies with The Trespasser...", died:date('1983-04-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/akmlp75ESHjtGOVtOCfJYxkX4eo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8629"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"8631", properties:{bornIn:"Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA", imdbId:"0647970", born:date('1928-07-14'), name:"Nancy Olson", bio:"Nancy Olson is an American screen, television, and stage actress.  She was an Academy Award Best Supporting Actress nominee for her portrayal of Betty Schaefer in Sunset Boulevard (1950)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/AoXxq1zmlQPHiayth7ywDdKtfEj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8631"}}, {tmdbId:"50998", properties:{bornIn:" Essex, England, UK", imdbId:"0842981", born:date('1894-04-23'), name:"Basil Sydney", bio:"Burly British character actor, on stage from 1909.  Served in the British\n\n Army during World War I.  Established himself as a matinée idol on the \n\nLondon stage in the 1920's.  In films tended to be cast in support, often\n\n as shifty opportunists, public servants, domineering fathers or \n\nmilitary types.  Occasionally seen in Shakespearean roles...", died:date('1968-01-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/myZrVjtZ6gjhwE29hH4l6mHhuCi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/50998"}}, {tmdbId:"52220", properties:{imdbId:"0280406", born:date('1896-05-18'), name:"Walter Fitzgerald", bio:"Walter Fitzgerald was a distinguished British character actor.    He was born in 1896 in Devon.    His first film was in 1932 in “Murder In Covent Garden”.    His cinema highlights include “In Which We Serve”, “San Demitro, London”, “The Fallen Idol” and “Treasure Island”.   He went to Hollywood in 1959 to make “Darby O’Gill and the Little People” for Walt Disney.     He died in 1976 in London at the age of 80...", died:date('1976-12-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lk0Bcc0OKnoO68LoMl6I8wslOpd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/52220"}}, {tmdbId:"31503", properties:{bornIn:"The Bronx, New York USA", imdbId:"0293099", born:date('1919-11-03'), name:"Bert Freed", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nBert Freed (November 3, 1919 — August 2, 1994) was a prolific American character actor, voice over actor, and the first actor to portray \"Detective Columbo\" on television. \n\nBorn and raised in The Bronx, New York, Freed began acting while attending Penn State University, and made his Broadway debut in 1942...", died:date('1994-08-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/S2d85cIDQIBovUTUguZIClPOI3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31503"}}, {tmdbId:"19402", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0346927", born:date('1925-10-11'), name:"Nancy Guild", died:date('1999-08-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nff1dy51zKf5CCUj55o1NGX9bRI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19402"}}, {tmdbId:"85940", properties:{bornIn:"Perth Amboy, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0291821", born:date('1920-02-29'), name:"Arthur Franz", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nArthur Franz (February 29, 1920 in Perth Amboy, New Jersey – June 17, 2006) was a B-movie actor whose most notable role was as Lieutenant, Junior Grade H.  Paynter, Jr.  in The Caine Mutiny.  He also appeared in Roseanna McCoy (1949), Invaders from Mars (1953), Abbott and Costello Meet the Invisible Man (1951) and The Unholy Wife (1957), among others.  In The Sniper (1952), he played a rare movie lead in the film's title role as a tormented killer...", died:date('2006-06-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fvqixexCQT6y7lF27doLuV7rCwM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85940"}}, {tmdbId:"6599", properties:{bornIn:"Semley, Wiltshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0605923", born:date('1908-05-26'), name:"Robert Morley", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRobert Adolph Wilton Morley CBE (26 May 1908 – 3 June 1992) was an English actor who, often in supporting roles, was usually cast as a pompous English gentleman representing the Establishment.  In Movie Encyclopedia, film critic Leonard Maltin describes Morley as \"recognizable by his ungainly bulk, bushy eyebrows, thick lips, and double chin, […] particularly effective when cast as a pompous windbag\"...", died:date('1992-06-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/38Ms5ijBMIZNA4cwhiRvmBM0fOS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6599"}}, {tmdbId:"6600", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0119988", born:date('1912-03-21'), name:"Peter Bull", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPeter Cecil Bull, DSC (21 March 1912 – 20 May 1984) was a British character actor...", died:date('1984-05-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cflWPWjQIj3BGlrqgwKV3J3S9ui.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6600"}}, {tmdbId:"67228", properties:{bornIn:"London, England", imdbId:"0064607", born:date('1938-06-28'), name:"Kathryn Beaumont", bio:"Kathryn Beaumont is an English actress, born 27 June 1938 in London (United Kingdom).  She voiced the characters of Alice in Alice in Wonderland (1951) and Wendy in Peter Pan (1953)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/i8UPNqUaHhf097nHxQeHNK8QKny.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67228"}}, {tmdbId:"5833", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA ", imdbId:"0943956", born:date('1886-11-09'), name:"Ed Wynn", bio:"Isaiah Edwin Leopold (November 9, 1886 – June 19, 1966), better known as Ed Wynn, was an American actor and comedian noted for his Perfect Fool comedy character, his pioneering radio show of the 1930s, and his later career as a dramatic actor. \n\nEd Wynn first appeared on television on July 7, 1936 in a brief, ad-libbed spot with Graham McNamee during an NBC experimental television broadcast...", died:date('1966-06-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/u0eEj1uzQNmSPQgBDcgGJaIHILR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5833"}}, {tmdbId:"29283", properties:{bornIn:"Camberwell, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0370821", born:date('1905-03-10'), name:"Richard Haydn", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRichard Haydn (March 10, 1905 – April 25, 1985) was an English comic actor in radio, films and television. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Richard Haydn, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1985-04-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7ot3ANjb8ZXk165XRAoxwRZUqRG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29283"}}, {tmdbId:"5320", properties:{bornIn:"Boulogne-Billancourt, Seine", imdbId:"0001989", born:date('1931-07-01'), name:"Leslie Caron", bio:"Leslie Claire Margaret Caron (born 1 July 1931) is a French-American actress and dancer. \n\nCaron is best known for the musical films An American in Paris (1951), Lili (1953), Daddy Long Legs (1955), and Gigi (1958), and for the nonmusical films Fanny (1961), The L-Shaped Room (1962), and Father Goose (1964).  She received two Academy Award nominations for Best Actress.  In 2006, she won a Primetime Emmy Award for her performance in Law & Order: Special Victims Unit...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8KaogFPimucFHFyUkdA0c0Bym5C.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5320"}}, {tmdbId:"27966", properties:{bornIn:"Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0505157", born:date('1906-12-27'), name:"Oscar Levant", bio:"Oscar Levant (December 27, 1906 – August 14, 1972) was an American pianist, composer, author, comedian, and actor. \n\nHe was more famous for his mordant character and witticisms, on the radio and in movies and television, than for his music...", died:date('1972-08-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mhChU0EruBOZcZIBiLx7qWaxT2M.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27966"}}, {tmdbId:"27967", properties:{bornIn:"Alexandria, Egypt", imdbId:"0350250", born:date('1915-02-08'), name:"Georges Guétary", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGeorges Guétary, born Lambros Worloou (February 8, 1915 – September 13, 1997) was a French singer, dancer, cabaret performer and film actor, best known his role in the 1951 musical An American in Paris. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Georges Guétary, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1997-09-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3buh7MC9qZwhPtoiPbNewbnGoR0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27967"}}, {tmdbId:"213495", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0043398", born:date('1924-02-24'), name:"Chikage Awashima", died:date('2012-02-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/p6CAnnLLVxk89Lsxz0oIaLpUuPR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/213495"}}, {tmdbId:"131016", properties:{bornIn:"Saitama, Japan", imdbId:"0594381", born:date('1916-09-17'), name:"Kuniko Miyake", bio:"Kuniko Miyake (三宅 邦子, Miyake Kuniko, 17 September 1916 – 4 November 1992) was a Japanese actress.  She appeared in more than 180 films from 1934 to 1991...", died:date('1992-11-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zLBRUKTnAcaTFcCT5gKUXs6XeRV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/131016"}}, {tmdbId:"20418", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0012443", born:date('1921-04-03'), name:"Jan Sterling", bio:"Most active in films during the 1950s, Jan Sterling received a Golden Globe Award for Best Supporting Actress for her performance in The High and the Mighty (1954), and was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress for the same performance.  Her career declined during the 1960s, however she continued to play occasional roles for television and theatre. \n\nSterling was born Jane Sterling Adriance in New York City, into a well-to-do family...", died:date('2004-03-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8seIbwahgz5T6AYeRgAqN2RD1vc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20418"}}, {tmdbId:"78304", properties:{bornIn:"Aberdeen, Washington, USA", imdbId:"0037816", born:date('1925-06-18'), name:"Robert Arthur", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRobert Arthur (born Robert Paul Arthaud; June 18, 1925 – October 1, 2008) was an American motion picture actor who appeared in dozens of films in the 1940s and 1950s.  He appeared in the 1949 war film Twelve O'Clock High as the comic relief–providing Sgt.  McIllhenny, in the 1951 Billy Wilder film Ace in the Hole, and in the 1950s television program The Lone Ranger.  Arthur was known for playing youthful teenage or young adult roles...", died:date('2008-10-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xoHKStYOwg54CCuSkHVCBLVP6Fh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78304"}}, {tmdbId:"251", properties:{bornIn:"Hamilton, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0064235", born:date('1909-10-19'), name:"Robert Beatty", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRobert Beatty (19 October 1909 – 3 March 1992) was a Canadian actor who worked in film, television and radio for most of his career and was especially known in the UK. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Robert Beatty, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1992-03-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ihB3jLo9i4p6wR6xJXjor9mav7W.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/251"}}, {tmdbId:"132720", properties:{bornIn:"Bearsden, Dumbartonshire, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0447016", born:date('1901-10-24'), name:"Moultrie Kelsall", died:date('1980-02-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iWaO3jRj7a8j1IMLnDOVxXDvtck.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/132720"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"12282", properties:{bornIn:"Bradford, Yorkshire, England", imdbId:"0719692", born:date('1909-08-25'), name:"Michael Rennie", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nMichael Rennie (25 August 1909 – 10 June 1971) was an English film, television, and stage actor, perhaps best known for his starring role as the space visitor Klaatu in the 1951 classic science fiction film The Day the Earth Stood Still. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article  Michael Rennie  licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1971-06-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/Af8eDakA6skhlquvwkLR3s56NL1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12282"}}, {tmdbId:"1934", properties:{bornIn:"Packard, Kentucky, USA", imdbId:"0623658", born:date('1926-01-20'), name:"Patricia Neal", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nPatricia Neal (January 20, 1926 – August 8, 2010) was an American actress of stage and screen.  She was best known for her roles as World War II widow Helen Benson in The Day the Earth Stood Still (1951), wealthy matron Emily Eustace Failenson in Breakfast at Tiffany's (1961), and middle-aged housekeeper Alma Brown in Hud (1963), for which she won the Academy Award for Best Actress...", died:date('2010-08-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/spdaTjYnm2TfYsOUYIM9zGdr4Ym.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1934"}}, {tmdbId:"18861", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0609216", born:date('1915-02-28'), name:"Zero Mostel", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSamuel Joel “Zero” Mostel (February 28, 1915 – September 8, 1977) was an American actor of stage and screen, best known for his portrayal of comic characters such as Tevye onstage in Fiddler on the Roof, Pseudolus onstage and onscreen in A Funny Thing Happened on the Way to the Forum, and Max Bialystock in the original film version of The Producers...", died:date('1977-08-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vOV8f7mQ2TqTQNupM8sVimAZOvh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18861"}}, {tmdbId:"2097", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0208125", born:date('1905-09-29'), name:"Ted de Corsia", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia  \n\nTed de Corsia (September 29, 1903 [or 1905] – April 11, 1973) was an American radio, film, and television actor best remembered for his role as a gangster who turned state's evidence in the film The Enforcer (1951)...", died:date('1973-04-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/koshCsy9aAqgwH5E15CyNS4J3VZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2097"}}, {tmdbId:"95271", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0747413", born:date('1904-11-06'), name:"Selena Royle", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nSelena Royle (November 6, 1904 – April 23, 1983) was an American actress (of stage, radio, television and film), and later, an author.   Royle was born in New York City to playwright Edwin Milton Royle and actress Selena Fetter (April 12, 1860 - May 10, 1955).  She had an older sister, Josephine Fetter Royle (1901–1992). \n\nHer mother recounted in a newspaper article that she used to take Selena along with her to her rehearsals and performances...", died:date('1983-04-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/SqFituJ8FRagYqvEX5tVFzbOXV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95271"}}, {tmdbId:"12274", properties:{bornIn:"Garches, Seine-et-Oise [now Hauts-de-Seine], France", imdbId:"0693560", born:date('1940-01-20'), name:"Georges Poujouly", bio:"Georges Poujouly (20 January 1940, Garches, Hauts-de-Seine – 28 October 2000, Villejuif, Val-de-Marne) was a French actor who gained international acclaim as a child for his performance in the award-winning film Forbidden Games.  In the 1950s, he appeared in a number of other high-profile films, notably Les Diaboliques, And God Created Woman and Ascenseur pour l'échafaud.  His later career was spent mainly in television, where he specialised in voiceover work...", died:date('2000-10-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7eUtIon4lj4ab0SVwp4lkxLENvW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12274"}}, {tmdbId:"1959", properties:{bornIn:"Tourcoing, Nord, France", imdbId:"0287637", born:date('1946-06-15'), name:"Brigitte Fossey", bio:"Brigitte Fossey, born June 15, 1946 in Tourcoing, Nord, is a French actress...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/99CVmP5p4I9MO5a9crsQy3vTSwI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1959"}}, {tmdbId:"18811", properties:{bornIn:"Boulogne-Billancourt, France", imdbId:"0046133", born:date('1928-06-15'), name:"Laurence Badie", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qBOTUsxN7DX5POBKq3PAvUXqLO9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18811"}}, {tmdbId:"4303", properties:{bornIn:"Benkelman, Nebraska, USA", imdbId:"0000955", born:date('1903-04-09'), name:"Ward Bond", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nWardell Edwin Bond (April 9, 1903 – November 5, 1960) was an American film character actor whose rugged appearance and easygoing charm were featured in more than 200 films, as well as in the NBC television series Wagon Train from 1957 to 1961.  Among his best-remembered roles are Bert the cop in Frank Capra's It's a Wonderful Life (1946) and Captain Clayton in John Ford's The Searchers (1956)...", died:date('1960-11-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5HbDXDgFcpA07HjPpGpYRzGXnfN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4303"}}, {tmdbId:"85736", properties:{imdbId:"0447405", born:date('1900-09-06'), name:"Charles Kemper", died:date('1950-05-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9PDABjue3mdA08bKvNUikZ8NM6Z.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85736"}}, {tmdbId:"8237", properties:{bornIn:"Cincinnati, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0000013", born:date('1922-04-03'), name:"Doris Day", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDoris Day (born Doris Mary Ann Kappelhoff; April 3, 1922 - May 13, 2019) was an American actress and singer, and an outspoken animal rights activist since her retirement from show business.  Her entertainment career began in the 1940s as a big band singer.  In 1945 she had her first hit recording, \"Sentimental Journey\".  In 1948, she appeared in her first film, Romance on the High Seas...", died:date('2019-05-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oXzKVAdHhGA7pkFtuj67rYAOq60.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8237"}}, {tmdbId:"82387", properties:{bornIn:"East Orange, New Jersey, United States", imdbId:"0534286", born:date('1921-03-12'), name:"Gordon MacRae", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nGordon MacRae (March 12, 1921 – January 24, 1986) was an American actor and singer, best known for his appearances in the film versions of two Rodgers and Hammerstein musicals, Oklahoma! (1955) and Carousel (1956) and movies with Doris Day like Starlift. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Gordon MacRae  licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1986-01-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2xyxaqCTOk9lvtPV8A7ZHXZVw35.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82387"}}, {tmdbId:"13994", properties:{bornIn:"Portland, Indiana, USA", imdbId:"0000748", born:date('1902-01-20'), name:"Leon Ames", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nLeon Ames (January 20, 1902 – October 12, 1993) was an American film and television actor.  He is best remembered for playing fatherly figures in such films as Meet Me in St.  Louis (1944), as Judy Garland's father, and in Little Women (1949). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Leon Ames licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1993-10-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pYwDTwWl34W7tLfN8IbSAK9QopA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13994"}}, {tmdbId:"121003", properties:{bornIn:"London, England", imdbId:"0665902", born:date('1913-05-02'), name:"Nigel Patrick", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nNigel Patrick (born Nigel Dennis Wemyss; 2 May 1913 - 21 September 1981) was an English actor and stage director born into a theatrical family. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Nigel Patrick, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1981-09-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sFm8kb8DGb1G88J9Z2eFs5Wo3Po.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/121003"}}, {tmdbId:"121004", properties:{bornIn:"Liverpool, England", imdbId:"0799257", born:date('1922-06-05'), name:"Sheila Sim", bio:"Sheila  Sim was an English film and theatre actress.   She was married to Sir Richard Attenborough...", died:date('2016-01-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pfyKwYJP6geRv0K421GeNZl7mXW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/121004"}}, {tmdbId:"10027", properties:{bornIn:"Edinburgh, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0192958", born:date('1878-01-20'), name:"Finlay Currie", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nFinlay Jefferson Currie (20 January 1878 – 9 May 1968) was a Scottish actor of stage, screen and television. \n\nBorn in Edinburgh, Scotland, Currie's acting career began on the stage.  He and his wife Maude Courtney (1884–1959) did a song and dance act in the US in the 1890s.  He made his first film (The Old Man) in 1931.  He appeared as a priest in the 1943 Ealing World War II movie Undercover...", died:date('1968-05-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uY1a5fZjLbWsVGqn18F4Y0BLqco.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10027"}}, {tmdbId:"82405", properties:{bornIn:"Portland, Oregon, USA", imdbId:"0007225", born:date('1929-04-01'), name:"Jane Powell", bio:"Jane Powell was singing and dancing at an early age.  She sang on the radio and performed in theaters before her screen debut in 1944.  Through the 1940s and 1950s, she had a successful career in movie musicals.  However, in 1957, her career in films ended, as she had outgrown her innocent girl-next-door image.  She has made brief returns to acting in front of the camera -- on television, in commercials, and in a workout video...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zU4GkEqdn8Qlv14V7rrx3clNjnF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82405"}}, {tmdbId:"176852", properties:{imdbId:"0161468", born:date('1914-10-07'), name:"Sarah Churchill", died:date('1982-09-24'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/176852"}}, {tmdbId:"45982", properties:{bornIn:"Rome, Lazio, Italy", imdbId:"0814773", born:date('1920-06-15'), name:"Alberto Sordi", bio:"Alberto Sordi (15 June 1920 – 25 February 2003) was an Italian actor.  He was also a film director and the dubbing voice of Oliver Hardy in the Italian version of the Laurel &amp; Hardy films...", died:date('2003-02-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9N3t4avUHP2BCX6aEHpwzYsY71O.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/45982"}}, {tmdbId:"937248", properties:{bornIn:"Padua, Italy", imdbId:"0100654", born:date('1932-03-04'), name:"Brunella Bovo", died:date('2017-02-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/u57RoYRHbPEpGBjF5wN6EcSVta4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/937248"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"14151", properties:{bornIn:"Reggio Calabria, Calabria, Italy", imdbId:"0872689", born:date('1917-05-03'), name:"Leopoldo Trieste", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLeopoldo Trieste (3 May 1917, Reggio Calabria – 25 January 2003) was an Italian actor, film director and script writer. \n\nTrieste was born in Reggio Calabria.  He worked with directors such as Pietro Germi, Francis Ford Coppola, Giuseppe Tornatore, Tinto Brass, Charles Vidor, René Clément and Federico Fellini. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Leopoldo Trieste, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2003-01-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3DEbCzT2gL4ebP4zAYROH0QWeGA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14151"}}, {tmdbId:"5402", properties:{bornIn:"San Giorgio di Piano, Italy", imdbId:"0556399", born:date('1921-02-22'), name:"Giulietta Masina", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGiulietta Masina (22 February 1921 – 23 March 1994) was an Italian film and stage actress.  She starred in La Strada and Nights of Cabiria, both winners of the Academy Award for Best Foreign Language Film, in 1956 and 1957, respectively.  Masina won the Best Actress award at the 1957 Cannes Film Festival for the later film. \n\nShe was the wife and muse of the Italian film director Federico Fellini, in whom she found an artistic equal and collaborator...", died:date('1994-03-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rngVu8zHDnzjWKSMpAV4kwoCLjj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5402"}}, {tmdbId:"20394", properties:{bornIn:"Edinburgh, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0799237", born:date('1900-10-09'), name:"Alastair Sim", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAlastair George Bell Sim, CBE (9 October 1900 – 19 August 1976) was a Scottish character actor who appeared in a string of classic British films.  He is best remembered in the role of Ebenezer Scrooge in the 1951 film Scrooge, and for his portrayal of Miss Fritton, the headmistress in two St.  Trinian's films...", died:date('1976-08-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uKsEHAt0AbUebvaCHOoVq5eQmp2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20394"}}, {tmdbId:"96421", properties:{imdbId:"0365692", born:date('1892-02-23'), name:"Kathleen Harrison", bio:"Kathleen Harrison was long a stalwart of British cinema.  Her place was always firmly below stairs – a cook perhaps, or a cleaning lady often answering the door with a puzzled expression always fearful that trouble was just around the corner. \n\nShe was born in 1892 in Blackburn in Lancashire.  She studied at RADA and then went to live in Agentina for some time.  On her return to Britain, she made her stage debut in 1926 in “The Constant Flirt”...", died:date('1995-12-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5e345uCFuNmp3D22BBp6PEyI0Wu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96421"}}, {tmdbId:"90643", properties:{bornIn:"Pembroke, Wales, UK", imdbId:"0424345", born:date('1899-02-18'), name:"Mervyn Johns", bio:"Father of actress Glynis Johns, who appeared with him in The Halfway House (1944) and The Sundowners (1960).  Stocky, benevolent-looking Welsh character who became an  unexpected star of British movies during WWII, then moved quickly into  post-war supports, with one of his fondly-remembered parts being that of  the cowering \"Bob Cratchit\" to Alastair Sim's cold-hearted \"Ebenezer Scrooge\" in the definitive film version of A Christmas Carol (1951)...", died:date('1992-09-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yzLrLZXfQYjiWFlyjqPCadP15q.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/90643"}}, {tmdbId:"5827", properties:{bornIn:"Broseley, Shropshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0045968", born:date('1906-11-13'), name:"Hermione Baddeley", bio:"Hermione Youlanda Ruby Clinton-Baddeley (13 November 1906 - 19 August 1986) was an English character actress of theatre, film and television. \n\nShe is the sister of Angela Baddeley, best known for playing Mrs Hudson in the television series 'Upstairs Downstairs'. \n\nShe died in California following a series of strokes on 19th August 1986...", died:date('1986-08-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eFXuOinjtdwuP73wCqRvV0TIPiX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5827"}}, {tmdbId:"39601", properties:{bornIn:"Gillespie, Illinois, U.S.", imdbId:"0444476", born:date('1919-04-13'), name:"Howard Keel", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Harold Clifford Keel (April 13, 1919 – November 7, 2004), known professionally as Howard Keel, was an American actor and singer.  He starred in many film musicals of the 1950s...", died:date('2004-11-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8pvdM0sFqs4Jq6Foh72UYhXXSh1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/39601"}}, {tmdbId:"3156", properties:{bornIn:"Holgate, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0113873", born:date('1892-07-28'), name:"Joe E. Brown", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJoseph Evans Brown (July 28, 1891 – July 6, 1973) was an American actor and comedian, remembered for his amiable screen persona, comic timing, and enormous smile.  In 1902 at the age of nine, he joined a troupe of circus tumblers known as the Five Marvelous Ashtons which toured the country on both the circus and vaudeville circuits.  Later he became a professional baseball player...", died:date('1973-07-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7lda0p575JsM2mbq6r5V3B7Hfc7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3156"}}, {tmdbId:"12498", properties:{bornIn:"Lynn, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0738746", born:date('1922-12-23'), name:"Ruth Roman", bio:"Ruth Roman (December 22, 1922 – September 9, 1999) was an American actress, principally appearing in dramas including the Alfred Hitchcock thriller Strangers on a Train (1951)...", died:date('1999-09-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8dfgFC7nSpemx5VYDDHcVtOgdtH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12498"}}, {tmdbId:"9857", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA ", imdbId:"0001500", born:date('1912-03-22'), name:"Karl Malden", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nKarl Malden (born Mladen George Sekulovich; March 22, 1912 – July 1, 2009) was an American actor.  He was primarily a character actor who for more than 60 years brought an intelligent intensity and a homespun authenticity to roles in theater, film and television, especially in such classic films as A Streetcar Named Desire (1951) — for which he won the Oscar for Best Supporting Actor — On the Waterfront (1954), Pollyanna (1960), and One-Eyed Jacks (1961)...", died:date('2009-07-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/njDua2jZ1X1f5SYLzpxDt0hIhYu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9857"}}, {tmdbId:"11496", properties:{bornIn:"Woolstock, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0001660", born:date('1914-01-05'), name:"George Reeves", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGeorge Reeves (January 5, 1914 – June 16, 1959) was an American actor best known for his role as Superman in the 1950s television program Adventures of Superman. \n\nHis death at age 45 from a gunshot remains a polarizing issue.  The official finding was suicide, but some believe he was murdered or the victim of an accidental shooting...", died:date('1959-06-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dnVVd91UdBz5inx7yF5Ba9SFPPJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11496"}}, {tmdbId:"31259", properties:{bornIn:"Wichita Falls, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0167659", born:date('1927-01-15'), name:"Phyllis Coates", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nPhyllis Coates (born Gypsie Ann Evarts Stell; January 15, 1927) is an American actress best known for her portrayal of reporter Lois Lane in the 1951 film Superman and the Mole-Men and in the first season of the television series Adventures of Superman. \n\nCoates signed a movie contract with Warner Bros.  extending from 1948 to 1956.  She co-starred with George O'Hanlon as the title character's wife in the studio's Joe McDoakes short-subject comedies...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9dC8P6uxXiTQeihFkZoAVyXEPjt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31259"}}, {tmdbId:"9596", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0179786", born:date('1914-08-10'), name:"Jeff Corey", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJeff Corey (August 10, 1914 – August 16, 2002) was an American stage and screen actor and director who became a well-respected acting teacher after being blacklisted in the 1950s. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jeff Corey,licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2002-08-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nDjlhfYkqlpOQPBQGUYARmjl2OH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9596"}}, {tmdbId:"95563", properties:{bornIn:"Bainbridge Island, Washington, USA", imdbId:"0715748", born:date('1916-02-10'), name:"Walter Reed", bio:"Walter Reed (born Walter Reed Smith), was an American stage, film and television actor.   Reed was born in 1916 in Fort Ward, Washington.  Following a stint as a Broadway actor, Reed broke into films in 1941.  He appeared in several features for RKO Radio Pictures, including the last two Mexican Spitfire comedies (in which Reed replaced Buddy Rogers as the Spitfire's husband)...", died:date('2001-08-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/e6smBlNUgVXIR3QGHI6yTndHQRo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95563"}}, {tmdbId:"66781", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0792212", born:date('1926-10-29'), name:"Margaret Sheridan", died:date('1982-05-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jVz2zqPrK0Ddb8xt3W451ibk2ai.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/66781"}}, {tmdbId:"103069", properties:{bornIn:"Oakland, California, U.S.", imdbId:"0864851", born:date('1917-03-23'), name:"Kenneth Tobey", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Kenneth Tobey (March 23, 1917 – December 22, 2002) was an American stage, television, and film actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Kenneth Tobey, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2002-12-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/t1LrNv667EbpLWj6YZuj4oRC95O.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/103069"}}, {tmdbId:"56444", properties:{bornIn:"St. Helens, Oregon, USA", imdbId:"0180452", born:date('1917-04-28'), name:"Robert Cornthwaite", died:date('2006-07-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6fcy9QCm5K0j2p92eROvtQaDN5m.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56444"}}, {tmdbId:"12356", properties:{bornIn:"Princeton, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0817930", born:date('1910-02-10'), name:"Douglas Spencer", died:date('1960-10-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mQA73ta5CoYSM5CiNYe6EHPEoDT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12356"}}, {tmdbId:"83622", properties:{imdbId:"0588322", born:date('1923-08-08'), name:"Eve Miller", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nEve Miller (8 August 1923 – 17 August 1973), was an American actress.  She appeared in 41 films between 1945 and 1961. \n\nShe was born in Los Angeles, California, USA and died in Van Nuys, California from cancer aged 50. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Eve Miller, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1973-08-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/c8nr2fnMAEyH8nRbqHbbSxPn14F.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83622"}}, {tmdbId:"4356", properties:{bornIn:"Miltonvale, Kansas, United States", imdbId:"0943867", born:date('1926-12-17'), name:"Patrice Wymore", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nPatrice Wymore (born December 17, 1926) is an American television, film, and stage actress of the 1950s and 1960s. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Patrice Wymore, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2014-03-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mKdALJBvg7hQzEV4K1FdDPZ2GKu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4356"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"11998", properties:{bornIn:"Rock Island, Illinois, U.S.", imdbId:"0000734", born:date('1906-04-22'), name:"Eddie Albert", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nEdward Albert Heimberger (April 22, 1906 – May 26, 2005), known professionally as Eddie Albert, was an American actor and activist.  He was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor in 1954 for his performance in Roman Holiday, and in 1973 for The Heartbreak Kid...", died:date('2005-05-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2xFo1VrdSxz3dDSnirQVH54t1aY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11998"}}, {tmdbId:"3149", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0000054", born:date('1926-06-01'), name:"Marilyn Monroe", bio:"Marilyn Monroe (born Norma Jeane Mortenson; June 1, 1926 – August 4, 1962) was an American actress, model, and singer.  Famous for playing comedic \"blonde bombshell\" characters, she became one of the most popular sex symbols of the 1950s and early 1960s and was emblematic of the era's changing attitudes towards sexuality.  She was a top-billed actress for only a decade, but her films grossed $200 million (equivalent to $2 billion in 2019) by the time of her death in 1962...", died:date('1962-08-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jCb0PQhXUtXpXtP6kNYYoloCHBO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3149"}}, {tmdbId:"69934", properties:{imdbId:"0186576", born:date('1912-01-11'), name:"Nick Cravat", died:date('1994-01-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hH6mdfZQYkMZsHgPHcVvKi5kIFz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69934"}}, {tmdbId:"69935", properties:{bornIn:"Budapest, Hungary", imdbId:"0058982", born:date('1927-06-18'), name:"Eva Bartok", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEva Bartok (18 June 1927 – 1 August 1998), born Eva Ivanova Szöke, was an actress born in Budapest, Hungary.  She began acting in films in 1950 and her last credited appearance was in 1966.  She is best known for appearances in Blood and Black Lace, The Crimson Pirate, Operation Amsterdam, and Ten Thousand Bedrooms. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Eva Bartok, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1998-08-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/udKSgl2sgY2W8JWYjT642ZsJFo2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69935"}}, {tmdbId:"10925", properties:{bornIn:"Bombay, British India, India", imdbId:"0857147", born:date('1905-01-15'), name:"Torin Thatcher", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nTorin Thatcher (15 January 1905 - 4 March 1981) was an English actor born in Bombay, British India, India), to English parents.  He was an imposing, powerfully built figure noted for his flashy portrayals of screen villains. \n\nHe was educated in England at Bedford School and at the Royal Academy of Dramatic Art.  He worked as a schoolmaster before first appearing on the London stage in 1927 and then entering British films in 1934...", died:date('1981-03-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/d5PZBimAcJjP239mVx98a2Ifv1o.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10925"}}, {tmdbId:"10017", properties:{bornIn:"Wilmette, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0000032", born:date('1923-10-04'), name:"Charlton Heston", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nCharlton Heston (October 4, 1923 – April 5, 2008) was an American actor of film, theatre and television.  Heston is known for heroic roles in films such as The Ten Commandments, Planet of the Apes and Ben-Hur, for which he won the Academy Award for Best Actor.  Heston was also known for his political activism...", died:date('2008-04-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/31Z0NOxctaaLPk7Nq60eeQaDHJa.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10017"}}, {tmdbId:"134429", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0419929", born:date('1924-04-29'), name:"Zizi Jeanmaire", bio:"Zizi Jeanmaire (born Renée Marcelle Jeanmaire 29 April 1924) is a French ballet dancer and the widow of renowned dancer and choreographer Roland Petit.  She became famous in the 1950s after playing the title role in the ballet Carmen, produced in London in 1949, and went on to appear in several Hollywood films. \n\nShe and Petit had one daughter, Valentine Petit, a dancer and actress...", died:date('2020-07-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qrstkEJi8A7yInwnYGnDENmQ0eu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/134429"}}, {tmdbId:"22035", properties:{imdbId:"0909715", born:date('1937-07-11'), name:"Joseph Walsh", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/22035"}}, {tmdbId:"4069", properties:{bornIn:" Guadalajara, Jalisco, Mexico", imdbId:"0432827", born:date('1924-01-16'), name:"Katy Jurado", bio:"Katy Jurado, born María Cristina Estela Marcela Jurado García, was a Mexican stage and screen actress. \n\nJurado had already established herself as an actress in Mexico in the 1940s when she came to Hollywood becoming a regular in Western films of the 1950s and 1960s...", died:date('2002-07-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rOM4I1J16cbAYapG5XwyI0ek8L4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4069"}}, {tmdbId:"33767", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0385443", born:date('1907-01-10'), name:"Shin'ichi Himori", bio:"Shinichi Himori (10 January 1907 – 12 September 1959), born Kazuo Moriyama, was a Japanese film actor.  He appeared in more than seventy films from 1925 to 1959...", died:date('1959-09-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uvdGhKmIIfjO705CqXAS13gO65X.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33767"}}, {tmdbId:"34375", properties:{bornIn:"Kyoto, Kyoto Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0848984", born:date('1912-03-25'), name:"Haruo Tanaka", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nHaruo Tanaka (田中 春男 Tanaka Haruo, 25 March 1912 – 21 February 1992) was a Japanese film actor noted for his supporting roles in a career that spanned seven decades. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Haruo Tanaka, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1992-03-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eziah9QZcIs3SVPgTS3iuyUpiW3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34375"}}, {tmdbId:"7454", properties:{bornIn:"Hokkaido, Japan", imdbId:"0156928", born:date('1917-04-28'), name:"Minoru Chiaki", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMinoru Chiaki (千秋 実 Chiaki Minoru) was a Japanese actor who appeared in such films as Akira Kurosawa's Seven Samurai and The Hidden Fortress. \n\nIn Seven Samurai he was the good-natured samurai Heihachi and he was the first of the samurai to be killed.  Ironically, in real life he turned out to be the last of the seven actors to die. \n\nLater in his career he appeared as a secondary actor in many Toei films...", died:date('1999-11-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7gxmZcpEK95BVskWxKJaJvJsTPZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7454"}}, {tmdbId:"85935", properties:{bornIn:"Wednesbury, Staffordshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0915077", born:date('1912-02-25'), name:"Richard Wattis", bio:"Richard Cameron Wattis (25 February 1912 – 1 February 1975) was an English actor. \n\nAfter leaving the family business, Wattis became an actor.  His debut was with Croydon Repertory Theatre, and he made many stage appearances in the West End in London.  His first appearance in a film was A Yank at Oxford (1938), but war service interrupted his career as an actor...", died:date('1975-02-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/szg1qIZ83gu9D579tbZzYJA6zju.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85935"}}, {tmdbId:"85934", properties:{bornIn:"Doncaster, South Yorkshire, England", imdbId:"0219221", born:date('1915-11-01'), name:"Michael Denison", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJohn Michael Terence Wellesley Denison CBE (1 November 1915 – 22 July 1998) was a noted English actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Michael Denison, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1998-07-22'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85934"}}, {tmdbId:"9112", properties:{bornIn:"Griswold, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0104507", born:date('1920-08-13'), name:"Neville Brand", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nNeville Brand (August 13, 1920 - April 16, 1992) was an American television and movie actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Neville Brand  licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1992-04-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pjdg8caE6wBStYDjMyMHD7bf2Gx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9112"}}, {tmdbId:"30119", properties:{bornIn:"Bethnal Green, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0060023", born:date('1921-04-08'), name:"Alfie Bass", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAlfred Bass  was an English actor.  He was born in Bethnal Green, London, the youngest in a Jewish family with ten children; their parents had fled persecution in Russia.  He appeared in a variety of stage, film, television and radio productions throughout his career. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Alfie Bass, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1987-07-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kDbvGBd6V7eeIbMxKh3GbAmo3n0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30119"}}, {tmdbId:"29545", properties:{bornIn:"Finchley, Middlesex, England, UK", imdbId:"0001954", born:date('1931-02-15'), name:"Claire Bloom", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPatricia Claire Blume, CBE (born 15 February 1931), better known by her stage name Claire Bloom, is an English film and stage actress...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/odfVnBPcv81kO66aV8MOJExo8Gb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29545"}}, {tmdbId:"14300", properties:{bornIn:"Hastings, Sussex, England, UK", imdbId:"0662116", born:date('1897-09-03'), name:"Cecil Parker", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nCecil Parker (3 September 1897 – 20 April 1971) was an English character and comedy actor with a distinctive husky voice, who usually played supporting roles in his 91 films made between 1928 and 1969. \n\nBorn Cecil Schwabe in Hastings, Sussex, he began his theatrical career in London in 1922 after serving in World War I...", died:date('1971-04-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bKRahLwOtk2EPYrE50zGjeZYsIO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14300"}}, {tmdbId:"3796", properties:{bornIn:"Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia", imdbId:"0001284", born:date('1916-11-24'), name:"Michael Gough", bio:"Francis Michael Gough (23 November 1916 – 17 March 2011) was an English character actor who made over 150 film and television appearances, known for his roles in the Hammer Horror Films from 1958 and for his recurring role as Alfred Pennyworth in all four films of the Tim Burton / Joel Schumacher Batman series...", died:date('2011-03-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/owcwnV6dymBd9YIQKDPzVA5EtZX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3796"}}, {tmdbId:"2750", properties:{bornIn:"Grosse Pointe Park, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0364915", born:date('1925-12-02'), name:"Julie Harris", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJulia Ann \"Julie\" Harris (born December 2, 1925) is an American stage, screen, and television actress.  She has won five Tony Awards, three Emmy Awards and a Grammy Award, and was nominated for an Academy Award.  In 1994, she was awarded the National Medal of Arts. [1] She is a member of the American Theatre Hall of Fame.  She also received the 2002 Special Lifetime Achievement Tony Award...", died:date('2013-08-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bs9yUHWYQ4H3wNz3mI6BqMJPxNb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2750"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"30511", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001121", born:date('1942-04-09'), name:"Brandon De Wilde", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAndre Brandon deWilde (April 9, 1942 – July 6, 1972) was an American theatre and film actor. He was born into a theatrical family in Brooklyn.  Debuting on Broadway at the age of 7, De Wilde became a national phenomenon by the time he completed his 492 performances for The Member of the Wedding[3][4] and was considered a child prodigy...", died:date('1972-07-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uoQw46AGnOUR37r9MHhK5GAxjDo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30511"}}, {tmdbId:"8233", properties:{bornIn:"Des Moines, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0569902", born:date('1914-05-10'), name:"Charles McGraw", bio:"Charles McGraw (born Charles Butters) was an American stage, screen, and television actor.  He developed into a leading man, especially in film noir classics during the late 1940s and early 1950s.  His gravelly voice and rugged looks enhanced his appeal in the noir stylistic genre and provided him many roles as cops, military officers, and the such...", died:date('1980-07-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pB6bFNUXvucYFM1PQUEzEykSb2v.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8233"}}, {tmdbId:"99752", properties:{bornIn:"Beverly Hills, Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0924916", born:date('1922-11-27'), name:"Jacqueline White", bio:"Jacqueline Jane White (born November 27, 1922) is an American actress...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/o2MEv8lzAOELPYlXNucmeLckZNr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/99752"}}, {tmdbId:"99348", properties:{bornIn:"Des Moines, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0311357", born:date('1941-10-17'), name:"Gordon Gebert", bio:"Gordon Gebert is a former screen and television child actor, best known for his roles in the films Holiday Affair (1949) and The Narrow Margin (1952).  He later turned away from acting, studied architecture, and became a college professor...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qFVHZlB9jhVcx4UgACwyo7zeSxV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/99348"}}, {tmdbId:"45232", properties:{bornIn:"Pen Argyl, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0712731", born:date('1926-09-25'), name:"Aldo Ray", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAldo Ray (born Aldo DaRe; September 25, 1926 – March 27, 1991) was an American actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Aldo Ray, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1991-03-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/PjIWgub8G5zxePasD1IuqFolxl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/45232"}}, {tmdbId:"81183", properties:{bornIn:"St. Louis, Missouri, U.S.", imdbId:"0157893", born:date('1913-10-02'), name:"William Ching", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nWilliam Ching, also credited as William Brooks, Bill Ching and William Brooks Ching (born 2 October 1913, St.  Louis, Missouri - died 1 July 1989, Tustin, California) was a United States character actor who appeared in almost 20 films and on television during the later 1940s and throughout the 1950s.  By the early 21st century Ching was most widely noted for his supporting role in Rudolph Maté's 1950 film noir drama D. O. A...", died:date('1989-07-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/noGb3EWltYBssnHFmpGbflokgsi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81183"}}, {tmdbId:"19414", properties:{bornIn:"Durango, Colorado, USA", imdbId:"0876451", born:date('1908-08-21'), name:"Tom Tully", bio:"Tom Tully (August 21, 1908 – April 27, 1982) was an American actor...", died:date('1982-04-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qi73NpsUzob7d7J1QedheooTZgE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19414"}}, {tmdbId:"7331", properties:{bornIn:"Cedarville, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0662223", born:date('1922-06-26'), name:"Eleanor Parker", bio:"Eleanor Jean Parker was born on June 26, 1922, in Cedarville, Ohio, the  last of three children born to a mathematics teacher and his wife.   Eleanor caught the acting bug early and began performing in school  plays.  She was was so serious about becoming a thespian, she attended  the Rice Summer Theatre on Martha's Vineyard in Massachusetts beginning  when she was 15 years old...", died:date('2013-12-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lW4JlEsaJC1MdX7V7nyeKOAGvmb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7331"}}, {tmdbId:"7302", properties:{bornIn:" Merced, California, USA", imdbId:"0001463", born:date('1927-07-06'), name:"Janet Leigh", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJanet Leigh (July 6, 1927 – October 3, 2004), born Jeanette Helen Morrison, was an American actress.  She was the wife of actor Tony Curtis from June 1951 to September 1962 and the mother of Kelly Curtis and Jamie Lee Curtis. \n\nDiscovered by actress Norma Shearer, Leigh secured a contract with MGM and began her film career in the late 1940s...", died:date('2004-10-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iFhbonauuPx1QT6JfOeWNtwSZ5g.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7302"}}, {tmdbId:"3754", properties:{bornIn:"Elberon, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0002072", born:date('1917-08-25'), name:"Mel Ferrer", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMel Ferrer (August 25, 1917 – June 2, 2008) was an American actor, film director and film producer...", died:date('2008-06-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hWYjmKZ5uk1PLxfgedTNnTa6tP9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3754"}}, {tmdbId:"13295", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0640307", born:date('1925-08-28'), name:"Donald O'Connor", bio:"Donald O’Connor (1925–2003) was an American dancer, singer, and actor who came to fame in a series of movies in which he co-starred alternately with Gloria Jean, Peggy Ryan, and Francis the Talking Mule.  He is best known today for his role in Singin' in the Rain...", died:date('2003-09-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sV7Dx16wcajPsxJItmW5dX4axoW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13295"}}, {tmdbId:"8857", properties:{bornIn:"El Paso, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0001666", born:date('1932-04-01'), name:"Debbie Reynolds", bio:"Mary Frances \"Debbie\" Reynolds (April 1, 1932 – December 28, 2016) was an American actress, singer, businesswoman, film historian, and humanitarian.  She was nominated for the Golden Globe Award for Most Promising Newcomer for her portrayal of Helen Kane in the 1950 film Three Little Words, and her breakout role was her first leading role, as Kathy Selden in Singin' in the Rain (1952)...", died:date('2016-12-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tCw9QRXX7oQ0aBjA9IUGS3PLDuK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8857"}}, {tmdbId:"14168", properties:{bornIn:"Ulm, Germany", imdbId:"0460651", born:date('1925-12-28'), name:"Hildegard Knef", bio:"Hildegard Frieda Albertine Knef (December 28, 1925 - February 1, 2002) was a German actress, singer and writer...", died:date('2002-02-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fb9vmaxT1k7Yg4nVxvMkl3BxCvh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14168"}}, {tmdbId:"145237", properties:{imdbId:"0533943", name:"Micheál MacLiammóir", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fyWcZUQBLQiLWZHr1ankuEDuauW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/145237"}}, {tmdbId:"92908", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0178509", born:date('1909-02-04'), name:"Robert Coote", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRobert Coote (4 February 1909 – 26 November 1982) was an English actor.  He played aristocrats or British military types in many films, and created the role of Colonel Hugh Pickering in the long-running original Broadway production of My Fair Lady. \n\nCoote was born in London and educated at Hurstpierpoint College in Sussex...", died:date('1982-11-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ojyivCELGaku5MoRZjhI6RWf3Wo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/92908"}}, {tmdbId:"130223", properties:{bornIn:"Ottawa, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0167235", born:date('1923-07-10'), name:"Suzanne Cloutier", died:date('2003-12-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cBqJTPI32zdxH8JACxESRHV7F0G.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/130223"}}, {tmdbId:"12336", properties:{bornIn:"Trento, Austria-Hungary (now Trento, Trentino-Alto Adige, Italy)", imdbId:"0061472", born:date('1882-10-10'), name:"Carlo Battisti", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nCarlo Battisti (10 October 1882 - 6 March 1977) was an Italian linguist and actor, famed for his starring role in Vittorio de Sica's Umberto D. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Carlo Battisti, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1977-03-06'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12336"}}, {tmdbId:"224209", properties:{bornIn:"L'Aquila, Italia", born:date('1935-05-05'), name:"Maria Pia Casilio", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMaria-Pia Casilio (5 May 1935 – 10 April 2012) was an Italian film actress, best known for her roles in Umberto D.  and Un americano a Roma. \n\nBorn in San Pio delle Camere, L'Aquila, Casilio was pretty active between 1952 and 1960, usually with the typical characterization of a querulous and naive small-town girl, then, after her marriage with the voice actor Giuseppe Rinaldi, she semi-retired from acting.  On the Criterion Collection DVD release of Umberto D...", died:date('2012-04-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2BN5YsymHm22FSjY6SvJlvGbcqR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/224209"}}, {tmdbId:"12338", properties:{bornIn:"Bologna, Emilia-Romagna, Italy", imdbId:"0312902", born:date('1911-03-22'), name:"Lina Gennari", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12338"}}, {tmdbId:"12339", properties:{imdbId:"0800837", name:"Ileana Simova", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12339"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"133769", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0371122", born:date('1915-06-25'), name:"Peter Lind Hayes", bio:"Peter Lind Hayes (born Joseph Conrad Lind; June 25, 1915 – April 21, 1998) was an American vaudeville entertainer, songwriter, and film and television actor. \n\nHayes made his vaudeville debut with his mother at the age of six.  In 1939, his mother sold some jewelry and borrowed $8,000 to open the Grace Hayes Lodge in Los Angeles, where he began working as a nightclub performer. \n\nHe appeared in films throughout the 1930s and 1940s, and had a significant television career in the 1950s...", died:date('1998-04-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ivK0Uiy0k7nszsIlVyoTxE4U9k.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/133769"}}, {tmdbId:"133770", properties:{bornIn:"New Orleans", imdbId:"0372351", born:date('1918-04-14'), name:"Mary Healy", bio:"Mary Healy was born on April 14, 1918 in New Orleans, Louisiana, USA.  She is an actress, known for The 5,000 Fingers of Dr.  T.  (1953), Strictly in the Groove (1942) and Second Fiddle (1939).  She was the wife of Peter Lind Hayes...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/133770"}}, {tmdbId:"16421", properties:{bornIn:"Baltimore, Maryland, USA", imdbId:"0175788", born:date('1917-04-15'), name:"Hans Conried", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nHans Georg Conried, Jr.  (April 15, 1917 – January 5, 1982) was an American actor, voice actor and comedian, who was very active in voice-over roles and known for providing the voices of Walt Disney's Mr.  George Darling and Captain Hook in Peter Pan (1953), for playing the title role in The 5,000 Fingers of Dr.  T (1953), Dr...", died:date('1982-01-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xCeZ4Ln7Fs8GdpKpVV3qHbU0W5J.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16421"}}, {tmdbId:"20099", properties:{bornIn:"Queens, New York, USA", imdbId:"0720568", born:date('1941-12-10'), name:"Tommy Rettig", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nThomas Noel \"Tommy\" Rettig (December 10, 1941 – February 15, 1996) was an American child actor and computer software engineer and author.  Rettig is best remembered for portraying the character \"Jeff Miller\" in the first three seasons of CBS's Lassie television series, from 1954–1957, later seen in syndicated re-runs as Jeff's Collie...", died:date('1996-02-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vxUvJ7wS6erxUPpHtlmX2dcU7tE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20099"}}, {tmdbId:"41226", properties:{bornIn:"Amarillo, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0001998", born:date('1921-03-08'), name:"Cyd Charisse", bio:"Cyd Charisse (March 8, 1922 - June 17, 2008) was an American actress and dancer.   Charisse entered films in the 1940s.  Her roles usually focused on her abilities as a dancer.  Her films include Singin' in the Rain, The Band Wagon and Silk Stockings.  She stopped dancing in films in the late 1950s, but continued acting in film and television, and in 1992 made her Broadway debut...", died:date('2008-06-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xD5qN7oF5VJeCmgf2Ms3mTcfrAO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41226"}}, {tmdbId:"160239", properties:{bornIn:"San Diego, California, USA", imdbId:"0264660", born:date('1920-10-27'), name:"Nanette Fabray", died:date('2018-02-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pV07ZPDi1LSG3gtTwKSq3nIxIdi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/160239"}}, {tmdbId:"96283", properties:{bornIn:" San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0104720", born:date('1919-11-18'), name:"Jocelyn Brando", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJocelyn Brando (November 18, 1919 – November 27, 2005) was an American film, stage and television actress. \n\nHer film debut came in the war movie China Venture (1953) with Edmond O'Brien and Barry Sullivan.  Her best-known movie role was as detective Glenn Ford's wife in the film noir The Big Heat (1953)...", died:date('2005-11-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/y5jELN38pydIPkKEme3rMlSo2zK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96283"}}, {tmdbId:"96284", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0780038", born:date('1913-11-13'), name:"Alexander Scourby", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAlexander Scourby (November 13, 1913 – February 22, 1985) was an American film, television, and voice actor known for his deep and resonant voice.  He is best known for his film role as the ruthless mob boss Mike Lagana in Fritz Lang's The Big Heat (1953), and is also particularly well-remembered in the English-speaking world for his landmark recordings of the entire King James Version audio Bible, which have been released in numerous editions...", died:date('1985-02-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aotUNzQHC46G1rIwckvjsuRXbUA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96284"}}, {tmdbId:"7685", properties:{bornIn:"New Westminster, British Columbia, Canada", imdbId:"0000994", born:date('1917-05-21'), name:"Raymond Burr", bio:"Raymond William Stacey Burr (May 21, 1917 – September 12, 1993) was a Canadian actor, primarily known for his title roles in the television dramas Perry Mason and Ironside.  His early acting career included roles on Broadway, radio, television and in film, usually as the villain.  He won two Emmy Awards in 1959 and 1961 for the role of Perry Mason, which he played for nine seasons between 1957 and 1966...", died:date('1993-09-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ytOh75gcfS1fxLXb0fHACDajscz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7685"}}, {tmdbId:"30273", properties:{bornIn:"Prescott, Arizona, USA", imdbId:"0213619", born:date('1910-11-14'), name:"Rosemary DeCamp", bio:"Rosemary DeCamp was an American radio, film, and television actress.  DeCamp first came to fame in November 1937, when she took the role of Judy Price, the secretary/nurse of Dr.  Christian in the long-running radio series of the same name.  She also played in The Career of Alice Blair, a transcribed syndicated soap opera that ran in 1939–1940. \n\nShe made her film debut in Cheers for Miss Bishop and appeared in many Warner Bros...", died:date('2001-02-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jNhDyOpBIXHLnWQZ12XoBrBVoB5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30273"}}, {tmdbId:"76382", properties:{bornIn:"Grand-Mère, Quebec, Canada", imdbId:"0572885", born:date('1926-12-01'), name:"Allyn Ann McLerie", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Allyn Ann McLerie (born December 1, 1926, Grand-Mère, Quebec, Canada)  is a Canadian-born, Brooklyn-reared actress, singer and dancer who worked with most of Golden Age musical theatre's major choreographers, including George Balanchine, Agnes de Mille, and Jerome Robbins.   McLerie made her Broadway debut as a teenager in Kurt Weill's One Touch of Venus...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nQjx4EpAkg00mYVdMSFg5fEQMP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/76382"}}, {tmdbId:"45291", properties:{bornIn:"Hackensack, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0137023", born:date('1925-07-15'), name:"Philip Carey", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPhilip Carey  (July 15, 1925 – February 6, 2009) was an American actor. \n\nCarey was born in Hackensack, New Jersey. [3] He served in the United States Marine Corps, was wounded as part of the ship's detachment of the USS Franklin during World War II, and served again in the Korean War. [4]\n\nOne of his earliest roles was Lt.  (jg) Bob Perry in John Wayne's Operation Pacific...", died:date('2009-02-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2aJshf8zLbBFYsjsWYYhz9h76jZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/45291"}}, {tmdbId:"543200", properties:{imdbId:"0759367", name:"Carmilla Salvatorelli", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/543200"}}, {tmdbId:"11168", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0717256", born:date('1920-01-16'), name:"Elliott Reid", bio:"Elliott Reid was born on January 16, 1920 in New York City, New York, as Edgeworth Blair Reid.  He was an actor and writer, known for Gentlemen Prefer Blondes (1953), Inherit the Wind (1960) and The Absent-Minded Professor (1961).  He died on June 21, 2013 in Studio City, Los Angeles, California...", died:date('2013-06-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ahqACyudgXF2ZLT4H80mQ2EaNTY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11168"}}, {tmdbId:"100348", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0268350", born:date('1922-06-26'), name:"Timothy Farrell", bio:"Timothy Farrell was an American film and television actor and deputy marshall...", died:date('1989-05-09'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100348"}}, {tmdbId:"99126", properties:{imdbId:"0298215", born:date('1923-03-10'), name:"Dolores Fuller", died:date('2011-05-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3Uou2DkJWQkB8humXwSoz2pY90K.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/99126"}}, {tmdbId:"89581", properties:{bornIn:"Detroit, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0848251", born:date('1915-02-04'), name:"William Talman", died:date('1968-08-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/v3EG7QdDBYDcBTPJtWzFrlCZEx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89581"}}, {tmdbId:"30307", properties:{imdbId:"0869064", born:date('1909-01-28'), name:"José Torvay", died:date('1973-01-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kjyVlz4J1UFvvhXB8hzlYE8aBt6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30307"}}, {tmdbId:"83262", properties:{bornIn:"Plainfield, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0456533", born:date('1927-09-18'), name:"Phyllis Kirk", bio:"Phyllis Kirk was an American actress...", died:date('2006-10-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dAox094OqiF9bnsoOpWP3aGr3xQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83262"}}, {tmdbId:"19109", properties:{bornIn:"Amarillo, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0427700", born:date('1930-04-28'), name:"Carolyn Jones", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nCarolyn Sue Jones (April 28, 1930 – August 3, 1983) was an American actress. \n\nJones began her film career in the early 1950s, and by the end of the decade had achieved recognition with a nomination for an Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress for The Bachelor Party (1957) and a Golden Globe Award as one of the most promising actresses of 1959...", died:date('1983-08-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kL9b19NTorUOSckbT5p9EcxPkcB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19109"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"14831", properties:{bornIn:"Traverse City - Michigan - USA", imdbId:"0915536", born:date('1914-01-30'), name:"David Wayne", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nDavid Wayne (January 30, 1914 – February 9, 1995) was an American actor with a career spanning nearly 50 years. \n\nEarly life and career\n\nWayne was born Wayne James McMeekan in Traverse City, Michigan, the son of Helen Matilda (née Mason) and John David McMeekan.  He grew up in Bloomingdale, Michigan...", died:date('1995-02-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wD2T2dUtO7yNQPWzS1Ef1UTkd5A.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14831"}}, {tmdbId:"74542", properties:{bornIn:"Denver, Colorado, USA", imdbId:"0750640", born:date('1927-01-04'), name:"Barbara Rush", bio:"Barbara Rush is an American Golden Globe Award-winning movie and television actress.  In 1954, Rush won the Golden Globe Award as most promising female newcomer for her role in the 1953 American black-and-white science fiction film, It Came From Outer Space...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6FhEO5tTf64aocluK57TLrRHw5l.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74542"}}, {tmdbId:"3341", properties:{bornIn:"Guelph, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0768178", born:date('1906-08-29'), name:"Joe Sawyer", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJoe Sawyer (born Joseph Sauers, August 29, 1906 – April 21, 1982) was a Canadian film actor.  He appeared in more than 200 films between 1927 and 1962, and was sometimes billed under his birth name.  He was born in Guelph, Ontario, Canada. \n\nSawyer gained acting experience in the Pasadena Playhouse.  Popular roles that he portrayed included Sergeant Biff O'Hara in the Rin Tin Tin television program, a film, and on radio...", died:date('1982-04-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4kS7mU7cXazhq9P9DyssW6P6BPw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3341"}}, {tmdbId:"236016", properties:{bornIn:"Bordeaux, Gironde, France", imdbId:"0201638", born:date('1917-05-01'), name:"Danielle Darrieux", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDanielle Darrieux (French pronunciation: ​[da. niɛl i. vɔn ma. ʁi ɑ̃. twa. nɛt daʁ. jø]) (1 May 1917 – 17 October 2017) was a French actress and singer, who appeared in more than 110 films after 1931.  She was one of France's great movie stars and her eight-decade career is among the longest in film history...", died:date('2017-10-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/AgvxGJ4HQLFYj00OqraKMnS5N3i.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/236016"}}, {tmdbId:"36209", properties:{imdbId:"0213581", born:date('1894-01-19'), name:"Jean Debucourt", died:date('1958-03-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iaoPXYhdrmF8NWOMa01o1eXnerb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/36209"}}, {tmdbId:"4070", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0000038", born:date('1929-11-12'), name:"Grace Kelly", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGrace Patricia Kelly (November 12, 1929 – September 14, 1982) was an American actress who, in April 1956, married Rainier III, Prince of Monaco, to become Princess consort of Monaco, styled as Her Serene Highness The Princess of Monaco, and commonly referred to as Princess Grace...", died:date('1982-09-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aMist7cww3a8FxJDg1eXoUNJCDM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4070"}}, {tmdbId:"39954", properties:{bornIn:"Plymouth, Devon, England, UK", imdbId:"0801786", born:date('1923-10-09'), name:"Donald Sinden", bio:"​Sir Donald Alfred Sinden CBE (born 9 October 1923) is an English actor of theatre, film and television.  Sinden was born in Plymouth, Devon, England, on 9 October 1923.  The son of Alfred Edward Sinden and his wife Mabel Agnes (née Fuller), he grew up in the Sussex village of Ditchling, where their home ('The Limes') doubled as the local chemist shop.  He was married to actress Diana Mahony from 1948 until her death in 2004.  He lives near Tenterden, Kent...", died:date('2014-09-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/x7xq2O7mqVwSnnQNo3E1YDndIx7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/39954"}}, {tmdbId:"19216", properties:{bornIn:"Canton, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0676492", born:date('1926-10-15'), name:"Jean Peters", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJean Peters (October 15, 1926 – October 13, 2000) was an American actress, known as a star of 20th Century Fox in the late 1940s and early 1950s and as the second (or possibly third) wife of Howard Hughes.  Although possibly best remembered for her siren role in Pickup on South Street (1953), Peters was known for her resistance to be turned into a sex symbol, preferring to play unglamorous, down-to-earth women...", died:date('2000-10-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mC1BxCRos4XJHG3MAErcoiOv8dX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19216"}}, {tmdbId:"85409", properties:{bornIn:"Caldwell, Kansas, USA", imdbId:"0795289", born:date('1917-06-02'), name:"Max Showalter", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMax Showalter (June 2, 1917 – July 30, 2000), also credited as Casey Adams, was an American film, television, and stage actor, as well as a composer, pianist, and singer.  One of Showalter's most memorable roles was as Jean Peters' character's husband in the 1953 film Niagara...", died:date('2000-07-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kOnSg2xSSDcUBtfbLBqOaLcTSsc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85409"}}, {tmdbId:"67230", properties:{bornIn:"Terre Haute, Indiana, USA", imdbId:"0859892", born:date('1913-07-08'), name:"Bill Thompson", died:date('1971-07-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/52fphnQBVzgf9yDlcIuZRLluKsA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67230"}}, {tmdbId:"7684", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0728812", born:date('1902-02-14'), name:"Thelma Ritter", died:date('1969-02-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6gZKUPYiAr5FJWPiR9SvSnt2Ijj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7684"}}, {tmdbId:"20100", properties:{imdbId:"0904531", born:date('1913-07-15'), name:"Murvyn Vye", died:date('1976-08-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tYlH6W5Nn0ZbDZ8wWgwAUy6yMJP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20100"}}, {tmdbId:"5341", properties:{bornIn:"Pontrhydyfen, Wales, UK", imdbId:"0000009", born:date('1925-11-10'), name:"Richard Burton", bio:"Richard Burton, CBE (10 November 1925 – 5 August 1984) was a Welsh actor.  He was nominated seven times for an Academy Award, six of which were for Best Actor in a Leading Role (without ever winning), and was a recipient of BAFTA, Golden Globe and Tony Awards for Best Actor.  Although never trained as an actor, Burton was, at one time, the highest-paid actor in Hollywood...", died:date('1984-08-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aEofbdM6kVs77cdJAGeOyM434rY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5341"}}, {tmdbId:"14500", properties:{bornIn:"Crouch Hill, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0001739", born:date('1929-01-31'), name:"Jean Simmons", bio:"Jean Merilyn Simmons, OBE (January 31, 1929 – January 22, 2010) was an English actress.  She appeared predominantly in motion pictures, beginning with films made in Great Britain during and after World War II – she was one of J.  Arthur Rank's 'well-spoken young starlets' – followed mainly by Hollywood films from 1950...", died:date('2010-01-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iCF8imUDR2jzQtg8SlD7ca9wOu3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14500"}}, {tmdbId:"1932", properties:{bornIn:"Ixelles, Belgium", imdbId:"0000030", born:date('1929-05-04'), name:"Audrey Hepburn", bio:"Audrey Hepburn (born Audrey Kathleen Ruston; 4 May 1929 – 20 January 1993) was a British actress and humanitarian.  Although modest about her acting ability, Hepburn remains one of the world's most famous actresses of all time, remembered as a film and fashion icon of the twentieth century...", died:date('1993-01-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2zBWqhiehplfYap7MVbpCfei7H4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1932"}}, {tmdbId:"11999", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York", imdbId:"0694403", born:date('1894-03-14'), name:"Hartley Power", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nHartley Power (1894–1966) was an American-born British film and television actor.   He is best remembered for two roles: \"Sylvester Kee\" the ventriloquist who is shot and almost killed by \"Maxwell Frere\" (Michael Redgrave) as a rival for his \"dummy\"'s affections in Dead of Night; the chief of the news agency that Gregory Peck worked for in Roman Holiday...", died:date('1966-01-29'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11999"}}, {tmdbId:"2565", properties:{bornIn:"Monsummano Terme, Pistoia, Tuscany, Italy", imdbId:"0598971", born:date('1921-10-13'), name:"Yves Montand", bio:"Ivo Livi, better known as Yves Montand (13 October 1921 – 9 November 1991), was an Italian-French actor and singer...", died:date('1991-11-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wewmvQm200D2jD14G4YjSmg0WVb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2565"}}, {tmdbId:"2566", properties:{bornIn:"Rennes, Ille-et-Vilaine, France", imdbId:"0889024", born:date('1892-08-21'), name:"Charles Vanel", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Charles-Marie Vanel, known as Charles Vanel (21 August 1892 in Rennes, France - 15 April 1989, in Cannes, France) was a French director and actor.  He made his screen debut in 1912, in Robert Péguy's Jim Crow.  His 77 year career comprised appearances in more than 200 films. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Charles Vanel, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1989-04-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zRqCT6pRUqhvRQP4gD7FcWD2kbT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2566"}}, {tmdbId:"2568", properties:{bornIn:"Florence, Tuscany, Italy", imdbId:"0525793", born:date('1912-07-03'), name:"Folco Lulli", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Folco Lulli (3 July 1912 – 23 May 1970) was an Italian film actor.  He appeared in 104 films between 1946 and 1970.  He was the brother of actor Piero Lulli. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Folco Lulli, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1970-05-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xgKFFh5Qb2mTyv53uX7oJM3AgH9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2568"}}, {tmdbId:"2567", properties:{bornIn:"Steinwehr, Pomerania, Germany [now Kamienny Jaz, Zachodniopomorskie, Poland]", imdbId:"0886870", born:date('1911-07-16'), name:"Peter van Eyck", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Peter van Eyck, born Götz von Eick (16 July 1911, Steinwehr, Pomerania, Germany (now Kamienny Jaz, Poland) – 15 July 1969, Männedorf near Zürich, Switzerland), was a German-American actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Peter van Eyck, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1969-07-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/104PEiOgll349FBLQZJtOzkv5Ns.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2567"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"7569", properties:{bornIn:"Stockholm, Sweden", imdbId:"0027683", born:date('1932-02-14'), name:"Harriet Andersson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nHarriet Andersson (born 14 February 1932, Stockholm) is a Swedish actress, known outside Sweden for being part of one of director Ingmar Bergman's stock company. \n\nShe often played impulsive working class characters and quickly established a reputation on screen for her youthful, unpretentious, full-lipped sensuality.  She disdains the use of makeup...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6uUPqEM4vs9mOylNZ9j5ewpi7kt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7569"}}, {tmdbId:"81232", properties:{bornIn:"Uppsala, Uppsala län, Sweden", imdbId:"0252299", born:date('1926-06-06'), name:"Lars Ekborg", died:date('1969-10-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/t6VQyuw0kUdnMQ319yW8Civpajx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81232"}}, {tmdbId:"146882", properties:{bornIn:" Stockholm, Stockholms län, Sweden", imdbId:"0247954", born:date('1891-10-01'), name:"Dagmar Ebbesen", died:date('1954-12-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qSV7xxmnF8gGuHZqgS8T6b2Zcjv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/146882"}}, {tmdbId:"6665", properties:{bornIn:"Gävle, Gävleborgs län, Sweden", imdbId:"0294882", born:date('1919-06-23'), name:"Åke Fridell", died:date('1985-08-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6uUCqabY28cJquzorlEANzJ2mMl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6665"}}, {tmdbId:"7347", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0833865", born:date('1913-11-08'), name:"Robert Strauss", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRobert Strauss (November 8, 1913 – February 20, 1975) was a gravel-voiced American actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Robert Strauss (actor), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1975-02-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pFLl1NpwRaTE6dwTYzAsGcX0xEv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7347"}}, {tmdbId:"19534", properties:{bornIn:"Subiaco, Rome, Italy", imdbId:"0518178", born:date('1927-07-04'), name:"Gina Lollobrigida", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGina Lollobrigida (Italian pronunciation: [ˈdʒiːna lɔlloˈbriːdʒida]; born 4 July 1927) is an Italian actress, photojournalist and sculptress.  She was one of the most popular European actresses of the 1950s and early 1960s.  She was also an iconic sex symbol of the 1950s.  Today, she remains an active supporter of Italian and Italian American causes, particularly the National Italian American Foundation (NIAF)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pdvbAneNNd17OjUXk9w99t44pe1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19534"}}, {tmdbId:"9208", properties:{bornIn:"Detroit - Michigan - USA", imdbId:"0001822", born:date('1930-02-10'), name:"Robert Wagner", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRobert John Wagner (born February 10, 1930) is an American actor of stage, screen, and television. \n\nA veteran of many films in the 1950s and 1960s, Wagner gained prominence in three American television series that spanned three decades: It Takes a Thief (1968–70), Switch (1975–78), and Hart to Hart (1979–84).  In movies, Wagner is known for his role as Number Two in the Austin Powers films (1997, 1999, 2002)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dgIN3MrOfX8Q4pzchO58dhMgrFb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9208"}}, {tmdbId:"80600", properties:{bornIn:"Dublin, Ireland", imdbId:"0198241", born:date('1934-01-21'), name:"Audrey Dalton", bio:"Audrey Dalton (born on January 21, 1934) is an Irish television and film actress, whose acting career spanned the 1950s through 1970s.   She appeared in several B-westerns and other B-movies.   Some of her best known movies include Kitten with a Whip and Titanic...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3C8ysXImywLJwRmDJ2NJ2TwzmY7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80600"}}, {tmdbId:"134307", properties:{bornIn:"Chiba, Japan", imdbId:"0383261", born:date('1890-09-30'), name:"Chieko Higashiyama", died:date('1980-05-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jnZHDwtO6hq5mUwp7jO3cw12E6k.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/134307"}}, {tmdbId:"108021", properties:{bornIn:"Onuma District, Fukushima Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0593930", born:date('1919-03-23'), name:"Mitsuko Mito", bio:"Mitsuko Mito (水戸光子 Mito Mitsuko, 23 March 1919 – 5 April 1981) was a Japanese actress.  She appeared in more than 50 films between 1935 and 1973...", died:date('1981-04-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fYX7FJf3AMr4xhIPBfkR94OljD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/108021"}}, {tmdbId:"24551", properties:{bornIn:"Shimonoseki, Yamaguchi Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0849011", born:date('1909-11-28'), name:"Kinuyo Tanaka", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nKinuyo Tanaka (田中 絹代 Tanaka Kinuyo, 29 November 1909 – 21 March 1977) was a Japanese actress and director. \n\nTanaka was born in Shimonoseki, Yamaguchi Prefecture, Japan.  She became a leading actress at an early age, appearing in Yasujirō Ozu's I Graduated, But. . .  in 1929.  The following year she played the lead in Aiyoku no ki, and in 1931 she appeared in Japan's first talkie, The Neighbor's Wife and Mine, directed by Heinosuke Gosho...", died:date('1977-03-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/noiEyzOXEtqAEN3zQDEJ10748L6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24551"}}, {tmdbId:"2633910", properties:{name:"Louis Pérault", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2633910"}}, {tmdbId:"11570", properties:{imdbId:"0239379", name:"André Dubois", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11570"}}, {tmdbId:"5766", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0296996", born:date('1904-07-05'), name:"Lucien Frégis", died:date('1979-08-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/en2a7fTlKd4ebRdyuquLq6Fi1kr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5766"}}, {tmdbId:"71140", properties:{bornIn:"Rome, Italy", imdbId:"0409421", born:date('1931-10-29'), name:"Franco Interlenghi", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nFranco Interlenghi (born 29 October 1931 at Rome) is an Italian actor. \n\nHe made his acting debut at 15 in Vittorio De Sica's Neorealist film Sciuscià. \n\nHe has worked with great directors such as Federico Fellini in I Vitelloni, Michelangelo Antonioni in I Vinti and Luchino Visconti in his stage adaptation of Death of a salesman. \n\nMarried to Antonella Lualdi, he has a daughter, Antonellina Interlenghi, who is an actress as well...", died:date('2015-09-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/a4WC5TzqfD64R8x0uk9WQjbxC2U.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71140"}}, {tmdbId:"30832", properties:{bornIn:"Cortemaggiore - Piacenza - Emilia-Romagna - Italy", imdbId:"0264770", born:date('1926-02-15'), name:"Franco Fabrizi", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nFranco Fabrizi (Cortemaggiore, 15 February 1926 - Cortemaggiore, 18 October 1995) was an Italian actor. \n\nSon of a barber and a cinema cashier, was a soap opera photo actor, for example, the fotoromanzo Arizona Kid, in the newspaper Avventuroso Film.  When he was 24 years old, with a few experience in cinema, has got a small important roll in Chronicle of a Love (Cronaca di un amore) (1950), Michelangelo Antonioni's long film debut...", died:date('1995-10-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kzGbtReGp7FgRsbLctmgblFgJxa.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30832"}}, {tmdbId:"56442", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0058001", born:date('1919-06-14'), name:"Gene Barry", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGene Barry (June 14, 1919 – December 9, 2009) was an American stage, screen, and television actor.  Barry is known for his portrayal of the title character in the TV series Bat Masterson, among many roles. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Gene Barry, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2009-12-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sWZecdUDduttm4vjDRrsYWbou2e.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56442"}}, {tmdbId:"103079", properties:{bornIn:"Hollywood, Los Angeles, California", imdbId:"0732378", born:date('1929-05-25'), name:"Ann Robinson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAnn Robinson (born May 25, 1929) is an American actress. \n\nRobinson was born in Hollywood, California to a bank employee father.  She began her professional life as a stunt woman.  Paramount signed her as an actress in the 1950s, and her first leading role was as \"Sylvia Van Buren\" in that studio's 1953 film, The War of the Worlds, a role she reprised 35 years later in three episodes of the War of the Worlds television series...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jFmvxs57XKtZiNDpGu4S9BGjIl5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/103079"}}, {tmdbId:"2648", properties:{bornIn:"Balham, London, England", imdbId:"0871876", born:date('1913-04-16'), name:"Les Tremayne", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLes Tremayne (16 April 1913 – 19 December 2003) was a radio, film, and television actor.  Born Lester Tremayne in England, he moved with his family at the age four to Chicago, where he began in community theater.  He danced as a vaudeville performer and worked as amusement park barker.  He began working in radio when he was 17 years old...", died:date('2003-12-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pYQXe5qlmcTzqQwfLjYETLqQQ1b.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2648"}}, {tmdbId:"53010", properties:{bornIn:"Spokane, Washington, USA", imdbId:"0570615", born:date('1907-06-27'), name:"John McIntire", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJohn Herrick McIntire (June 27, 1907 – January 30, 1991) was an American character actor who appeared in 65 theatrical films and many more television series.  McIntire is well known for having replaced Ward Bond, upon Bond's sudden death in November 1960, as the star of NBC's Wagon Train.  He played Christopher Hale, the leader of the wagon train (and successor to Bond's character, Seth Adams) from early 1961 to the series' end in 1965...", died:date('1991-01-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/A2Nl0VDQmZ4JxT9tj0UzBNNMZm1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53010"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"4960", properties:{bornIn:"Ehrenfeld, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0000314", born:date('1921-11-03'), name:"Charles Bronson", bio:"Charles Bronson was an American actor best known for his \"tough guy\" image.  Bronson starred in films such as Once Upon a Time in the West, The Magnificent Seven, The Dirty Dozen, The Great Escape, Rider on the Rain, The Mechanic, and the popular Death Wish series.  He was most often cast in the role of a police officer or gunfighter, often in revenge-oriented plot lines...", died:date('2003-08-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8LoFmQmUzBaoGef8pY7M2urSCk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4960"}}, {tmdbId:"38037", properties:{imdbId:"0330961", born:date('1912-05-23'), name:"Marius Goring", died:date('1998-09-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wWHj4cTsu4NsZdMLfXC2fhqE28E.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/38037"}}, {tmdbId:"121765", properties:{bornIn:" Montclair, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0829359", born:date('1930-05-31'), name:"Elaine Stewart", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nElaine Stewart was an American actress and model. \n\nStewart was born in Montclair, New Jersey as Elsy Steinberg.  She was one of five children born into a German Jewish family.  In 1961, nearing the end of her television career, she married actor Bill Carter.  After her divorce from Carter, she married television producer Merrill Heatter on December 31, 1964.  They had a son, Stewart, and a daughter, Gabrielle...", died:date('2011-06-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zZLzOusC08v8dA4lcQGU4yJC3Im.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/121765"}}, {tmdbId:"12515", properties:{bornIn:"Santurce, Puerto Rico", imdbId:"0001207", born:date('1912-01-08'), name:"José Ferrer", bio:"José Ferrer (January 8, 1912 – January 26, 1992), was a Puerto Rican actor and director.  He was the first Hispanic actor to win an Academy Award...", died:date('1992-01-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/691OuTieryNIqLINzL5NOIB0bOe.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12515"}}, {tmdbId:"33162", properties:{bornIn:"Jamaica", imdbId:"0000896", born:date('1927-03-01'), name:"Harry Belafonte", bio:"Harold George \"Harry\" Belafonte, Jr.  (originally Belafonete; born March 1, 1927) is an American of Jamaican and Martiniquan descent who is a singer, actor, and social activist.  He was dubbed the \"King of Calypso\" for popularizing the  Belafonte has starred in several films.  His first film role was in Bright Road (1953), in which he appeared alongside Dorothy Dandridge.  The two subsequently starred in Otto Preminger's hit musical Carmen Jones (1954)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8x9zZS36gSOKiTnUwoBqYKvnYg6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33162"}}, {tmdbId:"20155", properties:{bornIn:"Cleveland, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0199268", born:date('1922-11-09'), name:"Dorothy Dandridge", bio:"Dorothy Jean Dandridge was an actress and popular singer who was the first African American to be nominated for an Academy Award for Best Actress...", died:date('1965-09-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vIARchY1pN5mfwTaTscBIF55vO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20155"}}, {tmdbId:"20157", properties:{bornIn:"Newport News, Virginia, USA", imdbId:"0047440", born:date('1918-03-29'), name:"Pearl Bailey", bio:"Pearl Mae Bailey, born in Virginia on March 29, 1918, was an American actress and singer.  Bailey began by singing and dancing in Philadelphia’s black nightclubs in the 1930s, and soon started performing in other parts of the East Coast.  In 1941, during World War II, Bailey toured the country with the USO, performing for American troops.  After the tour, she settled in New York...", died:date('1990-08-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lgTte8XNXsh9VNysSbvjdWJEfyC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20157"}}, {tmdbId:"1594318", properties:{born:date('1929-02-16'), name:"Olga James", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1594318"}}, {tmdbId:"24938", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0743218", born:date('1909-02-23'), name:"Anthony Ross", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nAnthony Ross (February 23, 1909 – October 26, 1955) was a Broadway stage, television and film actor. \n\nBorn in New York City, he may be best remembered for being the first to play the character of \"the Gentleman Caller\" in the original 1944 production of Tennessee Williams' The Glass Menagerie...", died:date('1955-10-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/e5SWJOZ0IxOAsoN9ociF4Haow0x.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24938"}}, {tmdbId:"31169", properties:{bornIn:"Waterloo, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0011105", born:date('1926-10-17'), name:"Julie Adams", bio:"Julie Adams (1926–2019) was an American film and television actress...", died:date('2019-02-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uIHWhDTSISwHXziBttr7V34MXTt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31169"}}, {tmdbId:"54681", properties:{bornIn:"Poughkeepsie, New York, USA", imdbId:"0219396", born:date('1914-03-27'), name:"Richard Denning", bio:"Richard Denning (March 27, 1914 – October 11, 1998) was an American actor who starred in such movies as Creature from the Black Lagoon (1954) and An Affair to Remember (1957), and on radio with Lucille Ball as her husband George Cooper in My Favorite Husband (1948–1951), the forerunner of television's I Love Lucy, for which Denning was replaced by Ball's real-life husband, Desi Arnaz...", died:date('1998-10-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bbM10C9KNZZqTmnfHuZc4NhbwfG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54681"}}, {tmdbId:"30555", properties:{bornIn:"Madrid, Spain", imdbId:"0603875", born:date('1887-09-25'), name:"Antonio Moreno", bio:"Antonio \"Tony\" Moreno (born Antonio Garrido Monteagudo; September 26, 1887 – February 15, 1967) was a Spanish-born American actor and film director of the silent film era and through the 1950s...", died:date('1987-02-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gLQwSmw9P6KwlrF9jWlc61ZfzzH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30555"}}, {tmdbId:"222281", properties:{bornIn:"Simla, Punjab, India", imdbId:"0419982", born:date('1906-05-05'), name:"Ursula Jeans", bio:"Ursula Jeans was an English film, stage, and television actress, married to the actor Roger Livesey, with whom she appeared in 'The Life and Death of Colonel Blimp'...", died:date('1973-04-21'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/222281"}}, {tmdbId:"27931", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0141202", born:date('1885-08-16'), name:"Charles Carson", died:date('1977-08-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qc6tbPVk6zV2OOk8fO2c6YjUl9s.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27931"}}, {tmdbId:"985253", properties:{imdbId:"0885676", born:date('1911-05-04'), name:"Stanley Van Beers", died:date('1961-05-25'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/985253"}}, {tmdbId:"12266", properties:{bornIn:"Wiesbaden, Germany", imdbId:"0797531", born:date('1921-03-25'), name:"Simone Signoret", bio:"Simone Signoret (25 March 1921 – 30 September 1985) was a French cinema actress often hailed as one of France's greatest movie stars.  She became the first French person to win an Academy Award, for her role in Room at the Top (1959).  In her lifetime she also received a BAFTA, an Emmy, Golden Globe, Cannes Film Festival recognition and the Silver Bear for Best Actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Simone Signoret, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1985-09-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vRI2Vt3HX911uDrVK170waQsL8b.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12266"}}, {tmdbId:"2569", properties:{bornIn:"Rio de Janeiro, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil", imdbId:"0167243", born:date('1913-12-30'), name:"Véra Clouzot", bio:"Véra Gibson-Amado, known professionally as Véra Clouzot, (30 December 1913 – 15 December 1960) was a Brazilian-French film actress and screenwriter.  She is known for playing Linda in The Wages of Fear (1953), Christina Delassalle in Les Diaboliques (1955), and Lucie in Les Espions (1957).  Clouzot also co-wrote the screenplay for La Vérité (1960).  Her husband, director Henri-Georges Clouzot, named his production company after her, Véra Films...", died:date('1960-12-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tTs65EJdF5fkmFImaGxHja5OEuK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2569"}}, {tmdbId:"12267", properties:{bornIn:"Dunkerque, Nord, Nord-Pas-de-Calais, France", imdbId:"0582890", born:date('1912-12-21'), name:"Paul Meurisse", bio:"Paul Meurisse (21 December 1912, Dunkirk – 19 January 1979, Neuilly-sur-Seine) was a French actor who appeared in over 60 films and many stage productions.  Meurisse was noted for the elegance of his acting style, and for his versatility.  He was equally able to play comedic and serious dramatic roles.  His screen appearances ranged from the droll and drily humorous to the menacing and disturbing...", died:date('1979-01-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/TE1Ex5mFq3bAizmxjZh7n8gBc1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12267"}}, {tmdbId:"5182", properties:{bornIn:"Chalfont, Buckinghamshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0002369", born:date('1903-04-15'), name:"John Williams", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJohn Williams (15 April 1903 – 5 May 1983) was an English stage, film and television actor.  He is remembered for his role as chief inspector Hubbard in Alfred Hitchcock's Dial M For Murder, and as portraying the second \"Mr.  French\" on TV's Family Affair. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article John Williams (actor), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1983-05-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nGEtPGnWl2XUE7mx9hU4wbTjIoG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5182"}}, {tmdbId:"41216", properties:{bornIn:"Bronx, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000742", born:date('1917-10-07'), name:"June Allyson", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJune Allyson (October 7, 1917 – July 8, 2006) was an American film and television actress, popular in the 1940s and 1950s.  She was a major MGM contract star.  Allyson won the Golden Globe Award for Best Actress for her performance in Too Young to Kiss (1951).  From 1959–1961, she hosted and occasionally starred in her own CBS anthology series, The DuPont Show with June Allyson.  A later generation knew her as a spokesperson for Depend undergarments...", died:date('2006-07-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tAaKPP6a7WDu4vKvawPUIAT2FSq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41216"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"10487", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0540416", born:date('1925-01-30'), name:"Dorothy Malone", bio:"Dorothy Malone (January 29, 1924 – January 19, 2018) was an American actress.  Her film career began in 1943, and, in her early years, she played small roles, mainly in B-movies.  After a decade, she began to acquire a more glamorous image, particularly after her role in Written on the Wind (1956), for which she won the Oscar for Best Supporting Actress...", died:date('2018-01-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/n0iPTGMJuIcLHEUt4J3MeCBEiIs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10487"}}, {tmdbId:"85765", properties:{imdbId:"0137601", name:"Bruce Carlisle", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85765"}}, {tmdbId:"4073", properties:{bornIn:"Detroit, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0604702", born:date('1915-04-10'), name:"Harry Morgan", bio:"Harry Morgan (born Harry Bratsberg) was an American stage, screen, radio, and television actor.  He is perhaps best remembered for his television serials roles as Detective Bill Gannon on Dragnet and as Colonel Sherman T.  Potter on M*A*S*H...", died:date('2011-12-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wOcBYXYJsvGziclaLTkv0TEXDxe.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4073"}}, {tmdbId:"18615", properties:{bornIn:"Harbin, China", imdbId:"0847361", born:date('1934-04-29'), name:"Akira Takarada", bio:"Akira Takarada (born April 29, 1934 -) is a Japanese film actor who is most known in the west for his roles in the Godzilla film series. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Akira Takarada, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bnL8ZbICuHSXrTJlLYf3EDa3zfW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18615"}}, {tmdbId:"33768", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0442708", born:date('1932-03-07'), name:"Momoko Kôchi", bio:"Played the role of Emiko Yamane in Inoshiro Honda's \"Gojira\" (1954) and she replayed Emiko in her last film Godzilla vs.  Destoroyah in 1995...", died:date('1998-11-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/x9mlnUigygwesUYgENgahQVIKYR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33768"}}, {tmdbId:"30568", properties:{bornIn:"Seoul, Korea", imdbId:"0386284", born:date('1927-12-26'), name:"Akihiko Hirata", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Akihiko Hirata (  Hirata Akihiko ) (26 December 1927–25 July 1984) was a Japanese film actor.  While Hirata starred in many movies (including Hiroshi Inagaki's Samurai trilogy), he is most well known for his work in the kaiju genre, including such films as King Kong vs.  Godzilla, The Mysterians, and his most famous role of Dr.  Daisuke Serizawa, the brilliant but disturbed young scientist in the original Godzilla, released in 1954...", died:date('1984-07-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2vV3HKUKPOTBLVwJUU3e8GetHPb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30568"}}, {tmdbId:"8238", properties:{bornIn:"Manchester, England, UK", imdbId:"0207219", born:date('1909-07-28'), name:"Brenda de Banzie", bio:"Brenda D.  M.  De Banzie was a British actress of stage and screen.  She was the daughter of Edward De Banzie and his second wife Dorothy, whom he married in 1908.  In 1911, the family lived in Salford.  She appeared as Maggie Hobson in the David Lean film version of Hobson's Choice (1954) with John Mills and Charles Laughton.  Her most notable film role was as Phoebe Rice, the hapless wife of comedian Archie Rice (played by Laurence Olivier), in the 1960 film version of The Entertainer...", died:date('1981-03-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7RZFusD9nmheZQ5klG2vPSbrAhs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8238"}}, {tmdbId:"985061", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0026563", born:date('1922-04-27'), name:"Daphne Anderson", died:date('2013-01-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vXPvnOAJR5qaAKkD9BuHQakopk0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/985061"}}, {tmdbId:"2382976", properties:{name:"Samson De Brier", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2382976"}}, {tmdbId:"121366", properties:{imdbId:"0131669", name:"Marjorie Cameron", bio:"Marjorie Cameron Parsons Kimmel (1922-1995) was an artist, occultist, actress, and wife of rocket pioneer and occultist Jack Parsons.  Cameron played a major role in the 1946 Babalon Working ritual...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/121366"}}, {tmdbId:"1660303", properties:{name:"Joan Whitney", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tNR4h0f3hiQ6wNAyHlHqtmhIoQo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1660303"}}, {tmdbId:"2382977", properties:{name:"Katy Kadell", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2382977"}}, {tmdbId:"18737", properties:{bornIn:"Joliet, Illinois, U.S.", imdbId:"0564790", born:date('1916-03-16'), name:"Mercedes McCambridge", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Carlotta Mercedes McCambridge (March 16, 1916 – March 2, 2004) was an American actress.  Orson Welles called her \"the world's greatest living radio actress\".   She won an Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress for ¨All the King's Men¨ (1949) and was nominated in the same category for ¨Giant¨ (1956).  She also provided the voice of the demon ¨Pazuzu¨ in ¨The Exorcist¨ (1973)...", died:date('2004-03-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vgJsNh4g6PMBekuJfEoazWySqWs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18737"}}, {tmdbId:"18735", properties:{bornIn:"Winnetka, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0001369", born:date('1925-11-17'), name:"Rock Hudson", bio:"Roy Harold Scherer, Jr. , later Roy Harold Fitzgerald (November 17, 1925 – October 2, 1985), known professionally as Rock Hudson, was an American film and television actor, recognized as a romantic leading man during the 1950s and 1960s, most notably in several romantic comedies with Doris Day.  Hudson was voted \"Star of the Year\", \"Favorite Leading Man\", and similar titles by numerous movie magazines.  The 6 ft 5 in (1...", died:date('1985-10-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/reiGa8Kj40Mg9A23Emg6tp9qkm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18735"}}, {tmdbId:"522", properties:{bornIn:"Westhampton, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001768", born:date('1925-04-14'), name:"Rod Steiger", bio:"Rodney Stephen \"Rod\" Steiger (April 14, 1925 – July 9, 2002) was an American actor known for his performances in such films as In the Heat of the Night, Oklahoma!, Waterloo, The Pawnbroker, On the Waterfront, The Harder They Fall, Doctor Zhivago, and Jesus of Nazareth. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Rod Steiger, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2002-07-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/AmAbDnxUTQPMeu8m9zbKksqUCDA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/522"}}, {tmdbId:"48958", properties:{bornIn:" Denver, Colorado, USA", imdbId:"0656428", born:date('1933-08-19'), name:"Debra Paget", bio:"Debra Paget (born August 19, 1933) is an American actress and entertainer who rose to prominence in the 1950s and early-1960s in a variety of feature films including The Ten Commandments and Love Me Tender...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2xsilT7513NOMjhsC6c6tzIEXek.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/48958"}}, {tmdbId:"50833", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0358899", born:date('1879-06-30'), name:"Walter Hampden", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.  Walter Hampden is the artist name of Walter Hampden Dougherty (June 30, 1879 in Brooklyn – June 11, 1955 in Los Angeles) was a U. S.  actor and theatre manager.  He was the younger brother of the American painter Paul Dougherty (1877-1947). \n\nHe went to England for apprenticeship for six years.  Later, he played Hamlet, Henry V and Cyrano de Bergerac on Broadway.  In 1925, he became manager of the Colonial Theatre on Broadway...", died:date('1955-06-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rvtUY8BibmiwNKZgkDWI81ZwOph.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/50833"}}, {tmdbId:"76975", properties:{bornIn:"Ota, Gunma Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0586733", born:date('1923-01-20'), name:"Rentarô Mikuni", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRentaro Mikuni (三國 連太郎, Mikuni Rentarō, born January 20, 1923) is a Japanese actor from Gunma Prefecture.  He has appeared in over 150 films since making his screen debut in 1951, and has won three Japanese Academy Awards for Best Actor, and a further seven nominations.  He also won two Blue Ribbon Awards for Best Actor, in 1960 and in 1989.  Kōichi Satō is his son...", died:date('2013-04-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/o4zQO6RDWTH9v7hQNuRsfYgsJKq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/76975"}}, {tmdbId:"108019", properties:{imdbId:"0648802", name:"Kurôemon Onoe", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/108019"}}, {tmdbId:"108020", properties:{bornIn:"Osaka Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0944779", born:date('1931-01-06'), name:"Kaoru Yachigusa", bio:"Actress...", died:date('2019-10-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lt9L9VGRCTim2RjydCVhOYFbDFi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/108020"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"122429", properties:{imdbId:"0359298", name:"Yoshiaki Hanayagi", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4rp6sCsmPhq9RtXkhmpGf0LdEI6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/122429"}}, {tmdbId:"34374", properties:{bornIn:"Ibaragi, Japan", imdbId:"0434593", born:date('1931-12-05'), name:"Kyôko Kagawa", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nKyōko Kagawa (香川 京子 Kagawa Kyōko, born 5 December 1931) is a Japanese actress.  She has appeared in leading and supporting roles in such films as Akira Kurosawa's The Bad Sleep Well and High and Low, Yasujiro Ozu's Tokyo Story, and Kenji Mizoguchi's Sansho the Bailiff...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/q47wPwySJvhj6HQoYb7ON1TjbcV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34374"}}, {tmdbId:"122430", properties:{bornIn:" Fukuoka, Fukuoka Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0793879", born:date('1899-11-10'), name:"Eitarô Shindô", bio:"Eitarō Shindō (1899–1977) was a Japanese film actor.  He appeared in 93 films between 1936 and 1966...", died:date('1977-02-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rlNUaEsrEwYs9bWq1Ej9aDBkFFI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/122430"}}, {tmdbId:"121766", properties:{imdbId:"0724143", born:date('1922-11-01'), name:"Jeff Richards", died:date('1989-07-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9K7QzmR441E0TkUmWmuyXdR5eUP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/121766"}}, {tmdbId:"6725", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0848560", born:date('1934-12-30'), name:"Russ Tamblyn", bio:"Russell Irving \"Russ\" Tamblyn (born December 30, 1934) is an American film and television actor, who is arguably best known for his performance in the 1961 movie musical West Side Story as Riff, the leader of the Jets gang. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Russ Tamblyn, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sks5yKFl1ETfvvXAgiwbHjL8p22.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6725"}}, {tmdbId:"138393", properties:{imdbId:"0707720", born:date('1929-12-27'), name:"Tommy Rall", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oDsa71LAaG06elk45rbq5NfZXz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/138393"}}, {tmdbId:"20831", properties:{bornIn:"Tsushima, Nagasaki Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0875477", born:date('1926-02-07'), name:"Keiko Tsushima", bio:"Keiko Tsushima (津島 恵子 Tsushima Keiko, 7 February 1926 – 1 August 2012) was a Japanese actress, whose real name was Naoko Mori (森 直子 Mori Naoko).  She was notable for her prominent role in Akira Kurosawa's 1954 film Seven Samurai.  She also starred in Japanese television series such as Sakura and Kimi ga Jinsei no Toki...", died:date('2012-08-01'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20831"}}, {tmdbId:"554250", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0793616", born:date('1931-02-25'), name:"Yukiko Shimazaki", bio:"Yukiko Shimazaki (島崎 雪子 Shimazaki Yukiko, born 25 February 1931) is a Japanese actress and singer.  She appeared in more than twenty films from 1950 to 1964.  She was married to film director Tatsumi Kumashiro from 1955 to 1967...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/554250"}}, {tmdbId:"5404", properties:{bornIn:"Turin, Italy", imdbId:"0798570", born:date('1891-01-21'), name:"Aldo Silvani", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAldo Silvani (21 January 1891 – 12 November 1964) was an Italian film actor.  He appeared in 112 films between 1934 and 1964. \n\nHe was born in Turin, Italy and died in Milan, Italy. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Aldo Silvani, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1964-11-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8nrYSS8C5sYMhSmzSvRZR7tmiGo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5404"}}, {tmdbId:"18582", properties:{bornIn:"Dallas, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0309607", born:date('1926-02-01'), name:"Nancy Gates", bio:"Nancy Gates (February 1, 1926 - March 24, 2019) was an American film and television actress...", died:date('2019-03-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/r9PfeRZrAPaeVxfmkdScMWXhISA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18582"}}, {tmdbId:"68088", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, U.S.", imdbId:"0919730", born:date('1933-08-05'), name:"Joan Weldon", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nJoan Weldon (born as Joan Louise Welton on August 5, 1933, San Francisco, California) is an American film and television actress.  She began her career singing in the San Francisco Grand Opera Company chorus.  Later she became a contract actress with Warner Bros.  where she remained until her contract ended in 1954...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dHxBnorCYeBhANJieUlqE9Pgq4W.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/68088"}}, {tmdbId:"50304", properties:{bornIn:"Minneapolis, Minnesota, U.S.", imdbId:"0000790", born:date('1923-05-26'), name:"James Arness", bio:"The star of one of the longest-running shows in U. S.  television history, Gunsmoke  (1955).  Born of Norwegian heritage (the family name, Aurness (formerly  had been Aursness) in Minneapolis, Minnesota to Rolf and Ruth  Duesler Aurness.  His father was a traveling salesman of medical supplies  and his mother later became a newspaper columnist.  James attended West  High School in Minneapolis...", died:date('2011-06-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hLz1Lo6sfoLfFVlwnOSKMS2c1gY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/50304"}}, {tmdbId:"109897", properties:{bornIn:"Astoria, New York, USA", imdbId:"0581062", born:date('1908-01-16'), name:"Ethel Merman", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEthel Merman (January 16, 1908 – February 15, 1984) was an American actress and singer.  Known primarily for her powerful voice and roles in musical theatre, she has been called \"the undisputed First Lady of the musical comedy stage...", died:date('1984-02-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/j5dX6SrfJkuxu3P7PT35SnTcXqt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/109897"}}, {tmdbId:"82129", properties:{bornIn:"New York, New York, USA", imdbId:"0197314", born:date('1913-12-14'), name:"Dan Dailey", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDaniel James Dailey Jr.  (December 14, 1915 – October 16, 1978) was an American dancer and actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Dan Dailey, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1978-10-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fzjpdb2Y1M2J69uFzt1mv7r77gZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82129"}}, {tmdbId:"12351", properties:{imdbId:"0607504", born:date('1907-01-13'), name:"Jeff Morrow", bio:"New York-born Morrow developed an interest in the theater as a result of his studies at art school.  As \"Irving Morrow,\" he was acting on stage (in Pennsylvania) as early as 1927; he later appeared in such plays as \"Penal Law\", \"Once in a Lifetime\", \"A Midsummer Night's Dream\", \"Twelfth Night\", \"Romeo and Juliet\" and \"Macbeth\", treading the boards opposite stars like Katharine Cornell, Maurice Evans, Katharine Hepburn, Luise Rainer and Mae West...", died:date('1993-12-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rAW1Fsn3UOzZ6ZR8Ka5rSxeDIVZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12351"}}, {tmdbId:"85740", properties:{bornIn:"New Orleans, Louisiana, USA", imdbId:"0231409", born:date('1924-06-16'), name:"Faith Domergue", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nFaith Domergue (June 16, 1924 – April 4, 1999) was an American television and film actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Faith Domergue, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1999-04-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yJa5BnRfcMWZnrYExKewsIFNAPQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85740"}}, {tmdbId:"12353", properties:{imdbId:"0714155", born:date('1928-11-30'), name:"Rex Reason", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8RM8vG5ZUQ2yL6SreFCeB94vn3Q.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12353"}}, {tmdbId:"12354", properties:{bornIn:"Somerset, Kentucky, USA", imdbId:"0298282", born:date('1928-12-06'), name:"Lance Fuller", bio:"Lance Fuller (December 6, 1928 – December 22, 2001) was an American actor.  He was born in Somerset, Kentucky. \n\nHe was a contract actor for most of the 1950s with Universal-International. \n\nHe had many uncredited roles for the first several years of his Hollywood career.  His first role was in Frankenstein Meets the Wolf Man (1943), and he was featured (uncredited) in several movies into the 1950s, including Singin' in the Rain (1952)...", died:date('2001-12-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mwVv57nP36YgbMFTEAcqOWPDidj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12354"}}, {tmdbId:"77674", properties:{bornIn:"Maysville, Kentucky, USA", imdbId:"0167041", born:date('1928-05-23'), name:"Rosemary Clooney", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRosemary Clooney (May 23, 1928 – June 29, 2002) was an American singer and actress.  She came to prominence in the early 1950s with the song \"Come On-a My House\", which was followed by other pop numbers such as \"Botch-a-Me\", \"Mambo Italiano\", \"Tenderly\", \"Half as Much\", \"Hey There\" and \"This Ole House\".  She also had success as a jazz vocalist.  Clooney continued recording until her death in 2002...", died:date('2002-06-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9JlTu4OEBmDotx5MaMV7rSLyjW3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77674"}}, {tmdbId:"77675", properties:{bornIn:"Norwood, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0893584", born:date('1921-02-16'), name:"Vera-Ellen", bio:"Vera-Ellen began dancing at the age of 10, and a few years later became  one of the youngest Rockettes.  She appeared in several Broadway musicals  until she was spotted by film producer Samuel Goldwyn in 1945.  She was only 24 years old when Goldwyn cast her opposite Danny Kaye in Wonder Man (1945).  She danced with Fred Astaire in Three Little Words (1950) and with Gene Kelly in On the Town  (1949)...", died:date('1981-08-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kMpfnWzEnVmkrFUVumIOPjzYSmQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77675"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"51678", properties:{bornIn:"Washington, D.C., USA", imdbId:"0614500", born:date('1931-01-26'), name:"Mary Murphy", bio:"Mary Murphy (January 26, 1931 – May 4, 2011) was an American film actress of the 1950s, 1960s and 1970s.  She was born in Washington, D. C. , before moving to Los Angeles.  Shortly out of high school she was signed to appear in films for Paramount Pictures in the late 1940s. \n\nMurphy first gained attention in 1953, when she played a good-hearted girl who tries to reform Marlon Brando in The Wild One...", died:date('2011-05-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2xDJlqwO0W0n6kUDyHWzwAyIJ4a.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/51678"}}, {tmdbId:"46711", properties:{bornIn:"Fowler, Indiana, USA", imdbId:"0445290", born:date('1898-02-10'), name:"Robert Keith", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRobert Keith (February 10, 1898 – December 22, 1966) was an American stage and film actor who appeared in several dozen films, mostly in the 1950s as a character actor. \n\nHe is noted for his performance as the weak-willed father in Fourteen Hours (1951), as a tough cop in Guys and Dolls (1955), and his performance in the 1953 film The Wild One, starring Marlon Brando, in which he played the ineffectual sheriff and father of Brando's love interest...", died:date('1966-12-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2E4Ujpec5xMHetkfjErfuBvzJfO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/46711"}}, {tmdbId:"18391", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001511", born:date('1924-02-19'), name:"Lee Marvin", bio:"Was an American film actor.  Known for his gravelly voice, white hair and 6' 2\" stature, Marvin at first did supporting roles, mostly villains, soldiers and other hardboiled characters, but after winning an Academy Award for Best Actor for his dual roles in Cat Ballou (1965), he landed more heroic and sympathetic leading roles...", died:date('1987-08-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pTIekoTYUcWUUGr52kY7YZdie40.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18391"}}, {tmdbId:"16074", properties:{bornIn:"Syria", imdbId:"0030516", born:date('1922-04-15'), name:"Michael Ansara", bio:"Michael Ansara was a stage, screen and voice actor, best known for his portrayal of Cochise in the American television series Broken Arrow, Kane in the 1979–81 series Buck Rogers in the 25th Century, and as Commander Kang on three different Star Trek TV series...", died:date('2013-07-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pNhnbt9rGypREvKdeE9xqBcdB8u.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16074"}}, {tmdbId:"4090", properties:{bornIn:"Richmond, Virginia, USA", imdbId:"0000511", born:date('1934-04-24'), name:"Shirley MacLaine", bio:"Shirley MacLaine (born April 24, 1934) is an American film and theater actress, dancer, activist, and author, well-known for her beliefs in new age spirituality and reincarnation.  She has written a large number of autobiographical works, many dealing with her spiritual beliefs as well as her Hollywood career.  In 1983, she won the Academy Award for Best Actress for her role in Terms of Endearment.  She is the elder sister of actor Warren Beatty...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mpW9c34IAFPW0ODuKR8J0FAqN5i.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4090"}}, {tmdbId:"12309", properties:{bornIn:"Ossining, New York, USA", imdbId:"0004282", born:date('1930-09-16'), name:"Anne Francis", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAnne Lloyd Francis (September 16, 1930 – January 2, 2011) was an American actress, best known for her role in the science fiction film classic Forbidden Planet (1956), and as the female private detective in the television series Honey West (1965–1966).  She won a Golden Globe and was nominated for an Emmy award for her role in Honey West.  Francis holds the distinction of starring in the first TV series with a female detective character's name in the title...", died:date('2011-01-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hcckb43OvvQbrdqOotqWcvLPXbg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12309"}}, {tmdbId:"29313", properties:{bornIn:"Columbus Grove, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0415591", born:date('1903-11-07'), name:"Dean Jagger", bio:"Dean Jagger was an Academy Award-winning American screen, stage, and television actor...", died:date('1991-02-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8oowBYfGK3E0EntkS7KaCRSKNmZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29313"}}, {tmdbId:"20144", properties:{bornIn:"Baltimore, Maryland, USA", imdbId:"0293530", born:date('1926-06-10'), name:"Mona Freeman", bio:"Monica Elizabeth \"Mona\" Freeman (June 9, 1926 – May 23, 2014) was an American actress and painter.  A professional model while still in high school, Mona Freeman was signed to a movie contract by Howard Hughes, who then proceeded to sell her contract to Paramount.  Starting out in typical juvenile parts, she developed into a very competent actress...", died:date('2014-05-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dOoeaOfH7eLureq4LtL5WmqYjc0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20144"}}, {tmdbId:"45001", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0006752", born:date('1921-12-26'), name:"Steve Allen", bio:"Stephen Valentine Patrick William Allen was an American television personality, radio personality, musician, composer, actor, comedian, writer, and advocate of scientific skepticism.  In 1954, he achieved national fame as the co-creator and first host of The Tonight Show, which was the first late night television talk show. \n\nThough he got his start in radio, Allen is best known for his extensive network television career...", died:date('2000-10-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/smfesYmaX6pfZefpYU6L69ePwiG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/45001"}}, {tmdbId:"589537", properties:{imdbId:"0314929", name:"Berta Gersten", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/589537"}}, {tmdbId:"179367", properties:{imdbId:"0874137", name:"Barry Truex", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/179367"}}, {tmdbId:"88617", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0908695", born:date('1923-10-12'), name:"Jean Wallace", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nBorn Jean Walasek in Chicago to John T.  Walasek and Mary A.  Walasek (née Sharkey), Wallace began her career as a model then got her first small movie role at the age of seventeen.  She was married two times; once to her Jigsaw co-star Franchot Tone from 1941 to 1948 and once to actor Cornel Wilde (her co-star in The Big Combo and Lancelot and Guinevere) from 1951 to 1981.  She had two sons with Tone and one with Wilde...", died:date('1990-02-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/VKKLhz5K1tX6rBclvXzAFP2h3e.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88617"}}, {tmdbId:"81283", properties:{imdbId:"0371135", born:date('1916-12-05'), name:"Margaret Hayes", died:date('1977-01-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4gbSORZpipZrJZTFPw6hfPWqeBJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81283"}}, {tmdbId:"55778", properties:{imdbId:"0179783", born:date('1939-05-29'), name:"Isabelle Corey", died:date('2011-02-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iNKN0jLoBLrs0Pixb5ZxcNc5pLV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55778"}}, {tmdbId:"39093", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0146446", born:date('1930-03-13'), name:"Daniel Cauchy", died:date('2020-05-07'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/39093"}}, {tmdbId:"94603", properties:{bornIn:"Luxeuil-les-Bains, Haute-Saône, France", imdbId:"0239841", born:date('1906-07-26'), name:"Roger Duchesne", died:date('1996-12-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4PHh25N0YDIX3ixxH5QVeBtPDmn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94603"}}, {tmdbId:"1656", properties:{imdbId:"0213948", name:"Guy Decomble", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1656"}}, {tmdbId:"100796", properties:{imdbId:"0426363", born:date('1903-10-19'), name:"Tor Johnson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.  \n\n \n\nTor Johnson (19 October 1903 – 12 May 1971) was a Swedish professional wrestler (billed as The Super Swedish Angel) and actor.  He is perhaps best remembered for his roles in a number of B-movies, including police inspector turned zombie Daniel Clay in Plan 9 from Outer Space and playing the role of a recurring lab assistant often named \"Lobo\"...", died:date('1971-05-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zRpcpchynj9UjnwlKlCs0hf6rvm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100796"}}, {tmdbId:"1313952", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles - California - USA", imdbId:"0566815", born:date('1924-07-05'), name:"Tony McCoy", died:date('2000-08-02'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1313952"}}, {tmdbId:"115446", properties:{imdbId:"0455010", name:"Loretta King", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/115446"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"50571", properties:{bornIn:"Fort Worth, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0662240", born:date('1924-08-16'), name:"Fess Parker", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nFess Elisha Parker, Jr.  (August 16, 1924 – March 18, 2010) was an American film and television actor best known for his portrayals of Davy Crockett in the Walt Disney 1954–1955 TV miniseries, which aired on ABC, and as Daniel Boone in an NBC television series from 1964 to 1970.  He was also known as a winemaker and resort owner-operator...", died:date('2010-03-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/opFddnb0NRzG3gbZ3HyctQ3Jh34.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/50571"}}, {tmdbId:"100919", properties:{bornIn:"Jersey City, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0752278", born:date('1888-07-24'), name:"Basil Ruysdael", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nBasil Ruysdael (July 24, 1888 - October 10, 1960) was an American film actor and opera singer. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Basil Ruysdael, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia. \n\nHe started his career as a baritone singer for the Metropolitan Opera Company in the early 1900's and appeared on the New York stage in 1918.  Moving to California in 1923, he was a voice teacher for many actors...", died:date('1960-10-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tP97JMEoRqPkVaw2izTSNBwpwho.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100919"}}, {tmdbId:"14242", properties:{bornIn:"Antwerp, Belgium", imdbId:"0785771", born:date('1910-09-24'), name:"Jean Servais", bio:"Jean Servais was a Belgian actor best known for the French heist movie 'Rififi' and Luis Bunuel's 'Fever Mounts at El Pao'...", died:date('1976-02-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9mkdvvPhJfjeZM0hnZYxMxiPacz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14242"}}, {tmdbId:"11937", properties:{bornIn:" Vienna, Austria", imdbId:"0617846", born:date('1921-08-11'), name:"Carl Möhner", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nCarl Martin Rudolf Möhner was an Austrian film actor.  He appeared in more than 40 films between 1949 and 1976.  He was born in Vienna, Austria, and died in McAllen, Texas from Parkinson's disease.  His most famous role was as Ernst Lindemann, Captain of the Bismarck in the 1960 film Sink the Bismarck! opposite Kenneth More...", died:date('2005-01-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rs3V2EYLQMdiF43Z3h5ZBS634Tn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11937"}}, {tmdbId:"14243", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0544275", born:date('1916-09-07'), name:"Robert Manuel", died:date('1995-12-09'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14243"}}, {tmdbId:"14244", properties:{bornIn:"Asnières-sur-Seine, France", imdbId:"0201009", born:date('1917-01-14'), name:"Janine Darcey", died:date('1993-10-01'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14244"}}, {tmdbId:"2749", properties:{bornIn:"Marion, Indiana, USA", imdbId:"0000015", born:date('1931-02-08'), name:"James Dean", bio:"James Byron Dean (February 8, 1931 – September 30, 1955) was an American actor.  He is remembered as a cultural icon of teenage disillusionment and social estrangement, as expressed in the title of his most celebrated film, Rebel Without a Cause (1955), in which he starred as troubled teenager Jim Stark.  The other two roles that defined his stardom were loner Cal Trask in East of Eden (1955) and surly ranch hand Jett Rink in Giant (1956)...", died:date('1955-09-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5oaDvEoQssXlDt1KSQVl0M4rgBn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2749"}}, {tmdbId:"83488", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0130794", born:date('1925-04-30'), name:"Corinne Calvet", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nCorinne Calvet (April 30, 1925 – June 23, 2001), born Corinne Dibos, was a French actress who appeared mostly in American films. \n\nCalvet made her debut in French radio, stage plays and cinema in the 1940s before being brought to Hollywood in the 1940s by producer Hal B.  Wallis.  He cast her in Rope of Sand (1949) opposite Burt Lancaster and Paul Henreid...", died:date('2001-06-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2yhat5QruvDXXZ1Ns01Lx1jO4bM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83488"}}, {tmdbId:"50570", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0001996", born:date('1918-12-15'), name:"Jeff Chandler", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJeff Chandler (born Ira Grossel; December 15, 1918 – June 17, 1961) was an American actor, film producer and singer best remembered for playing Cochise in Broken Arrow (1950), for which he was Oscar nominated.  He was one of Universal Pictures's most popular male stars of the 1950s, his best known other credits including Sword in the Desert (1948), Deported (1950), Female on the Beach (1955) and Away All Boats (1956)...", died:date('1961-06-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7jpocARKbxHRYZq1yfDhDnhpB3f.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/50570"}}, {tmdbId:"113585", properties:{imdbId:"0287769", born:date('1928-10-31'), name:"Dianne Foster", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4Lfqn52YXxBma4NyJjijty8NtUj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/113585"}}, {tmdbId:"115990", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0528658", born:date('1926-10-07'), name:"Diana Lynn", bio:"She was a child prodigy, pianist, at age 10, and her first movie role  was one of the children in, \"They Shall Have Music\" (1939).  You see her  playing the piano.  She made another movie using her 'real name' - Dolly  in, \"There's Magic in Music\" (1941).  She signed a long term contract  with Paramount in 1942, and had her named changed to Diana Lynn.  She had  good roles in, \"The Major, and the Minor\" (1942); \"The Miracle of  Morgan's Creek\", and, \"Our Hearts Were Young, and Gay\" - both in 1944...", died:date('1971-12-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fSjZ1D8wMdAbu8HcUWOOCL11Di3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/115990"}}, {tmdbId:"19217", properties:{bornIn:"Kingston, British West Indies [now Kingston, Jamaica]", imdbId:"0798826", born:date('1914-07-24'), name:"Frank Silvera", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nFrank Silvera (July 24, 1914 – June 11, 1970) was an American actor and theatrical director. \n\nSilvera was born in Kingston, Jamaica the son of a mixed race Jamaican mother, Gertrude Bell and Spanish Jewish father, Alfred Silvera.  His family emigrated to the United States when he was six-years old, settling in Boston.  Silvera became interested in acting and began performing in amateur theatrical groups and at church...", died:date('1970-06-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zdZrLaqChrDscljRGCOnN372uom.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19217"}}, {tmdbId:"62601", properties:{imdbId:"0808600", name:"Jamie Smith", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/62601"}}, {tmdbId:"62602", properties:{imdbId:"0437325", name:"Irene Kane", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/62602"}}, {tmdbId:"276364", properties:{imdbId:"0418911", name:"Jerry Jarrett", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/276364"}}, {tmdbId:"31844", properties:{bornIn:"Mount Kisco, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001955", born:date('1928-08-16'), name:"Ann Blyth", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAnn Marie Blyth (born August 16, 1928) is an American actress and singer, often cast in Hollywood musicals, but also successful in dramatic roles.  Her performance as Veda Pierce in the 1945 film Mildred Pierce was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Ann Blyth, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/53EOEssiuPBAqv9475t6QvvRxEX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31844"}}, {tmdbId:"39602", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0336576", born:date('1924-06-07'), name:"Dolores Gray", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDolores Gray (June 7, 1924 – June 26, 2002) was an American stage and film actress.  During her successful music career, she sang Marilyn Monroe's part on the Decca records soundtrack album of There's No Business Like Show Business (1954). \n\nBorn as Dolores Stein to Barbara Gray and Henry Stein in Chicago, Dolores Gray was briefly signed with MGM, appearing in Kismet (1955) and It's Always Fair Weather(1955)...", died:date('2002-06-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7y7GQ1xB4I0imsQWXnuEDDpqhdA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/39602"}}, {tmdbId:"39603", properties:{imdbId:"0198954", born:date('1928-06-12'), name:"Vic Damone", bio:"Vic Damone (born Vito Rocco Farinola in New York, June 12, 1928) is an American singer and entertainer.  His father was an electrician; and his mother taught piano.  His cousin was the actress and singer Doretta Morrow.  Inspired by his favorite singer, Frank Sinatra, Damone began taking voice lessons.   \n\n  By mid 1947, Damone had signed a contract with Mercury Records.  His first release, \"I Have But One Heart\", reached #7 on the Billboard chart.  \"You Do\" reached the same peak...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qutr19WqOvAR18NLxFycQlxCHoH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/39603"}}, {tmdbId:"14562", properties:{bornIn:"Minneapolis, Minnesota, United States", imdbId:"0576127", born:date('1920-11-21'), name:"Ralph Meeker", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRalph Meeker (born Ralph Rathgeber; November 21, 1920 – August 5, 1988) was an American film, stage, and television actor.  He first rose to prominence for his roles in the Broadway productions of Mister Roberts (1948–1951) and Picnic (1953), the former of which earned him a Theatre World Award for his performance.  In film, Meeker is perhaps best known for his portrayal of Mike Hammer in Robert Aldrich's 1955 film noir cult classic Kiss Me Deadly...", died:date('1988-08-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kw49AcV9vDgTZY2ts6qrPHSTS76.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14562"}}, {tmdbId:"11033", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0829717", born:date('1908-03-13'), name:"Paul Stewart", bio:"Paul Stewart (March 13, 1908 – February 17, 1986) was an American character actor known for his tough, guttural voice.  He frequently portrayed villains and mobsters throughout his lengthy career. \n\nBorn Paul Sternberg in New York City, Stewart graduated from Columbia University and made his Broadway theatre debut in the play Two Seconds in 1931...", died:date('1986-02-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2sYUlDzOJcjE6W3S80hYpkwcAzN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11033"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"82613", properties:{bornIn:"San Juan, Puerto Rico", imdbId:"0379621", born:date('1896-07-19'), name:"Juano Hernandez", bio:"An Afro-Puerto Rican stage and film actor who was a pioneer in the African American film industry...", died:date('1970-07-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ylo9FMmXNff7lnUezh8bEPKhNR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82613"}}, {tmdbId:"64870", properties:{bornIn:"Jamestown, New York, USA", imdbId:"0498007", born:date('1920-05-26'), name:"Peggy Lee", bio:"Peggy Lee was an American jazz and popular music singer, songwriter, composer and actress, in a career spanning six decades.  From her beginning as a vocalist on local radio to singing with Benny Goodman's big band, she forged a sophisticated persona, evolving into a multi-faceted artist and performer.  She wrote music for films, acted, and created conceptual record albums—encompassing poetry, jazz, chamber pop, and art songs...", died:date('2002-01-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/n2VgRpO6cV7jDpMWX1dqUBwMeU1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/64870"}}, {tmdbId:"64872", properties:{bornIn:"Cleveland, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0731333", born:date('1926-09-28'), name:"Larry Roberts", died:date('1992-07-17'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/64872"}}, {tmdbId:"1022053", properties:{imdbId:"0061649", born:date('1910-05-05'), name:"Bill Baucom", died:date('1981-03-16'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1022053"}}, {tmdbId:"14503", properties:{bornIn:"Prague, Bohemia, Austria-Hungary", imdbId:"0007042", born:date('1917-09-12'), name:"Herbert Lom", bio:"Herbert Lom (born Herbert Charles Angelo Kuchačevič ze Schluderpacheru; 11 September 1917 – 27 September 2012) was a Czech-born British film and television actor who moved to the United Kingdom in 1939.  In a career lasting more than 60 years, he appeared in character roles, often portraying criminals or villains early in his career and professional men in later years. \n\nLom was noted for his precise, elegant enunciation of English...", died:date('2012-09-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1sqfpn8EzsCgQdwmB8NP4bLWYlP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14503"}}, {tmdbId:"29523", properties:{bornIn:"Saint-Mandé, Val-de-Marne, Île-de-France, France", imdbId:"0138987", born:date('1920-05-16'), name:"Martine Carol", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nMartine Carol (16 May 1920 – 6 February 1967) was a French film actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Martine Carol, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1967-02-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jOqTFRobNv1fQshZmeAhZaHJsec.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29523"}}, {tmdbId:"14501", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0001811", born:date('1921-04-16'), name:"Peter Ustinov", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia  \n\n  Sir Peter Alexander Ustinov CBE ( 16 April 1921 – 28 March 2004) was an English actor, writer and dramatist.  He was also renowned as a filmmaker, theatre and opera director, stage designer, author, screenwriter, comedian, humourist, newspaper and magazine columnist, radio broadcaster and television presenter.  A noted wit and raconteur, he was a fixture on television talk shows and lecture circuits for much of his career...", died:date('2004-03-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jpn50AKpGvvDjLRO56OWYCt6AEK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14501"}}, {tmdbId:"28609", properties:{bornIn:"Aix-en-Provence, France", imdbId:"0347541", born:date('1904-10-12'), name:"Henri Guisol", died:date('1994-05-11'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/28609"}}, {tmdbId:"95263", properties:{bornIn:"Cambridge, Cambridgeshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0255695", born:date('1893-03-16'), name:"Isobel Elsom", bio:"Isobel Elsom (March 16, 1893 — January 12, 1981) was an English screen, stage, and television actress...", died:date('1981-01-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qJR2LoiQziyso5Ezzqnt4Oe3gjE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95263"}}, {tmdbId:"5729", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0001571", born:date('1933-02-13'), name:"Kim Novak", bio:"Marilyn Pauline Novak (born February 13, 1933), known professionally as Kim Novak, is an American retired film and television actress. \n\nShe began her career in 1954 after signing with Columbia Pictures.  There, she became a successful actress, starring in a string of movies, among them the critically acclaimed Picnic (1955).  She later starred in such popular successes as The Man with the Golden Arm (1955) and Pal Joey (1957)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xvIOwqOD1BXkpFZEwzkb6aamaEL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5729"}}, {tmdbId:"7332", properties:{bornIn:"Manhattan, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0822205", born:date('1918-09-28'), name:"Arnold Stang", bio:"Arnold Stang (September 28, 1918 – December 20, 2009) was an American comic actor who played a small and bespectacled, yet brash and knowing big-city type...", died:date('2009-12-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/d6JMdwwrMZeVy2uV8ZMZIfbK6tS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7332"}}, {tmdbId:"78935", properties:{bornIn:"Italy", imdbId:"0591034", born:date('1888-03-18'), name:"Esther Minciotti", died:date('1962-04-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/liqG65mQVONkL7m3q787GRtUQ9X.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78935"}}, {tmdbId:"78936", properties:{imdbId:"0162557", born:date('1901-05-19'), name:"Augusta Ciolli", died:date('1967-02-03'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78936"}}, {tmdbId:"78937", properties:{imdbId:"0544064", born:date('1915-12-21'), name:"Joe Mantell", died:date('2010-09-29'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78937"}}, {tmdbId:"15644", properties:{imdbId:"0824606", born:date('1931-03-20'), name:"Karen Steele", died:date('1988-03-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hk2CsuEUpr8JSOufjvdbrHNfOSi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15644"}}, {tmdbId:"3151", properties:{bornIn:"Newton, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0000493", born:date('1925-02-08'), name:"Jack Lemmon", bio:"John Uhler \"Jack\" Lemmon III (February 8, 1925 – June 27, 2001) was an American actor and musician...", died:date('2001-06-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4yowflZgO62PGTPADoFzkYSrZv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3151"}}, {tmdbId:"11989", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0099677", born:date('1925-11-06'), name:"Michel Bouquet", bio:"Michel Bouquet (born 6 November 1925) is a French film actor.  He has appeared in over 90 films since 1947.  He was born in Paris, France...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eXqvrJ3Q6YQfBvjsLEQhDXw45HJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11989"}}, {tmdbId:"11990", properties:{bornIn:"Halle an der Saale, Germany", imdbId:"0382193", born:date('1904-03-07'), name:"Reinhard Heydrich", bio:"Reinhard Tristan Eugen Heydrich (7 March 1904 – 4 June 1942), also known as The Hangman was a high-ranking German Nazi official.  He was SS-Obergruppenführer (English: General) and General der Polizei, chief of the Reich Main Security Office (including the SD, Gestapo and Kripo) and Stellvertretender Reichsprotektor (Deputy Reich-Protector) of Bohemia and Moravia.  In August 1940, he was appointed and served as President of Interpol (the international law enforcement agency)...", died:date('1942-06-04'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11990"}}, {tmdbId:"11991", properties:{bornIn:"München, Germany", imdbId:"0385441", born:date('1900-10-07'), name:"Heinrich Himmler", bio:"Heinrich Luitpold Himmler ( 7 October 1900 – 23 May 1945) was Reichsführer of the SS, a military commander, and a leading member of the Nazi Party.  As Chief of the German Police and later the Minister of the Interior, Himmler oversaw all internal and external police and security forces, including the Gestapo (Secret State Police)...", died:date('1945-05-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/Aljparz5AOPTPrgVFDFahutWBak.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11991"}}, {tmdbId:"129521", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0339307", born:date('1890-06-25'), name:"Charlotte Greenwood", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nFrances Charlotte Greenwood (25 June 1890 - 28 December 1977) was an American actress and dancer.  Born in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, Greenwood started in vaudeville, and eventually starred on Broadway, movies and radio.  Standing around six feet tall, she was best known for her long legs and high kicks.  She earned the unique praise of being, in her words, the \". . . only woman in the world who could kick a giraffe in the eye...", died:date('1977-12-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/adgq5Q3VR4W6dan8RV3etTni37l.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/129521"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"142924", properties:{imdbId:"0012994", name:"Hanne Agesen", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/142924"}}, {tmdbId:"142925", properties:{imdbId:"0248681", name:"Sylvia Eckhausen", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/142925"}}, {tmdbId:"47155", properties:{bornIn:"Copenhagen, Denmark", imdbId:"0270147", born:date('1925-09-06'), name:"Birgitte Federspiel", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBirgitte Federspiel (6 September 1925 – 2 February 2005) was a Danish film, theater and TV actress.  She won two Bodil Awards for best actress in 1955 (Ordet) and 1959 (En fremmed banker på). \n\nBorn Karen Birgitte Federspiel in Copenhagen, she was the daughter of actor Ejner Federspiel and Gunver Fönss...", died:date('2005-02-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/w6MrtziJkhdIXYubAsu8Z7PNNnm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/47155"}}, {tmdbId:"13762", properties:{bornIn:"Jodhpur, Rajasthan, India", imdbId:"0052333", born:date('1905-06-20'), name:"Kanu Bannerjee", died:date('1983-01-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4Si1KHQMsgIlmRtxoMualY6Iazv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13762"}}, {tmdbId:"45593", properties:{imdbId:"0222447", name:"Chunibala Devi", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8IOUdR2D9Elw7JH2eqaqokdlzvT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/45593"}}, {tmdbId:"45591", properties:{imdbId:"0201871", name:"Uma Das Gupta", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nanvcNhfI5bGEJTASI0RfaugLOr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/45591"}}, {tmdbId:"30043", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York", imdbId:"0001782", born:date('1938-05-22'), name:"Susan Strasberg", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSusan Elizabeth Strasberg (May 22, 1938 – January 21, 1999) was an American actress and daughter of Lee and Paula Strasberg of the Actors Studio. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Susan Strasberg, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1999-01-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/e3vIJilx5ouDgvPV39fwhkQVARW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30043"}}, {tmdbId:"2769", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0000081", born:date('1938-07-20'), name:"Natalie Wood", bio:"Natalie Wood (born Natalia Nikolaevna Zakharenko; July 20, 1938 – November 29, 1981) was an American actress. \n\nWood began acting in movies at the age of four and became a successful child actor in such films as Miracle on 34th Street (1947).  A well received performance opposite James Dean in Rebel Without a Cause (1955) earned her a nomination for the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress and helped her to make the transition from a child performer...", died:date('1981-11-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tmYB8aXfb5fe2K1wquhRLfMGViu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2769"}}, {tmdbId:"2770", properties:{bornIn:"The Bronx, New York, United States", imdbId:"0000543", born:date('1939-01-10'), name:"Sal Mineo", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSalvatore Mineo, Jr.  (January 10, 1939 – February 12, 1976), better known as Sal Mineo, was an American film and theatre actor, best known for his performance opposite James Dean in the film Rebel Without a Cause. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Sal Mineo, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1976-02-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/glfs6BXlFIMprrJSuiT74VzJIOJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2770"}}, {tmdbId:"2771", properties:{bornIn:"Cleveland, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0000822", born:date('1913-02-25'), name:"Jim Backus", bio:"Jim Backus (1913–1989) was a radio, television, film, and voice actor. \n\nAmong his most famous credits are The Alan Young Radio Show, I Married Joan, Gilligan's Island, and Rebel Without a Cause.  He also starred on his own show The Jim Backus Show...", died:date('1989-07-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pTubdwxikemaqIVmrjSEe3bdnzi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2771"}}, {tmdbId:"117617", properties:{bornIn:"Cagliari, Sardinia, Italy", imdbId:"0667542", born:date('1932-06-19'), name:"Marisa Pavan", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nMarisa Pavan (born Maria Luisa Pierangeli on 19 June 1932) is an Italian-born actress who first became famous as the twin sister to movie star Pier Angeli (Anna Maria Pierangeli) before achieving movie stardom on her own.  Her breakthrough came in the film The Rose Tattoo as Anna Magnani's daughter; her role was first assigned to her twin, who at the time was unable to play the part...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rE8njj3bmn0KUoqQbvqOhnZnSmR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/117617"}}, {tmdbId:"151470", properties:{bornIn:"Hartford, Connecticut, USA", imdbId:"0177879", born:date('1933-09-30'), name:"Ben Cooper", bio:"Ben Cooper was an American screen, radio, and television actor.  He began his career on Broadway as a child stage actor.  In 2005 Cooper won a Golden Boot Award for his work in Westerns...", died:date('2020-02-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6Vdr2Tan8SxAUDmXVlqrF2EjXLd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/151470"}}, {tmdbId:"108024", properties:{bornIn:"Hamamatsu, Shizuoka Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0875465", born:date('1924-12-06'), name:"Kôji Tsuruta", bio:"Actor and singer...", died:date('1987-06-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jEwWRgYuFeXG9tsn3cUldFjzu4O.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/108024"}}, {tmdbId:"108018", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0645422", born:date('1933-01-11'), name:"Mariko Okada", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMariko Okada (1933) is a Japanese actress.  She is married to film director Yoshishige Yoshida. \n\nHer father was the noted silent film actor Tokihiko Okada, who before his early death (the year following his daughter's birth) starred in Yasujiro Ozu's Tokyo Chorus (1931).  As an adult, Mariko herself was cast by Ozu, appearing for example in An Autumn Afternoon (1962), the director's final film...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/smKu9qNcgBxFvg7zCWDMnRBlijH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/108018"}}, {tmdbId:"66075", properties:{bornIn:"Boston, Massachusetts U.S.", imdbId:"0876211", born:date('1911-07-16'), name:"Sonny Tufts", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSonny Tufts (born Bowen Charlton Tufts III, July 16, 1911, Boston, Massachusetts - June 4, 1970, Santa Monica, California) was a United States film actor. \n\nTufts was born into a prominent banking family, whose patriarch had supposedly sailed to America from England in 1683.  He broke with the family banking tradition by studying opera at Yale, where he was a member of Skull and Bones...", died:date('1970-06-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mD7Zs09U3w2TpgHIUJ00L8A0Ygn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/66075"}}, {tmdbId:"25888", properties:{bornIn:"Gothenburg, Västra Götalands län, Sweden", imdbId:"0414965", born:date('1929-05-23'), name:"Ulla Jacobsson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nUlla Jacobsson (23 May 1929, Mölndal – 20 August 1982, Vienna, buried at the Wiener Zentralfriedhof) was a Swedish actress who is perhaps best known for playing one of the very few female roles in the film Zulu. \n\nJacobsson was born in Gothenburg, Sweden.  Originally a stage actress, she started appearing in English language films in the early 1960s and tended to play serious and anxious looking characters...", died:date('1982-08-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rF0ANqdfpP7i2ctD5LJkg8QbXfO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25888"}}, {tmdbId:"70276", properties:{imdbId:"0196992", born:date('1920-03-08'), name:"Eva Dahlbeck", bio:"Eva Dahlbeck (8 March 1920 – 8 February 2008) was a Swedish actress and author.  Eva Dahlbeck was born in Saltsjö-Duvnäs near Stockholm.  She attended the prestigious acting school of the Royal Dramatic Theatre (in Swedish: Dramatens elevskola) from 1941 to 1944, and acted on the Theatre's stage from 1944 to 1964.  She made her film debut in the role of Botilla in Rid i natt! in 1942...", died:date('2008-02-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4yjjJ3ffl7SyuKnjWGGcmPYHCYN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70276"}}, {tmdbId:"70277", properties:{bornIn:"Stockholm, Sweden", imdbId:"0137808", born:date('1932-02-11'), name:"Margit Carlqvist", bio:"Margit Carlqvist is a Swedish stage and screen actress.  She was admitted to the Royal Dramatic Theatre's acting school in 1949 at the age of 17.  She made her film debut in Ingmar Bergman's \"Till glädje/To Joy\" (1950).   She starred in many movies during the 1950s, mostly as some kind of vamp.  Internationally she is perhaps most known for her role in Ingmar Bergman's \"Smiles of a Summer Night\" (1955)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/88lGpSoVZlXS7IjHsrBlmt8sPyT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70277"}}, {tmdbId:"29327", properties:{bornIn:"Bologna, Emilia-Romagna, Italy", imdbId:"0106387", born:date('1916-09-18'), name:"Rossano Brazzi", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRossano Brazzi (18 September 1916 – 24 December 1994) was an Italian actor.  Brazzi was born in Bologna to Adelmo and Maria (née Ghedini) Brazzi.  He attended San Marco University in Florence, Italy, where he was raised from the age of four.  He made his film debut in 1939...", died:date('1994-12-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qEpEMTG9gKN5D8ZpCfoQzd2kMFc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29327"}}, {tmdbId:"31696", properties:{bornIn:"Milan, Lombardy, Italy", imdbId:"0592109", born:date('1909-07-05'), name:"Isa Miranda", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nIsa Miranda (5 July 1909 – 8 July 1982) was an Italian actress with an international film career. \n\nShe worked as a typist whilst attending the drama academy in Milan and training as a stage actress.  She went on to play bit parts in Italian films in Rome.  Success came with Max Ophüls' film La Signora di tutti (Everybody's Woman) (1934) in which she played Gaby Doriot, a famous film star and fascinating adventuress with whom men cannot help falling in love...", died:date('1982-07-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/AfpmUezFswpfmc4sGHtuTfrS0Vs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31696"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"7333", properties:{bornIn:"Spokane, Washington, U.S.", imdbId:"0569000", born:date('1922-05-07'), name:"Darren McGavin", bio:"Was an American actor best known for playing the title role in the television horror series Kolchak: The Night Stalker and his portrayal in the film A Christmas Story of the grumpy father given to bursts of profanity that he never realizes his son overhears.  He appeared as the tough-talking, funny detective in the 1950s television series Mickey Spillane's Mike Hammer.  From 1959-1961, McGavin starred in the NBC western series Riverboat, first with Burt Reynolds and then with Noah Beery, Jr...", died:date('2006-02-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/w2r1GQOOzyB6Ku79nGelHv4VaNd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7333"}}, {tmdbId:"56923", properties:{bornIn:"Santa Monica, California, USA", imdbId:"0179408", born:date('1930-01-03'), name:"Mara Corday", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMara Corday (born Marilyn Joan Watts on January 3, 1930 in Santa Monica, California) is a showgirl, model, actress, Playboy Playmate and a 1950s cult figure. \n\nWanting a career in films, Mara Corday came to Hollywood while still in her teens and found work as a showgirl at the Earl Carroll Theatre on Sunset Boulevard.  Her physical beauty brought jobs as a photographer's model that led to a bit part as a showgirl in the 1951 film Two Tickets to Broadway...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/obV6gAKcNon1aqcm3EYwmJVYZ8I.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56923"}}, {tmdbId:"56924", properties:{bornIn:"Fresno, California", imdbId:"0656980", born:date('1905-06-30'), name:"Nestor Paiva", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nNestor Paiva (June 30, 1905 - September 9, 1966) was a prolific American actor of Portuguese descent who portrayed the innkeeper on Walt Disney's live-action television series Zorro by ABC and its feature film The Sign of Zorro which was shot in Burbank's Walt Disney Studios...", died:date('1966-09-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tVOOKRvdvPgEvWCEpjvZXFqyTXJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56924"}}, {tmdbId:"2640", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0484829", born:date('1904-11-25'), name:"Jessie Royce Landis", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJessie Royce Landis (November 25, 1904 – February 2, 1972) was an American actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jessie Royce Landis, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1972-02-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2s3SklsN2T7Wge79EXw41fDCwvD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2640"}}, {tmdbId:"50962", properties:{bornIn:"Kingston, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0001559", born:date('1924-06-20'), name:"Audie Murphy", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Audie Leon Murphy (June 20, 1924 – May 28, 1971)  was a fifth grade dropout from an extremely poor family who became the most decorated American soldier of World War II.  After the war he became a celebrated movie star for over two decades, appearing in 44 films.   He also found some success as a country music composer. \n\nMurphy became the most decorated United States soldier of the war during twenty-seven months in action in the European Theatre...", died:date('1971-05-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/afAOHCieGEvozfBbHwDVhMMoS2T.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/50962"}}, {tmdbId:"84233", properties:{bornIn:"Peoria, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0860471", born:date('1925-11-27'), name:"Marshall Thompson", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nMarshall Thompson (November 27, 1925 – May 18, 1992) was an American film and television actor.  He was born James Marshall Thompson in Peoria, Illinois.  In 1943 Thompson, known for his boy-next-door good looks, was signed by Universal Pictures.  He played quiet, thoughtful teens in Universal's feature films, including a lead opposite singing star Gloria Jean in Reckless Age, earning $350 weekly...", died:date('1992-05-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1VmHSu2Xrlqpe25mfQdGNygAlRN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/84233"}}, {tmdbId:"12311", properties:{imdbId:"0446438", born:date('1927-09-16'), name:"Jack Kelly", died:date('1992-11-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iSZeoIt47fGYrrrep7mkfx3yTJL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12311"}}, {tmdbId:"24367", properties:{bornIn:"Penns Grove, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0001234", born:date('1918-01-29'), name:"John Forsythe", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nJohn Forsythe (born Jacob Lincoln Freund; January 29, 1918 – April 1, 2010) was an American stage, television and film actor...", died:date('2010-04-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oNbhR7LqUmuRedsQh6rgxyRzcuI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24367"}}, {tmdbId:"12969", properties:{bornIn:"Baltimore, Maryland, U.S.", imdbId:"0622450", born:date('1905-06-19'), name:"Mildred Natwick", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nMildred Natwick (June 19, 1905 – October 25, 1994) was an American stage, film and television actress.  In 1967, she earned an Academy Award nomination for her supporting role in Barefoot in the Park.  She was nominated for two Tony Awards in 1957 and 1972 and won a Primetime Emmy Award for her work in the miniseries The Snoop Sisters, opposite Helen Hayes...", died:date('1994-10-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mts101uvIclwa0Ee14Sa3sx6XL4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12969"}}, {tmdbId:"68642", properties:{bornIn:"Baltimore, Maryland, U.S.", imdbId:"0242972", born:date('1901-01-25'), name:"Mildred Dunnock", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nMildred Dunnock (January 25, 1901 – July 5, 1991) was an American theater, film and television actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Mildred Dunnock, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1991-07-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7Uz07I2HyDPlJPqq1A0q0Kabq5D.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/68642"}}, {tmdbId:"1112521", properties:{bornIn:"Metsämaa, Finland", imdbId:"0459206", born:date('1920-02-29'), name:"Kosti Klemelä", died:date('2006-11-26'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1112521"}}, {tmdbId:"1112522", properties:{bornIn:"Pori, Finland", imdbId:"0767880", born:date('1922-04-09'), name:"Heikki Savolainen", bio:"Heikki Savolainen (9 April 1922 in Pori – 22 January 1975) was a Finnish stage and screen actor renowned for the part of Urho Hietanen in Edvin Laine's 1955 The Unknown Soldier (The Unknown Soldier).  He also played several comedic roles in 50's Finnish movies, as well as performing in several radio plays...", died:date('1975-01-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bHiGHi3FuFAgVOwOitvDRkHwePr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1112522"}}, {tmdbId:"1112523", properties:{imdbId:"0866271", name:"Reino Tolvanen", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1112523"}}, {tmdbId:"1559762", properties:{bornIn:"Riihimäki, Finland", imdbId:"0802410", born:date('1926-09-30'), name:"Veikko Sinisalo", died:date('2003-12-16'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1559762"}}, {tmdbId:"29675", properties:{bornIn:"Hackney, London", imdbId:"0467311", born:date('1919-11-24'), name:"David Kossoff", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDavid Kossoff (24 November 1919 – 23 March 2005) was a British actor.  Following the death of his son Paul, a rock musician, he became an anti-drug campaigner.  In 1971 he was also actively involved in the Nationwide Festival of Light protesting against the commercial exploitation of sex and violence, and advocating the teaching of Christ as the key to re-establishing moral stability in Britain...", died:date('2005-03-23'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29675"}}, {tmdbId:"14528", properties:{bornIn:"Vladivostok, Russia", imdbId:"0000989", born:date('1920-07-11'), name:"Yul Brynner", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nYul Brynner ( July 11, 1920 – October 10, 1985) was a Russian-born American actor of stage and film.  He was best known for his portrayal of Mongkut, king of Siam, in the Rodgers and Hammerstein musical The King and I, for which he won an Academy Award for Best Actor for the film version; he also played the role more than 4,500 times on stage.  He is also remembered as Rameses II in the 1956 Cecil B...", died:date('1985-10-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/i6OvEN6To9h6IaHAp4MrRZw8GGq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14528"}}, {tmdbId:"1559071", properties:{imdbId:"0011967", name:"Kamala Adhikari", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1559071"}}, {tmdbId:"1559072", properties:{imdbId:"0051837", name:"Lalchand Banerjee", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1559072"}}, {tmdbId:"1094825", properties:{imdbId:"0052332", name:"Kali Bannerjee", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1094825"}}, {tmdbId:"29518", properties:{bornIn:"Santa María La Redonda, Mexico City, Distrito Federal, Mexico", imdbId:"0134594", born:date('1911-08-12'), name:"Cantinflas", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nFortino Mario Alfonso Moreno Reyes (August 12, 1911 – April 20, 1993) was a Mexican comedian and stage and film actor, known professionally as Cantinflas.  He often portrayed impoverished campesinos or a peasant of pelado origin.  The character came to be associated with the national identity of Mexico, and allowed Cantinflas to establish a long, successful film career that included a foray into Hollywood...", died:date('1993-04-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iASObohpLJzqYQM6bQzyup3QvEs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29518"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"14701", properties:{bornIn:"Johnstown, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0004647", born:date('1931-05-28'), name:"Carroll Baker", bio:"Carroll Baker (born May 28, 1931) is a former American actress who has enjoyed popularity as both a serious dramatic actress and, particularly in the 1960s, as a movie sex symbol...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iLjfUkmVv9B9WAvvuJpcKpVNpZA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14701"}}, {tmdbId:"3265", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0908919", born:date('1915-12-07'), name:"Eli Wallach", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nEli Herschel Wallach (December 7, 1915-June 24, 2014) was an American film, television and stage actor, who gained fame in the late 1950s.  For his performance in Baby Doll he won a BAFTA Award for Best Newcomer and a Golden Globe nomination.  One of his most famous roles is that of Tuco in The Good, the Bad and the Ugly (1966)...", died:date('2014-06-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cjOzKNXOrwc8ZgGWmJEM8A3HZ19.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3265"}}, {tmdbId:"94036", properties:{bornIn:"Lowell, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0446715", born:date('1921-03-25'), name:"Nancy Kelly", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nNancy Kelly (March 25, 1921 – January 2, 1995) was an American actress.  She became a movie leading lady in the late 1930s, while still in her teens.  She made 36 movies between 1926 and 1977, including portraying Tyrone Power's love interest in the classic Jesse James (1939), and playing opposite Spencer Tracy in Stanley and Livingstone later that same year...", died:date('1995-01-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/thJSFffWA4XIxQxZeGLXK6dIVd1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94036"}}, {tmdbId:"125026", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, United States", imdbId:"0566478", born:date('1945-08-21'), name:"Patty McCormack", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPatty McCormack (born August 21, 1945) is an American actress with a career in theater, films and television. \n\nShe achieved success as a child actress, and received a nomination for an Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress for her performance in The Bad Seed (1956).  Her acting career has continued with supporting roles in film and television, including a more recent performance as Pat Nixon in Frost/Nixon (2008)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/d25kSBAa03zbu7XlBPpfwndixfE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/125026"}}, {tmdbId:"5732", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, U.S.", imdbId:"0428216", born:date('1912-08-01'), name:"Henry Jones", bio:"Henry Burk Jones (August 1, 1912 – May 17, 1999) was an American actor of stage, film and television. \n\nJones was born in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, the son of Helen (née Burk) and John Francis Xavier Jones.  He was the grandson of Pennsylvania Representative Henry Burk.  He attended the Jesuit-run Saint Joseph's Preparatory School. \n\nJones is remembered for his role as handyman Leroy Jessup in the movie The Bad Seed (1956), a role he originated on Broadway...", died:date('1999-05-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xRVx21ItvMO6B4ClVzAfz96xHTm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5732"}}, {tmdbId:"40618", properties:{bornIn:"Columbus, Ohio, U.S.", imdbId:"0373012", born:date('1919-03-29'), name:"Eileen Heckart", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEileen Heckart was an American actress of stage, screen, and television.   Born Anna Eileen Herbert, her career spanned nearly 60 years.  She first became known for her role as schoolteacher Rosemary Sydney in the original 1953 cast of William Inge's play Picnic on Broadway...", died:date('2001-12-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7bXAy2ItipHc72pAwVDj4mercoF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/40618"}}, {tmdbId:"78186", properties:{imdbId:"0483740", name:"Pascal Lamorisse", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/whoRiCRmUGd8GLs8dqFAL3a62Qv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78186"}}, {tmdbId:"142935", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0783399", born:date('1893-02-25'), name:"Georges Sellier", died:date('1988-09-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iWYzinq4HgKu8GSmLsRbNk6gP0A.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/142935"}}, {tmdbId:"1189122", properties:{name:"Vladimir Popov", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1189122"}}, {tmdbId:"1189121", properties:{imdbId:"0673413", name:"Paul Perey", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1189121"}}, {tmdbId:"213464", properties:{imdbId:"0946660", born:date('1928-08-16'), name:"Shôji Yasui", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yMvWiA9EEZxZHjVVz1TTyaCK0Mo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/213464"}}, {tmdbId:"97629", properties:{bornIn:"Fukuoka, Japan", imdbId:"0357307", born:date('1906-02-07'), name:"Jun Hamamura", died:date('1995-06-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ekJCrTOo9qwGNNJbN41x9VRYIy0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/97629"}}, {tmdbId:"213465", properties:{bornIn:"Kokura, Fukuoka Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0619821", born:date('1926-06-16'), name:"Taketoshi Naitô", died:date('2012-08-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hkjjzo0bnag3nPsT2GutNbeUHyt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/213465"}}, {tmdbId:"60158", properties:{bornIn:"Charleroi, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0429250", born:date('1934-03-31'), name:"Shirley Jones", bio:"Shirley Mae Jones (born March 31, 1934) is an American singer and actress of stage, film and television.  In her six decades of television, she starred as wholesome characters in a number of well-known musical films, such as Oklahoma! (1955), Carousel (1956), and The Music Man (1962).  She won the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress for playing a prostitute in Elmer Gantry (1960)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2m0Y7d2mRlndVdHodXsNAgZU5ys.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/60158"}}, {tmdbId:"44728", properties:{bornIn:"Dallastown, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0593192", born:date('1918-11-04'), name:"Cameron Mitchell", bio:"Cameron Mitchell (November 4, 1918 – July 6, 1994) was an American film, television and Broadway actor with close ties to one of Canada's most successful families, and considered, by Lee Strasberg, to be one of the founding members of The Actor's Studio in New York City...", died:date('1994-07-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/niLc67b00QIa0oDWp47mXcv319e.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/44728"}}, {tmdbId:"128000", properties:{bornIn:"Pasadena, California, U.S.", imdbId:"0749539", born:date('1932-12-23'), name:"Barbara Ruick", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\n​Barbara Ruick (December 23, 1930 – March 3, 1974) was an American actress and singer. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Barbara Ruick, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1974-03-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6ipCjt72DoNBqCZNl1eYZZiyw5b.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/128000"}}, {tmdbId:"5826", properties:{bornIn:"Pretoria, South Africa", imdbId:"0424318", born:date('1923-10-05'), name:"Glynis Johns", bio:"A retired husky voiced British stage, television and film actress, dancer, pianist, and singer.  Born on October 6, 1923 in Pretoria, South Africa as Glynis Margaret P.  Johns, while her parents were on tour.  She is the daughter of actor Mervyn Johns and Alice (Alyce) Maud Steele Wareham (1901 - 1970) who was an Australian concert pianist.  Another source gives the spelling of her name as Alys Maude Steel-Payne...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/st4IdzYEfXActXFbVnR3DLptpTw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5826"}}, {tmdbId:"3783", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0000003", born:date('1934-09-28'), name:"Brigitte Bardot", bio:"Brigitte Anne-Marie Bardot (born 28 September 1934) is a French former fashion model, actress and singer, and animal rights activist. \n\nIn her early life, Bardot was an aspiring ballet dancer.  She started her acting career in 1952 and, after appearing in 16 films, became world-famous due to her role in her then-husband Roger Vadim's controversial film And God Created Woman.  She later starred in Jean-Luc Godard's 1963 cult film, Contempt...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/prEu5JJslUBTjOSAxsO9VU4OoYq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3783"}}, {tmdbId:"10459", properties:{bornIn:"Solln , Germany", imdbId:"0432007", born:date('1915-12-13'), name:"Curd Jürgens", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nCurd Gustav Andreas Gottlieb Franz Jürgens (13 December 1915 – 18 June 1982) was a German-Austrian stage and film actor.  He was usually billed in English-speaking films as Curt Jurgens. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Curd Jürgens, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1982-06-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jVYPQqJlDpAMY8O6GWm8SrKrWA0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10459"}}, {tmdbId:"1352", properties:{bornIn:"Piolenc, Vaucluse, France", imdbId:"0004462", born:date('1930-12-11'), name:"Jean-Louis Trintignant", bio:"Jean-Louis Trintignant (born 11 December 1930) is a French actor who has enjoyed an international acclaim.  He won the Best Actor Award at the 1969 Cannes Film Festival. \n\nTrintignant was born in Piolenc, Vaucluse, France, the son of Claire (née Tourtin) and Raoul Trintignant, an industrialist.  At the age of twenty, Trintignant moved to Paris to study drama, and made his theatrical debut in 1951 going on to be seen as one of the most gifted French actors of the post-war era...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pNcpelmMkveMiGXZQNTkXMwoLiG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1352"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"25160", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, Ile-de-France, France01-13", imdbId:"0548355", born:date('1895-01-13'), name:"Jane Marken", died:date('1976-12-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/z1XlCXQERkqIj0dR7hJf3IbnK5P.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25160"}}, {tmdbId:"7633", properties:{bornIn:"Regina, Saskatchewan, Canada", imdbId:"0000558", born:date('1926-02-11'), name:"Leslie Nielsen", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLeslie William Nielsen, OC (11 February 1926 – 28 November 2010) was a Canadian and naturalized American actor and comedian.  Nielsen appeared in over one hundred films and 1,500 television programs over the span of his career, portraying over 220 characters.  Born in Regina, Saskatchewan, Nielsen enlisted in the Royal Canadian Air Force and worked as a disc jockey before receiving a scholarship to Neighborhood Playhouse...", died:date('2010-11-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/u5vWl5dw69Nf89f905Qb5JqEVL3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7633"}}, {tmdbId:"12310", properties:{bornIn:"Clark's Summit, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0828838", born:date('1919-11-02'), name:"Warren Stevens", bio:"Warren Albert Stevens was an American stage, screen, and television actor.   A founding member of The Actor's Studio in New York, Stevens received notice on Broadway in the late 1940s, and thereafter was offered a Hollywood contract at 20th Century Fox.  His first Broadway role was in The Life of Galileo; his first movie role followed in The Frogmen...", died:date('2012-03-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fUgrPN5x99MYr8yB9Nu77kFWivm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12310"}}, {tmdbId:"83315", properties:{bornIn:"Santa Monica, California, USA", imdbId:"0264134", born:date('1945-05-06'), name:"Richard Eyer", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRichard Ross Eyer (born May 6, 1945, Santa Monica, California) is a former American child actor during the 1950s and 1960s who taught elementary school in the eastern Sierra city of Bishop in Inyo County until he retired in 2006.  He is the older brother of Robert Eyer (b.  May 6, 1948), another child actor of the period who is deceased...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5j8JL93cFHpcSUnZTYMD1fTLlAf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83315"}}, {tmdbId:"30980", properties:{bornIn:"Washington DC, USA", imdbId:"0485485", born:date('1933-01-06'), name:"Mike Lane", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nMike Lane born Michael Lane January 6 1933 in Washington DC is an American professional wrestler and actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Mike Lane, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ajc0634lUSwTJDwaZbCrcOZJFHe.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30980"}}, {tmdbId:"128330", properties:{bornIn:"Tripoli", imdbId:"0687958", born:date('1934-06-20'), name:"Rossana Podestà", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRossana Podestà (born Carla Podestà, Tripoli, June 20 1934 – Rome, December 10 2013) was an Italian actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Rossana Podestà, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2013-12-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/97g6foFR7NRcNXzMiVsTjrC55IG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/128330"}}, {tmdbId:"102026", properties:{bornIn:"Kaunas, Lithuania", imdbId:"0785286", born:date('1925-07-30'), name:"Jacques Sernas", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJacques Sernas (Lithuanian: Jurgis Šernas; sometimes credited as Jack Sernas; born 30 July 1925, died 3 July 2015) was a Lithuanian-born French actor with an international film career. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jacques Sernas, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2015-07-0