er (8 June 1931 – 5 May 2011) was a German-born British actress, who was brought up in England and Southern Africa.  She appeared in film and television for more than forty years beginning in the 1950s, most notably in the original version of Invasion of the Body Snatchers...", died:date('2011-05-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bDShxBNCKS6KIrWsEHcJ3RaMJGc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69810"}}, {tmdbId:"3640", properties:{bornIn:"St. Paul, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0309588", born:date('1915-09-24'), name:"Larry Gates", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLarry Gates (September 24, 1915 – December 12, 1996) was an American actor probably best known for his role as H. B.  Lewis on daytime's Guiding Light and as Doc Baugh in the film version of Cat on a Hot Tin Roof.  He played the role of Lewis from 1983 to 1996 and received the Emmy for Outstanding Supporting Actor at the 1985 awards...", died:date('1996-12-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jug7pKx92ghcdyvl5DR1DBB6d5g.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3640"}}, {tmdbId:"69811", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0233014", born:date('1918-01-25'), name:"King Donovan", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia...", died:date('1987-06-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2O22SEHCVd84KXK7G3AeiOtZh5C.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69811"}}, {tmdbId:"3337", properties:{bornIn:" Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0250436", born:date('1928-07-09'), name:"Vince Edwards", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Vince Edwards (July 9,  1928 - March 11, 1996) was an American actor, director, and singer, best known for the role of TV doctor \"Ben Casey\". \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Vincent Edwards, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1996-03-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2Jy9AnTesAZFjBGbJeBZoNZCHOh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3337"}}, {tmdbId:"13299", properties:{bornIn:"Humacao, Puerto Rico", imdbId:"0001549", born:date('1931-12-11'), name:"Rita Moreno", bio:"Rita Moreno (born December 11, 1931) is a Puerto Rican singer, dancer and actress.  She is the first and only Hispanic person and one of the few performers who have won an Emmy, a Grammy, an Oscar, and a Tony and at the time the second Puerto Rican to win an Academy Award...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/A1qAUZhaCP3Gi8uGqmjYgXJTkj4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13299"}}, {tmdbId:"9912", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0072578", born:date('1918-08-10'), name:"Martin Benson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMartin Benjamin Benson (10 August 1918 – 28 February 2010) was an English character actor, who appeared in films, theatre and television.  He appeared in both British and Hollywood productions. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Martin Benson (actor), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2010-02-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mH5csoJ1RJjzRCtzwJeJhxxgRWb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9912"}}, {tmdbId:"30551", properties:{bornIn:"New Orleans, Louisiana, USA", imdbId:"0001374", born:date('1926-11-25'), name:"Jeffrey Hunter", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJeffrey Hunter (November 25, 1926 – May 27, 1969) was an American film and television actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jeffrey Hunter, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1969-05-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/enQuu8yfrL0VX7BL3FqsM7DGcqF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30551"}}, {tmdbId:"110727", properties:{bornIn:"Cleveland, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0500702", born:date('1925-10-15'), name:"Virginia Leith", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nVirginia Leith (October 15, 1925 - November 4, 2019) was an American film and television actress. \n\nLeith starred in a few films, with her most productive period coming in the 1950s.  Her debut in 1953 was also the first film directed by Stanley Kubrick, a self-financed art house film, Fear and Desire...", died:date('2019-11-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gS9WqbgLzPEeJCPiy4w8gPGNOj1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/110727"}}, {tmdbId:"109410", properties:{bornIn:"Thomasville, Georgia, USA", imdbId:"0940946", born:date('1930-02-27'), name:"Joanne Woodward", bio:"Joanne Gignilliat Trimmier Woodward (born February 27, 1930) is an American actress, producer, and philanthropist.  She is best known for her performance in The Three Faces of Eve (1957), which earned her an Academy Award for Best Actress and a Golden Globe Award for Best Actress in a Motion Picture – Drama...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vUwRHy2UTY3fS4JyoBlq04vpQo9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/109410"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"8239", properties:{bornIn:"Uxbridge, Hillingdon, Middlesex, England, UK", imdbId:"0587061", born:date('1907-09-27'), name:"Bernard Miles", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBernard James Miles, Baron Miles, CBE (27 September 1907–14 June 1991) was an English character actor, writer and director.  He opened the Mermaid Theatre in London in 1959, the first new theatre opened in the City of London since the 17th century. \n\nMiles was born in Uxbridge, Middlesex and attended Bishopshalt School in Hillingdon.  While his parents were respectively a farm labourer and a cook, he was educated at Pembroke College, Oxford...", died:date('1991-06-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wcg0mbHJEU7IXK5lihpMXEVy0jn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8239"}}, {tmdbId:"9767", properties:{bornIn:"Nancy, Meurthe-et-Moselle, France", imdbId:"0545352", born:date('1920-01-10'), name:"Georges Marchal", bio:"Georges Marchal was one of the most important lead actors in French cinema in the '50s, together with Jean Marais...", died:date('1997-11-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eAERwieF5K8KmEBUkL9Ko3xtvM7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9767"}}, {tmdbId:"3784", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0681566", born:date('1925-12-27'), name:"Michel Piccoli", bio:"Michel Piccoli (1925-2020) was a French actor.  He was born in Paris to a musical family; his mother was a pianist and his father a violinist.  He appeared in many different roles, from seducer to cop to gangster, in more than 170 movies...", died:date('2020-05-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mLqCtXhm6f8xjaghb6k1a4NxHIX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3784"}}, {tmdbId:"32791", properties:{bornIn:"Bayonne, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0001417", born:date('1921-11-14'), name:"Brian Keith", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBrian Keith (November 14, 1921 – June 24, 1997) was an American film, television, and stage actor who in his four decade-long career gained recognition for his work in movies such as the 1961 Disney family film The Parent Trap, the 1966 comedy The Russians Are Coming, the Russians Are Coming, and the 1975 adventure saga The Wind and the Lion, in which he portrayed Theodore Roosevelt...", died:date('1997-06-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6T6BWdpIxEAVrhTrmvt3xRDuwYd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32791"}}, {tmdbId:"10774", properties:{bornIn:"Bronx, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000843", born:date('1931-09-17'), name:"Anne Bancroft", bio:"Anne Bancroft (born Anna Maria Louisa Italiano; September 17, 1931 – June 6, 2005) was an American actress, director, screenwriter, and singer associated with the method acting school, having studied under Lee Strasberg.  Respected for her acting prowess and versatility, Bancroft was acknowledged for her work in film, theatre, and television.  She won one Academy Award, three BAFTA Awards, two Golden Globes, two Tony Awards, and two Emmy Awards, and several other awards and nominations...", died:date('2005-06-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ydabiabIsMBe2HsNmx43gBpqzxx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10774"}}, {tmdbId:"108044", properties:{bornIn:"Kyoto, Kyoto Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0755953", born:date('1935-03-01'), name:"Michiko Saga", died:date('1992-08-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cHye8GUhxyp577lFmn0OMxLw0aA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/108044"}}, {tmdbId:"7303", properties:{bornIn:"Boise City, Oklahoma, USA", imdbId:"0587256", born:date('1929-08-23'), name:"Vera Miles", bio:"Born in Boise City, Oklahoma, Vera Miles attended school in Pratt,  Kansas and Wichita, Kansas.  The patrician beauty of Miss Miles won her  the title of \"Miss Kansas\" in 1948, leading soon to small roles in  Hollywood films and television series.  Fame came to the forthright,  spirited Miles when she attracted the attention of two master directors,  Alfred Hitchcock and John Ford...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/chZhoLoGFZVyNCI5zYmLSQ0ta9T.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7303"}}, {tmdbId:"18613", properties:{bornIn:"Kanagawa, Japan", imdbId:"0756292", born:date('1932-05-14'), name:"Kenji Sahara", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Kenji Sahara (  Sahara Kenji, born Tadashi Ishihara) (born May 14, 1932) is a Japanese actor.  He was born in Kawasaki City, Kanagawa.  His real name is Masayoshi Kato ( Katō Masayoshi).  Initially he used the name Tadashi Ishihara before changing it when he secured the lead role in Rodan (1956). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Kenji Sahara, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8G26qlzfoyLK6qIOzmehuwvLlvr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18613"}}, {tmdbId:"128665", properties:{bornIn:"Shinagawa, Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0794205", born:date('1936-10-21'), name:"Yumi Shirakawa", died:date('2016-06-14'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/128665"}}, {tmdbId:"1189033", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0462181", born:date('1920-05-03'), name:"Akio Kobori", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1189033"}}, {tmdbId:"26183", properties:{bornIn:"Margny-lès-Compiègne, Oise, Picardie, France", imdbId:"0504641", born:date('1929-05-26'), name:"François Leterrier", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/i2zDAUl9Y3AHKYz23OsTDuvqoka.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/26183"}}, {tmdbId:"96794", properties:{imdbId:"0494179", name:"Charles Le Clainche", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xSZvvlVnHHs2wX60NHBjsVU6PAT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96794"}}, {tmdbId:"96795", properties:{imdbId:"0066519", name:"Maurice Beerblock", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jPZ1ZIcBLzYpiga30RnFbdVnhK2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96795"}}, {tmdbId:"39438", properties:{imdbId:"0598394", name:"Roland Monod", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nvO7xFrUwsVAVJfNuDGW24jX7wj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/39438"}}, {tmdbId:"44846", properties:{bornIn:"Charleston, Washington, U.S.", imdbId:"0003318", born:date('1913-11-24'), name:"Howard Duff", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nHoward Green Duff (November 24, 1913 – July 8, 1990) was an American actor of film, television, stage, and radio. \n\nDuff was born in Charleston, Washington, now a part of Bremerton.  He graduated from Roosevelt High School in Seattle in 1932 where he began acting in school plays only after he was cut from the basketball team.  His first film role was as an inmate in Brute Force...", died:date('1990-07-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/k4yDXRwtshW5O7yDqCIaE1jva01.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/44846"}}, {tmdbId:"1936", properties:{bornIn:"Bronx, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000842", born:date('1919-11-04'), name:"Martin Balsam", bio:"Martin Henry Balsam (November 4, 1919 – February 13, 1996) was an American character actor.  He is best known for a number of film roles, including detective Milton Arbogast in Alfred Hitchcock's Psycho (1960), Arnold Burns in A Thousand Clowns (1965), which earned him the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor, Juror #1 in 12 Angry Men (1957), and Mr...", died:date('1996-02-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2j4LJJfTPQtvnjp8LfSGOvWFATO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1936"}}, {tmdbId:"5247", properties:{bornIn:"Platteville, Wisconsin, USA", imdbId:"0275835", born:date('1925-02-03'), name:"John Fiedler", bio:"Typical of busy character actors, John Fielder has made his face--and voice--recognizable to millions.  Many would know the bald-pated Fiedler as therapy patient Mr.  Peterson on TV's \"The Bob Newhart Show\" (1972); others might first recognize him for the 1968 movie and spin-off TV series \"The Odd Couple\" (1970) (or perhaps even from the Broadway play that preceded them)...", died:date('2005-06-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6vfLLGeGuO6Ko0VRnyhgE2v6RUu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5247"}}, {tmdbId:"5249", properties:{bornIn:"Owatonna, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0550855", born:date('1914-06-18'), name:"E.G. Marshall", bio:"E.  G.  Marshall (June 18, 1914 – August 24, 1998) was an American actor, best known for his television roles as the lawyer Lawrence Preston on The Defenders in the 1960s, and as neurosurgeon David Craig on The Bold Ones: The New Doctors in the 1970s.  Among his film roles, he is perhaps best known as the unflappable Juror #4 in Sidney Lumet's courtroom drama 12 Angry Men (1957). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia E.  G.  Marshall, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1998-08-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bZeu3BhYFP99dwIMobFR2xuRfRy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5249"}}, {tmdbId:"76979", properties:{bornIn:"Westchester County, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0268012", born:date('1932-10-04'), name:"Felicia Farr", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nFelicia Farr (born October 4, 1932) is a former American actress and model. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Felicia Farr, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iXpZNhxJcJeUenrkou0uoLWWZiZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/76979"}}, {tmdbId:"76980", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0199070", born:date('1923-04-01'), name:"Leora Dana", died:date('1983-12-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2cxww6C5uNqCnTlIROEjLRlIjIM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/76980"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"54682", properties:{bornIn:"Nevada, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0666332", born:date('1920-02-10'), name:"Neva Patterson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Neva Louise Patterson(10 February 1920 – 14 December 2010) was an American character actress. \n\nBorn on a farm near Nevada in Story County in central Iowa, she and her parents moved to New York City in 1938.  She made her Broadway debut in 1947's The Druid Circle.  In 1952, she played \"Helen Sherman\" in The Seven Year Itch...", died:date('2010-12-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/47AbuaObL09XEVij3L2lPAMezPd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54682"}}, {tmdbId:"24810", properties:{bornIn:"Jacksonville, Florida, USA", imdbId:"0004769", born:date('1934-06-01'), name:"Pat Boone", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nPat Boone (born Charles Eugene Patrick Boone on June 1, 1934) is an American singer, actor and writer who was a successful pop singer in the United States during the 1950s and early 1960s.  He covered black artists' songs (when part of the country was segregated) and sold more copies than his black counterparts.  He sold over 45 million albums, had 38 Top 40 hits and appeared in more than 12 Hollywood movies...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/k6uElklYgUWljgdH4hwu5v3kaB9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24810"}}, {tmdbId:"52126", properties:{bornIn:"Kansas City, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"1255831", born:date('1933-01-30'), name:"Dolores Michaels", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDolores Michaels was an American actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Dolores Michaels , licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2001-09-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tMTZ9aCxqgQUh8iC5jxXeM7OtHZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/52126"}}, {tmdbId:"857", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0640023", born:date('1908-03-29'), name:"Arthur O'Connell", bio:"Arthur O'Connell (March 29, 1908 – May 18, 1981) was an American stage and film actor.  He appeared in films (starting with a small role in Citizen Kane) in 1941 and television programs (mostly guest appearances).  Among his screen appearances were Picnic, Anatomy of a Murder, and as the watch-maker who hides Jews during WWII in The Hiding Place...", died:date('1981-05-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wjhhpfICbe7NtbFLO7Uyrye06HP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/857"}}, {tmdbId:"129427", properties:{bornIn:"Cardiff, Wales, UK", imdbId:"0440542", born:date('1934-09-30'), name:"Anna Kashfi", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAnna Kashfi (born September 30, 1934) is a former film actress, who had a brief Hollywood career in the 1950s and is best known for having been married to Marlon Brando. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Anna Kashfi, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2015-08-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kBIMWYr0JsW5Hwgvksrl3izkgys.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/129427"}}, {tmdbId:"96850", properties:{bornIn:"Cedar Rapids, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0214529", born:date('1913-08-25'), name:"Don DeFore", bio:"Donald John \"Don\" DeFore (August 25, 1913 – December 22, 1993) was an American actor.  He is best known for his roles in the sitcom The Adventures of Ozzie and Harriet from 1952 to 1957 and the sitcom Hazel from 1961 to 1965, the former which earned him a Primetime Emmy Award nomination...", died:date('1993-12-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9j6WjEcMsRUZ3lddLSIvVJbZ2IK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96850"}}, {tmdbId:"9111", properties:{bornIn:"Minneapolis, Minnesota, United States", imdbId:"0336335", born:date('1926-03-18'), name:"Peter Graves", bio:"Peter Graves was born Peter Duesler Aurness on March 18, 1926 on Minneapolis, Minnesota.  While growing up in Minnesota, he excelled at sports and music (as a saxophonist), and by age 16, he was a radio announcer at WMIN in Minneapolis.  After two years in the United States Air Force, he studied drama at the University of Minnesota and then headed to Hollywood, where he first appeared on television and later made his film debut in Rogue River (1951)...", died:date('2010-03-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4Zyc3GHgmA0302cOziQa0HCwEmD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9111"}}, {tmdbId:"116493", properties:{bornIn:"Appalachia, Virginia, USA", imdbId:"0145312", born:date('1927-12-22'), name:"Peggie Castle", died:date('1973-08-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ofTN8pBlyHkosKiD9QmPOLQwuYt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/116493"}}, {tmdbId:"81182", properties:{bornIn:"Danville, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0030194", born:date('1896-08-28'), name:"Morris Ankrum", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMorris Ankrum (born Morris Nussbaum, August 28, 1896 – September 2, 1964) was an American radio, television and film character actor. \n\nBefore signing with Paramount Pictures in the 1930s, Nussbaum had already changed his last name to Ankrum.  Upon signing with the studio, he chose to use the name \"Stephen Morris\" before changing it to Morris Ankrum in 1939...", died:date('1964-09-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vLlnpSWAParcYOFMKL0nrNCYW3o.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81182"}}, {tmdbId:"151610", properties:{bornIn:"New York, New York, USA", imdbId:"0943660", born:date('1919-05-02'), name:"Than Wyenn", died:date('2015-01-15'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/151610"}}, {tmdbId:"10018", properties:{bornIn:"Wood Green, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0370144", born:date('1910-09-14'), name:"Jack Hawkins", bio:"John Edward Hawkins, CBE (14 September 1910 – 18 July 1973) was an English actor who worked on stage and in film from the 1930s until the 1970s.  One of the most popular British film stars of the 1950s, he was best known for his portrayal of military men in films like Angels One Five (1951), The Cruel Sea (1953), Bridge on the River Kwai (1957), Ben Hur (1959) and Lawrence of Arabia (1962)...", died:date('1973-07-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pfpe9NQrcrTrxMeU0xGsh1XRBOK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10018"}}, {tmdbId:"12249", properties:{bornIn:"Nanaura, Chiba, Japan", imdbId:"0370564", born:date('1889-06-10'), name:"Sessue Hayakawa", bio:"Sessue Hayakawa (June 10, 1889 – November 23, 1973) was a Japanese and American Issei (Japanese immigrant) actor who starred in American, Japanese, French, German, and British films.  Hayakawa was the first and one of the few Asian actors to find stardom in the United States as well as Europe.  Between the mid-1910s and the late 1920s, he was as well known as actors Charlie Chaplin and Douglas Fairbanks...", died:date('1973-11-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/86WeKuinDzwTK3N2QKKs5acfNpk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12249"}}, {tmdbId:"5", properties:{bornIn:"Kenley, Surrey, England, UK", imdbId:"0001088", born:date('1913-05-26'), name:"Peter Cushing", bio:"Peter Wilton Cushing, OBE  (26 May 1913 – 11 August 1994) was an English actor, known for his many appearances in Hammer Films, in which he played Baron Frankenstein and Dr.  Van Helsing, amongst many other roles, often appearing opposite Christopher Lee, and occasionally Vincent Price...", died:date('1994-08-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vXdutUFoGVgrey3Je1pdDo1uvGj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5"}}, {tmdbId:"101499", properties:{bornIn:"Sutton Coldfield, Warwickshire, England", imdbId:"0183764", born:date('1926-02-10'), name:"Hazel Court", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nHazel Court (10 February 1926 – 15 April 2008) was an English actress best known for her roles in horror films during the 1950s and early 1960s. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Hazel Court, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2008-04-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qj36ImC6tuukuSqymwNWFruU65H.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101499"}}, {tmdbId:"30187", properties:{bornIn:"Ullapool, Scotland", imdbId:"0882048", born:date('1921-10-16'), name:"Robert Urquhart", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Robert Urquhart (16 October 1921 – 21 March 1995) was a Scottish character actor who mainly worked in British television during his career. \n\nHe was born in Ullapool, Scotland on 16 October 1921, educated at George Heriot's School in Edinburgh and made his stage debut in 1947...", died:date('1995-03-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4KhbRBOTLpBnNEIiecM73TtaJwN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30187"}}, {tmdbId:"113", properties:{bornIn:"Belgravia, Westminster, England", imdbId:"0000489", born:date('1922-05-27'), name:"Christopher Lee", bio:"Sir Christopher Frank Carandini Lee, CBE, CStJ (born May 27, 1922, died June 7, 2015) was an English actor and musician.  Lee initially portrayed villains and became famous for his role as Count Dracula in a string of Hammer Horror films.  Other notable roles include Lord Summerisle in The Wicker Man (1973), Francisco Scaramanga in The Man with the Golden Gun (1974), Count Dooku in Star Wars episodes II and III (2002, 2005) and Saruman in The Lord of the Rings film trilogy (2001–2003)...", died:date('2015-06-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yzE2U4sS46sVRyCUKpgs3lYZaMy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/113"}}, {tmdbId:"10226", properties:{bornIn:"Providence, Rhode Island, USA", imdbId:"0373314", born:date('1927-05-20'), name:"David Hedison", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAlbert David Hedison, Jr.  (May 20, 1927-July 18, 2019, Providence, Rhode Island) was an Armenian-American film, television, and stage actor.  He was billed as Al Hedison in his early film work.  In 1959, when he was cast in the role of Victor Sebastian in the short-lived espionage television series Five Fingers, NBC insisted that he change his name.  It was proposed that he use his middle name and was known as David Hedison ever after...", died:date('2019-07-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lMK8ZajrXCSWLlovWZWGhZvktUF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10226"}}, {tmdbId:"6609", properties:{bornIn:" Vienna, Austria", imdbId:"0000942", born:date('1924-05-02'), name:"Theodore Bikel", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nTheodore Meir Bikel (born May 2, 1924) is a character actor, folk singer and musician.  He made his film debut in The African Queen (1951) and was nominated for an Academy award for his supporting role as Sheriff Max Muller in The Defiant Ones (1958). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Theodore Bikel, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2015-07-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/EDDXnXUmyzxvUUMUDZ4zKcFqgI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6609"}}, {tmdbId:"65562", properties:{bornIn:"Mount Airy, North Carolina, USA", imdbId:"0341431", born:date('1926-06-01'), name:"Andy Griffith", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAndy Samuel Griffith (born June 1, 1926) was an American actor, director, producer, Grammy Award-winning Southern-gospel singer, and writer.  He gained prominence in the starring role in director Elia Kazan's epic film A Face in the Crowd (1957) before he became better known for his television roles, playing the lead characters in the 1960-68 situation comedy, The Andy Griffith Show, and in the 1986-95 legal drama, Matlock...", died:date('2012-07-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2LE5YIxIIxT3SGOTmuYQGPE4PVa.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/65562"}}, {tmdbId:"106179", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0290047", born:date('1928-10-25'), name:"Anthony Franciosa", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nAnthony Franciosa (October 25, 1928 – January 19, 2006) was an American actor, usually billed as Tony Franciosa during the height of his career. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Anthony Franciosa,  licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2006-01-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zXzRQbzccIjSBQWlyspOvyZlcs8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/106179"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"6837", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000527", born:date('1920-10-01'), name:"Walter Matthau", bio:"Walter Matthau (October 1, 1920 – July 1, 2000) was an American actor and comedian.  He has won an Academy Award, a Golden Globe Award, a BAFTA, and two Tony Awards, and has been nominated for a Primetime Emmy Award...", died:date('2000-07-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/c3dCBlyf12yTNhS2sdSXRFaBatj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6837"}}, {tmdbId:"83393", properties:{bornIn:"St. Louis, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0860373", born:date('1909-11-09'), name:"Kay Thompson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nKay Thompson (November 9, 1909 — July 2, 1998) was an American author, composer, musician, actress and singer.  She is best known as the creator of the Eloise children's books. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Kay Thompson, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1998-07-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/m3gUVOyFhowNEbxV1it45bUYgR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83393"}}, {tmdbId:"9746", properties:{bornIn:"Koblenz - Germany", imdbId:"0041509", born:date('1922-09-14'), name:"Michel Auclair", bio:"Michel Auclair, de son vrai nom Vladimir Vujovic, est un acteur français né à Coblence, Allemagne, le 14 septembre 1922 et mort le 7 janvier 1988, à Saint-Paul-en-Forêt dans le Var, France. \n\n Durant les années 50, 60 et 70, il apparaît occasionnellement dans des productions internationales comme Drôle de frimousse avec Fred Astaire et Audrey Hepburn.   Il meurt, victime d'une hémorragie cérébrale, et est inhumé à Saint-Paul-en-Forêt dans le Var...", died:date('1988-01-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iELvzr8YZ0MOM37dop3NCNFmXwA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9746"}}, {tmdbId:"2752", properties:{bornIn:"Oakland, California, U.S.", imdbId:"0886888", born:date('1914-12-30'), name:"Jo Van Fleet", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Jo Van Fleet (December 30, 1914 – June 10, 1996) was an American theatre and film actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jo Van Fleet, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1996-06-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xdingRjzTi1lbFV1mepFeM9nMxA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2752"}}, {tmdbId:"6931", properties:{bornIn:" Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, U.S", imdbId:"0300010", born:date('1912-06-19'), name:"Martin Gabel", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nMartin Gabel (June 19, 1912 – May 22, 1986) was an American actor, film director and film producer. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article  Martin Gabel, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1986-05-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/50lp2oS1KK3BNC2ofdJrt1YGFNJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6931"}}, {tmdbId:"30141", properties:{bornIn:"London, England", imdbId:"0041602", born:date('1923-04-29'), name:"Maxine Audley", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nMaxine Audley (29 April 1923 – 23 July 1992) was an English theatre and film actress.  She made her professional stage debut in July 1940 at the Open Air Theatre.  Throughout her career, Audley performed with both the Old Vic company and the Royal Shakespeare Company multiple times.  She appeared in more than 20 films, the first of which was the 1948 adaptation of Anna Karenina...", died:date('1992-06-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7UeGD4PlZTXOdKVmUm6qOFHsYcF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30141"}}, {tmdbId:"102514", properties:{bornIn:"Linthorpe, Middlesbrough, England", imdbId:"0221491", born:date('1908-07-20'), name:"Jerry Desmonde", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJerry Desmonde (20 July 1908 - 11 February 1967) was an English stage musical, film, and television actor principally in comedies and drama.  He is probably best known as a straight man to Norman Wisdom.  Jerry is sometimes credited as Jerry Desmond. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jerry Desmonde, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1967-02-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pilrR1zNDJs1gDW6PA3cWVPgOSn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/102514"}}, {tmdbId:"29308", properties:{imdbId:"0426799", born:date('1888-04-30'), name:"Oliver Johnston", died:date('1966-12-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pfVdF7LIkbdGii7U9RR5gpjbEP2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29308"}}, {tmdbId:"16531", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0641197", born:date('1912-11-23'), name:"George O'Hanlon", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGeorge Samuel O'Hanlon (November 23, 1912 – February 11, 1989) was an American actor, comedian, writer and director.  He was best known for his role as Joe McDoakes in the Warner Bros. ' live-action Joe McDoakes short subjects from 1942 to 1956 and as the voice of George Jetson in Hanna-Barbera's 1962 prime-time animated television series The Jetsons and its 1985 revival...", died:date('1989-02-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gq8ueQObgDjDIPUFpxLm6FCU213.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16531"}}, {tmdbId:"33761", properties:{bornIn:"Osaka, Japan", imdbId:"0945222", born:date('1917-02-05'), name:"Isuzu Yamada", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nIsuzu Yamada (山田 五十鈴 Yamada Isuzu, 5 February 1917  – 9 July 2012) is a Japanese actress on stage and screen whose career has spanned eight decades...", died:date('2012-07-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3b029DnOGOGBCj9rzg8RQFfYPHw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33761"}}, {tmdbId:"30469", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0473530", born:date('1936-12-01'), name:"Akira Kubo", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAkira Kubo (久保明, born 1 December 1936) is a Japanese actor.  He has appeared in 75 films since 1952.  He starred in the film Arashi, which was entered into the 7th Berlin International Film Festival...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1LHRxdubczb6JzFe2O2qzXIoiCe.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30469"}}, {tmdbId:"99662", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0310989", born:date('1931-09-04'), name:"Mitzi Gaynor", bio:"A leading lady of light musicals, the bright-eyed Gaynor is best  remembered for \"South Pacific\".  She also hosted a string of successful  annual musical TV specials in the late 1960s and early 1970s...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ffwGqqY9aPkGEIatzwArvd8kjNg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/99662"}}, {tmdbId:"142385", properties:{imdbId:"0447608", born:date('1927-05-21'), name:"Kay Kendall", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nKay Kendall (21 May 1927 – 6 September 1959) was an English actress. \n\nKendall began her film career in the musical film London Town (1946).  Though the film was a financial failure, Kendall continued to work regularly until her appearance in the comedy film Genevieve (1953) brought her widespread recognition...", died:date('1959-09-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fzFl5H1Mi6HKWzzohduXPjzdGwZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/142385"}}, {tmdbId:"42109", properties:{bornIn:"Helsinki, Finland", imdbId:"0253359", born:date('1930-03-09'), name:"Taina Elg", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nTaina Elg (born 9 March 1930, Helsinki, Finland) is a Finnish-American actress and dancer.  She has appeared on stage, film and television. \n\nShe was born in Helsinki, but later raised in Turku by her parents, Helena Dobroumova (of Russian descent) and Åke Elg, a pianist.  In 1957 she won the Golden Globe for the Foreign Newcomer Award - Female...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bZgqmSaObkAFG8c7ILfXkuniMgf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/42109"}}, {tmdbId:"233207", properties:{bornIn:"Leningrad, USSR (St. Petersburg, Russia)", imdbId:"0759967", born:date('1934-05-04'), name:"Tatyana Samoylova", bio:"Tatiana Yevgenyevna Samoilova (Russian: Татья́на Евге́ньевна Само́йлова; 4 May 1934 – 4 May 2014) was a Soviet and Russian film actress best known for her lead role in The Cranes Are Flying.  She received a number of awards for the film, including a special mention at the Cannes Film Festival.  Samoilova had several major roles in the 1960s before largely disappearing from public life.  In 1993, she was named a People's Artist of Russia...", died:date('2014-05-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cKnswgxIVaC7CoEQ9yVNPQpRewb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/233207"}}, {tmdbId:"87001", properties:{bornIn:"Vladimir, Russian SFSR, USSR [now Russia]", imdbId:"0060692", born:date('1928-11-20'), name:"Aleksey Batalov", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAleksey Vladimirovich Batalov (Russian: Алексе́й Влади́мирович Бата́лов; born 20 November 1928) is a Soviet and Russian actor who has been acclaimed for his portrayal of noble and positive characters.  He was named a People's Artist of the USSR in 1976 and a Hero of Socialist Labour in 1989...", died:date('2017-06-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6dgzimnivd1abx8Sz1yCMJlcnA3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/87001"}}, {tmdbId:"86851", properties:{bornIn:"Ostrov, Pskov Governorate, Russian Empire [now Pskov Oblast, Russia]", imdbId:"0580959", born:date('1904-04-06'), name:"Vasiliy Merkurev", died:date('1978-05-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tefCC9tZ0PDdxzhG3oUooBrWZq9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/86851"}}, {tmdbId:"1008337", properties:{imdbId:"0796085", name:"Aleksandr Shvorin", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1008337"}}, {tmdbId:"112972", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0002001", born:date('1888-09-12'), name:"Maurice Chevalier", bio:"Maurice Auguste Chevalier (September 12, 1888 – January 1, 1972) was a French actor, cabaret singer and entertainer.  He is perhaps best known for his signature songs, including \"Livin' In The Sunlight\", \"Valentine\", \"Louise\", \"Mimi\", and \"Thank Heaven for Little Girls\" and for his films, including The Love Parade, The Big Pond, The Smiling Lieutenant, One Hour with You and Love Me Tonight.  His trademark attire was a boater hat and tuxedo. \n\nChevalier was born in Paris...", died:date('1972-01-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zABRw3iRFqqKV0xB3Z3VcsJDfad.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/112972"}}, {tmdbId:"1943", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0569410", born:date('1913-11-05'), name:"John McGiver", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJohn Irwin McGiver (November 5, 1913 – September 9, 1975) was a character actor who made more than a hundred appearances in television and motion pictures over a two-decade span from 1955 to 1975. \n\nThe owl-faced, portly actor with the mid-Atlantic accent was known for his performances as the religious fanatic Mr...", died:date('1975-09-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/beFNp5X9L5KQUspLPDcVLlJWIyA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1943"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"21457", properties:{bornIn:"Tupelo, Mississippi, USA", imdbId:"0000062", born:date('1935-01-08'), name:"Elvis Presley", bio:"Elvis Aaron Presley (January 8, 1935 – August 16, 1977) was one of the most popular American singers of the 20th century.  A cultural icon, he is widely known by the single name Elvis.  He is often referred to as the \"King of Rock and Roll\" or simply \"the King\". \n\nBorn in Tupelo, Mississippi, Presley moved to Memphis, Tennessee, with his family at the age of 13...", died:date('1977-08-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6YzYARfQO9a2mCEXNhLFuqKMAW6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21457"}}, {tmdbId:"5764", properties:{bornIn:"Vienna, Austria-Hungary, now Austria", imdbId:"0957645", born:date('1916-02-05'), name:"Jean-Pierre Zola", died:date('1979-01-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rw2Dgl0wTLYWqSvpElqehHsFBxh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5764"}}, {tmdbId:"5765", properties:{imdbId:"0785792", name:"Adrienne Servantie", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rDGoKY8amKDL5YyRlwQCNbYyqnb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5765"}}, {tmdbId:"5767", properties:{imdbId:"0773723", name:"Betty Schneider", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qw4AzLOmiDgS60DnHyMJA1sCR41.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5767"}}, {tmdbId:"27440", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0673749", born:date('1919-11-10'), name:"François Périer", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nFrançois Périer, (10 November 1919 – 29 June 2002), born François Pillu in Paris, was a French actor. \n\nHe made over 110 film and TV appearances between 1938 and 1996.  He was also prominent in the theatre.  Among his most notable parts was that of Hugo in the first production of Jean-Paul Sartre's Les Mains Sales in 1948.  He was the narrator of the French-language version of Fantasia...", died:date('2002-06-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aTgZII5M2ZW936lQJIUh94wQTFV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27440"}}, {tmdbId:"543085", properties:{bornIn:"Rome, Italy ", imdbId:"0555807", born:date('1926-08-18'), name:"Franca Marzi", died:date('1989-03-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/u385UEcDZjrZGUrcAXNJpdOD8jD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/543085"}}, {tmdbId:"125357", properties:{imdbId:"0336582", born:date('1928-02-02'), name:"Dorian Gray", died:date('2011-02-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yfpyOFqx9Lz15eBxhIHkC4FM74r.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/125357"}}, {tmdbId:"34470", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0948714", born:date('1912-03-23'), name:"Jeff York", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJeff York (March 23, 1912 - October 11, 1995) was an American film and television actor who began his career in the late 1930s using his given name Granville Owen Schofield.  He was also sometimes credited as Jeff Yorke. \n\nDuring his early career, the tall, dark haired actor was a natural to play characters such as Pat Ryan in the 1940 serial Terry and the Pirates and was given the lead in the 1940 film Li'l Abner...", died:date('1995-10-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mEq8UDwnnPwopoanaLHN357wNsM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34470"}}, {tmdbId:"27747", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0175200", born:date('1921-04-10'), name:"Chuck Connors", bio:"​Chuck Connors (April 10, 1921 – November 10, 1992) was an American actor, writer, and professional basketball and baseball player.  His best known role from his forty-year film career was Lucas McCain in the 1960s ABC hit Western series The Rifleman. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Chuck Connors, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1992-11-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lTVYSb6Vcx7024kA4VgTtMPp49Q.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27747"}}, {tmdbId:"124879", properties:{bornIn:"Santa Ana, California, USA", imdbId:"0707251", born:date('1917-01-29'), name:"John Raitt", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJohn Emmett Raitt (January 19, 1917 – February 20, 2005) was an American actor and singer best known for his performances in musical theater...", died:date('2005-02-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/upsBk262wTxvceBApVKM94r4RpN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/124879"}}, {tmdbId:"124880", properties:{bornIn:"New Bedford, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0359776", born:date('1924-12-24'), name:"Carol Haney", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nCarol Haney (December 24, 1924 – May 10, 1964) was an American dancer and actress.  After assisting Gene Kelly in choreographing films, Haney won a Tony Award for her role in The Pajama Game.  She then shifted to choreography, being nominated for three more Tonys for her choreography work on Broadway...", died:date('1964-05-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jfaLF3cJLFYr8f64wllmaj6F5F0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/124880"}}, {tmdbId:"30278", properties:{bornIn:"New Rochelle, New York, USA", imdbId:"0289376", born:date('1905-02-04'), name:"Eddie Foy Jr.", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEddie Foy Jr.  (February 4, 1905 - July 15, 1983) was an American character actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Eddie Foy Jr...", died:date('1983-07-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lgfqFD8GtvQDsBMwPuMNu9ia1lW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30278"}}, {tmdbId:"14575", properties:{bornIn:"Mineola, New York, USA", imdbId:"0629539", born:date('1928-12-10'), name:"Barbara Nichols", bio:"Barbara Marie Nickerauer (December 10, 1928 - October 5, 1976), better known by her stage name, Barbara Nichols, was an American actress and model, who became prominent in the 1950s and 1960s for playing brassy, comic roles in film and television...", died:date('1976-10-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1sgk7EqBUInEGT1uBLbhNE92njs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14575"}}, {tmdbId:"55449", properties:{imdbId:"0680097", born:date('1927-01-10'), name:"Lee Philips", died:date('1999-03-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2KfPg0pcdgPSNRKi2BItvBEjoBq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55449"}}, {tmdbId:"119342", properties:{bornIn:"Balcombe, Sussex, England", imdbId:"0395004", born:date('1898-07-14'), name:"David Horne", died:date('1970-03-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7FkB36qWz6EFz3sl1lWtGjaidLt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/119342"}}, {tmdbId:"18762", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0818215", born:date('1937-07-16'), name:"Jeremy Spenser", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/u1LwaYWPaxfa7rc7j6qju39T3vT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18762"}}, {tmdbId:"20399", properties:{imdbId:"0861345", born:date('1882-10-24'), name:"Sybil Thorndike", died:date('1976-06-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/a32kzcTI7WMuo8WJBXwZt6962dt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20399"}}, {tmdbId:"84659", properties:{bornIn:"Tacoma, Washington, USA", imdbId:"0656712", born:date('1922-09-16'), name:"Janis Paige", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Janis Paige (born as Donna Mae Tjaden, September 16, 1922, Tacoma, Washington) is an American film, musical theatre and television actress.  She began singing in public from the age of five in local amateur shows.  She then moved to Los Angeles after graduating from high school and then got a job as a singer at the Hollywood Canteen during World War II. \n\nThe Canteen, which was a studio-sponsored gathering spot for servicemen, is where Warner Bros...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/onXWK9cPJBiCk9yU4tqkop6SMAd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/84659"}}, {tmdbId:"6649", properties:{bornIn:"Stockholm, Stockholms län, Sweden", imdbId:"0085038", born:date('1909-11-13'), name:"Gunnar Björnstrand", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGunnar Björnstrand (13 November 1909 – 26 May 1986) was a Swedish actor known for his frequent work with writer/director Ingmar Bergman.  He was born in Stockholm.  He appeared in over 120 films. \n\nBjörnstrand at first had trouble finding work but got an engagement in Helsinki with his wife 1936-1938.  Back in Stockholm he met Ingmar Bergman, at that time a mostly unknown theatre director...", died:date('1986-05-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vkEY3nex3G0PMMnJ11Kamt4yod.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6649"}}, {tmdbId:"6656", properties:{bornIn:"Stockholm, Stockholms län, Sweden", imdbId:"0252345", born:date('1920-02-08'), name:"Bengt Ekerot", bio:"Nils Bengt Folke Ekerot was a Swedish actor and director.  He had several important roles in Swedish films, but he became immortalized in 1957 when he starred in Ingmar Bergman's The Seventh Seal, portraying Death as a white-faced man in a black cloak, an archetype that has influenced the representation of Death in countless instances in film and other media since then.  All in all Bengt Ekerot appeared in 35 feature films and directed 7 from 1940 to 1968...", died:date('1971-11-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4UxoMzIdE9PR4THNr3U2PL17veu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6656"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"6658", properties:{bornIn:"Malmö, Skåne län, Sweden", imdbId:"0691555", born:date('1908-05-31'), name:"Nils Poppe", died:date('2000-06-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qPXSktfOnVn2zlGFSoYUn8BQUhf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6658"}}, {tmdbId:"2201", properties:{bornIn:"Lund, Skåne län, Sweden", imdbId:"0001884", born:date('1929-04-10'), name:"Max von Sydow", bio:"Max von Sydow (10 April 1929-8 March 2020) was a Swedish actor.  He also held French citizenship since 2002.  He starred in many films and had supporting roles in dozens more.  He performed in films filmed in many languages, including Swedish, Norwegian, English, Italian, German, Danish, French and Spanish...", died:date('2020-03-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nWtTRLZunptwUDyiLo8yZDQ2HqK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2201"}}, {tmdbId:"6657", properties:{bornIn:"Kungsholmen, Stockholm, Stockholms län, Sweden", imdbId:"0000761", born:date('1935-11-11'), name:"Bibi Andersson", bio:"Her artistic dreams came early in life and were further supported by her older sister Gerd Andersson who became a ballet dancer at the Royal Opera and made her acting debut in 1951.  Bibi, on the other side, had to make do with bit parts and commercials.  She debuted in Dum-Bom (1953), playing against Nils Poppe.  Eventually, she was able to start at the Royal Dramatic Theatre's acting school in 1954...", died:date('2019-04-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6EGqmWOR3R3jv3IgrEZmCjTAVGv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6657"}}, {tmdbId:"8742", properties:{bornIn:"Sollefteå, Västernorrlands län, Sweden", imdbId:"0862026", born:date('1926-01-27'), name:"Ingrid Thulin", bio:"Ingrid Lilian Thulin (Swedish pronunciation: [ˈɪŋːrɪd tɵˈliːn]; 27 January 1926 – 7 January 2004) was a Swedish film actress. \n\nThulin was born in Sollefteå, Ångermanland, northern Sweden, the daughter of Nanna (née Larsson) and Adam Thulin, a fisherman.  She took ballet lessons as a girl and was accepted by The Royal Dramatic Theatre (\"Dramaten\") in Stockholm 1948...", died:date('2004-01-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3bK4vBwxyRU6cIfQzsjxOnqnT4W.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8742"}}, {tmdbId:"8608", properties:{bornIn:"Washington, North Carolina, United States", imdbId:"0358069", born:date('1923-03-24'), name:"Murray Hamilton", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMurray Hamilton (March 24, 1923 – September 1, 1986) was an American stage, screen, and television actor who appeared in such memorable films as The Hustler, The Graduate and Jaws...", died:date('1986-09-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/g586NceO9Vcor4LmlqWY5Mv0hTF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8608"}}, {tmdbId:"129994", properties:{bornIn:"New Haven, Connecticut, U.S.", imdbId:"0809514", born:date('1930-02-20'), name:"Patricia Smith", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Patricia Smith Lasell (February 20, 1930 – January 2, 2011) was an American actress who appeared in film and television roles from the early 1950s through the 1990s. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Patricia Smith (actress), licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2011-01-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dFk2zSIf8l0zcQ3hxNXteTGdn5b.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/129994"}}, {tmdbId:"129995", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0732397", born:date('1912-12-09'), name:"Bartlett Robinson", died:date('1986-03-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lzyyrYAIq9ZjZMs8xYAh350eb2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/129995"}}, {tmdbId:"3150", properties:{bornIn:"Bronx, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000348", born:date('1925-06-03'), name:"Tony Curtis", bio:"Tony Curtis (June 3, 1925 – September 29, 2010) was an American film actor whose career spanned six decades, but had his greatest popularity during the 1950s and early 1960s.  He acted in over 100 films in roles covering a wide range of genres, from light comedy to serious drama.  In his later years, Curtis made numerous television appearances. \n\nAlthough his early film roles were partly the result of his good looks, by the later half of the 1950's he became a notable and strong screen presence...", died:date('2010-09-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4aSmN9M4BbFJbNaMSnjGJHffehQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3150"}}, {tmdbId:"14572", properties:{bornIn:"Leesburg, Florida, United States", imdbId:"0365893", born:date('1938-08-26'), name:"Susan Harrison", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Susan Harrison (born August 26, 1938 in Leesburg, Florida) is an American actress.  She is most famous for her appearance in the 1957 film noir classic Sweet Smell of Success as the sister for whom Burt Lancaster has an unhealthy affection as well as in The Twilight Zone episode \"Five Characters in Search of an Exit...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6zDf2O60k7UrSsfo3rWRbaKv5Lb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14572"}}, {tmdbId:"14573", properties:{bornIn:"Detroit, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0590398", born:date('1931-12-28'), name:"Martin Milner", bio:"Martin Milner (1931–2015) was an American actor best known for his performances on Adam-12 and Route 66...", died:date('2015-09-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2sEL4PauMRhLGnOyVwYtw5QP1YL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14573"}}, {tmdbId:"109411", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0422015", born:date('1885-12-30'), name:"Edwin Jerome", died:date('1959-09-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yNBHxLMMrS8kSedeZX9UuSJmHk3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/109411"}}, {tmdbId:"37469", properties:{bornIn:"East Chicago, Indiana, USA", imdbId:"0658133", born:date('1926-11-01'), name:"Betsy Palmer", bio:"Betsy Palmer (November 1, 1926 – May 29, 2015) was an American actress, best known as a regular panelist on the game show I've Got a Secret and later for playing Pamela Voorhees in the slasher film Friday the 13th...", died:date('2015-05-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/MAUKhwThCVlwxcbXX2AhZuX2Jg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/37469"}}, {tmdbId:"105633", properties:{imdbId:"0712935", born:date('1944-07-21'), name:"Michel Ray", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/f9YhZADuPRJ43hIw25nGNyga1iF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/105633"}}, {tmdbId:"14505", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0831905", born:date('1913-03-03'), name:"Harold J. Stone", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Harold J.  Stone (March 3, 1913 – November 18, 2005) was an American film and television character actor. \n\nBorn Harold Hochstein to a Jewish acting family, he began his career on Broadway in 1939 and appeared in five plays in the next six years, including One Touch of Venus and Stalag 17, following which he made his motion picture debut in the Alan Ladd film noir classic The Blue Dahlia (1946)...", died:date('2005-11-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/caNcgDTJP7J311sCWMhxFN1iNHU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14505"}}, {tmdbId:"91638", properties:{bornIn:"Seattle, Washington, USA", imdbId:"0558663", born:date('1926-01-08'), name:"Kerwin Mathews", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nKerwin Mathews (January 8, 1926 – July 5, 2007) was an American actor best known for playing the titular heroes in The 7th Voyage of Sinbad (1958), The Three Worlds of Gulliver (1960) and Jack the Giant Killer (1962). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Kerwin Mathews, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2007-07-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/m1sBtAUgD1qg9YNsvqF36sMVpuQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/91638"}}, {tmdbId:"861", properties:{bornIn:"Houston, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0335497", born:date('1933-11-25'), name:"Kathryn Grant", bio:"Kathryn Crosby (born November 25, 1933) is an American actress and singer who also performed under the stage-name Kathryn Grant. \n\nBorn Olive Kathryn Grandstaff in Houston, Texas, she graduated from the University of Texas at Austin with a Bachelor of Fine Arts in 1955.  Two years later she became Bing Crosby's second wife.  The couple had three children, Harry, Mary Frances, and Nathaniel.  She appeared as a guest star on her husband's 1964–1965 ABC sitcom The Bing Crosby Show...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/c739OZ40Czy0D3Q2fCj9npNmh8X.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/861"}}, {tmdbId:"41214", properties:{bornIn:"Plainfield, Indiana, USA", imdbId:"0875861", born:date('1919-02-12'), name:"Forrest Tucker", bio:"Forrest Tucker was an American screen and television actor who appeared in nearly a hundred films...", died:date('1986-10-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yqdE1cqCXWhLTgIRHDgqHJMrJlY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41214"}}, {tmdbId:"87513", properties:{bornIn:"Melbourne, Australia", imdbId:"0114982", born:date('1913-07-23'), name:"Coral Browne", bio:"Coral Browne was an Australian stage and screen actress...", died:date('1991-05-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qedlTPM2tk5ZIcv3y1inUod66tt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/87513"}}, {tmdbId:"8632", properties:{bornIn:"Lincoln, California, USA", imdbId:"0163939", born:date('1914-03-19'), name:"Fred Clark", bio:"Fred Clark was an American stage, screen, radio, and television actor...", died:date('1968-12-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wyy3p7yZEjXk73Uwne2HGAjttre.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8632"}}, {tmdbId:"20602", properties:{bornIn:"Trenton, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0468237", born:date('1919-01-23'), name:"Ernie Kovacs", bio:"Ernie Kovacs (January 23, 1919 – January 13, 1962) was an American comedian and actor...", died:date('1962-01-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/z1CYO4WexaP3bAj0BhuoKhxEeOS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20602"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"56138", properties:{bornIn:"Hutchinson, Kansas, U.S.", imdbId:"0181080", born:date('1933-11-03'), name:"Aneta Corsaut", died:date('1995-11-06'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56138"}}, {tmdbId:"56139", properties:{bornIn:"Riverside, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0746505", born:date('1920-08-21'), name:"Earl Rowe", died:date('2002-02-01'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56139"}}, {tmdbId:"34209", properties:{bornIn:"Denver, Colorado, USA", imdbId:"0398250", born:date('1886-02-10'), name:"Olin Howland", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nOlin Ross Howland (February 10, 1886 – September 20, 1959) was an American film and theatre actor. \n\nHowland was born in Denver, Colorado, to Joby A.  Howland, one of the youngest enlisted participants in the Civil War, and Mary C.  Bunting.  His older sister was the famous stage actress Jobyna Howland. \n\nFrom 1909 to 1927, Howland appeared on Broadway in musicals, occasionally performing in silent films...", died:date('1959-09-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tQ7PbeH4KAhDWD70AKVR7ZInc8e.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34209"}}, {tmdbId:"76519", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0002147", born:date('1931-07-11'), name:"Tab Hunter", bio:"Arthur Andrew Gelien (née Kelm; July 11, 1931 – July 8, 2018), known professionally as Tab Hunter,  was an American actor, singer, producer and author...", died:date('2018-07-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tB7qHETdoR5ktEroMJEDDOQXawo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/76519"}}, {tmdbId:"54122", properties:{bornIn:"Culver City, Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0893862", born:date('1925-01-13'), name:"Gwen Verdon", bio:"Gwyneth Evelyn \"Gwen\" Verdon was an American actress and dancer.  She won four Tony Awards for her musical comedy performances, and served as an uncredited choreographer's assistant and specialty dance coach for theater and film.  With flaming red hair and a quaver in her voice, Verdon was a critically acclaimed performer on Broadway from the 1950s-70s...", died:date('2000-10-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/grudYGaOSskLbTWfRimaObOnTOb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54122"}}, {tmdbId:"4093", properties:{bornIn:"New Orleans, Louisiana, USA", imdbId:"0001827", born:date('1914-12-02'), name:"Ray Walston", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRay Walston (December 2, 1914 – January 1, 2001) was an American stage, television and film actor best known as the title character on the 1960s situation comedy My Favorite Martian.  In addition, he was also known for his role as high school teacher Mr.  Hand in the 1982 film Fast Times at Ridgemont High and Judge Henry Bone on the drama series Picket Fences...", died:date('2001-01-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6ZJSMeqL7mFr0462q7imrlWFxTZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4093"}}, {tmdbId:"866", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0114612", born:date('1892-05-30'), name:"Russ Brown", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRussell Brown (May 30, 1892; Philadelphia, Pennsylvania – October 19, 1964; Englewood, New Jersey) was an American Tony Award-winning actor of stage and film...", died:date('1964-10-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/t1lcK0xgH5aCIrLvG8nndSMlmCo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/866"}}, {tmdbId:"70794", properties:{bornIn:"Gourock, Scotland", imdbId:"0834320", born:date('1927-11-07'), name:"Melissa Stribling", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMelissa Stribling (7 November 1927 – 22 March 1992) was a Scottish film and television actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Melissa Stribling, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1992-03-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ust0gMTkH1GN70FKy5UHwUom7BL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70794"}}, {tmdbId:"70564", properties:{bornIn:"Golden, British Columbia, Canada", imdbId:"0654433", born:date('1925-01-17'), name:"Patricia Owens", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPatricia Owens (17 January 1925, Golden, British Columbia - 31 August 2000, Lancaster, California) was a Canadian-born American actress, working in Hollywood.  She appeared in about 40 films and 10 TV episodes in a career lasting from 1943 to 1968. \n\nCanadian-born actress Patricia Owens moved to England with her parents in 1933, and ten years later, at age 18, she made her motion-picture debut in Val Guest's musical comedy Miss London Ltd...", died:date('2000-08-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3QOT7VgaeYU7883771FB6BA6yoi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70564"}}, {tmdbId:"20603", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0320006", born:date('1897-12-09'), name:"Hermione Gingold", bio:"Hermione Gingold (9 December 1897 – 24 May 1987) was an English actress known for her sharp-tongued, eccentric persona, an image enhanced by her sharp nose and chin, as well as her deepening voice, a result of vocal nodes which her mother reportedly encouraged her not to remove.  She starred on stage, on radio, in films, on television, and in recordings.  She also appeared on the NBC interview program Here's Hollywood...", died:date('1987-05-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/e7wwMLsdW0AAYVqVmKvApMoQpAP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20603"}}, {tmdbId:"78853", properties:{imdbId:"0645120", born:date('1927-07-03'), name:"Carol Ohmart", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9HjqNHPiabjLbTDOv1Ys8HFKVi9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78853"}}, {tmdbId:"78852", properties:{imdbId:"0519160", born:date('1927-12-17'), name:"Richard Long", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRichard Long  (December 17, 1927 – December 21, 1974) was an American actor better known for his leading roles in several ABC television series, including The Big Valley and Nanny and the Professor...", died:date('1974-12-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4jh5Wp4qi94ri6GfS8HOufC3jIQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78852"}}, {tmdbId:"78854", properties:{bornIn:" Sydney, New South Wales, Australia", imdbId:"0550701", born:date('1909-01-30'), name:"Alan Marshal", bio:"Alan Marshal (born Alan Marshal Willey; 29 January 1909 – 9 July 1961) was an actor who performed on stage in the United States and in Hollywood films...", died:date('1961-07-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vIPF0CyxC3iK3W8Z9vg8FStuGIQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78854"}}, {tmdbId:"16757", properties:{bornIn:" Rome, Italy", imdbId:"0000047", born:date('1934-09-20'), name:"Sophia Loren", bio:"Sophia Loren, OMRI (born Sofia Villani Scicolone; 20 September 1934) is an Italian actress. \n\nIn 1962, Loren won the Academy Award for Best Actress for her role in Two Women, along with 21 awards, becoming the first actress to win an Academy Award for a non-English-speaking performance.  Loren has won 50 international awards, including an Oscar, seven Golden Globe Awards, a Grammy Award, a BAFTA Award and a Laurel Award...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/94Kglg5dsAgOKG76230FFN7m6W3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16757"}}, {tmdbId:"16759", properties:{bornIn:"Fort Worth, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0405054", born:date('1924-08-10'), name:"Martha Hyer", bio:"Martha Hyer (August 10, 1924, Fort Worth, Texas - May 31, 2014, Santa Fe, New Mexico) was an American actress. \n\nShe attended Northwestern University and was a member of Pi Beta Phi fraternity.  After completing her education, she next appeared in The Locket in 1946...", died:date('2014-05-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/56HFKAZAQKLOpmDzbB4WhFOf0Ax.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16759"}}, {tmdbId:"14785", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0345340", born:date('1925-12-23'), name:"Harry Guardino", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nHarry Guardino (December 23, 1925—July 17, 1995) was an American actor whose career spanned from the early 1950s to the early 1990s.  In 1964, he was cast in a short-lived CBS series entitled The Reporter, a drama about a hard-hitting investigative journalist named Danny Taylor.  His principal co-star was Gary Merrill as city editor Lou Sheldon. \n\nBorn in Brooklyn, New York, Guardino appeared on stage, in films, and on television...", died:date('1995-07-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/t3uLoPdmTp7x07E4PLq0FcgDjoP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14785"}}, {tmdbId:"16420", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0095524", born:date('1917-06-18'), name:"Richard Boone", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRichard Allen Boone (June 18, 1917 – January 10, 1981) was an American actor who starred in over 50 films and was notable for his roles in Westerns and for starring in the TV series Have Gun – Will Travel. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Richard Boone, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1981-01-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3jr6nbojJHrDvc0xQFrGOBwXt0M.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16420"}}, {tmdbId:"111840", properties:{bornIn:"McKeesport, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0561049", born:date('1931-02-26'), name:"Peggy Maurer", died:date('2012-07-27'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/111840"}}, {tmdbId:"119381", properties:{bornIn:"Attleboro, Massachusetts, U.S.", imdbId:"0808473", born:date('1893-08-12'), name:"Howard Smith", bio:"Howard Irving Smith (August 12, 1893 in – January 10, 1968) was an American character actor with a 50-year career in vaudeville, theater, radio, films and television.  In 1938 he performed in Orson Welles's short-lived stage production and once-lost film, Too Much Johnson, and in the celebrated radio production, \"The War of the Worlds\".  He portrayed Charley in the original Broadway production of Death of a Salesman and recreated the role in the 1951 film version...", died:date('1968-01-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vvshXhclnmRG4HDTSK0t9rrV7yN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/119381"}}, {tmdbId:"14063", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0643000", born:date('1915-08-28'), name:"Simon Oakland", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nSimon Oakland (August 28, 1915 – August 29, 1983) was an American actor of stage, screen, and television. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Simon Oakland, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1983-08-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nA6CmjgGE6HKT2SGoQM87h5fu24.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14063"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"101768", properties:{bornIn:"Goshen, New York, USA", imdbId:"0898782", born:date('1924-05-03'), name:"Virginia Vincent", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ftTCV0sVhvckFF2QJzGYC8wuhTY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101768"}}, {tmdbId:"89534", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0130829", born:date('1915-02-18'), name:"Phyllis Calvert", bio:"Phyllis Calvert (18 February 1915 – 8 October 2002) was an English film, stage and television actress. \n\nBorn Phyllis Hannah Bickle in Chelsea, she trained at the Margaret Morris School of Dancing and performed from the age of ten, gaining her first film role at the age of 12, in The Arcadians (1927), also known as The Land of Heart's Desire.  Calvert performed in repertory theatre and in several films, before making her London stage debut in A Woman's Privilege in 1939...", died:date('2002-10-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6kBp7r6vYrJhdRMQHAtm62HgHhW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89534"}}, {tmdbId:"130942", properties:{imdbId:"0203008", born:date('1930-05-23'), name:"Michael David", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/130942"}}, {tmdbId:"96552", properties:{bornIn:"Fukagawa, Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0297869", born:date('1905-01-15'), name:"Kamatari Fujiwara", bio:"Kamatari Fujiwara (藤原 釜足 Fujiwara Kamatari, January 15, 1905 - December 21, 1985) was a Japanese actor. \n\nFujiwara was born in Tokyo, on January 15, 1905, in Tokyo, Japan.  Fujiwara's parents ran a printing business.  The business did not go well, so at the age of 10, Fujiwara started working at a local confectionery store.  By the age of 14 he had started selling timber for building and manufacturing in Shizuoka prefecture.  A year later he returned to Tokyo to study as a pharmacist...", died:date('1985-12-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3tP8kqLcrqvk7iCvOmI1S8M4rrw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96552"}}, {tmdbId:"30907", properties:{bornIn:"Kurume, Fukuoka, Japan", imdbId:"0297843", born:date('1912-01-08'), name:"Susumu Fujita", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSusumu Fujita (藤田 進  Fujita Susumu, 8 January 1912 – 23 March 1991) was a Japanese film and television actor.  He played the lead role in Akira Kurosawa's first feature, Sanshiro Sugata, and appeared other Kurosawa film including The Men Who Tread On the Tiger's Tail (as Togashi, commander of the border guards) and The Hidden Fortress (as General Tadokoro).  Later, he was a supporting actor in Ishirō Honda's Mothra vs.  Godzilla, among many other films...", died:date('1991-03-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sSnAxPTb4YEI3Mw15Y2isBbC22K.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30907"}}, {tmdbId:"83391", properties:{imdbId:"0366247", born:date('1938-10-20'), name:"Dolores Hart", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/glEohETEgIOmogPkWaOCya2x8DX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83391"}}, {tmdbId:"213493", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo - Japan", imdbId:"0847197", born:date('1926-10-20'), name:"Teiji Takahashi", died:date('1959-11-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/whFvr8JkrLLe2vWKGQxdHe3Cy2o.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/213493"}}, {tmdbId:"213497", properties:{bornIn:"Kanagawa, Japan", imdbId:"0595105", born:date('1917-01-28'), name:"Yûko Mochizuki", died:date('1977-12-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5TUdCo50ZN3aX8mYw152hBb9rqL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/213497"}}, {tmdbId:"1888164", properties:{name:"Danko Ichikawa", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1888164"}}, {tmdbId:"150341", properties:{bornIn:"Tucumán, Argentina", imdbId:"0530244", born:date('1924-06-20'), name:"Marga López", bio:"Marga López (21 June 1924 – 4 July 2005), born Catalina Margarita López Ramos, was an Argentine-born Mexican actress.  Born in Argentina, she later acquired Mexican nationality...", died:date('2005-07-03'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/150341"}}, {tmdbId:"9768", properties:{bornIn:"Águilas, Murcia, Región de Murcia, Spain", imdbId:"0704719", born:date('1926-03-08'), name:"Francisco Rabal", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nFrancisco Rabal (March 8, 1926 – August 29, 2001), perhaps better known as Paco Rabal, was a Spanish actor born in Águilas, a small town in the province of Murcia, Spain. \n\nIn 1936, after the Spanish Civil War broke out.  Rabal and his family left Murcia and moved to Madrid.  Young Francisco had to work as a street salesboy and in a chocolate factory.  When he was 13 years old, he left school to work as an electrician at Estudios Chamartín...", died:date('2001-08-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4SXneju54P5QjrF7ZmAlU09HHxX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9768"}}, {tmdbId:"150342", properties:{bornIn:"Mexico City, Mexico.", imdbId:"0479872", born:date('1928-12-08'), name:"Rita Macedo", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRita Macedo was a Mexican actress who performed during the Golden Age of Mexican cinema.  She was nominated for an Ariel Award for her 1956 performance in \"Ensayo de un crimen\" and in 1991 for a TVyNovelas Prize for \"Alcanzar una estrella\".  She won the Best Actress Ariel Award in 1972 for \"Tú, yo, y nosotros\".  She also was instrumental in bringing many works of international writers to the Mexican stage...", died:date('1993-12-06'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/150342"}}, {tmdbId:"116992", properties:{bornIn:"Mexico City, Distrito Federal, Mexico", imdbId:"0529964", born:date('1925-01-15'), name:"Ignacio López Tarso", bio:"Ignacio López Tarso (born Ignacio López López on January 15, 1925 in Mexico City, Mexico) is a Mexican actor of stage, film and television.  He has acted in about 50 films and appeared in documentaries and in one short feature.  In 2007 he was given the Ariel de Oro lifetime achievement award.  He has also been honored multiple times at the TVyNovelas Awards...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/116992"}}, {tmdbId:"67676", properties:{bornIn:"Gerrards Cross, Buckinghamshire, England", imdbId:"0603336", born:date('1914-09-20'), name:"Kenneth More", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nKenneth Gilbert More CBE (20 September 1914 – 12 July 1982) was a highly successful English film actor during the post-World War II era and starred in many feature films, often in the role of an archetypal carefree and happy-go-lucky middle-class gentleman. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Kenneth More, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1982-07-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sN8z4fBdpVrWl8Ly1Qf7An6t6wQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67676"}}, {tmdbId:"31297", properties:{bornIn:"Reading, Berkshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0021004", born:date('1930-12-16'), name:"Ronald Allen", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRonald Allen (16 December 1930 [some sources say 1934] in Reading, Berkshire – 18 June 1991) was an established English character actor. \n\nHe studied at Leighton Park School in Reading and trained at the Royal Academy of Dramatic Art (RADA) in London, worked in repertory theatre, had a season at the Old Vic, London and made several films, including the Titanic classic A Night to Remember, as well as achieving fame as a soap opera star...", died:date('1991-06-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vIhLDwvBxGA8t8V5O9jkKXjGEpQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31297"}}, {tmdbId:"67677", properties:{imdbId:"0044010", born:date('1914-12-11'), name:"Robert Ayres", died:date('1968-11-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kuzstgrmOCgU1f0NzciK1Zi81qL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67677"}}, {tmdbId:"9907", properties:{bornIn:"Plaistow, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0000303", born:date('1925-08-22'), name:"Honor Blackman", bio:"Honor Blackman (22 August 1925 - 5 April 2020) was an English actress, known for the roles of Cathy Gale in The Avengers (1962–64) and Bond girl Pussy Galore in Goldfinger (1964)...", died:date('2020-04-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gPx90Zfv3zb4llA3oFCN2AVXrw7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9907"}}, {tmdbId:"69025", properties:{bornIn:"Havana, Cuba", imdbId:"0668626", born:date('1944-11-22'), name:"Felipe Pazos", bio:"Felipe Pazos (September 27, 1912 – February 26, 2001) was a Cuban economist who initially supported the Cuban Revolution of Fidel Castro, but became disillusioned with the increasingly radical nature of the revolutionary government.  Born in Havana, Pazos earned a doctorate from the University of Havana in 1938.  He was a member of the Cuban delegation to the 1944 Bretton Woods conference...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69025"}}, {tmdbId:"69026", properties:{bornIn:"Hillsboro, Illinois", imdbId:"0068772", born:date('1905-02-12'), name:"Harry Bellaver", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.  Harry Bellaver (February 12, 1905 – August 8, 1993) was an American stage, film and television actor who appeared in many roles from the 1930s through the 1980s.    Description above from the Wikipedia article Harry Bellaver, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1993-08-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vHR1bbJD1L1by6QduzHqXOQJzIk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69026"}}, {tmdbId:"69027", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York United States", imdbId:"0224614", born:date('1921-06-04'), name:"Don Diamond", bio:"Brooklyn-born Don Diamond's most famous role is probably that of the scheming and ambitious, but inept and somewhat cowardly, underling Crazy Cat to Frank DeKova's Chief Wild Eagle in the cult western comedy series F Troop (1965).  By the time he got that role he had been an actor for quite some time, starting out in radio in the early 1940s, where he discovered that he had a knack for picking up dialects, especially Spanish...", died:date('2011-06-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vLQfRVZjABqcDty9yF3X7rWz65q.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69027"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"41279", properties:{bornIn:"Wendell, North Carolina, USA", imdbId:"0906966", born:date('1928-01-13'), name:"Gregory Walcott", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGregory Walcott (born January 13, 1928) is an American television and film actor.  He is perhaps best known for having appeared in the 1959 Ed Wood film, the cult classic Plan 9 from Outer Space. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Gregory Walcott, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2015-03-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fzEZM9TbG88zFA37jFszPEn20Kt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41279"}}, {tmdbId:"65498", properties:{bornIn:"Tennessee, USA", imdbId:"0571958", born:date('1929-05-01'), name:"Mona McKinnon", died:date('1990-03-12'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/65498"}}, {tmdbId:"65499", properties:{imdbId:"0601146", born:date('1913-07-15'), name:"Duke Moore", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDuke Moore, (July 15, 1913 as James Moore – November 16, 1976), is an American actor who has the distinction of spending his entire on-screen career in productions by Edward D.  Wood, Jr. ...", died:date('1976-11-16'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/65499"}}, {tmdbId:"65500", properties:{bornIn:"Rochester, New York, USA", imdbId:"0444740", born:date('1896-12-30'), name:"Tom Keene", bio:"Tom Keene (1896–1963) was an American actor known mostly for his roles in B Westerns...", died:date('1963-08-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rrOqF1UWdMtOmgOVYOxDrknK0NN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/65500"}}, {tmdbId:"40914", properties:{bornIn:"Kniaże, Polska", imdbId:"0194193", born:date('1927-11-03'), name:"Zbigniew Cybulski", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nZbigniew Cybulski Polish pronunciation: [ˈzbiɡɲɛf t͡sɨˈbulskʲi] (November 3, 1927 – January 8, 1967) was a Polish actor, one of the best-known and most popular personalities of the post-World War II history of Poland. \n\nZbigniew Cybulski was born November 3, 1927 in a small village of Kniaże near Śniatyń, Poland (now a part of Sniatyn Raion, Ivano-Frankivsk Oblast, Ukraine).  After World War II he joined the Theatre Academy in Kraków...", died:date('1967-01-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zGZA2ccRwff9IcMLqQsJg2AlN8V.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/40914"}}, {tmdbId:"40619", properties:{bornIn:"Warsaw, Mazowieckie, Poland", imdbId:"0473109", born:date('1939-02-07'), name:"Ewa Krzyzewska", bio:"Ewa Krzyzewska was born on February 7, 1939 in Kraków, Malopolskie, Poland.  She was an actress, known for Ashes and Diamonds (1958), Pharaoh (1966) and Zbrodniarz i panna (1963).  She was married to Boleslaw Kwiatkowski.  She died on July 30, 2003 in Spain...", died:date('2003-07-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2by3Ejb4kSOwc9ok8i0fCyzvyLW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/40619"}}, {tmdbId:"40915", properties:{imdbId:"0953664", name:"Waclaw Zastrzezynski", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3UwkbU9uZy23jb5egcIIiidL8RD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/40915"}}, {tmdbId:"40916", properties:{bornIn:"Warszawa, Poland", imdbId:"0668044", born:date('1925-01-01'), name:"Adam Pawlikowski", died:date('1976-01-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hBFx4aSxTo9AQEIDB6j8NbeGivf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/40916"}}, {tmdbId:"11163", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0768334", born:date('1935-08-05'), name:"John Saxon", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJohn Saxon (born Carmine Orrico; August 5, 1935 – July 25, 2020) was an American actor and martial artist who worked on more than 200 projects during a span of 60 years.  Saxon is known for his work in Westerns and horror movies, often playing police officers and detectives...", died:date('2020-07-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rQh2ddJYtP3x2g1mnlFBQz547FO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11163"}}, {tmdbId:"89808", properties:{bornIn:"Bayonne, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0000364", born:date('1942-04-23'), name:"Sandra Dee", bio:"Sandra Dee was born Alexandria Zuck on April 23, 1942 in Bayonne, New  Jersey.  Her mother envisioned a show business career for her daughter  and would often lie about her age in order to get Sandy where she wanted  to go.  For example, her mother enrolled her in school early so she  could have a head start.  Sandy was only four years old when she entered  the second grade.  Sandra was an extremely pretty young lady, which  enabled her to get into modeling...", died:date('2005-02-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9sT0fVpSwJOxGwjPDMpY4XveDdu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89808"}}, {tmdbId:"5251", properties:{bornIn:"Newark, New Jersey, USA ", imdbId:"0912001", born:date('1920-09-18'), name:"Jack Warden", bio:"Jack Warden was an American television and film character actor, born John Warden Lebzelter in Newark, New Jersey.  He was twice nominated for an Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor for Shampoo (1975) and Heaven Can Wait (1978).  He also received a BAFTA nomination for the former movie and won an Emmy for his performance in Brian's Song (1971)...", died:date('2006-07-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hSShXiYMfRpMByaB5euZ59qCKN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5251"}}, {tmdbId:"14529", properties:{bornIn:"Goldfield, Nevada, USA", imdbId:"0223290", born:date('1917-04-09'), name:"Brad Dexter", bio:"Brad Dexter (born Veljko Soso; April 9, 1917 – December 12, 2002) was an American actor and film producer.  He is known for tough-guy and western roles including the 1960 film The Magnificent Seven (1960) and producing several films for Sidney J.  Furie such as Lady Sings the Blues.  He is also known for a short marriage to Peggy Lee, a friendship with Marilyn Monroe and for saving Frank Sinatra from drowning...", died:date('2002-12-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sZTKZ63BNQSRCW5Kt4GGSRUiEoY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14529"}}, {tmdbId:"62881", properties:{bornIn:"New York, New York, USA", imdbId:"0449734", born:date('1931-11-15'), name:"John Kerr", bio:"John Grinham Kerr (November 15, 1931 – February 2, 2013), was an American actor and lawyer.  He made his Broadway debut in 1953 in Mary Coyle Chase's Bernardine, a high-school comedy for which he won a Theatre World Award.  In 1953-54, he received critical acclaim as a troubled prep school student in Robert Anderson's play Tea and Sympathy.  In 1954, he won a Tony Award for his performance, and he starred in the film version in 1956...", died:date('2013-02-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nCpJUyot5fb9R1ySzA0NIeWMZvC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/62881"}}, {tmdbId:"5731", properties:{bornIn:"London, England", imdbId:"0375738", born:date('1904-01-04'), name:"Tom Helmore", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nTom Helmore (4 January 1904 – 12 September 1995) was an English film actor.  He appeared in over 50 films between 1927 and 1972, including three directed by Alfred Hitchcock. \n\nHe was born in London and died in Longboat Key, Florida...", died:date('1995-09-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3cXsDyWScmmOVeSAh50mee2nH6G.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5731"}}, {tmdbId:"21874", properties:{bornIn:" North Shields, Tyne-and-Wear, England, UK", imdbId:"0949241", born:date('1919-11-19'), name:"Alan Young", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAlan Young  (born November 19, 1919) is an English-Canadian actor, best known for his television role in Mister Ed and as the voice of Scrooge McDuck.  During the 1940s and 1950s he starred in his own shows on radio and television...", died:date('2016-05-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vhHipWAikSU1P8WoARKv5cnqZui.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21874"}}, {tmdbId:"189843", properties:{bornIn:"Karachi, British India", imdbId:"0861185", born:date('1931-06-08'), name:"June Thorburn", bio:"June Thorburn (8 June 1931 – 4 November 1967) was a popular English actress whose career was cut short by her death in an air crash.  She was pregnant with her third child when returning to London from Spain on Iberia Airlines Flight 062 when it crashed into Blackdown Hill, Sussex, killing all 37 people aboard...", died:date('1967-11-04'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/189843"}}, {tmdbId:"29427", properties:{bornIn:"Finchley, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0856103", born:date('1911-07-14'), name:"Terry-Thomas", bio:"Terry-Thomas (1911–1990) was an English comic actor.  He was famous for his portrayal of disreputable members of the upper classes...", died:date('1990-01-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8DISWwlhkrzq2SL7vjnsd5iE1f2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29427"}}, {tmdbId:"855", properties:{bornIn:"Quincy, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0001665", born:date('1935-12-14'), name:"Lee Remick", bio:"Lee Ann Remick (December 14, 1935 – July 2, 1991) was an American actress.  She was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Actress for the 1962 film Days of Wine and Roses, and for the 1966 Tony Award for Best Actress in a Play for her Broadway theatre performance in Wait Until Dark. \n\nRemick made her film debut in 1957 in A Face in the Crowd.  Her other notable film roles include Anatomy of a Murder (1959), Wild River (1960), The Detective (1968), The Omen (1976), and The Europeans (1979)...", died:date('1991-07-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/90TB8k134kouctQkNU641aHkiHm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/855"}}, {tmdbId:"856", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001262", born:date('1930-08-28'), name:"Ben Gazzara", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBiagio Anthony Gazzarra (August 28, 1930 – February 3, 2012), known as Ben Gazzara, was an American film, stage, and television actor and director.  His best known films include Anatomy of a Murder (1959), Voyage of the Damned (1976), Inchon (1981), Road House (1989), The Big Lebowski (1998), Happiness (1998), The Thomas Crown Affair (1999), Summer of Sam (1999), Dogville (2003) and Paris, je t'aime (2006)...", died:date('2012-02-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eGvi9AtDsxB3HYarc3hB512R0Gn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/856"}}, {tmdbId:"13752", properties:{bornIn:"Krishnanagar, Bengal Presidency, British India", imdbId:"0154164", born:date('1935-01-19'), name:"Soumitra Chatterjee", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSoumitra Chatterjee or Soumitra Chattopadhyay (Shoumitro Chôttopaddhae; born 19 January 1935) is an Indian Bengali film and stage actor and poet.  He is best known for his collaborations with Oscar-winning film director Satyajit Ray, with whom he worked in fourteen films, and his constant comparison with the Bengali cinema screen idol Uttam Kumar, his contemporary leading man of the 1960s and 1970s...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dX0OzIQD4mF7Z7A9sNmHrKzIOJC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13752"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"13753", properties:{bornIn:"Kanpur, Uttar Pradesh, India", imdbId:"0846616", born:date('1946-12-08'), name:"Sharmila Tagore", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/plWY8GzysrR8bBwpfO0PoJjr7IB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13753"}}, {tmdbId:"13755", properties:{imdbId:"0149845", name:"Alok Chakravarty", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vnc7YuyyGzw9KCko8Hsg66ktHpT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13755"}}, {tmdbId:"13756", properties:{imdbId:"0611575", name:"Swapan Mukherjee", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13756"}}, {tmdbId:"10019", properties:{bornIn:"Haifa, Israel", imdbId:"0361823", born:date('1931-09-20'), name:"Haya Harareet", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nHaya Harareet (sometimes credited as Haya Hararit; born 20 September 1931 in Haifa) is an Israeli actress. \n\nHarareet began her career in Israeli films with Hill 24 Doesn't Answer (1955), but her most widely seen performance in international cinema was as Esther in Ben Hur (1959) opposite Charlton Heston.  She also starred in Edgar G.  Ulmer's Journey Beneath The Desert (1961) with Jean-Louis Trintignant...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gurUharioqQL9f9zdTXbt4fJLPE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10019"}}, {tmdbId:"10020", properties:{bornIn:"Glengormley, Northern Ireland, UK", imdbId:"0000963", born:date('1931-07-04'), name:"Stephen Boyd", bio:"Stephen Boyd, born William Millar, was a Northern Irish/American stage and screen actor.  As a teenager  he joined the Ulster Group Theatre where he learned the tasks of the theatre.   In 1956  he toured North America performing \"A Streetcar Named Desire\" in the lead role as Stanley Kowalski. \n\nBoyd who appeared in around 60 feature films, most notably in the role of Messala in the 1959 film \"Ben-Hur\"...", died:date('1977-06-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/64KLW9XGjGLUl3RbtjfMRPFEDYu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10020"}}, {tmdbId:"3382", properties:{bornIn:"Redding, Connecticut, USA", imdbId:"0486136", born:date('1933-11-28'), name:"Hope Lange", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nHope Lange (November 28, 1933 – December 19, 2003) was an American film, stage, and television actress. \n\nLange was nominated for the Best Supporting Actress Golden Globe and the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress for her portrayal of Selena Cross in the 1957 film Peyton Place.  In 1969 and 1970, she won the Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Lead Actress in a Comedy Series for her role as Carolyn Muir in the sitcom The Ghost &amp; Mrs.  Muir...", died:date('2003-12-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6G38YvZ3JqlVfw0H6irEtGqqhgj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3382"}}, {tmdbId:"145861", properties:{imdbId:"0662646", born:date('1932-10-28'), name:"Suzy Parker", died:date('2003-05-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kkm5jQVen2cNH4EDq3r33eKvPJF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/145861"}}, {tmdbId:"16089", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0263645", born:date('1922-01-02'), name:"Jason Evers", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJason Evers (January 2, 1922 - March 13, 2005) was an American actor. \n\nEvers was born Herb Evers in New York City, New York.  After quitting high school to join the United States Army, Evers was so inspired by stars like John Wayne (whom he would later appear with in The Green Berets) that he decided to try acting.  A stint on Broadway led to Hollywood, where his first big break was the 1960 NBC series western Wrangler...", died:date('2005-03-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jbm0AiJvYowMoaDOEZQCcAoiEOx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16089"}}, {tmdbId:"27842", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0200012", born:date('1918-04-22'), name:"Anthony La Penna", bio:"Anthony La Penna was born on April 22, 1918 in New York, New York, USA...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4uWNXxq3846bUtneOcDA08N6qKD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27842"}}, {tmdbId:"110729", properties:{imdbId:"0483641", name:"Adele Lamont", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/110729"}}, {tmdbId:"115334", properties:{bornIn:"San Mateo, California, USA", imdbId:"0890215", born:date('1938-02-23'), name:"Diane Varsi", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nDiane Marie Antonia Varsi (February 23, 1938 – November 19, 1992) was an American film actress best known for her performances in Peyton Place – her film debut, and for which she was nominated for an Academy Award – and the cult film Wild in the Streets.  She left Hollywood in order to pursue personal and artistic aims, notably at Bennington College in Vermont, where she studied poetry with poet and translator Ben Belitt, among others...", died:date('1992-11-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7fH2WgvC5ffpFt1eEzzw1Ysqv22.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/115334"}}, {tmdbId:"18647", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0226947", born:date('1930-04-14'), name:"Bradford Dillman", bio:"Bradford Dillman was an American stage, screen, and television actor, as well as an author starred in the taut crime drama Compulsion (1959).   The lanky, dark-haired Dillman also played Robert Redford's best friend J. J.  in The Way We Were (1973). \n\nDillman also appeared opposite Clint Eastwood in the Dirty Harry films The Enforcer (1976) and Sudden Impact (1983)...", died:date('2018-01-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hMu3bG27HBzlGGtAKFl2B4IY3Xr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18647"}}, {tmdbId:"83783", properties:{bornIn:"Belfast, Ireland", imdbId:"0789185", born:date('1885-04-15'), name:"Albert Sharpe", died:date('1970-02-13'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83783"}}, {tmdbId:"83129", properties:{bornIn:"Blackpool, England, UK", imdbId:"0613130", born:date('1934-09-28'), name:"Janet Munro", bio:"Born Janet Neilson Horsburgh, Janet Munro, was an English actress, best known for Darby O'Gill and the Little People (1959) for which she won a Golden Globe Award.  and Life for Ruth (1962), for which she received a BAFTA Film Award nomination.   She died aged 38 of a heart condition...", died:date('1972-12-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wVOisYojJx2FhC8B3wqfnsDqTSA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83129"}}, {tmdbId:"738", properties:{bornIn:"Fountainbridge, Edinburgh, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0000125", born:date('1930-08-25'), name:"Sean Connery", bio:"Sir Thomas Sean Connery (born 25 August 1930) is a Scottish actor and producer who has won an Academy Award, two BAFTA Awards (one of them being a BAFTA Academy Fellowship Award) and three Golden Globes. \n\nConnery is best-known for portraying the character James Bond, starring in seven Bond films between 1962 and 1983 (six \"official\" EON productions films and the non-official Kevin McClory-helmed Thunderball remake, Never Say Never Again)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cd0zKpYJ6eSutkrZkLFxQCGjhnF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/738"}}, {tmdbId:"1157304", properties:{bornIn:"Dublin, Ireland ", imdbId:"0640618", born:date('1899-04-26'), name:"Jimmy O'Dea", died:date('1965-01-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5lWqtLn39gSyZKwVDww12ub3IZA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1157304"}}, {tmdbId:"26142", properties:{bornIn:"Passaic, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0674012", born:date('1938-05-12'), name:"Millie Perkins", bio:"Perkins was working as a receptionist at a New York City advertising agency when she caught the eye of a visiting photographer with a resultant career as a model; by 1958 Perkins was an international cover girl.  However, in 1958, she was vigorously pursued, and then selected, to appear in her first film, in the title role of The Diary of Anne Frank...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/go1PNFwnfuUuMcVLSKpua2dUIRk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/26142"}}, {tmdbId:"6679", properties:{bornIn:"Avoca, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0000937", born:date('1938-02-20'), name:"Richard Beymer", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGeorge Richard Beymer, Jr.  (born February 20, 1938) is an American actor known for playing Tony in the 1961 film version of West Side Story and Ben Horne on the 1990 television series Twin Peaks. \n\n \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Richard Beymer, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jXRpmeLvK9YNHzNHHf3AKKrukJ0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6679"}}, {tmdbId:"100318", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, United States", imdbId:"0201626", born:date('1936-06-08'), name:"James Darren", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nJames William Ercolani, known by his stage name James Darren, is an American television and film actor, television director, and singer.  He wanted to be an actor and studied in New York City with Stella Adler for a number of years.  He would also occasionally sing although he later said \"I wasn't really a singer.  I was a kid in Philly whose dad would take him to bars and nightclubs and I would get up and sing two songs...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/finbHXyPodyPEb1j2ETRFpAl8ee.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100318"}}, {tmdbId:"19153", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, U.S.A.", imdbId:"0731772", born:date('1923-09-09'), name:"Cliff Robertson", bio:"Was an American actor with a film and television career that spans half of a century.  Robertson won the 1968 Academy Award for Best Actor for his role in the movie Charly.  His most recent film roles were as \"Uncle Ben Parker\" in the Spider-Man film series. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Cliff Robertson, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2011-09-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pLDmdmRIRvfGDt08Oj8zLORwz12.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19153"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"267962", properties:{bornIn:"Cheniménil, France", imdbId:"0728938", born:date('1927-02-24'), name:"Emmanuelle Riva", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nEmmanuelle Riva was a French actress, best known for her roles in the films Hiroshima mon amour and Amour. \n\nIn 2013, Riva won the BAFTA Award and the César Award for her lead role in Michael Haneke's Amour as Anne Laurent, and was nominated for the Academy Award for the same role. [2][3] She had previously been nominated for a BAFTA Award in 1960 for Hiroshima mon amour, and had won Best Actress at the Venice Film Festival in 1962 for Thérèse Desqueyroux...", died:date('2017-01-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pDPGIHy001boz5yBBWTjNUf4aOO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/267962"}}, {tmdbId:"25466", properties:{bornIn:"Chōshi, Chiba, Japan", imdbId:"0645402", born:date('1920-06-13'), name:"Eiji Okada", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEiji Okada (13 June 1920 Chōshi, Chiba, Japan – 14 September 1995 Japan) was a Japanese film actor.  Okada served in the Japanese army during World War II, and was a miner and traveling salesman before becoming an actor...", died:date('1995-09-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/psadJTgSSEqaVKDpsk40tb5ypbg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25466"}}, {tmdbId:"44020", properties:{imdbId:"0202072", name:"Stella Dassas", bio:"Stella Dassas is an actress, known for Hiroshima Mon Amour (1959), Veronica and Her Dunce (1958) and Snobbarna (1961)...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/44020"}}, {tmdbId:"44021", properties:{bornIn:"Saint-Eugène, Algiers, Algeria", imdbId:"0053289", born:date('1911-10-10'), name:"Pierre Barbaud", bio:"Pierre Barbaud was born on October 10, 1911 in Saint-Eugène, Algiers, Algeria.  He was a composer and actor, known for Hiroshima Mon Amour (1959), Den sommaren (1961) and La Pointe Courte (1955).  He died on September 10, 1990 in Nice, Alpes-Maritimes, France...", died:date('1990-09-10'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/44021"}}, {tmdbId:"10029", properties:{bornIn:"St. Pancras, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0603682", born:date('1909-08-20'), name:"André Morell", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAndré Morell (20 August 1909 – 28 November 1978; sometimes credited as Andre Morell) was a British actor.  He appeared frequently in theatre, film and on television from the 1930s to the 1970s.  His best known screen roles were as Professor Bernard Quatermass in the BBC Television serial Quatermass and the Pit (1958–59), and as Doctor Watson in the Hammer Film Productions version of The Hound of the Baskervilles (1959)...", died:date('1978-11-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3YpAUiuLp9ZXL67W99W2XYdJ3se.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10029"}}, {tmdbId:"70510", properties:{imdbId:"0484762", name:"Marla Landi", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMarla Landi (born 1939) is an Italian-born British film actress. \n\nHer major roles included Mary in Across the Bridge (1957) and Cecille Stapleton in Hammer's The Hound of the Baskervilles (1959). \n\n'Marla Landi' was her stage name. \n\nShe was a Play School presenter and presented Parliamo Italiano. \n\nShe was also a top photographic model and had a number of magazine covers including Vogue, Harper's Bazaar and Tatler...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8LAC8RnztAKpoT1VAjDEZPrzs7n.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70510"}}, {tmdbId:"7304", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0001260", born:date('1931-04-08'), name:"John Gavin", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJohn Gavin (April 8, 1931 – February 9, 2018) was an American actor who was the United States Ambassador to Mexico (1981–86) and the president of the Screen Actors Guild (1971–73).  He was best known for his performances in the films Imitation of Life (1959), Spartacus (1960), Psycho (1960), and Thoroughly Modern Millie (1967), playing leading roles in a series of films for producer Ross Hunter. \n\nBorn Juan Vincent Apablasa Jr...", died:date('2018-02-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/Y0MsuRKkmYZNwoFteh76pX4IsF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7304"}}, {tmdbId:"131742", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, U.S.A", imdbId:"0463435", born:date('1936-11-11'), name:"Susan Kohner", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ukGHFINonI8ZKSgHnYUBAjjye5N.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/131742"}}, {tmdbId:"44881", properties:{bornIn:"Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0006428", born:date('1928-08-11'), name:"Arlene Dahl", bio:"Arlene Carol Dahl (born August 11, 1925) is an American film actress and former MGM contract star, who achieved notability during the 1950s.  She is the mother of actor Lorenzo Lamas. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Arlene Dahl, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1FtddzZbFT1Amp7BR5gnrSxN6UW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/44881"}}, {tmdbId:"6930", properties:{bornIn:"Hollywood, California, USA", imdbId:"0000832", born:date('1938-02-25'), name:"Diane Baker", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.     Diane Carol Baker (born February 25, 1938) is an American actress who has appeared in motion pictures and on television since 1959.   Description above from the Wikipedia article Diane Baker, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/604pSqQ2EuieEv1P2BErJoCE5hJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6930"}}, {tmdbId:"40185", properties:{bornIn:"Powderly, Kentucky, USA", imdbId:"0078940", born:date('1926-07-26'), name:"James Best", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJames Best (born Jewel Franklin Guy; July 26, 1926 – April 6, 2015) was an American television, film, character, voice, and stage actor, as well as a writer, director, acting coach, artist, college professor, and musician, whose career spanned seven decades of television.  He appeared as a guest on various country music and talk shows...", died:date('2015-04-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nqeXfqjJdM8gUKIky2tVE0IrHIS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/40185"}}, {tmdbId:"248787", properties:{name:"Ingrid Goude", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/248787"}}, {tmdbId:"30554", properties:{bornIn:"Lamar, Colorado, USA", imdbId:"0193411", born:date('1916-07-02'), name:"Ken Curtis", died:date('1991-04-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/q8QfxJsVdx0aGJ6l64DZIzhQv0l.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30554"}}, {tmdbId:"999981", properties:{imdbId:"0572741", name:"Gordon McLendon", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/999981"}}, {tmdbId:"3830", properties:{bornIn:"Marshalltown, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0781029", born:date('1938-11-13'), name:"Jean Seberg", bio:"Jean Dorothy Seberg (November 13, 1938 – August 30, 1979) was an American actress who lived half her life in France. \n\nShe appeared in 34 films in Hollywood and in Europe, including Saint Joan, Bonjour Tristesse, Breathless, Lilith, The Mouse That Roared, Moment to Moment, A Fine Madness, Paint Your Wagon, Airport, Macho Callahan, and Gang War in Naples. \n\nShe was also one of the best-known targets of the FBI COINTELPRO project...", died:date('1979-08-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mNW6MJ5YAiFWAnH9pCmi0PjKXc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3830"}}, {tmdbId:"73245", properties:{bornIn:"St. Pancras, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0367156", born:date('1908-01-08'), name:"William Hartnell", bio:"William Henry Hartnell (8 January 1908 – 23 April 1975), also known as Billy Hartnell or Bill Hartnell, was an English actor.  Hartnell played the first incarnation of the Doctor in Doctor Who, from 1963 to 1966.  He was also known for his roles as Sergeant Grimshaw, the title character of the first Carry On film, Carry On Sergeant in 1958, and Company Sergeant Major Percy Bullimore in the sitcom The Army Game from 1957 until 1958, and again in 1960...", died:date('1975-04-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jt6xUpjrgTWvu5T5ehFAm5hUBKr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/73245"}}, {tmdbId:"5962", properties:{bornIn:"Lille, Nord, Nord-Pas-de-Calais, France", imdbId:"0299014", born:date('1928-05-11'), name:"Yvonne Furneaux", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nYvonne Furneaux (born Elisabeth Yvonne Scarcherd; 11 May 1928, Lille, Nord-Pas-de-Calais, France) is a French film actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Yvonne Furneaux, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qbwcJG0oiCS6IefC6ZwqjxVZ3nX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5962"}}, {tmdbId:"69249", properties:{bornIn:"Birmingham, England, UK", imdbId:"0125952", born:date('1911-01-31'), name:"Eddie Byrne", died:date('1981-08-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mWivEyJoTjfhOZ1m4EQJGn9lCZh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69249"}}, {tmdbId:"70131", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0619938", born:date('1932-12-13'), name:"Tatsuya Nakadai", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nTatsuya Nakadai (仲代 達矢 Nakadai Tatsuya,  born Motohisa Nakadai December 13, 1932) is a Japanese leading film actor.  He became a star after he was discovered working as a Tokyo shop clerk by filmmaker Masaki Kobayashi during the early 1950s.  He became the favorite leading man of internationally-acclaimed director Akira Kurosawa after a well publicized fallout between Kurosawa and the legendary Toshirō Mifune...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eHeai93QELb3gbLHz0WwEbFf6kv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70131"}}, {tmdbId:"85307", properties:{bornIn:"Nara, Japan", imdbId:"0033171", born:date('1930-01-15'), name:"Michiyo Aratama", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nMichiyo Aratama (新珠 三千代, Aratama Michiyo, 15 January 1930 – 17 March 2001) was a Japanese actress who appeared in leading and supporting roles in such films as Hiroshi Inagaki's Chushingura, Kihachi Okamoto's Samurai Assassin and Sword of Doom, and Masaki Kobayashi's Kwaidan, Hymn to a Tired Man and The Human Condition trilogy. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Michiyo Aratama, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2001-03-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1iaZBOpb6NAr9naDph4y4kUhPWU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85307"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"213492", properties:{bornIn:"Osaka, Japan", imdbId:"0034836", born:date('1932-04-03'), name:"Ineko Arima", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5mgUhLZMpC4w8NaDD34bANXUmeV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/213492"}}, {tmdbId:"2639", properties:{bornIn:"Newark, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0001693", born:date('1924-07-04'), name:"Eva Marie Saint", bio:"Eva Marie Saint is an American actress who has starred in films, on Broadway, and on television in a career spanning seven decades, she's known for bringing emotional depth and complexity to her roles, in which she generally played women who appear fragile but have great inner strength...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1uBwAKbToanmjBgJHRpbnMnuWh2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2639"}}, {tmdbId:"39816", properties:{bornIn:"Hartford, Connecticut, USA", imdbId:"0003225", born:date('1901-03-25'), name:"Ed Begley", bio:"Ed Begley was a Tony and Academy Awards-winning American stage, screen, radio, and television actor...", died:date('1970-04-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yagsfcxUsMRoMW0nf4GFDNxIzgp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/39816"}}, {tmdbId:"55890", properties:{bornIn:"Cambridge, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0639613", born:date('1936-02-14'), name:"Joan O'Brien", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/txhFaBy7io6XIvya2CEii2UXc6Q.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55890"}}, {tmdbId:"58414", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0581277", born:date('1925-12-09'), name:"Dina Merrill", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nDina Merrill was an American actress and socialite...", died:date('2017-05-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/98RkUmwtc1qAOSQ6SGdl8itUZ3b.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/58414"}}, {tmdbId:"274344", properties:{bornIn:"Porto Alegre, Rio Grande do Sul, Brazil", imdbId:"0578039", born:date('1931-09-07'), name:"Breno Mello", died:date('2008-07-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3Ff0HeKPoMVeUd2PxSdhgEgATNi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/274344"}}, {tmdbId:"17581", properties:{bornIn:"Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0206026", born:date('1934-01-03'), name:"Marpessa Dawn", bio:"Marpessa Dawn (January 3, 1934 — August 25, 2008), also known as Gypsy Marpessa Dawn Menor was an American-born French actress, singer, and dancer.  Born in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania of African-American and Filipino heritage, she is best-remembered for her role as \"Eurydice\" in the film Black Orpheus.  She and her fellow lead from that film, Brazilian actor Breno Mello, died just 42 days apart in 2008, both from heart attacks...", died:date('2008-08-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dpKZQWEwqSrt3y2zP44RERoZvHW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/17581"}}, {tmdbId:"1116071", properties:{name:"Fausto Guerzoni", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1116071"}}, {tmdbId:"10355", properties:{imdbId:"0489425", born:date('1935-01-01'), name:"Martin LaSalle", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10355"}}, {tmdbId:"10356", properties:{bornIn:"Södermalm, Stockholm, Stockholms län, Sweden", imdbId:"0338126", born:date('1943-06-21'), name:"Marika Green", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMarika Nicolette Green (born 21 June 1943) is a Swedish-French actress.  She is mostly famous for appearing in Pickpocket (1959) and Emmanuelle (1974).  Born in Södermalm, Stockholm, Stockholm County, she left Sweden for France in 1953.  She played the lead female role in Robert Bresson's Pickpocket at the age of 16.  She is the aunt of Eva Green and older sister of Walter Green, husband of Marlène Jobert...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/l1BmEYbCrU5lxi0c2TIA2vk8ZPk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10356"}}, {tmdbId:"10357", properties:{bornIn:"Rovigo, French Algeria", imdbId:"0701798", born:date('1920-06-20'), name:"Jean Pélégri", bio:"Jean Pélégri (June 20, 1920 – September 24, 2003) was a writer and professor of literature.  Of French descent, he was born in Algeria, but left as part of the diaspora of French colonists referred to as pied-noirs following the Algerian War. \n\nHe was friends with many Algerian writers (such as Mohammed Dib and Kateb Yacine) and, like Jean Sénac, Pélégri considered himself to be one of them; he always saw himself as an \"Algerian at heart\"...", died:date('2003-09-24'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10357"}}, {tmdbId:"10358", properties:{imdbId:"0768739", name:"Dolly Scal", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10358"}}, {tmdbId:"40206", properties:{bornIn:"Tulsa, Oklahoma, USA", imdbId:"0709704", born:date('1920-02-26'), name:"Tony Randall", bio:"Tony Randall (February 26, 1920 – May 17, 2004) was a U. S.  actor, comic, producer and director...", died:date('2004-05-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8UyliAMUnMOsLdwBYz455QjESoi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/40206"}}, {tmdbId:"9626", properties:{bornIn:"Temple, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0001800", born:date('1931-02-06'), name:"Rip Torn", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nElmore Rual Torn, Jr.  (born February 6, 1931), better known as Rip Torn, was an American actor of stage, screen and television. \n\nTorn received an Academy Award nomination as Best Supporting Actor for his role in the 1983 film Cross Creek.  His work includes the role of Artie, the producer, on The Larry Sanders Show, for which he was nominated for six Emmy Awards, winning in 1996...", died:date('2019-07-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cvB3Z3HRX48LS0DNQndeSUQBSwS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9626"}}, {tmdbId:"1933", properties:{bornIn:"Detroit, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0000577", born:date('1928-10-01'), name:"George Peppard", bio:"George Peppard, Jr.  (October 1, 1928 – May 8, 1994) was an American film and television actor. \n\nPeppard secured a major role when he starred alongside Audrey Hepburn in Breakfast at Tiffany's (1961), and later portrayed a character based on Howard Hughes in The Carpetbaggers (1964).  On television, he played the title role of millionaire insurance investigator and sleuth Thomas Banacek in the early-1970s mystery series Banacek.  He played Col...", died:date('1994-05-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/i5kxTQ9GSGKY6CaI8F3cdwoF3KD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1933"}}, {tmdbId:"1653", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0529543", born:date('1944-05-28'), name:"Jean-Pierre Léaud", bio:"Jean-Pierre Léaud is a French actor, best known for playing Antoine Doinel in François Truffaut's series of films about that character, beginning with The 400 Blows (1959).  He also worked with Aki Kaurismäki, Pier Paolo Pasolini, Jacques Rivette, and Tsai Ming-liang.  He is a significant figure of the French New Wave, having appeared in eight films by Jean-Luc Godard and seven by François Truffaut...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bpzGSYITgIZTkHbhC9VPOho4LnK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1653"}}, {tmdbId:"1654", properties:{bornIn:"Ceret, France", imdbId:"0561158", born:date('1929-03-27'), name:"Claire Maurier", bio:"Claire Maurier (born Odette-Michelle-Suzanne Agramon; March 27, 1929) is a French actress who has appeared in more than 90 films since 1947. \n\nMaurier was born Odette-Michelle-Suzanne Agramon on March 27, 1929 in the French commune of Céret, in the Pyrénées-Orientales region, which is in the southwest of France. \n\nShe started her acting career in small film roles at the end of the 1940s...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rlMYKpiTIzZCw2ee3YGENJZQKPC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1654"}}, {tmdbId:"1655", properties:{bornIn:"Sèvres, Seine-et-Oise [now Hauts-de-Seine], France", imdbId:"0753716", born:date('1911-04-09'), name:"Albert Rémy", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAlbert Rémy was a French actor best known for his supporting roles in François Truffaut's first two feature films.  He played Antoine Doinel's father in The 400 Blows and Charlie Koller's (Charles Aznavour) brother in Shoot the Piano Player.  He also appeared in Marcel Carné's Les Enfants du Paradis, John Frankenheimer's The Train and Rene Clement's Is Paris Burning?...", died:date('1967-01-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/k0IZ9pO6Be6pR0mRtdzVyPeuM3f.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1655"}}, {tmdbId:"31896", properties:{bornIn:"Santa Ana, California, USA ", imdbId:"0357020", born:date('1933-06-20'), name:"Brett Halsey", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBrett Halsey (born June 20, 1933, in Santa Ana, California), is an American film actor, sometimes credited as Montgomery Ford.  He is best known as the original John Abbott on the soap opera The Young and the Restless, a role he held from May 1980 to March 1981, before being replaced by Jerry Douglas. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Brett Halsey, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mPfkWXhMJTiNEOAGVBNxngM9YW9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31896"}}, {tmdbId:"16063", properties:{bornIn:"Kent, England", imdbId:"0291301", born:date('1926-02-16'), name:"David Frankham", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nDavid Frankham (born 16 February 1926) is a film and television actor.  After serving in India and Malaya in WWII, Frankham worked first as a news reader, and then a writer, interviewer and producer for the BBC from 1948 through 1955. \n\nIn 1955 Frankham moved to Hollywood to pursue a career as an actor.  He soon found work, appearing on five episodes of the live television program Matinee Theater...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pwp6ytllu8ZJPrPGCcemZbjxlHD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16063"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"100589", properties:{bornIn:"Rawalpindi, British India", imdbId:"0840330", born:date('1908-10-23'), name:"John Sutton", bio:"John Sutton (October 22, 1908 – July 10, 1963) who was born in Rawalpindi, British India (now Rawalpindi, Punjab, Pakistan) was actor of British parentage...", died:date('1963-07-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rjrGLNykcBxaBe4Hg5H7bNd9JTa.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100589"}}, {tmdbId:"4300", properties:{bornIn:"Teaneck, New Jersey, U.S.", imdbId:"0625699", born:date('1940-05-08'), name:"Ricky Nelson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEric Hilliard Nelson (May 8, 1940 – December 31, 1985), better known as Ricky Nelson or Rick Nelson, was an American singer-songwriter, instrumentalist, and actor.  He placed fifty-three songs on the Billboard Hot 100 between 1957 and 1973, including nineteen top-ten hits, and was inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame on January 21, 1987...", died:date('1985-12-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iV49nm6JthHK9PRMXKhamnrbGjy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4300"}}, {tmdbId:"4301", properties:{bornIn:"Kulm, North Dakota, USA", imdbId:"0001141", born:date('1931-09-30'), name:"Angie Dickinson", bio:"An American actress.  She has appeared in more than fifty films, including Rio Bravo, Ocean's 11, Dressed to Kill and Pay It Forward, and starred on television as Sergeant Suzanne \"Pepper\" Anderson on the 1970s crime series Police Woman. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article  Angie Dickinson, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qYOZXjxyySMrbcsOGblgPKpKuxG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4301"}}, {tmdbId:"14729", properties:{bornIn:"Jonischkis, Lithuania", imdbId:"0002131", born:date('1928-10-01'), name:"Laurence Harvey", bio:"Laurence Harvey (1 October 1928 – 25 November 1973) was a Lithuanian-born actor who achieved fame in British and American films...", died:date('1973-11-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iSKq4IsgLEDdzboqtthn2RWkJlv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14729"}}, {tmdbId:"97571", properties:{imdbId:"0780765", born:date('1935-09-28'), name:"Heather Sears", died:date('1994-01-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/er8zgQAYNom6c8HFjGXJO5OOQHI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/97571"}}, {tmdbId:"14372", properties:{imdbId:"0938372", born:date('1902-04-20'), name:"Donald Wolfit", died:date('1968-02-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eRs3Bo7H3D2JwXbiurg9W40CgJb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14372"}}, {tmdbId:"83130", properties:{bornIn:"Louisville, Kentucky, U.S.", imdbId:"0456565", born:date('1941-12-10'), name:"Tommy Kirk", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nThomas Lee \"Tommy\" Kirk (born December 10, 1941) is a former American actor, and later a businessman. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Tommy Kirk, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3UFrcRbz8D37jAzpIOyeh0ZN1Ck.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83130"}}, {tmdbId:"82777", properties:{bornIn:"Utica, New York, USA", imdbId:"0002088", born:date('1942-10-21'), name:"Annette Funicello", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nAnnette Joanne Funicello (October 22, 1942 – April 8, 2013) is an American singer and actress.  She was Walt Disney's most popular cast member of the original Mickey Mouse Club, and went on to appear in a series of beach party films. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article  Annette Funicello , licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2013-04-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9N8sJ5qLX6mjqJVAtpw5JnDwXyj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82777"}}, {tmdbId:"67287", properties:{imdbId:"0182250", born:date('1930-04-05'), name:"Mary Costa", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mg6gsqucGQZi6ASO5UZt0l6nj5e.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67287"}}, {tmdbId:"67288", properties:{bornIn:"Indianapolis - Indiana - USA", imdbId:"0794301", born:date('1921-07-06'), name:"Bill Shirley", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nWilliam Jesse \"Bill\" Shirley (July 6, 1921 – August 27, 1989) was an American actor and tenor/lyric baritone singer who later became a Broadway theatre producer.  He is perhaps best known as the speaking and singing voice of Prince Phillip in Walt Disney's 1959 animated classic Sleeping Beauty. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia Bill Shirley licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1989-08-27'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67288"}}, {tmdbId:"93105", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0250724", born:date('1921-07-29'), name:"Richard Egan", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRichard Egan (July 29, 1921 - July 20, 1987) was an American actor.  In some films he is credited as Richard Eagan. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Richard Egan, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1987-07-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gGFqcXl4lSjnX1KsmzjInFEv5Eg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/93105"}}, {tmdbId:"7686", properties:{bornIn:"Seneca, South Dakota, USA", imdbId:"0263393", born:date('1909-03-20'), name:"Judith Evelyn", died:date('1967-05-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7TaDGrr3oTrU5AVkYXDmVvxZy4e.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7686"}}, {tmdbId:"81481", properties:{bornIn:"Hollywood, Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0382718", born:date('1931-07-29'), name:"Darryl Hickman", bio:"Darryl Gerard Hickman (28 July 1931) is an American film and television actor, television executive, and acting coach...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ab7cYxqRyhwV4e1E8sBeHyESAXc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81481"}}, {tmdbId:"96458", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0194036", born:date('1926-07-20'), name:"Patricia Cutts", died:date('1974-09-06'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96458"}}, {tmdbId:"24300", properties:{bornIn:"Saint-Hippolyte, France", imdbId:"0562831", born:date('1936-01-22'), name:"Juliette Mayniel", bio:"Juliette Mayniel (born 22 January 1936) is a French actress.  She appeared in 35 films and television shows between 1958 and 1978.  At the 10th Berlin International Film Festival, she won the Silver Bear for Best Actress for her role in the film The Fair.   From 1964-68 she was the partner of the Italian actor Vittorio Gassman with whom she had a son, Alessandro, an actor too...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/a8LJbBAIbjgJZmmJTJGP4ifrK46.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24300"}}, {tmdbId:"36212", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0726777", born:date('1901-02-14'), name:"Alexandre Rignault", died:date('1985-03-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gzGK1SG19jNSGPfgYLsWWP4dgei.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/36212"}}, {tmdbId:"3829", properties:{bornIn:"Neuilly-sur-Seine, Seine [now Hauts-de-Seine], France", imdbId:"0000901", born:date('1933-04-09'), name:"Jean-Paul Belmondo", bio:"Jean-Paul Belmondo (born 9 April 1933) is a French actor initially associated with the New Wave of the 1960s. \n\nBorn in Neuilly-sur-Seine, Hauts-de-Seine, west of Paris, Belmondo did not perform well in school, but developed a passion for boxing and football.  Belmondo made his amateur boxing debut on 10 May 1949 in Paris, France, when he knocked out Rene DesMarais in one round.  Belmondo's boxing career was undefeated, but brief...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1XNXClPazdrXenfwTnWkBEBqhBD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3829"}}, {tmdbId:"3573", properties:{bornIn:"Compiègne, Oise, France", imdbId:"0099429", born:date('1922-01-24'), name:"Daniel Boulanger", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.  Daniel Boulanger (Compiègne, Oise, 24 January 1922) is a French novelist, playwright, poet and screenwriter.  He has also played secondary roles in films and has been a member of the Académie Goncourt since 1983.  Description above from the Wikipedia article Daniel Boulanger , licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2014-10-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sdXg9TM9ox0ANO95CHpWUD9siUH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3573"}}, {tmdbId:"3832", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0400142", born:date('1930-03-27'), name:"Henri-Jacques Huet", died:date('2009-06-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/79xy417RrUaRcfHPxcqT9H7IQ5n.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3832"}}, {tmdbId:"16764", properties:{imdbId:"0378517", born:date('1948-12-02'), name:"Charles Herbert", died:date('2015-10-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sAygzGPy4JPLGr5pNwwUY3j4idL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16764"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"104810", properties:{imdbId:"0607507", born:date('1939-11-01'), name:"Jo Morrow", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/r0LLhUdYidFwV1IuoiqfQt4Ssna.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/104810"}}, {tmdbId:"22092", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, U.S.", imdbId:"0000811", born:date('1939-09-18'), name:"Frankie Avalon", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nFrankie Avalon (born September 18, 1940) is an American actor, singer, and former teen idol...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wReq9zPodyO5mM6fYhPauCMxNQY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/22092"}}, {tmdbId:"89162", properties:{imdbId:"0164153", born:date('1927-06-04'), name:"Ken Clark", died:date('2009-06-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sFZrOhdCbZPeuw0hsAZ5oLF76En.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89162"}}, {tmdbId:"89163", properties:{bornIn:"Kansas City, Missouri, U.S.", imdbId:"0896035", born:date('1928-08-26'), name:"Yvette Vickers", bio:"Yvette Vickers (born Yvette Iola Vedder) was an American actress, pin-up model and singer.  She attended the University of California, Los Angeles, and studied journalism.  While at UCLA, she took a class in acting and discovered that she enjoyed it, so she changed her major to drama.  She began making television commercials.   Her last film appearance was in the 1991 horror film, \"Evil Spirits...", died:date('2010-01-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nG7Pr9ac3u0dnm4TGX8QsDQuoMD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89163"}}, {tmdbId:"83811", properties:{imdbId:"0791629", born:date('1928-03-19'), name:"Jan Shepard", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/AbslRMg8iyNybznCg8CWa2Ps4Ru.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83811"}}, {tmdbId:"89165", properties:{imdbId:"0256523", name:"Michael Emmet", died:date('2009-01-01'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89165"}}, {tmdbId:"4961", properties:{bornIn:"Rome, Italy", imdbId:"0275213", born:date('1925-03-17'), name:"Gabriele Ferzetti", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nGabriele Ferzetti (born Pasquale Ferzetti on 17 March 1925 in Rome, Italy) is an Italian actor.  He has more than 160 credits to his name across film, television and stage.  His career was at its peak in the 1950s and 1960s. \n\nA prominent figure in Italian cinema since the 1950s, Ferzetti's first leading role came in 1950 in the film Lo Zappatore.  He portrayed Puccini twice in 1953 and 1954 in the films Puccini and Casa Ricordi respectively...", died:date('2015-12-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vQxVIzRZPAi37hZzpqqhd0fi5bh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4961"}}, {tmdbId:"41779", properties:{bornIn:"Rome, Italy", imdbId:"0900143", born:date('1931-11-03'), name:"Monica Vitti", bio:"Monica Vitti (born 3 November 1931) is an Italian actress most widely noted for her frosty expressiveness and starring roles during the early 1960s in films directed by Michelangelo Antonioni, her lover at that time. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article  Monica Vitti, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8BCb0bcKHLCYA7kE88BxRxyF483.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41779"}}, {tmdbId:"20882", properties:{bornIn:"Rome, Italy", imdbId:"0557159", born:date('1933-06-30'), name:"Lea Massari", bio:"Anna Maria Massetani better known as Lea Massari (born 30 June 1933) is an Italian actress.  When she was 22, she changed her name to Lea Massari after the death of her fiancé Leo.  She studied architecture in Switzerland.  Massari become a celebrity in art cinema for two roles, the missing girl Anna in Michelangelo Antonioni's L'avventura (1960), and as Clara, the mother of a sexually precocious 14 year old boy named Laurent (Benoît Ferreux) in Louis Malle's Murmur of the Heart (1971)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vufMNp3eqjkH7IWcNZ31LFwsHu4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20882"}}, {tmdbId:"38243", properties:{bornIn:" Paris, France", imdbId:"0087017", born:date('1927-06-02'), name:"Dominique Blanchar", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/y2HdZG6BMpNk1yosiTw7aP9AXmy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/38243"}}, {tmdbId:"90516", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, United States", imdbId:"0279472", born:date('1928-08-10'), name:"Eddie Fisher", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nEdwin John Fisher (August 10, 1928 – September 22, 2010), better known as Eddie Fisher, was an American singer and entertainer, who was one of the world's most famous and successful singers in the 1950s, selling millions of records and hosting his own TV show.  His divorce from his first wife, Debbie Reynolds, to marry his best friend's widow, Elizabeth Taylor, garnered scandalously unwelcome publicity at the time.  He was also married to Connie Stevens...", died:date('2010-09-22'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/90516"}}, {tmdbId:"78778", properties:{bornIn:"Manhattan, New York, USA", imdbId:"0314778", born:date('1904-10-06'), name:"Alex Gerry", died:date('1993-05-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4QZ2dhwYxtXZ8iEtcCPQUiAKJYs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78778"}}, {tmdbId:"78779", properties:{imdbId:"0165667", born:date('1922-08-17'), name:"Bob Clayton", died:date('1979-11-01'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78779"}}, {tmdbId:"78780", properties:{imdbId:"0762370", name:"Sonnie Sands", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78780"}}, {tmdbId:"14731", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0798328", born:date('1928-09-15'), name:"Henry Silva", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nHenry Silva (born September 15, 1928) is an American actor who has played a wide variety of movie roles. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Henry Silva, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lPXDv2K8tkFMnEQsDGmeIMSPxiq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14731"}}, {tmdbId:"5676", properties:{bornIn:"Fontana Liri, Latium, Italy", imdbId:"0000052", born:date('1924-09-28'), name:"Marcello Mastroianni", bio:"Marcello Vincenzo Domenico Mastroianni was an Italian film actor.  His honours have included British Film Academy Awards, Best Actor awards at the Cannes Film Festival and two Golden Globe Awards...", died:date('1996-12-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/u0Vsb6Hs7d0Hb6tKzdiwheCYjem.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5676"}}, {tmdbId:"5961", properties:{bornIn:"Malmö - Skåne län - Sweden", imdbId:"0001179", born:date('1931-09-29'), name:"Anita Ekberg", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nKerstin Anita Marianne Ekberg (born 29 September 1931 in Malmö, Skåne - died 11 January 2015 Rocca di Papa - Rome - Italy) was a Swedish model, actress and cult sex symbol.  She is best known for her role as Sylvia in the 1960 Federico Fellini film, La Dolce Vita, which features the legendary scene of her cavorting in Trevi Fountain alongside Marcello Mastroianni...", died:date('2015-01-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iSjTtIMfLncDc2E4TVbNrMCcMVP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5961"}}, {tmdbId:"5682", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0000733", born:date('1932-04-27'), name:"Anouk Aimée", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAnouk Aimée (born 27 April 1932) is a French film actress.  Aimée has appeared in 70 films since 1947. \n\nAimée was born Françoise Sorya Dreyfus in Paris, France, the daughter of actors Geneviève Sorya (née Durand) and Henri Murray (born Dreyfus). \n\nAimée began her film career in 1947 at age 14.  In 1958 she portrayed the tragic artist Jeanne Hébuterne in the film Les Amants de Montparnasse.  She later appeared in La dolce vita, 8½ and Jacques Demy's Lola...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9pPY3jiJ79wQ5pvLqVqlTlPnkZ6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5682"}}, {tmdbId:"24809", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, United States", imdbId:"0000839", born:date('1937-11-12'), name:"Ina Balin", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nIna Balin (November 12, 1937 – June 20, 1990) was an American actress on Broadway and in film. \n\nBorn as Ina Rosenberg to a Jewish family in Brooklyn, she first appeared on television on The Perry Como Show.  She also did summer stock, which led to roles on Broadway, and in 1959, she won the \"Theatre World Award\" for her performance in the Broadway comedy, A Majority of One, starring Gertrude Berg and Sir Cedric Hardwicke...", died:date('1990-06-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pLWJTp4QRh6yZwoA9thNgTC7LjI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24809"}}, {tmdbId:"83389", properties:{bornIn:"Bombay, Bombay Presidency, British India", imdbId:"0699120", born:date('1936-09-25'), name:"Juliet Prowse", bio:"Juliet Anne Prowse was a dancer, whose four-decade career included stage, television and film.  She was raised in South Africa, where her family emigrated after World War II.  Known for her attractive legs, she was described after her death as having \". . .  arguably the best legs since Betty Grable. \"\n\nIn her early twenties, she was dancing at a club in Paris when she was spotted by a talent agent and eventually signed to play the role of Claudine in the Walter Lang film Can-Can...", died:date('1996-09-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6KZ7n4SPQN5kJd7h2c5t2RP7guP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83389"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"78772", properties:{bornIn:"Seattle, Washington, United States", imdbId:"0412251", born:date('1934-12-11'), name:"Robert Ivers", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRobert Ivers, AKA Bob Ivers, (December 11, 1934 - 13 February 2003 was an American actor who appeared in films and television in the 1950s and 1960s. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Robert Ivers, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2003-02-13'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78772"}}, {tmdbId:"1212945", properties:{imdbId:"0235093", name:"James Douglas", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1Jkkf1Rg4mKp2oPUvHA7OlKimI7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1212945"}}, {tmdbId:"113640", properties:{bornIn:"Vancouver, Canada", imdbId:"0666304", born:date('1929-03-31'), name:"Lee Patterson", died:date('2007-02-14'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/113640"}}, {tmdbId:"6890", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois", imdbId:"0198941", born:date('1933-04-22'), name:"Mark Damon", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMark Damon (born Alan Harris on April 22, 1933, in Chicago, Illinois) is an American film actor and producer.  He started his career in his native country, appearing in such films as Young and Dangerous (1957) and Roger Corman's House of Usher.  In an attempt to boost his career, he relocated to Italy, where he starred in several spaghetti westerns and B-movies, playing either the hero or the antagonist...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dMs895o1Eh7icrvuapCMYlKN8Cz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6890"}}, {tmdbId:"100989", properties:{bornIn:"Carmel, Maine", imdbId:"0265196", born:date('1933-03-12'), name:"Myrna Fahey", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMyrna Fahey (12 March 1933 - 6 May 1973) was an American actress best known for her role as Maria Crespo in Walt Disney's Zorro, and as Madeline Usher in the film version of Edgar Allan Poe's, The Fall of the House of Usher.  She appeared in episodes of 37 television series from the 1950s into the 1970s, including Bonanza, The Time Tunnel, Maverick, Perry Mason, and Batman .  Fahey also became the subject of death threats while dating Joe DiMaggio in 1964...", died:date('1973-05-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7YQTO3UzV7NUOuGPe30FYiXWzG8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100989"}}, {tmdbId:"100990", properties:{bornIn:"Atlanta, Georgia, USA", imdbId:"0254041", born:date('1901-01-15'), name:"Harry Ellerbe", died:date('1992-12-02'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100990"}}, {tmdbId:"19877", properties:{bornIn:"Fort Wayne, Indiana, U.S.", imdbId:"0948685", born:date('1928-09-04'), name:"Dick York", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRichard Allen \"Dick\" York (September 4, 1928 – February 20, 1992) was an American actor.  He is best remembered for his role as the first Darrin Stephens on the ABC television fantasy sitcom Bewitched.  His most well known motion picture role was, arguably, as teacher Bertram Cates in the 1960 film Inherit The Wind. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Dick York, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1992-02-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jLN1mMJUEwuEKTkVuAptNhPMp6R.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19877"}}, {tmdbId:"70359", properties:{bornIn:"Stockholm, Stockholms län, Sweden", imdbId:"0883517", born:date('1916-12-16'), name:"Birgitta Valberg", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nBirgitta Valberg (born 16 December 1916; Stockholm) is a Swedish actress who attended the Dramatens elevskola...", died:date('2014-03-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2ju8g2NRsGnOkmSvtlPsO8SkHX0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70359"}}, {tmdbId:"6662", properties:{bornIn:"Gothenburg, Sweden", imdbId:"0511458", born:date('1931-12-18'), name:"Gunnel Lindblom", bio:"Gunnel Lindblom (born Gunnel Märtha Ingegärd Lindblom, 18 December 1931 Gothenburg, Sweden), is a Swedish film actress and director.  As an actor she has been particularly associated with the work of Ingmar Bergman, though in 1965 she performed the lead role in Miss Julie for BBC Television.  She also played the key-role of The Mummy in Bergman's staging of Strindberg's The Ghost Sonata in 1998-2000, a performance that earned her much critical acclaim...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/93heWge7LBJtmTlvVUvCHRogcmJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6662"}}, {tmdbId:"70361", properties:{bornIn:"Uppsala, Sweden", imdbId:"0678555", born:date('1939-01-07'), name:"Birgitta Pettersson", bio:"Ingrid Birgitta Pettersson is a Swedish stage and screen actress.  She made her film debut in \"Salka Valka\" (1954), and graduated from Malmö City Theatre Academy in 1959.  Birgitta Pettersson received international attention in Ingmar Bergman's \"Virgin Spring\" (1960).  The rose as \"Karin\" was her second film with Bergman...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aPdYBqa7T4QrxLVrFuqEDyu6oQx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70361"}}, {tmdbId:"29903", properties:{bornIn:"South Kensington, London, England", imdbId:"0002075", born:date('1916-09-27'), name:"Peter Finch", bio:"Frederick George Peter Ingle Finch (28 September 1916 – 14 January 1977) was an English-Australian actor.  He is best remembered for his role as crazed television anchorman Howard Beale in the 1976 film Network, which earned him a posthumous Academy Award for Best Actor, his fifth Best Actor award from the BAFTA, and a Best Actor award from the Golden Globes.  He was the first of two people to win a posthumous Academy Award in an acting category; the other was fellow Australian Heath Ledger...", died:date('1977-01-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1Rku0aVOGNP4LPPjPaesKCqynp7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29903"}}, {tmdbId:"83128", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, U.S.", imdbId:"0531279", born:date('1937-12-08'), name:"James MacArthur", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nJames Gordon MacArthur (December 8, 1937 – October 28, 2010) was an American actor best known for the role of Danny \"Danno\" Williams, the reliable second-in-command of the fictional Hawaiian State Police squad Hawaii Five-O. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article James MacArthur,  licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2010-10-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yv6fJk944okWVyCRS5jUaZI6HgF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83128"}}, {tmdbId:"9874", properties:{bornIn:"Brentford, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0496866", born:date('1908-01-10'), name:"Bernard Lee", bio:"John Bernard \"Bernard\" Lee (10 January 1908 – 16 January 1981) was an English actor, best known for his role as M in the first eleven James Bond films. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Bernard Lee, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1981-01-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/45i7qeexJgzn03KcvDlS8ALSMRD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9874"}}, {tmdbId:"98452", properties:{bornIn:"Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0371918", born:date('1929-04-01'), name:"Jonathan Haze", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jKyiDmjWRz3PEIiyBG1PdZXbN07.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/98452"}}, {tmdbId:"16182", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0430604", born:date('1934-11-07'), name:"Jackie Joseph", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJackie Joseph (born November 7, 1934) is an American character actress, voice artist, and writer known for portraying the film characters of: Audrey Fulquard in the original The Little Shop of Horrors, Sheila Futterman in both Gremlins films, and the voice of Melody in the animated television series Josie and the Pussycats and Josie and the Pussycats in Outer Space...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16182"}}, {tmdbId:"102441", properties:{bornIn:"The Bronx, New York, USA", imdbId:"0588241", born:date('1928-12-25'), name:"Dick Miller", bio:"An American character actor who appeared in more than 180 films, including many produced by Roger Corman.  He later appeared in the films of directors who began their careers with Corman, including James Cameron and Joe Dante, with the distinction of appearing in every film directed by Dante...", died:date('2019-01-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zyQXh8BkLg0DDo23pxJN2dy6Bqj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/102441"}}, {tmdbId:"5685", properties:{bornIn:"Birkenhead, Cheshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0824489", born:date('1937-12-29'), name:"Barbara Steele", bio:"Barbara Steele (born December 29, 1937, Birkenhead, Merseyside, England) is an English film actress.  She is best known for starring in Italian gothic horror films of the 1960s.  Her breakthrough role came in Italian director Mario Bava's Black Sunday (1960), now hailed as a classic. \n\nSteele starred in a string of horror films, including The Horrible Dr...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/m5rKaeUo5kwTBqZpBonzfPwkuIn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5685"}}, {tmdbId:"31545", properties:{imdbId:"0724623", born:date('1934-01-19'), name:"John Richardson", bio:"John Richardson (born January 19, 1934) is an English actor, who appeared in movies from the 1950s until the 1990s. \n\nHe appeared in many Italian films, including Mario Bava's Black Sunday (1960).  His best known role was perhaps in One Million Years B. C.  (1966), in which he played a grunting caveman who fell in love with Raquel Welch...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/esmjGJyeVTNyYu39utLcGRSf2fK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31545"}}, {tmdbId:"45036", properties:{bornIn:"Firenze", imdbId:"0154804", born:date('1916-10-21'), name:"Andrea Checchi", died:date('1974-03-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/u17146Cldv7L8mjSdNkOx76n01r.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/45036"}}, {tmdbId:"84251", properties:{imdbId:"0307995", born:date('1924-02-06'), name:"Ivo Garrani", died:date('2015-03-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qpDEJjGAeUExV3LbyW2Vjsu2N8r.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/84251"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"20156", properties:{bornIn:"Harlem, Manhattan, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0002035", born:date('1925-12-08'), name:"Sammy Davis Jr.", bio:"Samuel George \"Sammy\" Davis, Jr.  (December 8, 1925 – May 16, 1990) was an American entertainer. \n\nPrimarily a dancer and singer, Davis was a childhood vaudevillian who became known for his performances on Broadway and in Las Vegas, as a recording artist, television and film star, and as a member of Frank Sinatra's \"Rat Pack\"...", died:date('1990-05-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/t9YaZa4luUcXNE3rq1I6IfBdjFh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20156"}}, {tmdbId:"6251", properties:{bornIn:"Darmstadt, Germany", imdbId:"0003337", born:date('1928-03-16'), name:"Karlheinz Böhm", bio:"Karlheinz Böhm  (born 16 March 1928 in Darmstadt, Germany) is an Austrian actor.  The son of conductor Karl Böhm, he is best known internationally for his role as Mark, the psychopathic protagonist of Peeping Tom, directed by Michael Powell.  Before that, he had played the young Emperor Franz Joseph I of Austria in the three Sissi movies.  He made three notable U. S.  films in 1962...", died:date('2014-05-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gyBHovQS9mP59VGtL00hKr3PPd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6251"}}, {tmdbId:"68422", properties:{bornIn:"Dunfermline, Fife, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0790452", born:date('1926-01-17'), name:"Moira Shearer", bio:"Moira Shearer, Lady Kennedy (17 January 1926 – 31 January 2006), was an internationally famous Scottish ballet dancer and actress.  She is best known for her debut acting role in the 1948 film The Red Shoes, which first garnered her international attention...", died:date('2006-01-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2bD84fnD9du68LPsU82dbC0B1R0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/68422"}}, {tmdbId:"8227", properties:{bornIn:"Thakeham, West Sussex, England, UK", imdbId:"0557281", born:date('1937-08-11'), name:"Anna Massey", bio:"Anna Raymond Massey, CBE, was an English stage, screen, and television actress.  She was the daughter of Hollywood actor Raymond Massey...", died:date('2011-07-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sBlRr3oC9r4NiqhVDc85JfITIBL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8227"}}, {tmdbId:"143406", properties:{bornIn:"Weatherford, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0552756", born:date('1913-12-01'), name:"Mary Martin", bio:"Mary Virginia Martin was an American actress, singer, and Broadway star.  A muse of Rodgers and Hammerstein, she originated many leading roles over her career including Nellie Forbush in South Pacific and Maria von Trapp in The Sound of Music.  She was named a Kennedy Center Honoree in 1989.  She was the mother of actor Larry Hagman. \n\nMartin began her radio career in 1939 as the vocalist on a short-lived revival of The Tuesday Night Party on CBS...", died:date('1990-11-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rtAagO01YssbCjO0rR6jZEx7pls.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/143406"}}, {tmdbId:"7393", properties:{bornIn:"Sydney, New South Wales, Australia", imdbId:"0728509", born:date('1897-12-01'), name:"Cyril Ritchard", died:date('1977-12-18'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7393"}}, {tmdbId:"943044", properties:{bornIn:"Woodford, Essex, England, UK", imdbId:"0285007", born:date('1887-12-06'), name:"Lynn Fontanne", bio:"From Wikipedia\n\nLynn Fontanne (/fɒnˈtæn/; 6 December 1887 – 30 July 1983) was a British-born American-based actress and major stage star in the United States for over 40 years.  She teamed with her husband, Alfred Lunt.  Lunt and Fontanne shared a special Tony Award in 1970.  They both won Emmy Awards in 1965, and Broadway's Lunt-Fontanne Theatre was named for them.  Fontanne was also a Kennedy Center honoree in 1980...", died:date('1983-07-30'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/943044"}}, {tmdbId:"2666923", properties:{name:"Maureen Bailey", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2666923"}}, {tmdbId:"20369", properties:{bornIn:"Colorado Springs, Colorado, USA", imdbId:"0001981", born:date('1886-10-17'), name:"Spring Byington", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSpring Byington (October 17, 1886 – September 7, 1971) was an American actress.  Her career included a seven-year run on radio and television as the star of December Bride.  She was a key MGM contract player, appearing in films from the 1930s through the 1960s...", died:date('1971-09-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/h29Xb3qmrpdUSvSOf4LekGBUqcN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20369"}}, {tmdbId:"15135", properties:{bornIn:"Sceaux, Seine, France", imdbId:"0001128", born:date('1935-11-08'), name:"Alain Delon", bio:"Alain Fabien Maurice Marcel Delon is a French-Swiss actor.  He rose quickly to stardom, and by the age of 23 was already being compared to French actors such as Gérard Philipe and Jean Marais, as well as American actor James Dean.  He was even called the male Brigitte Bardot. \n\nOver the course of his career, Delon has worked with many well-known directors, including Luchino Visconti, Jean-Luc Godard, Jean-Pierre Melville, Michelangelo Antonioni and Louis Malle...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3QGWfT4saSHiTJdhLD4IyuRbYDF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15135"}}, {tmdbId:"15395", properties:{bornIn:"Nice, Alpes-Maritimes, Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur, France", imdbId:"0740067", born:date('1927-04-13'), name:"Maurice Ronet", bio:"Maurice Ronet (13 April 1927 – 14 March 1983) was a French film actor, director and writer...", died:date('1983-03-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kNoCaKscnlHGTUucSUwjla7QT1v.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15395"}}, {tmdbId:"39644", properties:{bornIn:"Soulac-sur-Mer, Gironde, France", imdbId:"0481030", born:date('1939-10-05'), name:"Marie Laforêt", bio:"Marie Laforêt (born 5 October 1939 - November 2, 2019) is a French singer and actress.  In 1978, she moved to Geneva, Switzerland and acquired Swiss citizenship. \n\nHer career began accidentally in 1959 when she replaced her sister at the last minute in a French radio talent contest Naissance d'une étoile (birth of a star) and won...", died:date('2019-11-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vn6ZiZWC9O7FjHbiEbfFSXFC0G1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/39644"}}, {tmdbId:"37728", properties:{bornIn:"Biserta, Tunisia", imdbId:"0187927", born:date('1924-03-10'), name:"Erno Crisa", died:date('1968-04-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uVlVZLULiheiXQc8AWL9M46TsIM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/37728"}}, {tmdbId:"36819", properties:{bornIn:"Marylebone, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0001539", born:date('1946-04-19'), name:"Hayley Mills", bio:"Hayley Catherine Rose Vivien Mills (born 18 April 1946) is an English actress...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mvnrDGmfEDDvjscI1l7W12Xxzg0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/36819"}}, {tmdbId:"3926", properties:{bornIn:"Salford, Greater Manchester, England, UK", imdbId:"0001215", born:date('1936-05-09'), name:"Albert Finney", bio:"Albert Finney (9 May 1936 – 7 February 2019) was an English actor.  He attended the Royal Academy of Dramatic Art and worked in the theatre before attaining prominence on screen in the early 1960s, debuting with The Entertainer (1960), directed by Tony Richardson, who had previously directed him in the theatre.  He maintained a successful career in theatre, film and television...", died:date('2019-02-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tAwXUmAbQGka31CTGQ0xS89QNYC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3926"}}, {tmdbId:"83909", properties:{bornIn:"Bolton, Lancashire, England, UK ", imdbId:"0276043", born:date('1938-06-27'), name:"Shirley Anne Field", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dzVWdz4HExydHhAiIQHKo10g2o1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83909"}}, {tmdbId:"82495", properties:{bornIn:"Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada", imdbId:"1212051", born:date('1978-04-08'), name:"Rachel Roberts", bio:"Rachel Roberts began her career at age sixteen in her hometown of Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1nDy90bkMIK2LfqU5KWBumbciDn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82495"}}, {tmdbId:"200323", properties:{bornIn:"Farnworth, Lancashire, England, UK", born:date('1905-02-04'), name:"Hylda Baker", died:date('1986-05-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nG0GpyE0Fd5jDMcJKuObYP6ublm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/200323"}}, {tmdbId:"39025", properties:{bornIn:"Kingston-Upon-Hull, East Riding of Yorkshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0138428", born:date('1920-06-18'), name:"Ian Carmichael", bio:"Ian Gillett Carmichael, OBE (18 June 1920 – 5 February 2010)[1] was an English actor best known for his roles in the films of the Boulting brothers such as Private's Progress (1956) and I'm All Right Jack (1959).  Later he played Dorothy L.  Sayers's Gentleman Detective, Lord Peter Wimsey, on television and radio.  Carmichael also had a career on stage...", died:date('2010-02-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7O4wMIk8bkw8v0tUyk11y3UkbXs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/39025"}}, {tmdbId:"74155", properties:{bornIn:"Morecambe, Lancashire, England, UK", imdbId:"0779285", born:date('1938-12-14'), name:"Janette Scott", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Thora Janette Scott (born 14 December 1938) is an English actress.  She was born in Morecambe, England.  She is the daughter of actors Jimmy Scott and Thora Hird.  She started her acting career as a child actress, known as Janette Scott, and became a popular leading lady...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/44PykNpOUHIfc7c5ySE6udI4AKW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74155"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"8229", properties:{bornIn:"Sydney - New South Wales - Australia", imdbId:"0001792", born:date('1930-01-11'), name:"Rod Taylor", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRodney Sturt \"Rod\" Taylor (born 11 January 1930  – 7 January 2015) was an Australian-born American actor of film and television.  He appeared in over 50 films, including leading roles in The Time Machine, Seven Seas to Calais, The Birds, Sunday in New York, Young Cassidy, Dark of the Sun, The Liquidator, and The Train Robbers...", died:date('2015-01-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nSpfs8lXHxWcksZW3qC9ArMLAqZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8229"}}, {tmdbId:"21876", properties:{bornIn:"Hollywood - Los Angeles - California - USA", imdbId:"0590796", born:date('1942-01-08'), name:"Yvette Mimieux", bio:"An actress and writer, known for The Time Machine (1960), Where the Boys Are (1960), The Black Hole (1979) and Dark of the Sun (1968).  She has been married to Howard Ruby since December 20, 1986.  She was previously married to Stanley Donen...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uGXko0Q8kzxUzwtFOqGNzNSWgYq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21876"}}, {tmdbId:"21877", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0001982", born:date('1918-07-06'), name:"Sebastian Cabot", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nCharles Sebastian Thomas Cabot  (July 6, 1918 – August 22, 1977) was an English film and television actor, best remembered as the gentleman's gentleman, \"Giles French,\" opposite Brian Keith's character, in the 1960s sitcom Family Affair.  He was also known for playing Dr.  Carl Hyatt in the series Checkmate and for doing the voice of Bagheera in The Jungle Book...", died:date('1977-08-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uAgoTmwvabGX00LnYyDfyL7TPUP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21877"}}, {tmdbId:"10268", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0002198", born:date('1924-05-22'), name:"Charles Aznavour", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nCharles Aznavour, OC (May 22, 1924 - October 1, 2018) was an Armenian-French singer, songwriter, actor, public activist and diplomat.  Besides being one of France's most popular and enduring singers, he is also one of the best-known singers in the world.  Charles Aznavour (pronounced in French as Sharl Aznavour) is known for his characteristic short figure and unique tenor voice; clear and ringing in its upper reaches, with gravelly and profound low notes...", died:date('2018-10-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zAWJHQT4hY0ELK6aaSXRoAgEJbT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10268"}}, {tmdbId:"18218", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0239447", born:date('1937-01-12'), name:"Marie Dubois", bio:"Marie Dubois (born January 12, 1937 – 15 October 2014) was a French actress. \n\nShe made her film debut in 1959, and first gained notice in Shoot the Piano Player.  She has since played mainly supporting roles, and in the 1960s she appeared in New Wave films such as Jules and Jim and The Thief of Paris, thrillers like Hot Line, and comedies like La Ronde, La Grande Vadrouille, and Monte Carlo or Bust...", died:date('2014-10-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9CY4MOKCAYC9dex7J4xcYkEq2wp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18218"}}, {tmdbId:"19269", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, Ile-de-France, France", imdbId:"0074303", born:date('1934-06-12'), name:"Nicole Berger", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nNicole Berger (born Nicole Gouspeyre, 12 June 1934[2] - 13 April 1967) was a French actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Nicole Berger, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1967-04-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/reT51hjkYj99XOJDN5VMSvLWTcc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19269"}}, {tmdbId:"19270", properties:{bornIn:"Nice, France", imdbId:"0580440", born:date('1939-01-01'), name:"Michèle Mercier", bio:"Michèle Mercier, (born January 1, 1939 as Jocelyne Yvonne Renée Mercier) is a French actress.  In the course of her career she has worked with leading directors like François Truffaut, Jean-Pierre Melville, Jacques Deray, Dino Risi, Mario Monicelli, Mario Bava, Peter Collinson and Ken Annakin.  Her leading men have included Marcello Mastroianni, Vittorio Gassman, Jean-Paul Belmondo, Jean Gabin, Charles Aznavour, Robert Hossein, Charles Bronson, Tony Curtis and Charlton Heston...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vd0xQATybtKAJHtGPyLjN1FkHbK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19270"}}, {tmdbId:"100606", properties:{bornIn:"St. Paul, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0330629", born:date('1949-07-27'), name:"Susan Gordon", bio:"Susan Lynn Gordon (July 27, 1949 — December 11, 2011) was an American child actress who appeared in films and numerous episodes of television programs such as The Twilight Zone, My Three Sons, and The Donna Reed Show. \n\nGordon was born in Saint Paul, Minnesota, the daughter of film director Bert I.  Gordon and his wife Flora (Lang)...", died:date('2011-12-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bABkShtFmi86fxNsUsi3QaFS5ro.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100606"}}, {tmdbId:"101229", properties:{imdbId:"0761644", name:"Lugene Sanders", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kCxoP7xjoEqh34EJu7Un4QQnqIz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101229"}}, {tmdbId:"101230", properties:{imdbId:"0714915", born:date('1935-11-28'), name:"Juli Reding", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sF8CLTM5i0eVQ2xhQuERzYqNcyr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101230"}}, {tmdbId:"101478", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0791176", born:date('1932-02-13'), name:"Barbara Shelley", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBarbara Shelley (born 13 February 1932) is an English film and television actress. \n\nShe is now retired, but was at her busiest in the late 1950s (Blood of the Vampire) and 1960s when she became Hammer Horror's number one female star, with The Gorgon (1964), Dracula, Prince of Darkness (1966), Rasputin, the Mad Monk (1966), and Quatermass and the Pit (1967) among her credits...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8pZ98RQv1inVfxAQ8PwNRHHYuXU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101478"}}, {tmdbId:"70447", properties:{bornIn:"Southgate, Middlesex, England", imdbId:"0827101", born:date('1948-07-30'), name:"Martin Stephens", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMartin Stephens (born 30 July 1948) is an English former child actor, best known for his performances in the films Village of the Damned and The Innocents.  Stephens appeared in fourteen films between 1954 and 1966, then chose to drop out of acting and made his adult career outside the profession. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Martin Stephens (actor), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70447"}}, {tmdbId:"30705", properties:{bornIn:"Bath, Somerset, England, U.K.", imdbId:"0350372", born:date('1916-11-30'), name:"Michael Gwynn", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMichael Gwynn (30 November 1916 in Bath – 29 January 1976 in London) was an English actor.  He attended Mayfield College near Mayfield, East Sussex.  During the Second World War he served in East Africa as a Major and was Adjutant to the 2nd.  Nyasaland Battalion, Kings African Rifles...", died:date('1976-01-29'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30705"}}, {tmdbId:"69248", properties:{bornIn:"Broken Hill, New South Wales, Australia", imdbId:"0706256", born:date('1909-03-26'), name:"Chips Rafferty", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nChips Rafferty MBE (26 March 1909 – 27 May 1971) was an iconic Australian actor.  Called \"the living symbol of the typical Australian\", Rafferty's career stretched from the 1940s until his death in 1971, and during this time he performed regularly in major Australian feature films as well as appearing in British and American productions.  He appeared in commercials in Britain during the late 1950s, encouraging British emigration to Australia...", died:date('1971-05-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eCQ9NtjETICZC9WNSxrQdsboeIB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69248"}}, {tmdbId:"98162", properties:{bornIn:"Boston, Massachusetts, U.S.", imdbId:"0127693", born:date('1927-07-09'), name:"Susan Cabot", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nSusan Cabot (July 9, 1927 – December 10, 1986) was an American actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Susan Cabot,   licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1986-12-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/umE8fMtDL29FpQ0vPsGrUTAvC3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/98162"}}, {tmdbId:"30687", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA ", imdbId:"0252111", born:date('1925-01-19'), name:"Anthony Eisley", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Anthony Eisley (January 19, 1925 – January 20, 2003) was born Frederick Glendinning Eisley in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, whose father  was a general sales manager for a large corporation.  Father of Amanda Eisley, Jonathan Eisley,  Nan R.  Eisley,  David Glen Eisley  and grandfather of actress  India Eisley. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Anthony Eisley, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2003-01-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vujQYZIf9JJ0QT89QWyzWrqJGfO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30687"}}, {tmdbId:"89037", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0606371", born:date('1932-10-22'), name:"Barboura Morris", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nBarboura Morris (1932–1975) was an American actor.  She acted under some other names. \n\nShe acted in several of Roger Corman's films, including Rita in the cult classic Sorority Girl. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Barboura Morris, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1975-10-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3IM8FY8R6KgCouyw5KKDzVHQGK1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89037"}}, {tmdbId:"98163", properties:{bornIn:"Hoboken, NJ", imdbId:"0736418", born:date('1911-12-17'), name:"William Roerick", bio:"William George Roerick was an American actor.  He is particularly associated with the stage, but also played in many films and TV productions.  He was also a stage manager and writer...", died:date('1995-11-30'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/98163"}}, {tmdbId:"3267", properties:{bornIn:"Memphis, Tennessee, U.S.", imdbId:"0001313", born:date('1939-08-12'), name:"George Hamilton", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGeorge Stevens Hamilton is an American film and television actor.  He began his film career in 1958 and although he has a substantial body of work in film and television he is, perhaps, most famous for his debonair style and his perpetual suntan.  Bo Derek writes in her autobiography that \"there was an ongoing contest between John [Derek] and George Hamilton as to who was tanner\"...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/za0jt4pZEjHf3kzUecbIC6hpX7I.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3267"}}, {tmdbId:"94550", properties:{bornIn:"Binghamton, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001380", born:date('1934-05-31'), name:"Jim Hutton", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDana James Hutton (May 31, 1934 – June 2, 1979), usually credited as Jim Hutton, was an American actor in film and television probably best remembered for his role as Ellery Queen in the 1970s TV series of the same name. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jim Hutton, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1979-06-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kTJ0knKe6mYz5wuxxsEELuh2qaL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94550"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"12692", properties:{bornIn:" Brooklyn, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0758692", born:date('1928-03-11'), name:"Albert Salmi", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAlbert Salmi (March 11, 1928 – April 22, 1990) was an American actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Albert Salmi, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1990-04-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bGCVttGNO0xcTHJ9ULBmOEKatoO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12692"}}, {tmdbId:"29908", properties:{bornIn:"Hong Kong, British Crown Colony [now China]", imdbId:"0477088", born:date('1939-05-19'), name:"Nancy Kwan", bio:"Nancy Kwan is a Hong Kong-born Eurasian-American actress, who played a pivotal role in the acceptance of actors of Asian ancestry in major Hollywood film roles.  Widely praised for her beauty, Kwan was considered a sex symbol in the 1960s...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oGeV1ipDhW2QXRtXPHi3ZvVsTjt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29908"}}, {tmdbId:"15736", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0843401", born:date('1934-01-06'), name:"Sylvia Syms", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSylvia M.  L.  Syms OBE (born 6 January 1934) is an English actress.  She is probably best known for her roles in the films Woman in a Dressing Gown (1957), Ice-Cold in Alex (1958), No Trees in the Street (1959) and The Tamarind Seed (1974).  She remains active in films, television and theatre. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Sylvia Syms, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/itv1B0z5unMZ8VQ6nrCfn2dxf98.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15736"}}, {tmdbId:"25957", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0218633", born:date('1950-05-16'), name:"Catherine Demongeot", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/46K3gfr8Pwh7gnlyKsZwTlMCdz8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25957"}}, {tmdbId:"24366", properties:{bornIn:"Lille, Nord, France", imdbId:"0634159", born:date('1930-10-01'), name:"Philippe Noiret", bio:"Philippe Noiret (born 1 October 1930 in Lille – died 23 November 2006 in Paris) was a French film actor...", died:date('2006-11-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/13vb0RuOI0t8I1y04pnz81vLptl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24366"}}, {tmdbId:"25958", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0220997", born:date('1923-09-13'), name:"Hubert Deschamps", bio:"Hubert Deschamps (September 13, 1923 – December 29, 1998) was a French actor...", died:date('1998-12-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kgZNTYPOOumOYt4Sp7Hcf2zHYy4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25958"}}, {tmdbId:"25959", properties:{bornIn:"Parigi, Francia", imdbId:"0549150", born:date('1937-01-01'), name:"Carla Marlier", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wQQXUNqyLKoGt9cPt4Ws8cbtjc8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25959"}}, {tmdbId:"44860", properties:{bornIn:"Roma, Lazio, Italia", imdbId:"0162948", born:date('1935-04-23'), name:"Franco Citti", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nFranco Citti (born 23 April 1938 in Rome) is an Italian actor.  He came to fame at the age of 26, playing the title role in Pier Paolo Pasolini's film Accattone.  In 1967 he appeared in the title role in Pasolini's version of Oedipus Rex. \n\nHe is perhaps best-known to non-Italian audienes as Calo in The Godfather I and III and uttering the line 'In Sicily, women are more dangerous than shotguns'...", died:date('2016-01-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mttQPjOHaql4RKsfYriUA7HuROE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/44860"}}, {tmdbId:"72472", properties:{bornIn:"Italy", imdbId:"0665186", born:date('1936-01-01'), name:"Franca Pasut", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tSdN5I9cCNPbURgyyWbihfhxda7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/72472"}}, {tmdbId:"72473", properties:{imdbId:"0181122", name:"Silvana Corsini", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/72473"}}, {tmdbId:"72474", properties:{imdbId:"0346751", name:"Paola Guidi", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/72474"}}, {tmdbId:"3508", properties:{bornIn:"Beirut, Lebanon", imdbId:"0786891", born:date('1932-04-10'), name:"Delphine Seyrig", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDelphine Claire Beltiane Seyrig (April 10, 1932, Beirut, Lebanon – October 15, 1990) was a stage and film actress and a film director...", died:date('1990-10-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xffVQ7uiMhO8zDHRCtfVjEAWxOu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3508"}}, {tmdbId:"34593", properties:{imdbId:"0016617", born:date('1923-08-20'), name:"Giorgio Albertazzi", died:date('2016-05-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yfhMwbRjOnJUUL19Li86VsL8tta.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34593"}}, {tmdbId:"34594", properties:{bornIn:"Geneva, Switzerland", imdbId:"0685782", born:date('1920-03-11'), name:"Sacha Pitoëff", died:date('1990-07-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/frRFjzSz54j2DAf6PYh22pbkgbF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34594"}}, {tmdbId:"28676", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0078097", born:date('1925-09-23'), name:"Françoise Bertin", bio:"Françoise Bertin was born on September 23, 1925 in Paris, France as Françoise Marie Suzanne Bertin...", died:date('2014-10-26'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/28676"}}, {tmdbId:"23086", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0762378", born:date('1937-08-27'), name:"Tommy Sands", bio:"Thomas Adrian Sands is an American pop music singer and actor.  Working in show business as early as 1949, Sands became an overnight sensation and instant teen idol when he appeared on Kraft Television Theater in January 1957 as \"The Singin' Idol\".  The song from the show, \"Teen-Age Crush\", reached No.  2 on the Billboard Hot 100 and No.  1 on Cashbox...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/23086"}}, {tmdbId:"83443", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, U.S.", imdbId:"0085751", born:date('1938-05-17'), name:"Joan Blackman", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Joan Blackman (born May 18, 1938 in San Francisco, California) is an American actress.   Description above from the Wikipedia article Joan Blackman, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3c7eiI6X5lfmhB85qWwotV8ncqa.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83443"}}, {tmdbId:"83821", properties:{bornIn:"Lake County, Florida, USA", imdbId:"0910322", born:date('1933-06-29'), name:"Nancy Walters", died:date('2009-09-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bY65JindgaZFFiuopZfGrS5eQ8C.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83821"}}, {tmdbId:"16896", properties:{bornIn:"Norman, Oklahoma, USA", imdbId:"0001258", born:date('1928-04-07'), name:"James Garner", bio:"James Garner (born James Scott Bumgarner; April 7, 1928 – July 19, 2014) was an American actor, producer, and voice artist...", died:date('2014-07-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ebquWZIxVpCABQbD6F6l7eO0HiI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16896"}}, {tmdbId:"38761", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0926183", born:date('1928-02-01'), name:"Stuart Whitman", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nStuart Maxwell Whitman (February 1, 1928 – March 16, 2020) was an American actor. \n\nWhitman was arguably best-known for playing Marshal Jim Crown in the western television series Cimarron Strip in 1967.  Whitman also starred with John Wayne in the Western movie, The Comancheros, in 1961, and received top billing as the romantic lead in the extravagant aerial epic Those Magnificent Men in Their Flying Machines in 1965...", died:date('2020-03-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cRov050vMurqfIsDG6TgVWxoYMq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/38761"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"3160", properties:{bornIn:"Jerusalem, Palestine Mandate", imdbId:"0675490", born:date('1919-08-02'), name:"Nehemiah Persoff", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nNehemiah Persoff (born August 2, 1919) is a former American film and television character actor.  He was born in Jerusalem, Palestine Mandate. \n\nBorn in what is now part of Israel, Persoff emigrated with his family to the United States in 1929.  He began to take an interest in acting in the 1940s, and after serving in the Army during World War II, he began to pursue his acting career in the New York Theater...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/k32WMgl0GncvKOwnVTEB6LIfmEv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3160"}}, {tmdbId:"5789", properties:{bornIn:"Berlin, Germany", imdbId:"0001976", born:date('1933-12-04'), name:"Horst Buchholz", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nHorst Werner Buchholz  (4 December 1933 – 3 March 2003) was a German actor, remembered for his part in The Magnificent Seven and Nine Hours to Rama.  He appeared in over sixty films during his acting career from 1952–2002.  He was married to French actress Myriam Bru from 1958 to his death, and one of their two children is the actor Christopher Buchholz...", died:date('2003-03-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jSjuFaq4PjnZ6qNNc4L5UhzfUlq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5789"}}, {tmdbId:"1667288", properties:{imdbId:"0290025", name:"Francis Francine", bio:"Frank di Giovanni, elevator operator, was the first of the Andy Warhol transvestite superstars. \n\nFrancine had been intended as the star of Flaming Creatures, 1962, but disappeared partway through filming, leaving Mario Montez the throne. \n\nHe was given star treatment in the Andy Warhol/Paul Morrissey film Lonesome Cowboys, 1968, as a the transvestite sheriff.  The camera lingers as he puts on drag and makeup.  This in a cowboy village partly owned by John Wayne...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1667288"}}, {tmdbId:"2362369", properties:{name:"Sheila Bick", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2362369"}}, {tmdbId:"1899244", properties:{name:"Joel Markman", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1899244"}}, {tmdbId:"105057", properties:{bornIn:"Ponce, Puerto Rico", imdbId:"0599689", born:date('1935-07-20'), name:"Mario Montez", bio:"René Rivera, (July 20, 1935 – September 26, 2013), known professionally as Mario Montez, was one of the Warhol superstars, appearing in thirteen of Andy Warhol's underground films from 1964 to 1966.  He took his name as a male homage to the actress Maria Montez, an important gay icon in the fifties and sixties.  Before appearing in Warhol's films, he appeared in Jack Smith's important underground films Flaming Creatures and Normal Love...", died:date('2013-09-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yFzOT9ZvKt8kbuQ9xxfiYiUP1FE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/105057"}}, {tmdbId:"14882", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001276", born:date('1916-02-26'), name:"Jackie Gleason", bio:"Jackie Gleason was an American comedian, actor, writer, composer and conductor...", died:date('1987-06-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9oATJRNf1z2b3P4Jc6K99FzTKCb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14882"}}, {tmdbId:"6721", properties:{bornIn:"Detroit, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0001453", born:date('1932-01-22'), name:"Piper Laurie", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nPiper Laurie (born Rosetta Jacobs; January 22, 1932) is an American actress of stage and screen best known for her roles in the television series Twin Peaks and the films The Hustler, Carrie, and Children of a Lesser God, all of which brought her Academy Award nominations.  In 1991 she won a Golden Globe Award for her portrayal of Catherine Martell in Twin Peaks...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/huDPKTgm9IHFaX8dLwCnLqqAA8f.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6721"}}, {tmdbId:"862", properties:{bornIn:"Wise, Virginia, USA", imdbId:"0001715", born:date('1927-10-18'), name:"George C. Scott", bio:"George Campbell Scott (October 18, 1927 – September 22, 1999) was an American actor, director and producer.  He was best known for his stage work, as well as his portrayals of the prosecutor Claude Dancer in Anatomy of a Murder (1959), General Buck Turgidson in Stanley Kubrick's Dr.  Strangelove (1964), General George S.  Patton in the film Patton (1970), and Ebenezer Scrooge in Clive Donner's film A Christmas Carol (1984). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article George C...", died:date('1999-09-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1dL9hx7nC0cACIVpp6xS1jqJJN7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/862"}}, {tmdbId:"22529", properties:{bornIn:"Marseille, Bouches-du-Rhône, France", imdbId:"0943936", born:date('1928-08-23'), name:"Peter Wyngarde", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPeter Paul Wyngarde  (born Cyril Goldbert, 23 August 1928) is an Anglo-French actor best known for playing the character Jason King, a bestselling novelist turned sleuth, in two British television series in the late 1960s and early 1970s: Department S (1969–1970) and Jason King (1971–1972)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/H4MMNUpJTpm0kW41IDF2dUw62s.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/22529"}}, {tmdbId:"47398", properties:{imdbId:"0420923", born:date('1917-04-21'), name:"Megs Jenkins", bio:"An engineer's daughter, she had first planned on becoming a ballerina, using her original Christian name Muguette, but abandoned those plans by the age of 17 when she realized that her physique was more in keeping with her other first name, Megs.  She trained in Liverpool at the School of Dancing and Dramatic Art and then joined the Liverpool Repertory Company in 1933 before moving to London to appear at the Player's Theatre four years later...", died:date('1998-10-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nGx7nFSU93haAq2AU2e6G5ZdRIY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/47398"}}, {tmdbId:"14812", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0603402", born:date('1928-01-23'), name:"Jeanne Moreau", bio:"Jeanne Moreau (23 January 1928 – 31 July 2017) was a French actress, singer, screenwriter, and director. \n\nShe made her theatrical debut in 1947, and established herself as one of the leading actresses of the Comédie-Française.  She began playing small roles in films in 1949 and eventually achieved prominence as the star of Lift to the Scaffold (UK)/Elevator to the Gallows (USA) (1958), directed by Louis Malle, and Jules et Jim (1962), directed by François Truffaut...", died:date('2017-07-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mYRXwbzmZgqQOr1mYqbtcdugCkV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14812"}}, {tmdbId:"18216", properties:{bornIn:"Vienna, Austria", imdbId:"0921459", born:date('1922-11-13'), name:"Oskar Werner", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nOskar Werner (November 13, 1922, Gumpendorf [now a part of Mariahilf, Vienna]  – October 23, 1984) was an Austrian actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Oskar Werner, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1984-10-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dv640qU6wBncoUw6IhDzqJ00EGq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18216"}}, {tmdbId:"18217", properties:{bornIn:"Sète, France", imdbId:"0785676", born:date('1931-02-26'), name:"Henri Serre", bio:"Henri Serre, né le 26 février 1931 à Sète, est un acteur français.   Principalement acteur de théâtre et de comédie, il a travaillé avec de grandes actrices, comme Jeanne Moreau ou Romy Schneider.  Le film qui le fit remarquer fut Jules et Jim de François Truffaut.   Il est le père de Martin Serre avec lequel il a tourné une série télé diffusée dans les années 1970 : \"Mon Fils\" (histoire d'un père qui fait tout pour son fils dans une vie qui le lui arrache)...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18217"}}, {tmdbId:"18220", properties:{bornIn:"Florence - Tuscany - Italy", imdbId:"0881752", born:date('1929-03-18'), name:"Vanna Urbino", bio:"Vanna Urbino was born on March 18, 1929 in Florence, Tuscany, Italy.  She is an actress...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18220"}}, {tmdbId:"14012", properties:{bornIn:"Belfast, Northern Ireland, UK", imdbId:"0571430", born:date('1923-05-24'), name:"Siobhan McKenna", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nSiobhán McKenna (May 24, 1923 – November 16, 1986) was an Irish stage and screen actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Siobhán McKenna, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1986-11-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hBWTNcFzhvtdBKd54JnlCJWf8HO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14012"}}, {tmdbId:"115308", properties:{bornIn:"Sydney, New South Wales, Austrailia", imdbId:"0709681", born:date('1918-10-08'), name:"Ron Randell", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRonald Egan \"Ron\" Randell (8 October 1918 – 11 June 2005) was an Australian film and stage actor who also worked in Great Britain and the United States...", died:date('2005-06-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5DPq8pWOJ23hNWjB5O7za7N7CSZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/115308"}}, {tmdbId:"96551", properties:{bornIn:"Osaka, Japan", imdbId:"0620131", born:date('1902-02-17'), name:"Ganjirô Nakamura", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nGanjiro Nakamura (17 February 1902 – 13 April 1983) was a Japanese film actor.  He appeared in 48 films between 1957 and 1982.  He starred in the film The End of Summer, which was entered into the 12th Berlin International Film Festival. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Ganjiro Nakamura, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1983-04-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/16VYL6FQhIUfUviAjQooKgTiNkF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96551"}}, {tmdbId:"70811", properties:{bornIn:"Sakaiminato, Japan", imdbId:"0875362", born:date('1934-08-20'), name:"Yôko Tsukasa", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nYouko Tsukasa (司葉子 Tsukasa Yōko, born 20 August 1934) is a Japanese actress.  She won the award for best actress at the 17th Blue Ribbon Awards for Kinokawa\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Youko Tsukasa, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cEF3udfW1Miuo4f3wUiFejVukRC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70811"}}, {tmdbId:"4098", properties:{bornIn:"Kingston, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0010944", born:date('1927-04-16'), name:"Edie Adams", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEdie Adams (April 16, 1927 – October 15, 2008) was an American singer, Broadway, television and film actress and comedienne.  Adams, a Tony Award winner, \"both embodied and winked at the stereotypes of fetching chanteuse and sexpot blonde. \" She was well-known for her impersonations of female stars on stage and television, most particularly, Marilyn Monroe...", died:date('2008-10-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kyVNLdS4EjKnFgUfs5rr0En75pa.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4098"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"80608", properties:{bornIn:"Kagoshima, Japan", imdbId:"0756998", born:date('1929-02-13'), name:"Furankî Sakai", bio:"Frankie Sakai, born Masatoshi Sakai (堺 正俊; 13 February 1929 – 10 June 1996), was a Japanese comedian, actor, and musician...", died:date('1996-06-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5mwIPkudcnoqHsxKmj6miUNeTdI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80608"}}, {tmdbId:"18607", properties:{bornIn:"Kamakura, Japan", imdbId:"0463590", born:date('1926-08-12'), name:"Hiroshi Koizumi", bio:"Hiroshi Koizumi was a Japanese actor.  He was born in Kamakura,  Japan...", died:date('2015-05-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/37i54gRXt1mvLXt9K7dxlXmPee6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18607"}}, {tmdbId:"25536", properties:{bornIn:"Poona, Maharashtra, British India", imdbId:"0185954", born:date('1928-01-27'), name:"Michael Craig", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMichael Craig (born Michael Francis Gregson; 27 January 1928) is a British actor, known for his work in film and television in both the United Kingdom and Australia.  Craig was born in Poona, Maharashtra, British India, the son of Donald Gregson, a captain in the 3rd Indian Cavalry.  He came to England with his family when aged three, and went to Canada when he was ten.  At sixteen he joined the Merchant Navy...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bppJsRhuJu8ECbhQNCQujlN9Qn0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25536"}}, {tmdbId:"30928", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0130286", born:date('1935-11-22'), name:"Michael Callan", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMichael Callan (born November 22, 1935) is an American actor. \n\nBorn Martin Harris Calinieff in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, Callan began his career as Mickey Calin, and it was with this name he appeared on Broadway in The Boy Friend (1954), Catch a Star (1955), and West Side Story (1957-1959). \n\nCallan's film career began in 1959 where he was contracted with Columbia Pictures and had roles in two films, They Came to Cordura and The Flying Fontaines...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dFoGc7I1u7Hnd8qI3WGA4VKeroG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30928"}}, {tmdbId:"71779", properties:{imdbId:"0314867", born:date('1914-04-20'), name:"Betty Lou Gerson", died:date('1999-01-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ckAgpj1QIPLnT92V6kA9i9Mw5b5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71779"}}, {tmdbId:"71780", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0921131", born:date('1889-06-02'), name:"Martha Wentworth", bio:"Verna Martha Wentworth (June 2, 1889 - March 8, 1974) was an American actress.   Originally a radio actress, she became a film actress in the 1940s, starring in several Red Ryder Western films.  She went on to do voice work for Walt Disney Studios in One Hundred and One Dalmatians and The Sword in the Stone, her final credited film appearance...", died:date('1974-03-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/EggkNv8jtDwoAIRdJwgJ0Xjij9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71780"}}, {tmdbId:"5790", properties:{bornIn:"Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, USA", imdbId:"0863016", born:date('1942-10-13'), name:"Pamela Tiffin", bio:"Pamela Tiffin (born October 13, 1942) is a retired American film actress...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sIzbKORhYIe8bzBjkKRudoyt5EX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5790"}}, {tmdbId:"5791", properties:{bornIn:"Boston, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0290086", born:date('1907-10-20'), name:"Arlene Francis", bio:"Arlene Francis (born Arline Francis Kazanjian) was an American actress, radio talk show host, and game show panelist.  She is known for her long-standing role as a panelist on the television game show What's My Line?, on which she regularly appeared for 25 years, from 1950 through the mid-1970s...", died:date('2001-05-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/u6dNWXP49lIf0Sn17tZ9DkcYFP9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5791"}}, {tmdbId:"77485", properties:{bornIn:"New York, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0026035", born:date('1938-05-12'), name:"Luana Anders", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLuana Anders (May 12, 1938 – July 21, 1996) was an American film and television actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Luana Anders, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1996-07-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uoapFspZeq5AwxQKRgTkJZJNkmA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77485"}}, {tmdbId:"103939", properties:{imdbId:"0573871", born:date('1917-08-13'), name:"Claudia McNeil", died:date('1993-11-25'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/103939"}}, {tmdbId:"15532", properties:{bornIn:"Cleveland - Ohio - USA", imdbId:"0002039", born:date('1924-10-27'), name:"Ruby Dee", bio:"Ruby Dee (October 27, 1924 - 11 June, 2014) was an American actress, poet, playwright, screenwriter, journalist, and activist, perhaps best-known for co-starring in the film A Raisin in the Sun (1961). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Ruby Dee, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2014-06-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ciYR9GSo0F2FcEGl7yenbernok.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15532"}}, {tmdbId:"103940", properties:{imdbId:"0762305", name:"Diana Sands", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/103940"}}, {tmdbId:"3798", properties:{bornIn:"Miami, Florida, USA", imdbId:"0385757", born:date('1924-07-19'), name:"Pat Hingle", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nMartin Patterson \"Pat\" Hingle (July 19, 1924 – January 3, 2009) was an American actor. Hingle was traditionally known for playing judges, police officers, and other authority figures.  He was a guest star on the early NBC legal drama Justice, based on case histories of the Legal Aid Society of New York. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Pat Hingle, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2009-01-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/QBAxFVZQ0Hu6rxlFavhwUq0zug.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3798"}}, {tmdbId:"83566", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0160287", born:date('1912-06-27'), name:"Audrey Christie", died:date('1989-12-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3rwDMkQxE0lfYrT5eU1zOEXsKdT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83566"}}, {tmdbId:"123012", properties:{imdbId:"0517056", born:date('1932-07-08'), name:"Barbara Loden", bio:"Barbara Loden (July 8, 1932 – September 5, 1980) was a Broadway Tony award-winning American stage and film actress, model, and stage/film director.  She was the first woman to write, direct and star in her own feature film, Wanda, which won the International Critics Award at the 1970 Venice Film Festival.  Loden also directed several off-Broadway plays...", died:date('1980-09-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pFvBlK0m4g7rFgp0QFfvqTOiVSh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/123012"}}, {tmdbId:"69981", properties:{bornIn:"Borås, Västra Götalands län, Sweden", imdbId:"0664885", born:date('1941-02-14'), name:"Lars Passgård", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLars Passgård (14 February 1941 – 16 March 2003) was a Swedish actor.  He appeared in 38 films and television shows between 1961 and 2002.  He starred in the 1965 film The Chasers, which won the Silver Bear Extraordinary Jury Prize at the 16th Berlin International Film Festival...", died:date('2003-03-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hhotDr0uvj6aTvSAQGYlE3iUiaQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69981"}}, {tmdbId:"21605", properties:{bornIn:"Hampstead, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0001958", born:date('1921-03-28'), name:"Dirk Bogarde", bio:"Sir Derek Jules Gaspard Ulric Niven van den Bogaerde (28 March 1921 – 8 May 1999), known professionally as Dirk Bogarde, was an English actor and writer.  Initially a matinée idol in films such as Doctor in the House (1954) for the Rank Organisation, he later acted in art-house films.  In a second career, he wrote seven best-selling volumes of memoirs, six novels and a volume of collected journalism, mainly from articles in The Daily Telegraph...", died:date('1999-05-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/f0S6MxxcYb367KtnXWTH8DoWHMt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21605"}}, {tmdbId:"25643", properties:{bornIn:" Windsor, Berkshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0629458", born:date('1902-10-16'), name:"Anthony Nicholls", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAnthony Nicholls  (16 October 1902 – 22 February 1977) was an English film, television, and stage actor...", died:date('1977-02-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kHTuYeYns9XbjwHtZTBV71Lagf6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25643"}}, {tmdbId:"37505", properties:{bornIn:"Guaymas, Sonora, Mexico", imdbId:"0683831", born:date('1931-09-12'), name:"Silvia Pinal", bio:"Silvia Pinal (born Silvia Pinal Hidalgo on September 12, 1931 in Guaymas, Sonora) is a Mexican actress, who had roles in several of Luis Buñuel's movies such as El ángel exterminador and Viridiana.  Pinal is also considered as one of the few surviving legends of the Golden Age of Mexican cinema...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aBz6rnfdEZCnVksNYwhAAbnuG1s.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/37505"}}, {tmdbId:"14821", properties:{bornIn:"A Coruña, Galicia, Spain", imdbId:"0721073", born:date('1917-09-20'), name:"Fernando Rey", bio:"Fernando Rey  (September 20, 1917 – March 9, 1994) — best known as Fernando Rey — was a Spanish film, theatre, and TV actor, who worked in both Europe and the United States.  A suave, international actor best known for his roles in the films of surrealist director Luis Buñuel (Tristana, 1970; Discreet Charm of the Bourgeoisie, 1972; That Obscure Object of Desire, 1977) and as a drug lord in The French Connection (1971), he appeared in more than 150 films over half a century...", died:date('1994-03-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dK8oBtRU5z8pA0LvMqh09leXQVc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14821"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"16311", properties:{bornIn:"Madrid, Spain", imdbId:"0130952", born:date('1916-03-03'), name:"José Calvo", bio:"José Calvo (March 3, 1916 – May 16, 1980) was a Spanish film actor best known for his roles in western films or historical dramas. \n\nHe made around 150 appearances mostly in films between 1952 and his death in 1980.  He entered film in 1952 and was prolific as an actor throughout the 1950s and 1960s.  He made many appearances in crime dramas, often with a historical theme and appeared in a high number of western films...", died:date('1980-05-16'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16311"}}, {tmdbId:"22090", properties:{bornIn:"Tucson, Arizona, USA", imdbId:"0001174", born:date('1931-08-23'), name:"Barbara Eden", bio:"Barbara Eden (born August 23, 1931, height 5' 3¾\" (1,62 m)) is an American film, stage, and television actress and singer.  She is best known for her starring role of \"Jeannie\" in the sitcom I Dream of Jeannie.  Eden was born Barbara Jean Morehead in Tucson, Arizona, the daughter of Alice Mary (née Franklin) and Hubert Henry Morehead...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wFTdqWI7RDAbOlcejwHwKUOn4mr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/22090"}}, {tmdbId:"29719", properties:{bornIn:"Griffin, Georgia, U.S.", imdbId:"0028647", born:date('1914-10-09'), name:"Edward Andrews", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nEdward Andrews (October 9, 1914 – March 8, 1985) was an American actor, one of the most recognizable character actors on television and films between the 1950s and the 1980s.  His stark white hair, portly build and horn-rimmed glasses added to the type of roles he received, as he was often cast as an ornery boss, a cagey businessman, or a strict disciplinarian of some type...", died:date('1985-03-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3Dm2WcoxINcW42vHRgSHiu4wW3V.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29719"}}, {tmdbId:"6442", properties:{imdbId:"0622263", born:date('1921-10-26'), name:"Vivian Nathan", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6442"}}, {tmdbId:"12520", properties:{bornIn:"Rome, Latium, Italy", imdbId:"0542146", born:date('1930-04-21'), name:"Silvana Mangano", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Silvana Mangano (21 April 1930  – 16 December 1989)  was an Italian actress. \n\nRaised in poverty during World War II, Mangano trained as a dancer and worked as a model before winning a \"Miss Rome\" beauty pageant in 1946.   This led to work in films; she achieved a notable success in Bitter Rice (1949) and continued working in films for almost four more decades. \n\nThe Bosnian singer Silvana Armenulić took her stage name from Mangano...", died:date('1989-12-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wS40j2uCvA0LenVP8MEhitetnfA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12520"}}, {tmdbId:"40175", properties:{bornIn:"Knoxville, Tennessee, U.S.", imdbId:"0000917", born:date('1930-07-14'), name:"Polly Bergen", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPolly Bergen (born Nellie Paulina Burgin; July 14, 1930) is an American actress, singer, and entrepreneur...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aKXXcGl20O9Z8Rx55v70DdOIChc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/40175"}}, {tmdbId:"69103", properties:{bornIn:"Glendale, California, U.S.", imdbId:"0552700", born:date('1947-04-18'), name:"Lori Martin", bio:"Lori Martin, born Dawn Catherine Menzer, was an American actress and singer.  In 1962, she got the role of Nancy Bowden in the film \" \"Cape Fear\" in a close call with  Hayley Mills...", died:date('2010-04-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gCSg0IoP6z5xyOvEZDGwhh6uAsP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69103"}}, {tmdbId:"79298", properties:{bornIn:"Huron, South Dakota, USA", imdbId:"0385010", born:date('1935-08-14'), name:"Candace Hilligoss", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nCandace Hilligoss (born August 14, 1935, Huron, South Dakota) is an American actress. \n\nAfter three years at the University of Iowa, she came to New York City to study acting at the American Theatre Wing and made her professional debut in summer stock in Pennsylvania...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2snLWDrBcNfkOIf0f8TlBG404eV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/79298"}}, {tmdbId:"79299", properties:{imdbId:"0270766", born:date('1903-05-13'), name:"Frances Feist", died:date('1981-03-11'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/79299"}}, {tmdbId:"79300", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0074367", born:date('1935-07-25'), name:"Sidney Berger", died:date('2013-02-15'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/79300"}}, {tmdbId:"79301", properties:{imdbId:"0255156", born:date('1899-07-24'), name:"Art Ellison", died:date('1994-02-11'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/79301"}}, {tmdbId:"245", properties:{bornIn:"Cleveland, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0001158", born:date('1936-05-30'), name:"Keir Dullea", bio:"Keir Dullea (born May 30, 1936) is an American actor best known for the character of astronaut David Bowman, whom he portrayed in the 1968 film 2001: A Space Odyssey and in 1984's 2010: The Year We Make Contact, as well as his roles in the films Bunny Lake is Missing (1965) and Black Christmas (1974)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dL9i0nCk2fCgInZNaYVjGck2IBp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/245"}}, {tmdbId:"10558", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0546755", born:date('1943-07-25'), name:"Janet Margolin", bio:"Janet Margolin (July 25, 1943 – December 17, 1993) was an American theater, television and film actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Janet Margolin, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1993-12-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7EwM5B9uvvsX03Ue5Hit4Np6hoQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10558"}}, {tmdbId:"50572", properties:{bornIn:"Bois-Colombes, Hauts-de-Seine, Île-de-France, France", imdbId:"0561072", born:date('1925-12-20'), name:"Nicole Maurey", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nNicole Maurey (December 20, 1925 - March 11, 2016) was a French actress, who appeared in 65 film and television productions between 1945 and 1997.  Born in Bois-Colombes, a northwestern suburb of Paris, she was originally a dancer before being cast in her first film role in 1944.  She remains most noted as Charlton Heston's leading lady in Secret of the Incas (1954), often cited as the primary inspiration for Raiders of the Lost Ark (1981)...", died:date('2016-03-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4ivm3iKGjl8ZcUMxxxsbJy6ddY2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/50572"}}, {tmdbId:"101678", properties:{bornIn:"Skibbereen, County Cork, Ireland", imdbId:"0601476", born:date('1924-10-05'), name:"Kieron Moore", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nKieron Moore (born Ciarán Ó hAnnracháin Anglicised Kieron O’Hanrahan) (5 October 1924 – 15 July 2007) was an Irish film and television actor whose career was at its peak in the 1950s and 1960s.  He may be best remembered for his role as Count Vronsky in the 1948 film adaptation of Anna Karenina opposite Vivien Leigh. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Kieron Moore, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2007-07-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bAzDkmWMwDK8bRBry4cuexF5iyr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101678"}}, {tmdbId:"5250", properties:{bornIn:"philadelphia, PA, USA", imdbId:"0001430", born:date('1922-04-27'), name:"Jack Klugman", bio:"As a film character actor, Klugman was the epitome of the everyman.  He was one of the pioneers of television acting in the 1950s, and is best remembered for his 1970s TV work as Oscar Madison on \"The Odd Couple\" (1970) and as the medical examiner on \"Quincy M. E. \" (1976)...", died:date('2012-12-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7nJaWFPn1ppfbp3Ai3CnTtUm0PE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5250"}}, {tmdbId:"9871", properties:{bornIn:"Ostermundigen, Bern, Switzerland", imdbId:"0000266", born:date('1936-03-19'), name:"Ursula Andress", bio:"Ursula Andress is a Swiss-American actress and former sex symbol.  She is best known for her role as Bond girl Honey Ryder in the first James Bond film, Dr.  No, for which she won a Golden Globe.  She later starred as Vesper Lynd in the Bond-parody Casino Royale...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/v3Y0VE2tCyISMt4ri2OtLKnerDP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9871"}}, {tmdbId:"9872", properties:{bornIn:"Montreal, Quebec, Canada", imdbId:"0936476", born:date('1918-05-15'), name:"Joseph Wiseman", bio:"Joseph Wiseman (May 15, 1918 – October 19, 2009) was a Canadian theater and film actor, best known for starring as the titular antagonist of the first James Bond film, Dr.  No, as well as his career on Broadway.  He was once called \"the spookiest actor in the American theater\". \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Joseph Wiseman, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2009-10-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7QS6Z4rZ8kVimx10eeZ3r882Ahk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9872"}}, {tmdbId:"9873", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0520437", born:date('1920-12-30'), name:"Jack Lord", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nJohn Joseph Patrick Ryan (December 30, 1920 – January 21, 1998), best known by his stage name Jack Lord, was an American television, film, and Broadway actor.  He was known for his starring role as Steve McGarrett in the American television program Hawaii Five-O from 1968 to 1980.  Lord appeared in feature films earlier in his career, among them Man of the West (1958)...", died:date('1998-01-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ox4HCSd8jYd6LqDaflR7PytIrLG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9873"}}, {tmdbId:"1196207", properties:{name:"Paul Wallace", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fF0FbNIE4f1DNi89PHVJ5SReDoh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1196207"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"76977", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0410968", born:date('1935-01-29'), name:"Akira Ishihama", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sQC3XSIR0LeYPz11VJt8nJoeRKY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/76977"}}, {tmdbId:"76976", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Tokyo Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0412615", born:date('1941-01-03'), name:"Shima Iwashita", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nShima Shinoda, better known as Shima Iwashita (born January 3, 1941, in Tokyo, Japan) is a Japanese actress.  She is married to film director Shinoda Masahiro.  She won the award for best actress at the 2nd Hochi Film Award for Ballad of Orin...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9pAJxJtPOXrDW4W7a3uCgR3Nvgr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/76976"}}, {tmdbId:"10071", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0848533", born:date('1922-07-17'), name:"Tetsurô Tanba", bio:"Tetsurō Tamba (July 17, 1922 - September 25, 2006) was a Japanese actor...", died:date('2006-09-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ihugQ2afio03fcKSGXdkcQKTVmt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10071"}}, {tmdbId:"37777", properties:{bornIn:"Berlin - Germany", imdbId:"0473228", born:date('1928-04-12'), name:"Hardy Krüger", bio:"Hardy Krüger (born Franz Eberhard August Krüger; 12 April 1928) is a German actor.  He is thought of as one of the greatest German actors of the 1960s.  He was born in Wedding, Berlin, Germany. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Hardy Krüger, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mCAYIY4DDIaYnCEoGdRL7t1sw4Z.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/37777"}}, {tmdbId:"29428", properties:{bornIn:"Grosseto, Tuscany, Italy", imdbId:"0553349", born:date('1935-01-30'), name:"Elsa Martinelli", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nElsa Martinelli (3 August 1932 or 30 January 1935, according to different sources) was an Italian actress and former fashion model. \n\nBorn Elisa Tia in Grosseto, Tuscany, she moved to Rome with her family and in 1953 was discovered by Roberto Capucci who introduced her to the world of fashion.  She became a model and began playing small roles in films...", died:date('2017-07-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gEj3dtY4Dxlb5GmzQOubdwu0dOk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29428"}}, {tmdbId:"7503", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000999", born:date('1919-02-05'), name:"Red Buttons", bio:"Although Red Buttons is best known as a stand-up comic, he is also a successful songwriter, an Academy Award-winning actor (and has been nominated for two Golden Globe awards) and an accomplished singer.  Born Aaron Chwatt on February 5, 1919 (Aquarius) in New York City's Lower East Side, stood at a height of 5' 6\" (1. 68 m).  Buttons (who got his name from a uniform he wore while working as a singing bellhop), also known as Cpl...", died:date('2006-07-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bZYvuKzOnF181Tz0wqT4sbPZLnc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7503"}}, {tmdbId:"15387", properties:{bornIn:"Bourton-on-the-Water, Gloucestershire, England, UK", imdbId:"0405035", born:date('1903-05-12'), name:"Wilfrid Hyde-White", bio:"Wilfrid Hyde-White (12 May 1903 — 6 May 1991) was an English character actor...", died:date('1991-05-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dqdw6iQgMxHp7v5wdI5a2VI6Rwp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15387"}}, {tmdbId:"13709", properties:{bornIn:"Moscow, USSR [now Russia]", imdbId:"0122168", born:date('1946-08-03'), name:"Nikolay Burlyaev", bio:"Nikolay Burlyaev is a Soviet and Russian stage and film actor, best known for his title role in Andrei Tarkovsky's Ivan's Childhood...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fRiS9kWiolLH3J8ZhfLqmq51igm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13709"}}, {tmdbId:"119567", properties:{imdbId:"0958284", name:"Valentin Zubkov", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/obZNOJVpvgJJQvtjcFIyQBEUTbk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/119567"}}, {tmdbId:"90360", properties:{bornIn:"Moscow, USSR", imdbId:"0955529", born:date('1941-02-26'), name:"Evgeniy Zharikov", died:date('2020-01-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ckH5yBlv9MbM372BM7YDWVp07Eu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/90360"}}, {tmdbId:"119568", properties:{bornIn:"village Gorodok, Vyazma uyezd, Smolensk Governorate, Russian Empire [now Vyazemsky District, Smolensk Oblast, Russia]", imdbId:"0472989", born:date('1910-02-14'), name:"Stepan Krylov", died:date('1998-02-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xjc6HE2eRdGbNFJa7i8OVwwnqEp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/119568"}}, {tmdbId:"9960", properties:{bornIn:"Constantine, Algeria, France", imdbId:"0639058", born:date('1920-12-04'), name:"Jean Négroni", bio:"Jean Négroni (4 December 1920 – 28 May 2005) was a French actor and theatre director particularly known for his voice work, such as his role as the narrator in La Jetée (1962). \n\nJean Négroni was educated in theater by Albert Camus, and was an early companion of Jean Vilar at the Théâtre National Populaire and at the Festival d'Avignon.  Négroni founded the Maison des arts et de la culture de Créteil at Créteil in 1968, and was its director until 1978...", died:date('2005-05-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xYAVdEbiIvYJgDjlW6gROBSAf0L.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9960"}}, {tmdbId:"9961", properties:{bornIn:"City of Brussels, Belgium", imdbId:"0154001", born:date('1935-12-28'), name:"Hélène Chatelain", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nHélène Chatelain is a French actress who appeared as \"the woman\" in Chris Marker's La jetée (1962)[2] and later worked with playwright Armand Gatti and Iossif Pasternak.  She also is a writer, translator and filmmaker (Goulag). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Hélène Chatelain, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2020-04-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/l6Tu41ajygOXSOH9zwM4ETrjTjd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9961"}}, {tmdbId:"9962", properties:{imdbId:"0359871", name:"Davos Hanich", bio:"Davos Hanich is an actor, known for La Jetée (1962) and A Grin Without A Cat (1977)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vhsWyObZgbZc1maiGis4dvBDsOC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9962"}}, {tmdbId:"9963", properties:{bornIn:"Warsaw, Poland", imdbId:"0496617", born:date('1921-07-21'), name:"Jacques Ledoux", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJacques Ledoux (born in 1921 in Warsaw and died 6 June 1988 in Brussels) was a Belgian cinema specialist, curator of the Royal Film Archive of Belgium (Cinémathèque royale de Belgique) from 1948 to 1988 and the founder of the Cinema Museum in Brussels (Musée du cinéma de Bruxelles) in 1962. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jacques Ledoux, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1988-06-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jgrUVlLQwnLeuhtMWmCnkDYVlKj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9963"}}, {tmdbId:"18612", properties:{bornIn:"Kobe, Japan", imdbId:"0847396", born:date('1930-07-27'), name:"Tadao Takashima", died:date('2019-06-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rfncG3rr2W1orpjnPYlaKFolIHO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18612"}}, {tmdbId:"144797", properties:{imdbId:"0297741", born:date('1931-03-02'), name:"Yû Fujiki", died:date('2005-12-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eEM2qR278vyQHTOUkIeYvMX3GNC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/144797"}}, {tmdbId:"931388", properties:{bornIn:"Nagoya, Aichi Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0034889", born:date('1916-03-01'), name:"Ichirô Arishima", died:date('1987-07-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lexqwPhFtt9aSNIH63FRWCxDxwp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/931388"}}, {tmdbId:"11390", properties:{bornIn:"Connemara, County Galway, Ireland", imdbId:"0000564", born:date('1932-08-02'), name:"Peter O'Toole", bio:"Peter Seamus Lorcan O'Toole (born 2 August 1932) was an Irish actor of stage and screen who achieved stardom in 1962 playing T.  E.  Lawrence in Lawrence of Arabia.  He went on to become a highly-honoured film and stage actor.  He has been nominated for eight Academy Awards, and holds the record for most competitive Academy Award acting nominations without a win.  He has won four Golden Globes, a BAFTA, and an Emmy, and was the recipient of an Honorary Academy Award in 2003 for his body of work...", died:date('2013-12-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bk2AIN5yjqkthDUxUH0Q4U2ekRH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11390"}}, {tmdbId:"12445", properties:{bornIn:"Davenport, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0528987", born:date('1946-07-10'), name:"Sue Lyon", bio:"Sue Lyon was an American screen and television actress.  She joined the entertainment industry as a model at the age of 13, and later rose to prominence and won a Golden Globe for playing the title role in the film Lolita (1962).  Her other notable film appearances included The Night of the Iguana (1964), 7 Women (1966), Tony Rome (1967), and Evel Knievel (1971)...", died:date('2019-12-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1eVgz4ysRoFWQpOaa9XdPGjSgTK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12445"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"12450", properties:{imdbId:"0168324", name:"Gary Cockrell", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xBTcZhZUaiMutrP1voqkzj7zHbh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12450"}}, {tmdbId:"4800", properties:{bornIn:"Madison, Wisconsin, USA", imdbId:"0001687", born:date('1930-06-19'), name:"Gena Rowlands", bio:"Virginia Cathryn \"Gena\" Rowlands (born June 19, 1930) is an American actress.  A four-time Emmy and two-time Golden Globe winner, she is known for her collaborations with her late actor-director husband John Cassavetes in ten films, including A Woman Under the Influence (1974) and Gloria (1980), which earned her nominations for the Academy Award for Best Actress.  She also won the Silver Bear for Best Actress for Opening Night (1977)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qkEeCpF7k4fE1QNQeYf2fdMpu6q.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4800"}}, {tmdbId:"72659", properties:{bornIn:"Montreal, Québec, Canada", imdbId:"0437395", born:date('1922-03-21'), name:"Michael Kane", died:date('2007-12-14'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/72659"}}, {tmdbId:"4765", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0001673", born:date('1922-07-26'), name:"Jason Robards", bio:"Jason Nelson Robards Jr.  (July 26, 1922 – December 26, 2000) was an American actor.  He was a winner of a Tony Award, two Academy Awards and an Emmy Award, making him one of 24 Triple Crown of Acting winners.  He was also a United States Navy decorated combat veteran of World War II. \n\nHe became famous playing works of American playwright Eugene O'Neill and regularly performed in O'Neill's works throughout his career.  Robards was cast both in common-man roles and as well-known historical figures...", died:date('2000-12-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1HEKkA5x5fddJIcy8CIkPDLfx9I.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4765"}}, {tmdbId:"77260", properties:{bornIn:"Ottawa, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0001912", born:date('1941-07-30'), name:"Paul Anka", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8Qx0tMaYEPAWkUOwOnsnm4lZad5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77260"}}, {tmdbId:"6103", properties:{bornIn:"Bucarest, Romania", imdbId:"0336842", born:date('1923-11-27'), name:"Nadia Gray", died:date('1994-06-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sk9BOUtmToAwp13YHX4Ujr42EwD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6103"}}, {tmdbId:"38358", properties:{bornIn:"Tonypandy, Rhondda, Glamorgan, Wales, UK", imdbId:"0396819", born:date('1923-11-06'), name:"Donald Houston", bio:"Donald Daniel Houston  was a Welsh actor ...", died:date('1991-10-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yKFK8f6BaewAWF5NuMwC8SPD0bl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/38358"}}, {tmdbId:"120002", properties:{imdbId:"0112791", name:"Liliane Brousse", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vYtm8F2Z9y0vYaLCR0KwVjJASfS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/120002"}}, {tmdbId:"15666", properties:{bornIn:"Dawson City, Yukon Territory, Canada", imdbId:"0430460", born:date('1902-11-23'), name:"Victor Jory", bio:"Victor Jory was a Canadian stage, film and television actor, best known for his role as Jonas Wilkerson, the brutal and opportunistic overseer, in \"Gone with the Wind\", and as Lamont Cranston, aka 'The Shadow', in the 1942 serial film \"The Shadow\"...", died:date('1982-02-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nCTEVZ6H8nf57MJVwY2Xvl8j2CZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15666"}}, {tmdbId:"15667", properties:{bornIn:"Omaha, Nebraska, USA", imdbId:"0842421", born:date('1932-12-29'), name:"Inga Swenson", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nInga Swenson (born December 29, 1932; Omaha, Nebraska) is an American actress. \n\nInga Swenson was a graduate of Central High School in Omaha, Nebraska, Class of 1950.  Swenson was a member of Alpha Phi sorority at Northwestern University where she studied in their famed Drama Department...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/c09amkuxllrFkiX8mXwrIdcn0H7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15667"}}, {tmdbId:"15668", properties:{bornIn:"Jennings, Hamilton County, Florida, U.S.", imdbId:"0697785", born:date('1936-02-14'), name:"Andrew Prine", bio:"Andrew Lewis Prine (born February 14, 1936) is an American film, stage, and television actor. \n\nPrine was born in Jennings, Florida.  After graduation from Miami Jackson High School in Miami, Prine made his acting debut three years later in an episode of United States Steel Hour.  His next role was in the 1959 Broadway production of Thomas Wolfe's Look Homeward, Angel.  In 1962, Prine was cast in Academy Award-nominated film The Miracle Worker as Helen Keller's older brother James...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hq6XfkWiXOgK9Qkh3tuTvZ44wTX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15668"}}, {tmdbId:"67393", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0004983", born:date('1924-08-31'), name:"Buddy Hackett", bio:"Buddy Hackett  (1924–2003) was an American comedian and actor...", died:date('2003-06-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tc9A8gHLAwMliIwRUs9O9QzlYZF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67393"}}, {tmdbId:"194", properties:{bornIn:"Limerick City, Munster, Ireland", imdbId:"0001321", born:date('1930-10-01'), name:"Richard Harris", bio:"Richard St.  John Harris was an Irish actor, singer-songwriter, theatrical producer, film director and writer.  He appeared on stage and in many films, and is perhaps best known for his roles as King Arthur in Camelot (1967), as Oliver Cromwell in Cromwell (1970) and as Albus Dumbledore in Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone (2001) and Harry Potter and the Chamber of Secrets (2002), his last film...", died:date('2002-10-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/51wDHVFNqrYgvUBMOcACAt4sJU9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/194"}}, {tmdbId:"10021", properties:{bornIn:"Marianglas, Anglesey, Wales, UK", imdbId:"0341518", born:date('1912-05-30'), name:"Hugh Griffith", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nHugh Emrys Griffith (30 May 1912 – 14 May 1980) was an Oscar-winning Welsh film, stage and television actor. \n\n \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Hugh Griffith, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1980-05-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xs1M8RQAwQJ01HzlesOdgpYJkzH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10021"}}, {tmdbId:"28834", properties:{bornIn:"Warsaw, Poland", imdbId:"0631102", born:date('1923-12-15'), name:"Leon Niemczyk", bio:"Leon Stanisław Niemczyk (15 December 1923, Warsaw – 29 November 2006, Łódź) was a Polish actor. \n\nNiemczyk appeared in over 500 films and television shows over the course of his very long career.  His most memorable roles were Fulko de Lorche in Aleksander Ford's The Teutonic Knights and Andrzej in Roman Polanski's Knife in the Water...", died:date('2006-11-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sYFISJFz0OmENcUPUeMXjikJoUL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/28834"}}, {tmdbId:"69632", properties:{imdbId:"0880840", name:"Jolanta Umecka", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69632"}}, {tmdbId:"22931", properties:{bornIn:"Wilno, Wilenskie, Poland [now Vilnius, Lithuania]", imdbId:"0538931", born:date('1938-02-04'), name:"Zygmunt Malanowicz", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nZygmunt Malanowicz (born 4 February 1938) is a Polish film actor.  He has appeared in 30 films since 1962...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/n4cnL3XwuQTKkHjp4p9mPZIw5mc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/22931"}}, {tmdbId:"179399", properties:{imdbId:"0415214", name:"Roger Jacquet", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/179399"}}, {tmdbId:"179400", properties:{imdbId:"0180103", name:"Anne Cornaly", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/179400"}}, {tmdbId:"179401", properties:{imdbId:"0488702", name:"Anker Larsen", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/179401"}}] AS row
