nNorma Crane (November 10, 1928 — September 28, 1973) was an actress of stage, film and television.  Among her best known roles was that of Golde in the 1971 film adaptation of Fiddler on the Roof.  She also starred in They Call Me MISTER Tibbs! and Penelope.  Crane was born in New York City but raised in El Paso, Texas...", died:date('1973-09-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/udldU8UL1lVvKQodSWi2z7OcuiL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/129550"}}, {tmdbId:"112253", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York", imdbId:"0294600", born:date('1938-09-04'), name:"Leonard Frey", bio:"Leonard Frey (September 4, 1938 – August 24, 1988) was an American actor...", died:date('1988-08-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/l8EVoH2d9zHc4ktARpg90jm2K6l.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/112253"}}, {tmdbId:"129551", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, USA", imdbId:"0682000", born:date('1898-06-01'), name:"Molly Picon", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMolly Picon ( February 28, 1898 – April 6, 1992) was an American actress of stage, screen and television, as well as a lyricist.  She was first and foremost a star in Yiddish theatre and film, but as Yiddish theatre faded she began to perform in English-language productions. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Molly Picon, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1992-04-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yTI5UBeIcWiDAy6S4psb0lnK7fM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/129551"}}, {tmdbId:"6355", properties:{bornIn:"Orange, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0001702", born:date('1932-11-10'), name:"Roy Scheider", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nRoy Richard Scheider (November 10, 1932 – February 10, 2008) was an American actor.  He was best known for his role as police chief Martin C.  Brody in Jaws, as choreographer and film director Joe Gideon in All That Jazz, detective Buddy \"Cloudy\" Russo in The French Connection and his role as Captain Nathan Bridger in science fiction television series seaQuest DSV...", died:date('2008-02-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yyZ0DwUz3qAelJIUGVoOktGgMIh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6355"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"15183", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0516215", born:date('1936-10-19'), name:"Tony Lo Bianco", bio:"Tony Lo Bianco (born October 19, 1936) is an American actor in films and television.  Lo Bianco was born in Brooklyn, New York, the son of a taxi driver.  He is known for his roles in the cult films The Honeymoon Killers, God Told Me To, and The French Connection.  Lo Bianco was a Golden Gloves boxer and also founded the Triangle Theatre in 1963, serving as its artistic director for six years.  He also works for OTM Servo Mechanism...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ua1ZOFdDx20yzj3iHPM0u3M98Zf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15183"}}, {tmdbId:"10341", properties:{bornIn:"Stockholm, Sweden", imdbId:"0001180", born:date('1942-10-06'), name:"Britt Ekland", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nBritt-Marie Ekland (born 6 October 1942) is a Swedish actress long resident in the United Kingdom.  She is best known for her roles as a Bond girl in The Man with the Golden Gun, and in the British cult horror film The Wicker Man, as well as her marriage to actor Peter Sellers, and her high-profile social life. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Britt-Marie Ekland, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xwqKmseMHCXwLQGxardWgPTtAcW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10341"}}, {tmdbId:"33323", properties:{bornIn:"Fulham, London, England", imdbId:"0651570", born:date('1929-12-12'), name:"John Osborne", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJohn James Osborne (12 December 1929 – 24 December 1994) was an English playwright, screenwriter, actor and critic of the Establishment.  The success of his 1956 play Look Back in Anger transformed English theatre. \n\nIn a productive life of more than 40 years, Osborne explored many themes and genres, writing for stage, film and TV.  His personal life was extravagant and iconoclastic...", died:date('1994-12-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9oc0faLHrjvZlCnHu62KTNe1f9X.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33323"}}, {tmdbId:"5564", properties:{bornIn:"Milan, Lombardy, Italy", imdbId:"0599998", born:date('1935-06-26'), name:"Maria Monti", bio:"Maria Monti is an Italian film and television actress, singer and songwriter...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/epA2iUetucAGujhIKfR6F54nSgZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5564"}}, {tmdbId:"4971", properties:{bornIn:"New Rochelle, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001069", born:date('1948-03-29'), name:"Bud Cort", bio:"Bud Cort (born Walter Edward Cox on March 29, 1948) is an American film and stage actor, writer, and director.  He is best known for his portrayals of Harold in Hal Ashby's 1971 film Harold and Maude and the titular hero in Robert Altman's 1970 film Brewster McCloud.  Both films have large cult followings today...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/agiubl6msYlKM7DpghIYDw1pcBN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4971"}}, {tmdbId:"19616", properties:{imdbId:"0681954", born:date('1931-10-21'), name:"Vivian Pickles", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19616"}}, {tmdbId:"2549", properties:{bornIn:"Bedford Hills, New York, USA", imdbId:"0400464", born:date('1915-07-16'), name:"Barnard Hughes", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBernard Aloysius Kiernan “Barnard” Hughes (July 16, 1915 – July 11, 2006) was an American actor of theater and film.  Hughes became famous for a variety of roles; his most notable roles came after middle age, and he was often cast as a dithering authority figure or grandfatherly elder. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Barnard Hughes, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2006-07-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1QwqpJ37wE5cjrDxHoTWfZk4oVs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2549"}}, {tmdbId:"15413", properties:{bornIn:"Boston, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0246004", born:date('1929-03-30'), name:"Richard Dysart", bio:"Was an American actor, perhaps best known for his role as Leland McKenzie on the NBC legal drama L. A.  Law.  Dysart served for four years in the Air Force during the Korean War.  In 1979, he was featured in the film Being There, portraying a good-hearted physician.  In 1980, he portrayed Abraham Lincoln's Secretary of War Edwin Stanton in the TV movie The Ordeal of Dr.  Mudd...", died:date('2015-04-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lmjA0ecxTxjZ4j9R7DKNq97Ffil.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15413"}}, {tmdbId:"6354", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0162541", born:date('1935-10-31'), name:"Charles Cioffi", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tNnflWmSuSPjJzthbfkkrYZZmoo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6354"}}, {tmdbId:"234424", properties:{imdbId:"1273131", name:"Fini Straubinger", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/234424"}}, {tmdbId:"1464014", properties:{imdbId:"2786840", name:"M. Baaske", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1464014"}}, {tmdbId:"1464012", properties:{imdbId:"1271751", name:"Heinrich Fleischmann", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1464012"}}, {tmdbId:"19207", properties:{bornIn:"Santa Barbara, California, USA", imdbId:"0000961", born:date('1951-08-30'), name:"Timothy Bottoms", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nTimothy James Bottoms is an American actor and film producer.   He is best known for playing the lead in Johnny Got His Gun; Sonny Crawford in The Last Picture Show; The Paper Chase; and for playing President George W.  Bush multiple times, including on the sitcom That's My Bush!; in the comedy film The Crocodile Hunter: Collision Course and the docudrama DC 9/11: Time of Crisis...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qF99X2tCETDjqV9msKsp7CA6usC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19207"}}, {tmdbId:"1229", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0000313", born:date('1949-12-04'), name:"Jeff Bridges", bio:"American actor Jeff Bridges has starred in over 50 films during his lengthy career.  He comes from a family of performers and was introduced to show business by his father Lloyd.  Jeff is most famous for his work in the films Big Lebowski (1998), Seabiscuit (2003), Crazy Heart (2009), and most recently True Grit (2010).  His accolades include a long list of Academy Award nominations, and one win for Best Actor in 2010. \n\nBridges was born in 1949 and grew up in Los Angeles, California...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xms1RAY6q7Lzp7wNeRCB0kzhucn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1229"}}, {tmdbId:"1036", properties:{bornIn:"Memphis, Tennessee, USA", imdbId:"0001732", born:date('1950-02-18'), name:"Cybill Shepherd", bio:"Cybill Lynne Shepherd is an American actress, singer and former model.  Her best known roles include starring as Jacy in The Last Picture Show, as Betsy in Taxi Driver, as Maddie Hayes on Moonlighting, as Cybill Sheridan on Cybill, and as Phyllis Kroll on The L Word...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hG2RJvjvgy4ch0glP2kLMuoBc7R.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1036"}}, {tmdbId:"8223", properties:{bornIn:"Caterham, Surrey, England", imdbId:"0277424", born:date('1941-03-02'), name:"Jon Finch", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJon Finch (born 2 March 1941) is an English actor noted for many Shakespearean roles.  Perhaps his most notable role was Macbeth in Roman Polanski's film adaptation of Macbeth (1971). \n\nFinch was born in Caterham, Surrey...", died:date('2012-12-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/q0bqeLBrpYcEnE2A2HktLjdajoj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8223"}}, {tmdbId:"12513", properties:{bornIn:"Kensington, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0000768", born:date('1945-05-14'), name:"Francesca Annis", bio:"Francesca Annis (born 14 May 1945) is a British actress, known for her film and television appearances, most recently in the BBC series Wives and Daughters, Cranford, and Deceit. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Francesca Annis, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rtbYkuenkq8Kfc5LwzWYtVD3eNH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12513"}}, {tmdbId:"68985", properties:{imdbId:"0789864", born:date('1945-01-21'), name:"Martin Shaw", bio:"Martin Shaw is an English actor.  He is known for his roles in the television series The Professionals, The Chief, Judge John Deed and Inspector George Gently.  He has also acted on stage and in film, and has narrated numerous audiobooks and presented various television series, including the 2006 series Martin Shaw: Aviators...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/p4EBXNz2nLQGHoAfsTrieqLX4nn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/68985"}}, {tmdbId:"10732", properties:{imdbId:"0063027", name:"Terence Bayler", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ui0sfTzTnum4IkFVrLdpOsUbJDL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10732"}}, {tmdbId:"9807", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0041281", born:date('1940-06-01'), name:"Rene Auberjonois", bio:"An American actor, known for portraying Father Mulcahy in the movie version of M-A-S-H and for creating a number of characters in long-running television series, including Clayton Endicott III on Benson (for which he was nominated for an Emmy Award), Odo on Star Trek: Deep Space Nine, and attorney Paul Lewiston on Boston Legal. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article René Auberjonois (actor), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2019-12-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qejqtzg4Ol2qIupgGAINeJoNjul.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9807"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"21416", properties:{bornIn:"Albany, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001137", born:date('1939-09-05'), name:"William Devane", bio:"William Joseph Devane (born September 5, 1937) is an American film, television and theater actor,  known for his role as Greg Sumner on the primetime soap opera Knots Landing and as James Heller on the Fox serial drama 24, the role he reprised in Live Another Day.  He is also known for his supporting roles in films such as McCabe & Mrs.  Miller,  Family Plot), Marathon Man, Rolling Thunder and Space Cowboys...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7MGLsJXn3URkYeZzqzAcgpYXFum.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21416"}}, {tmdbId:"980357", properties:{imdbId:"0300991", name:"Jacques Gagnon", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/980357"}}, {tmdbId:"980358", properties:{imdbId:"0150619", name:"Lyne Champagne", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/980358"}}, {tmdbId:"1191548", properties:{bornIn:"Montréal, Québec, Canada", imdbId:"0239760", born:date('1923-10-25'), name:"Jean Duceppe", died:date('1990-12-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8WLceWfLB6Jgvoi12q3jPwXmgUV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1191548"}}, {tmdbId:"980739", properties:{imdbId:"0857789", name:"Olivette Thibault", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/980739"}}, {tmdbId:"32067", properties:{bornIn:"Worcestershire, England, UK", imdbId:"0122784", born:date('1936-03-30'), name:"Mark Burns", died:date('2007-05-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1qNP7OEcbaX1nBYB5v5getK5ED2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32067"}}, {tmdbId:"32066", properties:{imdbId:"0723235", born:date('1924-07-19'), name:"Nora Ricci", died:date('1976-04-16'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32066"}}, {tmdbId:"12522", properties:{bornIn:"Gwaun-Cae-Gurwen, Glamorgan, Wales", imdbId:"0680795", born:date('1934-05-14'), name:"Siân Phillips", bio:"Siân Phillips (born Jane Elizabeth Ailwên Phillips in Gwaun-Cae-Gurwen, Glamorgan, Wales) is a Welsh actress, author and singer. \n\nPhillips was the daughter of Sally (née Thomas), a teacher, and David Phillips, a steelworker-turned-policeman.  She is a Welsh-speaker and in the first volume of her autobiography, \"Private Faces\", she notes that she spoke only Welsh for much of her childhood, learning English by listening to the radio...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oWEEaFtcysvSG6KnT1GALh7sY1y.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12522"}}, {tmdbId:"100095", properties:{bornIn:"Mainz-Kastel, Wiesbaden, Germany", imdbId:"0418111", born:date('1935-10-04'), name:"Horst Janson", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/AnK3j2kmIizi0AVeSx50Se6OdB3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100095"}}, {tmdbId:"2516", properties:{bornIn:"Long Beach, California, USA", imdbId:"0001875", born:date('1936-05-20'), name:"Anthony Zerbe", bio:"Anthony Zerbe is an American stage, film and Emmy-winning television actor, best known as the post-apocalyptic cult leader Matthias in the feature film \"The Omega Man\", and as Milton Krest in the 1989 James Bond film \"Licence to Kill\"...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/i6bSWWUJrzh3KeckBeE7uNeZ6KM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2516"}}, {tmdbId:"43976", properties:{bornIn:"Atlantic City, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0143614", born:date('1938-12-31'), name:"Rosalind Cash", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nRosalind Cash (December 31, 1938 – October 31, 1995) was an American singer and actress, whose best known film role was as Charlton Heston's character's love interest Lisa, in the 1971 science fiction cult classic, The Omega Man.  To soap audiences, she is probably best remembered as Mary Mae Ward on General Hospital from 1994–1995. \n\nCash was the second of four children.  Her siblings were John (1936–1998), Robert, and Helen...", died:date('1995-10-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/W2KSFKmajoGQTVNmhQYm2jeQw0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/43976"}}, {tmdbId:"68681", properties:{bornIn:"Germany", imdbId:"0467178", born:date('1944-06-27'), name:"Paul Koslo", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nPaul Koslo (June 27, 1944 - January 9, 2019) was a German-Canadian actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Paul Koslo, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2019-01-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qrDQ6z3qt9qmgLMfbaVieNlL6fn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/68681"}}, {tmdbId:"130138", properties:{imdbId:"0493394", born:date('1940-09-25'), name:"Mert Lawwill", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMert Lawwill is an American dirt-track and road racer, born on September 25, 1940 in Boise, Idaho. \n\nHe started his racing career as an amateur racer on the local TT track in Boise and, later, scramble races across the United States Northwest . \n\nHe turned professional in 1963 after moving to California and, in 1964, signed a contract to race dirt-track for manufacturer Harley-Davidson, with which he would stay for the rest of his racing career...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/130138"}}, {tmdbId:"41232", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0910055", born:date('1941-01-31'), name:"Jessica Walter", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJessica Walter (born January 31, 1941) is an American actress, known for the film Play Misty for Me and for her role as Lucille Bluth on the sitcom Arrested Development.  She had a starring role for the first half of season 1 of 90210.  She currently does the voice for Malory Archer in the FX animated series Archer and stars as Elaine Robbins in Retired at 35...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zPHpjVlg6nTKnyXWq8rreW6q1x.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41232"}}, {tmdbId:"50234", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0005234", born:date('1940-12-11'), name:"Donna Mills", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDonna Mills (born December 11, 1942) is an American actress, most well known for her role as Abby Fairgate Cunningham Ewing Sumner on the primetime soap opera Knots Landing. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Donna Mills, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9GbcmJlKxGM8OJFsg4FCVkEsxRd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/50234"}}, {tmdbId:"95564", properties:{bornIn:"Salem, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0488024", born:date('1914-10-04'), name:"John Larch", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJohn Larch (October 4, 1914 - October 16, 2005) was an American film and television actor. \n\nAfter his lead role in the radio serial Captain Starr of Space (1953–54), John Larch entered films in 1954.  He usually appeared in westerns (How The West Was Won) and action films, including Miracle of the White Stallions as General George S.  Patton Jr.  (1963), Collision Course: Truman vs...", died:date('2005-10-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/toed6dnkBQGYOg3e5uk4inCVdLN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95564"}}, {tmdbId:"7710", properties:{bornIn:"Casalecchio di Reno, Bologna", imdbId:"0079341", born:date('1927-05-01'), name:"Laura Betti", died:date('2004-07-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bmHSSa73UxMnUJjmooKzPv1INWp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7710"}}, {tmdbId:"29429", properties:{bornIn:"Bari, Puglia, Italy", imdbId:"0190977", born:date('1924-09-05'), name:"Riccardo Cucciolla", bio:"Riccardo Cucciolla (5 September 1924 – 17 September 1999) was an Italian actor and voice actor.  He appeared in 60 films between 1953 and 1999.  He won the Best Actor Award at the 1971 Cannes Film Festival for the film Sacco & Vanzetti. \n\nBorn in Bari, in southern Italy, Cucciolla gained a degree in law, then made his stage debut in an amateur production in his home city...", died:date('1999-09-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xIGvGLXRTitBTGfm5WbsRIVBruU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29429"}}, {tmdbId:"236087", properties:{bornIn:"San Severo, Italy", imdbId:"0292318", born:date('1951-03-13'), name:"Rosanna Fratello", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cwtx2tQxjrkX8AQRrcSOjyp5y3n.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/236087"}}, {tmdbId:"6487", properties:{bornIn:"New Rochelle, New York, USA", imdbId:"0745780", born:date('1942-07-09'), name:"Richard Roundtree", bio:"An American actor and former fashion model.  He is best known for his portrayal of private detective John Shaft in the 1971 film Shaft and in its two sequels, Shaft's Big Score (1972) and Shaft in Africa (1973). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Richard Roundtree, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cF7WMpXLQb6pKHconoUXQ46irQE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6487"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"6561", properties:{bornIn:"St. Louis, Missouri, U.S.", imdbId:"0348214", born:date('1929-10-02'), name:"Moses Gunn", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMoses Gunn (October 2, 1929 – December 17, 1993) was an American actor.  An Obie Award-winning stage player, he co-founded the Negro Ensemble Company in the 1960s.  His 1962 Broadway debut was in Jean Genet's The Blacks.  He was nominated for a 1976 Tony Award as Best Actor (Play) for The Poison Tree and played Othello on Broadway in 1970...", died:date('1993-12-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dycf1254iAtH5t90sNAUvizVsie.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6561"}}, {tmdbId:"6562", properties:{imdbId:"0820626", born:date('1966-07-15'), name:"Christopher St. John", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nChristopher St.  John (sometimes credited at Chris St.  John) is an African-American film and television actor.  He is also a film producer, film director and screenwriter.  He also played a minor role in Remington Steele. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Christopher St...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6DzoUdWL4MAdvWUu5bFe8VHvVHo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6562"}}, {tmdbId:"12121", properties:{bornIn:"Glendale, California, USA", imdbId:"0693420", born:date('1942-01-05'), name:"Cliff Potts", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nCliff Potts (born January 5, 1942) is an American television and film actor most noted for supporting roles and guest appearances in more than sixty episodic television series between 1967 and 1999. \n\nPotts was a regular supporting player during the first season of The Name of the Game, a revolving 90-minute 1968 series about a publishing empire that featured Tony Franciosa, Gene Barry, and Robert Stack...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/j9GiQcnufGNAeKkB0QoNxxIuKyk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12121"}}, {tmdbId:"12122", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0726492", born:date('1939-10-31'), name:"Ron Rifkin", bio:"Ron Rifkin (born October 31, 1939) is an American actor.  His is best-known for his roles as Arvin Sloane on the spy drama Alias and as Saul Holden on the American family drama Brothers &amp; Sisters. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Ron Rifkin  licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fj2u4t6nG0HGYFtRVDUTNbUtEtl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12122"}}, {tmdbId:"12123", properties:{bornIn:"Tulsa, Oklahoma, USA", imdbId:"0006956", name:"Jesse Vint", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/h87WgEkcFDjXFmQ5lQ8yYiC3cmI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12123"}}, {tmdbId:"38913", properties:{imdbId:"0274731", born:date('1955-09-29'), name:"Benoît Ferreux", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/38913"}}, {tmdbId:"24814", properties:{bornIn:"Angers, Maine-et-Loire, France", imdbId:"0004625", born:date('1921-05-19'), name:"Daniel Gélin", bio:"Ancien élève du lycée Institution Saint-Malo, Daniel Gélin était dans les mêmes classes que Jean Le Bot, professeur des universités et amateur de marine.  Il monte à Paris où il suit les cours d'art dramatique de René Simon.  Il entre ensuite auConservatoire national d'art dramatique et y rencontre Louis Jouvet.  Il commence une carrière au théâtre et fait sa première apparition à l'écran en 1940...", died:date('2002-11-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mHuIOb9nmdITI4APqvlIyeWzMpX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24814"}}, {tmdbId:"14947", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0001265", born:date('1950-07-26'), name:"Susan George", bio:"Susan Melody George (born 26 July 1950) is an English stage and screen actress, movie and television show producer...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nihYEUW4gr8027tuSpNRvJKlAp3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14947"}}, {tmdbId:"386", properties:{bornIn:"Wem, Shropshire, England", imdbId:"0891092", born:date('1923-04-04'), name:"Peter Vaughan", bio:"Peter Vaughan (1923-2016) was a British character actor famous for playing imposing, menacing or authoritative figures in film and television across several decades...", died:date('2016-12-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oOW4ZZeLc9KArDs94k15qEVGzKJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/386"}}, {tmdbId:"1589813", properties:{bornIn:"Mullagh, County Cavan, Ireland", born:date('1929-02-07'), name:"T.P. McKenna", bio:"Born in Mullagh, County Cavan, Ireland, Thomas Patrick 'T. P. ' McKenna was a distinguished character actor of film and TV and a prolific stage actor.  He made his stage debut in \"Summer and Smoke\" by Tennessee Williams at the Pike Theatre in Dublin in 1954 and his film debut in the 1960 film The Night Fighters...", died:date('2011-02-13'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1589813"}}, {tmdbId:"26662", properties:{bornIn:"Rio de Janeiro, Brazil", imdbId:"0642198", born:date('1948-02-20'), name:"Jennifer O'Neill", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJennifer O'Neill (born February 20, 1948) is an American actress and author. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jennifer O'Neill, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9lljBGppyGHVs3hwASl3nsiOAKI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/26662"}}, {tmdbId:"119796", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0342201", born:date('1955-06-02'), name:"Gary Grimes", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGary Grimes (born June 2, 1955, in San Francisco) is an American actor. \n\nGary Grimes' first major role was in the 1971 motion picture Summer of '42, playing a teenager who has an affair with a beautiful older woman, played by Jennifer O'Neill.  For that role, Grimes was nominated in 1972 for a Golden Globe Award as Most Promising Newcomer—Male and a BAFTA Award as Best Newcomer...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jEcNeIDMyG6vyDFwUCbZZgaUcMH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/119796"}}, {tmdbId:"51517", properties:{bornIn:"L.A., California", imdbId:"0396749", born:date('1952-07-14'), name:"Jerry Houser", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJerry Houser (born July 14, 1952) is an American character actor and voice actor in film and television. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jerry Houser, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/A3HHKhK5PC5EgL14ENhhkiBvYGQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/51517"}}, {tmdbId:"937333", properties:{imdbId:"0174179", name:"Oliver Conant", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/937333"}}, {tmdbId:"231333", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0372158", born:date('1946-03-05'), name:"Murray Head", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3rwe4tCE6iU2HWyUSVhZmTI3GU8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/231333"}}, {tmdbId:"3672", properties:{bornIn:"Croydon, Surrey, England, UK", imdbId:"0001919", born:date('1907-12-22'), name:"Peggy Ashcroft", bio:"​Dame Edith Margaret Emily Ashcroft, DBE, (22 December 1907 - 14 June 1991) known professionally as Peggy Ashcroft, was an English actress whose career spanned more than sixty years.  Born to a comfortable middle-class family, Ashcroft was determined from an early age to become an actress, despite parental opposition...", died:date('1991-06-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bF2GD1brYDKT17j25ANkZQR739R.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3672"}}, {tmdbId:"70332", properties:{imdbId:"0947935", born:date('1953-07-29'), name:"Maria Yi", bio:"Maria Yi, also known as Yi Yi (Chinese: 衣依) and Maria Yi Dut Wei Lina, ;( born 29 July 1953) is a retired Chinese actress from Shanghai.  She appeared in films by Hong Kong's Golden Harvest Productions in the 1970s, most notably in The Big Boss and Fist of Fury, both starring Bruce Lee...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fR4csLcNuSsyzh1vH4hFrQzO1wQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70332"}}, {tmdbId:"62427", properties:{imdbId:"0862875", born:date('1942-05-28'), name:"James Tien", bio:"James Tien-chun (Chinese: 田俊; born 28 May 1942) is a Hong Kong actor from Guangdong, China.  He appeared in almost 70 films, primarily in Hong Kong action cinema, including roles in the films of martial arts stars including Bruce Lee, Jackie Chan and Sammo Hung.  He often played villains or supporting roles.  He retired from the Hong Kong film industry in 1996...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7Zy46kcjJvojGeCog3pnr0oK0xt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/62427"}}, {tmdbId:"1084494", properties:{imdbId:"0062531", name:"Marilyn Bautista", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xge84OdKZrtv9uCqE7v6WsVZNid.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1084494"}}, {tmdbId:"64929", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0318527", born:date('1908-07-25'), name:"Jack Gilford", bio:"​Jack Gilford (July 25, 1908 - June 4, 1990) was an American stage, film and television actor...", died:date('1990-06-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/b8e1DdQjzZJFR53QE32uJG6FaMY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/64929"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"1225450", properties:{bornIn:"Sharon, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0712644", born:date('1924-09-24'), name:"Lester Rawlins", died:date('1988-03-22'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1225450"}}, {tmdbId:"85148", properties:{bornIn:"Chile", imdbId:"0423526", born:date('1962-10-27'), name:"Brontis Jodorowsky", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/slgotPPxOycH80huLLVhZ4fpp8R.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85148"}}, {tmdbId:"85149", properties:{imdbId:"0499191", name:"José Legarreta", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85149"}}, {tmdbId:"97351", properties:{bornIn:"Boston, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0852510", born:date('1948-03-12'), name:"James Taylor", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lzpOysJYGxDPHHuXB7kSinJEU7P.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/97351"}}, {tmdbId:"97352", properties:{bornIn:"Long Island, New York, USA", imdbId:"0083401", born:date('1953-09-26'), name:"Laurie Bird", died:date('1979-06-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7WEvPfn9dgcT6SM7pOmIpfc37nR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/97352"}}, {tmdbId:"23187", properties:{imdbId:"0933287", name:"Dennis Wilson", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/23187"}}, {tmdbId:"27860", properties:{bornIn:"Boston, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0628017", born:date('1938-11-07'), name:"Barry Newman", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nBarry Foster Newman is an American film, television, and stage actor, famous for his interpretation of Kowalski in the movie Vanishing Point.  He has been nominated for a Golden Globe and Emmy awards. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Barry Newman, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lO5YVjEjM9zHsZ8kjz4QtGy7Der.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27860"}}, {tmdbId:"68091", properties:{bornIn:"Chickasha - Oklahoma - USA", imdbId:"0001476", born:date('1939-06-01'), name:"Cleavon Little", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nCleavon Jake Little (June 1, 1939 – October 22, 1992) was an American film and theatre actor, known for his lead role as Bart in the 1974 Mel Brooks comedy Blazing Saddles and as the irreverent Dr.  Jerry Noland in the early 1970s sitcom Temperatures Rising.  In 1978 he played \"The Prince of Darkness\" in the radio station comedy FM.  He was also in the 1984 action film Toy Soldiers and acted out the role of Super Soul in the film Vanishing Point in 1971...", died:date('1992-10-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jkscUqCsLY4kGS1hpq0M96gvlnM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/68091"}}, {tmdbId:"71019", properties:{imdbId:"0575845", name:"Victoria Medlin", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/biYx4vLxyxbedDAypv4JvS5w4Mu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71019"}}, {tmdbId:"14464", properties:{bornIn:"Taunton, Somerset, England, UK", imdbId:"0000256", born:date('1952-12-20'), name:"Jenny Agutter", bio:"Jennifer Ann \"Jenny\" Agutter (born 20 December 1952) is an English film and television actress.  She began her career as a child actress in the mid 1960s, starring in the BBC television series The Railway Children and the film adaptation of the same book, before moving on to adult roles and relocating to Hollywood. \n\nShe played Alex Price in An American Werewolf in London, Jessica 6 in Logan's Run, Joanne Simpson in Child's Play 2 and Jill Mason in Equus...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hxroyCTMk54hesfCRo4g6Jwc8dT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14464"}}, {tmdbId:"40148", properties:{bornIn:"Wandsworth, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0736312", born:date('1962-01-26'), name:"Luc Roeg", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dxCGEwpEt8Ga6gBqI7nH8sT3Van.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/40148"}}, {tmdbId:"53023", properties:{bornIn:"Arnhem Land, Northern Territory, Australia", imdbId:"0347858", born:date('1953-07-01'), name:"David Gulpilil", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDavid Gulpilil Ridjimiraril Dalaithngu (Gurlpilil is linguistically correct though he is sometimes credited as David Gumpilil; born 1 July 1953), is an Indigenous Australian traditional dancer and actor.  His first starring role was Walkabout.  A portrait of Gulpilil by Craig Ruddy won the 2004 Archibald Prize, Australia's best known art prize...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/d5xb4nF5C1ucsp8JgbyplVey849.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53023"}}, {tmdbId:"42841", properties:{bornIn:"Mosman, Sydney, New South Wales, Australia", imdbId:"0576851", born:date('1934-05-01'), name:"John Meillon", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJohn Meillon  (1 May 1934 – 11 August 1989) was an legendary Australian actor, most widely known outside Australia for his role as Walter Reilly in the films Crocodile Dundee and Crocodile Dundee II.  He also voiced Victoria Bitter beer commercials until his death. \n\nMeillon was born in Mosman, Sydney.  He began his acting career at the age of eleven in the ABC's radio serial \"Stumpy\", and made his first stage appearance the following year...", died:date('1989-08-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/k9x2VwKqiTxTKP1WIgOM1AtZf2G.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/42841"}}, {tmdbId:"3461", properties:{bornIn:"Malden, Massachusetts, U.S.", imdbId:"0016776", born:date('1907-06-16'), name:"Jack Albertson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Jack Albertson (June 16, 1907 – November 25, 1981) was an American character actor dating to vaudeville.   A comedian, dancer, singer, and musician, Albertson is perhaps best known for his roles as Manny Rosen in The Poseidon Adventure (1972), Grandpa Joe in the 1971 version of Willy Wonka and the Chocolate Factory, Amos Slade in the 1981 animated film \"The Fox and the Hound\" (1981), and as Ed Brown in the 1974-1978 television sitcom Chico and the Man...", died:date('1981-11-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6Ed6n1sfOlOvr0F7sEDiHvQnp96.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3461"}}, {tmdbId:"3462", properties:{bornIn:"Dallas, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0652578", born:date('1957-11-01'), name:"Peter Ostrum", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.  Peter Ostrum   (born 1957/1958 in Dallas, Texas)  is an American large animal veterinarian and former child actor whose only film role was Charlie Bucket in the 1971 motion picture Willy Wonka & the Chocolate Factory.  A native of Cleveland,  Ostrum practices in Glenfield, New York,  and lives in nearby Lowville  with his wife Loretta (née Lepkowski), and two children: his son Leif and daughter Helenka...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/a3jbe78Rs8gjJrFxl0PoVtayNbf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3462"}}, {tmdbId:"3463", properties:{bornIn:"Wigan, Lancashire, England, UK", imdbId:"0455702", born:date('1934-01-08'), name:"Roy Kinnear", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Roy Mitchell Kinnear (8 January 1934 – 20 September 1988) was an English character actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Roy Kinnear, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1988-09-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cuKguENjdEiNhNArAL5CqIaTEfE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3463"}}, {tmdbId:"20546", properties:{bornIn:"Mexico City, Distrito Federal, Mexico", imdbId:"0737928", born:date('1944-08-18'), name:"Helena Rojo", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6Fi8mqFuyZovj5lQpxJKvDJRBSJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20546"}}, {tmdbId:"20547", properties:{imdbId:"0215683", name:"Del Negro", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20547"}}, {tmdbId:"20548", properties:{bornIn:"Maputo, Moçambique", imdbId:"0346087", born:date('1931-08-22'), name:"Ruy Guerra", bio:"Ruy Alexandre Guerra Coelho Pereira (born August 22, 1931) is a Portuguese-Brazilian film director, screenwriter, film editor, and actor.  Guerra was born a Portuguese citizen in Lourenço Marques (today Maputo) in Mozambique, when it was still Portuguese colony. \n\nGuerra studied at IDHEC film school in Paris from 1952.  In 1958 he started his career as an assistant director in several French films.  Later on he immigrated to Brazil, where he directed his first feature film, Os Cafajestes (1962)...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20548"}}, {tmdbId:"20017", properties:{bornIn:"Kiel, Germany", imdbId:"0141380", born:date('1940-02-29'), name:"Margit Carstensen", bio:"Margit Carstensen (born 29 February 1940) is a German theatre and film actress, best known outside Germany for roles in the works of film director Rainer Werner Fassbinder...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/g4uPTjUFsuBjxC9dSK0Yk8wQ9M5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20017"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"10627", properties:{bornIn:"Tegernsee, Germany", imdbId:"0559837", born:date('1954-12-14'), name:"Eva Mattes", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/63ET2xZ3ezbDGKwXxz2eqwX0pxB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10627"}}, {tmdbId:"10767", properties:{bornIn:"Hollywood, California, USA", imdbId:"0001347", born:date('1948-02-05'), name:"Barbara Hershey", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.  Barbara Hershey (born Barbara Lynn Herzstein; February 5, 1948),  also known as Barbara Seagull,  is an American actress.  In a career spanning nearly 50 years, she has played a variety of roles on television and in cinema, in several genres including westerns and comedies.  Although she began acting at age 17 in 1965, Hershey did not achieve much critical acclaim until the latter half of the 1980s...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1Jx1dL18h6GTASqiEQc0Mgiqn9j.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10767"}}, {tmdbId:"141", properties:{bornIn:"Hollywood, Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0001016", born:date('1936-12-08'), name:"David Carradine", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.  David Carradine (born John Arthur Carradine; December 8, 1936 – June 3, 2009) was an American character actor, best known for his role as warrior monk, Kwai Chang Caine, in the 1970s television series, Kung Fu  which later had a 1990s sequel series, Kung Fu: The Legend Continues.  He was a member of a productive acting family dynasty that began with his father, John Carradine...", died:date('2009-06-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vOmuNT6lazTKKacbpCs6SgOB3Y7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/141"}}, {tmdbId:"73194", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York USA", imdbId:"0697587", born:date('1938-02-16'), name:"Barry Primus", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nBarry Primus (born February 16, 1938) is an American television and film actor. \n\nPrimus is primarily an actor, but has also doubled and tripled as writer and director.  He worked on stage for the first decade of his career.  He gained some experience on TV in shows like The Defenders, East Side/West Side and The Virginian.  He then made his screen bow in the Manhattan-filmed The Brotherhood (1968)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aHGNNA8YkPQfRavLvLhKodoCkdf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/73194"}}, {tmdbId:"10939", properties:{bornIn:"West Virginia, USA", imdbId:"0143378", born:date('1939-06-08'), name:"Bernie Casey", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBernard Terry \"Bernie\" Casey (June 8, 1939 – September 19, 2017) was a renowned professional actor who initially had a stellar career as an interscholastic, intercollegiate and professional football player.  Casey was also a record-breaking track and field athlete for Bowling Green State University.  As one of the nation's best high-hurdlers; Casey earned All-America recognition and a trip to the finals at the 1960 United States Olympic Trials...", died:date('2017-09-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mFvNFSX8cDHwKyC9GxmjOAgCAA5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10939"}}, {tmdbId:"3799", properties:{bornIn:"New York City - New York - USA", imdbId:"0001850", born:date('1937-04-06'), name:"Billy Dee Williams", bio:"William December \"Billy Dee\" Williams Jr.  (born April 6, 1937) is an American actor, voice actor, and artist.  He is best known as Lando Calrissian in the Star Wars franchise, first in the early 1980s, and nearly forty years later in The Rise of Skywalker (2019), marking one of the longest intervals between onscreen portrayals of a character by the same actor in American film history...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dCiHLiCapPuRwKkM1ytVZ7PwYQY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3799"}}, {tmdbId:"41218", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0001902", born:date('1951-02-20'), name:"Edward Albert", bio:"Edward Albert was an American film and television actor.   The only son of actor Eddie Albert and Mexican actress Margo, he was also known as Edward Laurence Albert and Laurence Edward Albert (to further avoid confusion with his same-named father), as well as occasionally Eddie Albert, Jr...", died:date('2006-09-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/a48LqHHjoqO4ObEeMhFBq7gsEL8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41218"}}, {tmdbId:"13919", properties:{bornIn:"Fulmer, Buckinghamshire, England", imdbId:"0001868", born:date('1942-03-27'), name:"Michael York", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMichael York, OBE (born Michael Hugh Johnson; 27 March 1942) is an English actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Michael York (actor), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tutdIz0uuQ6fyPMoQ4HpCgy2uQu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13919"}}, {tmdbId:"32059", properties:{bornIn:"Hamburg, Germany", imdbId:"0340926", born:date('1932-04-06'), name:"Helmut Griem", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nHelmut Griem (born April 6, 1932 in Hamburg – November 19, 2004 in Munich) was a German actor. \n\nGriem was primarily a German-speaking stage actor, appearing at the Thalia Theater in Hamburg, the Deutsches Schauspielhaus in Hamburg, the Burgtheater in Vienna, the Staatliches Schauspielbühnen in Berlin, in the Munich Kammerspiele, and finally in the Staatstheater am Gärtnerplatz, also in Munich...", died:date('2004-11-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hWZ4VvejLSQzl3xJb5IqAGZxXKQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32059"}}, {tmdbId:"6748", properties:{bornIn:"Cleveland - Ohio - USA", imdbId:"0001297", born:date('1932-04-11'), name:"Joel Grey", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJoel Grey (born April 11, 1932) is an American stage and screen actor, singer, and dancer, best known for his role as the Master of Ceremonies in both the stage and film adaptation of the Kander &amp; Ebb musical Cabaret.  He has won the Academy Award, Tony Award and Golden Globe Award.  He also originated the role of the Wizard in the acclaimed musical Wicked.  Grey is currently featured in the Broadway revival of Anything Goes as Moonface Martin...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/JTvL1BdxNErOj0r5HOCiYdEjuc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6748"}}, {tmdbId:"1039", properties:{bornIn:"Norristown, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0001967", born:date('1935-10-18'), name:"Peter Boyle", bio:"Peter Lawrence Boyle, Jr.  (October 18, 1935 – December 12, 2006) was an American actor, best known for his role as Frank Barone on the sitcom Everybody Loves Raymond, and as a comical monster in Mel Brooks' film spoof Young Frankenstein (1974). \n\nBoyle, who won an Emmy Award in 1996 for a guest-starring role on the science-fiction drama The X-Files, won praise in both comedic and dramatic parts following his breakthrough performance in the 1970 film Joe...", died:date('2006-12-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6TapQmC46mPDYrwm67tyJaEM97I.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1039"}}, {tmdbId:"94294", properties:{bornIn:"Miami, Oklahoma, USA", imdbId:"0692093", born:date('1912-09-24'), name:"Don Porter", bio:"Donald \"Don\" Porter  was an American actor who appeared in a number of films in the 1940s, including Top Sergeant and Eagle Squadron.   On television, he portrayed the widowed father of 15-year-old Frances \"Gidget\" Lawrence (Sally Field) in the 1965 ABC sitcom Gidget.   Besides his work in film and television, Porter was active on stage, as he acted in more than 200 plays, including The Front Page, Plaza Suite, and Any Wednesday...", died:date('1997-02-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mDueUqwwsaVrD5uY1ZHbQEUAnXW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94294"}}, {tmdbId:"15753", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0409866", born:date('1936-04-24'), name:"Jill Ireland", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJill Dorothy Ireland (April 24, 1936 – May 18, 1990) was an English actress, best known for her many films with her second husband, Charles Bronson. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jill Ireland, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1990-05-18'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15753"}}, {tmdbId:"14814", properties:{bornIn:"Verona, Italy", imdbId:"0157067", born:date('1924-03-02'), name:"Walter Chiari", died:date('1991-12-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nNyGI07f0bXhiMtC3Rc3Veo3cVq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14814"}}, {tmdbId:"24684", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0291289", born:date('1905-06-29'), name:"Paul Frankeur", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPaul Frankeur (29 June 1905 - 27 October 1974) was a French actor who appeared in films by Jacques Tati (Jour de fête) and Luis Buñuel (The Discreet Charm of the Bourgeoisie and The Phantom of Liberty).  He was sometimes credited as Paul Francoeur...", died:date('1974-10-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mbKwqRsKZv6vf1hUdCTMDDePv6T.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24684"}}, {tmdbId:"38341", properties:{bornIn:"Boulogne-Billancourt, Seine [now Hauts-de-Seine], France", imdbId:"0644680", born:date('1939-08-09'), name:"Bulle Ogier", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nBulle Ogier (born Marie-France Thielland on 9 August 1939) is a French actress. \n\nOgier's first appearance on screen was in Voilà l'Ordre, a short film directed by Jacques Baratier with a number of the then-emerging young singers of the 1960s in France, including Boris Vian, Claude Nougaro, etc...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mmZ0t8OP2qE35YlcxXBRTfyUZiS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/38341"}}, {tmdbId:"18666", properties:{bornIn:"Hollywood, California, USA", imdbId:"0614916", born:date('1929-07-31'), name:"Don Murray", bio:"Donald Patrick \"Don\" Murray (born July 31, 1929) is an American actor. \n\nMurray was born in Hollywood, California.  He attended East Rockaway High School (class of 1947) in East Rockaway, New York where he played football and track, was a member of the student government and glee club and joined the Alpha Phi Chapter of the Omega Gamma Delta Fraternity.  From high school he went on to the American Academy of Dramatic Arts...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6bLMnvN8xL3kIfR84m8HqqCbdYG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18666"}}, {tmdbId:"98797", properties:{imdbId:"0722440", born:date('1932-04-10'), name:"Hari Rhodes", died:date('1992-01-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tYEmkxghF55Bv2GcyIVbyOyn36P.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/98797"}}, {tmdbId:"13726", properties:{bornIn:"Louisville, Kentucky, USA", imdbId:"0000885", born:date('1937-07-06'), name:"Ned Beatty", bio:"Ned Thomas Beatty (born July 6, 1937) is an American actor.  He has been nominated for an Academy Award, two Emmy Awards and a Golden Globe Award; and has won a Drama Desk Award. \n\nThese nominations stemmed from his performances in films and TV series like Network (1976), Friendly Fire (1979), Last Train Home (1990), Hear My Song (1991) and the adaptation movie \"Cat on a Hot Tin Roof\" (2004)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/j7Uf78DCxB4OAGxkoFxLZkktVrm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13726"}}, {tmdbId:"780", properties:{bornIn:" Cloudcroft, New Mexico, U.S.", imdbId:"0001074", born:date('1938-07-23'), name:"Ronny Cox", bio:"Daniel Ronald \"Ronny\" Cox (born July 23, 1938) is an American character actor, singer/songwriter, and guitarist...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/q8jgkSXRPi0uWCbKnBuq4PlSJtR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/780"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"82830", properties:{bornIn:"Santa Rosa, California, USA", imdbId:"0067146", born:date('1925-11-03'), name:"Robert Quarry", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRobert Walter Quarry (3 November 1925 – 20 February 2009) was an American actor, known for several prominent horror film roles. \n\nQuarry was born in Santa Rosa, California, the son of Mable and Paul Quarry, a doctor.  His films include Count Yorga, Vampire (1970), its sequel The Return of Count Yorga (1971), and Dr.  Phibes Rises Again (1972), in which he played alchemist Dr...", died:date('2009-02-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lr88ZEjDtRCvIz2iuNhWKyUgRcr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82830"}}, {tmdbId:"42572", properties:{bornIn:"Hereford, Herefordshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0717189", born:date('1919-06-17'), name:"Beryl Reid", bio:"Beryl Elizabeth Reid, OBE (17 June 1919 – 13 October 1996) was a British actress of stage and screen. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Beryl Reid, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1996-10-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4e4RkRKMVBwlLvvbmhKwfPu4wDY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/42572"}}, {tmdbId:"86670", properties:{bornIn:"Terijoki, Vyborg, Finland [now Zelenogorsk, Kurortny District, St. Petersburg, Russia]", imdbId:"0900120", born:date('1917-04-05'), name:"Georgiy Vitsin", died:date('2001-10-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ou7ngCUELxCH7UhSxTDtEpiErZA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/86670"}}, {tmdbId:"86669", properties:{imdbId:"0613638", born:date('1928-10-21'), name:"Radner Muratov", died:date('2004-12-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/q7MayoKp9FZ7wiPL5heVnfAEfSO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/86669"}}, {tmdbId:"1190224", properties:{imdbId:"0469434", born:date('1934-10-13'), name:"Saveliy Kramarov", died:date('1995-06-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qK4uiAx5Y2CMPjY9zDzFiIAT4eZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1190224"}}, {tmdbId:"942574", properties:{imdbId:"0693449", born:date('1959-04-08'), name:"Nell Potts", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/942574"}}, {tmdbId:"171271", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0908933", born:date('1955-08-02'), name:"Roberta Wallach", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/r1J7aGycvH9PQlGPCjszM1CeGQp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/171271"}}, {tmdbId:"193808", properties:{bornIn:"Fort Sill, Oklahoma, USA ", imdbId:"0523337", born:date('1890-07-27'), name:"Judith Lowry", bio:"Judith Carter Lowry (née Ives; July 27, 1890 – November 29, 1976) was an American actress...", died:date('1976-11-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9849vWYLDiWLGwshaIkgxPg0M1A.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/193808"}}, {tmdbId:"825", properties:{bornIn:"Savannah - Georgia - USA", imdbId:"0005078", born:date('1941-06-02'), name:"Stacy Keach", bio:"Walter Stacy Keach, Jr.  (born June 2, 1941) is an American actor and narrator.  He is most famous for his dramatic roles; however, he has done narration work in educational programming on PBS and the Discovery Channel, as well as some comedy (particularly his role in the FOX sitcom Titus as Ken, the hard-drinking, chain-smoking, womanizing father of comedian Christopher Titus) and musical roles...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ArZIr5uWnAuCQ1rWFfpviSoK6iN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/825"}}, {tmdbId:"59369", properties:{bornIn:" San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0879073", born:date('1945-03-18'), name:"Susan Tyrrell", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSusan Tyrrell (born March 18, 1945) is an American actress of Irish descent, known for her role as Ramona Rickettes in the film Cry-Baby...", died:date('2012-06-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eI03iUgb6rc2UCB6GKPizXePzTy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/59369"}}, {tmdbId:"12407", properties:{bornIn:"Norman, Oklahoma, USA", imdbId:"0163748", born:date('1947-06-20'), name:"Candy Clark", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nCandace June \"Candy\" Clark (born June 20, 1947) is an American film and television actress, well known for her role as Debbie Dunham in the 1973 film American Graffiti, which garnered her an Academy Award nomination as Best Supporting Actress, a character she reprised in 1979 for the sequel More American Graffiti...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eDWbn53Q6vNECgOj68z8NymLv7D.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12407"}}, {tmdbId:"33566", properties:{imdbId:"0930858", name:"Jason Williams", bio:"Actor who appeared in movies starting in 70's thru the 90's and starred in the sci-fi porno spoof \"Flesh Gordon...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/njrqD2ALdn7waEBhGG2TjMKiM3r.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33566"}}, {tmdbId:"33567", properties:{imdbId:"0394131", born:date('1950-01-01'), name:"Suzanne Fields", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ft5jbldEFQiZCvlpumb06KuVACj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33567"}}, {tmdbId:"33568", properties:{imdbId:"0399710", name:"Joseph Hudgins", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33568"}}, {tmdbId:"33569", properties:{imdbId:"0402669", name:"William Dennis Hunt", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pocrsBdZKPmOwTsAX6XUSVhVlCy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33569"}}, {tmdbId:"8224", properties:{bornIn:"Tunbridge Wells, Kent", imdbId:"0566680", born:date('1925-05-26'), name:"Alec McCowen", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nAlexander Duncan \"Alec\" McCowen CBE (born 26 May 1925) is an English actor.  He is known for his work in numerous film and stage productions.  He was awarded the CBE in the 1985 New Year's Honours List. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Alec McCowen, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1ZbsYy9j2QLebJFrg2zTJ62jG2X.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8224"}}, {tmdbId:"8225", properties:{bornIn:"Beeston, Nottinghamshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0287687", born:date('1927-08-21'), name:"Barry Foster", died:date('2002-02-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1RYaB5p1ps1sbKkzKdXoOCYNLyr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8225"}}, {tmdbId:"8226", properties:{bornIn:" Coventry, England", imdbId:"0925794", born:date('1932-06-06'), name:"Billie Whitelaw", bio:"Billie Honor Whitelaw, CBE  was an English stage and screen actress.  She worked in close collaborration with Irish playwright Samuel Beckett for 25 years and wass regarded as one of the foremost interpreters of his works.  She was also known for her portrayal of Mrs Baylock, the demonic nanny in The Omen...", died:date('2014-12-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6KIxHQkGAmXYZRWR12eQyaccDgC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8226"}}, {tmdbId:"73029", properties:{bornIn:" Chincoteague Island, Virginia U.S.", imdbId:"0385830", born:date('1940-11-12'), name:"Skip Hinnant", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSkip Hinnant (born September 12, 1940) is an American actor and comedian. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Skip Hinnant, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/73029"}}, {tmdbId:"73030", properties:{bornIn:" New York City, New York, United States", imdbId:"0502158", born:date('1911-08-08'), name:"Rosetta LeNoire", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRosetta LeNoire (August 8, 1911 - March 17, 2002) was an American stage, screen, and television actress, as well as a Broadway producer and casting agent. \n\nAs a young girl LeNoire suffered from rickets, which her godfather, Bill \"Bojangles\" Robinson, helped her overcome by teaching her to dance.  LeNoire made her acting debut in a 1939 production of The Hot Mikado, starring Robinson, in which she played \"Little Maid From School\" Peep-Bo...", died:date('2002-03-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bI7IRVBXANRTIj65dagqEhoWXCG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/73030"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"73031", properties:{bornIn:"Anderson, South Carolina, USA", imdbId:"0567315", born:date('1928-10-18'), name:"John McCurry", died:date('1989-03-05'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/73031"}}, {tmdbId:"4978", properties:{imdbId:"0257568", name:"Judy Engles", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uWyN2f9QWemnjJd2iw7v3bQ8NIs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4978"}}, {tmdbId:"49352", properties:{bornIn:"Portland, Oregon, USA", imdbId:"0001783", born:date('1948-07-28'), name:"Sally Struthers", bio:"Cute as a button and with a petite, porcelain prettiness and vulnerability that endeared her to the American public, Sally Struthers nabbed a series role in the early 1970s and became a solid part of TV history as a member of a dysfunctional family quartet in the milestone sitcom, \"All in the Family\" (1971).  She was born Sally Ann Struthers on July 28, 1948, in Portland, Oregon and raised there, pursuing an acting career following high school...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9EeuFTEUG1mfPiZwNw38U3ovUa.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/49352"}}, {tmdbId:"3086", properties:{bornIn:"The Bronx, New York, U.S", imdbId:"0144710", born:date('1933-09-04'), name:"Richard S. Castellano", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRichard Salvatore Castellano  (September 4, 1933 – December 10, 1988) was an American actor who is best remembered for his role as Peter Clemenza in The Godfather. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Richard S...", died:date('1988-12-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1vr75BdHWret81vuSJ3ugiCBkxw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3086"}}, {tmdbId:"24501", properties:{bornIn:"Valenciennes, France", imdbId:"0007069", born:date('1934-08-16'), name:"Pierre Richard", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.  Pierre Richard (born Pierre-Richard Maurice Charles Léopold Defays (originally de Fays, his grandfather changed the spelling for unknown reasons), 16 August 1934 in Valenciennes, Nord) is a popular French actor best known for the roles of a clumsy daydreamer in comedy films.  Richard is considered by many, such as Louis de Funès and Gérard Depardieu, to be one of the greatest and most talented French comedians in the last 50 years...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/s3P7GFbSU60YDwogCgPH8p9hDfj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24501"}}, {tmdbId:"24421", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0734000", born:date('1930-04-29'), name:"Jean Rochefort", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nJean Rochefort (born 29 April 1930) is a French actor, with a career that has spanned over five decades. \n\nRochefort was born in Paris, France.  He was educated at the Lycée Pierre Corneille in Rouen He was 19 years old when he entered the Centre d'Art Dramatique de la rue Blanche.  Later he joined the Conservatoire National.  After his national service, in 1953, he worked with the Compagnie Grenier Hussenot as a theatre actor for seven years...", died:date('2017-10-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/arbKHQcsq9FzGkVqfy75SFoE79C.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24421"}}, {tmdbId:"39646", properties:{bornIn:"Toulon, France", imdbId:"0200999", born:date('1938-05-15'), name:"Mireille Darc", bio:"Mireille Darc, who was born in 1938, was often compared to Brigitte Bardot.  Her film career began in 1960 and she went on to make about 50 movies, including 1964’s Dandelion By The Roots which kicked off her work with Lautner.  The pair would go on to make more than a dozen films together including The Great Spy Chase and 1967’s La Grande Sauterelle whose title also became her nickname...", died:date('2017-08-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nUYm3DevxC5yN2KcwUEVm4Jzu93.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/39646"}}, {tmdbId:"14312", properties:{bornIn:"Cincinnati, Ohio, U.S.", imdbId:"0752751", born:date('1928-01-11'), name:"Mitchell Ryan", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMitchell Ryan (born January 11, 1934[1]) is an American actor most recently known for playing Edward Montgomery (Greg's father) on the sitcom Dharma &amp; Greg.  He also worked with his on-screen wife from Dharma &amp; Greg, Susan Sullivan, in the short-lived series Julie Farr, M. D. . \n\nRyan was born in Cincinnati, Ohio and raised in Louisville, Kentucky.  He served in the U. S.  Navy during the Korean War...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8ZILBVAfe5uKy7IQiLtnsmSjPIV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14312"}}, {tmdbId:"24494", properties:{bornIn:"Buenos Aires, Argentina.", imdbId:"0210274", born:date('1923-01-21'), name:"Alberto de Mendoza", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAlberto Manuel Rodríguez-Gallego González de Mendoza was an Argentine film actor who appeared in 114 films between 1930 and 2005, spanning eight decades. \n\nA lifelong figure in Argentine films, De Mendoza appeared in film such as Adán y la serpiente in 1946 and A hierro muere in 1962 often working alongside Olga Zubarry.  In the late 1960s and 1970 he appeared in a number of spaghetti Westerns...", died:date('2011-12-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ogEgFu8N2cxcVyGO2HI4e2osImR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24494"}}, {tmdbId:"70990", properties:{bornIn:"Frankfort, Indiana, USA", imdbId:"0002095", born:date('1902-03-09'), name:"Will Geer", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nWill Geer (March 9, 1902 – April 22, 1978) was an American actor and social activist.  His original name was William Aughe Ghere.  He is remembered for his portrayal of Grandpa Zebulon Tyler Walton in the 1970s TV series, The Waltons.   \n\nGeer made his Broadway debut as Pistol in a 1928 production of Much Ado About Nothing, created the role of Mr...", died:date('1978-04-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7Agfs3T3JRbdibUhF5MSIfnNUQf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70990"}}, {tmdbId:"70991", properties:{bornIn:"USA", imdbId:"0093386", born:date('1947-11-30'), name:"Delle Bolton", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lj4Oiq02vFUu6gsNuG7xinMSlaH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70991"}}, {tmdbId:"70992", properties:{bornIn:"USA", imdbId:"0016365", born:date('1959-09-19'), name:"Josh Albee", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJosh Albee is an American television actor, known for his work as a child actor during the 1970s, and for the role as the young, mute boy in the feature film, Jeremiah Johnson. \n\nAlbee appears to have remained active in the acting profession through the early 1980s.  His later work was mostly in television...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/toBbyR9kLKxb7aMNtneMeQAyytt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70992"}}, {tmdbId:"57723", properties:{bornIn:"Hong Kong - China", imdbId:"0583963", born:date('1952-02-08'), name:"Nora Miao", bio:"Nora Miao (Chinese: 苗可秀, born 8 February 1952) is a Chinese actress, most well known for her roles in Bruce Lee's \"Big Boss\", \"Fist of Fury\" and \"Way of the Dragon\".  Despite her petite frame and cute looks, she proved to be an effective and strong female on the big screen.  She was launched as a sword fighting queen in the movie \"The Comet Strikes\", though she will forever be remembered as the only woman to share an onscreen kiss with Bruce Lee in \"Fist of Fury\"...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gphqT3byol0m7ruKyio3fXoFG1I.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57723"}}, {tmdbId:"9560", properties:{bornIn:"Detroit, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0000995", born:date('1932-12-07'), name:"Ellen Burstyn", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEllen Burstyn  (born December 7, 1932) is an American actress, who has worked in film, stage and television.  Her acting career began in theatre during the late 1950s, and over the next ten years, Burstyn appeared in several films and television series before joining the Actors Studio in 1967.  She achieved recognition for her roles in The Last Picture Show (1971) and The Exorcist (1973), receiving Academy Award nominations for both performances...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cAR8sU569iSJqLy1PwtcBT1syjJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9560"}}, {tmdbId:"1046164", properties:{imdbId:"0732783", born:date('1951-03-04'), name:"Julia Anne Robinson", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1046164"}}, {tmdbId:"73428", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0423663", born:date('1929-09-01'), name:"Tomisaburô Wakayama", bio:"Tomisaburō Wakayama (若山 富三郎), born Masaru Okumura (奥村 勝) was a Japanese actor.   His son is actor Kiichriō Wakayama...", died:date('1992-04-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zQryn4fQE2WgroGsHun01yTAMma.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/73428"}}, {tmdbId:"24548", properties:{bornIn:"Osaezaki-cho, Shizuoka, Japan", imdbId:"0441351", born:date('1938-02-04'), name:"Gô Katô", died:date('2018-06-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wDbLvnl2QM8YvLovV6DBYfcr63N.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24548"}}, {tmdbId:"134020", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0945299", born:date('1915-07-25'), name:"Isao Yamagata", died:date('1996-06-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/x1MgVQC8gT7LwuuJ3NGUOi5QdtB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/134020"}}, {tmdbId:"32715", properties:{bornIn:"Detroit, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0005384", born:date('1944-03-26'), name:"Diana Ross", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDiana Ross (born March 26, 1944) is an American singer, actress, and record producer.  Born and raised in Detroit, Michigan, Ross rose to fame as the lead singer of the vocal group the Supremes, which, during the 1960s, became Motown's most successful act, and are the best charting female group in US history, as well as one of the world's best-selling girl groups of all time...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6xVBaLk6mBeneEQSJchsQ276FTX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32715"}}, {tmdbId:"47759", properties:{bornIn:"Grand Rapids, Michigan, USA ", imdbId:"0130210", born:date('1930-10-04'), name:"James T. Callahan", died:date('2007-08-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tmVnvC6bjxX5PBj1OniCjuahLrc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/47759"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"101582", properties:{bornIn:" Portland, Oregon, USA", imdbId:"0144053", born:date('1948-01-11'), name:"Sandra Cassel", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSandra Peabody (born 11 January 1948) is an American film and stage actress, screenwriter, producer and acting coach.  She is best known for her role as Mari Collingwood in Wes Craven's 1972 film The Last House on the Left (1972).  A cult hit, the film established her as a prominent actress in horror, and she subsequently starred in Voices of Desire (1972), Massage Parlor Murders (1973), and Legacy of Satan (1974)...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101582"}}, {tmdbId:"101583", properties:{bornIn:" Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0335715", born:date('1951-10-13'), name:"Lucy Grantham", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101583"}}, {tmdbId:"101575", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0381450", born:date('1936-09-19'), name:"David Hess", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDavid Alexander Hess (born September 19, 1942) is an American actor and songwriter. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article David Hess, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2011-10-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4NQQLnrzKhcDagcotqh6ez5YwVF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101575"}}, {tmdbId:"100267", properties:{bornIn:"Manhattan, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0511107", born:date('1937-01-19'), name:"Fred J. Lincoln", bio:"Fred J.  Lincoln (born Fred Perna) was an American actor, director, and producer of pornographic films...", died:date('2013-01-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7gmocNn5m2L9nIEgZVzUEqtvz42.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100267"}}, {tmdbId:"51576", properties:{bornIn:"Ryan, Oklahoma", imdbId:"0001569", born:date('1940-03-10'), name:"Chuck Norris", bio:"Carlos Ray \"Chuck\" Norris (born March 10, 1940) is an American martial artist and actor.  After serving in the United States Air Force, he began his rise to fame as a martial artist and has since founded his own school, Chun Kuk Do.  As a result of his \"tough guy\" image, an Internet phenomenon began in 2005 known as Chuck Norris facts, ascribing various implausible or even impossible feats to Norris...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vHUM7KJmapRAKiGO0leQzuJ6um8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/51576"}}, {tmdbId:"143190", properties:{bornIn:"Nanjing, Jiangsu, China", born:date('1929-11-29'), name:"Ping Ou Wei", bio:"Wei Ping-ao (Chinese: 魏平澳, 29 November 1929 – 3 December 1989), also known as Paul Wei, was a Hong Kong-based Chinese actor who started his career in the Shaw Brothers Studio.  He is best known for playing cunning interpreters in Bruce Lee's 1972 films Fist of Fury and Way of the Dragon, in which he dubbed his own voice, and also appeared in films such as Deaf Mute Heroine (1971), Hapkido (1972) and Fists of Bruce Lee (1978).  He suffered from jaundice in his later years...", died:date('1989-12-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oGbzxwMhZViTmTcps75B1tmqQSo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/143190"}}, {tmdbId:"10369", properties:{bornIn:"Towson, Maryland, USA", imdbId:"0001145", born:date('1945-10-19'), name:"Divine", bio:"Divine (19 October 1945 – 7 March 1988), né Harris Glenn Milstead, was an American actor, singer and drag queen.  Described by People magazine as the \"Drag Queen of the Century\", Divine often performed female roles in both cinema and theater and also appeared in women's clothing in musical performances.  Even so, he considered himself to be a character actor and performed male roles in a number of his later films...", died:date('1988-03-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/A3uiSXlOpCJ5ycYO0TGZ0YF9VRT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10369"}}, {tmdbId:"10370", properties:{bornIn:"Baltimora, Maryland, Stati Uniti", imdbId:"0516634", born:date('1944-08-21'), name:"David Lochary", died:date('1977-07-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9ItfkgQsyHyNEQHOscknN3gNkDo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10370"}}, {tmdbId:"10371", properties:{bornIn:"Baltimore, Maryland, USA", imdbId:"0668976", born:date('1947-11-09'), name:"Mary Vivian Pearce", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8sMhO1VeTpPGFPvtXwGAs8b1Vqt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10371"}}, {tmdbId:"9292", properties:{bornIn:"Baltimore, Maryland, USA", imdbId:"0831467", born:date('1947-08-25'), name:"Mink Stole", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nNancy Paine Stoll (born August 25, 1947) better known by the stage name Mink Stole, is an American actress from Baltimore, Maryland.  She began her career working for director John Waters, having appeared in all of his feature films to date (a distinction shared only with Mary Vivian Pearce).  Because of her work with Waters, she is considered one of the Dreamlanders, Waters' ensemble of regular cast and crew members...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tmJc1MwvLUpNMCcHBt1Bw4KsCm5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9292"}}, {tmdbId:"70013", properties:{bornIn:"Sioux City, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0480379", born:date('1936-03-27'), name:"Jerry Lacy", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7CTTjm8Wh2SKH6Cb4RIpNjjn1zn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70013"}}, {tmdbId:"45002", properties:{bornIn:"Albany, California, U.S.", imdbId:"0866986", born:date('1943-12-20'), name:"Angel Tompkins", bio:"Angel Tompkins (born December 20, 1942) is an American actress and Golden Globe nominee, who appeared in several films and television shows. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Angel Tompkins, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/45002"}}, {tmdbId:"2707885", properties:{name:"Hugh Owens", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2707885"}}, {tmdbId:"39024", properties:{bornIn:"Hayfield, Derbyshire, England", imdbId:"0522884", born:date('1915-09-22'), name:"Arthur Lowe", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nArthur Lowe (22 September 1915 – 15 April 1982) was a BAFTA Award winning English actor.  He was best known for playing Captain George Mainwaring in the popular British sitcom Dad's Army from 1968 until 1977. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Arthur Lowe, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1982-04-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8QkpkLQvEnJQavSgZ4heaEujN0A.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/39024"}}, {tmdbId:"38998", properties:{imdbId:"0878302", born:date('1930-04-08'), name:"Dorothy Tutin", died:date('2001-08-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yrpNH2MU3xM3fJGHSMaXTet8vEB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/38998"}}, {tmdbId:"107328", properties:{imdbId:"2014587", born:date('1950-06-29'), name:"Scott Antony", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/107328"}}, {tmdbId:"15735", properties:{bornIn:"Hammersmith, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0000545", born:date('1945-07-26'), name:"Helen Mirren", bio:"Dame Helen Lydia Mirren DBE (née Mironoff) is an English actor.  Mirren began her acting career with the Royal Shakespeare Company in 1967, and is one of the few performers who have achieved the Triple Crown of Acting, having won the Academy Award for Best Actress in 2007, after two previous nominations, for her performance as Queen Elizabeth II in The Queen...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1reKRrsdsHXJaRVHVyOEg4oPTcZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15735"}}, {tmdbId:"119942", properties:{bornIn:"South Shields, England, UK", imdbId:"0447330", born:date('1938-05-03'), name:"Lindsay Kemp", bio:"Lindsay Kemp was an English dancer, actor, teacher, mime artist, and choreographer.  He collaborated with David Bowie as he invented theatrical personas such as Ziggy Stardust and taught Kate Bush how to dance.  He starred in The Wicker Man and collaborated on films with auteurs like Ken Russell and Derek Jarman...", died:date('2018-08-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3eOKl3pMG8nIcil9ZwiVnrruuk1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/119942"}}, {tmdbId:"41278", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0755310", born:date('1948-09-11'), name:"Michael Sacks", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMichael Sacks (born September 11, 1948) is an American actor and tech executive who played the role of Billy Pilgrim in George Roy Hill's Slaughterhouse Five, an adaptation from the novel by Kurt Vonnegut. \n\nSacks also appeared in Steven Spielberg's The Sugarland Express, as the kidnapped highway patrolman; The Amityville Horror, as James Brolin's character's friend and coworker; and Hanover Street, with Harrison Ford...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/61ZvsHCX3O0R6BFubfMa6eukkqF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41278"}}, {tmdbId:"5372", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0500038", born:date('1937-10-11'), name:"Ron Leibman", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRonald Leibman (October 11, 1937 – December 6, 2019) was an American actor.  He won both the Tony Award for Best Actor in a Play and the Drama Desk Award for Outstanding Actor in a Play in 1993 for his performance as Roy Cohn in Angels in America.  Leibman also won a Primetime Emmy Award for his role as Martin 'Kaz' Kazinsky in his short-lived crime drama series Kaz...", died:date('2019-12-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2eGDEZaDFu64AKNsnND9PiwS95g.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5372"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"35370", properties:{bornIn:"Boston, Massachusetts, U.S.", imdbId:"0733929", born:date('1928-09-22'), name:"Eugene Roche", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEugene Harrison Roche (September 22, 1928 - July 28, 2004) was an American actor.  He was the original \"Ajax Man\" in 1970s television commercials. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Eugene Roche, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2004-07-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cY9u3TxO4UlSkxrhqS8TPhpdzzT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/35370"}}, {tmdbId:"91962", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York", imdbId:"0304535", born:date('1942-07-29'), name:"Sharon Gans", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSharon Gans (born July 29, 1942, in New York City) is an American actress.  She played the part of Valencia, Billy Pilgrim's wife, in George Roy Hill's Slaughterhouse Five.  Gans starred in the award-winning documentary Artists and Orphans: A True Drama. \n\nIn October 1988, Gans directed the play The Legend of Sharon Shashanovah, presented at the 47th Street Theater in New York City...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/91962"}}, {tmdbId:"14936", properties:{imdbId:"0147250", name:"Alec Cawthorne", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14936"}}, {tmdbId:"14937", properties:{imdbId:"0560064", name:"John Matthews", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14937"}}, {tmdbId:"124658", properties:{imdbId:"0916354", name:"Chad Webber", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/124658"}}, {tmdbId:"124659", properties:{imdbId:"0463410", name:"Robin Kohn", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8Nne24vOgz0t1nUjvBCIDkVK2ZQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/124659"}}, {tmdbId:"124049", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0790344", born:date('1961-12-21'), name:"Stephen Shea", bio:"Stephen Shea standing in at 6' (1...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dLYwgpoa0jsGihonRhzXMo5hqVQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/124049"}}, {tmdbId:"130916", properties:{imdbId:"0136931", name:"David Carey", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/130916"}}, {tmdbId:"1190211", properties:{bornIn:"Mosca, Russia", imdbId:"0094081", born:date('1950-05-10'), name:"Natalya Bondarchuk", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nNatalya Sergeyevna Bondarchuk (born May 10, 1950) is a Soviet and Russian actress and film director, best known for her appearance in Andrei Tarkovsky's Solaris as \"Hari\".  She is the daughter of the Ukrainian actor Sergei Bondarchuk and the Russian actress Inna Makarova.  Her brother is the film director and actor Fyodor Bondarchuk, her sister is the actress Elena Bondarchuk...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1190211"}}, {tmdbId:"1190206", properties:{bornIn:"Kaunas, Lithuania", imdbId:"0052023", born:date('1924-04-28'), name:"Donatas Banionis", bio:"Donatas Banionis (28 April 1924 – 4 September 2014) was a Lithuanian actor.  He is best known for his performance in the lead role of Tarkovsky's Solaris as Kris Kelvin.  He was born in Kaunas, Lithuania...", died:date('2014-09-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vz0TKZFu1qW5HZFhvIi0JZG9W7D.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1190206"}}, {tmdbId:"8474", properties:{bornIn:"Tallinn, Estonia", imdbId:"0433525", born:date('1919-06-18'), name:"Jüri Järvet", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJüri Järvet (18 June 1919 – 5 July 1995) was an Estonian actor.  His name sometimes appears as Yuri Yevgenyevich Yarvet, an incorrect back-transliteration from the Russian transliteration Юри Евгеньевич Ярвет.  His birthname was Georgi Kuznetsov, and he took the Estonian form in 1938. \n\nJärvet is best known in the West for the role of Dr.  Snaut in Andrei Tarkovsky's Solaris, but he played in numerous other films both in Russian and his native Estonian...", died:date('1995-07-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uTbBreOWl7Yp4t0SXmlUSE4HtaL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8474"}}, {tmdbId:"8476", properties:{bornIn:"Omsk, Soviet Union", imdbId:"0245367", born:date('1939-04-26'), name:"Vladislav Dvorzhetskiy", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nVladislav Dvorzhetsky (26 April 1939 – 28 May 1978) was a Soviet film actor.  He appeared in eighteen films between 1970 and 1978\n\nDvorzhetsky was born in Omsk.  In 1955 he entered the Omsk military medical school.  In 1959 he started active service in the Soviet Army at Sakhalin Island as senior feldsher of the regiment.  During this time he married the first time. \n\nIn 1964 he went back to Omsk and entered the actors' school of Omsk...", died:date('1978-05-28'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8476"}}, {tmdbId:"18249", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001807", born:date('1924-12-19'), name:"Cicely Tyson", bio:"Cicely Tyson was born in Harlem, New York City, where she was raised by her devoutly religious parents, from the Caribbean island of Nevis.  Her mother, Theodosia, was a domestic, and her father, William Tyson, was a carpenter and painter.  She was discovered by a fashion editor at Ebony magazine and, with her stunning looks, she quickly rose to the top of the modeling industry.  In 1957, she began acting in Off-Broadway productions...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iaQjeWcfENq6WYbQK078Vwrb8qf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18249"}}, {tmdbId:"1818", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0934902", born:date('1939-05-22'), name:"Paul Winfield", bio:"Was an American television, film, and stage actor.  He was known for his portrayal of a Louisiana sharecropper who struggles to support his family during the Great Depression in the landmark film Sounder which earned him an Academy Award nomination.  Winfield also portrayed Dr.  Martin Luther King, Jr.  in the television miniseries King, for which he was nominated for an Emmy Award...", died:date('2004-03-07'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6NLUJEFJCJ2Hog1ZOz4K2iyDvMZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1818"}}, {tmdbId:"132357", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0558618", born:date('1914-05-08'), name:"Carmen Mathews", died:date('1995-08-31'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/132357"}}, {tmdbId:"55841", properties:{bornIn:"Utica, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0641938", born:date('1937-09-01'), name:"Ron O'Neal", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \t\n\nRon O'Neal (September 1, 1937 in Utica, New York – January 14, 2004 in Los Angeles, California) was an American actor, director and screenwriter...", died:date('2004-01-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aqcIHjX3MfbdViZlb4jPfzaDsEp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55841"}}, {tmdbId:"88147", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0496942", born:date('1926-11-22'), name:"Carl Lee", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \t\n\nCarlton \"Carl\" Vincent Canegata.  (born November 22, 1926, New York City, New York, - died April 17, 1986, New York City, New York) was an African-American television and stage actor.  He was also the son of late pioneering African American actor/professional boxer Canada Lee (1907–1952). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Carl Lee (actor), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1986-04-17'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88147"}}, {tmdbId:"173682", properties:{imdbId:"0292631", name:"Sheila Frazier", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/krxaCjh6RFbkxfAPcsrxqAOAl8w.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/173682"}}, {tmdbId:"6772", properties:{imdbId:"0364918", born:date('1923-08-17'), name:"Julius Harris", died:date('2004-10-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/s6N2iYTFXdddFQSCiXdv5uGEheg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6772"}}, {tmdbId:"67521", properties:{bornIn:"Stockholm, Stockholms län, Sweden", imdbId:"0843306", born:date('1940-10-15'), name:"Kari Sylwan", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nKari Sylwan (born 15 October 1940) is a Swedish actress, dancer and choreographer.  Sylwan started as a dancer in 1956 at the Royal Swedish Ballet and at the Cullberg Ballet.  She later played in the Ingmar Bergman films Cries and Whispers and Face to Face.  From 1996 to 2005 she was the vice-chancellor of the University College of Dance in Stockholm.  In 2005 she was awarded the H.  M.  The King's Medal of the 12th order for her contributions to dance...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dsm1G7mk86VMqKJiOchcokcncDk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67521"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"29803", properties:{bornIn:"Boston, Massachusetts, U.S.", imdbId:"0001404", born:date('1942-09-29'), name:"Madeline Kahn", bio:"Madeline Gail Kahn was an American actress, comedian, voice actress, and singer, known for comedic roles in films directed by Peter Bogdanovich and Mel Brooks, including What's Up, Doc?, Young Frankenstein...", died:date('1999-12-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gkJiblIpFJ6Tlz5JmsRZsjvHeh6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29803"}}, {tmdbId:"5266", properties:{bornIn:"Warthausen", imdbId:"0901057", born:date('1942-05-14'), name:"Rüdiger Vogler", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8q5HOiqdWC2Y23IHjnOnsTeUBX8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5266"}}, {tmdbId:"22611", properties:{imdbId:"0745467", born:date('1964-01-01'), name:"Yella Rottländer", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/22611"}}, {tmdbId:"22612", properties:{bornIn:"Hof, Germany", imdbId:"0471079", born:date('1945-12-02'), name:"Lisa Kreuzer", bio:"Lisa Kreuzer (born Elisabeth Kreuzer; December 2, 1945) is a German television and film actress with credits for appearances in over 120 films and television series. \n\nKreuzer featured with Dennis Hopper in Wim Wenders' film The American Friend (1977), a German-French co-production.  Other Wenders' films featuring Kreuzer include Alice in the Cities (1974) and Kings of the Road (1976)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iDlFoZkpOL856wiEDlJT3ksfzP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/22612"}}, {tmdbId:"22613", properties:{bornIn:"Vienna, Austria", imdbId:"0477785", born:date('1942-02-28'), name:"Edda Köchl", bio:"Edda Köchl-König was an Austrian stage and screen actress and an illustrator.  She was married to Wim Wenders 1968-74...", died:date('2015-09-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nRVdFv798naYWZDGRJYu8NZ764i.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/22613"}}, {tmdbId:"3037", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000377", born:date('1947-10-29'), name:"Richard Dreyfuss", bio:"An American actor best known for starring in a number of film, television, and theater roles since the late 1960s, including the films American Graffiti, Jaws, Close Encounters of the Third Kind, The Goodbye Girl, Stakeout, Always, What About Bob? and Mr.  Holland's Opus.  Dreyfuss won the Academy Award for Best Actor in 1977 for The Goodbye Girl, and was nominated in 1995 for Mr.  Holland's Opus...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xUefyViZWFxuuLzNV6YSLiOWGVl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3037"}}, {tmdbId:"12406", properties:{bornIn:"Rahway - New Jersey - USA", imdbId:"0494432", born:date('1945-09-22'), name:"Paul Le Mat", bio:"Paul Le Mat (born September 22, 1945) is an American actor who first came to prominence in the 1973 film American Graffiti, which won him the Golden Globe Award for New Star Of The Year - Actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article  Paul Le Mat  licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ceReeqXIX5yZFZsOaDpt73urYtZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12406"}}, {tmdbId:"8349", properties:{bornIn:"Dayton, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0000640", born:date('1940-08-03'), name:"Martin Sheen", bio:"Ramón Gerardo Antonio Estévez  (born August 3, 1940), better known by his stage name Martin Sheen, is a film actor best known for his performances in the films Badlands (1973) and Apocalypse Now (1979), and in the television series The West Wing from 1999 to 2006.  In film he has won the Best Actor award at the San Sebastián International Film Festival for his performance as Kit Carruthers in Badlands.  His portrayal of Capt...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/m2Y3Q0uyuW6htrn2W9UWCWMkpZu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8349"}}, {tmdbId:"5606", properties:{bornIn:"Quitman, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0000651", born:date('1949-12-25'), name:"Sissy Spacek", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSissy Spacek (born Mary Elizabeth Spacek; December 25, 1949) is an American actress and singer.  She won the Academy Award for Best Actress for her role as country star Loretta Lynn in the 1980 film Coal Miner's Daughter.  She has been nominated for an Oscar a total of six times...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xAxenjxjLNQFq4v1ccS2to3Mnoq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5606"}}, {tmdbId:"33060", properties:{bornIn:"Hartford, Connecticut, USA", imdbId:"0081560", born:date('1929-06-16'), name:"Ramon Bieri", bio:"Heavy-set American character actor whose typical screen personae tended to be gruff westerners, irate cops and hard-boiled gangsters.  A decorated Korean War veteran, Bieri appeared on stage from 1954, both on ('Death of a Salesman', 1975) and off-Broadway.  He latterly acted with the ensemble of San Diego's Old Globe Theatre (notably, as the tough captain in 'Mr.  Roberts', 1995)...", died:date('2001-05-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rYzyiXLWajSyRFTXhh18eZZhXWr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33060"}}, {tmdbId:"21030", properties:{bornIn:"Detroit, Michigan, U.S.", imdbId:"0605363", born:date('1941-04-05'), name:"Michael Moriarty", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMichael Moriarty (born April 5, 1941) is an American-Canadian actor of stage and screen, and a jazz musician.  He played Benjamin Stone for four seasons on the TV series Law &amp; Order. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Michael Moriarty, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2EY162LDxpVVG6g10lm70uxkNJp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21030"}}, {tmdbId:"14830", properties:{bornIn:"Naples, Italy", imdbId:"0306696", born:date('1920-01-07'), name:"Vincent Gardenia", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nVincent Gardenia  (January 7, 1920 – December 9, 1992) was an Italian American stage, film, and television actor...", died:date('1992-12-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xoJsXDJTNV4MUCqciN3ThcQrPdP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14830"}}, {tmdbId:"4307", properties:{bornIn:"Nelson, Georgia, U.S.", imdbId:"0015391", born:date('1926-05-25'), name:"Claude Akins", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nClaude Marion Akins (May 25, 1926 – January 27, 1994) was an American actor with a long career on stage, screen and television.  Powerful in appearance and voice, Akins could be counted on to play the clever (or less than clever) tough guy, on the side of good or bad, in movies and television.  He is best remembered as Sheriff Lobo in the 1970s TV series B.  J...", died:date('1994-01-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oBoSdz6meVMFrXN8vfaXGQAQsEa.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4307"}}, {tmdbId:"99829", properties:{imdbId:"0201089", born:date('1929-11-09'), name:"Severn Darden", died:date('1995-05-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kWMiUbAuprhewB5I7zbov7bImgT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/99829"}}, {tmdbId:"103825", properties:{imdbId:"0140889", name:"Lane Carroll", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/103825"}}, {tmdbId:"47883", properties:{bornIn:"Steubenville, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0534032", born:date('1944-11-25'), name:"Will MacMillan", died:date('2015-12-02'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/47883"}}, {tmdbId:"103826", properties:{imdbId:"0428197", name:"Harold Wayne Jones", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/103826"}}, {tmdbId:"103827", properties:{imdbId:"0390915", name:"Lloyd Hollar", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/103827"}}, {tmdbId:"74636", properties:{bornIn:"Englewood Cliffs, New Jersey, U.S.", imdbId:"0886556", born:date('1941-03-09'), name:"Trish Van Devere", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8Ubs9bntyIQGSUnCeqDmRtaFj0D.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74636"}}, {tmdbId:"7004", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn - New York City - New York - USA", imdbId:"0000649", born:date('1939-04-13'), name:"Paul Sorvino", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Paul Anthony Sorvino (born April 13, 1939) is an American actor.  He is the father of actress Mira Sorvino.  He often portrays authority figures on both sides of the law, and is possibly best known for his roles as Paulie Cicero in the film Goodfellas and Sgt.  Phil Cerreta on the TV series Law &amp; Order...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6qmQEQvtadHIUI5pbphflPFG9yu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7004"}}] AS row
