ance as Lenny in The Homecoming and the 1998 Laurence Olivier Award for Best Actor for his performance in the title role of King Lear...", died:date('2020-06-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cOJDgvgj4nMec6Inzj1H5nugTO5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/65"}}, {tmdbId:"38559", properties:{bornIn:"Great Neck, Long Island, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000483", born:date('1957-03-29'), name:"Christopher Lambert", bio:"Christophe Guy Denis \"Christopher\" Lambert (born 29 March 1957) is an American-born French actor who has appeared in American, as well as French and other European productions.  He is best known for his role as Connor MacLeod, or simply \"The Highlander\", from the movie and subsequent movie franchise series of the same name...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eKx856pdLyrh9sKgC8HuvuYZxlf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/38559"}}, {tmdbId:"1218958", properties:{imdbId:"0396757", name:"Patrick Houser", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1218958"}}, {tmdbId:"173136", properties:{imdbId:"0810212", name:"Tracy Smith", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/173136"}}, {tmdbId:"557433", properties:{bornIn:"Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0716555", born:date('1952-02-22'), name:"John Patrick Reger", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/557433"}}, {tmdbId:"32393", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA ", imdbId:"0005204", born:date('1961-01-19'), name:"Paul McCrane", bio:"Paul McCrane (born January 19, 1961) is an American actor, director and singer...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32393"}}, {tmdbId:"64119", properties:{bornIn:"Toronto, Ohio", imdbId:"0001810", born:date('1946-12-19'), name:"Robert Urich", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRobert Urich (December 19, 1946 – April 16, 2002) was an American actor.  He played the starring role in the television series Spenser: For Hire (1985–1988) and Vega$ (1978–1981).  He also appeared in other television series over the years including: S. W. A. T.  (1975), Soap (1977), and The Lazarus Man (1996), as well as in several feature films including Turk 182!, The Ice Pirates, and Magnum Force.  Urich died in 2002 in Thousand Oaks, California...", died:date('2002-04-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mouupy0SwJa4zCuEjdLmntlyZlU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/64119"}}, {tmdbId:"18465", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0002026", born:date('1959-09-14'), name:"Mary Crosby", bio:"Mary Crosby is an American actress, daughter of Bing Crosby.  She famously portrayed Kristin Shepard, shooter of J. R.  Ewing, on the television series Dallas...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/AeJKoATj6VIjr4CV1bFqiVST1l3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18465"}}, {tmdbId:"5146", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York,  USA", imdbId:"0731426", born:date('1947-12-25'), name:"Michael D. Roberts", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMichael D.  Roberts (born December 25, 1947) is an American actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Michael D.  Roberts, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rWuWAX0uS5kc4zJcQE1JGmTcxwz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5146"}}, {tmdbId:"689", properties:{bornIn:"Fort Worth, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0001009", born:date('1953-11-03'), name:"Kate Capshaw", bio:"Kate Capshaw  (born November 3, 1953) is an American actress.  She is known for her role as Willie Scott in Indiana Jones and the Temple of Doom...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/379hIr71jb3pk9Zd1hEeVaeNdlM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/689"}}, {tmdbId:"690", properties:{bornIn:"Saigon, Vietnam", imdbId:"0702841", born:date('1971-08-20'), name:"Jonathan Ke Quan", bio:"Jonathan Luke Ke Huy Quan is a Vietnamese-born American actor.  He is best known for his appearances in the 1980s Steven Spielberg presentations of Indiana Jones and the Temple of Doomand The Goonies. \n\nQuan was born in Saigon, South Vietnam.  He was forced to leave his country when the Army of the Republic of Vietnam was defeated during the Fall of Saigon.  His family was selected for political asylum and immigrated to the United States...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kkmtlUjeOL4xyFqVw6p3P0oKKoH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/690"}}, {tmdbId:"691", properties:{bornIn:"Jalandhar, Punjab, India", imdbId:"0700869", born:date('1932-06-22'), name:"Amrish Puri", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAmrish Lal Puri (June 22, 1932 - January 12, 2005) was an iconic theater and film actor from India, who was a key player in the Indian theater movement that picked up steam in the 1960s.  He worked with notable playwrights of the time, such as Satyadev Dubey and Girish Karnad.  However, he is primarily remembered for essaying some iconic negative roles in Hindi cinema.  He is most remembered for his role as Mogambo in the Hindi film Mr India (1987)...", died:date('2005-01-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/f9F456K0ydJCIIUS5YSmQWAgEgI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/691"}}, {tmdbId:"80868", properties:{bornIn:"Passaic, New Jersey, U.S.", imdbId:"0685472", born:date('1951-06-17'), name:"Joe Piscopo", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJoseph Charles John \"Joe\" Piscopo (pronounced PIS-ka-po) (born June 17, 1951) is an American comedian and actor best known for his work on Saturday Night Live. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Joe Piscopo, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80868"}}, {tmdbId:"21619", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois United States", imdbId:"0000447", born:date('1952-04-06'), name:"Marilu Henner", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nMary Lucy Denise Henner (born April 6, 1952), known professionally as Marilu Henner, is an American actress, producer, and New York Times best-selling author best-known for her role as Elaine O'Connor Nardo on the sitcom Taxi from 1978 to 1983. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article  Marilu Henner, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/10t8hp04H7rAFnCMpUYVyGToud.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21619"}}, {tmdbId:"23915", properties:{bornIn:"Isleton, California, USA", imdbId:"0001552", born:date('1932-06-28'), name:"Pat Morita", bio:"Pat Morita was an American actor of Japanese descent who was well-known for playing the role of Matsuo \"Arnold\" Takahashi on Happy Days and known as Mr.  Miyagi in the The Karate Kid movie series, in which he was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor in 1984. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Pat Morita, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2005-11-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/urxkD8FV5ajhjiFTyVQlbECGyRI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/23915"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"1951", properties:{bornIn:"Wilmington, Delaware, USA", imdbId:"0000223", born:date('1963-10-06'), name:"Elisabeth Shue", bio:"Elisabeth Judson Shue (born October 6, 1963) is an American actress, best known for her starring roles in the films The Karate Kid (1984), Adventures in Babysitting (1987), Cocktail (1988), Back to the Future Part II (1989), Back to the Future Part III (1990), Soapdish (1991), Leaving Las Vegas (1995), The Saint (1997), Hollow Man (2000), and Piranha 3D (2010).  She has won several acting awards and has been nominated for an Academy Award, a Golden Globe and a BAFTA...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wofhdwRvSLE07tcHPRyNApVzIl9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1951"}}, {tmdbId:"56117", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York,  USA", imdbId:"0184392", born:date('1947-03-06'), name:"Martin Kove", bio:"An American actor who has appeared in both feature films and television series. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Martin Kove, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vKfS55g6rqldWekNdy4JifuJQsw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56117"}}, {tmdbId:"613", properties:{bornIn:"Kōchi, Japan", imdbId:"0793585", born:date('1954-12-08'), name:"Sumi Shimamoto", bio:"Sumi Shimamoto is a Japanese voice actress...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bBA5xY4wrOUIpGnY6QPPQ9vNJB1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/613"}}, {tmdbId:"614", properties:{imdbId:"0875332", name:"Mahito Tsujimura", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nB2XEl1ZZujLm8kNwNCAOrXBDlc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/614"}}, {tmdbId:"615", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0477449", born:date('1935-02-22'), name:"Hisako Kyôda", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fv3D3Q5j5U1D9ddoKrjoLwm4KxL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/615"}}, {tmdbId:"616", properties:{bornIn:"Hakodate, Hokkaido, Japan", imdbId:"0623214", born:date('1929-11-17'), name:"Gorô Naya", bio:"Gorō Naya (納谷悟朗) was a Japanese actor, voice actor, narrator, and theater director.   He is most famous for voicing Inspector Kōichi Zenigata in the \"Lupin III\" anime series, and for his Japanese voice-overs of roles played by Clark Gable, Charlton Heston, and John Wayne.   He died in 2013 due to chronic respiratory failure...", died:date('2013-03-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/v5R3cjPEVeLRPWlZPziYP8ooV5w.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/616"}}, {tmdbId:"8976", properties:{bornIn:"Samrong Young, Cambodia", imdbId:"0628955", born:date('1940-03-22'), name:"Haing S. Ngor", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDr.  Haing Somnang Ngor (March 22, 1940 – February 25, 1996) was a Cambodian American physician, actor and author who is best known for winning the 1985 Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor for his debut performance in the movie The Killing Fields, in which he portrayed Cambodian journalist and refugee Dith Pran.  His mother was Khmer and his father was of Chinese descent...", died:date('1996-02-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5X7BHtzfS9rypQiQ12VnyASktjP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8976"}}, {tmdbId:"6104", properties:{bornIn:"Otley, Yorkshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0001696", born:date('1958-01-04'), name:"Julian Sands", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nJulian R.  Sands (born 4 January 1958) is an English actor, known for his roles in the Best Picture nominee The Killing Fields, the cult film Warlock, A Room with a View, Arachnophobia, Vatel and the television series 24...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8TYtEyKZle2B3cUYT7FBM9HJRtZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6104"}}, {tmdbId:"61702", properties:{bornIn:" Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0476484", born:date('1925-04-25'), name:"Kay E. Kuter", died:date('2003-11-12'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/61702"}}, {tmdbId:"158655", properties:{imdbId:"0556660", name:"Dan Mason", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/158655"}}, {tmdbId:"16213", properties:{bornIn:"Saratoga, California, USA", imdbId:"0346411", born:date('1960-07-21'), name:"Lance Guest", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLance R.  Guest (born July 21, 1960) is an American actor.  He developed a serious interest in acting in the 9th grade, and he majored in theater while attending UCLA. \n\nGuest has starred in many theatrical films including his role as Jimmy alongside actress Jamie Lee Curtis in the film Halloween II and also starred in I Ought to Be in Pictures...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rfLT0dxqWcAsN5rcEia6tHt2UpW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16213"}}, {tmdbId:"6752", properties:{bornIn:"Ljubljana - Slovenia", imdbId:"0411964", born:date('1957-08-15'), name:"Zeljko Ivanek", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nŽeljko Ivanek ([ˈʒeʎko iˈʋanək]; born 15 August 1957) is an Emmy award-winning Slovenian American actor.  He currently stars as Blake Sterling on the NBC series The Event...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/m7tPQiaHiKM15F8XUkYoJkATARD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6752"}}, {tmdbId:"101606", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0131985", born:date('1934-10-29'), name:"Hamilton Camp", bio:"Hamilton Camp (30 October 1934 – 2 October 2005) was a British-American singer-songwriter and actor...", died:date('2005-10-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1ftUhoIOkYzzPW9lmkMYrskxgXT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101606"}}, {tmdbId:"1217504", properties:{bornIn:"New York - USA", imdbId:"0579561", born:date('1954-09-21'), name:"John Mengatti", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1217504"}}, {tmdbId:"548089", properties:{imdbId:"0450848", born:date('1960-12-20'), name:"Mark Keyloun", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_