UNWIND [{tmdbId:"149466", properties:{imdbId:"0679750", name:"Mark Phelan", bio:"Mark Phelan is an actor and writer, known for Sea of Love (1989), Another 48 Hrs.  (1990) and Stand and Deliver (1988)...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/149466"}}, {tmdbId:"1903765", properties:{name:"Virginia Paris", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1903765"}}, {tmdbId:"12646", properties:{bornIn:"Sault Sainte Marie, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0642368", born:date('1952-07-15'), name:"Terry O'Quinn", bio:"Terry O'Quinn is an American film and television actor, best known for playing the Emmy Awarded role of John Locke on the television series \"Lost\"...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/utIgNhnBMX7q9s7iQbB2mTKW3uY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12646"}}, {tmdbId:"100870", properties:{bornIn:"Burbank, California, USA", imdbId:"0774337", born:date('1963-03-21'), name:"Jill Schoelen", bio:"A more unconventional husky-voiced \"scream queen\" heroine of the 1980s was Jill Schoelen, daughter of well-known fashion designer Dorothy Schoelen.  Born and raised in Burbank, she studied at the Acting for Life Theatre in Burbank and started off on TV as a teen in the Fame-influenced TV pilot called Best of Times (1981) (TV) starring the up-and-coming Nicolas Cage and Crispin Glover.  She gained in experience with a number of innocuous films geared mostly toward the young, including D. C...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/apPtHK3DP69O20GoACiXOQwPfsY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100870"}}, {tmdbId:"100871", properties:{bornIn:"Kirkland, Washington, USA", imdbId:"0487260", born:date('1942-07-10'), name:"Charles Lanyer", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100871"}}, {tmdbId:"58622", properties:{imdbId:"0748683", name:"Dick Rude", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDick Rude (born 1964) is a writer, director, and actor known for his appearance in and contributions to many Alex Cox films.  He has directed the music videos \"Catholic School Girls Rule\" and \"Universally Speaking\" for the Red Hot Chili Peppers, as well as their live concert DVD, Off the Map. \n\nHis most recent film is Let's Rock Again!, a documentary about Joe Strummer...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/Ac0Tq1zWRfhiav8dA9lBuxEpnqe.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/58622"}}, {tmdbId:"58623", properties:{bornIn:"Cincinnati, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0724784", born:date('1941-06-04'), name:"Sy Richardson", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nSy Richardson is an American film and television actor. Richardson made his film debut as the Fairy Godmother, in the 1977 American erotic musical comedy Cinderella.  He is perhaps best known as a regular in the films of Alex Cox, having appeared in Repo Man, Sid and Nancy, Straight to Hell, Walker, The Winner and Searchers 2. 0.  He played \"Turbo\" in the 1990 film Tripwire.  He recently had a recurring role as the coroner on the TV series Pushing Daisies...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kPlnnAmAbqQB33OcEVXiScK1Brr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/58623"}}, {tmdbId:"7621", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0001482", born:date('1964-07-09'), name:"Courtney Love", bio:"Courtney Michelle Love is an American rock musician and actress.  Love is primarily known as lead singer, guitarist and lyricist for alternative rock band Hole. \n\nFollowing a turbulent childhood, Love made her debut in the entertainment industry with a bit part in Alex Cox's Sid and Nancy (1986).  Eventually finding her passion in rock music rather than acting, Love formed Hole in 1989 with guitarist Eric Erlandson...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/n9bgfSViact39jhtuWoU3D0uz6G.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7621"}}, {tmdbId:"58296", properties:{bornIn:"Ankara, Turkey", imdbId:"0835329", born:date('1952-08-21'), name:"Joe Strummer", bio:"John Graham Mellor (21 August 1952 – 22 December 2002), known from May of 1975 as Joe Strummer, was a British musician, singer, composer, actor and songwriter who was the co-founder, lyricist, rhythm guitarist and co-lead vocalist of the Clash, a rock band formed in 1976 as part of the original wave of British punk rock...", died:date('2002-12-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1OnNvVlWmtyqDfjQTsQ8lQOYEo9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/58296"}}, {tmdbId:"88445", properties:{imdbId:"0480123", name:"Mike Lackey", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88445"}}, {tmdbId:"88446", properties:{imdbId:"0155723", name:"Bill Chepil", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88446"}}, {tmdbId:"88447", properties:{imdbId:"0636595", name:"Vic Noto", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88447"}}, {tmdbId:"1171468", properties:{imdbId:"3125507", name:"Mark Sferrazza", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1171468"}}, {tmdbId:"19728", properties:{bornIn:"Burbank - California - USA", imdbId:"0001319", born:date('1951-09-02'), name:"Mark Harmon", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMark Harmon (born September 2, 1951) is an American actor who has been starring in U. S.  television programs and films since the mid-1970s, after a career as a collegiate football player with the UCLA Bruins.  Since 2003, Harmon has starred as Leroy Jethro Gibbs in the CBS series NCIS...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lMqKPig7zBoGfou7wWf88sZEGHo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19728"}}, {tmdbId:"41465", properties:{bornIn:"Pittsfield, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0859450", born:date('1949-02-12'), name:"Robin Thomas", bio:"An American stage, film and television actor.  He holds a BFA in Acting and Sculpture from Carnegie-Mellon University, Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/seivBO3KRFAKqNgL3wnvpwxHwKz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41465"}}, {tmdbId:"114876", properties:{bornIn:" Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0479779", born:date('1965-07-22'), name:"Patrick Labyorteaux", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/114876"}}, {tmdbId:"1539681", properties:{imdbId:"3934723", name:"Merrill Gruver", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1539681"}}, {tmdbId:"75027", properties:{bornIn:"Castro Valley, California, USA", imdbId:"0250218", born:date('1944-09-24'), name:"Michael Edwards", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/B8HtKwNGk8bdHGFQAhV5vtef3q.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/75027"}}, {tmdbId:"1539683", properties:{imdbId:"3947623", name:"Melissa Brown", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1539683"}}, {tmdbId:"42708", properties:{bornIn:"Minneapolis - Minnesota - USA", imdbId:"0005588", name:"Rob LaBelle", bio:"Rob LaBelle was born in Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA.  He is an actor and producer...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oUFFrEGiRe94dNVL9KbWaPOabWk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/42708"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"166827", properties:{imdbId:"0624207", name:"Gail Neely", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/166827"}}, {tmdbId:"1271818", properties:{imdbId:"1106928", name:"Robert Harden", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1271818"}}, {tmdbId:"1073197", properties:{imdbId:"0107453", name:"Barry Brenner", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1073197"}}, {tmdbId:"97699", properties:{bornIn:"Carmel, California, USA", imdbId:"0928736", born:date('1963-06-11'), name:"Dawn Wildsmith", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eCcaRztus48JCKCDhPFl7mc2NdW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/97699"}}, {tmdbId:"3896", properties:{bornIn:"Ballymena, County Antrim, Northern Ireland", imdbId:"0000553", born:date('1952-06-07'), name:"Liam Neeson", bio:"An Irish actor who has been nominated for an Oscar, a BAFTA and three Golden Globe Awards.  He has starred in a number of notable roles including Oskar Schindler in Schindler's List, Michael Collins in Michael Collins, Peyton Westlake in Darkman, Jean Valjean in Les Misérables, Qui-Gon Jinn in Star Wars Episode I: The Phantom Menace, Alfred Kinsey in Kinsey, Ras Al Ghul in Batman Begins and the voice of Aslan in The Chronicles of Narnia film series...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wloLd5YrrlRPiTgfaMJsAx7U6hr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3896"}}, {tmdbId:"4251", properties:{bornIn:"Blackpool, Lancashire, England, UK", imdbId:"0001498", born:date('1940-06-20'), name:"John Mahoney", bio:"John Mahoney was a British actor, best known for playing Martin 'Marty' Crane, the retired police officer, father of Kelsey Grammer's Dr.  Frasier Crane, in the American sitcom \"Frasier\" (NBC, 1993–2004)...", died:date('2018-02-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9HhpD3Q6cBXddYkBTEzoPYlPL2h.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4251"}}, {tmdbId:"8978", properties:{bornIn:"Providence, Rhode Island, U.S.", imdbId:"0336960", born:date('1941-06-05'), name:"Spalding Gray", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSpalding Rockwell Gray (June 5, 1941 – ca.  January 10, 2004) was an American actor, playwright, screenwriter, performance artist, and monologuist.  He was primarily known for his \"trenchant, personal narratives delivered on sparse, unadorned sets with a dry, WASP, quiet mania. \" Gray achieved celebrity for writing and acting in the play Swimming to Cambodia, adapted into a film in 1987...", died:date('2004-01-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qmEBNepXpBuDnW3gdkY2sHeoGkq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8978"}}, {tmdbId:"28029", properties:{imdbId:"0923840", name:"Ira Wheeler", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/28029"}}, {tmdbId:"18331", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0001802", born:date('1961-09-21'), name:"Nancy Travis", bio:"Nancy Ann Travis (born September 21, 1961) is an American actress.  She has starred in films such as Greedy, Internal Affairs, Three Men and a Baby, So I Married an Axe Murderer and Fluke, as well as having starring roles in a number of television series, including Becker, Almost Perfect and The Bill Engvall Show. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Nancy Travis, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xC4XUFoOpDLN74BZoCfPp8FiS3W.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18331"}}, {tmdbId:"1953", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago - Illinois - USA", imdbId:"0797150", born:date('1961-03-17'), name:"Casey Siemaszko", bio:"Casey Siemaszko (born Kazimierz A.  Siemaszko) is a Polish-American actor and the brother of actress Nina Siemaszko.  The son of a fighter in the Polish Underground who survived the Sachsenhausen concentration camp, Siemaszko narrated the 1998 feature, The Polish-Americans.  Siemaszko was a graduate of the Goodman School of Drama at DePaul University in Chicago, which his sister, Nina Siemaszko later also attended...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xmy1MzLV0q39Wwq79UJKs9VuWjj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1953"}}, {tmdbId:"112304", properties:{imdbId:"0752414", name:"Annie Ryan", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/i9ImHRZCcqCAllBXNZRVbbvS3bw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/112304"}}, {tmdbId:"14700", properties:{bornIn:"Mobile, Alabama, USA", imdbId:"0879186", born:date('1961-02-13'), name:"Richard Tyson", bio:"Richard Martin Tyson (born February 13, 1961) is an American actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Richard Tyson, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14700"}}, {tmdbId:"49944", properties:{imdbId:"0001649", born:date('1929-09-01'), name:"Anne Ramsey", died:date('1988-08-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ne2o2YwaGzQy1Ne9ddZMwfEtkV7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/49944"}}, {tmdbId:"1271", properties:{bornIn:"Havana, Cuba", imdbId:"0000412", born:date('1956-04-12'), name:"Andy Garcia", bio:"Andrés Arturo García Menéndez (born April 12, 1956), professionally known as Andy García, is a Cuban American actor.  He became known in the late 1980s and 1990s, having appeared in several successful Hollywood films, including The Godfather: Part III, The Untouchables, Internal Affairs and When a Man Loves a Woman.  More recently, he has starred in Ocean's Eleven and its sequels, Ocean's Twelve and Ocean's Thirteen, and The Lost City...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aRooE4lECWf0YXd2NefeM4Wu4rn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1271"}}, {tmdbId:"42694", properties:{bornIn:"McKeesport, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0876645", born:date('1959-03-14'), name:"Tamara Tunie", bio:"Tamara Tunie is an American film and television actress, producer and director, best known for her portrayal of attorney Jessica Griffin on the CBS soap opera As the World Turns, and as medical examiner Melinda Warner on the NBC police drama Law & Order: Special Victims Unit...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vrkKfmpPSW0MhV8SYkNgRBG9ElV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/42694"}}, {tmdbId:"166598", properties:{bornIn:"Cleveland, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0184429", born:date('1928-11-20'), name:"Franklin Cover", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nFranklin Edward Cover (November 20, 1928 – February 5, 2006) was an American actor best known for starring in the sitcom The Jeffersons.  His character, Tom Willis, was half of one of the first interracial marriages to be seen on prime-time television. \n\nCover was born on November 20, 1928 in Cleveland, Ohio, to Britta (Schreck) and Franklin Held Cover.  He graduated from John Marshall High School in 1947...", died:date('2006-02-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8ZPM5GysUsVlCWtKa0fNilP8t6b.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/166598"}}, {tmdbId:"118757", properties:{imdbId:"0679406", name:"Chuck Pfeiffer", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7Mj0D03nFlR5a87Rg18ppiTUmzQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/118757"}}, {tmdbId:"184498", properties:{bornIn:"Elkridge, Maryland, USA", imdbId:"0911644", born:date('1970-02-24'), name:"Jonathan Ward", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/184498"}}, {tmdbId:"9980", properties:{bornIn:"Ottawa, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0551502", born:date('1967-09-14'), name:"K.C. Martel", bio:"Kevin Christopher Martel (born September 14, 1967) is a Canadian former child actor.  He played Mike Seaver's friend Eddie on Growing Pains from 1985-1992...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/88T5S7pDV6zoUqtwNxJc0XpI7Sb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9980"}}, {tmdbId:"20766", properties:{bornIn:"Mbabane, Swaziland", imdbId:"0001290", born:date('1957-05-05'), name:"Richard E. Grant", bio:"Richard E.  Grant (born Richard Esterhuysen; 5 May 1957) is a Swaziland-born English actor, screenwriter and director.  His most notable role came in the film Withnail and I. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Richard E.  Grant, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6UXv8E4WWvRCKMQx1FQ0FJVyu0a.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20766"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"47654", properties:{bornIn:"Kensington, Liverpool, England, UK", imdbId:"0001524", born:date('1959-11-14'), name:"Paul McGann", bio:"Paul McGann (born November 14, 1959) is an English actor who made his name on The Monocled Mutineer, in which he played the lead role.  He is also known for his role in Withnail and I, and for portraying the Eighth Doctor in the 1996 Doctor Who television movie as well as other media that features his incarnation of the character...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4NAtQI30CAaJuQRiot9twe7J9t9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/47654"}}, {tmdbId:"53916", properties:{bornIn:"Cambridge, Cambridgeshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0114460", born:date('1957-06-18'), name:"Ralph Brown", bio:"Ralph Brown was born on June 18, 1957.  He is an actor and writer...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/20VVWsUZHmTmN80xgHyy6LAFDuC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53916"}}, {tmdbId:"1284", properties:{bornIn:"London, England", imdbId:"0852965", born:date('1969-09-04'), name:"Noah Taylor", bio:"Born to Australian parents in London, Noah Taylor migrated to Australia at age five.  He left school at 16, and began his acting career in amateur theater...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rbgZcwy12lZX7L6qL19EDhgzYjO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1284"}}, {tmdbId:"85350", properties:{bornIn:"Adelaide, South Australia, Australia", imdbId:"0138389", born:date('1970-01-01'), name:"Loene Carmen", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLoene Carmen (born Adelaide, Australia) is an Australian singer/songwriter and actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Loene Carmen, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85350"}}, {tmdbId:"77335", properties:{bornIn:"Melbourne, Victoria, Australia", imdbId:"0578853", born:date('1969-04-03'), name:"Ben Mendelsohn", bio:"An Australian actor, who first rose to prominence in Australia for his role in The Year My Voice Broke (1987) and internationally for his role in the crime drama Animal Kingdom (2010). \n\nSince then he has had roles in films such as The Dark Knight Rises (2012), Starred Up (2013), Mississippi Grind (2015), Rogue One: A Star Wars Story (2016), and Captain Marvel (2019)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pA9mu9D2IolVA0v2Yo0tJm6uUyI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77335"}}, {tmdbId:"85351", properties:{bornIn:"Melbourne - Victoria - Australia", imdbId:"0089882", born:date('1945-07-08'), name:"Graeme Blundell", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGraeme Blundell (born 1945) is an Australian actor, director, producer, writer and biographer.  Blundell was born in Melbourne; he grew up in Clifton Hill, a suburb of Melbourne.  He was educated at University High School and the University of Melbourne.  In his early years, Blundell worked at La Mama Theatre, the Pram Factory, Hoopla, the Playbox Theatre Company, and the Melbourne Theatre Company...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gvJBWfxW9VJmi17ts7NEjsghKVZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85351"}}, {tmdbId:"77293", properties:{bornIn:"Englewood - New Jersey - USA", imdbId:"0772116", born:date('1966-05-01'), name:"Charlie Schlatter", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nCharles Thomas \"Charlie\" Schlatter (born May 1, 1966 in Englewood, New Jersey) is an American actor.  He has starred in numerous TV series and films, and is well-known for his role in the series Diagnosis: Murder as Dr.  Jesse Travis with Dick Van Dyke, and for his role in the film 18 Again! with George Burns.  Since 2004, he has been primarily a voice actor...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77293"}}, {tmdbId:"159753", properties:{imdbId:"0606360", born:date('1943-03-14'), name:"Anita Morris", died:date('1994-03-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zM8sk9jrt6XGHOojmeHk6bdfRCW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/159753"}}, {tmdbId:"23880", properties:{bornIn:"Lansing, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0000219", born:date('1952-04-10'), name:"Steven Seagal", bio:"An American action film star, producer, writer, martial artist, guitarist and a reserve deputy sheriff.  A 7th-dan black belt in Aikido, Seagal began his adult life as an Aikido instructor in Japan.  He became the first foreigner to operate an Aikido Dojo in Japan.  He later moved to the Los Angeles, California, area where he made his film debut in 1988 in Above the Law...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fGNIEpn3JqOckY3ahnJX9x3qA94.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/23880"}}, {tmdbId:"2230", properties:{bornIn:"Winston-Salem, North Carolina, USA", imdbId:"0000427", born:date('1949-05-26'), name:"Pam Grier", bio:"Pamela Suzette \"Pam\" Grier (born May 26, 1949) is an American actress.  She became famous in the early 1970s, after starring in a string of moderately successful women in prison and blaxploitation films such as 1974's Foxy Brown.  Her career was revitalized in 1997 after her appearance in Quentin Tarantino's film Jackie Brown.  She received a Golden Globe nomination for Best Actress...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sMGkXFfG0P8dRI26zXGJMDsrzvy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2230"}}, {tmdbId:"57597", properties:{imdbId:"0212939", name:"Ron Dean", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mgqdr4VFrTVZatkki2suNLYxeDG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57597"}}, {tmdbId:"87007", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, U.S.", imdbId:"0942195", born:date('1950-04-15'), name:"Amy Wright", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAmy Wright (born April 15, 1950) is an American actress.  She has appeared in such films as The Deer Hunter, Breaking Away, The Amityville Horror, Heartland, Wise Blood, Stardust Memories, The Accidental Tourist, Hard Promises, Crossing Delancey and Miss Firecracker.  Wright is married to actor Rip Torn and the couple have two daughters.  Wright is a graduate of the University of Chicago Laboratory School and Beloit College...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wejr7718NPsCjTF2mvyOOIukRsc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/87007"}}, {tmdbId:"67523", properties:{bornIn:"Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada", imdbId:"0183464", born:date('1965-01-01'), name:"Bernie Coulson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBernie Coulson (born Bernard, 1965) is a Canadian-born actor best known for his roles as The Thinker on the American television series The X Files, as well as Michael Reardon on the Canadian-based television series Intelligence and Pipefitter, the drummer of a reuniting punk band, in the Canadian mockumentary Hard Core Logo.  He also played the role of Rick Diesel in the cult classic Eddie and The Cruisers II, Eddie Lives...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/j8u5bLYdgav2P8KVjHVtTE0eZDi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67523"}}, {tmdbId:"67524", properties:{bornIn:"Trenton, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0744235", born:date('1946-06-26'), name:"Leo Rossi", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLeo Rossi  (born 1946) is an American actor and writer.  He is known for his role as Budd in the 1981 horror film Halloween II and as Turkell from the 1990 horror sequel Maniac Cop 2.  His other films include Heart Like a Wheel (1983), River's Edge (1986), The Accused (1988), Relentless (1989) and Analyze This (1999).  Rossi starred on the 1980s short-lived TV series Partners in Crime and appeared in made-for-TV movies...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/j18Nva8OAFwQrIvkfQHUF98SZFl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67524"}}, {tmdbId:"1678", properties:{bornIn:"Saitama Prefecture,Japan", imdbId:"0412628", born:date('1967-07-31'), name:"Mitsuo Iwata", bio:"Mitsuo Iwata was born on July 31, 1967 in Saitama, Japan.  He is an actor, known for Akira (1988), Paprika (2006) and D. Gray-man (2006).  He is married to Rikako Aikawa...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pTPgMpTgqRIA1cKkKaquRSzUxro.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1678"}}, {tmdbId:"1679", properties:{imdbId:"0765815", born:date('1967-01-25'), name:"Nozomu Sasaki", bio:"Nozomu Sasaki was born on January 25, 1967 in Hiroshima, Japan.  He is an actor, known for Yû Yû Hakusho (1992), Akira (1988) and Baburugamu kuraishisu (1987)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7usoPlvc9Xa1rDA2vxmVi0OvLDb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1679"}}, {tmdbId:"1680", properties:{bornIn:"Nishio, Aichi Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0468708", born:date('1955-01-17'), name:"Mami Koyama", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/t5LGiaUxOhqoApmJumZOv0wDnLh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1680"}}, {tmdbId:"1681", properties:{bornIn:"Okayama Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0312656", born:date('1948-05-20'), name:"Tesshô Genda", bio:"Tesshou Genda (born May 20, 1948 in Okayama Prefecture) is a Japanese voice actor, affiliated with 81 Produce.  When he debuted, he used his real name, Mitsuo Yokoi as an artist name...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7eJeYv2OCHKAadeFVdabVkpWldo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1681"}}, {tmdbId:"8657", properties:{imdbId:"0397441", name:"Kevyn Major Howard", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/utYdHRALnc34u49jm3Mc6U5R98u.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8657"}}, {tmdbId:"54768", properties:{bornIn:"Joutseno, Finland", imdbId:"0656999", born:date('1955-11-16'), name:"Turo Pajala", died:date('2007-02-28'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54768"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"54769", properties:{bornIn:"Helsinki, Finland", imdbId:"0352099", born:date('1957-10-20'), name:"Susanna Haavisto", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nSusanna Haavisto (born 20 October 1957, Helsinki) is a Finnish actress and singer. \n\nShe has taken part in several movies and TV programs.  She was UNICEF National Ambassador in 1980. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Susanna Haavisto, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lhjoqlBFCvshchMAd2lQLWV7z7I.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54769"}}, {tmdbId:"4826", properties:{bornIn:"Helsinki, Finland", imdbId:"0671231", born:date('1951-03-28'), name:"Matti Pellonpää", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMatti Pellonpää (28 March 1951 in Helsinki – 13 July 1995 in Vaasa) was an award-winning Finnish actor and a musician.  He rose to international fame with his roles in both Aki Kaurismäki's and Mika Kaurismäki's films; particularly being a regular in Aki's films, appearing in 18 of them. \n\nHe started his career in 1962 as a radio actor at the Finnish state-owned broadcasting company YLE...", died:date('1995-07-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1Qzhkkp3wFE2NMGKVyOra9931q2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4826"}}, {tmdbId:"54770", properties:{imdbId:"0383990", born:date('1981-01-19'), name:"Eetu Hilkamo", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54770"}}, {tmdbId:"9045", properties:{bornIn:"Massapequa, Long Island, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000286", born:date('1966-05-12'), name:"Stephen Baldwin", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nStephen Andrew Baldwin (born May 12, 1966) is an American actor, director, producer and author.  He is best known as the youngest of the Baldwin brothers and for his roles as William F.  Cody in the western show The Young Riders (1989–1992) and as Stuart in the movie Threesome (1994)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/w2nZjBsEsjboQDZJXEkysuGgue4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9045"}}, {tmdbId:"7447", properties:{bornIn:"Amityville, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000285", born:date('1958-04-03'), name:"Alec Baldwin", bio:"An American actor who has appeared on film, stage, and television.  Baldwin first gained recognition through television for his work, for two seasons (6 and 7), on the soap opera Knots Landing, in the role of Joshua Rush...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hzKy7x574eeUS3wt1R3yvWBRpeR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7447"}}, {tmdbId:"34536", properties:{imdbId:"0656276", name:"Maurice Page", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34536"}}, {tmdbId:"78934", properties:{bornIn:"Cliffside Park, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0086198", born:date('1923-12-11'), name:"Betsy Blair", bio:"Betsy Blair was an American actress of film and stage, long based in London.  Blair pursued a career in entertainment from the age of eight, and as a child worked as an amateur dancer, performed on radio, and worked as a model, before joining the chorus of Billy Rose's Diamond Horseshoe in 1940.  There she met Gene Kelly.  They were married the following year, when she was seventeen years old.  The couple divorced sixteen years later, in 1957...", died:date('2009-03-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yY48dqk7UWxYZZsqiU6SGkrvCeP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78934"}}, {tmdbId:"14698", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0000542", born:date('1964-01-13'), name:"Penelope Ann Miller", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPenelope Ann Miller (born January 13, 1964 as Penelope Andrea Miller), sometimes credited as Penelope Miller, is an American actress.  She began her career on Broadway, and starred in several major Hollywood films, particularly in the early 1990s, and has continued appearing in supporting roles in both film and television...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4I297JDKfIfXeKvYx1lzCeSdD98.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14698"}}, {tmdbId:"3124", properties:{bornIn:"Naples, Campania, Italy", imdbId:"0000420", born:date('1965-10-22'), name:"Valeria Golino", bio:"Valeria Golino is an Italian actress and director.  She is best known to English-language audiences for her roles in Rain Man, Big Top Pee-wee, and the two Hot Shots! movies.  In addition to the awards David di Donatello, Silver Ribbon, Golden Ciak, and Italian Golden Globe, she is also one of the three actresses who has won the Best Actress award at the Venice Film Festival twice...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/q8YUigxxcdcoc9uOvb70rNF19sE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3124"}}, {tmdbId:"85867", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia - Pennsylvania - USA", imdbId:"0611827", born:date('1960-07-21'), name:"Matt Mulhern", bio:"Matt Mulhern was trained as an actor by William Esper at Mason Gross School of the Arts, where he received a BFA in Acting.  He was first cast as Joseph Wykowski in Neil Simon's Tony Award winning \"Biloxi Blues\".  From there, he went on to a film, TV, and theater career as an actor, appearing in films such as \"One Crazy Summer,\" Extreme Prejudice,\" \"Biloxi Blues,\" \"Sunchaser,\" \"Infinity,\" and \"Walking To The Waterline,\" which he also wrote and directed for IFC films...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dtYWbp0VeAcU8pKRwciGJbleaWw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85867"}}, {tmdbId:"111902", properties:{imdbId:"0662160", born:date('1965-07-08'), name:"Corey Parker", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1pj3A5ce6dWG6oCu7o2dfwQzZPw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/111902"}}, {tmdbId:"27813", properties:{bornIn:"Montreal, Québec, Canada", imdbId:"0954677", born:date('1954-11-08'), name:"Michael Zelniker", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27813"}}, {tmdbId:"67392", properties:{imdbId:"0942789", born:date('1946-11-20'), name:"Samuel E. Wright", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jfJzbWIAba7Z6sslvL4aley0gPh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67392"}}, {tmdbId:"87385", properties:{bornIn:"Homerton, London, UK", imdbId:"0733153", born:date('1946-08-15'), name:"Tony Robinson", bio:"Sir Anthony Robinson is an English actor, comedian, author, presenter and political activist.  He played Baldrick in the BBC television series Blackadder and has hosted several historical documentaries including the Channel 4 programmes Time Team and The Worst Jobs in History...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9096kwFfytNtQeL04IvMCjM6FH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/87385"}}, {tmdbId:"6863", properties:{bornIn:"Mamaroneck, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001143", born:date('1965-08-19'), name:"Kevin Dillon", bio:"Kevin Brady Dillon (born August 19, 1965) is an American actor best known as Johnny \"Drama\" Chase on the HBO dramedy Entourage.  He has been nominated for three Primetime Emmy Awards and a Golden Globe Award for his performance on the show. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Kevin Dillon, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tIadFMFzA6LcXaAaVpJmrd7waXQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6863"}}, {tmdbId:"2138", properties:{bornIn:"Orangeburg, South Carolina, USA", imdbId:"0809938", born:date('1969-07-03'), name:"Shawnee Smith", bio:"An American film and television actress and musician.  Smith is best known for her roles as Amanda Young in the Saw films and Linda in the CBS sitcom Becker.  Smith once fronted the metal band Fydolla Ho, with which she toured the United States and the United Kingdom, and is half of Smith & Pyle, a desert country-rock band, with actress Missi Pyle.  Shawnee Smith is the second child of Patricia, an oncology nurse, and Jim Smith, a financial planner and former US Air Force pilot...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jQA9o25KGmJWmXoh6Cy6iu5bMgM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2138"}}, {tmdbId:"12645", properties:{bornIn:"Buffalo, New York, USA", imdbId:"0218810", born:date('1947-04-25'), name:"Jeffrey DeMunn", bio:"Jeffrey DeMunn (born April 25, 1947) is an American theatre, film and television actor. He is known as a favorite of director Frank Darabont, who has cast him in all four of his films, The Green Mile, The Shawshank Redemption, The Majestic and The Mist (he also appeared in the 1988 remake of The Blob, which Darabont co-wrote).  He also has an extensive television résumé, appearing in shows such as Kojak, Law & Order, and two of its spin-offs, SVU and Trial by Jury...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eSouAAduXaziFpqLw59AG55jtGY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12645"}}, {tmdbId:"41757", properties:{bornIn:"Port of Spain, Trinidad, Trinidad and Tobago", imdbId:"0018080", born:date('1934-12-19'), name:"Aki Aleong", bio:"Aki Aleong's career has spanned more than 60 years as an actor, singer, writer, producer and activist.  He has served on the National Board of the Screen Actors Guild, appointed National Chair of SAG'S EEOC and was a member of the President's Diversity/Affirmative Action Task Force.  Aki has also been Executive Director of AIM (Asians in Media), Vice President of The Media Coalition of Los Angeles and President of MANAA (Media Action Network for Asian-Americans)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/Aq3IiDVCgdiOc6nSpzCcmBJoZR4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41757"}}, {tmdbId:"129610", properties:{imdbId:"0364036", born:date('1973-01-20'), name:"Roland Harrah III", died:date('1995-01-03'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/129610"}}, {tmdbId:"129611", properties:{imdbId:"0453607", name:"Miki Kim", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/129611"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"123333", properties:{imdbId:"0372556", born:date('1965-01-04'), name:"Rick Hearst", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4hnHO8CEEE2BuMvWMuUCexLMAqW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/123333"}}, {tmdbId:"37152", properties:{imdbId:"0531737", name:"Gordon MacDonald", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/i8iGovP907pRhFXh0Huh80ZgfSm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/37152"}}, {tmdbId:"123335", properties:{imdbId:"0523330", name:"Jennifer Lowry", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jGtq1t0cifJVJFjBe87C3TlTbmK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/123335"}}, {tmdbId:"1687941", properties:{name:"Theo Barnes", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/matn01EAS2JPmF5GiUci96XB4T3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1687941"}}, {tmdbId:"83194", properties:{bornIn:"Sheboygan, Wisconsin, U.S.", imdbId:"0556750", born:date('1936-06-09'), name:"Jackie Mason", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJackie Mason (born June 9, 1936) is an American stand-up comedian. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jackie Mason, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83194"}}, {tmdbId:"65683", properties:{bornIn:"Newark, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0898571", born:date('1981-04-29'), name:"Alex Vincent", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nVincent was born in Newark, New Jersey and grew up in Maywood, New Jersey.  He graduated from Hackensack High School in Hackensack, New Jersey in 1999.  He also obtained an Associate Degree in Recording Arts from Full Sail University.  He never again acted in a major motion picture after his short-run as a child actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Alex Vincent (actor), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6TvXvFBMCuNeg9pzzHZy7An1vkR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/65683"}}, {tmdbId:"4812", properties:{bornIn:"Abidjan, Côte d'Ivoire", imdbId:"0207218", born:date('1957-08-12'), name:"Isaach De Bankolé", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nIsaach or Isaac de Bankolé (born 12 August 1957; Abidjan, Côte d'Ivoire) is an Ivorian actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Isaac de Bankolé, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tIihjWrBfzZahWaAwf8XFuYO0JS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4812"}}, {tmdbId:"556855", properties:{bornIn:"Rome, Lazio, Italy", imdbId:"0097817", born:date('1962-12-17'), name:"Giulia Boschi", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/556855"}}, {tmdbId:"24542", properties:{bornIn:"Bruxelles, Belgium", imdbId:"0011803", born:date('1958-01-01'), name:"Jean-Claude Adelin", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24542"}}, {tmdbId:"41686", properties:{bornIn:"Albuquerque, New Mexico, USA", imdbId:"0000439", born:date('1973-06-15'), name:"Neil Patrick Harris", bio:"Neil Patrick Harris (born June 15, 1973) is an American actor, singer, and magician.  Prominent roles of his career include the title role in Doogie Howser, M. D. , Colonel Carl Jenkins in Starship Troopers, the womanizing Barney Stinson in How I Met Your Mother, a fictionalized version of himself in the Harold &amp; Kumar series, and the title role in Joss Whedon's musical web series Dr.  Horrible's Sing-Along Blog...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oyy0Enz4ZX8KYRYihgSgOA18Xc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41686"}}, {tmdbId:"1907", properties:{bornIn:"Midland, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0000834", born:date('1950-06-08'), name:"Kathy Baker", bio:"Kathy Baker is an American stage, film and television actress...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/c5MAs0tvUg9pdxbayxRAFLm0Qz5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1907"}}, {tmdbId:"192", properties:{bornIn:"Memphis, Tennessee, USA", imdbId:"0000151", born:date('1937-06-01'), name:"Morgan Freeman", bio:"Morgan Porterfield Freeman, Jr.  is an American actor, film director, and narrator.  He is noted for his reserved demeanor and authoritative speaking voice.  Freeman has received Academy Award nominations for his performances in Street Smart, Driving Miss Daisy, The Shawshank Redemption and Invictus and won in 2005 for Million Dollar Baby.  He has also won a Golden Globe Award and a Screen Actors Guild Award...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oIciQWr8VwKoR8TmAw1owaiZFyb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/192"}}, {tmdbId:"15455", properties:{bornIn:"Tenafly, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0004883", born:date('1963-09-25'), name:"Tate Donovan", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nTate Buckley Donovan (born September 25, 1963) is an American actor.  He is most recently known for his role in the FX drama Damages, as \"Tom Shayes. \" He is also known for his role as \"Jimmy Cooper\" in the American teen drama television series The O. C. , and as the voice of the title character Hercules in Disney's thirty-fifth animated feature film of the same name, in the animated television series and in the video game Kingdom Hearts II...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1SVx1zVO2lR5mUoduURUL64mIDH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15455"}}, {tmdbId:"52878", properties:{bornIn:"Chagrin Falls - Ohio - USA", imdbId:"0051862", born:date('1955-07-09'), name:"Lisa Banes", bio:"Lisa Banes was born on July 9, 1955 in.  She is an actress...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bSYs9z8Su9Ewg71XO8LdiNu2OwU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/52878"}}, {tmdbId:"6938", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0112207", born:date('1950-01-30'), name:"Randy Brooks", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mSZl3TZZcrkfAlZT8IDX7iHF5EC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6938"}}, {tmdbId:"19260", properties:{imdbId:"0542994", born:date('1951-07-01'), name:"Terrence Mann", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nTerrence Vaughan Mann (born July 1, 1951) is an American actor, singer and dancer who has been prominent on the Broadway stage for the past three decades. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Terrence Mann, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/63WKMJI5V5iYMTNIF4v73i2dOMk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19260"}}, {tmdbId:"35092", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA ", imdbId:"0649210", born:date('1949-01-01'), name:"Don Keith Opper", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/35092"}}, {tmdbId:"99914", properties:{imdbId:"0308371", name:"Cynthia Garris", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/99914"}}, {tmdbId:"171155", properties:{bornIn:"Poland", imdbId:"0102536", born:date('1914-05-13'), name:"Reizl Bozyk", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nReizl Bozyk (born 13 May 1914, Poland – 30 September 1993, New York, New York, USA), also known as Rose Bozyk, was a Polish-born American actress of the Yiddish theatre. \n\nHer only claim to mainstream fame was her sole film role in which she played the interfering grandmother of Amy Irving in Joan Micklin Silver's film Crossing Delancey (1988)...", died:date('1993-09-30'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/171155"}}, {tmdbId:"1137477", properties:{imdbId:"1226256", name:"Dale Reeves", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1137477"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"199316", properties:{imdbId:"0389333", born:date('1979-02-25'), name:"David Hoflin", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pEvRjGOzfFDBwwuHSNVy8fAcGLV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/199316"}}, {tmdbId:"1276", properties:{bornIn:"New Orleans, Louisiana, USA", imdbId:"0165101", born:date('1959-12-29'), name:"Patricia Clarkson", bio:"Patricia Davies Clarkson (born December 29, 1959) is an American actress.  After studying drama on the East Coast, Clarkson launched her acting career in 1985, and has worked steadily in both film and television.  She twice won the Emmy for Outstanding Guest Actress in Six Feet Under.  Film roles included The Green Mile, Far From Heaven, The Station Agent and was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress for her performance in Pieces of April (2003)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rHHM9G83fpBAcFathbSyV4Tot5j.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1276"}}, {tmdbId:"66225", properties:{imdbId:"0453447", name:"Evan C. Kim", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEvan C.  Kim is an American actor...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rYuwmhfu8LttCgAANWLiwfyg3GZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/66225"}}, {tmdbId:"57881", properties:{bornIn:" Toronto, Canada", imdbId:"0902794", born:date('1960-10-09'), name:"Heidi von Palleske", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wyxULWXzC4tMHxKz2TLbIfPS41s.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57881"}}, {tmdbId:"5942", properties:{imdbId:"0329876", name:"Barbara Gordon", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5PYdOUfFGN1Jnf3KAahRPCEFz6M.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5942"}}, {tmdbId:"37935", properties:{bornIn:"Yonkers, New York, USA ", imdbId:"0878911", born:date('1948-03-26'), name:"Steven Tyler", bio:"Steven Tyler is an American singer-songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, and former television music competition judge, best known as the lead singer of the Boston-based rock band Aerosmith, in which he also plays the harmonica, and occasional piano and percussion.  He is known as the \"Demon of Screamin'\" due to his high screams and his wide vocal range.  He is also known for his on-stage acrobatics...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dr4NfsCtPK08HD61frZAoTht3kZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/37935"}}, {tmdbId:"235984", properties:{bornIn:"Lawrence, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0675128", born:date('1950-09-10'), name:"Joe Perry", bio:"Joe Perry is an American musician and lead guitarist of the Rock band Aerosmith...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2yM9WrIwIJe2XIhCU2tgJfjDrQ3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/235984"}}, {tmdbId:"35824", properties:{bornIn:"Detroit, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0004840", born:date('1948-02-04'), name:"Alice Cooper", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAlice Cooper (born Vincent Damon Furnier; February 4, 1948) is an American rock singer, songwriter and musician whose career spans more than five decades.  With a stage show that sometimes included a guillotine, gallows, electric chair, fake blood, boa constrictor and baby dolls, Cooper drew equally from horror movies, vaudeville and garage rock to pioneer a grandly theatrical and violent brand of heavy metal that was designed to shock...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nyJVaHPZSPMvJyS5aSal7a793qJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/35824"}}, {tmdbId:"7672", properties:{bornIn:"Queens, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001817", born:date('1952-08-16'), name:"Reginald VelJohnson", bio:"Reginald VelJohnson (born August 16, 1952) is an American actor of film, stage and television, well known for his role as Carl Winslow on the sitcom Family Matters, where he was the only cast member to appear in every single episode.  He also portrayed LAPD Sgt.  Al Powell in the film Die Hard (1988), its sequel Die Hard 2 (1990), and the Chuck episode \"Chuck Versus Santa Claus\" (2008)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dZtIIOI0PpD3dmTVfUOWiQzOY28.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7672"}}, {tmdbId:"28853", properties:{bornIn:"Wisbech, Cambridgeshire, UK", imdbId:"0734668", born:date('1933-01-10'), name:"Anton Rodgers", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nAnton Rodgers (born Anthony Rodgers; 10 January 1933 – 1 December 2007) was an English actor and occasional director.  He performed on stage, in film and in television dramas and sitcoms. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Anton Rodgers, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2007-12-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/x0bIlxGnC1865bK2SiHKXfb4Nhx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/28853"}}, {tmdbId:"11477", properties:{bornIn:"Newark, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0000501", born:date('1954-12-18'), name:"Ray Liotta", bio:"Raymond Allen \"Ray\" Liotta (born December 18, 1954) is an American actor, best known for his portrayal of Henry Hill in the crime-drama Goodfellas, directed by Martin Scorsese and his role as Shoeless Joe Jackson in Field of Dreams.  He has won an Emmy Award and been nominated for a Golden Globe Award.  Also, Ray has voiced Tommy Vercetti in the video game Grand Theft Auto:Vice City...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4trMXwGW6OZpyvDYQ7a5ZCxk9KL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11477"}}, {tmdbId:"1217995", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0505938", born:date('1931-09-04'), name:"Robert Levine", bio:"Robert Levine was an American film and television actor...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1217995"}}, {tmdbId:"162007", properties:{bornIn:"Bronx, New York, USA", imdbId:"0747933", born:date('1940-08-03'), name:"Phil Rubenstein", died:date('1992-06-26'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/162007"}}, {tmdbId:"124603", properties:{bornIn:"Long Island, New York, USA", imdbId:"0420901", born:date('1955-05-10'), name:"Larry Flash Jenkins", died:date('2019-04-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iriLZ3jKRlGp1Ykusqj3G65zLSu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/124603"}}, {tmdbId:"44810", properties:{bornIn:"Manhattan, Kansas, USA", imdbId:"0005308", born:date('1951-09-17'), name:"Cassandra Peterson", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nCassandra Peterson (born September 17, 1951) is an American actress best known for her on-screen horror hostess character Elvira, Mistress of the Dark.  She gained fame on Los Angeles television station KHJ wearing a black, gothic, cleavage-enhancing gown as host of Movie Macabre, a weekly horror movie presentation.  Her wickedly vampish appearance is offset by her comical character, quirky/quick-witted personality, and valley girl-type speech...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ykrDhr0lBHjVLjxvclbpvHaEi5L.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/44810"}}, {tmdbId:"172446", properties:{imdbId:"0293346", name:"Damita Jo Freeman", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hSPA8QpeBaDMJLB7Sei1h9TFmF5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/172446"}}, {tmdbId:"15833", properties:{imdbId:"0780528", born:date('1913-10-28'), name:"Douglas Seale", died:date('1999-06-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4RFHIJ3xbmOpgsr7JLZeRfY9yhb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15833"}}, {tmdbId:"75021", properties:{bornIn:"Woodstock, New York, USA", imdbId:"0662523", born:date('1971-12-25'), name:"Noelle Parker", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vov5YTd566G1KkGJk3plYoHA2wg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/75021"}}, {tmdbId:"8925", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0782561", born:date('1966-06-22'), name:"Emmanuelle Seigner", bio:"Emmanuelle Seigner (born 22 June 1966) is a French actress, former fashion model, and singer.  She is known for her roles in The Diving Bell and the Butterfly (2007), The Ninth Gate (1999) and Frantic (1988).  She has been nominated for a César Award for Best Actress for Venus in Fur (2013), and for two César Awards for Best Supporting Actress in Place Vendôme (1998) and La Vie En Rose (2007).  She has been married to Polish film director Roman Polanski since August 30, 1989...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xPRldoTHgFd1Z5TtGk3jo3TGvPL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8925"}}, {tmdbId:"66198", properties:{imdbId:"0815880", name:"Djiby Soumare", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/66198"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"166926", properties:{bornIn:"Riverside, California, USA", imdbId:"0052079", born:date('1978-11-08'), name:"Jennifer Banko", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4awafU85QdA8oV1D36zO8IrRwLc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/166926"}}, {tmdbId:"102576", properties:{imdbId:"0652965", name:"John Otrin", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pszSyyhGYG5DrRTQTaBPPHLn7Ga.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/102576"}}, {tmdbId:"19548", properties:{bornIn:"Saint Paul, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0089454", born:date('1948-07-12'), name:"Susan Blu", bio:"Susan Maria Blu (born July 12, 1948), sometimes credited as Sue Blu, is an American voice actress, voice director and casting director in American and Canadian cinema and television. \n\nShe most notably voiced Arcee in the original Transformers movie and Seasons 3 and 4 of The Transformers (she later reprised the role in Transformers Animated).  She is also known for playing the roles of Stormer and Lin-Z Pierce in the 80s animated series, Jem...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xDtrH8YqqVc11kAUThxG80AaaHP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19548"}}, {tmdbId:"64719", properties:{imdbId:"0661983", born:date('1961-05-12'), name:"Lar Park-Lincoln", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qgzZKuL57xGcWs08FeNxORSgbXg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/64719"}}, {tmdbId:"77022", properties:{bornIn:"St. Louis, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0641871", born:date('1916-05-25'), name:"Kevin O'Morrison", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Kevin O'Morrison (25 May 1916, St.  Louis, Missouri) is an American playwright and actor.  He started his career working as an actor in theatre, radio, television, and film in the 1940s.  He began writing plays in the 1960s, most of which have been performed Off-Broadway and in theatres throughout the United States, and two of which have been performed in Europe...", died:date('2016-12-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1WGvi5e02eqUkmHyqkFoPoKPq0f.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77022"}}, {tmdbId:"63910", properties:{imdbId:"0590731", name:"John Omirah Miluwi", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4C0HysaATd3hBLjqr8pMGA1FKGp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/63910"}}, {tmdbId:"1642", properties:{bornIn:"Bitburg, Rhineland-Palatinate, Germany", imdbId:"0000852", born:date('1960-09-27'), name:"Jean-Marc Barr", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJean-Marc Barr (born on 27 September 1960 in Bitburg, Rhineland-Palatinate, Germany) is a French-American film actor and director.  His mother is French.  His American father was in the US Air Force and served in the Second World War.  Jean-Marc Barr is primarily known as an actor, but is also a film director, screenwriter and producer...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ukdhuHD2vqBr5NKMiTQ52KRF75w.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1642"}}, {tmdbId:"1003", properties:{bornIn:"Casablanca, Morocco", imdbId:"0000606", born:date('1948-07-30'), name:"Jean Reno", bio:"A French actor.  Working in French, English, and Italian, he has appeared not only in numerous successful Hollywood productions such as The Pink Panther, Godzilla, The Da Vinci Code, Mission: Impossible, Ronin and Couples Retreat, but also in European productions such as the French films Les Visiteurs (1993) and Léon (1994) along with the 2005 Italian film The Tiger and the Snow...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4TcZEDVA0u6x5pF2oZMuslxZKHe.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1003"}}, {tmdbId:"14105", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn - New York - USA", imdbId:"0266995", born:date('1952-01-01'), name:"Stephanie Faracy", bio:"Stephanie Faracy is an actress...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14105"}}, {tmdbId:"516", properties:{bornIn:"Topeka, Kansas, USA", imdbId:"0000906", born:date('1958-05-29'), name:"Annette Bening", bio:"An American film and television actress.  She's a four-time Academy Awards nominee for her roles in the feature films The Grifters, American Beauty, Being Julia and The Kids Are All Right, winning Golden Globe Awards for the latter two films...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vVAvoiE6FQ4couqaB0ogaHR6Ef7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/516"}}, {tmdbId:"67949", properties:{imdbId:"0095122", born:date('1935-02-16'), name:"Sonny Bono", died:date('1998-01-05'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kOFuou8PBht8nEVlFUlXvNzgne6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67949"}}, {tmdbId:"67950", properties:{imdbId:"0114616", born:date('1928-01-30'), name:"Ruth Brown", died:date('2006-11-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lQCCsrnsygENgK9h6HDD9VyKYK1.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67950"}}, {tmdbId:"62589", properties:{bornIn:"Glen Cove, Long Island, New York, USA", imdbId:"0332081", born:date('1963-12-15'), name:"Ellie Cornell", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEllie Cornell (born December 15, 1963) is an American actress and movie producer, known primarily for her roles in horror films.  After her marriage to producer Mark Gottwald, she is sometimes credited as Ellie Gottwald. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Ellie Cornell, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yuS2DcheBpVKmVZKoYsB2pr7wBb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/62589"}}, {tmdbId:"21320", properties:{bornIn:"Daytona Beach, Florida, USA", imdbId:"0364583", born:date('1977-06-01'), name:"Danielle Harris", bio:"Danielle was born in Daytona Beach, Florida and then her family moved to Port Orange, Florida when she was in the fourth grade, where she attended Spruce Creek Elementary School.  She was only there a very short while after winning a children's beauty contest her family them moved to Queens, New York City, New York...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/66hlVnuKl1uWuraHmlSKuVo9iKS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21320"}}, {tmdbId:"69129", properties:{imdbId:"0928111", name:"George P. Wilbur", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fOuVakMHvCwlPYMcLAm9oEucQUz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69129"}}, {tmdbId:"26258", properties:{bornIn:"Dunfermline - Scotland - UK", imdbId:"0186469", born:date('1944-12-12'), name:"Kenneth Cranham", bio:"Scottish born actor Kenneth Cranham is one of the most recognisable character actors in Britain.  Having trained at the National Youth Theatre and RADA, Cranham first came to prominence as Noah Claypole in the 1968 Carol Reed musical Oliver! In the late '70s, Cranham memorably played Sapper Salt in Euston Films' Danger UXB, before taking the title role in the popular postwar set period comedy drama Shine on Harvey Moon.  His most famous film role from around this time was Dr...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9lzTbNgaoArlxpEkYtWQfOyiYwu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/26258"}}, {tmdbId:"56918", properties:{imdbId:"0095567", born:date('1971-05-13'), name:"Imogen Boorman", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oE36ZgQXekL1Pd31EGh74FwOYvh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56918"}}, {tmdbId:"53367", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0790689", born:date('1952-01-01'), name:"Ruth Sheen", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRuth Sheen (born 1952) is an English actress. \n\nBorn in London, Sheen began her career by training at the East 15 Acting School, and has appeared regularly on British television and in British films since 1988.  On television, she had recurring roles as Nanny Simmons in Berkeley Square (1998), and as Nurse Ethel Carr in the series Bramwell (1995–1998).  She has also appeared as four different characters in six episodes of The Bill between 1989 and 2004...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bcrbxcgVPpMlDUPD3OY4BONzpTd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53367"}}, {tmdbId:"72316", properties:{bornIn:"Bromley, Kent, England", imdbId:"0234270", born:date('1921-05-31'), name:"Edna Doré", bio:"Born Edna Lillian Gorring on May 31, 1921 in Bromely, Kent Edna Doré was an actress, best known for playing the battleaxe Mo Butcher in EastEnders from 1988 to 1990 and for the films Les Misérables (1998),  and the Mike Leigh films Another Year, All or Nothing and High Hopes, the latter saw her receive the award for Best Supporting Player at the 1989 European Film Awards.  She was married to Alexander Doré.  She died on April 11, 2014 in Sussex, England at the age of 92...", died:date('2014-04-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/460Kg55xkzmtPfS0bnZIf9HMQDq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/72316"}}, {tmdbId:"25532", properties:{bornIn:"Retford, Nottinghamshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0413946", born:date('1948-06-18'), name:"Philip Jackson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nPhilip Jackson (born 18 June 1948) is an English actor, known for his many television and film roles, most notably as Chief Inspector Japp in the television series Agatha Christie's Poirot and as Abbot Hugo, one of the recurring adversaries in the cult 1980s series Robin of Sherwood...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eC7p4UAj6xB4TtQ4cPcIJtubPnw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25532"}}] AS row
