UNWIND [{tmdbId:"32645", properties:{bornIn:"Starnberg, Bavaria, Germany", imdbId:"0845270", born:date('1945-08-27'), name:"Marianne Sägebrecht", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Marianne Sägebrecht (born 27 August 1945, Starnberg, Bavaria) is a German actress, most famous for her appearance in the movies Sugarbaby, Bagdad Café, and The War of the Roses. \n\nThis Rubenesque character player with a heart-shaped face and child-like features began her career as a leading producer and performer of Germany's alternative theater/cabaret scene...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nTsZ2QAbtxzDVy18QvwXMuQgM4Y.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32645"}}, {tmdbId:"30485", properties:{bornIn:"Georgetown, British Guiana", imdbId:"0001634", born:date('1952-12-25'), name:"CCH Pounder", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nCarol Christine Hilaria Pounder (born December 25, 1952), known professionally as C.  C.  H.  Pounder (styled \"CCH Pounder\"), is a Guyanese-American film and television actress.  She has appeared in numerous films, made-for-television films, television miniseries and plays, and has made guest appearances on notable television shows...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/c0ey32ObHhJIQVQYqGejaxOS23x.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30485"}}, {tmdbId:"3762", properties:{bornIn:"Lengdorf, Styria, Austria", imdbId:"0442304", born:date('1945-01-11'), name:"Christine Kaufmann", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nChristine Maria Kaufmann (born January 11, 1945) is a German actress.  In 1961 she won the Golden Globe Award for New Star Of The Year - Actress, the only German to be so honoured. \n\nBorn to a German father and a French mother in Lengdorf, Styria, Kaufmann became a ballerina at the Munich Opera.  She started her film career at the age of seven in the 1952 adaptation of Im weißen Rößl (White Horse Inn)...", died:date('2017-03-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5dOT16uZw2wKekuv1ogvRwS3y5U.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3762"}}, {tmdbId:"6474", properties:{bornIn:"Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0001457", born:date('1962-04-27'), name:"James Le Gros", bio:"James Le Gros is an American film and television actor...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rI6wK1WHBTYF9dYC04kUO0kr8oX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6474"}}, {tmdbId:"79584", properties:{bornIn:"Kansas City, Kansas, USA", imdbId:"0780133", born:date('1926-08-10'), name:"Angus Scrimm", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nAngus Scrimm (born Lawrence Rory Guy; August 19, 1926 – January 9, 2016) was an American actor and author, best known for playing the Tall Man in the 1979 horror film Phantasm and its sequels. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Angus Scrimm, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2016-01-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tBDDTCXXybeyzDmFwAuPCb6ePCT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/79584"}}, {tmdbId:"87127", properties:{bornIn:"Hollywood, Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0410211", born:date('1968-06-22'), name:"Paula Irvine", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nPaula Irvine (born June 22, 1968) is an American actress.  Irvine began acting in 1987 by making guest appearances.  In 1988 she starred in Phantasm II playing Liz Reynolds, and in 1990 she also appeared on Beverly Hills, 90210 during the first season as Sheryl and on Growing Pains as Lori McNeil.  She is best known for her portrayal of the second Lily Blake Capwell on the NBC daytime drama Santa Barbara from 1991 to 1993.  She retired from acting in 1994...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8HMkuLjpw4GFOyFiGDnI7PdDGdO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/87127"}}, {tmdbId:"22252", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, United States", imdbId:"0247579", born:date('1949-07-29'), name:"Leslie Easterbrook", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLeslie Eileen Easterbrook (born July 29, 1949) is an American actress...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cgivmDAMFWTMGKGr12Z0HjEcBgN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/22252"}}, {tmdbId:"10091", properties:{bornIn:"Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, U.S.", imdbId:"0748289", born:date('1933-05-28'), name:"Zelda Rubinstein", bio:"Zelda Rubinstein was an American actress and human rights activist, known as eccentric medium Tangina Barrons in the Poltergeist film series.  Playing 'Ginny', she was a regular on David E.  Kelley's Emmy Award winning television series Picket Fences for several seasons.  She also made guest appearances in the TV show Poltergeist: The Legacy (1996), as seer 'Christina' and was the voice ofSkittles candies in their long-running 'Taste the Rainbow' ad campaign...", died:date('2010-01-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/x6iNhGFo2s4NxQVmACPU3ZhTe97.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10091"}}, {tmdbId:"942808", properties:{bornIn:"Monroe, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0001973", born:date('1954-02-02'), name:"Christie Brinkley", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xwqx23ftStrkB3gA89TCumnz2ox.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/942808"}}, {tmdbId:"1040841", properties:{bornIn:"Wadowice, Poland", imdbId:"0937552", born:date('1920-05-18'), name:"Pope John Paul II", died:date('2005-04-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dQmMDHDU7O3iMkowtAjizD6xPoY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1040841"}}, {tmdbId:"95778", properties:{imdbId:"0711710", name:"Dan Rather", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95778"}}, {tmdbId:"53088", properties:{bornIn:"Kansas City, Missouri USA", imdbId:"0247532", born:date('1957-10-27'), name:"Jeff East", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Jeff East (born October 27, 1957) is an American actor.  His best-known role is in the 1978 hit film Superman as the teenage Clark Kent. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jeff East, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rU43pn639rgSA1DsS0UJrdTjVaM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53088"}}, {tmdbId:"158094", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0195383", born:date('1958-04-14'), name:"John D'Aquino", bio:"John D'Aquino is an American film and television actor...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/158094"}}, {tmdbId:"147957", properties:{bornIn:"Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0743590", born:date('1959-10-08'), name:"Kimberly Ross", died:date('2006-12-19'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/147957"}}, {tmdbId:"2211", properties:{bornIn:"Great Falls, Montana, USA", imdbId:"0596520", born:date('1935-01-06'), name:"Gerald R. Molen", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGerald Robert Molen (born January 6, 1935) is a high profile American film producer.  He works very closely with Steven Spielberg, having produced five of his films, and won an Academy Award for co-producing Schindler's List.  Gerald \"Jerry\" Molen is now semi-retired and spends his time alternating between Montana and Las Vegas, Nevada. \n\nMolen was born in Great Falls, Montana, the son of Edith Lorraine (née Meyer) and Gerald Richard Molen...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/m1C2E9MWClm3ITzxQzUxmE1qphL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2211"}}, {tmdbId:"255923", properties:{bornIn:"Nancy, Meurthe-et-Moselle, France", imdbId:"0209030", born:date('1949-02-16'), name:"Marc de Jonge", died:date('1996-06-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/a0BfIL3Ru4QpievnOWMN9RUJEU2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/255923"}}, {tmdbId:"2115", properties:{bornIn:"New Lisbon, Wisconsin, USA", imdbId:"0001748", born:date('1943-07-03'), name:"Kurtwood Smith", bio:"Kurtwood Larson Smith (born July 3, 1943) is an American television and film actor.  He is best known for playing Clarence Boddicker in RoboCop and stern parental characters (That '70s Show, Dead Poets Society, Worst Week), and for his appearances in the genre of science fiction (Star Trek, The X-Files).  He also starred in the seventh season of 24.  Description above from the Wikipedia article Kurtwood Smith, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mMH8TpD1RC5yTL64SG8rpzjNnzk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2115"}}, {tmdbId:"8658", properties:{bornIn:"Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0642522", born:date('1946-07-04'), name:"Ed O'Ross", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6hzovUAs5hFcrZvPdk84NR3KcHU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8658"}}, {tmdbId:"10682", properties:{bornIn:"Syracuse - New York - USA", imdbId:"0823289", born:date('1963-06-06'), name:"Anthony Starke", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAnthony Starke (born June 6, 1963) is an American actor.  Starke is well known for his one episode role in Seinfeld, playing the 3rd person-speaking character Jimmy in \"The Jimmy\", as well as playing Jack on The George Carlin Show, on Fox...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yznwRo83YXsEA850qgRMB6LXElj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10682"}}, {tmdbId:"106128", properties:{bornIn:"Rochester, New York, USA", imdbId:"0592960", born:date('1961-03-20'), name:"Karen M. Waldron", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bPO5MOjc8UZ52tzWyjeRCG0Jd6A.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/106128"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"121816", properties:{bornIn:"Atlanta, Georgia, USA", imdbId:"0526557", born:date('1961-02-20'), name:"Steve Lundquist", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/121816"}}, {tmdbId:"92852", properties:{bornIn:"USA", imdbId:"0448959", born:date('1975-01-01'), name:"Michael Kenworthy", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/92852"}}, {tmdbId:"92853", properties:{imdbId:"0887421", name:"Thor Van Lingen", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/92853"}}, {tmdbId:"92854", properties:{imdbId:"0389545", name:"Jason Hogan", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/92854"}}, {tmdbId:"76181", properties:{bornIn:"Canberra, Australian Capital Territory, Australia", imdbId:"0861600", born:date('1959-02-12'), name:"Sigrid Thornton", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/czkKwrZmuFfM3WRHJfcseacqo5c.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/76181"}}, {tmdbId:"76182", properties:{imdbId:"0247031", name:"Nicholas Eadie", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/76182"}}, {tmdbId:"82787", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0009413", born:date('1975-05-12'), name:"Jonas Abry", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82787"}}, {tmdbId:"1528560", properties:{imdbId:"0787359", name:"Shafiq Syed", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1528560"}}, {tmdbId:"1528561", properties:{imdbId:"0900009", name:"Hansa Vithal", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1528561"}}, {tmdbId:"1528562", properties:{imdbId:"0788870", name:"Chanda Sharma", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1528562"}}, {tmdbId:"52974", properties:{bornIn:"Jabalpur, Madhya Pradesh, India", imdbId:"0944834", born:date('1957-06-25'), name:"Raghuvir Yadav", bio:"Raghubir Yadav or Raghuvir Yadav is an Indian film, stage and television actor, music composer, singer and set designer.  He made his film debut with Massey Sahib (1985), in which he played the title role.  He has garnered two International Awards as Best Actor for Massey Sahib, FIPRESCI Critic's Award, Venice Film Festival, 1986 and the IFFI Best Actor Award (Male): Silver Peacock Award at the 11th International Film Festival of India, 1987...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yTkHzgL5luZumoOPHxK2HOZxpzL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/52974"}}, {tmdbId:"32161", properties:{bornIn:"Pietermaritzburg, South Africa", imdbId:"0424368", born:date('1925-09-22'), name:"Stratford Johns", died:date('2002-01-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ab1HO2yR8dY4tDNcqmR761jQtAR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32161"}}, {tmdbId:"63611", properties:{bornIn:"West Kirby, Merseyside, England, UK", imdbId:"0333380", born:date('1947-11-21'), name:"Nickolas Grace", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/a4Kehtv9RJIW6Iyw6F5Uua1f2RM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/63611"}}, {tmdbId:"80149", properties:{bornIn:"Plymouth, Regno Unito", imdbId:"0388061", born:date('1960-02-25'), name:"Douglas Hodge", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ePGYx2w4cM9nSaBvfg9LdEieAtT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80149"}}, {tmdbId:"121612", properties:{bornIn:"Ponce, Puerto Rico", imdbId:"0740875", born:date('1970-06-27'), name:"Draco Rosa", bio:"Draco Cornelius Rosa Suárez originally garnered fame as a member of boy band Menudo in the 1980s, singing lead on the band's biggest stateside hit, \"Hold Me\" and featuring prominently in the accompanying music video.  In 1988, at age 19, he made his motion picture debut in the film Salsa, which was a big hit in Puerto Rico.  During the filming of the movie, he met actress Angela Alvarado who would later become his wife...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/121612"}}, {tmdbId:"6386", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania", imdbId:"0367696", born:date('1967-07-31'), name:"Rodney Harvey", bio:"Rodney Michael Harvey (July 31, 1967 – April 11, 1998) was an American actor and model from Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.  Harvey began appearing in films in 1985 and went on to play roles in films such as Five Corners (1987), My Own Private Idaho (1991) and Guncrazy (1992).  Harvey had a main role on the television show The Outsiders (1990) and also appeared in the pilot episode of Twin Peaks (1990).  Harvey died at the Hotel Barbizon in Los Angeles on April 11, 1998 as a result of a drug overdose...", died:date('1998-04-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fwJn1IP80k4f9BTlmbBjPplIno8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6386"}}, {tmdbId:"121613", properties:{imdbId:"0023169", name:"Magali Alvarado", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/121613"}}, {tmdbId:"4202", properties:{imdbId:"0308449", name:"Miranda Garrison", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zoLVZJBteUYTeeifeUEDfAtfcuz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4202"}}, {tmdbId:"2975", properties:{bornIn:"Augusta, Georgia, USA", imdbId:"0000401", born:date('1961-07-30'), name:"Laurence Fishburne", bio:"An American actor of screen and stage, as well as a playwright, director, and producer.  He is perhaps best known for his roles as Morpheus in the Matrix science fiction film trilogy and as singer-musician Ike Turner in the Tina Turner biopic What's Love Got to Do With It.  He became the first African-American to portray Othello in a motion picture by a major studio when he appeared in Oliver Parker's 1995 film adaption of the Shakespeare play...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8suOhUmPbfKqDQ17jQ1Gy0mI3P4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2975"}}, {tmdbId:"4808", properties:{bornIn:"Copenhagen, Denmark", imdbId:"0002064", born:date('1958-04-26'), name:"Giancarlo Esposito", bio:"Born in Denmark, Giancarlo Esposito is an Italian American stage, film and television actor and director, best known for playing many supporting characters in television shows, such as Gustavo \"Gus\" Fring in \"Breaking Bad\" and \"Better Call Saul\"...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9TnBZoJchBufSi0WaooA3ZuhrGp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4808"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"141823", properties:{bornIn:"Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, USA", imdbId:"0132896", born:date('1968-10-13'), name:"Tisha Campbell-Martin", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/keuc8jAfEM2fRce0P8FvLclwlYg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/141823"}}, {tmdbId:"1219219", properties:{imdbId:"0477425", name:"Kyme", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1219219"}}, {tmdbId:"47458", properties:{bornIn:"Johannesburg, South Africa", imdbId:"0596310", born:date('1934-08-05'), name:"Zakes Mokae", died:date('2009-09-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qLQfTAYvufmy3X6WI4OHrABL2ap.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/47458"}}, {tmdbId:"54246", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0295334", born:date('1949-04-24'), name:"Peter Friedman", bio:"Peter Friedman (born April 24, 1949) is an American stage, screen, and television actor.  Born in New York City, Friedman graduated from Hofstra University before making his Broadway debut in The Great God Brown in 1972.  Additional theatre credits include The Visit (1973), Piaf and A Soldier's Play (both 1981), The Heidi Chronicles (1989), Ragtime (1998), and Twelve Angry Men (2004)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3pyU0yQsRIqSZw1fYapFRXJ3EHp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54246"}}, {tmdbId:"85238", properties:{imdbId:"2720556", name:"James Ray", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85238"}}, {tmdbId:"1036563", properties:{bornIn:"Connecticut, USA", born:date('1959-04-23'), name:"Tim Blaney", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8KkdDVZhzXyTEGt0rBOkVviIQ9R.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1036563"}}, {tmdbId:"1913732", properties:{name:"Gene Bervoets", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4R6nme1YDzI5bOuUkgBmKXspXEh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1913732"}}, {tmdbId:"55851", properties:{bornIn:"Wierden, Overijssel, Netherlands", imdbId:"0824373", born:date('1961-05-10'), name:"Johanna ter Steege", bio:"Johanna ter Steege is a Dutch stage and screen actress.  She won the European Film Award for Best Supporting Actress for her movie debut in The Vanishing (1988).  Among her other films are Robert Altman's Vincent & Theo (1990), István Szabó's Meeting Venus (1991) and Sweet Emma, Dear Böbe (1992), Bernard Rose's Immortal Beloved (1994), and Bruce Beresford's Paradise Road (1997)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/scRkVtx0DSdq1C9nS2VRjhi5bYX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55851"}}, {tmdbId:"55852", properties:{imdbId:"0248680", name:"Gwen Eckhaus", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55852"}}, {tmdbId:"20914", properties:{bornIn:"St. Louis, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0110398", born:date('1940-02-04'), name:"Kent Broadhurst", bio:"Kent Broadhurst (born February 4, 1940) is an American actor, playwright, and screenwriter. \n\nHe has appeared in a number of off-Broadway and regional theater productions.  Broadhurst has also acted in films, including The Verdict, Silkwood, and Silver Bullet, and in television productions including Babylon 5, Law & Order, War and Remembrance, and Kane and Abel...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jcR9n3N6bCmsQbbpgFf1D3hmDdY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20914"}}, {tmdbId:"10866", properties:{bornIn:"Woburn, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0091899", born:date('1953-04-24'), name:"Eric Bogosian", bio:"Eric Bogosian (born April 24, 1953) is an American actor, playwright, monologist, and novelist...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lUtLCWoLh18UFVOHBFr1VpUpoYJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10866"}}, {tmdbId:"11885", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001525", born:date('1959-08-03'), name:"John C. McGinley", bio:"An American actor, most notable for his roles as Perry Cox in Scrubs, Bob Slydell in Office Space, and Sergeant Red O'Neill in Oliver Stone's Platoon.  He has also written and produced for television and film.  Apart from acting, McGinley is also an author and a spokesperson for the National Down Syndrome Society. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article John C.  McGinley, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/a9Oc7STg83syQh3X22u2TroAifk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11885"}}, {tmdbId:"67091", properties:{bornIn:"Musashino, Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0846630", born:date('1957-11-30'), name:"Tomorowo Taguchi", bio:"Tomorowo Taguchi (born November 30, 1957) is a Japanese actor. \n\nAfter leaving Dokkyo University without graduating, he started to earn his living as an illustrator, writer and pornographic cartoonist.  He joined a theatre called Hakken no Kai in 1978 and he made a screen debut in Zokubutsu Zukan (based on the book by Yasutaka Tsutsui) in 1982.  He was also a prominent cult musician in the Tokyo underground scene with his band Bachikaburi in the 1980s and early 1990s...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/z1YgwqQMxRyeMg0QQw8cOrFCljX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67091"}}, {tmdbId:"126453", properties:{imdbId:"0437099", name:"Nobu Kanaoka", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5sAkS5scWe6MLl7eQr0p9S9NyD2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/126453"}}, {tmdbId:"44240", properties:{bornIn:"Saskatoon, Saskatchewan, Canada", imdbId:"0684929", born:date('1954-04-17'), name:"Roddy Piper", bio:"Roderick George Toombs  (April 17, 1954 – July 31, 2015) , better known by his ring name \"Rowdy\" Roddy Piper, was a Canadian professional wrestler and film actor currently signed to World Wrestling Entertainment.  Although he was Canadian, due to his Scottish heritage, he was billed as coming from Glasgow, Scotland and was known for his signature kilt and bagpipe entrance music...", died:date('2015-07-31'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3LZvHroOYjUe8mKP3AWL87ML8d7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/44240"}}, {tmdbId:"54564", properties:{bornIn:"Milton-Freewater, Oregon, USA", imdbId:"0002668", born:date('1937-10-28'), name:"George 'Buck' Flower", bio:"George Buck Flower (October 28, 1937 – June 18, 2004) was an American actor, writer, producer, assistant director, production manager, and casting director.  He was sometimes credited as Buck Flower, George \"Buck\" Flower, George Flower, Buck Flowers, C.  D.  LaFleur, C. D.  LaFleure, C. D.  Lafleuer, and C. D.  Lafleur. \n\nDue to his gruff appearance, he was often cast as a drunk or homeless character.  Director John Carpenter gave Flower a cameo role in almost every film he made throughout the 1980s...", died:date('2004-06-18'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9qmc0d452N45uSTuCGEaUg8sKQK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54564"}}, {tmdbId:"1414776", properties:{imdbId:"0011278", name:"Randall Adams", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1414776"}}, {tmdbId:"206088", properties:{bornIn:"Jefferson County, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0364595", born:date('1960-10-19'), name:"David Harris", bio:"David Harris was born on October 19, 1960 in Jefferson County, Texas, USA as David Ray Harris.  He died on June 30, 2004 in Huntsville, Texas...", died:date('2004-06-30'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/206088"}}, {tmdbId:"1414777", properties:{imdbId:"0741410", name:"Gus Rose", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1414777"}}, {tmdbId:"1697857", properties:{imdbId:"0425278", name:"Jackie Johnson", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1697857"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"89461", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago - Illinois - USA", imdbId:"0426666", born:date('1933-10-24'), name:"J.J. Johnston", bio:"J. J.  Johnston (born James William Johnston, October 24, 1933, Chicago, Illinois) is an American theatre and film actor and boxing historian and writer...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5CoCxaxf2EGUOgNem0hKU8sn8X3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89461"}}, {tmdbId:"55664", properties:{imdbId:"0757076", name:"Chika Sakamoto", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rzBLHST5Icmm1gYGHOZvAGk6BNs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55664"}}, {tmdbId:"55663", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0847054", born:date('1925-02-26'), name:"Hitoshi Takagi", died:date('2004-02-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kQab69jvurfdWZEaziUzhsPaSmd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55663"}}, {tmdbId:"55662", properties:{bornIn:"Chiyoda, Tokyo, Giappone", imdbId:"0383022", born:date('1962-05-31'), name:"Noriko Hidaka", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/w757PVYKSDvj2weQrPSCZL5mZh9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55662"}}, {tmdbId:"55665", properties:{bornIn:"Maebashi, Gunma Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0411790", born:date('1948-11-10'), name:"Shigesato Itoi", bio:"Japanese writer and copywriter, best known in the west for creating the Mother/Earthbound series...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2VVkwc8Fk3sZERhImqYhcifVfIp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55665"}}, {tmdbId:"6681", properties:{bornIn:"Detroit, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0000145", born:date('1965-02-01'), name:"Sherilyn Fenn", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nSherilyn Fenn (born February 1, 1965) is an American actress.  She came to international attention for her performance as Audrey Horne on the 1990 cult TV series Twin Peaks.  She is also known for her roles in Of Mice and Men, Ruby, Boxing Helena and Rude Awakening, and for portraying actress Elizabeth Taylor in Liz: The Elizabeth Taylor Story...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wHWnkSh3vQhjNKRHsOsDA4NE5XJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6681"}}, {tmdbId:"33684", properties:{bornIn:"Dublin, Ireland", imdbId:"0095104", born:date('1960-05-10'), name:"Bono", bio:"Paul David Hewson, better known by his stage name Bono, is an Irish singer-songwriter, musician, venture capitalist, businessman, and philanthropist.  He is best recognized as the frontman of the Dublin-based rock band U2.  Bono was born and raised in Dublin, Ireland, and attended Mount Temple Comprehensive School where he met his future wife, Alison Stewart, and the future members of U2.  Bono writes almost all U2 lyrics, frequently using religious, social, and political themes...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/r1jCFctRrEAHBHOyJun8rWCH0AD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33684"}}, {tmdbId:"82426", properties:{bornIn:"Barking, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0857253", born:date('1961-08-08'), name:"The Edge", bio:"David Howell Evans (born 8 August 1961), better known by his stage name the Edge (or just Edge), is an Irish musician and songwriter best known as the lead guitarist, keyboardist, and backing vocalist of the rock band U2.  A member of the group since its inception, he has recorded 14 studio albums with the band and one solo record.  As a guitarist, the Edge has crafted a minimalistic and textural style of playing...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xHPqYog6UiYKdw8PcQaW4unGvg7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82426"}}, {tmdbId:"82427", properties:{imdbId:"0165651", name:"Adam Clayton", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7YMNUrUte44ZajlvYbflpOKLZQo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82427"}}, {tmdbId:"82428", properties:{bornIn:"Artane, Ireland", imdbId:"0611979", born:date('1961-10-31'), name:"Larry Mullen Jr.", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zL4CxIHJSeBeL324fBLraEPkbDN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82428"}}, {tmdbId:"1137", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0000300", born:date('1964-03-09'), name:"Juliette Binoche", bio:"Juliette Binoche (born 9 March 1964) is a French actress, artist and dancer.  She has appeared in more than 40 feature films, been recipient of numerous international accolades, is a published author and has appeared on stage across the world.  Coming from an artistic background, she began taking acting lessons during adolescence...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/htdZZIroEyJaeHQAUTqokNfkPgl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1137"}}, {tmdbId:"5313", properties:{bornIn:"Stockholm, Stockholms län, Sweden", imdbId:"0000565", born:date('1955-03-22'), name:"Lena Olin", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLena Maria Jonna Olin (born 22 March 1955) is a Swedish actress.  She has been nominated for several acting awards, including a Golden Globe for The Unbearable Lightness of Being (1988) and an Academy Award for Enemies, A Love Story (1989).  Other well-known films in which she has appeared include Chocolat (2000), directed by her husband Lasse Hallström, Queen of the Damned (2002), Casanova (2005) and The Reader (2008)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nEQxqLb7MFdcvXR3s3Q2i7d9zoF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5313"}}, {tmdbId:"9128", properties:{bornIn:"The Hague, Zuid-Holland, Netherlands", imdbId:"0513190", born:date('1950-07-17'), name:"Derek de Lint", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDick Hein de Lint, known as Derek de Lint, (born 17 July 1950) is a Dutch film and television actor. \n\nDe Lint was born in The Hague.  In 1977, he played the character Alex in the film Soldier of Orange, directed by Paul Verhoeven.  In 1986 he played the role of Anton Steenwijk in The Assault, which won the Academy Award for Best Foreign Language Film in 1986.  In 2006, De Lint starred in Verhoeven's Black Book as Gerben Kuipers...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8fRRmh8EYZBlUtu1Wlop0j22QcP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9128"}}, {tmdbId:"1721557", properties:{name:"Hercules Vilchez", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1721557"}}, {tmdbId:"1721558", properties:{name:"Jerry Vichi", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1721558"}}, {tmdbId:"74954", properties:{bornIn:"Camp Lejeune, North Carolina", imdbId:"0001959", born:date('1958-10-18'), name:"Corinne Bohrer", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Corinne Vilhelma Bohrer (born October 18, 1958) is an American movie and television actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Corinne Bohrer, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74954"}}, {tmdbId:"87957", properties:{bornIn:"Oak Park, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0843775", born:date('1952-12-02'), name:"Keith Szarabajka", bio:"Keith Szarabajka is an actor and writer...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/drXhJoVUmm352h4G1QWnvHZgudT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/87957"}}, {tmdbId:"19427", properties:{bornIn:"Surrey, England, UK", imdbId:"0142616", born:date('1930-06-16'), name:"Christopher Cary", died:date('2000-04-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8OtPURlaSjcpcTZW6I00BawCmGP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19427"}}, {tmdbId:"184400", properties:{imdbId:"0132491", born:date('1940-11-30'), name:"Graeme Campbell", died:date('1992-01-18'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/184400"}}, {tmdbId:"1086322", properties:{imdbId:"0640915", name:"Dan O'Dowd", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1086322"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"16170", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0002090", born:date('1964-02-14'), name:"Zach Galligan", bio:"Zachary Wolfe \"Zach\" Galligan (born February 14, 1964) is an American actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia Zach Galligan, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mIqahCZcPw63km6dFnm1B1coAiY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16170"}}, {tmdbId:"169906", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA ", imdbId:"0060257", born:date('1942-07-22'), name:"Jennifer Bassey", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/169906"}}, {tmdbId:"181486", properties:{bornIn:"London, England UK", imdbId:"0048589", born:date('1928-12-14'), name:"Joe Baker", died:date('2001-05-16'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/181486"}}, {tmdbId:"593", properties:{bornIn:"Haddonfield - New Jersey - USA", imdbId:"0001026", born:date('1945-08-02'), name:"Joanna Cassidy", bio:"Joanna Cassidy (born August 2, 1945, height 5' 9\" (1,75 m)) is an American film and television actress.  She is known for her role replicant Zhora in the Ridley Scott's film Blade Runner (1982).  She also has starred in films such as Under Fire, The Fourth Protocol, Who Framed Roger Rabbit, The Package, Where the Heart Is and Don't Tell Mom the Babysitter's Dead, Vampire in Brooklyn and Ghosts of Mars...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8R9H1GvaMaFiSDkOTMBwrL0qhWN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/593"}}, {tmdbId:"12826", properties:{bornIn:"Washington, D.C., United States", imdbId:"0281486", born:date('1950-08-27'), name:"Charles Fleischer", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nCharles Fleischer (born August 27, 1950) is an American actor, stand-up comedian and voice artist. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Charles Fleischer, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iZ32sao16c0ZZIg30hwRfqNHNui.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12826"}}, {tmdbId:"12656", properties:{bornIn:"Salford, Manchester, England, UK", imdbId:"0000695", born:date('1961-08-25'), name:"Joanne Whalley", bio:"Joanne Whalley (born 25 August 1961) is an English actress who began her career in 1974.  She has since amassed numerous credits, primarily on television, but also in nearly 30 feature films, including Dance with a Stranger (1985), Willow (1988), Scandal (1989), The Secret Rapture (1993) and Mother's Boys (1994).  Following her marriage to Val Kilmer in 1988, she was credited as Joanne Whalley-Kilmer until their divorce in 1996...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ijTNoEyDNnYTE8A3QsRhXixHT59.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12656"}}, {tmdbId:"11184", properties:{bornIn:"Epsom, Surrey, England, UK", imdbId:"0001116", born:date('1970-02-03'), name:"Warwick Davis", bio:"Warwick Ashley Davis is an English actor, television presenter, writer, director, comedian, and producer.  He played the title characters in Willow and the Leprechaun film series, the Ewok Wicket in Star Wars Episode VI: Return of the Jedi and Professor Filius Flitwick and Griphook in the Harry Potter films...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4iqtDreLUQgevd2IjJOl2fonlJv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11184"}}, {tmdbId:"61808", properties:{imdbId:"0494189", name:"Odile Le Clezio", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/61808"}}, {tmdbId:"61809", properties:{bornIn:"Sydney, New South Wales, Australia", imdbId:"0933957", born:date('1940-02-25'), name:"Peewee Wilson", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/61809"}}, {tmdbId:"1538", properties:{bornIn:"Prince Albert, Saskatchewan, Canada", imdbId:"0239958", born:date('1956-07-03'), name:"Rick Ducommun", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRichard \"Rick\" Ducommun (born July 3, 1956) is a Canadian actor and comedian, often seen in supporting roles on both television and the silver screen. \n\nDucommun was born in Prince Albert, Saskatchewan...", died:date('2015-06-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/usW5QTa85JuonyRktb3s5HjDD84.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1538"}}, {tmdbId:"30151", properties:{bornIn:"Louisville, Kentucky, USA", imdbId:"0122238", born:date('1944-02-01'), name:"Leo Burmester", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Leo Burmester (February 1, 1944 - June 28, 2007) was an American actor.  Burmester worked for director John Sayles several times, including in Passion Fish (1992) and Lone Star (1996), and also for directors such as John Schlesinger and Sidney Lumet, and as the Apostle Nathaniel in Martin Scorsese's The Last Temptation of Christ (1988)...", died:date('2007-06-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/o7ZXSICrTDzhxIyd95HBwVjBi1f.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30151"}}, {tmdbId:"12642", properties:{bornIn:"Willesden, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0627453", born:date('1925-05-02'), name:"John Neville", bio:"John Neville, OBE, CM was an English theatre and film actor who moved to Canada with his family in 1972.  He enjoyed a resurgence of international attention as a result of his starring role in Terry Gilliam's \"The Adventures of Baron Munchausen\". \n\nHe was appointed to the Order of Canada, that nation's highest civilian honor, in 2006. \n\nAccording to publicists at Canada's Stratford Shakespeare Festival, Neville died \"peacefully surrounded by family\" on 19 November 2011, aged 86...", died:date('2011-11-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/q9dqdcETh7fejWKYpIRz1tWnkN3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12642"}}, {tmdbId:"69604", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, United States", imdbId:"0601610", born:date('1945-10-29'), name:"Melba Moore", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nBeatrice Melba Smith (born October 29, 1945), known by her stage name, Melba Moore is an American disco, R&amp;B singer and actress.  She is the daughter of saxophonist Teddy Hill and R&amp;B singer Bonnie Davis...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69604"}}, {tmdbId:"36067", properties:{bornIn:"Tucson, Arizona, USA", imdbId:"0424635", born:date('1959-10-24'), name:"Brad Johnson", bio:"An American actor and former Marlboro Man.  Johnson's first acting credit was in the low-budget biker film The Nam Angels (1989), and shortly after he had his first co-starring role in a major film when he played the role of Ted Baker in the 1989 film Always, directed by Steven Spielberg.  His other movie credits include Flight of the Intruder, Philadelphia Experiment II, Copperhead and Supergator.  He also played the role of Rayford Steele in the Left Behind film series, and played Dr...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lntKJkWc71dPBx1FtGvLs0WVn6z.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/36067"}}, {tmdbId:"11180", properties:{bornIn:"York, North Yorkshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0103195", born:date('1942-04-17'), name:"David Bradley", bio:"David Bradley is an English character actor.  He has recently become known for playing the caretaker of Hogwarts, Argus Filch, in the Harry Potter series of films. \n\nBradley was born in York, England.  He became an actor in 1971, first appearing on television that year in the successful comedy Nearest and Dearest playing a police officer.  He was awarded a Olivier Award in 1991 for his supporting actor role in King Lear at the Royal National Theatre...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/znpkwHitb3pcaJbUmgDqG0YenYp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11180"}}, {tmdbId:"88163", properties:{bornIn:"Long Beach, California", imdbId:"0331374", born:date('1944-01-14'), name:"Marjoe Gortner", bio:"Hugh Marjoe Ross Gortner, generally known as Marjoe Gortner (born January 14, 1944, in Long Beach, California), is a former revivalist who first gained a certain fame in the late 1940s when he became the youngest ordained preacher at the age of four.  He then gained outright notoriety in the 1970s when he starred in an Oscar-winning, behind-the-scenes documentary about the lucrative business of Pentecostal preaching.  The name \"Marjoe\" is a portmanteau of the names \"Mary\" and \"Joseph\"...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/AmVU5U1LGDuxZbfGauMSDYpD4US.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88163"}}, {tmdbId:"94082", properties:{imdbId:"0151034", name:"Michele B. Chan", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dpk6v14Ag74x7KRfOsqbTMFKG06.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94082"}}, {tmdbId:"1065", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0001855", born:date('1959-04-15'), name:"Thomas F. Wilson", bio:"Thomas Francis Wilson (born April 15, 1959) is an American actor, writer, musician, painter, voice-over artist and stand-up comedian.  He is best known for playing Biff Tannen (and his grandson Griff Tannen and great-grandfather Buford \"Mad Dog\" Tannen) in the Back to the Future trilogy and Coach Ben Fredricks on NBC's Freaks and Geeks. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Thomas F.  Wilson, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gg04BCW4bTagLqxTxvw4eUAUoOx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1065"}}, {tmdbId:"4040", properties:{bornIn:"Union, New Jersey, U.S.", imdbId:"0943237", born:date('1951-10-09'), name:"Robert Wuhl", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRobert Wuhl (born October 9, 1951) is an American actor, comedian and writer. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Robert Wuhl, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uPLdA7NX6YLpAACoBHZ91a8V75I.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4040"}}, {tmdbId:"82442", properties:{imdbId:"0722221", born:date('1960-09-07'), name:"Phillip Rhee", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPhillip Rhee (born September 7, 1960) is a Korean-American actor and director, most famous for his role in the Best of the Best movie series.  Rhee holds ranks of 6th degree black belt in Tae Kwon Do, 3rd degree black belt in Hap Ki Do and 1st degree black belt in Kendo.  He is also skilled in Wing Chun Kung fu and is a good boxer.  He is the younger brother of Simon Rhee. \n\nHe currently lives in the Los Angeles vicinity and is working on a screenplay...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8DPwKPYUWqpHO2BBbYR3D9HlC1j.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82442"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"12134", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000476", born:date('1941-10-31'), name:"Sally Kirkland", bio:"Sally Kirkland is a American film and television actress...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lHTewZ3kzzXe49W8d2vRs7tbCPh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12134"}}, {tmdbId:"141046", properties:{bornIn:"Orange County, California, USA ", imdbId:"0519489", born:date('1967-01-05'), name:"Emily Longstreth", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/141046"}}, {tmdbId:"22131", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0000687", born:date('1943-09-28'), name:"J.T. Walsh", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nJames Thomas Patrick \"J.  T. \" Walsh (September 28, 1943 – February 27, 1998) was an American character actor.  He appeared in many well-known films, including Nixon, Hoffa, A Few Good Men, Backdraft, Miracle on 34th Street and Breakdown. \n\nWalsh was known for his roles as \"quietly sinister white-collar sleazeballs\" (quote from Leonard Maltin) in numerous feature films, and was described as \"everybody's favorite scumbag\" by Playboy magazine...", died:date('1998-02-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mBa1UnbbKryNtQKT3VOnzER1HiQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/22131"}}, {tmdbId:"18355", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0935664", born:date('1965-07-17'), name:"Alex Winter", bio:"Alexander Ross \"Alex\" Winter (born July 17, 1965) is an English-born American actor, film director, and film writer, best known for his role as Bill S.  Preston Esq.  in the 1989 film Bill & Ted's Excellent Adventure and its 1991 sequel Bill & Ted's Bogus Journey.  He is also well known for his role as Marko in the 1987 cult classic The Lost Boys and for co-writing, co-directing and starring in the 1993 film Freaked...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/a29D9okJ4WA2tSPiFbXs6f5JmvO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18355"}}, {tmdbId:"15903", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"0137506", born:date('1937-05-12'), name:"George Carlin", bio:"George Denis Patrick Carlin (May 12, 1937 – June 22, 2008) was an American stand-up comedian, social critic, actor and author, who won five Grammy Awards for his comedy albums.   Carlin was noted for his black humor as well as his thoughts on politics, the English language, psychology, religion, and various taboo subjects.  Carlin and his \"Seven Dirty Words\" comedy routine were central to the 1978 U. S.  Supreme Court case F. C. C.  v...", died:date('2008-06-22'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sLNjoQaPucmxx5Yw1NB1cGOOOHX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15903"}}, {tmdbId:"18359", properties:{bornIn:"Malta", imdbId:"0131811", born:date('1949-01-01'), name:"Terry Camilleri", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nTerry Camilleri (born 1949) is an Australian actor. \n\nCamilleri was born in Malta and made his feature film debut in Peter Weir's 1974 film The Cars That Ate Paris.  He portrayed the Emperor Napoleon I in the 1989 film Bill &amp; Ted's Excellent Adventure.  He also made a cameo appearance in Weir's The Truman Show. \n\nOther appearances include as Special Branch police officer Hemmings in the science fiction film Incident at Raven's Gate...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7snba5wE56wgHLUrASQxZySSm8C.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18359"}}, {tmdbId:"73427", properties:{bornIn:"Kitakyūshū, Fukuoka, Japan", imdbId:"0847264", born:date('1931-02-16'), name:"Ken Takakura", bio:"Ken Takakura (高倉 健, Takakura Ken), born Gouichi Oda (February 16, 1931, in Kitakyūshū, Fukuoka, Japan), is a Japanese actor best known for his brooding style and the stoic presence he brings to his roles.  Takakura gained his streetwise swagger and tough-guy persona watching yakuza turf battles over the lucrative black market and racketeering in postwar Fukuoka...", died:date('2014-11-10'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dcxZ3mpr8bJADQNbrbFj1PMnKCn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/73427"}}, {tmdbId:"12139", properties:{bornIn:"London, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0000357", born:date('1961-07-15'), name:"Lolita Davidovich", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLolita Davidovich (born July 15, 1961) is a Canadian film and television actress...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vQlk518qlef94XXJqtrkIqS3izo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12139"}}, {tmdbId:"89141", properties:{bornIn:" Dallas, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0362222", born:date('1929-11-20'), name:"Jerry Hardin", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8YOmaPciLNRPAp6WR7jrEBozb8a.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89141"}}, {tmdbId:"2886", properties:{bornIn:"Tulsa, Oklahoma, USA", imdbId:"0765605", born:date('1946-09-18'), name:"Gailard Sartain", bio:"Graduated from the University of Tulsa with a BFA.  A successful illustrator, Sartain's artistic credits range from record cover designs such as Leon Russell's \"Will O' the Wisp\" to illustrations for nationally published magazines.  Sartain created and hosted Tulsa's first late night off-the-wall comedy program, \"Dr.  Mazeppa Pompazoidi's Uncanny Film Festival and Camp Meeting\"...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oYCs7TlrvnwcNujQ2yzG4x7fz7f.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2886"}}, {tmdbId:"10361", properties:{bornIn:"Hempstead, Long Island, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000855", born:date('1939-03-14'), name:"Raymond J. Barry", bio:"Raymond J.  Barry (born March 14, 1939) is an American film, television and stage actor...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gDAchPBmFMKtUsqgHfzn3mX6SEM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10361"}}, {tmdbId:"1044946", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0262923", born:date('1971-01-16'), name:"Josh Evans", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1044946"}}, {tmdbId:"138020", properties:{imdbId:"0669733", born:date('1956-10-24'), name:"Tony Peck", bio:"Tony Peck was born on October 24, 1956.  He is an actor and writer, known for Sliver (1993), Pirates (1986) and El río que nos lleva (1989).  He was previously married to Cheryl Tiegs...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8vnwyAPsiY7mQHP1DAptfO09loU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/138020"}}, {tmdbId:"1280", properties:{bornIn:"St. Clair Shores, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0367496", born:date('1960-05-31'), name:"Don Harvey", bio:"Don Patrick Harvey II is an American actor and voice actor.  Harvey was born and raised in St.  Clair Shores, Michigan, the sixth of eight children.  He started acting in high school.  He did several shows before graduating and moving on to the University of Michigan where he studied English and Economics and did two years of classical ballet.  He then attended the Yale School of Drama and received a Masters of Fine Arts in Acting...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6lIpsq1ubKZMPMPA9tDixpn85PT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1280"}}, {tmdbId:"4764", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0000604", born:date('1965-05-24'), name:"John C. Reilly", bio:"John Christopher Reilly (born May 24, 1965), better known as John C.  Reilly is an American film and theatre actor.  Debuting in Casualties of War in 1989, he is one of several actors whose careers were launched by Brian De Palma.  To date, he has appeared in more than fifty films, including three separate films in 2002, each of which was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Picture...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/emZGoEa7iWPVbjQaiVMeLdq8KgH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4764"}}, {tmdbId:"79456", properties:{bornIn:"Atsugi, Kanagawa, Japan", imdbId:"0463592", born:date('1966-02-04'), name:"Kyôko Koizumi", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1sVS7oSLHwmY1L87tsBgSwBriw8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/79456"}}, {tmdbId:"1116684", properties:{imdbId:"4230239", name:"Milo", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1116684"}}, {tmdbId:"240606", properties:{bornIn:"Uganda", imdbId:"0609348", name:"Colin Mothupi", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6UgKaeheokO3CeRqm80XcjI9rcj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/240606"}}, {tmdbId:"163567", properties:{bornIn:"Palo Alto - California - USA", imdbId:"0484713", born:date('1950-08-22'), name:"Timothy Landfield", bio:"Timothy Landfield is an actor...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/163567"}}, {tmdbId:"2320382", properties:{name:"David Mandell", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2320382"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"43773", properties:{bornIn:"St. Louis, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0441537", born:date('1946-05-18'), name:"Andreas Katsulas", bio:"Andrew \"Andreas\" Katsulas (May 18, 1946 – February 13, 2006) was a Greek-American actor known for his roles as Ambassador G'Kar in the science fiction television series Babylon 5, as the one-armed villain Sykes in the film The Fugitive (1993), and as the Romulan Commander Tomalak on Star Trek: The Next Generation.  He also played Vissian Captain Drennik in the Star Trek: Enterprise episode \"Cogenitor\"...", died:date('2006-02-13'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/olrhsor8mhNkxyMv9MGPYO7McF3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/43773"}}, {tmdbId:"143265", properties:{imdbId:"0856778", name:"Anne Teyssèdre", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/143265"}}, {tmdbId:"38170", properties:{bornIn:"Échemiré, Maine-et-Loire, France", imdbId:"0703364", born:date('1948-08-05'), name:"Hugues Quester", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nHugues Quester (born 5 August 1948 in Échemiré, Maine-et-Loire) is a French actor.  He has appeared in over 60 films and television shows since 1969.  He starred in Raúl Ruiz's 1983 film City of Pirates. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Hugues Quester, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dZkFGlVW8y3HpcoKRCEk0wKFkgc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/38170"}}, {tmdbId:"37923", properties:{imdbId:"0201151", born:date('1968-01-01'), name:"Florence Darel", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uzAS55wo86DViezCbrv1jnzwXt9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/37923"}}, {tmdbId:"143266", properties:{imdbId:"0071744", name:"Eloïse Bennett", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/143266"}}, {tmdbId:"1367", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0397102", born:date('1937-08-05'), name:"Alan Howard", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAlan MacKenzie Howard, CBE, (born 5 August 1937) is an English actor known for his roles on stage, television and film. \n\nHe was a member of the Royal Shakespeare Company from 1966 to 1983, and played leading roles at the Royal National Theatre between 1992 and 2000. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Alan Howard, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2015-02-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jYHkGkFzRGrVRoX568Omr3ipmde.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1367"}}, {tmdbId:"7538", properties:{imdbId:"0077007", name:"Bill Bernstein", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7538"}}, {tmdbId:"58539", properties:{bornIn:"Boston, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0745029", born:date('1963-01-07'), name:"Stephanie Roth Haberle", bio:"Stephanie Roth Haberle is an American theatre and film actress, best known for her roles in \"Crimes and Misdemeanors\", \"Philadelphia\" and \"Deconstructing Harry\"...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/58539"}}, {tmdbId:"2227", properties:{bornIn:"Honolulu, Hawaii, USA", imdbId:"0000173", born:date('1967-06-20'), name:"Nicole Kidman", bio:"An American-born Australian actress, fashion model, singer and humanitarian.  After starring in a number of small Australian films and TV shows, Kidman's breakthrough was in the 1989 thriller Dead Calm.  Her performances in films such as To Die For (1995) and Moulin Rouge! (2001) received critical acclaim, and her performance in The Hours (2002) brought her the Academy Award for Best Actress, a BAFTA Award and a Golden Globe Award...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qaO2MTBhIKcAJg2rjMmoKCIBcXF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2227"}}, {tmdbId:"1954", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA ", imdbId:"0000708", born:date('1966-02-24'), name:"Billy Zane", bio:"William George \"Billy\" Zane, Jr.  (born February 24, 1966) is an American actor, producer and director.  He is probably best known for his roles as Caledon \"Cal\" Hockley in Titanic, The Phantom from The Phantom, John Wheeler in Twin Peaks and Mr.  E in CQ...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9HIubetYWAVLlHNb9aObL0fc0sT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1954"}}, {tmdbId:"75397", properties:{bornIn:"Hereford, England, UK", imdbId:"0612367", name:"Rod Mullinar", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7KfajqctENHJcdiDWjSHQ8Wd6y2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/75397"}}, {tmdbId:"2692", properties:{bornIn:"Westwood, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0000494", born:date('1969-02-28'), name:"Robert Sean Leonard", bio:"​Robert Sean Leonard (born February 28, 1969) is an award-winning American actor. \n\nHe has regularly starred in Broadway and off-Broadway productions, but is most known for his roles on House and in Dead Poets Society...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jXehZM0AWLJ2OIz4o0jFtHEzcMI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2692"}}, {tmdbId:"2694", properties:{bornIn:"Baltimore, Maryland, USA", imdbId:"0001038", born:date('1971-09-15'), name:"Josh Charles", bio:"Josh Charles is an American stage, film and television actor.  He is best known for the roles of Daniel \"Dan\" Rydell on \"Sports Night\" and as Will Gardner on \"The Good Wife\"...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iQMo7eUfOHKBi9z4PhKOtALnr4N.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2694"}}, {tmdbId:"70003", properties:{bornIn:"Newark, New Jersey", imdbId:"0086000", born:date('1941-05-10'), name:"Taurean Blacque", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nTaurean Blacque (born Herbert Middleton Jr.  in Newark, New Jersey, May 10, 1941) is an American television and stage actor, best known for his role as Detective Neal Washington on the series Hill Street Blues.  He also is a past national spokesman for adoptive services, having been one of the first single black men in the United States to adopt a child...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70003"}}, {tmdbId:"64778", properties:{bornIn:"Wadsworth, Ohio", imdbId:"0263583", born:date('1957-11-30'), name:"Nancy Everhard", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nNancy Everhard (born 30 November 1957 in Wadsworth, Ohio) is an American actress...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4wqKRYJUgXOZkyC4kNc9BkY2wGY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/64778"}}, {tmdbId:"70004", properties:{bornIn:"South Amboy, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0263760", born:date('1953-10-14'), name:"Greg Evigan", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGregory Ralph \"Greg\" Evigan (born October 14, 1953) is an American actor best known for the TV series B. J.  and the Bear, My Two Dads, P. S.  I Luv U and TekWar...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uzA9IZ0ieuk5qwXTjzGon5lmVbN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70004"}}, {tmdbId:"15860", properties:{bornIn:"Santa Monica, California, USA", imdbId:"0001208", born:date('1955-02-07'), name:"Miguel Ferrer", bio:"Miguel Ferrer (1955–2017) was an American actor and voice actor mostly known for villainous roles...", died:date('2017-01-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kQBRwJc9vzfUZXwUxTpdev9Gp4M.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15860"}}, {tmdbId:"67046", properties:{bornIn:"Taipei, Taiwan", imdbId:"0947313", born:date('1961-09-30'), name:"Sally Yeh", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nPjYA3Jp2iba7A6aWqPdfyOgs8V.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67046"}}, {tmdbId:"15531", properties:{bornIn:"Miami Beach, Florida, USA", imdbId:"0001115", born:date('1917-12-18'), name:"Ossie Davis", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nOssie Davis  (December 18, 1917 – February 4, 2005) was an African-American film actor, director, poet, playwright, writer, and social activist...", died:date('2005-02-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/552luZvO9bR8xIOMCMFZAVBwXNH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15531"}}, {tmdbId:"5699", properties:{bornIn:"Northport, Long Island, New York, USA", imdbId:"0526985", born:date('1949-04-21'), name:"Patti LuPone", bio:"Patti LuPone (born April 21, 1949) is an American singer and actress, known for her Tony Award-winning performances as Eva Perón in the 1979 musical Evita and as Rose in the 2008 revival of Gypsy, and for her Olivier Award-winning performance as Fantine in the original London cast of Les Misérables...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3Y3P7uqw9prGPQLbWHGGjfMY9cP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5699"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"6473", properties:{bornIn:"Golden Valley, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0001488", born:date('1959-01-31'), name:"Kelly Lynch", bio:"Kelly Lynch (born January 31, 1959) is an American actress.  Once a model for the Elite modeling agency, Lynch appeared in the film Drugstore Cowboy which starred Matt Dillon, and the film Road House which starred Patrick Swayze. \n\nLynch was born in Golden Valley, Minnesota, the daughter of Barbara, a modern dancer, and Robert Lynch, a restaurateur.  Lynch has been married to producer and writer Mitch Glazer since 1992 and has a daughter, Shane, born 1985, from a previous relationship...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ldsrzVrqPqVrer0eQSBCUx5FTo4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6473"}}, {tmdbId:"69122", properties:{bornIn:"Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA", imdbId:"0001287", born:date('1970-01-29'), name:"Heather Graham", bio:"Heather Joan Graham (born January 29, 1970) is an American actress.  She has appeared in such films as Austin Powers: the Spy Who Shagged Me, Lost in Space, Bowfinger, From Hell, Anger Management, and The Hangover.  She received critical acclaim for her performance in the 1989 film Drugstore Cowboy and for her role as Rollergirl in 1997's Boogie Nights, directed by Paul Thomas Anderson...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/avYdNkeg1oTvmrNJbFDcTlBCkKs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69122"}}, {tmdbId:"22675", properties:{bornIn:"Harlem, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001834", born:date('1960-09-04'), name:"Damon Wayans", bio:"Damon Kyle Wayans (born September 4, 1960) is an American stand-up comedian, writer and actor, one of the Wayans brothers...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pdSOalf1r7GKlcUhpKeBntAqgA6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/22675"}}, {tmdbId:"21399", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0798779", born:date('1946-07-02'), name:"Ron Silver", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRonald Arthur \"Ron\" Silver (July 2, 1946 – March 15, 2009) was an American actor, director, producer, radio host and political activist. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Ron Silver, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2009-03-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6urQBScK7Vq6q5niaMMEmzW3DGP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21399"}}, {tmdbId:"78718", properties:{bornIn:"Warsaw, Mazowieckie, Poland", imdbId:"0825555", born:date('1956-01-31'), name:"Malgorzata Zajaczkowska", bio:"Malgorzata Zajaczkowska is a Polish film and television actress...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/65PjAXN1lAPSri55M4uV44DCmuY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78718"}}, {tmdbId:"70243", properties:{bornIn:"South Carolina, USA", imdbId:"0457755", born:date('1927-01-17'), name:"Eartha Kitt", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEartha Mae Kitt (January 17, 1927 – December 25, 2008) was an American actress, singer and cabaret star.  She was perhaps best known for her highly distinctive singing style and her 1953 hit Christmas song \"Santa Baby\".  Orson Welles once called her the \"most exciting woman in the world. \" She took over the role of Catwoman for the third season of the 1960s Batman television series, replacing Julie Newmar, who was unavailable for the final season...", died:date('2008-12-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/e1Lc2KU1ejimRNOMAL3mHegQFvc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70243"}}, {tmdbId:"67377", properties:{imdbId:"0704618", born:date('1977-06-02'), name:"Ellie Raab", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67377"}}, {tmdbId:"12930", properties:{bornIn:"New York, City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000451", born:date('1982-01-08'), name:"Gaby Hoffmann", bio:"Gabrielle Mary Hoffmann (born January 8, 1982) is an American film and television actress best known for her roles on Sleepless in Seattle, Transparent and Girls, which garnered her nominations for the Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Supporting Actress in a Comedy Series and Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Guest Actress in a Comedy Series in 2015, respectively.  Additionally, she is remembered as a child actress from the films Field of Dreams, Uncle Buck, Now and Then, and Volcano...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/51X4CaXZNRawchUDSj1tOPeMguK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12930"}}, {tmdbId:"105962", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0680541", born:date('1960-05-06'), name:"Julianne Phillips", bio:"Julianne Phillips is an American model and actress.  She began her career as a model in the early 1980s, moved on to acting, attracted attention as the first wife of Bruce Springsteen, and later portrayed Francesca \"Frankie\" Reed on the television drama series Sisters...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4n9oCCsZ2jR7PLdOpUEIXwuApaZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/105962"}}, {tmdbId:"21283", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0724673", born:date('1926-09-01'), name:"Lee Richardson", died:date('1999-10-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yqJMNzrKEwLIGnHky1DZZ9Gj4jw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21283"}}, {tmdbId:"7852", properties:{bornIn:"Cleveland, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0522554", born:date('1928-03-25'), name:"Jim Lovell", bio:"James \"Jim\" Arthur Lovell, Jr. , (born March 25, 1928) is a former NASA astronaut and a retired captain in the United States Navy, most famous as the commander of the Apollo 13 mission, which suffered a critical failure en route to the Moon but was brought back safely to Earth by the efforts of the crew and mission control.  Lovell was also the command module pilot of Apollo 8, the first Apollo mission to enter lunar orbit...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fTxVmhcG3noMlycNvIJLcffumcj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7852"}}, {tmdbId:"106838", properties:{bornIn:"Neptune, New Jersey", imdbId:"0777749", born:date('1935-10-25'), name:"Russell Schweickart", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRussell Louis \"Rusty\" Schweickart aka Schweikart (born October 25, 1935) is an American astronaut.  Schweickart was born in Neptune, New Jersey.  He earned an B. S.  and M. S.  in Aeronautics/Astronautics from MIT in 1956 and 1963 respectively.  He is also a former member of the 101st Tactical Fighter Squadron. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Russell Schweickart, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/106838"}}, {tmdbId:"106839", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, United States", imdbId:"0148646", born:date('1934-03-14'), name:"Eugene Cernan", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEugene Andrew Cernan was an American astronaut, naval aviator, electrical engineer, aeronautical engineer, and fighter pilot.  During the Apollo 17 mission, Cernan became the eleventh person to walk on the Moon.  Since he re-entered the lunar module after Harrison Schmitt on their third and final lunar excursion, he was the last person to have walked on the Moon...", died:date('2017-01-16'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/106839"}}, {tmdbId:"106840", properties:{bornIn:"Rome, Italy", imdbId:"0172531", born:date('1930-10-31'), name:"Michael Collins", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMichael Collins (born October 31, 1930 in Rome, Italy) is a former American astronaut and test pilot.  Selected as part of the third group of fourteen astronauts in 1963, he flew in space twice.  His first spaceflight was Gemini 10, in which he and command pilot John Young performed two rendezvous with different spacecraft and Collins undertook two EVAs.  His second spaceflight was as the command module pilot for Apollo 11...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9YjcTp3TJZ69AWpAipmoiMn0ARr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/106840"}}, {tmdbId:"64730", properties:{bornIn:"New Westminster, British Columbia, Canada", imdbId:"0129445", born:date('1969-01-21'), name:"Todd Caldecott", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nTodd Caldecott (born January 21, 1969) is a clinical herbalist, Ayurvedic practitioner in Vancouver, British Columbia, author of the textbook Ayurveda: The Divine Science of Life, and a former actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Todd Caldecott, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iMZmsvMWNmXNQmybcEzt7HvcyLG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/64730"}}, {tmdbId:"64731", properties:{imdbId:"0667330", name:"Tiffany Paulsen", bio:"Tiffany Paulsen is a film actress, writer, director and producer...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8xJqAYlky3Fht5OuJP802i2TYGB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/64731"}}, {tmdbId:"61126", properties:{bornIn:"Burbank, California, USA", imdbId:"0592428", born:date('1979-01-01'), name:"Tim Mirkovich", bio:"Tim Mirkovich is an American film editor...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/61126"}}, {tmdbId:"62596", properties:{bornIn:"Auburn, California, USA", imdbId:"0387987", born:date('1955-04-08'), name:"Kane Hodder", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nKane Warren Hodder (born April 8, 1955) is an American actor and stuntman.  Standing 6 ft 2. 5 in (189. 2 cm), he is best known for his portrayal of Jason Voorhees in four films from the Friday the 13th film series (parts VII through X).  He is also known for his role as Victor Crowley in Hatchet...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mIZm6YOk0I9jCLDhxGVzUubgx8d.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/62596"}}, {tmdbId:"64062", properties:{bornIn:"Louisville, Kentucky, USA", imdbId:"0511270", born:date('1968-04-01'), name:"Traci Lind", bio:"Traci Lind (born April 1, 1968 in Louisville, Kentucky) is an American film actress who is known for playing Alex Young in Fright Night II and Missy McCloud in My Boyfriend's Back.  She also starred in The Road to Wellville and The End of Violence.  She was billed in Fright Night II as Traci Lin.  She began modeling at age 13 after being discovered by Elite's head, John Casablancas...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jqnzAcNrZMW4j7lXTreFK1axgzc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/64062"}}, {tmdbId:"137952", properties:{imdbId:"0083467", born:date('1963-02-13'), name:"Jesse Birdsall", bio:"Jesse Birdsall (born 13 February 1963) is an English actor, known for his role as Marcus Tandy in the BBC1 soap opera Eldorado, his role in the adventure series Bugs (1995–1999) as Nick Beckett, his role in Footballers' Wives as football manager, Roger Webb between 2004 and 2006, and his roles as Fraser Black in Hollyoaks and as villain Ron Gregory in a few episodes of The Bill...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pCN4ozHAznWkDflzeoXukFzF1ou.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/137952"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"34902", properties:{bornIn:"Rawtenstall, Lancashire, England", imdbId:"0001363", born:date('1964-01-18'), name:"Jane Horrocks", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBarbara Jane Horrocks (born 18 January 1964) is an English stage, screen and television actress, voice artist, musician, and singer.  She is best known for her role as \"Bubble\" in the TV series Absolutely Fabulous as well as her distinctive voice. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jane Horrocks, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1Uru2m9LC2ptTa67bEIh1TEgl6r.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34902"}}, {tmdbId:"70965", properties:{bornIn:"New York, New York, U.S.A.", imdbId:"0268602", born:date('1951-06-01'), name:"Lena Farugia", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70965"}}, {tmdbId:"70966", properties:{bornIn:"Durban, Natal, South Africa", imdbId:"0835415", name:"Hans Strydom", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70966"}}, {tmdbId:"70967", properties:{imdbId:"0251907", name:"Eiros", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70967"}}, {tmdbId:"42308", properties:{bornIn:"Queens, New York, USA", imdbId:"0823462", born:date('1944-01-01'), name:"Beau Starr", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yFNI54Z6lZGZ7jqeDvZ9UhyLEfB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/42308"}}, {tmdbId:"56949", properties:{bornIn:"St. Louis, Missouri, U.S.", imdbId:"0289359", born:date('1922-12-09'), name:"Redd Foxx", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJohn Elroy Sanford (December 9, 1922 – October 11, 1991), better known by his stage name Redd Foxx,  was an American comedian and actor, best known for his starring role on the sitcom Sanford and Son. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Redd Foxx, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of  contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1991-10-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kWpXo9XUjhs2KDXrwGeod4iMMld.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56949"}}, {tmdbId:"1920", properties:{bornIn:"Winona, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0000213", born:date('1971-10-29'), name:"Winona Ryder", bio:"Winona Laura Horowitz (born October 29, 1971) better known under her professional name Winona Ryder, is an American actress.  She made her film debut in the 1986 film Lucas.  Ryder's first significant role came in Tim Burton's Beetlejuice (1988) as a goth teenager, which won her critical and commercial recognition...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5yteOSY2lgGOgSWmRTlxqfY59MS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1920"}}, {tmdbId:"19144", properties:{bornIn:"Memphis, Tennessee, USA", imdbId:"0001147", born:date('1971-04-12'), name:"Shannen Doherty", bio:"​Shannen Doherty (born April 12, 1971) is an American actress, producer, author and television director, known for her work in Heathers as well as on Beverly Hills, 90210 and Charmed...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lxzxWLKvQ699o2LGXxP6rldPt5S.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19144"}}, {tmdbId:"4801", properties:{imdbId:"0266170", born:date('1964-12-03'), name:"Lisanne Falk", bio:"Lisanne Falk (born December 3, 1964) is an American actress and film producer. \n\nFalk is a former child model who worked at the Ford Modeling Agency with a young Brooke Shields.  She portrays the seemingly upset young woman in a men's restroom on the cover of the Foreigner's 1979 album Head Games.  Her modeling work was featured in the book Lisanne: A Young Model. \n\nShe played the role of Heather McNamara in the black comedy film Heathers (1988) alongside Winona Ryder...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pt84JI4xUFqHlf53o515JXjfSW7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4801"}}, {tmdbId:"47493", properties:{bornIn:"Bristol, England", imdbId:"0791871", born:date('1956-08-20'), name:"Simon Shepherd", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ok3v0YQE7kpMl2PcYE5IZ5XO3JO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/47493"}}, {tmdbId:"66250", properties:{imdbId:"0488289", name:"James Larkin", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/66250"}}, {tmdbId:"82406", properties:{bornIn:"Prostějov, Czechoslovakia (present-day Czech Republic)", imdbId:"0005320", born:date('1965-04-09'), name:"Paulina Porizkova", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPaulina Porizkova-Ocasek (born Pavlína Pořízková on 9 April 1965) is a Czechoslovakian model and actress.  At the age of eighteen years, she became the first woman from Eastern Europe to grace the cover of the Sports Illustrated swim-suit issue.  She was the second woman (after Christie Brinkley) to be featured on the swim-suit issue's front cover consecutive times (1984 and 1985)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sHv11p0zlCJxgezzL3KlzHHblqc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82406"}}, {tmdbId:"24685", properties:{imdbId:"0267232", born:date('1938-02-24'), name:"James Farentino", died:date('2012-01-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bC8ZMVBiqGrVrCpPWnYDriAi3Jk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24685"}}, {tmdbId:"40009", properties:{bornIn:"Washington, District of Columbia, USA", imdbId:"0001242", born:date('1958-01-04'), name:"Matt Frewer", bio:"Matt Frewer is an American Canadian singer, comedian, film and television actor, best known for creating television icon Max Headroom.  He is a graduate in Acting from the Bristol Old Vic Drama School, Bristol, England, UK...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5yQeoDfwsSOnO8H2g8UjPLg6buG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/40009"}}, {tmdbId:"57418", properties:{imdbId:"0833519", born:date('1948-04-28'), name:"Marcia Strassman", died:date('2014-10-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7pihpMY2GlwpAvpGLRYMbOj2T3Y.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57418"}}, {tmdbId:"57419", properties:{bornIn:"Boise, Idaho, USA", imdbId:"0840133", born:date('1955-04-17'), name:"Kristine Sutherland", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tYlPr78jZePpa3NDelqiAx2Ymt0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57419"}}, {tmdbId:"6684", properties:{bornIn:"Davenport, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0001223", born:date('1970-03-24'), name:"Lara Flynn Boyle", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.  Lara Flynn Boyle  (born March 24, 1970) is an American film and television actress best known for her performances as Laura Palmer's best friend Donna Hayward in Twin Peaks and Assistant District Attorney Helen Gamble in The Practice.  She has had a number of movie roles from the late 1980s through the present but has found the most recognition through her roles in television series...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jP9XCLHYGhnnyDYlHkH9gwEtWQm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6684"}}, {tmdbId:"57453", properties:{bornIn:"Greenville, Mississippi, USA", imdbId:"0141617", born:date('1960-03-09'), name:"Finn Carter", bio:"Finn Carter (born Elizabeth Fearn Carter) is an American actress.  She is the daughter of former United States State Department Assistant Secretary of State for Public Affairs, Hodding Carter III, and his first wife, the former Margaret Ainsworth Wolfe...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fzPKYx7CvTrSffYD9P8AVx3hBHy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57453"}}, {tmdbId:"1093948", properties:{imdbId:"0934019", born:date('2018-05-01'), name:"Richard Wilson", bio:"Richard Wilson (born 23 October 1984 in Leicester, England) is a British-born Australian actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Richard Wilson (Australian actor), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1093948"}}, {tmdbId:"219498", properties:{bornIn:"Bristol, England, UK", imdbId:"0867233", born:date('1951-05-21'), name:"Jacqueline Tong", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJacqueline Tong (born 21 May 1951) is an English actress who is best known for playing Daisy Barnes in the period drama Upstairs, Downstairs from 1973 to 1975.  In 1975, she was nominated for Outstanding Supporting Actress in a Drama Series in the Primetime Emmy Awards. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jacqueline Tong, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/219498"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"739", properties:{bornIn:"Dublin, Ireland", imdbId:"0233145", born:date('1966-11-11'), name:"Alison Doody", bio:"Alison Doody was born in Dublin in 1966, in a well-off family.  She is the youngest of three children.  She was educated in a convent, where she gained a passion for the arts.  She later studied at the National College of Fine Arts in Dublin, but left because she lacked the motivation and thought she would take a year off to think it out.  Meanwhile, while sitting in a café with friends, she was approached by a still photographer who asked her if she would be interested to model...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kXFUXzdTxcmT76G3yiuLoIOTK3R.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/739"}}, {tmdbId:"33533", properties:{bornIn:"St. Louis, Missouri", imdbId:"0711058", born:date('1944-08-07'), name:"David Rasche", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDavid Rasche (born August 7, 1944) is an American actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article David Rasche, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bWPhfa4m8pXVneP1gf37xvuMUCA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33533"}}, {tmdbId:"38524", properties:{bornIn:"Montréal, Québec, Canada", imdbId:"0089937", born:date('1957-04-14'), name:"Lothaire Bluteau", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nLothaire Bluteau (born 14 April 1957) is a Canadian Québécois actor.  He was born in Montreal, Quebec and performs in both French and English.  He had a recurring role in the third season of the television series 24 as the character Marcus Alvers. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Lothaire Bluteau licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/d7861HYA8NKxorco4wijxjZAvqz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/38524"}}, {tmdbId:"32946", properties:{imdbId:"0929075", born:date('1963-07-16'), name:"Catherine Wilkening", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jVHrATav41qzL9gqSYFtmWD6uPz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/32946"}}, {tmdbId:"38525", properties:{imdbId:"0871928", born:date('1950-01-01'), name:"Johanne-Marie Tremblay", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vjaIzsYH7qxImdpEO65hBVr3MpZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/38525"}}, {tmdbId:"38526", properties:{bornIn:"Jonquière, Quebec, Canada", imdbId:"0320721", born:date('1950-08-10'), name:"Rémy Girard", bio:"Rémy Girard (born August 10, 1950) is a Canadian actor and former television host from Quebec...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ka9GhZNqJMdWT3KZUaGXeXC65a5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/38526"}}, {tmdbId:"60705", properties:{bornIn:"Hartford, Connecticut, USA", imdbId:"0001299", born:date('1962-03-18'), name:"Thomas Ian Griffith", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nThomas Ian Griffith (born March 18, 1962) is an American actor who has starred in films and on television. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Thomas Ian Griffith, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7Ax4V3Aod20tKMmLRPP5UNiiCq0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/60705"}}, {tmdbId:"64655", properties:{bornIn:"Vacaville, California, United States", imdbId:"0018966", born:date('1959-03-12'), name:"Dennis Alexio", bio:"Dennis \"The Terminator\" Alexio is considered to be one of, if not the, greatest heavyweight kick boxing champion in the sport's history.  His record is an outstanding 70-2, with 65 wins by way of knockout.  Alexio developed a strong friendship with Jean-Claude Van Damme and the two made the highly popular and successful film, The Kickboxer together.  Alexio is retired from fighting, but appears at many functions for both the film and martial art's communities...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/52JnJl2obmRKsOTHtJLriQsEQuK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/64655"}}, {tmdbId:"64662", properties:{bornIn:"Hong Kong, British Crown Colony [now China]", imdbId:"0150862", born:date('1949-05-25'), name:"Dennis Chan", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wW90J7wyACpndFPgwq5TFtyKHaO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/64662"}}, {tmdbId:"222508", properties:{bornIn:"Taza, Marocco", imdbId:"0702680", born:date('1962-09-12'), name:"Michel Qissi", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/soDGuFZFfNhcxkq24WYx0aw05BX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/222508"}}, {tmdbId:"37822", properties:{bornIn:"Red Bank, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0229930", born:date('1964-07-16'), name:"Peter Dobson", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hvBUOf3hLnjUGbZuSwZWG5m76ur.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/37822"}}, {tmdbId:"18292", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0865119", born:date('1946-07-11'), name:"Beverly Todd", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBeverly Todd (born July 11, 1946) is an American actress, producer and writer.  Todd gained major work during the 1970s, appearing in notable films such as The Lost Man (1969), They Call Me MISTER Tibbs! (1970), Brother John (1971) and A Piece of the Action (1977).  This eventually led to other distinguished and more important work.  Her more memorable roles came in Lean on Me and the film Crash...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18292"}}, {tmdbId:"53584", properties:{bornIn:"The Bronx, New York, USA", imdbId:"0635978", born:date('1920-12-23'), name:"Alan North", bio:"After wartime naval service, Alan North began his show business career as a stage manager in New York.  He first worked on Broadway in \"Plain and Fancy\", doubling up as understudy for the small part of Isaac Miller.  The play had a successful run between 1955 and 1956 (461 performances) and this led to further acting work in diverse productions, ranging from musical comedy to straight dramatic parts, both on and off Broadway...", died:date('2000-01-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3aMTGX3cy2siUCkxwvHbB9ovC0K.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53584"}}, {tmdbId:"122402", properties:{bornIn:"Ivalo, Finland", imdbId:"0904901", born:date('1953-09-17'), name:"Kari Väänänen", bio:"Kari Kyösti Väänänen (born 17 September 1953 in Ivalo) is a Finnish actor and director.  Domestically he is a member of the Ryhmäteatteri group of actors.  He was introduced to international audiences by Aki Kaurismäki; and belongs to the list of his \"trusted\" stable of actors. \n\nHis most challenging role has been the eponymous mafia hitman of Rosso, for which he learned all his lines phonetically, without previously speaking a word of Italian...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qKl4FvzpHQVIqTUtP7a8fjTIixQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/122402"}}, {tmdbId:"69552", properties:{imdbId:"0433520", name:"Sakke Järvenpää", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69552"}}, {tmdbId:"69553", properties:{imdbId:"0450212", name:"Heikki Keskinen", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69553"}}, {tmdbId:"57116", properties:{bornIn:"Staten Island, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0423774", born:date('1950-01-09'), name:"David Johansen", bio:"David Roger Johansen (born January 9, 1950) is an American rock, protopunk, blues, and pop singer, songwriter and actor.  He is best known as a member of the seminal protopunk band The New York Dolls.  He is also known for his work under the pseudonym Buster Poindexter.   David has appeared in several films including Car 54, Where Are You? and Scrooged with Bill Murray...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57116"}}, {tmdbId:"7906", properties:{bornIn:"Harbor City, California, USA", imdbId:"0000236", born:date('1958-09-16'), name:"Jennifer Tilly", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJennifer Tilly (born September 16, 1958) is an American actress and poker player.  She is an Academy Award nominee, and a World Series of Poker Ladies' Event bracelet winner.  She is sister to Academy-Award-nominated actress Meg Tilly. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jennifer Tilly, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/umv1NMi6EFt436jZO2SE1xN82Lf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7906"}}, {tmdbId:"14324", properties:{bornIn:"North Kensington, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0000722", born:date('1928-02-29'), name:"Joss Ackland", bio:"Sidney Edmond Jocelyn Ackland CBE (born 29 February 1928), known as Joss Ackland, is an English actor who has appeared in more than 130 films in his career, as well as numerous television appearances. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Joss Ackland, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/k8GQrf54DLILcLBmnMq94xijA6z.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14324"}}, {tmdbId:"10679", properties:{bornIn:"Huntington, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000508", born:date('1961-02-11'), name:"Carey Lowell", bio:"Carey Lowell (born February 11, 1961) is an American actress and former model. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Carey Lowell, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nNfJD8JESNzsTt3PU6npwWg5aqi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10679"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"2055", properties:{bornIn:"Astoria, Queens, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001108", born:date('1951-06-26'), name:"Robert Davi", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRobert John Davi (born June 26, 1953) is an American actor and singer.  He played roles such as Vietnam veteran and Special Agent Johnson in Die Hard the villainous, singing Fratelli brother, Jake, in The Goonies, and Al Torres in the cult classic Showgirls...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yizOUAKs59CwKM6pU30gIP9gTup.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2055"}}, {tmdbId:"10680", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000650", born:date('1967-03-27'), name:"Talisa Soto", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nTalisa Soto (born March 27, 1967) is an American model and actress. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Talisa Soto, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/omoSOpZTct2gc9BotGWv7e2JpVS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10680"}}, {tmdbId:"31468", properties:{bornIn:"Portland, Maine", imdbId:"0055549", born:date('1972-11-07'), name:"Christopher Daniel Barnes", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nChristopher Daniel Barnes (born November 7, 1972), also known professionally as C. D.  Barnes and C. B.  Barnes, is an American actor.  He is best known for providing the voice of Peter Parker/Spider-Man on the 1994 Fox animated television series Spider-Man: The Animated Series, and for his portrayal of Greg Brady in the films The Brady Bunch Movie and A Very Brady Sequel.  He was once the national teenage spokesperson for Greenpeace...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9bxL5NR3HteEOQ9kzJRSuaXLZg8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31468"}}, {tmdbId:"63978", properties:{bornIn:"Rockford, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0072533", born:date('1961-10-10'), name:"Jodi Benson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJodi Marie Benson (born Jodi Marie Marzorati on October 10, 1961) is an American voice actress and soprano singer.  She is best known for providing both the speaking and the singing voices of Disney's Princess Ariel in The Little Mermaid and its sequels.  In 2002 and 2006, she reprised the role of Ariel in the English versions of the Kingdom Hearts series...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2qX8QKHCaFWnCcIhb3VgZeX9HPz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/63978"}}, {tmdbId:"35232", properties:{bornIn:"Louisiana, USA", imdbId:"0140946", born:date('1927-05-05'), name:"Pat Carroll", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/r7JwQ9wmolpgPUFz8iSmgPy0SbH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/35232"}}, {tmdbId:"77920", properties:{bornIn:"North York, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0005177", born:date('1955-11-29'), name:"Howie Mandel", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nHoward Michael \"Howie\" Mandel (born November 29, 1955) is a Canadian stand-up comedian, television host, and actor.  He is well known as host of the NBC game show Deal or No Deal, as well as the show's daytime and Canadian-English counterparts.  Before his career as a game show host, Mandel was best known for his role on the NBC medical drama St.  Elsewhere.  He is also well-known for being the creator and star of the children's cartoon Bobby's World...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yqnHDPtu3gFdnVmE9YmyEG5IaPM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77920"}}, {tmdbId:"27012", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0320180", born:date('1948-11-14'), name:"Robert Ginty", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRobert Ginty (November 14, 1948 – September 21, 2009) was an American movie actor, producer, scenarist, and director of movies and TV series episodes. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Robert Ginty, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2009-09-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jpPeOev6AMggRqlwikBOz4emSs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27012"}}, {tmdbId:"105197", properties:{bornIn:" Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0883940", born:date('1965-12-16'), name:"Nancy Valen", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pHQWEKwnKreQkkhuPIfpPTKLnLK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/105197"}}, {tmdbId:"68470", properties:{bornIn:"Adachi, Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0847439", born:date('1964-05-05'), name:"Minami Takayama", bio:"Minami Takayama (高山 みなみ Takayama Minami, born Izumi Arai (新井 泉 Arai Izumi), May 5, 1964) is a Japanese voice actress and singer.  Minami is also a member of the pop group Two-Mix, and a part of DoCo when it was active. \n\nShe is best known for her roles in Kiki's Delivery Service as both Kiki and Ursula, Ranma ½ as Nabiki Tendo, Moomin as Moomin, Yaiba as Yaiba Kurogane, Nintama Rantarō as Rantarō Inadera, Danganronpa series as Hajime Hinata and Izuru Kamukura and Detective Conan as Conan Edogawa...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/68470"}}, {tmdbId:"218144", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0757290", born:date('1965-01-05'), name:"Rei Sakuma", bio:"Rei Sakuma is a Japanese voice actress affiliated with 81 Produce...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6imR1sDeylS2EoF7LHdp1ALeNTm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/218144"}}, {tmdbId:"68472", properties:{bornIn:" Fukuoka, Fukuoka Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0945322", born:date('1965-05-23'), name:"Kappei Yamaguchi", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMitsuo Yamaguchi (  Yamaguchi Mitsuo ), better known by his stage name of Kappei Yamaguchi ( Yamaguchi Kappei?) (May 23, 1965 - ) is a Japanese seiyū and actor from Fukuoka, affiliated with Gokū  and 21st Century Fox...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sbeWiK7FuUvPqF4yG6XR5CkPAqF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/68472"}}, {tmdbId:"57736", properties:{bornIn:"Nagoya, Aichi, Japan", imdbId:"0865078", born:date('1957-09-12'), name:"Keiko Toda", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vL9jUWw87TOHuEe7S81Ol7JJrtz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57736"}}, {tmdbId:"21246", properties:{bornIn:"North Hollywood, California, USA", imdbId:"0000929", born:date('1954-09-07'), name:"Corbin Bernsen", bio:"An American actor and director, known for his work on television.  He is best known from his role of Arnold Becker on L. A.  Law during the late 1980s and early 1990s,  and has appeared regularly on other shows, including General Hospital, Cuts, and Psych...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mLftTYHrvct0VBB8pGhJjLHZUXQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21246"}}, {tmdbId:"81882", properties:{imdbId:"0611833", name:"Danny Mulheron", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pFqdJM0Uo2IvWzAPVhuJ9M2taVu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81882"}}, {tmdbId:"81875", properties:{imdbId:"0015223", name:"Donna Akersten", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xllFmtKnxf2yQq8M9LZruEKAArL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81875"}}, {tmdbId:"81876", properties:{imdbId:"0222313", name:"Stuart Devenie", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oMsTZA7S5lzOyi16QmfclW0CzkV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81876"}}, {tmdbId:"81877", properties:{imdbId:"0352921", born:date('1957-01-01'), name:"Mark Hadlow", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7F4xB8CsTBbDK6IoYeI2QynAJ1u.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81877"}}, {tmdbId:"36169", properties:{bornIn:"Huron - South Dakota - USA", imdbId:"0001440", born:date('1951-07-12'), name:"Cheryl Ladd", bio:"Cheryl Ladd  (born Cheryl Jean Stoppelmoor; July 12, 1951) is an American actress, singer and author.  Ladd is best known for her role as Kris Munroe in the television series Charlie's Angels, hired amid a swirl of publicity prior to its second season in 1977 to replace the departing Farrah Fawcett-Majors.  Ladd remained with the show until its cancellation in 1981...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/s6L9CSbyT99sn5YK0bugJGLstnb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/36169"}}, {tmdbId:"36170", properties:{bornIn:"Kenosha, Wisconsin, USA", imdbId:"0871240", born:date('1940-03-07'), name:"Daniel J. Travanti", bio:"The highly regarded actor Daniel J.  Travanti was born Danielo Giovanni Travanty in the southeastern part of Wisconsin on March 7, 1940, but raised for a time in Iowa before returning to his native state.  The youngest son of an American Motors auto worker, he showed both athletic and academic prowess in high school on both the football and debate teams...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lxujL6z7nCJS4sI3fGbWlm3ONzx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/36170"}}, {tmdbId:"51544", properties:{bornIn:"Phoenix, Arizona, U.S.", imdbId:"0001858", born:date('1959-05-16'), name:"Mare Winningham", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMare Winningham (born May 16, 1959), born Mary Megan Winningham, is an American actress and singer-songwriter.  She has been nominated once for an Academy Award, Golden Globe and Drama Desk, 6 times for Emmy Awards (winning two), and has also won an Independent Spirit Award and two Screen Actors Guild Award nominations. \n\nShe is known for her role as Georgia Flood in the film Georgia, which earned her an Academy Award nomination...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ufNKjUzTzOkrVrIWtYBYjFkXJ9C.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/51544"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"11756", properties:{bornIn:"Fort Worth, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0359393", born:date('1924-02-25'), name:"Lou Hancock", died:date('1995-12-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1NGv178QgomuVC9kTc9gAThATMv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11756"}}, {tmdbId:"121012", properties:{bornIn:"Villemonble, Seine-Saint-Denis, France", imdbId:"0862006", born:date('1964-10-24'), name:"Luc Thuillier", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLuc Thuillier is a French actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Luc Thuillier, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lPOFXpb7uc3Zp2mdE6hlXvzlrlB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/121012"}}, {tmdbId:"20853", properties:{bornIn:"Strasbourg, France", imdbId:"0932870", born:date('1947-04-29'), name:"André Wilms", bio:"André Wilms (born 29 April 1947 in Strasbourg) is a French film and television actor who has also appeared in German and Finnish films.  Wilms was the winner of the Best Supporting European Actor award at the 1992 European Film Awards for his work in Aki Kaurismäki's La Vie de Bohème. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article André Wilms, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oZxIzqgLG5jsRab3AlwxqgP1lML.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20853"}}, {tmdbId:"18345", properties:{bornIn:"Dublin, Ireland", imdbId:"0002084", born:date('1945-02-17'), name:"Brenda Fricker", bio:"Brenda Fricker (born February 17, 1945 in Dublin) is an Irish actress of theatre, film and television.  She had appeared in more than 30 films and television roles.  In 1989, she won the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress for My Left Foot.   Description above from the Wikipedia article Brenda Fricker, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/osvE1ZFs7SsqCzTpoTia8pUwamX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18345"}}, {tmdbId:"64039", properties:{imdbId:"0924009", name:"Alison Whelan", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/64039"}}, {tmdbId:"68973", properties:{bornIn:"Miyazaki, Miyazaki Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0619185", born:date('1966-07-15'), name:"Masatoshi Nagase", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/i4FjAoP2xPtG82lEGnIkL7mFc6g.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/68973"}}, {tmdbId:"942004", properties:{bornIn:"Cleveland, Ohio, U.S.", imdbId:"0370221", born:date('1929-07-18'), name:"Screamin' Jay Hawkins", bio:"Jalacy \"Screamin' Jay\" Hawkins was an American singer, songwriter, musician, and actor.  Famed chiefly for his powerful, operatic vocal delivery and wildly theatrical performances of songs such as \"I Put a Spell on You\" (1956), he sometimes used macabre props onstage, making him an early pioneer of shock rock...", died:date('2000-02-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/s9qV12bWhOsy5aGssukatbqf651.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/942004"}}, {tmdbId:"13603", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0497046", name:"Cinqué Lee", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13603"}}, {tmdbId:"3196", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0000496", born:date('1973-06-21'), name:"Juliette Lewis", bio:"Juliette Lake Lewis is an American actress and singer known for her portrayals of offbeat characters, often in films with dark themes.  She began her career with small film and television roles in the late 1980s...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vvitS2sZSM9RupCf5B0sZYNS6wT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3196"}}, {tmdbId:"16478", properties:{bornIn:"Bree, Belgium", imdbId:"0301959", born:date('1975-04-30'), name:"Johnny Galecki", bio:"Johnny Galecki is a Belgian-born American actor, best known for his roles as David Healy in Roseanne, Rusty Griswold in National Lampoon's Christmas Vacation, and as Leonard Hofstadter in The Big Bang Theory...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ta3YYBteR0qB2h5Qx1r42pFYcda.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16478"}}, {tmdbId:"58529", properties:{imdbId:"0154059", born:date('1927-04-24'), name:"Marvin Chatinover", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/58529"}}, {tmdbId:"58530", properties:{bornIn:"The Bronx, New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0703362", born:date('1908-09-13'), name:"Mae Questel", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMae Questel (September 13, 1908–January 4, 1998) was an American actress and vocal artist best known for providing the voices for the animated characters Betty Boop and Olive Oyl.  She began in vaudeville, and played occasional small roles in films and television later in her career, most notably the role of Aunt Bethany in 1989's National Lampoon's Christmas Vacation...", died:date('1998-01-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gb87p0KZj0y0kxlwmdeiPVk8xyM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/58530"}}, {tmdbId:"9994", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0000166", born:date('1963-06-15'), name:"Helen Hunt", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nHelen Elizabeth Hunt (born June 15, 1963) is an American actress, film director, and screenwriter.  She starred in the sitcom Mad About You for seven years, before being cast in the romantic comedy As Good as It Gets (for which she won the Academy Award for Best Actress) and The Curse of the Jade Scorpion.  Some of her other Hollywood credits include Twister, Cast Away, What Women Want and Pay It Forward...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vMxBCquKrYRMi7xROpEY0AlBVVt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9994"}}, {tmdbId:"63917", properties:{bornIn:"Columbia, Missouri, U.S.", imdbId:"0928244", born:date('1964-04-27'), name:"Lisa Wilcox", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLisa E.  Wilcox (born April 27, 1964) is an American actress who has starred in film and television. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Lisa Wilcox, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/63917"}}, {tmdbId:"63046", properties:{bornIn:"North Trenton, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0591702", born:date('1966-09-24'), name:"Kelly Jo Minter", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/a0HavDt0usax8VNTGZ6PVrklSce.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/63046"}}, {tmdbId:"104275", properties:{bornIn:"Red Bluff, California, USA", imdbId:"0368397", born:date('1967-12-07'), name:"Danny Hassel", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/104275"}}, {tmdbId:"16620", properties:{bornIn:"Augusta, Georgia, USA", imdbId:"0001356", born:date('1953-08-11'), name:"Hulk Hogan", bio:"Terry Gene Bollea, known by his ring name Hulk Hogan, is an American professional wrestler, actor, television personality, and musician best known for his time working for WWE.  Hogan enjoyed mainstream popularity in the 1980s and 90s as the all-American character Hulk Hogan in the World Wrestling Federation (NKA WWE), and as Hollywood Hogan, the villainous leader of the New World Order, in World Championship Wrestling (WCW).  Hogan was inducted into the WWE Hall of Fame in 2005...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pNKuTK7r8SS69tePps9491KFSjg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16620"}}, {tmdbId:"18891", properties:{bornIn:"Houston, Texas, U.S.", imdbId:"0000220", born:date('1958-12-23'), name:"Joan Severance", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nJoan Severance (born December 23, 1958) is an American actress and former fashion model. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Joan Severance, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jWEwLQtzVxTUZ8a05XUx1yoPpR5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18891"}}, {tmdbId:"29685", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, United States", imdbId:"0298281", born:date('1953-09-16'), name:"Kurt Fuller", bio:"Kurt Fuller is an American character actor.  He has appeared in a number of television, film, and stage projects.  He graduated from Lincoln High School in Stockton, California in 1971, and the University of California, Berkeley, in 1976...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kV02XLACLFd1YYQdSOgqy6lFmQ3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29685"}}, {tmdbId:"8396", properties:{bornIn:"Compton, California, USA", imdbId:"0001474", born:date('1958-06-24'), name:"Tommy 'Tiny' Lister", bio:"Tommy \"Tiny\" Lister (born Thomas Lister, Jr. ; June 24, 1958) is a character actor and former wrestler best known for his role as the neighborhood bully Deebo in the Friday series of movies.  He also had a short-lived professional wrestling career, wrestling Hulk Hogan in the World Wrestling Federation (WWF) after appearing as \"Zeus\" in Hogan's movie No Holds Barred.  Lister is blind in his right eye...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fwZoX5VWtXM55Mb11eLguixyIXI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8396"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"74296", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, USA ", imdbId:"0854418", born:date('1948-02-14'), name:"Teller", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nTeller (born Raymond Joseph Teller on February 14, 1948) is an American magician, illusionist, comedian, writer, and the frequently silent half of the comedy magic duo known as Penn &amp; Teller, along with Penn Jillette.  He is known for his advocacy of atheism, libertarianism, free-market economics, and scientific skepticism.  He legally changed his name from \"Raymond Joseph Teller\" to just \"Teller\"...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ixB8pYJHevXQP1aHXaHa8uXy6Tu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74296"}}, {tmdbId:"1737", properties:{bornIn:"Detroit, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0446314", born:date('1951-01-23'), name:"David Patrick Kelly", bio:"David Patrick Kelly (born January 23, 1951) is an American actor and musician who has appeared in numerous films, including some major roles. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article David Patrick Kelly, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pTlRWsOxiTRiKk4SEEOsIwlCSUp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1737"}}, {tmdbId:"56265", properties:{bornIn:"Chance, Maryland, USA", imdbId:"0001535", born:date('1959-07-01'), name:"Dale Midkiff", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nDale Alan Midkiff (born July 1, 1959) is an American actor...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lOxrQtMLFlbZQs8hykfCQzPfMSg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56265"}}, {tmdbId:"56266", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001304", born:date('1926-07-10'), name:"Fred Gwynne", bio:"An American actor.  Gwynne was best known for his roles in the 1960s sitcoms Car 54, Where Are You? and The Munsters, as well as his later roles in The Cotton Club, Pet Sematary and My Cousin Vinny...", died:date('1993-07-02'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iPWorQens6mGiB4jSJza5RxHfB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56266"}}, {tmdbId:"1743", properties:{bornIn:"Hollywood, California, USA", imdbId:"0000344", born:date('1957-11-24'), name:"Denise Crosby", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDenise Michelle Crosby is an American actress best known for portraying Security Chief Tasha Yar on Star Trek: The Next Generation.  She is also known for her numerous film and television roles, for starring in and producing the film Trekkies, and for being the granddaughter of Bing Crosby...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1Eoo8o3xRGflJ9kHxg1eFVwAwQa.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1743"}}, {tmdbId:"56267", properties:{bornIn:"Fort Meade, Maryland, USA", imdbId:"0339159", born:date('1959-10-08'), name:"Brad Greenquist", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eQTpC1PtQ9Q9J6VajNNoCrAyIao.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56267"}}, {tmdbId:"2440", properties:{bornIn:"Caterham, Surrey, England, United Kingdom", imdbId:"0631490", born:date('1949-12-12'), name:"Bill Nighy", bio:"William Francis \"Bill\" Nighy (pronounced /ˈnaɪ/ ny) is a British actor and comedian. \n\nHe worked in theatre and television before his first cinema role in 1981, and made his name in television with The Men's Room in 1991, in which he played the womanizer Prof.  Mark Carleton, whose extra-marital affairs kept him \"vital\"...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/acbigDOU1L1vMWAL3Wf0r8h8qLA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2440"}}, {tmdbId:"3093", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001820", born:date('1921-02-24'), name:"Abe Vigoda", bio:"Tall, dour-faced and slouch-shouldered character actor Abe Vigoda proved himself in both gritty dramatic roles, and as an actor with wonderful comedic timing. \n\nVigoda was born in Brooklyn, New York, to Lena (Moses) and Samuel Vigoda, both Russian Jewish immigrants.  His father was a tailor on the Lower East Side.  He made his first stage appearance at the age of 17 and plodded away in small theater shows for over 20 years...", died:date('2016-01-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/luWKPNb58IgJ2ovrtgPAzHGLLYL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3093"}}, {tmdbId:"1212249", properties:{bornIn:"Sudbury, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0174860", name:"Tim Conlon", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2spxhPR3kozQQNLXbr5ITTomDHc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1212249"}}, {tmdbId:"1213299", properties:{bornIn:"Toronto - Ontario - Canada", imdbId:"0696395", born:date('1968-05-18'), name:"Cynthia Preston", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nHeight     5' 6\" (1,68 m)\n\nCynthia Preston (born May 18, 1968), sometimes credited as Cyndy Preston, is a Canadian television and film actress. \n\nPreston was born in Toronto, Ontario, Canada.  Best known internationally for playing Faith Rosco on the American soap opera General Hospital from 2002 to 2005, and also for providing the voice of Zelda in The Legend of Zelda segments that aired as part of The Super Mario Bros.  Super Show in 1989...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tN8cuin62jQHbzrID5yXlJPclY2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1213299"}}, {tmdbId:"199303", properties:{imdbId:"0833635", name:"David Stratton", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/199303"}}, {tmdbId:"1087657", properties:{imdbId:"0852175", name:"Courtney Taylor", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1087657"}}, {tmdbId:"56182", properties:{imdbId:"0594540", born:date('1951-01-04'), name:"Kim Miyori", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56182"}}, {tmdbId:"21282", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, New York City, United States", imdbId:"0382676", born:date('1927-09-19'), name:"William Hickey", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nWilliam Edward Hickey (September 19, 1927 – June 29, 1997) was an American actor.  He was best known for his Oscar-nominated role as Don Corrado Prizzi in the John Huston 1985 film Prizzi's Honor, as well as the voice of Dr.  Finklestein in Tim Burton's The Nightmare Before Christmas (1993). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article William Hickey (actor), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1997-06-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/giWiDBa8ZQqUucVSpPv8IZ3KqhZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21282"}}, {tmdbId:"133771", properties:{bornIn:"Hot Springs, Arkansas, USA", imdbId:"0803765", born:date('1944-12-20'), name:"Jimmie F. Skaggs", died:date('2004-07-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aAu74ASz8HLACIP2vuhBqTIPJP2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/133771"}}, {tmdbId:"31364", properties:{bornIn:"Stratford-Upon-Avon, Warwickshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0235243", born:date('1952-12-12'), name:"Sarah Douglas", bio:"Sarah Douglas (born 12 December 1952) is an English actress.  She is perhaps best known for playing the Kryptonian supervillain Ursa in the first two Superman movies (1978 and 1980), and for her role as Pamela Lynch in the 1980s primetime drama series Falcon Crest (1983–85)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kAyLaj9EuRp1iUsusgLmsyg9CYs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31364"}}, {tmdbId:"82507", properties:{bornIn:"South Bend, Indiana, USA", imdbId:"0244270", born:date('1937-01-18'), name:"Dick Durock", bio:"An American actor and stuntman who appeared in over eighty films and over seven hundred television episodes.  He was best known for playing Swamp Thing in both the feature films Swamp Thing and The Return of Swamp Thing...", died:date('2009-09-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5hdL18WGSGGgjQMxSVZ9DOvFMza.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82507"}}, {tmdbId:"55188", properties:{bornIn:"Mosta, Malta", imdbId:"0119541", born:date('1963-05-12'), name:"Valerie Buhagiar", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55188"}}, {tmdbId:"234", properties:{bornIn:"Amherst, Nova Scotia, Canada", imdbId:"0703499", name:"Gerry Quigley", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nfnrdHOtFYhggXrpZvHF4CDAVdH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/234"}}, {tmdbId:"1640749", properties:{name:"Larry Hudson", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1640749"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"1374979", properties:{imdbId:"0809792", name:"Roger B. Smith", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1374979"}}, {tmdbId:"1374980", properties:{imdbId:"0110222", name:"Rhonda Britton", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1374980"}}, {tmdbId:"1090751", properties:{imdbId:"1208872", name:"Fred Ross", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1090751"}}, {tmdbId:"109622", properties:{bornIn:"Mexico City, Distrito Federal, Mexico", imdbId:"0019578", born:date('1956-12-12'), name:"Ana Alicia", bio:"Born in Mexico City, Mexico on December 12, 1956, Ana Alicia became the third of four children to Carlos Celestino Ortiz and Alicia Torres Ortiz.  She grew up in El Paso, Texas from age 6 after the passing of her father.  There, she lived with her grandmother, widowed mother, her uncle Louie and three siblings in a house her father had purchased for her grandmother. \n\nAna Alicia received a full scholarship to attend the prestigious Wellesley College in Massachusetts...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kIDoN8m2lIZ156lvfPu3a0qbbCx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/109622"}}, {tmdbId:"88031", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0892455", born:date('1958-06-04'), name:"Eddie Velez", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88031"}}, {tmdbId:"143443", properties:{bornIn:"Mexico City, Mexico", imdbId:"0423525", born:date('1965-07-24'), name:"Axel Jodorowsky", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/r9aZPxeHVFrjgAnjuOWHroDJtFi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/143443"}}, {tmdbId:"86489", properties:{bornIn:"Mexico City, Distrito Federal, Mexico", imdbId:"0345999", born:date('1953-01-10'), name:"Blanca Guerra", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nBlanca Guerra is a Mexican actress.  She was born in 1953 and in 1973 she has had various parts in the films Walker, Santa Sangre, Clear and Present Danger and several Mexican soap operas.  She was also a judge in the 1998 Miss Universe pageant. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Blanca Guerra, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/86489"}}, {tmdbId:"93655", properties:{bornIn:"Hollywood, California, USA", imdbId:"0830967", born:date('1934-11-16'), name:"Guy Stockwell", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGuy Harry Stockwell (November 16, 1934 – February 6, 2002) was an American actor who appeared in nearly 30 movies and 250 television series episodes. \n\nStockwell was born in Hollywood, California, the son of Nina Olivette (née Elizabeth Margaret Veronica), an actress and dancer, and Harry Bayless Stockwell, or Harry Stockwell, an actor and singer...", died:date('2002-02-06'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kUT8VPWDVTOvgyhHf29w2ggCIJx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/93655"}}, {tmdbId:"143444", properties:{imdbId:"0864622", name:"Thelma Tixou", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/143444"}}, {tmdbId:"2233", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0000403", born:date('1964-01-27'), name:"Bridget Fonda", bio:"Bridget Jane Fonda (born 27 January 1964) is an American actress.  She is best known for her roles in films such as The Godfather Part III, Single White Female, Point of No Return, It Could Happen to You, and Jackie Brown.  She is the daughter of Peter Fonda. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Bridget Fonda, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6XSABYzJ0mQWgBP4NJweqXdsdZy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2233"}}, {tmdbId:"1327", properties:{bornIn:"Burnley, Lancashire, England, UK", imdbId:"0005212", born:date('1939-05-25'), name:"Ian McKellen", bio:"Sir Ian Murray McKellen, CH, CBE (born 25 May 1939) is an English actor.  He is the recipient of six Laurence Olivier Awards, a Tony Award, a Golden Globe Award, a Screen Actors Guild Award, a BIF Award, two Saturn Awards, four Drama Desk Awards and two Critics' Choice Awards.  He has also received two Academy Award nominations, eight BAFTA film and TV nominations and five Emmy Award nominations...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5cnnnpnJG6TiYUSS7qgJheUZgnv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1327"}}, {tmdbId:"12132", properties:{bornIn:"Jasper, Alabama, USA", imdbId:"0740264", born:date('1955-04-06'), name:"Michael Rooker", bio:"Michael Rooker (born April 6, 1955) is an American actor...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dq3xFKDWJsQjPffm1bmB3TbMilq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12132"}}, {tmdbId:"9306", properties:{bornIn:"Honolulu, Hawaii, United States", imdbId:"0168892", born:date('1964-05-01'), name:"Scott Coffey", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nScott Coffey (born May 1, 1967) is an American actor, director, producer, screenwriter.  His acting credits include films such as Shag, Some Kind of Wonderful, Dream Lover, and Mulholland Drive.  As a director he made \"Ellie Parker\" in 2005 and the upcoming \"Jupiter\". \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Scott Coffey, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pNnNXyFpJzawKX0G6DrOw6yEVWb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9306"}}, {tmdbId:"18298", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001103", born:date('1951-04-21'), name:"Tony Danza", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nTony Danza (born Anthony Salvatore Iadanza; April 21, 1950) is an Italian-American actor best known for starring on the TV series Taxi and Who's the Boss?, for which Danza was nominated for an Emmy Award and four Golden Globe Awards.  In 1998, Danza won the People's Choice Award for Favorite Male Performer in a New Television Series for his work on the sitcom The Tony Danza Show...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9dTcKYiZV6pHUGNxx6auoBaHFqT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18298"}}, {tmdbId:"14835", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0642143", born:date('1928-08-29'), name:"Dick O'Neill", died:date('1998-11-17'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14835"}}, {tmdbId:"46393", properties:{bornIn:"Salt Lake City, Utah, USA", imdbId:"0001683", born:date('1952-11-03'), name:"Roseanne Barr", bio:"Roseanne Cherie Barr (born November 3, 1952) is an American actress, comedian, writer, television producer and director. \n\nBarr began her career in stand-up comedy at clubs in Colorado in the 1980s.  Her big break came in 1987 when she was cast in her own sitcom, Roseanne.  The show was a hit and lasted nine seasons, from 1988 to 1997.  Barr won both an Emmy Award and a Golden Globe Award for Best Actress for her work on the show...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oyY5lWTFzhymLB4sJ1OODseI3jR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/46393"}}, {tmdbId:"83437", properties:{bornIn:"Exmouth, Devon, England, UK", imdbId:"0172604", born:date('1940-09-03'), name:"Pauline Collins", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nPauline Collins, OBE (born 3 September 1940) is an English actress of the stage, television, and film.  She first came to prominence portraying Sarah Moffat in Upstairs, Downstairs and its spin-off Thomas & Sarah during the 1970s.  She later drew acclaim for playing the title role in the play Shirley Valentine for which she received Laurence Olivier, Tony, and Drama Desk awards...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/s5z4i4ixiOdh7h4GoDsJ18YHGcS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83437"}}, {tmdbId:"71010", properties:{bornIn:"Paisley, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0002018", born:date('1941-11-22'), name:"Tom Conti", bio:"Tom Conti (born 22 November 1941) is a Scottish actor, theatre director and novelist...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2OqrVBoTYX5oeU1Qt8tfq3i9JUQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71010"}}, {tmdbId:"83438", properties:{bornIn:"Enfield, Middlesex, England", imdbId:"0571549", born:date('1941-02-17'), name:"Julia McKenzie", bio:"​She was awarded the Laurence Olivier Theatre Award in 1983 (1982 season) for Best Actress in a Musical, Guys and Dolls.  She was awarded the Laurence Olivier Theatre Award in 1994 (1993 season) for Best Actress in a Musical for her performance in Sweeney Todd at the Royal National Theatre. \n\nShe was awarded the 1987 London Evening Standard Theatre Award for Best Actress for her performance in Woman in Mind...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kNQTuGDiu6s1A9yLqm4EjDmT8cd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83438"}}, {tmdbId:"47699", properties:{bornIn:"Liverpool, England, UK", imdbId:"0824102", born:date('1946-08-26'), name:"Alison Steadman", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAlison Steadman (born 26 August 1946) is an English actor.  She won the 1991 National Society of Film Critics Award for Best Actress for the Mike Leigh (her husband 1973-2001) film Life is Sweet, and the 1993 Olivier Award for Best Actress for her role as Mari in the original production of The Rise and Fall of Little Voice.  In a 2007 Channel 4 poll, the \"50 Greatest Actors\" voted for by other actors, she was ranked No.  42...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lPthoSzhSr8KDgFKOmILAYUkJ2l.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/47699"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"37211", properties:{bornIn:"Wien, Austria", imdbId:"0231085", born:date('1958-03-09'), name:"Birgit Doll", bio:"Birgit Doll was an Austrian stage and film actress and theatre director.  She graduated at the Max Reinhardt Seminar in 1976 and made her stage debut at the Salzburg State Theater.  Birgit Doll has worked with Ingmar Bergman, Michael Haneke,  Maximilian Schell, Otto Schenk and Peter Patzak...", died:date('2015-10-26'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wvJ2X0mQGt6povp5VKHTeBxPHDf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/37211"}}, {tmdbId:"141388", properties:{bornIn:"Vienna, Austria", imdbId:"0076679", born:date('1944-08-31'), name:"Dieter Berner", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6ILfskQ6R7SH6FEo7806FnoHPWy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/141388"}}, {tmdbId:"141389", properties:{imdbId:"0849892", name:"Leni Tanzer", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sA19vuXDNLS7X2JRcBR65x63svv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/141389"}}, {tmdbId:"6264", properties:{bornIn:"Trier-Eitelsbach, Germany", imdbId:"0759797", born:date('1953-06-25'), name:"Udo Samel", bio:"Udo Samel (born 25 June 1953) is a German actor.  He has appeared in more than 80 films and television shows since 1977.  He starred in the 1994 film Back to Square One, which was entered into the 44th Berlin International Film Festival. \n\nSource: Article \"Udo Samel\" from Wikipedia in english, licensed under CC-BY-SA 3. 0...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9l15dhFSnE6i9hqplfECsJiomUl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6264"}}, {tmdbId:"19262", properties:{bornIn:"Anaheim, California, USA", imdbId:"0715295", born:date('1958-01-11'), name:"Alyson Reed", bio:"Alyson Reed (born January 11, 1958) is an American dancer and actress, known for her role as Ms.  Darbus in the High School Musical series...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iSWg3DSnsc0FVWJsDR3eNjkAlqw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19262"}}, {tmdbId:"72421", properties:{bornIn:"New York City - New York - USA", imdbId:"0112063", born:date('1949-12-17'), name:"Joel Brooks", bio:"Joel Brooks was born on December 17, 1949.  He is an actor...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/202IdzSEDlz3dlqFEWKQvAarCmc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/72421"}}, {tmdbId:"83665", properties:{imdbId:"0693317", born:date('1964-01-01'), name:"Madeleine Potter", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cmMRzgJk8UrRUncx4qpLSOr5hKI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83665"}}, {tmdbId:"124262", properties:{bornIn:"Espoo, Finland", imdbId:"0617427", born:date('1959-03-10'), name:"Taneli Mäkelä", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3WdJLnVQWBBLNEHXuTeI5NubaLZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/124262"}}, {tmdbId:"53509", properties:{bornIn:"Lappeenranta, Finland", imdbId:"0896801", born:date('1956-05-24'), name:"Vesa Vierikko", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53509"}}, {tmdbId:"228650", properties:{bornIn:"Kerava, Finland", imdbId:"0868039", born:date('1958-02-01'), name:"Timo Torikka", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6mt2zA5ry5gi5FmahjBKt4fDNch.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/228650"}}, {tmdbId:"994246", properties:{imdbId:"0655013", name:"Heikki Paavilainen", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/994246"}}, {tmdbId:"10742", properties:{bornIn:"Palo Alto, California, USA", imdbId:"0000159", born:date('1964-12-08'), name:"Teri Hatcher", bio:"Teri Lynn Hatcher (born December 8, 1964) is an American actress.  She is known for her television roles as Susan Mayer on the ABC comedy-drama series Desperate Housewives, and Lois Lane on the ABC comedy-drama series Lois &amp; Clark: The New Adventures of Superman.  In 2005 her Desperate Housewives work won her the Golden Globe Award for Best Actress and the Screen Actor's Guild Award for Outstanding Performance by a Female Actress in a Comedy Series...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rgdIWxYCCe1wK1ycdKiPhMBI9Fs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10742"}}, {tmdbId:"80622", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA ", imdbId:"0235336", born:date('1957-04-12'), name:"Suzzanne Douglas", bio:"Suzzanne Douglas is an American film, television and stage actress, singer, composer, dancer, and producer, best known for her role as matriarch Jerri Peterson in the television sitcom \"The Parent 'Hood\".  She holds an MFA in Music from the Manhattan School of Music, New York...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ldfCErLjjST3HBZSK8G4KBMDZhR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80622"}}, {tmdbId:"80623", properties:{bornIn:"Newark, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0323174", born:date('1973-11-19'), name:"Savion Glover", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSavion Glover (born November 19, 1973) is an American tap dancer, actor, and choreographer.  He was nominated for Best Actor for this musical as well.  As a learning prodigy, he was taught by notable dancers from previous generations.  Glover is currently interested in restoring African roots to tap.  He wants to put tap back into the contemporary black context...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aFHZ4jGO2ITjR4KmsMUfjfXeJbs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80623"}}, {tmdbId:"108209", properties:{imdbId:"0233956", born:date('1983-01-01'), name:"Sarah Rowland Doroff", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/g6WsSKpB8FhaiCeaY9GmN5e2aom.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/108209"}}, {tmdbId:"99039", properties:{imdbId:"0269793", name:"Ron Fazio", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/99039"}}, {tmdbId:"103861", properties:{imdbId:"0022658", name:"John Altamura", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/103861"}}, {tmdbId:"1073042", properties:{imdbId:"0499294", name:"Phoebe Legere", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/t2tNyDueA9Te2n4DorUlgfiXQOl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1073042"}}, {tmdbId:"98330", properties:{imdbId:"0172635", name:"Rick Collins", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/98330"}}, {tmdbId:"27862", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA ", imdbId:"0343444", born:date('1953-03-25'), name:"Mary Gross", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nMary Gross (born March 25, 1953) is an American comedian and actress, perhaps best known for her four-year stint on Saturday Night Live from 1981 to 1985.  Her credits also include minor roles on Animaniacs, Boston Legal and Sabrina, the Teenage Witch.  Gross's trademark is her soft, treacly voice. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Mary Gross, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9s20j6Hg9WTnKH8dbjqgLUgwR9W.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27862"}}] AS row
