UNWIND [{tmdbId:"8985", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn - New York - USA", imdbId:"0171513", born:date('1958-05-26'), name:"Margaret Colin", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMargaret Colin (born May 26, 1958) is an American actress.  She is known for her role as Margo Montgomery Hughes # 1 on As the World Turns and for her role as Eleanor Waldorf-Rose on Gossip Girl...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tsg9bGtD1mY1FLKIeIFUNeD5jpm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8985"}}, {tmdbId:"56120", properties:{bornIn:" Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0645785", born:date('1959-04-20'), name:"Yuji Okumoto", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eACYrrdj8kZnYMCpUTghbpJ9nVk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56120"}}, {tmdbId:"5999", properties:{bornIn:"Helsinki, Finland", imdbId:"0653669", born:date('1961-08-17'), name:"Kati Outinen", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAnna Katriina Outinen (born August 17, 1961), is a Finnish actress who has often played leading female roles in Aki Kaurismäki's films. \n\nOutinen was born in Helsinki.  Having studied under Jouko Turkka during his \"reign\" of drama studies in Finland, she nevertheless has never been associated with the \"turkkalaisuus\" school of acting methodology...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mi78e4O4hQBQygxVVtwXdV2xqiu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5999"}}, {tmdbId:"53507", properties:{bornIn:"Sipoo, Finland", imdbId:"0758825", born:date('1936-03-09'), name:"Elina Salo", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nElina Salo (born 9 March 1936 in Sipoo, Finland) is a Finnish film, theatre and television actress who has also done work in radio as a voice actor in children’s programming.  In her career that began in 1956, Salo has appeared in over 50 films and television shows but she is best known for her work in Aki Kaurismäki’s films.  She has been awarded three Jussi Awards for her work.  In 2010, she was awarded the Ordre des Arts et des Lettres (Commandeur)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8xl7jABTROPb9hsrW6KsQ2xLGxu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53507"}}, {tmdbId:"53508", properties:{bornIn:"Lapua, Finland", imdbId:"0631741", born:date('1938-11-23'), name:"Esko Nikkari", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEsko Nikkari (23 November 1938 Lapua, Finland – 17 December 2006 in Seinäjoki, Finland) was a prolific Finnish actor who made more than 70 appearances on film and television.  He debuted in 1974 in the movie Karvat. \n\nNikkari was a workhorse of the Kaurismäki brothers, with whom he first worked on Rikos ja rangaistus in 1983.  His last role with Aki Kaurismäki was in Man without a Past in 2002...", died:date('2006-12-17'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mNiyD3BOzWba4CB0VTbIqA4EAVm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53508"}}, {tmdbId:"71041", properties:{bornIn:"Lynwood, California, USA", imdbId:"0946148", born:date('1959-10-23'), name:"'Weird Al' Yankovic", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAlfred Matthew \"Weird Al\" Yankovic (born October 23, 1959) is an American singer-songwriter, music producer, actor, comedian, writer, satirist, and parodist.  Yankovic is known for his humorous songs that make light of popular culture and that often parody specific songs by contemporary musical acts...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1MjdjnXHokywKz6LZ1b26O5FklA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71041"}}, {tmdbId:"30366", properties:{bornIn:"Miami, Florida, USA", imdbId:"0414130", born:date('1959-08-02'), name:"Victoria Jackson", bio:"Victoria Jackson (born August 2, 1959) is an American comedian, actress, and singer best known as a cast member of the NBC television sketch comedy series Saturday Night Live (SNL) from 1986 to 1992. \n\nStarting in 2008, she has appeared on various television shows.  She has received attention as a vocal critic of President Barack Obama, an active participant in the Tea Party movement, and a vocal proponent of Barack Obama citizenship conspiracy theories...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30366"}}, {tmdbId:"50807", properties:{bornIn:"Culver City, Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0724245", born:date('1949-07-24'), name:"Michael Richards", bio:"Michael Anthony Richards (born July 24, 1949) is an American actor, comedian, writer and television producer, best known for his portrayal of the eccentric Cosmo Kramer on the television sitcom Seinfeld. \n\nRichards began his career as a stand up comedian, first stepping into a national spotlight when he was featured on Billy Crystal's first cable TV special.  He went on to become a series regular on ABC's Fridays...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bAYwmBdPJAiFkossWq56pEDmUh4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/50807"}}, {tmdbId:"26495", properties:{bornIn:"Worcester, Massachusetts, United States", imdbId:"0446465", born:date('1972-03-09'), name:"Jean Louisa Kelly", bio:"Jean Louisa Kelly (born March 9, 1972) is an American actress and singer.  She is perhaps best known for her long-running role as Kim Warner on the television sitcom Yes, Dear. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jean Louisa Kelly, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia ...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hUaXI2x27HNIKc4WXcnvNkl4wF9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/26495"}}, {tmdbId:"11510", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000346", born:date('1980-08-26'), name:"Macaulay Culkin", bio:"Macaulay Carson Culkin (born August 26, 1980) is an American actor, musician, and web host.  He is known for playing Kevin McCallister in the Christmas films Home Alone (1990), which he was nominated for a Golden Globe Award for Best Actor – Motion Picture Musical or Comedy for, and Home Alone 2: Lost in New York (1992)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hVagDqi5o8lZ21b1kXAl45Sj9wt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11510"}}, {tmdbId:"55267", properties:{bornIn:"Omaha, Nebraska, USA", imdbId:"0435218", born:date('1939-08-01'), name:"Terry Kiser", bio:"Terry Kiser (born August 1, 1939) is an American actor, best known for his portrayal of the dead title-character in the comedy Weekend at Bernie's, and its sequel, Weekend at Bernie's II. \n\nTerry was a regular on two soap operas, The Secret Storm on CBS and The Doctors on NBC.  Kiser has guest-starred numerous times on episodic television, particularly sitcoms, though he made a notable appearance as a comedian Vic Hitler (aka, Vic the Narcoleptic Comic) on the drama Hill Street Blues...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mlbKBknv4TndoeeEtPXhAtRJpAh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55267"}}, {tmdbId:"169141", properties:{imdbId:"0392725", name:"Maria Holvoe", bio:"Maria Holvoe is an actress, known for Willow (1988), Worth Winning (1989) and The Equalizer (1985)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yonrAZYnEC0qPHl9hTwCBSVcfY0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/169141"}}, {tmdbId:"1533", properties:{bornIn:"Gaffney, South Carolina, USA", imdbId:"0000510", born:date('1958-04-21'), name:"Andie MacDowell", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRosalie Anderson \"Andie\" MacDowell (born April 21, 1958) is an American model and actress.  She has received the Golden Camera and an Honorary César. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Andie MacDowell, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xq68QEPBJVu6kwDa4sEQ1HvSlMK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1533"}}, {tmdbId:"1212", properties:{bornIn:"Hoboken, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0000624", born:date('1962-11-14'), name:"Laura San Giacomo", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLaura San Giacomo (born November 14, 1962) is an American actress known for playing the role of Maya Gallo on the NBC sitcom Just Shoot Me! and Kit De Luca in the film Pretty Woman, as well as other work on television and in films.  She most recently played the role of Holly Hunter's childhood best friend on the TNT crime drama series Saving Grace...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xOPY9e0HN6zYmI5HrmRSbwygEzy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1212"}}, {tmdbId:"57906", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn - New York - USA", imdbId:"0001048", born:date('1957-09-29'), name:"Andrew Dice Clay", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nAndrew Dice Clay (born Andrew Clay Silverstein; September 29, 1957) is an American comedian and actor.  Clay is known for a style of comedy that has sparked controversy and much media coverage.  He is loved by some and reviled by others, who feel that his act is crude, misogynistic, racist, homophobic and degrading...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9w5uxW2A8nWSqnP81vgVBbTszzy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57906"}}, {tmdbId:"10681", properties:{bornIn:"Roanoke, Virginia, USA", imdbId:"0628611", born:date('1942-04-03'), name:"Wayne Newton", bio:"Wayne Newton is a singer and stage performer from the 1960s to the present.  He is of English, Irish, Scottish, Welsh and German as well as Native American (specifically Powhatan and Cherokee) ancestry.  In the 1960s, he was a very popular singer with a very clean cut youthful appearance, with hits like \"Danke Schon\"...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/v888Enog3fIBHXO5jYSS09BvJIj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10681"}}, {tmdbId:"38570", properties:{bornIn:"Dayton, Ohio", imdbId:"0420898", born:date('1940-08-28'), name:"Ken Jenkins", bio:"Ken Jenkins (born August 28, 1940) is an American actor, best known for his role as Dr.  Bob Kelso, the curmudgeonly Chief of Medicine on the American comedy Scrubs. \n\nIn 1969, he co-founded the Actors Theatre of Louisville and served as the Associate Artistic Director for three years.  This institution has produced playwrights such as Beth Henley and Marsha Norman...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/basRrWk50y03ydjm0DW8A6AxH1o.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/38570"}}, {tmdbId:"35515", properties:{bornIn:"Vandalia - Illinois - USA", imdbId:"0820053", born:date('1929-11-06'), name:"June Squibb", bio:"Squibb began working in musical theatre at the St.  Louis Muny and trained at the Cleveland Play House, and at the HB Studio.  While at the Cleveland Play House, she performed in productions of Marseilles, The Play's the Thing, Goodbye, My Fancy, The Heiress, Detective Story, Antigone, Ladies in Retirement and Bloomer Girl.  In 1958, she played Dulcie in The Boyfriend Off-Broadway.  In 1959, she starred in an Off-Broadway revival of Lend an Ear with Elizabeth Allen...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jF7A6NMWZQyIgTdyoZbayIqal60.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/35515"}}, {tmdbId:"239348", properties:{bornIn:"La Rochelle, France", imdbId:"0154299", born:date('1961-01-01'), name:"Emmanuelle Chaulet", bio:"Emmanuelle Chaulet is a French actress.  She starred in Eric Rohmer's 1987 comedy Boyfriends and Girlfriends and Jon Jost's 1990 film All the Vermeers in New York. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Emmanuelle Chaulet, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/d83KFpDnmEGMN6EVyk55KDFJidJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/239348"}}, {tmdbId:"1904840", properties:{name:"Katherine Bean", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1904840"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
