UNWIND [{tmdbId:"57119", properties:{bornIn:"Benton Harbor, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0005435", born:date('1956-11-10'), name:"Sinbad", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDavid Adkins  (born November 10, 1956), better known by his professional name of Sinbad, is an American stand-up comedian and actor.  He became well known in the 1990s from being featured on his own HBO specials, appearing on several television series, and starring in the films Houseguest, First Kid and Jingle All the Way...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/u5DxTDoOarNPiSSE47LiMYXhk3H.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57119"}}, {tmdbId:"14104", properties:{bornIn:"Brantford, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0367005", born:date('1948-09-24'), name:"Phil Hartman", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPhilip Edward \"Phil\" Hartman  (September 24, 1948 – May 28, 1998) was a Canadian-born American actor, comedian, screenwriter, and graphic artist.  Born in Brantford, Ontario, Hartman and his family immigrated to the United States when he was ten.  After graduating from California State University, Northridge with a degree in graphic arts, he designed album covers for bands like Poco and America...", died:date('1998-05-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6LLX6bfWMD1MDN4DV2di8nzFZil.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14104"}}, {tmdbId:"42059", properties:{bornIn:"Olympia, Washington, USA", imdbId:"0614448", born:date('1974-02-08'), name:"Kim Murphy", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1i4ne7aFw00iklRFIej2wgk7hLa.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/42059"}}, {tmdbId:"146044", properties:{bornIn:"Tianjin, China", imdbId:"0069994", born:date('1935-01-01'), name:"Ben Niu", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4OotJ4kv3BbLHfdBl5qRHyD25U3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/146044"}}, {tmdbId:"79088", properties:{imdbId:"0942925", name:"Whittni Wright", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8BN51oulcgW79gK5U80FKaIXzRf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/79088"}}, {tmdbId:"43120", properties:{bornIn:"Charleston, South Carolina, U.S", imdbId:"0004873", born:date('1965-12-21'), name:"Andy Dick", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Andrew Ryan \"Andy\" Dick (born December 21, 1965) is an American comedian, actor, musician and television/film producer.  Dick became well known for his sensationalistic and controversial behavior related to drug and alcohol abuse.  His first regular television role was on the short-lived but highly influential Ben Stiller Show.  In the mid-1990s, he had a long-running stint on NBC's NewsRadio...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ecXKtxy3tVTndFySQQUv0P03oj0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/43120"}}, {tmdbId:"114674", properties:{bornIn:"New York City - New York - USA", imdbId:"0877270", born:date('1947-01-31'), name:"Glynn Turman", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGlynn Russell Turman (born January 31, 1946) is an American stage, television, and film actor as well as a writer, director, and producer.  He is perhaps best known for his roles as high school student Leroy \"Preach\" Jackson in the 1975 coming-of-age film Cooley High, math professor and retired Army colonel Bradford Taylor on the NBC sitcom A Different World, and fictional Baltimore mayor Clarence Royce on the HBO drama series The Wire...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yTVUsD09sfrwu010jmtTLIPZ1uT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/114674"}}, {tmdbId:"1407747", properties:{imdbId:"0566114", name:"Virginia McCollam", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1407747"}}, {tmdbId:"17859", properties:{bornIn:"New Orleans, Louisiana, USA", imdbId:"0682495", born:date('1963-12-08'), name:"Wendell Pierce", bio:"Wendell Pierce (born December 8, 1962) is an American actor, best known for his portrayal of Detective Bunk Moreland on the HBO drama The Wire. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Wendell Pierce, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uOsldo9Pkl0E79UbIXX5tZZmC8F.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/17859"}}, {tmdbId:"21290", properties:{bornIn:"Toronto, Ontario,  Canada", imdbId:"0004929", born:date('1963-01-04'), name:"Dave Foley", bio:"Dave Foley (born January 4, 1963) is a Canadian comedian, writer, director, and producer best known for his work in The Kids in the Hall, NewsRadio, A Bug's Life, and Celebrity Poker Showdown...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yDmTBUOsyeahPebx32YKWyDi2Os.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21290"}}, {tmdbId:"7867", properties:{imdbId:"0734236", born:date('1949-08-24'), name:"Charles Rocket", died:date('2005-10-07'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7867"}}, {tmdbId:"3138", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0004980", born:date('1960-11-04'), name:"Kathy Griffin", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nKathleen Mary \"Kathy\" Griffin (born November 4, 1960) is an American actress, model, stand-up comedian, television personality, New York Times best-selling author and an LGBT rights advocate.  Griffin first gained recognition for appearances on two episodes of Seinfeld, and then for her supporting role on the NBC sitcom Suddenly Susan...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/psg895Ye46vGenRdX0EXvGOm92p.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3138"}}, {tmdbId:"95899", properties:{bornIn:"Leningrad, Russian SFSR, Soviet Union", imdbId:"0326751", born:date('1966-10-09'), name:"Yekaterina Golubeva", bio:"Yekaterina Golubeva (also known as Katya Golubyova) was a Russian actress, best known for her role in the 1999 French film, Pola X. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Yekaterina Golubeva, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2011-08-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sdFIDlOkge67bR8l4F0NVuXh4dD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95899"}}, {tmdbId:"240050", properties:{imdbId:"0183675", name:"Richard Courcet", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/240050"}}, {tmdbId:"1546002", properties:{name:"Vincent Dupont", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1546002"}}, {tmdbId:"20772", properties:{bornIn:"Saint-Mandé, Val-de-Marne, France", imdbId:"0344932", born:date('1961-06-18'), name:"Laurent Grévill", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20772"}}, {tmdbId:"9575", properties:{bornIn:"Baltimore, Maryland, USA", imdbId:"0000586", born:date('1971-09-18'), name:"Jada Pinkett Smith", bio:"Jada Koren Pinkett Smith is an American actress, singer-songwriter, and businesswoman.  She began her career in 1990, when she made a guest appearance in the short-lived sitcom True Colors.  She starred in A Different World, produced by Bill Cosby, and she featured opposite Eddie Murphy in The Nutty Professor (1996).  She starred in dramatic films such as Menace II Society (1993) and Set It Off (1996)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vt1Z1Fsu7gjp4L0OHey9Aa79lWj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9575"}}, {tmdbId:"71913", properties:{bornIn:"Harlem, New York, USA", imdbId:"0940158", born:date('1973-04-13'), name:"Bokeem Woodbine", bio:"Bokeem Woodbine (born April 13, 1973) is an American film and television actor...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pnPyA5pJn94zUzuLWTNkGBNZxza.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71913"}}, {tmdbId:"62817", properties:{bornIn:"East Orange, Newark, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0188025", born:date('1970-12-02'), name:"Anthony 'Treach' Criss", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAnthony Criss (born December 2, 1970), better known by his stage name Treach, is an American rapper and actor.  He is best known as the lead rapper of the hip hop group Naughty by Nature. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Treach, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iRMfIuyuJqmOwXfJZjuIuNVXmDo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/62817"}}, {tmdbId:"77761", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York,", imdbId:"0107322", born:date('1961-12-01'), name:"John G. Brennan", bio:"John Gerard Brennan \"Johnny\" Brennan (born December 1, 1961 in New York City, New York, U. S. ) is an American actor, film writer, and voice actor.  He is a member of the Jerky Boys; a prank call duo with Kamal Ahmed from 1989 to 2001, and restarted by Brennan in 2006...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77761"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"83480", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, NY", imdbId:"0436379", born:date('1966-05-07'), name:"Kamal Ahmed", bio:"Kamal Ahmed (born May 7, 1966), usually called Kamal, is an Bangladeshi American comedian and former member of the Jerky Boys prank phone calling group.  He has acted in and directed several films, including Rapturious, completed in 2006...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83480"}}, {tmdbId:"82396", properties:{imdbId:"0620429", born:date('1973-01-18'), name:"Shinobu Nakayama", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Shinobu Nakayama (Nakayama Shinobu , born January 18, 1973) is an actress and a former J-pop singer.  She was born in Tokyo, Japan, and released her first single on 2 November 1988.  Her final release as a J-pop artist was on 1 March 1991.  She was a member of the short-lived idol groups Nanatsuboshi and Rakutenshi.  She is the younger sister of actress Miho Nakayama...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dCm2REQb3TJglF2aZMyVwfBJWdd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82396"}}, {tmdbId:"239961", properties:{bornIn:"Canada", imdbId:"0159435", born:date('1958-08-24'), name:"Billy Chow", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nBilly Chow (born Chow Bei-lei August 24, 1958 in Canada), (also credited as Billy Chau and Billy Chow Bei-lei) is an Chinese Canadian actor, martial artist and the former world kickboxing champion.  Chow is perhaps best known for his role as General Fujita in 1994 film Fist of Legend and Wong, Great Kick of the North in 1996 film Tai Chi Boxer...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7V4SpRxyAxw7PP8zR1ONpddDlSS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/239961"}}, {tmdbId:"17286", properties:{bornIn:"Hamilton, Bermuda", imdbId:"0372176", born:date('1973-10-03'), name:"Lena Headey", bio:"Lena Headey (born 3 October, 1973) is a Bermuda-born  English actress, screenwriter and director best known for portraying Queen Cersei Lannister in HBO's hit fantasy series Game of Thrones since 2011.  She is also known for playing Sarah Connor on Fox's Terminator: The Sarah Connor Chronicles, as well as appearing in such films as The Remains of the Day, Possession, Imagine Me and You, The Brothers Grimm, The Broken, 300 and The Red Baron...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xR2IBnBlUdyBe5hecaVdtRuQqUE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/17286"}}, {tmdbId:"14631", properties:{bornIn:"Worms, Germany", imdbId:"0252091", born:date('1967-10-28'), name:"André Eisermann", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7yg9uAvBPhUWYpsCqJ4L6HUIb4a.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14631"}}, {tmdbId:"73172", properties:{bornIn:"Dorney, Buckinghamshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0167403", born:date('1941-03-22'), name:"Jeremy Clyde", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lYnebcsfw1UCBXqeah2WCwFPji3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/73172"}}, {tmdbId:"7043", properties:{imdbId:"0713327", name:"Martin Raymond", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7043"}}, {tmdbId:"7044", properties:{imdbId:"0150073", name:"Eric Pascal Chaltiel", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7044"}}, {tmdbId:"110077", properties:{bornIn:"Liverpool, England", imdbId:"0734156", born:date('1958-09-23'), name:"Crissy Rock", bio:"Award winning actress, stand-up comedian, author and reality TV star from Liverpool.  Rock shot to fame in 1994 with the lead role in Ken Loach's Ladybird Ladybird, winning the Silver Bear for Best Actress award at the 44th Berlin International Film Festival.  Best actor that year was Tom Hanks for Philadelphia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zAgdji0ZNaokLJdHHbGJ8y2kAmS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/110077"}}, {tmdbId:"195410", properties:{bornIn:"Molina, Cile", imdbId:"0891927", name:"Vladimir Vega", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/195410"}}, {tmdbId:"1168012", properties:{imdbId:"0491843", name:"Sandie Lavelle", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1168012"}}, {tmdbId:"1168013", properties:{imdbId:"0893004", name:"Mauricio Venegas", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1168013"}}, {tmdbId:"25819", properties:{bornIn:"Ascoli Satriano, Puglia, Italy", imdbId:"0686375", born:date('1946-05-19'), name:"Michele Placido", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vXDSKdLcTcXFebUEgR61djSzXBQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25819"}}, {tmdbId:"1149435", properties:{imdbId:"0587549", born:date('1939-01-05'), name:"Piro Milkani", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1149435"}}, {tmdbId:"1180060", properties:{bornIn:"Ragusa, Italia", imdbId:"0224076", born:date('1918-09-13'), name:"Carmelo Di Mazzarelli", died:date('2010-06-13'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1180060"}}, {tmdbId:"1002069", properties:{imdbId:"0101717", name:"Brittany Boyd", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1002069"}}, {tmdbId:"236056", properties:{imdbId:"0713552", name:"Michael Raysses", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/236056"}}, {tmdbId:"1376870", properties:{imdbId:"0679885", name:"Zack Phifer", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1376870"}}, {tmdbId:"53283", properties:{bornIn:"Bethlehem, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0001795", born:date('1981-09-08'), name:"Jonathan Taylor Thomas", bio:"Jonathan Taylor Thomas is an American actor, voice actor, former child star, and teen idol. \n\nHe is well known for his role of middle child Randy Taylor on the sitcom Home Improvement, as Tom Sawyer in the Disney film Tom and Huck, and as the voice of the young Simba in Disney's The Lion King...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/E4cAiS5ge08euPEXrGLKhQX7cj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53283"}}, {tmdbId:"12077", properties:{bornIn:"Youngstown, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0191906", born:date('1952-11-03'), name:"Jim Cummings", bio:"Jim Cummings (born November 3, 1952) is an American voice actor who has appeared in almost 100 roles...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/c0sQPRCM5Ri3F4gVyxPr4AcPmIq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12077"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"155492", properties:{imdbId:"0189524", born:date('1960-08-25'), name:"Ashley Crow", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/155492"}}, {tmdbId:"112080", properties:{bornIn:"Glendale, California, USA", imdbId:"0907323", born:date('1982-01-25'), name:"Shawna Waldron", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nShawna Langill Waldron (born January 25, 1982) is an American actress.  Little Giants is considered her first feature film debut (the film The New Kid, in which she also acted, has never been released).  After starring in Little Giants, Waldron went on to play Michael Douglas' daughter in the movie The American President.  Waldron's first television role was in the pilot for CBS's Morning Glory.  She then guest-starred on the series Malony...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/quG2h6qGGZToR4Qx2s2C4CrEljC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/112080"}}, {tmdbId:"50398", properties:{bornIn:"Vancouver - British Columbia - Canada", imdbId:"0001701", born:date('1978-09-07'), name:"Devon Sawa", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDevon Edward Sawa (born September 7, 1978 height 6' (1,83 m)) is a Canadian actor. \n\nLife and career\n\nSawa was born in Vancouver, British Columbia, the son of Edward and Joyce Sawa.  Sawa has two siblings.  His father is Polish, and his mother is \"a little bit of everything\".  His love of acting began when he starred in a school play in kindergarten, and since then, he has had many roles on TV and in movies...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iWJLjN29XjFFVON1Jjeq7W7Mp9G.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/50398"}}, {tmdbId:"67378", properties:{bornIn:" Dallas, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0853779", born:date('1988-08-19'), name:"Travis Tedford", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67378"}}, {tmdbId:"67379", properties:{imdbId:"0940673", name:"Kevin Jamal Woods", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67379"}}, {tmdbId:"67380", properties:{imdbId:"0912296", born:date('1986-11-21'), name:"Jordan Warkol", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67380"}}, {tmdbId:"67381", properties:{bornIn:"Plano, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0531118", born:date('1990-01-19'), name:"Zachary Mabry", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67381"}}, {tmdbId:"17187", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000746", born:date('1967-01-10'), name:"Trini Alvarado", bio:"Trinidad \"Trini\" Alvarado  (born January 10, 1967) is an American actress best known for her performances as Margaret \"Meg\" March in the 1994 film adaptation of Louisa May Alcott's novel Little Women and Lucy Lynskey in the comedy/horror film The Frighteners.  She also has notable stage performances to her credit and considerable singing talent.  Her latest appearance was on the Fox show Fringe...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mBXnTuUlllTWiGbJfbkw63WxV2U.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/17187"}}, {tmdbId:"95023", properties:{bornIn:"Dorset, England, UK", imdbId:"0586958", born:date('1973-02-25'), name:"Oliver Milburn", bio:"Oliver Milburn is an English actor...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95023"}}, {tmdbId:"33395", properties:{bornIn:"Dublin, Ireland ", imdbId:"0597047", born:date('1946-01-01'), name:"Dearbhla Molloy", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33395"}}, {tmdbId:"1667", properties:{bornIn:"Bradford, West Yorkshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0192279", born:date('1969-05-29'), name:"Danny Cunningham", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1667"}}, {tmdbId:"2462", properties:{bornIn:"Alton, Hampshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0001517", born:date('1972-04-03'), name:"Catherine McCormack", bio:"Catherine McCormack (born 1 January 1972) is an English actress, known for her stage acting as well as her screen performances in films such as Braveheart, Spy Game and Dangerous Beauty. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Catherine McCormack, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vYyMCGKeIUTZMdEgVwQCgX7q1T3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2462"}}, {tmdbId:"52865", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0788009", born:date('1949-11-29'), name:"Garry Shandling", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGarry Emmanuel Shandling (born November 29, 1949) was an American stand-up comedian, actor, director, writer, and producer.  He was best known for his work in It's Garry Shandling's Show and The Larry Sanders Show. \n\nShandling began his career writing for sitcoms such as Sanford and Son and Welcome Back, Kotter.  He made a successful stand-up performance on The Tonight Show with Johnny Carson and became a frequent guest-host on the show...", died:date('2016-03-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/d8fSX4f5GtX7hwJWWEvgC50Jgrb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/52865"}}, {tmdbId:"6575", properties:{bornIn:"Vancouver, British Columbia, Canada", imdbId:"0004743", born:date('1967-06-28'), name:"Gil Bellows", bio:"Gil Bellows (born June 28, 1967) is a Canadian film and television actor.  He is best known for the roles of Tommy Williams in The Shawshank Redemption, Billy Thomas in the television series Ally McBeal and as CIA agent Matt Callan in the television series The Agency...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eCOIv2nSGnWTHdn88NoMyNOKWyR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6575"}}, {tmdbId:"9137", properties:{bornIn:"Katy, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0000250", born:date('1969-04-25'), name:"Renée Zellweger", bio:"Renée Kathleen Zellweger (born April 25, 1969) is an American actress and producer.  Zellweger first gained widespread attention for her role in the film Jerry Maguire (1996) in which she played the romantic interest of Tom Cruise's character.  Zellweger later won acclaim in One True Thing (1998) opposite William Hurt and Meryl Streep, and in Neil LaBute's Nurse Betty opposite Morgan Freeman.  The role garnered the actress her first of three Golden Globe Awards...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6aSRq8LBE7FULueg9K5JEA3GLTy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9137"}}, {tmdbId:"51792", properties:{bornIn:"Syracuse, New York, USA", imdbId:"0168262", born:date('1972-02-28'), name:"Rory Cochrane", bio:"Rory Cochrane (born February 28, 1972) is an American actor.   He is known for playing Ron Slater in Dazed and Confused, Lucas in Empire Records, and Tim Speedle in CSI: Miami...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pKcfuI1Tg0nQ4xoQ0DA2r65oT4K.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/51792"}}, {tmdbId:"53918", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago - Illinois - USA", imdbId:"0724757", born:date('1967-11-23'), name:"Salli Richardson-Whitfield", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSalli Elise Richardson-Whitfield (born November 23, 1967, height 5' 4\" (1,63 m)) is an American television and film actress.  She is known for her role as Dr.  Allison Blake on the sci-fi TV series Eureka and her voice acting as Elisa Maza on the Disney animated series Gargoyles. \n\nEarly life\n\nRichardson-Whitfield was born in Chicago, Illinois, the daughter of an African American mother and an Irish-Italian father...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wMQaIzY5kyRQd8UwF1lphKK6oQm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53918"}}, {tmdbId:"59031", properties:{bornIn:"Alger, Algérie", imdbId:"0099828", born:date('1959-01-23'), name:"Didier Bourdon", bio:"Didier Bourdon (born 23 January 1959) is a French Algerian-born actor, screenwriter and film director. \n\nHe first reached stardom in France when he created the comedic trio Les Inconnus with Bernard Campan and Pascal Légitimus, which was very popular throughout the 1990s. \n\nSource: Article \"Didier Bourdon\" from Wikipedia in english, licensed under CC-BY-SA 3. 0...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1aG9v7B8fmmACeee9BcjGRII3fk.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/59031"}}, {tmdbId:"38541", properties:{bornIn:"Stuttgart, Baden-Württemberg, Germany", imdbId:"0944255", born:date('1967-09-07'), name:"Natalia Wörner", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dgfNjturfC8seIKCpWsmMVtpOlu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/38541"}}, {tmdbId:"67786", properties:{imdbId:"0086379", name:"Joseph Blaire", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fAPcoC4KPPmH7T6f4SJ0LWWpz1b.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67786"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"11803", properties:{bornIn:"Montclair, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0338886", born:date('1965-10-08'), name:"Peter Greene", bio:"Peter Greene (born Peter Green; October 8, 1965) is an American character actor. \n\nA native of Montclair, New Jersey, Greene did not pursue a career in acting until his mid 20s.  He initially landed several roles in cinema and television in the early 1990s. \n\nGreene's breakthrough came in 1994-1995 with a roles in Pulp Fiction, The Mask, Clean, Shaven, and The Usual Suspects.  Greene is possibly best remembered for his role in Pulp Fiction, as Zed who rapes Marsellus Wallace...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/n49XdJsMwNRdc4qT9XVAGb3fIQW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11803"}}, {tmdbId:"1631713", properties:{name:"Maya Lin", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1631713"}}, {tmdbId:"14592", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0000703", born:date('1960-10-24'), name:"BD Wong", bio:"BD Wong (born October 24, 1960) is an American actor, best-known for his roles on Law & Order: Special Victims Unit, Oz, and for his starring role in the Broadway production of M.  Butterfly...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/w7Hs9m6ocS2qlibvrLOvmyCKbAN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14592"}}, {tmdbId:"56486", properties:{imdbId:"0141824", born:date('1981-11-24'), name:"Michael Patrick Carter", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56486"}}, {tmdbId:"66838", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0859740", born:date('1966-06-24'), name:"Florence Thomassin", bio:"Florence Thomassin (born 24 June 1966) is a French actress and sculptor.  In 2001, Thomassin was nominated for a César Award for Best Supporting Actress for her role of Beatrice in Bernard Rapp's A Question of Taste (\"Une affaire de goût\"). \n\nSource: Article \"Florence Thomassin\" from Wikipedia in english, licensed under CC-BY-SA 3. 0...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/olgTml2VB0uEdmp4cbyc0obGKfX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/66838"}}, {tmdbId:"49946", properties:{bornIn:"Lausanne, Switzerland", imdbId:"0959897", born:date('1959-07-08'), name:"Jean-Philippe Écoffey", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/49946"}}, {tmdbId:"3053", properties:{bornIn:"Newcastle, New South Wales, Australia", imdbId:"0498275", born:date('1968-08-07'), name:"Sophie Lee", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSophie Lee (born 7 August 1968 in Newcastle, New South Wales) is an Australian film, stage and television actress and author...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3053"}}, {tmdbId:"3054", properties:{imdbId:"0358774", name:"Roz Hammond", bio:"Rosalind Hammond, often credited as Ros or Roz, is an Australian comic actress and writer...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/n6WgYNWc0E1Nnh5RSw8E4ncCFov.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3054"}}, {tmdbId:"3051", properties:{bornIn:"Sydney, New South Wales, Australia", imdbId:"0001057", born:date('1972-11-01'), name:"Toni Collette", bio:"An Australian actress and musician, known for her acting work on stage, television and film as well as a secondary career as the lead singer of the band Toni Collette & the Finish. \n\nCollette's acting career began in the early 1990s with comedic roles in films such as Spotswood (1992) and Muriel's Wedding (1994), for which she was nominated for a Golden Globe Award for Best Actress...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6QllXhefzi294BcqrV8RUR4xhsy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3051"}}, {tmdbId:"3057", properties:{imdbId:"0418917", name:"Belinda Jarrett", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3057"}}, {tmdbId:"545828", properties:{bornIn:"Moscow, Russia", imdbId:"0958461", born:date('1965-09-03'), name:"Marina Zudina", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/56g1gES3rohL7L8vIgkhbt6Nh0D.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/545828"}}, {tmdbId:"102754", properties:{bornIn:"Wimbledon, London, England", imdbId:"0728004", born:date('1966-06-28'), name:"Fay Ripley", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/m4LMoCAOj0llge24ffCAaQzZALn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/102754"}}, {tmdbId:"88519", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0724084", born:date('1975-03-25'), name:"Evan Richards", bio:"Actor, filmmaker / producer.  \n\nAs an actor Evan has starred or co-starred in various film and television projects including \"Down and Out in Beverly Hills\" and the television series of \"Bill and Ted's Excellent Adventures\".  As a filmmaker, Evan's short film \"Woman X\" was shortlisted for a BAFTA award and was shown on HBO and Starz.  His other short film that he wrote and starred in \"Cloud Nine\" was a Skky Vodka Short Film Festival finalist and was seen on HBO...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88519"}}, {tmdbId:"58119", properties:{bornIn:"Eugene, Oregon, U.S.A", imdbId:"0639432", born:date('1981-05-11'), name:"Austin O'Brien", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAustin O'Brien (born May 11, 1981) is an American actor from Eugene, Oregon.  He may be best known for playing the co-lead Danny Madigan in the Arnold Schwarzenegger-movie Last Action Hero, followed by his turn into romance as Nick Zsigmond in My Girl 2, and a part in both The Lawnmower Man and its sequel.  \n\nO'Brien is the son of Valerian O'Brien and the older brother of actor Trever O'Brien...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xwi3aavC7lkWRVuihWr6tHHL7oW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/58119"}}, {tmdbId:"1337469", properties:{imdbId:"0711846", name:"Nic Ratner", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1337469"}}, {tmdbId:"27176", properties:{bornIn:" Dublin, Ireland", imdbId:"0311297", born:date('1972-05-31'), name:"Karl Geary", bio:"Karl John Geary (born May 31, 1972) is an Irish-born American actor and club owner. \n\nGeary was born in Dublin in 1972.  At the age of 15 he moved to the United States; he later obtained a green card in a visa lottery for Irish illegals, and ultimately became a naturalized citizen. \n\nGeary appeared in Madonna's Sex book.  His acting roles include Sex and the City, Hysteria – The Def Leppard Story, and Hamlet (2000).  He wrote and appeared in Coney Island Baby (2003)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ex3VfDXZPirfULVqzyTKVcKHFt2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27176"}}, {tmdbId:"163115", properties:{bornIn:"Inglewood, California, USA", imdbId:"0281234", born:date('1973-12-30'), name:"Maureen Flannigan", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/163115"}}, {tmdbId:"42738", properties:{bornIn:"Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.", imdbId:"0358972", born:date('1968-06-15'), name:"Demetra Hampton", bio:"Demetra Lisa Ann Hampton (born June 15, 1968) is an American actress and model.  She is best known for portraying the character of Valentina in the eponymous Italian television series.  Born in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, she first began her career as a model in New York City, before being chosen for the character and moving to Italy.  She went on to appear in films such as Three Columns in the News (1990), Kreola (1993), National Lampoon's Last Resort (1994) and Chicken Park (1994)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iu9dmSuOviNShtTLUfFMrjKDOz6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/42738"}}, {tmdbId:"57236", properties:{bornIn:"Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0443139", born:date('1981-01-01'), name:"Melody Kay", bio:"Melody was born in Michigan and did local theater.  She was in Life commercials and acted on and off Broadway.  Melody is married with 2 children and has one sister...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/r9pIws6ACrCGMPXIqMLAoild0P8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57236"}}, {tmdbId:"70851", properties:{bornIn:"Santa Monica, California, USA", imdbId:"0085312", born:date('1969-08-28'), name:"Jack Black", bio:"An American comedian, actor and musician.  He makes up one half of the comedy and satirical rock duo Tenacious D.  The group has two albums as well as a television series and a film.  His acting career is extensive, starring primarily as bumbling, cocky, but internally self-conscious outsiders in comedy films.  He was a member of the Frat Pack, a group of comedians who have appeared together in several Hollywood films, and has been nominated for a Golden Globe award...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rtCx0fiYxJVhzXXdwZE2XRTfIKE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70851"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"134063", properties:{imdbId:"0278092", name:"Carole Finn", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/134063"}}, {tmdbId:"448", properties:{bornIn:"Lincoln, Nebraska, USA", imdbId:"0005476", born:date('1974-07-30'), name:"Hilary Swank", bio:"Hilary Ann Swank (born July 30, 1974) is an American actress and film producer.  Swank's film career began with a small part in Buffy the Vampire Slayer (1992) and then a major part in The Next Karate Kid (1994), as Julie Pierce, the first female protégé of sensei Mr.  Miyagi.  She won the Academy Award for Best Actress twice, as Brandon Teena, a transman in Boys Don't Cry (1999) and as struggling waitress-turned-boxer, Maggie Fitzgerald, in Million Dollar Baby (2004)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rYetl0tRJrF8oQNhu00n9Ku4PNr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/448"}}, {tmdbId:"5130", properties:{bornIn:"Lubbock, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0174192", born:date('1964-08-14'), name:"Cristi Conaway", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5130"}}, {tmdbId:"15886", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0000506", born:date('1961-01-13'), name:"Julia Louis-Dreyfus", bio:"Julia Scarlett Elizabeth Louis-Dreyfus (born January 13, 1961, height 5' 3\" (1,60 m)) is an American actress and comedian, widely known for her sitcom roles in Seinfeld and The New Adventures of Old Christine. \n\nShe rose to prominence as one of the regular cast members of Saturday Night Live in the early 1980s.  She was later cast in the role of Elaine Benes on the NBC sitcom Seinfeld...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pDzlVQhjxKQBpb9NcQ3hR20kz3z.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15886"}}, {tmdbId:"9251", properties:{imdbId:"0003299", born:date('1959-10-22'), name:"Marc Shaiman", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9251"}}, {tmdbId:"1664611", properties:{imdbId:"0008412", name:"Youssef Abed-Alnour", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1664611"}}, {tmdbId:"7241", properties:{bornIn:"Bay of Islands, New Zealand", imdbId:"0654240", born:date('1962-07-22'), name:"Rena Owen", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nRena Owen is a New Zealand actress in film, theatre and television.  She is of Maori and Pakeha (European) descent.  Owen is most well known in the lead role of Beth in the cult classic movie Once Were Warriors (1994) directed by Lee Tamahori.  The role earned Owen a number of awards including Best Actress at the Montreal World Film Festival and San Diego International Film Festival...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/648ZdDBmlx6OFDFRmgAbh6q5LBo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7241"}}, {tmdbId:"7242", properties:{bornIn:"Rotorua, Île du Nord, Nouvelle-Zélande", imdbId:"0607325", born:date('1960-12-26'), name:"Temuera Morrison", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nTemuera Derek Morrison (born December 26, 1960) is a New Zealand actor.  He has become one of the country's most famous stars for his roles as the abusive Jake \"the Muss\" Heke in 1994's Once Were Warriors and as bounty hunter Jango Fett and the Clone Troopers in the Star Wars series.  He also voiced Boba Fett in the 2004 special edition of Star Wars Episode V: The Empire Strikes Back...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1ckHDFgKXJ8pazmvLCW7DeOKqA0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7242"}}, {tmdbId:"7243", properties:{imdbId:"0449828", name:"Mamaengaroa Kerr-Bell", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7243"}}, {tmdbId:"7244", properties:{imdbId:"0032810", name:"Julian Arahanga", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/g2YkF3PWSJU1vTKuURBH0DOMblm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7244"}}, {tmdbId:"12799", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0005315", born:date('1965-07-26'), name:"Jeremy Piven", bio:"Jeremy Samuel Piven (born July 26, 1965) is an American film producer and actor best known for his role as Ari Gold in the television series Entourage for which he has won three Primetime Emmy Awards as well as several other nominations for Best Supporting Actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jeremy Piven, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dPCFGmNhrF3niEJMPIbC1fiIqyI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12799"}}, {tmdbId:"27504", properties:{bornIn:"Chambersburg, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0949385", born:date('1971-04-28'), name:"Chris Young", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27504"}}, {tmdbId:"179851", properties:{bornIn:"Austin, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0397940", born:date('1981-06-20'), name:"Kanin Howell", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/179851"}}, {tmdbId:"947356", properties:{imdbId:"0456943", name:"Alexis Kirschner", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/947356"}}, {tmdbId:"951963", properties:{imdbId:"0456954", name:"Jessica Kirschner", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/951963"}}, {tmdbId:"79581", properties:{bornIn:"Detroit, Michigan", imdbId:"0377840", name:"Gloria Lynne Henry", bio:"Gloria Lynne Henry was born in Detroit.  Her acting career started very early as she has been performing on stage since the age of eight.  After receiving her B. F. A.  in theater arts at Wayne State University in Detroit, Gloria helped to create a children's' theater program at Detroit's Attic theater.  She has also traveled with the international group 'Up With People', on its European tour and performed in Equity playhouses across the United States...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oltO7ytuIwTKsoZfNq56I2p5Lyt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/79581"}}, {tmdbId:"57351", properties:{bornIn:"Helsinki, Finland", imdbId:"0310960", born:date('1917-05-16'), name:"George Gaynes", bio:"George Gaynes (1917–2016) is a Finnish-born American actor of stage, screen and television. \n\nHe may be best-known as Commandant Eric Lassard in the Police Academy film series, and to television fans as Henry Warnimont on Punky Brewster...", died:date('2016-02-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iXG1TjYQK7JHff9bqFPAxtCuo7q.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57351"}}, {tmdbId:"67792", properties:{bornIn:"San Giorgio a Cremano", imdbId:"0873385", born:date('1953-02-19'), name:"Massimo Troisi", died:date('1994-06-04'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/t3u1YkX8W5j95ZLnpREycgPu1x9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67792"}}, {tmdbId:"10777", properties:{bornIn:"Messina, Sicily, Italy", imdbId:"0002029", born:date('1968-07-27'), name:"Maria Grazia Cucinotta", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMaria Grazia Cucinotta (born 27 July 1968) is an Italian actress who has featured in films and television series since 1990.  She also worked as a film producer, screenwriter and model.  Internationally she is best known for her roles in Il Postino and as the Bond girl, credited as the Cigar Girl, in the James Bond film The World Is Not Enough...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ezxT803bVCF5nXA30OZQ6KuGydn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10777"}}, {tmdbId:"14149", properties:{bornIn:"Milan - Lombardy - Italy", imdbId:"0769237", born:date('1939-01-01'), name:"Renato Scarpa", bio:"Renato Scarpa (né en 1939 à Milan, en Lombardie) est un acteur italien...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wVWEERHioQVxnB4jFeDDZIzdSPX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14149"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"1118", properties:{bornIn:"Bunić, Croatia", imdbId:"0784884", born:date('1946-07-27'), name:"Rade Serbedzija", bio:"Rade Šerbedžija (Serbian Cyrillic: Раде Шербеџија; born July 27, 1946) is a Serbian actor, director and musician. \n\nHe was one of the most popular Yugoslav actors in the 1970s and 1980s.  He is internationally known mainly for his supporting roles in Hollywood films such as Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows: Part 1, X-Men: First Class, The Saint, Mission: Impossible II and Taken 2, and for his recurring role on 24...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eGK40yJnDCJOhtGXZrhkrkfVOwu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1118"}}, {tmdbId:"136170", properties:{bornIn:"Châtenay-Malabry, Hauts-de-Seine, France", imdbId:"0171499", born:date('1975-07-25'), name:"Grégoire Colin", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nGrégoire Colin (born July 27, 1975 in Châtenay-Malabry) is a French actor...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jtolsceVVsMT1wWi8m8pdtaUE4f.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/136170"}}, {tmdbId:"113758", properties:{bornIn:"Skopje, SR Macedonia, SFRY", imdbId:"0593865", born:date('1975-01-01'), name:"Labina Mitevska", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLabina Mitevska (Macedonian: Лабина Митевска) (born 1975 in Skopje, Socialist Republic of Macedonia, Yugoslavia) is a Macedonian actress. \n\nMitevska began her acting career aged 19 after studying in Skopje, Denmark and the University of Arizona.  She starred in Milčo Mančevski's 1994 Oscar nominated film Before the Rain...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/113758"}}, {tmdbId:"3900", properties:{bornIn:"Manchester, Greater Manchester, England, UK", imdbId:"0730070", born:date('1964-02-01'), name:"Linus Roache", bio:"Linus William Roache (born 1 February 1964) is an English actor...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/u98VM2S9mbUMCMPvCpk2OUn4Eg2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3900"}}, {tmdbId:"207", properties:{bornIn:"Leeds, West Yorkshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0929489", born:date('1948-02-05'), name:"Tom Wilkinson", bio:"Thomas Geoffrey \"Tom\" Wilkinson, OBE is an English actor.  He has twice been nominated for an Academy Award for his roles in In The Bedroom and Michael Clayton.  In 2009, he won The Golden Globe and Primetime Emmy Award for best Supporting Actor in a Miniseries or Movie for John Adams...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/d5yLk0PK8q7EKR3E3G2txO758IW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/207"}}, {tmdbId:"18023", properties:{bornIn:"Glasgow, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0001015", born:date('1961-04-14'), name:"Robert Carlyle", bio:"Robert Carlyle, OBE (born 14 April 1961) is a Scottish film and television actor.  He is known for a variety of roles including those in Trainspotting, Hamish Macbeth, The Full Monty, The World Is Not Enough, Angela's Ashes, The 51st State, and 28 Weeks Later.  He also portrayed Doctor Nicholas Rush in Stargate Universe...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dLNeFPfJACiCiUz3oEdAjeKIwvZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18023"}}, {tmdbId:"42134", properties:{bornIn:"Melbourne, Victoria, Australia", imdbId:"0400998", born:date('1952-07-29'), name:"Wendy Hughes", bio:"Wendy Hughes (29 July 1952 – 8 March 2014) was an Australian actress known for her work in theatre, film and television.  Hughes was an award-winning actress.  Her career spanned more than forty years and established her reputation as one of Australia's finest and most prolific actors.  Her biggest role was in Lonely Hearts, played in 1982 (this film was the beginning of a long collaboration with director Paul Cox)...", died:date('2014-03-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lY0ldUGzwJ9A0N47Lw1HoNtUS09.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/42134"}}, {tmdbId:"11807", properties:{imdbId:"0522503", name:"Laura Lovelace", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1MLB30laQt2k80i15kdn0X7Zn5U.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11807"}}, {tmdbId:"52602", properties:{bornIn:"New Rochelle, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001555", born:date('1962-09-21'), name:"Rob Morrow", bio:"Rob Morrow (born September 21, 1962) is an American actor.  He is known for his portrayals on Numb3rs and on Northern Exposure...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2n3lF3BFehzegyF3elvrb06S01S.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/52602"}}, {tmdbId:"84690", properties:{bornIn:"Winchester, Virginia, USA", imdbId:"0000903", born:date('1956-06-18'), name:"Brian Benben", bio:"Brian Benben (born June 18, 1956) is an American actor of stage and television...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tSOFH0cUVzGGonl9HanOiKiqTyU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/84690"}}, {tmdbId:"21197", properties:{bornIn:" Newton, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0000413", born:date('1964-09-28'), name:"Janeane Garofalo", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.  Janeane Garofalo (born September 28, 1964) is an American stand-up comedian, actress, political activist and writer.  She is the former co-host on the now defunct Air America Radio's The Majority Report.  Garofalo continues to circulate regularly within New York City's local comedy and performance art scene.  Description above from the Wikipedia article Janeane Garofalo, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/syz0cfmWODrPjpAsbh118oFhsSP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21197"}}, {tmdbId:"18324", properties:{bornIn:"Marshall, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0001872", born:date('1967-11-13'), name:"Steve Zahn", bio:"Steven James Zahn (born November 13, 1967) is an American actor and comedian.  His films include Reality Bites (1994), That Thing You Do! (1996), Out of Sight (1998), Happy, Texas (1999), Riding in Cars with Boys (2001), Shattered Glass (2003), Sahara (2005), Rescue Dawn (2007), the first three Diary of a Wimpy Kid movies, Dallas Buyers Club (2013), and War for the Planet of the Apes (2017)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/32NCu4XdTME47w9HAyRRDzB7MHd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18324"}}, {tmdbId:"76995", properties:{bornIn:"Pittsburgh, PA", imdbId:"0826198", born:date('1978-07-29'), name:"Robert J. Steinmiller Jr.", bio:"Robert J Steinmiller was born on July 29, 1978 in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, USA, and he has acted in all three venues of the acting profession: THEATRICAL, MOTION PICTURE, and TELEVISION.  He began his acting career in 1989 in a Theatrical production of Les Miserables.  He starred in several Motion Pictures in the early 1990's including Bingo (1991), Rudy (1993) and The Ref (1994).  He appeared on Television in an episode of The Untouchables, and several McDonalds commercials...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/76995"}}, {tmdbId:"10297", properties:{bornIn:"Uvalde, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0000190", born:date('1969-11-04'), name:"Matthew McConaughey", bio:"Matthew David McConaughey (born November 4, 1969) is an American actor.  After a series of minor roles in the early 1990s, McConaughey gained notice for his breakout role in Dazed and Confused (1993).  It was in this role that he first conceived the idea of his catch-phrase \"Well alright, alright. \" He then appeared in films such as A Time to Kill, Contact, U-571, Tiptoes, Sahara, and We Are Marshall...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wJiGedOCZhwMx9DezY8uwbNxmAY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10297"}}, {tmdbId:"934061", properties:{bornIn:"Monterey, California, USA", imdbId:"0413211", born:date('1959-08-09'), name:"Robert Jacks", died:date('2001-08-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ZlbVd2m7R3ox8nQ6XVnBDoJAep.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/934061"}}, {tmdbId:"975230", properties:{bornIn:"Austin, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0673304", born:date('1959-04-23'), name:"Tonie Perensky", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/l1AZvcoHFwAbqw9jlAdvJAoEBYX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/975230"}}, {tmdbId:"4003", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0002056", born:date('1953-02-21'), name:"Christine Ebersole", bio:"Christine Ebersole won the 2007 Tony Award for Best Actress in a Musical for her work in \"Grey Gardens\".  Previously, she was awarded the Drama Desk Award, the Outer Critics Circle Award, the Drama League awarded her both a citation and the Outstanding Performance of the Year, and she was named to its dais for 2007.  She also received a special citation from the New York Drama Critics' Circle and the Obie for her off-Broadway turn in \"Grey Gardens\"...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zVui49UEgcaSN8oetT39FJT6sWK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4003"}}, {tmdbId:"4787", properties:{bornIn:"Rhinebeck - New York - USA", imdbId:"0001515", born:date('1983-09-21'), name:"Joseph Mazzello", bio:"Joseph Mazzello III (born September 21, 1983) is an American actor who is best known for his roles as Tim Murphy in Jurassic Park, Eugene Sledge in the HBO miniseries The Pacific, and Dustin Moskovitz in The Social Network.  Mazzello was born in Rhinebeck, New York, and raised in Hyde Park, New York, the son of Ginnie and Joseph Mazzello, Jr. , who owned a performing arts school.  He has one older sister, Mary Mazzello, and a younger brother, John Mazzello, who have both appeared in films...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/44gsv7TlXOOKDGg5aRtqxZjM9ae.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4787"}}, {tmdbId:"56490", properties:{imdbId:"0768217", name:"Stephanie Sawyer", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56490"}}, {tmdbId:"59807", properties:{bornIn:"Montreuil-sous-Bois, Seine-Saint-Denis, Île-de-France, France", imdbId:"0001965", born:date('1973-04-05'), name:"Élodie Bouchez", bio:"Élodie Bouchez-Bangalter (born 5 April 1973) is a French actress.  She is best-known in the United States for her role as Renée Rienne on the fifth and final season of the television show Alias.  She is also well-known for playing Maïté Alvarez in the movie Wild Reeds. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Élodie Bouchez, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dGIb8TskCHotel0feCrkMd0LaYV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/59807"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"49855", properties:{bornIn:"Villefranche-sur-Saône, Rhône, France", imdbId:"0603588", born:date('1972-09-25'), name:"Gaël Morel", bio:"Gaël Morel (born September 25, 1972) is a French film director, screenwriter and actor...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8xGh0cdS2EQPbOjZGfgsCyv70BI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/49855"}}, {tmdbId:"49859", properties:{bornIn:"Agen, France", imdbId:"0725794", born:date('1976-07-25'), name:"Stéphane Rideau", bio:"Stéphane Rideau (born 25 July 1976) is a French actor born near Agen.  Although intending to pursue a career in sports, he was discovered in 1992 at a rugby game and then auditioned for a role in the film Wild Reeds by André Téchiné.  He was, at the time, sixteen years old. \n\nHe would later on play the role of a gay teenager in Come Undone by director Sébastien Lifshitz.  Rideau has a long acting experience that includes the films Loin, Le Ventre de Juliette, Le Clan, and Le Cadeau d'Élena...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/78VnBXkHRUT13JOg5NJnZmjisE9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/49859"}}, {tmdbId:"96628", properties:{imdbId:"0331202", born:date('1973-09-06'), name:"Frédéric Gorny", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96628"}}, {tmdbId:"12898", properties:{bornIn:"Denver, Colorado, USA", imdbId:"0000741", born:date('1953-06-13'), name:"Tim Allen", bio:"Tim Allen (born Timothy Allen Dick; June 13, 1953) is an American comedian, actor, voice-over artist, and entertainer, known for his role in the sitcom Home Improvement.  He is also known for his film roles in several popular movies, including the Toy Story series, The Santa Clause series, and Galaxy Quest...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6qlDjidQSKNcJFHzTXh0gQS83ub.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12898"}}, {tmdbId:"27564", properties:{bornIn:"Glendale, California, U.S.", imdbId:"0005156", born:date('1986-05-19'), name:"Eric Lloyd", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Eric Lloyd (born David Eric Lloyd Morelli;  May 19, 1986) is an American actor.  Lloyd is best known for work as a child actor between 1992 and 2003, in such roles as Charlie Calvin in The Santa Clause film trilogy,  and as \"Little John\" Warner in the NBC television series Jesse.   Description above from the Wikipedia article Eric Lloyd , licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27564"}}, {tmdbId:"144523", properties:{imdbId:"0183926", name:"Jeni Courtney", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/144523"}}, {tmdbId:"1813030", properties:{name:"Pat Slowey", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1813030"}}, {tmdbId:"199942", properties:{imdbId:"0240518", name:"Dave Duffy", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/199942"}}, {tmdbId:"1508585", properties:{imdbId:"0360426", name:"Declan Hannigan", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1508585"}}, {tmdbId:"70233", properties:{bornIn:"Hastings-on-Hudson, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001442", born:date('1968-09-21'), name:"Ricki Lake", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRicki Pamela Lake (born September 21, 1968) is an American actress and television host, best known for her starring role as Tracy Turnblad in the original Hairspray and for her talk show. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Ricki Lake, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lSMyrx9Znuy110ecuf37qDxJH2x.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/70233"}}, {tmdbId:"26457", properties:{bornIn:"Lansing - Michigan - USA", imdbId:"0000498", born:date('1970-01-24'), name:"Matthew Lillard", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMatthew Lyn Lillard (born January 24, 1970, height 6' 4\" (1,93 m)) is an American actor and producer.  He is best known for his roles as Stu Macher in Scream, Stevo in SLC Punk (awarded Best Actor at the Mar del Plata Film Festival), and Shaggy Rogers in the Scooby-Doo film series, animated movies, and one episode from Batman: The Brave and the Bold...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gXOanRx8ebM5jL9ZN9clKfFlQL0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/26457"}}, {tmdbId:"2040", properties:{bornIn:"Salford, Lancashire, England, UK", imdbId:"0001172", born:date('1964-02-16'), name:"Christopher Eccleston", bio:"An English stage, film and television actor.  His films include Let Him Have It, Shallow Grave, Elizabeth, 28 Days Later, Gone in 60 Seconds, The Others, and G. I.  Joe: The Rise of Cobra.  In 2005, he became the ninth incarnation of The Doctor in the British television series Doctor Who. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Christopher Eccleston, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/848SScSMTnjiOJRM7McbGiaEo1Q.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2040"}}, {tmdbId:"3061", properties:{bornIn:"Perth, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0000191", born:date('1971-03-31'), name:"Ewan McGregor", bio:"Ewan Gordon McGregor was born 31 March 1971 in Crieff, Scotland.  At 16, he left Crieff and Morrison Academy to join the Perth Repertory Theatre.  His parents encouraged him to leave school and pursue his acting goals rather than be unhappy.  McGregor studied drama for a year at Kirkcaldly in Fife, then enrolled at London's Guildhall School of Music and Drama for a three-year course...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aEmyadfRXTmmR7UW7OXsm5a6smS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3061"}}, {tmdbId:"25136", properties:{bornIn:"Edinburgh, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0832792", born:date('1957-10-19'), name:"Ken Stott", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nKenneth Campbell \"Ken\" Stott (born 1955) is a Scottish actor, particularly known in the United Kingdom for his many roles in television. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Ken Stott, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qmmhRvSwfoJ7TOF5L6p2VMQQz3u.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25136"}}, {tmdbId:"4029", properties:{bornIn:"Santa Monica, California, USA", imdbId:"0348409", born:date('1945-11-15'), name:"Bob Gunton", bio:"Robert Patrick \"Bob\" Gunton, Jr.  (born November 15, 1945) is an American actor.  He is known for playing strict, authoritarian characters, with his best known roles as Warden Samuel Norton in the 1994 prison film The Shawshank Redemption, Chief George Earle in 1993's Demolition Man, and President Juan Peron in the original Broadway cast of Evita. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Bob Gunton , licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rr2KDCKK4t0f5YhZibCpLCAsJxc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4029"}}, {tmdbId:"41381", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0001244", born:date('1965-06-19'), name:"Sadie Frost", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSadie Frost (born 19 June 1965) is an English actress, who currently runs fashion label Frost French and has designed the kitchens for a new development in the East End of London...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/27KovPsQ5nds49REXqmKD4wdThC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41381"}}, {tmdbId:"9642", properties:{bornIn:"Lewisham, London, England, UK", imdbId:"0000179", born:date('1972-12-29'), name:"Jude Law", bio:"An English actor, film producer and director.  He began acting with the National Youth Music Theatre in 1987, and had his first television role in 1989.  After starring in films directed by Andrew Niccol, Clint Eastwood and David Cronenberg, he was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor in 1999 for his performance in Anthony Minghella's The Talented Mr.  Ripley.  In 2000 he won a Best Supporting Actor BAFTA Award for his work in the film...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/A6Y0m7qEe04ZTHKyYDLbnyCHNzn.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9642"}}, {tmdbId:"28848", properties:{bornIn:"London - England - UK", imdbId:"0675730", born:date('1964-06-04'), name:"Sean Pertwee", bio:"​Sean Pertwee (born 4 June 1964) is an English actor well known for his film and voice over work.  He is the son of Jon Pertwee, who was best known for playing the third incarnation of The Doctor in the long-running television series Doctor Who...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/j4pAEMhKL5vA61ADrkxxLFtcI4c.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/28848"}}, {tmdbId:"30087", properties:{imdbId:"0416508", name:"Fraser James", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mGAPQG2OKTgdKFkp9YpvCSqcbgY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30087"}}, {tmdbId:"350", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0001473", born:date('1964-02-05'), name:"Laura Linney", bio:"Laura Leggett Linney (born February 5, 1964) is an American actress.  She is the recipient of several awards, including two Golden Globe Awards and four Primetime Emmy Awards, and has been nominated for three Academy Awards and four Tony Awards...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/opwZ2rIXDdJz9decuUwSnmoTjZz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/350"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"47615", properties:{bornIn:"Cuckfield, Sussex, England", imdbId:"0001216", born:date('1967-09-18'), name:"Tara Fitzgerald", bio:"Tara Anne Cassandra Fitzgerald (born 18 September 1967) is an English actress who has appeared in feature films, television, radio and the stage.  Fitzgerald won the New York Drama Desk Award for Outstanding Featured Actress in a Play in 1995 as Ophelia opposite Ralph Fiennes in Hamlet.  She won the Best Actress Award at The Reims International Television Festival in 1999 for her role of Lady Dona St.  Columb in Frenchman's Creek...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iHUWICdusPNhqvZATGCuFfruW5a.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/47615"}}, {tmdbId:"5590", properties:{bornIn:"Killara, Sydney, Australia", imdbId:"0000512", born:date('1964-03-29'), name:"Elle Macpherson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nElle Macpherson (born 29 March 1963) is an Australian model, actress, and businesswoman nicknamed \"The Body\".  She is perhaps best known for her record six cover appearances for the Sports Illustrated Swimsuit Issue beginning in the 1980s.  She is also known as the founder and primary model for a series of business ventures including Elle Macpherson Intimates, a lingerie line, and \"The Body\", a line of skin care products...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zxc6kgrG6nkRfwORwQztLLferom.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5590"}}, {tmdbId:"4654", properties:{bornIn:"Saugus, California, USA", imdbId:"0001111", born:date('1969-10-08'), name:"Jeremy Davies", bio:"Jeremy Davies (born October 8, 1969) is an American film and television actor.  He is known for portraying the interpreter Cpl.  Timothy E.  Upham in the film Saving Private Ryan and the physicist Daniel Faraday on the television series Lost.  He most recently appeared in the FX series, \"Justified\", as Dickie Bennett...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/b15bF582QuQjyw2Jgr5wxErWrDM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4654"}}, {tmdbId:"128427", properties:{imdbId:"0627850", name:"Elizabeth Newett", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/128427"}}, {tmdbId:"128428", properties:{bornIn:"Huntington - Long Island - New York - USA", imdbId:"0376770", born:date('1950-08-26'), name:"Benjamin Hendrickson", died:date('2006-07-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4ultgQSqarLpUMHesR4BU1hIKtf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/128428"}}, {tmdbId:"19958", properties:{bornIn:"Toronto, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0914491", born:date('1955-03-06'), name:"Alberta Watson", bio:"Faith Susan Alberta Watson, known professionally as Alberta Watson, was a Canadian movie and television series actress...", died:date('2015-03-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zUShDQufrKQcpnRYchZX6iNPwm7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19958"}}, {tmdbId:"33527", properties:{bornIn:"Ashern, Manitoba, Canada", imdbId:"0063440", born:date('1972-11-11'), name:"Adam Beach", bio:"Adam Ruebin Beach (born November 11, 1972) is a Canadian Saulteaux actor.  He is best known for his roles as Tommy on Walker, Texas Ranger, Kickin' Wing in Joe Dirt, Marine Private First Class Ira Hayes in Flags of Our Fathers, Private Ben Yahzee in Windtalkers, Dr.  Charles Eastman (Ohiyesa) in Bury My Heart at Wounded Knee, Chester Lake in Law & Order: Special Victims Unit, and Officer Jim Chee in the film adaptions of Skinwalkers, Coyote Waits, and A Thief of Time...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nu9H2cfl8PPA7Af6KOnRkh2sem5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33527"}}, {tmdbId:"240609", properties:{bornIn:"Morton, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0937981", name:"Sheldon Peters Wolfchild", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/240609"}}, {tmdbId:"65529", properties:{bornIn:"Anchorage, Alaska, USA", imdbId:"0065942", born:date('1967-07-22'), name:"Irene Bedard", bio:"Irene Bedard is a Native American film and television actress, director and producer, best known for voicing the title character in the _Pocahontas_ animation feature film franchise...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nCm5940cLixwcSoB5kIqLAKNmGL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/65529"}}, {tmdbId:"2387", properties:{bornIn:"Mirfield, West Yorkshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0001772", born:date('1940-07-13'), name:"Patrick Stewart", bio:"An English film, television and stage actor.  He has had a distinguished career in theatre and television for around half a century.  He is most widely known for his television and film roles, as Captain Jean-Luc Picard in Star Trek: The Next Generation and as Professor Charles Xavier in the X-Men films...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wEy5qSDT5jT3ZASc2hbwi59voPL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2387"}}, {tmdbId:"1213786", properties:{bornIn:"Houston - Texas - USA", imdbId:"0000653", born:date('1949-02-02'), name:"Brent Spiner", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nBrent Jay Spiner (/ˈspaɪnər/, born February 2, 1949, height 5' 10\" (1,78 m)) is an American actor, best known for his portrayal of the android Lieutenant Commander Data in the television series Star Trek: The Next Generation and four subsequent films.  His portrayal of Data in Star Trek: First Contact and of Dr.  Brackish Okun in Independence Day, both in 1996, earned him a Saturn Award and Saturn Award nomination respectively...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wHaOTfxOEKOPssDYaSSB5zenml4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1213786"}}, {tmdbId:"228173", properties:{bornIn:"Riverside, California, USA", imdbId:"0001109", born:date('1968-03-21'), name:"Jaye Davidson", bio:"Jaye Davidson was born Alfred Amey on March 21, 1968 in Riverside, California.  He and his family left the United States for the United Kingdom when he was two and a half years old.  He grew up in Hertfordshire, England...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1gvLTgrBpRreybxQ56dgjjKkVrh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/228173"}}, {tmdbId:"22137", properties:{bornIn:"Uppsala, Uppsala län, Sweden", imdbId:"0511798", born:date('1920-12-29'), name:"Viveca Lindfors", bio:"Elsa Viveca Torstensdotter Lindfors was a Swedish stage and screen actress, writer and director.  She was brought to Hollywood in 1946 by Warner Brothers in the hope that she would become a new Greta Garbo or Ingrid Bergman.  Viveca Lindfors appeared in almost 150 feature films and television productions...", died:date('1995-10-25'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/imttItGZIiYM9sYamQp6LwX8lVR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/22137"}}, {tmdbId:"21702", properties:{bornIn:"Coloane Island, Macau", imdbId:"0001840", born:date('1963-11-20'), name:"Ming-Na Wen", bio:"Ming-Na (born November 20, 1963) is a Macanese-born American actress.   She is known for her roles in the Mulan films and Kingdom Hearts video game series as well as ER.  She was a regular on As the World Turns, Vanished, and The Batman.  Besides television she is notable for starring in films such as The Joy Luck Club and Street Fighter...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eX7U4rXvXNsscog43qF02cPHUWI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21702"}}, {tmdbId:"96460", properties:{imdbId:"0447992", name:"Deborah Kennedy", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/z5Toskoh0D7yXX4gQEr47oEyEUJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96460"}}, {tmdbId:"88946", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles - California - USA", imdbId:"0569294", born:date('1953-11-05'), name:"Howard McGillin", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nHoward McGillin (born November 5, 1953, Los Angeles, California) is a Tony-nominated stage, screen and television actor, perhaps best-known for being the world's longest running Phantom in Andrew Lloyd Webber's The Phantom of the Opera. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Howard McGillin, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88946"}}, {tmdbId:"9260", properties:{bornIn:"Washington, D.C., U.S.", imdbId:"0629264", born:date('1960-03-31'), name:"Michelle Nicastro", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMichelle Nicastro (March 31, 1960 – November 4, 2010) was an American actress and singer. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Michelle Nicastro, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('2010-11-04'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/9260"}}, {tmdbId:"58828", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0130356", born:date('1961-04-13'), name:"Liz Callaway", bio:"Liz Callaway is a Tony nominee and Emmy Award-winning actress, singer and recording artist.  She made her Broadway debut in Stephen Sondheim’s Merrily We Roll Along, received a Tony Award nomination for her performance in Baby, and for five years won acclaim as Grizabella in Cats.  She has also starred in the original Broadway casts of Miss Saigon, The Three Musketeers, and The Look of Love...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zCPIvHAFAMSEHQxfbl6taChMsVu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/58828"}}, {tmdbId:"93592", properties:{bornIn:"Neuilly-sur-Seine, France", imdbId:"0221022", born:date('1947-10-05'), name:"Jérôme Deschamps", bio:"Jérôme Deschamps, born Neuilly-sur-Seine on 5 October 1947, is an actor, director and stage author, as well as a cinema actor and director associated with the Famille Deschiens troupe founded by Macha Makeïeff in 1978.  In 2003 he was appointed Artistic Director of the Théâtre national de Nîmes, leaving that post for the equivalent at the Théâtre national de l'Opéra-Comique in June 2007, where he remained until 2015...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yjV8LhSnlVSU5anv230HwQGocDf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/93592"}}, {tmdbId:"13688", properties:{bornIn:"Rouen, France", imdbId:"0895759", born:date('1966-01-24'), name:"Karin Viard", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nKarin Viard (born 24 January 1966) is a multi-award-winning French actress.  She made her film debut in Tatie Danielle in 1990.  Since then she has appeared in such films as Delicatessen, L'Emploi du temps (Time Out), Adultère, mode d'emploi and La parenthèse enchantée.  She was a member of the 2003 Cannes Film Festival jury. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Karin Viard  licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/o12F6rIgJNPAyJa1aUsFSntRmf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/13688"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"95189", properties:{imdbId:"0915462", born:date('1961-10-16'), name:"Kim Wayans", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95189"}}, {tmdbId:"107368", properties:{imdbId:"0066480", name:"Daniel Beer", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mTiFrOhZn8gIzIALkaizt0BOiQM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/107368"}}, {tmdbId:"44054", properties:{bornIn:" Washington, District of Columbia, USA", imdbId:"0114578", born:date('1949-06-12'), name:"Roger Aaron Brown", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vfHCepS0orjw3JabJqUj6WCEUEQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/44054"}}, {tmdbId:"156828", properties:{imdbId:"0648406", name:"Sharon Omi", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ePI4YXCf8fiALsNdkYhWw7URP6u.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/156828"}}, {tmdbId:"1216002", properties:{imdbId:"0621238", born:date('1958-01-01'), name:"Ken Narasaki", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9w3cVZqQatZP7gJLuIKYpBZLlzU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1216002"}}, {tmdbId:"2304856", properties:{name:"Lenny Lang", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2304856"}}, {tmdbId:"1860228", properties:{name:"Jenny Woo", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aL4tJCKCqcfOnoLwDdpkMtjsV4N.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1860228"}}, {tmdbId:"19578", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0000793", born:date('1969-07-28'), name:"Alexis Arquette", bio:"Alexis Arquette was an American actress, cabaret performer, underground cartoonist, and activist.  Actors Rosanna, Richmond, Patricia, and David Arquette were her siblings...", died:date('2016-09-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jNRBwGKXOZFWLI2ceff1sMUdxcE.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19578"}}, {tmdbId:"74492", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0174581", born:date('1932-01-30'), name:"Gino Conforti", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/u1eyPOCnqApU2WmLbAQJZhfygM8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74492"}}, {tmdbId:"148115", properties:{bornIn:"Atlanta, Georgia, USA", imdbId:"1631606", born:date('1927-10-25'), name:"Barbara Cook", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBarbara Cook (born October 25, 1927) is an American singer and actress who first came to prominence in the 1950s after starring in the original Broadway musicals Candide (1956) and The Music Man (1957) among others, winning a Tony Award for the latter.  She continued performing mostly in theatre until the mid 1970s, when she began a second career that continues to this day as a cabaret and concert singer...", died:date('2017-08-08'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/FA04JD7KsJYKd5d9pRcDZDjf6q.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/148115"}}, {tmdbId:"40352", properties:{bornIn:"Cleveland, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0752900", born:date('1939-11-13'), name:"Will Ryan", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nWill Ryan (born November 13, 1939) is an American voice actor and producer–writer–composer, well-known for singing about the American West.  In the late seventies he teamed up with Phil Baron as Willio and Phillio.   They had regular gigs on television, radio and comedy clubs and universities throughout the US...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/40352"}}, {tmdbId:"1366128", properties:{bornIn:"Taipei, Taiwan", imdbId:"0849916", born:date('1962-10-10'), name:"Tsung-hua Tuo", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sa3yzL4XYvyjKORErYh6Lpl1VgP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1366128"}}, {tmdbId:"18998", properties:{bornIn:"Ashby, Suffolk, England, UK", imdbId:"0365281", born:date('1927-09-19'), name:"Rosemary Harris", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRosemary Ann Harris (born 19 September 1927) is an English actress and a member of the American Theatre Hall of Fame.  Throughout her career she has been nominatied for an Academy Award, a BAFTA Award and has won a Golden Globe, an Emmy, a Tony Award, an Obie, and five Drama Desk Awards. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Rosemary Harris, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cvbL3u9KZ6AxF5rhG4hBuMpMlb2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18998"}}, {tmdbId:"49965", properties:{imdbId:"0244957", name:"Tim Dutton", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/49965"}}, {tmdbId:"1354", properties:{imdbId:"0270073", name:"Frédérique Feder", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vHCAJPYuFb2JJeX18yVo8hJmQeY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1354"}}, {tmdbId:"1356", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0521051", born:date('1960-11-29'), name:"Jean-Pierre Lorit", bio:"Jean-Pierre Lorit (born 29 November 1960) is a French actor. \n\nHis most recognizable role is in the film Three Colors: Red. \n\nIn 2005, he performed August Strindberg's Créanciers directed by Hélène Vincent, with Lambert Wilson and Emmanuelle Devos.  And he got nominated for a 2006 Molière Awards Best supporting role. \n\nSource: Article \"Jean-Pierre Lorit\" from Wikipedia in english, licensed under CC-BY-SA 3. 0...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6XU3uso54eYB4cyQa2zi0Qqej3M.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1356"}}, {tmdbId:"74036", properties:{bornIn:"Ottumwa, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0000792", born:date('1959-03-06'), name:"Tom Arnold", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nThomas Duane \"Tom\" Arnold (born March 6, 1959) is an American actor and comedian.  He has appeared in many films, perhaps most notably True Lies (1994).  He was the host of The Best Damn Sports Show Period for four years. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Tom Arnold (actor), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/z2ajL1ozVCS4Ug04zOGCNH06OPP.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74036"}}, {tmdbId:"1145", properties:{bornIn:"Brzeziny, Polonia", imdbId:"0952498", born:date('1961-07-17'), name:"Zbigniew Zamachowski", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mLntjL4Jp1LEz41NgcrHlsB7OmB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1145"}}, {tmdbId:"1147", properties:{bornIn:"Dąbrowa Górnicza, Polska", imdbId:"0301515", born:date('1939-09-23'), name:"Janusz Gajos", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6JMVmicFJvsSsRkOpgqV2cetre.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1147"}}, {tmdbId:"44917", properties:{bornIn:"Hong Kong, British Crown Colony [now China]", imdbId:"0611315", born:date('1963-10-10'), name:"Anita Mui", bio:"Anita Mui Yim-fong (10 October 1963 – 30 December 2003) was a popular Hong Kong singer and actress.  During her prime years she made major contributions to the cantopop music scene, while receiving numerous awards and honours.  She remained an idol throughout most of her career, and was generally regarded as a cantopop diva.  Mui once held a sell-out concert at Hammersmith, London, England, where she was dubbed the \"Madonna of Asia\"...", died:date('2003-12-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nGLogfEGhhVqGlECQqDFmQZ6Tid.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/44917"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"71655", properties:{bornIn:"Folingcun, Huizhou, China", imdbId:"0939059", born:date('1961-09-04'), name:"Felix Wong", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5kkHpqFdbu32xZqxJeZXqgAQbAD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71655"}}, {tmdbId:"82795", properties:{bornIn:"Moscow, USSR [now Russia]", imdbId:"0579823", born:date('1960-11-08'), name:"Oleg Menshikov", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nOleg Evgenyevich Menshikov (born 8 November 1960) is a Soviet and Russian entertainer.  He is a film and theatre actor, singer and director.  He started his film career in the early 1980s playing in the comedy Pokrovskie vorota and in Nikita Mikhalkov's Rodnya.  In 1993, Menshikov collaborated again with Mikhalkov in their most famous film, Burnt by the Sun...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7PkJF7BU31ZSZlrhRPKaXSJcCo4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82795"}}, {tmdbId:"14593", properties:{bornIn:"Vilnius, USSR [now Lithuania]", imdbId:"0200848", born:date('1963-01-20'), name:"Ingeborga Dapkunaite", bio:"Ingeborga Dapkūnaitė is a Lithuanian actress, who stars mostly in Russian movies...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rQko9No6HQSB2z1FE8bEeFmGbuO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14593"}}, {tmdbId:"500625", properties:{imdbId:"0586486", name:"Nadezhda Mikhalkova", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xCc6YjkpVP8yxzOUykQnyS0UGNV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/500625"}}, {tmdbId:"109471", properties:{imdbId:"0104515", name:"Phoebe Brand", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/109471"}}, {tmdbId:"55459", properties:{bornIn:"Waterloo, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0562420", born:date('1941-05-12'), name:"Jerry Mayer", died:date('2003-02-03'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55459"}}, {tmdbId:"8790", properties:{bornIn:"Bremen, Germany", imdbId:"0000888", born:date('1969-01-15'), name:"Meret Becker", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yPi5MesrPi9z1AQIiCVXNTV9c5U.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8790"}}, {tmdbId:"680", properties:{bornIn:"Suhl, Germany", imdbId:"0362896", born:date('1954-10-16'), name:"Corinna Harfouch", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/teqUjjqHzqy0mlrvnQBrwd0xOxz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/680"}}, {tmdbId:"44637", properties:{bornIn:"Burghausen - Germany", imdbId:"0957706", born:date('1969-02-21'), name:"Anian Zollner", bio:"Zollner wurde in Bayern geboren, wuchs in München auf und legte sein Abitur am dortigen Maximiliangymnasium ab.  Nach dem Zivildienst nahm er sein Studium an der Hochschule für Schauspielkunst Ernst Busch in Berlin auf, das er 1995 abschloss.  1996 wurde Anian Zollner dann in einer Hauptrolle von Regisseurin Margarethe von Trotta im Kinofilm Das Versprechen besetzt.  Es folgten weitere Rollen in Kinofilmen, auch wurde das Fernsehen auf ihn aufmerksam...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/44637"}}, {tmdbId:"11951", properties:{bornIn:"Urbana, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0957178", born:date('1956-01-07'), name:"August Zirner", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lYBV75sY8P8BWyvItcOSDiYxQV0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11951"}}, {tmdbId:"78717", properties:{bornIn:"Houston, Texas, U.S.A", imdbId:"0709634", born:date('1980-01-01'), name:"Lexi Randall", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLexi Randall (born January 1, 1980 in Houston, Texas) is a former child actor in films and television.  She appeared in the film The Long Walk Home and The War with Kevin Costner and Elijah Wood.  Randall starred in the three television movies made from the novel Sarah, Plain and Tall.  She also was in In the Best Interest of the Children and was a recurring character in the television series Designing Women.  She is married and has a child...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78717"}}, {tmdbId:"161731", properties:{bornIn:"Portland, Maine, USA", imdbId:"0204794", born:date('1964-03-31'), name:"Jeff Davis", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/161731"}}, {tmdbId:"8186", properties:{bornIn:"Apple Valley, California, USA", imdbId:"0400816", born:date('1986-02-22'), name:"Miko Hughes", bio:"Miko John Hughes (born February 22, 1986) is an American actor best known for his film roles as a child actor as Gage Creed in Pet Sematary (1989), as an autistic boy opposite Bruce Willis in Mercury Rising (1998) and as Dylan, Heather Langenkamp's son in Wes Craven's New Nightmare (1994). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Miko Hughes, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/apmHxkgtWe5bucTOrw92caoJftz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8186"}}, {tmdbId:"35521", properties:{imdbId:"0935616", born:date('1970-02-03'), name:"Matt Winston", bio:"Matt Winston is an actor and producer...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/et38vhCb9y8yGleMRNY2j4nDDyr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/35521"}}, {tmdbId:"135162", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0798076", born:date('1963-06-05'), name:"Karen Sillas", bio:"Karen Sillas is an American stage, film and television actress.  She is a graduate from the Acting Conservatory of the State University of New York, USA...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kjvCblLqywvFknAxmQgHAtKabPx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/135162"}}, {tmdbId:"65352", properties:{bornIn:"Taiwan", imdbId:"0911096", born:date('1971-07-29'), name:"Yu-Wen Wang", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nWang Yu-Wen (born July 29, 1971 in Taiwan) is a Taiwanese actress.  She has had starring roles in Five Girls and a Rope and Eat Drink Man Woman. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Yu-Wen Wang, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors  on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bnm7tCCKlu96qVd9OyHXZ5FEDJm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/65352"}}, {tmdbId:"1485122", properties:{name:"Chien-Lien Wu", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1485122"}}, {tmdbId:"54615", properties:{bornIn:"Montreal, Québec, Canada", imdbId:"0161198", born:date('1970-09-19'), name:"Christy Chung", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nChristy Chung (born 19 September 1970) is a Canadian actress and restaurateur.  She is best known for starring in films Mermaid Got Married， The Bodyguard from Beijing, Love on Delivery and Jan Dara...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eJk7Nz4koZGp8wq2ODJqlIE1n4O.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54615"}}, {tmdbId:"52908", properties:{bornIn:"Taiwan, China", imdbId:"0628877", born:date('1967-08-11'), name:"Collin Chou", bio:"Collin Chou is a Taiwanese actor and martial artist.  Chou is best known in the United States for his portrayal of Seraph in the films The Matrix Reloaded and The Matrix Revolutions.  In Asian cinema, Chou has co-starred with Jet Li, Donnie Yen and Sammo Hung in martial arts films such as Fearless (2006), and Flash Point (2007)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uUZ60sZTVhinijIPORMSCwIt0eg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/52908"}}, {tmdbId:"920426", properties:{bornIn:"Isfahan, Iran", imdbId:"0450185", born:date('1930-04-15'), name:"Mohamad Ali Keshavarz", bio:"Mohammadali Keshavarz is an actor of cinema, theater, and television who was born in 1930 in Isfahan, Iran.  After graduating from the dramatic arts academy, his first movie was \"Shabe Quzi\" by Farokh Ghaffari.  Among the most enduring works of Mohammad Ali Keshavarz, Ali Hatami's \"Mother\", Ali Hatami's \"Kamal-ol-Molk\", Mohsen Makhmalbaf's \"Once Upon a Time, Cinema\", Dariush Mehrjui's \"Mr.  Hallo\", and \" \"Through the Olive Trees\" directed by Abbas Kiarostami can be named...", died:date('2020-06-14'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/t2VuPmYvmqEY2ryOYw32jIuuSh9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/920426"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"930120", properties:{imdbId:"0451604", name:"Farhad Kheradmand", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/930120"}}, {tmdbId:"930122", properties:{imdbId:"0794477", name:"Zarifeh Shiva", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/930122"}}, {tmdbId:"930123", properties:{imdbId:"0722089", name:"Hossein Rezai", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/930123"}}, {tmdbId:"49971", properties:{bornIn:"Winston-Salem, North Carolina, USA", imdbId:"0000383", born:date('1969-12-29'), name:"Jennifer Ehle", bio:"Jennifer Ehle is an American stage, film and television actress, best known for her BAFTA winning role as Elizabeth Bennet in the 1995 miniseries Pride and Prejudice as well as for her supporting roles in feature films such as Zero Dark Thirty, The Ides of March, The King's Speech, and the Fifty Shades movie franchise.  She's the daughter of British actress Rosemary Harris and American author John Ehle...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rmHaDj5xQu3ZPoI5XWgA5BZj3zH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/49971"}}, {tmdbId:"151808", properties:{imdbId:"0363117", born:date('1965-04-26'), name:"Susannah Harker", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/151808"}}, {tmdbId:"53328", properties:{imdbId:"0768018", born:date('1968-09-09'), name:"Julia Sawalha", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/57xZL2uZzRaRmWpzWxH4SnxOa2u.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53328"}}, {tmdbId:"3547", properties:{bornIn:"Basingstoke, Hampshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0573862", born:date('1950-10-02'), name:"Ian McNeice", bio:"Ian McNeice (born 2 October 1950) is a prolific English screen, stage, and television character actor...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mJ1AwYRoWycLvCs5VRGyeM7KxrG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3547"}}, {tmdbId:"57096", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0264330", name:"Maynard Eziashi", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMaynard Eziashi (born 1965 in London, England) is a British/Nigerian actor.  In 1991, he won the Silver Bear for Best Actor at the 41st Berlin International Film Festival for his starring role in Mister Johnson (1990) alongside Pierce Brosnan. \n\nOther films, where Eziashi has played a part, include Twenty-One (1991), Bopha! (1993) and Ace Ventura: When Nature Calls (1995)...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57096"}}, {tmdbId:"1467084", properties:{imdbId:"0722135", name:"Peter Reznick", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1467084"}}, {tmdbId:"1467085", properties:{imdbId:"0568159", name:"John McDonough", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1467085"}}, {tmdbId:"1467086", properties:{imdbId:"0388818", name:"Avi Hoffman", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1467086"}}, {tmdbId:"6171", properties:{imdbId:"0825692", name:"Victor Steinbach", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6171"}}, {tmdbId:"36190", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0004908", born:date('1963-07-05'), name:"Edie Falco", bio:"Edith \"Edie\" Falco  (born July 5, 1963) is an American television, film and stage actress, known for her role in Oz as Diane Wittlesey and her roles as both Carmela Soprano on the HBO series The Sopranos and the titular character on the Showtime series Nurse Jackie.  She is the first actress to win an Emmy for Outstanding Actress in a Comedy as well as Outstanding Actress in a Drama...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jS2Hnr5OmntpX0J7EpH70zAG0mz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/36190"}}, {tmdbId:"51214", properties:{bornIn:"Knoxville, Tennessee, U.S.", imdbId:"0000605", born:date('1982-07-25'), name:"Brad Renfro", bio:"Brad Barron Renfro  was an American actor born on July 25, 1982 in Knoxville, Tennessee, to Angela Denise McCrory and Mark Renfro, a factory worker.  He was discovered at age 10 by director Joel Schumacher and made his film debut cast in the lead role of the motion picture The Client (1994), which starred Susan Sarandon and Tommy Lee Jones.  Although this would be his zenith, he went on to appear in other films, including The Cure (1995), Tom and Huck (1995), Sleepers (1996), and Apt Pupil (1998)...", died:date('2008-01-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sboIOdBAvNZj894aP5XCqxF9zHG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/51214"}}, {tmdbId:"105288", properties:{imdbId:"0212480", name:"Bernie Van De Yacht", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/105288"}}, {tmdbId:"105289", properties:{imdbId:"0285675", name:"Heather Ford", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/105289"}}, {tmdbId:"105290", properties:{bornIn:"\tMinnesota, USA", imdbId:"0565827", born:date('1976-09-23'), name:"Yvette McClendon", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/h7a3KlFwFUDSLeIC5dlGkuKmNKY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/105290"}}, {tmdbId:"108210", properties:{bornIn:"New York City - New York - USA", imdbId:"0805429", born:date('1983-04-19'), name:"Ryan Slater", bio:"Christian Slater's halfbrother, they share the same mother but have different father's.  Ryan chose to use his mother's name instead of his father's...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/14Og8Pzmk2iSiQ3sazLy70IiJqV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/108210"}}, {tmdbId:"108211", properties:{bornIn:"Hangzhou-China", imdbId:"0227629", name:"Yi Ding", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nYi Ding is an Asian American actress.  She was born in Hangzhou, China and moved to the United States at the age of 9...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/108211"}}, {tmdbId:"1181794", properties:{imdbId:"0270505", name:"Wang Fei", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1181794"}}] AS row
