ex and Lucía), a 2001 Spanish drama film, written and directed by Julio Médem, with Paz Vega.  Currently, he is expecting his first child with Argentina actress, Carolina Román...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sglKcvdU3e8hTy1kOghEbT0GdHS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16441"}}, {tmdbId:"16443", properties:{bornIn:"Buenos Aires, Argentina", imdbId:"0293842", born:date('1961-12-29'), name:"Daniel Freire", bio:"Daniel Freire  (born 29 December 1961 in Buenos Aires) is an Argentine film actor. \n\nHe entered film in 1993 in Un Muro de silencio and has appeared in over 15 films including Las Aventuras de Dios 2000 in which he portrayed Jesus Christ and Arizona Sur in 2004. \n\nHowever in 2005 he appeared in 27 episodes of the Argentine TV series Motivos personales. \n\nHe has lived in Spain since 1999...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oGmcHkMKLznWXfthIounxGI6mHc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16443"}}, {tmdbId:"6014", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0320760", born:date('1931-10-25'), name:"Annie Girardot", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAnnie Girardot (25 October 1931 – 28 February 2011) was a French actress. \n\nShe began performing in 1955, making her film debut in Treize à table.  Girardot won the Prix Suzanne Bianchetti in 1956, and in 1977 won the César Award for Best Actress portraying the title character in Docteur Françoise Gailland.  At the Venice Film Festival she won the Volpi Cup (Best Actress), in 1965 for Trois chambres a Manhattan...", died:date('2011-02-28'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qNioeFO3GcaIHDT5Mhb8SYMLqC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6014"}}, {tmdbId:"143272", properties:{imdbId:"0541104", name:"Nargess Mamizadeh", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/143272"}}, {tmdbId:"143273", properties:{imdbId:"0021747", name:"Maryiam Palvin Almani", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/143273"}}, {tmdbId:"143274", properties:{imdbId:"0267077", name:"Mojgan Faramarzi", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/143274"}}, {tmdbId:"143275", properties:{imdbId:"0754850", name:"Elham Saboktakin", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/143275"}}, {tmdbId:"102314", properties:{bornIn:"\tNew Mexico, USA", imdbId:"0004264", name:"Judy Herrera", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJudy Herrera is an American actress.  She studied drama at the American Musical and Dramatic Academy in Manhattan. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Judy Herrera, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/102314"}}, {tmdbId:"54024", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0455895", born:date('1976-07-30'), name:"Nikolai Kinski", bio:"Nanhoï Nikolai Kinski (born July 30, 1976 in Paris, France) is a film actor, and the only acknowledged son of the prolific actor Klaus Kinski and his third wife, Minhoi Geneviève Loanic.  He is the half-brother of actresses Nastassja Kinski and Pola Kinski.  Nikolai was born in France, but was raised in California, United States.  He currently resides in Berlin, Germany and owns the dual citizenship of the United States and France...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hN81FHqEqFjLvU0x4Cy4Zni4n1v.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54024"}}, {tmdbId:"68000", properties:{bornIn:"Bethesda, Maryland, U.S.", imdbId:"0368125", born:date('1976-12-06'), name:"Colleen Haskell", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nColleen Marie Haskell (born December 6, 1976) is an American television producer and actress.  She was a contestant on the first season of the American reality show Survivor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Colleen Haskell, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/c6F9y7JXmPgoc0Yj3HpooiNpB3L.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/68000"}}, {tmdbId:"8169", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0879085", born:date('1978-12-30'), name:"Tyrese Gibson", bio:"Tyrese Darnell Gibson (born December 30, 1978), also known mononymously as Tyrese, is an American Grammy-nominated R&B singer, songwriter, actor, author, television producer, former fashion model and MTV VJ.  He is best known for his role as Roman Pearce in the The Fast and the Furious series...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eHhIFk7HOElgFCaD4igtAgn41kA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8169"}}, {tmdbId:"40036", properties:{bornIn:"Washington, District of Columbia, USA", imdbId:"0378245", born:date('1970-09-11'), name:"Taraji P. Henson", bio:"Taraji P.  Henson (born September 11, 1970) is an American actress, producer and singer.  She studied acting at Howard University and began her Hollywood career as guest star on several television shows before making her breakthrough in the movie Baby Boy (2001).  In 2005, she starred in Hustle &amp; Flow and played Queenie in David Fincher's The Curious Case of Benjamin Button (2008), for which she received an Academy Award nomination...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rxnEvzGlRBsE94s7lC4cMAiLluH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/40036"}}, {tmdbId:"88183", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0328954", born:date('1976-10-19'), name:"Omar Gooding", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nOmar M.  Gooding (born October 19, 1976) is an American actor.  He is the younger brother of veteran actor Cuba Gooding, Jr.  and the son of singer Cuba Gooding, Sr. \n\nGooding is best known for appearing in television shows such as Hangin' with Mr.  Cooper, Smart Guy, and Playmakers, and also the films Ghost Dad and Baby Boy.  He was one of the original hosts of the Nickelodeon television show Wild and Crazy Kids from 1990 to 1992.  Gooding played D. H...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qDZ8WVbMQ3inSUn4k7XWqgCAIvm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88183"}}, {tmdbId:"1689342", properties:{bornIn:"Syracuse, New York, United States", imdbId:"0060114", born:date('1978-03-23'), name:"Tamara LaSeon Bass", bio:"Tamara LaSeon Bass (born March 23, 1978) is an American actress, director and writer. \n\nHer acting career began when she was a mere 16 years old.  Bass began as an actress of the small screen, scoring roles in the series \"Sliders\" (1994-99), \"Moesha\" (UPN, 1995-2001) and \"Any Day Now\" (Lifetime, 1998-2002).  Later, Bass acted in \"Belly Fruit\" (1999), \"Boston Public\" (Fox, 2000-04) and \"The Fugitive\" (CBS, 2000-01).  She also appeared in \"Baby Boy\" (2001) and \"Haunted\" (UPN, 2002-03)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oJQKXhBhxN8inVnsmQw2w0iOJMx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1689342"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Actor;
