UNWIND [{tmdbId:"10099", properties:{bornIn:"Seoul, South Korea", imdbId:"0661791", born:date('1963-08-23'), name:"Chan-wook Park", bio:"Park Chan-wook is a South Korean film director, screenwriter, producer, and former film critic.  One of the most acclaimed and popular filmmakers in his native country, Park is most known for his films The Handmaiden and The Vengeance Trilogy (Sympathy for Mr.  Vengeance, Oldboy and Sympathy for Lady Vengeance).   His films are noted for their immaculate framing and often brutal subject matter...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/77mzx3qzwfUzapY8HogM3TUi8Kv.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10099"}}, {tmdbId:"78997", properties:{bornIn:"Havana, Cuba", imdbId:"0406687", born:date('1948-08-03'), name:"Leon Ichaso", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nLeon Ichaso (born August 3, 1948) is a Cuban American writer and film director. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Leon Ichaso, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78997"}}, {tmdbId:"64141", properties:{bornIn:"Little Rock, Arkansas, USA", imdbId:"0337773", born:date('1975-04-09'), name:"David Gordon Green", bio:"David Gordon Green is an American independent filmmaker.  He has directed dramas such as George Washington, All the Real Girls, and Snow Angels, as well as the thriller Undertow, all of which he wrote or co-wrote.  In 2008, he transitioned into comedy, directing the films Pineapple Express, Your Highness and The Sitter, as well as episodes of the HBO comedy Eastbound & Down.  In 2013, he returned to his more dramatic roots with the independent films Prince Avalanche and Joe...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3ASxWOzEbMsBqqeQHoIbWvhfkod.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/64141"}}, {tmdbId:"236655", properties:{name:"Ömer Vargi", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/236655"}}, {tmdbId:"1091281", properties:{imdbId:"0861129", name:"Yongyoot Thongkongtoon", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1091281"}}, {tmdbId:"76247", properties:{bornIn:"USA", imdbId:"0379237", born:date('1966-07-05'), name:"Charles Herman-Wurmfeld", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nCharles Herman-Wurmfeld (born July 5, 1966) is an American film director.  He has directed numerous films from 1995 to now. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Charles Herman-Wurmfeld, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/76247"}}, {tmdbId:"35208", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0785684", born:date('1947-10-29'), name:"Coline Serreau", bio:"Coline Serreau (born 29 October 1947) is a French actress, film director and writer. \n\nShe was born in Paris, the daughter of theatre director Jean-Marie Serreau and actress Geneviève Serreau.  In Paris, Serreau studied literature, music and theatre as well as the circus. \n\nIn 1970 she made her debut as an actress at the Théâtre du Vieux-Colombier. \n\nSerreau wrote her first screenplay in 1973...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qHGyprOAsbX1q5Ym6Jad0haBuuu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/35208"}}, {tmdbId:"17825", properties:{bornIn:"Montreal, Quebec, Canada", imdbId:"0506613", born:date('1968-01-01'), name:"Shawn Levy", bio:"Shawn Adam Levy (born 1968) is a Canadian-American director, producer and actor who directed the comedy films Big Fat Liar, Just Married, Cheaper by the Dozen, The Pink Panther, Night at the Museum, and Date Night.  He has also directed many television shows, including Cousin Skeeter, The Famous Jett Jackson and Pepper Dennis. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Shawn Levy, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uf9GPrYPclLZI6shR9Ho1QtBrw9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/17825"}}, {tmdbId:"54040", properties:{bornIn:"Longview, Texas, USA", imdbId:"0359387", born:date('1956-12-15'), name:"John Lee Hancock", bio:"John Lee Hancock, Jr.  (born December 15, 1956) is an American screenwriter, film director, and producer.  He is best known for directing the sports drama films The Rookie and The Blind Side...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ytGKxuC1sFUmd68jUwDA37Jn0LG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54040"}}, {tmdbId:"111883", properties:{imdbId:"0607365", name:"Billy Morrissette", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/111883"}}, {tmdbId:"31074", properties:{bornIn:"Mito, Ibaraki Prefecture Japan", imdbId:"0297935", born:date('1930-07-03'), name:"Kinji Fukasaku", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nKinji Fukasaku (3 July 1930 – 12 January 2003) was a Japanese film actor, screenwriter, and best known as a celebrated and innovative filmmaker.  He was born in Mito, Ibaraki, Japan, and died in Tokyo, from prostate cancer.  He is best known in the west for directing the Japanese portion of the Hollywood film Tora! Tora! Tora! (1970) and Battle Royale (2000)...", died:date('2003-01-12'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mrDEkUwgZOQz8ES5oMwTBfN4n7q.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31074"}}, {tmdbId:"2945", properties:{bornIn:"Louisville, Kentucky, U.S.", imdbId:"0300866", born:date('1965-05-06'), name:"Stephen Gaghan", bio:"Stephen Gaghan (born May 6, 1965) is an American screenwriter and director.  He is noted for writing the screenplay for Steven Soderbergh's film Traffic, based on a Channel 4 series, for which he won the Academy Award, as well as Syriana which he wrote and directed...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bApESY40VIkkjIu8pxgODTiiJFt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2945"}}, {tmdbId:"48583", properties:{bornIn:"Luxembourg", imdbId:"0284774", born:date('1959-07-15'), name:"Anne Fontaine", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAnne Fontaine (born in Luxembourg, 1959) is a filmmaker and screenwriter who used to be an actor.  She lives and works in France. \n\nBorn Fontaine Sibertin-Blanc, sister of actor Jean-Chrétien Sibertin-Blanc, she went as a young child to live in Lisbon, where her father, Antoine Sibertin-Blanc, is a music professor and cathedral organist...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/b9MFx57lqidHgfreWY8MgBn3dAy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/48583"}}, {tmdbId:"5713", properties:{bornIn:"Binghamton, New York, USA", imdbId:"0917188", born:date('1957-03-20'), name:"Chris Wedge", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJohn Christopher \"Chris\" Wedge (born March 20, 1957) is an American film director, best known for the films Ice Age and Robots. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Chris Wedge, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bYiy2vcXgJq5XZdZ15uIhBhnBF8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5713"}}, {tmdbId:"59210", properties:{imdbId:"0828099", name:"Patrick Stettner", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/59210"}}, {tmdbId:"90695", properties:{bornIn:"Osaka, Japan", imdbId:"0015085", born:date('1962-03-24'), name:"Kazuki Akane", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/90695"}}, {tmdbId:"90696", properties:{imdbId:"1988172", name:" Yoshiyuki Takei", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/90696"}}, {tmdbId:"21931", properties:{bornIn:"Soisy-sous-Montmorency, France", imdbId:"0619599", born:date('1968-12-05'), name:"Chris Nahon", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nChris Nahon is a French film director best known for directing the films Kiss of the Dragon, Empire of the Wolves, and Blood: The Last Vampire...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21931"}}, {tmdbId:"19272", properties:{bornIn:"Cleveland, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0751648", born:date('1971-07-08'), name:" Joe Russo", bio:"Anthony and Joe Russo, known together professionally as the Russo brothers, are Emmy Award-winning American film and television directors.  The brothers direct most of their work jointly, and they also occasionally work as producers, actors, and editors.  The Russos are from Cleveland, Ohio, and were born a year apart.  They are alumni of Case Western Reserve University...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/679Os4tbY1YsU01KdLhM1NPXNWu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19272"}}, {tmdbId:"84975", properties:{imdbId:"0444054", name:"Seth Kearsley", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/84975"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"56150", properties:{bornIn:"Christchurch, New Zealand", imdbId:"0253819", born:date('1970-08-12'), name:"Ellory Elkayem", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEllory Elkayem (born 12 August 1970) is a New Zealand film director. \n\nBorn in Christchurch, Ellory Elkayem began making films at a young age.  He later attended a film school designed to give students practical experience and preparation for a career in the film business...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/Ad1h4tzvq27oK63Ua2n6RrgYA8n.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56150"}}, {tmdbId:"102560", properties:{bornIn:"Recife, Pernambuco, Brazil", imdbId:"0037136", born:date('1953-12-12'), name:"Guel Arraes", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nDkWIjgHJWrYSBTdZHPjvAQlrAQ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/102560"}}, {tmdbId:"60220", properties:{bornIn:"McMinnville, Oregon, USA", imdbId:"0899139", born:date('1947-11-17'), name:"Will Vinton", bio:"Award-winning co-director of \"Closed Mondays\", the first Claymation (tm) film. \n\nWill Vinton was born on November 17, 1947 in McMinnville, Oregon, USA as William Gale Vinton.  He was a producer and director, known for Claymation Easter (1992), Martin the Cobbler (1977) and Moonwalker (1988).  He was married to Gillian Allred and Susan Shadburne.   He was a Claymation artist who coined the term...", died:date('2018-10-04'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/60220"}}, {tmdbId:"81256", properties:{bornIn:"London, England", imdbId:"0394199", born:date('1970-09-06'), name:"Joel Hopkins", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Joel Hopkins (born 1970) is a British independent film director and screenwriter best known for his films Jump Tomorrow (2001) and Last Chance Harvey (2008). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Joel Hopkins, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81256"}}, {tmdbId:"17496", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0002191", born:date('1952-04-30'), name:"Jacques Audiard", bio:"Jacques Audiard is a French film director, writer, actor and producer.  He is the son of Michel Audiard, also a notable screenwriter and film director.  Audiard won twice both the César Award for Best Film and the BAFTA Award for Best Film not in the English Language, in 2005 for The Beat That My Heart Skipped and in 2010 for A Prophet.  He also won the Grand Prix at the Cannes Film Festival...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dJ2XCySH5NKZTEEapYK3RaBtL61.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/17496"}}, {tmdbId:"16136", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0457541", born:date('1963-11-15'), name:"Hiroyuki Kitakubo", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16136"}}, {tmdbId:"4319", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles County, California, USA", imdbId:"0672769", born:date('1957-10-15'), name:"Stacy Peralta", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nStacy Peralta (born October 15, 1957) is an American director and entrepreneur.  He has previously been a professional skateboarder and team surfer as one of the original Z-Boys. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Stacy Peralta, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mT2TkPs1Yjh2DaJWnYJpcoRwm1H.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4319"}}, {tmdbId:"94643", properties:{imdbId:"0615231", name:"Rich Murray", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94643"}}, {tmdbId:"69797", properties:{bornIn:"Aylmer, Quebec", imdbId:"0213450", born:date('1970-06-07'), name:"Dean DeBlois", bio:"Dean DeBlois (born June 7, 1970) is a Canadian film director, film producer, screenwriter, animator, camera operator, and editor.  He is best known for co-writing and co-directing The Oscar-nominated animated films Lilo & Stitch (Walt Disney Feature Animation) and How to Train Your Dragon (Dreamworks Animation), and for directing the acclaimed Sigur Rós documentary/music film Heima...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qdp7vc24XR836glg8mwHBEEZE6C.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69797"}}, {tmdbId:"3722", properties:{bornIn:"Feldkirch, Austria", imdbId:"0918326", born:date('1970-11-02'), name:"Hans Weingartner", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3722"}}, {tmdbId:"3870", properties:{imdbId:"1170198", name:" Tobias Amann", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3870"}}, {tmdbId:"57030", properties:{bornIn:"Sale, Victoria, Australia", imdbId:"0429964", name:"Gregor Jordan", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGregor Jordan (born 1966) is an Australian film director. \n\nJordan's films include Two Hands (1999), Buffalo Soldiers (2001), and Ned Kelly (2003).  He has also directed the concert video These Days: Live in Concert (2004) by Australian rock band Powderfinger.  His film Two Hands won the Australian Film Institute Award for Best Direction and Best Screenplay in 1999...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57030"}}, {tmdbId:"54584", properties:{bornIn:"New York, USA", imdbId:"0245888", born:date('1966-01-06'), name:"Jesse Dylan", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJesse Dylan (b. January 6, 1966, New York City) is an American film director, and the founder of the media production company FreeForm. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jesse Dylan, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iKtSezKKjWHMqd1VDtuJNUEj1xl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54584"}}, {tmdbId:"5016", properties:{imdbId:"0363214", name:"Jan Harlan", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5016"}}, {tmdbId:"17397", properties:{bornIn:"San Antonio, Texas, U.S.", imdbId:"0451884", born:date('1957-11-27'), name:"Callie Khouri", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nCallie Khouri (born November 27, 1957, as Carolyn Ann Khouri) is an American screenwriter and film director.  In 1992 she won the Academy Award for Best Screenplay Written Directly for the Screen for the film, Thelma &amp; Louise. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Callie Khouri, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/17397"}}, {tmdbId:"486", properties:{imdbId:"0938645", name:"Wallace Wolodarsky", bio:"Wallace Wolodarsky is an American television writer and director.  He wrote for The Simpsons during the first four seasons; all of his episodes were co-written with former writing partner Jay Kogen.  Since he left, he has directed several films (the most notable being Sorority Boys)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/a6npTg5wUQIHkyH17m5FPc9hJPV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/486"}}, {tmdbId:"71849", properties:{imdbId:"0816110", name:" Lynne Southerland", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71849"}}, {tmdbId:"116583", properties:{imdbId:"0714261", born:date('1974-01-01'), name:"Juan Pablo Rebella", died:date('2006-07-05'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/116583"}}, {tmdbId:"25598", properties:{bornIn:"Cheam, Surrey, England, UK", imdbId:"0339030", born:date('1955-08-13'), name:"Paul Greengrass", bio:"Paul Greengrass (born 13 August 1955) is an English film director, screenwriter and former journalist.  He specialises in dramatisations of real-life events and is known for his signature use of hand-held cameras. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Paul Greengrass, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kJxQWrERq8p7gxRP2fIcS8suwme.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25598"}}, {tmdbId:"57581", properties:{bornIn:"Newcastle upon Tyne - England - UK", imdbId:"0551076", born:date('1970-05-25'), name:"Neil Marshall", bio:"Neil Marshall (born 25 May 1970) is an English film director, editor, and screenwriter.  Marshall began his career in editing and in 2002 directed his first feature film Dog Soldiers, which became a cult film.  He followed up with the critically acclaimed horror film The Descent in 2005.  Marshall also directed Doomsday in 2008, and wrote and directed Centurion in 2010...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/niiQO8m2fEIdmEBYdawulBSIzwY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57581"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"58552", properties:{bornIn:" Washington, D.C.", imdbId:"0824882", born:date('1965-10-08'), name:"Burr Steers", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBurr Gore Steers (born October 8, 1965) is an American actor, screenwriter and director. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Burr Steers, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/k9rAVWornL0SUIykpjd3K3IfSll.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/58552"}}, {tmdbId:"143589", properties:{imdbId:"0160429", born:date('1965-08-29'), name:"Angela Christlieb", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/143589"}}, {tmdbId:"78488", properties:{imdbId:"0539782", name:"Cathy Malkasian", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78488"}}, {tmdbId:"66739", properties:{bornIn:"Johannesburg, South Africa", imdbId:"0509448", born:date('1976-09-15'), name:"Jonathan Liebesman", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJonathan Liebesman (born September 15, 1976) is a South African film director. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jonathan Liebesman, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/66739"}}, {tmdbId:"58687", properties:{imdbId:"0318733", name:"Scott J. Gill", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/58687"}}, {tmdbId:"220775", properties:{bornIn:"South Africa", imdbId:"0035184", born:date('1964-01-01'), name:" Justine Shapiro", bio:"Born in South Africa, raised in San Francisco.  Studied History and  Theatre in College, eventually making her way to France to work as an  actress.  Best known as one of the presenters on \"The Lonely Planet\" (as  Justine Shapiro)...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/220775"}}, {tmdbId:"234749", properties:{imdbId:"0092632", name:" Carlos Bolado", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/234749"}}, {tmdbId:"20028", properties:{bornIn:" Zenica, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Yugoslavia (now Zenica, Bosnia and Herzegovina)", imdbId:"0849786", born:date('1969-02-20'), name:"Danis Tanovic", bio:"Danis Tanović (born 20 February 1969) is a Bosnian film director and screenwriter. \n\nTanović is best known for having directed and written the script for the 2001 Bosnian movie No Man's Land which won an Academy Award.  He was a member of the jury at the 2003 Cannes Film Festival.   Description above from the Wikipedia article Danis Tanović, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.  Photo by Wikipedia user KoljaHub, under CC-BY-SA...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20028"}}, {tmdbId:"1174204", properties:{imdbId:"0472947", name:"Michael Kruzan", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1174204"}}, {tmdbId:"21678", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0000801", born:date('1955-01-25'), name:"Olivier Assayas", bio:"Olivier Assayas (born January 25, 1955) is a French film director and screenwriter. \n\nHe made his debut in 1986, after directing some short films and writing for the influential film magazine Cahiers du cinéma. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Olivier Assayas, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qP35v7IAeiaXNQzkYTuIQCxa4MO.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21678"}}, {tmdbId:"127823", properties:{bornIn:"Madrid, Spain", imdbId:"0246503", name:"Agustín Díaz Yanes", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAgustín Díaz Yanes (Madrid, 1950) is a Spanish Goya Awards winner screenwriter and film director. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Agustín Díaz Yanes, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/127823"}}, {tmdbId:"57199", properties:{imdbId:"0617042", name:"Mark Mylod", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMark Mylod is a British film and television director.  Mylod has directed several shows both in the United States and in the United Kingdom, many of them being for the BBC.  Mylod is currently a co-producer on the HBO television series Entourage, of which he is also a regular director...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57199"}}, {tmdbId:"97296", properties:{bornIn:"Kapuivik, Nunavut, Canada", imdbId:"0994348", born:date('1957-11-27'), name:"Zacharias Kunuk", bio:"Zacharias Kunuk is a Canadian Inuk film writer, director and producer, best known for writing and directing the feature film _Atanarjuat: The Fast Runner_, the first indigenous film with all indigenous cast and entirely in Inuktitut...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/if0r0xGWIzUcJb0PgBCpLkC5kHa.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/97296"}}, {tmdbId:"57962", properties:{imdbId:"0622240", name:"Mort Nathan", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57962"}}, {tmdbId:"3115", properties:{bornIn:"Wrocław, Poland", imdbId:"0782900", born:date('1954-12-19'), name:"Andrzej Sekula", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAndrzej Sekuła (born 1954 in Wrocław, Poland) is a Polish cinematographer and film director.  He left his native Poland in 1980 and currently lives in Los Angeles.  His cinematography work has appeared in such prominent films as Reservoir Dogs and Pulp Fiction. \n\nIn Armored, Sekula's work helped convey the bleakness at the core of the film, critic A.  O.  Scott wrote in The New York Times...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uDGWSDyiofiND6Qqla19UZvNHEX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3115"}}, {tmdbId:"21768", properties:{bornIn:"Maison Laffitte, Yvelines, France", imdbId:"0158984", born:date('1963-11-10'), name:"Sylvain Chomet", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSylvain Chomet (born 1963) is a French comic writer, animator and film director. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Sylvain Chomet, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hi5lgXJVDlw5oL8BVjdNur3hTNS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21768"}}, {tmdbId:"213337", properties:{imdbId:"0873400", born:date('1959-12-31'), name:"Ondrej Trojan", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/213337"}}, {tmdbId:"122967", properties:{imdbId:"0566833", born:date('1971-03-31'), name:"Craig McCracken", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/122967"}}, {tmdbId:"20218", properties:{imdbId:"0107774", name:"Eric Bress", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEric Bress (Borrell) is an American screenwriter, film director and producer, probably best known for his work on the Final Destination series and The Butterfly Effect.  He frequently collaborates with J.  Mackye Gruber. \n\nHis most recent project, The Alchemyst: The Secrets of the Immortal Nicholas Flamel, is in development.  He also has another project in development Blindsighted with his writing partner J.  Mackye Gruber...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20218"}}, {tmdbId:"20219", properties:{imdbId:"0344259", name:" J. Mackye Gruber", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20219"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"736", properties:{imdbId:"0583675", name:"Menno Meyjes", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/736"}}, {tmdbId:"65134", properties:{imdbId:"0690770", born:date('1969-04-14'), name:"DJ Pooh", bio:"DJ Pooh is an American record producer, rapper, screenwriter and film director...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/65134"}}, {tmdbId:"96557", properties:{bornIn:"Nagasaki, Japan", imdbId:"0368031", born:date('1962-07-13'), name:"Ryosuke Hashiguchi", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eNPvbgc9U91pVUjSZJcT3uBJ8dW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96557"}}, {tmdbId:"61571", properties:{imdbId:"1032759", name:"Barry Skolnick", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/61571"}}, {tmdbId:"71307", properties:{imdbId:"0172989", born:date('1976-01-01'), name:"Laetitia Colombani", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71307"}}, {tmdbId:"18865", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0504642", born:date('1973-06-17'), name:"Louis Leterrier", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLouis Leterrier (born June 17, 1973) is a French film director whose notable films include the first two Transporter movies, Unleashed (2005), The Incredible Hulk (2008) and Clash of the Titans (2010)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/guZxKjoW47PfKY4aLFSVhyzyQW4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18865"}}, {tmdbId:"65133", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, United States", imdbId:"1048560", born:date('1965-11-30'), name:"Marcus Raboy", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMarcus Raboy (born November 30, 1965) is an American film and music video director. \n\nSince the early 1990s, Raboy has amassed a large number music video credits directing music videos for Mary J.  Blige, Dixie Chicks, Rihanna, Luther Vandross, Shakira, Santana and among other notable artists. \n\nHis feature film credits are Friday After Next (2002) and Janky Promoters (2009) both starring Ice Cube and Mike Epps...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kKl5cOGuiWRPx228Kg2eIgZrlbi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/65133"}}, {tmdbId:"20824", properties:{imdbId:"0086690", name:"Perry Andelin Blake", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20824"}}, {tmdbId:"43526", properties:{bornIn:"Reykjavík, Iceland", imdbId:"0348274", born:date('1951-01-01'), name:"Sturla Gunnarsson", bio:"Sturla Gunnarsson is a Canadian film director. \n\nGunnarsson was born in Iceland in 1951.  He moved to Vancouver, British Columbia, with his parents when he was seven years old...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/43526"}}, {tmdbId:"21031", properties:{bornIn:"Buenos Aires, Argentina", imdbId:"0002159", born:date('1961-06-02'), name:"Alejandro Agresti", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nAlejandro Agresti (born June 2, 1961 in Buenos Aires) is an Argentine film director and producer.  He has become increasingly influential in the United States and directed The Lake House with top Hollywood actors Sandra Bullock and Keanu Reeves in 2006. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia Alejandro Agresti, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21031"}}, {tmdbId:"27005", properties:{bornIn:"Newport Beach, California, USA", imdbId:"0666806", born:date('1963-04-17'), name:"Don Michael Paul", bio:"Don Michael Paul, (born April 17, 1963) is an actor, director, writer and producer.  He starred in the movie Heart of Dixie.  He wrote the screenplay for Harley Davidson and the Marlboro Man.  He was one of three brothers in the short-lived 1992 CBS detective series The Hat Squad.  (\"Winter People\") He also played a prominent role in Models Inc.  Robot Wars\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Don Michael Paul, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27005"}}, {tmdbId:"69938", properties:{imdbId:"1065068", name:"Chris Delaporte", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69938"}}, {tmdbId:"69940", properties:{imdbId:"0969927", name:" Pascal Pinon", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69940"}}, {tmdbId:"15287", properties:{bornIn:"Wellington, New Zealand", imdbId:"0138927", born:date('1966-09-20'), name:"Niki Caro", bio:"Niki Caro is an award winning film director, producer and screenwriter who was born in Wellington, New Zealand.  Her most significant film to date is Whale Rider from 2002.  It was critically praised and won a number of awards at international film festivals.  She went on to direct Charlize Theron in an Oscar-nominated performance in North Country.  Caro graduated BFA from the Elam School of Fine Arts at the University of Auckland in 1988, and MFA from Swinburne University of Technology...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ooJcmnhX9qJ0E7bCdSQCxr7JViH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15287"}}, {tmdbId:"239075", properties:{bornIn:"Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"1071898", born:date('1969-08-30'), name:"Dylan Kidd", bio:"Dylan Kidd is an American screenwriter, producer and director.  He directed the 2002 film Rodger Dodger, starring Campbell Scott and Jesse Eisenberg, which was very well received by critics despite its lack of box office success and won best feature at the Tribeca Film Festival.  He directed the film P. S.  in 2004...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/239075"}}, {tmdbId:"1286322", properties:{imdbId:"0187944", name:"Michael Criscione", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1286322"}}, {tmdbId:"95458", properties:{imdbId:"0362544", name:"Gary Hardwick", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95458"}}, {tmdbId:"138857", properties:{imdbId:"0167384", name:" Jacques Cluzaud", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/138857"}}, {tmdbId:"71280", properties:{bornIn:"London, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0236226", born:date('1973-04-19'), name:"Michael Dowse", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nMichael Dowse (born April 19, 1973) is a Canadian film director. \n\nBorn and raised in London, Ontario, he was trained as a film editor.  His first full-length movie, FUBAR was shot on a digital camera with a tiny budget, but was selected by the Sundance Film Festival and screened on the prestigious midnight slot, which had launched the revolutionary film The Blair Witch Project...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xShST7ecFRhXY8lGGyqmTnbUuXF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71280"}}, {tmdbId:"51534", properties:{bornIn:"Jenny Lind, California, USA", imdbId:"1031246", born:date('1975-11-01'), name:"Lucky McKee", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEdward Lucky McKee (born November 1, 1975 in Jenny Lind, California) is an American director, writer, and actor, largely known for the 2002 film May, which has acquired a cult following...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/51534"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"80215", properties:{imdbId:"0831690", name:"Charles Stone III", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Charles Stone III (born in 1966) is a film director, known for films such as Drumline starring Nick Cannon, Mr.  3000 starring Bernie Mac, and Paid in Full. \n\nStone directed the video to What They Do by The Roots, featuring the group running through many rap video clichés.   Stone was the creator of the popular United States advertising campaign, \"Whassup?\" for Budweiser...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80215"}}, {tmdbId:"946395", properties:{imdbId:"1099970", name:"AJ Schnack", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/946395"}}, {tmdbId:"4617", properties:{bornIn:"Gera, Germany", imdbId:"0237527", born:date('1963-08-16'), name:"Andreas Dresen", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aNgqbOIPxBNkrDnpM2qzXYBTanb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4617"}}, {tmdbId:"72205", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0075849", born:date('1963-07-13'), name:"Shari Springer Berman", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nShari Springer Berman (born July 1964 in New York City, New York, USA) and Robert Pulcini (born August 24, 1964 in New York City, New York, USA) are an award-winning team of documentarians who received critical acclaim and an Academy Award nomination for their feature film directorial debut, 2003's American Splendor.  In 2010, The Extra Man premiered at the Sundance festival...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/72205"}}, {tmdbId:"72206", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0700301", born:date('1964-08-24'), name:" Robert Pulcini", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nShari Springer Berman (born July 1964 in New York City, New York, USA) and Robert Pulcini (born August 24, 1964 in New York City, New York, USA) are an award-winning team of documentarians who received critical acclaim and an Academy Award nomination for their feature film directorial debut, 2003's American Splendor.  In 2010, The Extra Man premiered at the Sundance festival...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/72206"}}, {tmdbId:"944713", properties:{imdbId:"1104343", name:"John Stainton", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/944713"}}, {tmdbId:"88837", properties:{imdbId:"1117507", name:"Larry Blamire", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLarry Blamire is an American filmmaker, writer and artist best known for the independent film The Lost Skeleton of Cadavra. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Larry Blamire, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/w5c4BLQK8uyJDO503mWWZpV7zBc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88837"}}, {tmdbId:"937129", properties:{bornIn:"Arrondissement di Mirande, Francia", imdbId:"0994355", born:date('1963-07-01'), name:"Jean-Xavier de Lestrade", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nHaf06zq5xjiwKgh5zEZoegGBQX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/937129"}}, {tmdbId:"105764", properties:{imdbId:"0726123", born:date('1963-01-01'), name:"Thomas Riedelsheimer", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/105764"}}, {tmdbId:"65630", properties:{bornIn:"Honolulu, Hawaii, USA", imdbId:"1224299", born:date('1970-10-31'), name:" Rob Letterman", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRob Letterman is an American film director, writer and voice actor. \n\nBefore Letterman's filmic subjects took him into outer space with Monsters vs.  Aliens (2009), he was taken underwater, having directed and written DreamWorks Animation's 2004 Academy Award-nominated hit comedy Shark Tale, starring Will Smith, Renée Zellweger, Angelina Jolie and Jack Black.  His writing efforts on the film also netted him an Annie nomination...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bgsnUXYPWsRDuo3B0f9wthXKxll.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/65630"}}, {tmdbId:"65615", properties:{imdbId:"1126346", name:"Wych Kaosayananda", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nWych Kaosayananda is a Thai film director. \n\nHe is the son of famous Thai diplomat \"Kaosayananda\".  He lived and studied in Pakistan, where his father was posted in Islamabad as an ambassador. \n\nHis directorial debut was Fah, released in 1998, which at the time was the highest-budgeted film in the history of the Thai film industry but failed in the Thai box office...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/65615"}}, {tmdbId:"17329", properties:{bornIn:"Connecticut, US", imdbId:"1139726", name:"Neil Burger", bio:"Neil Burger is an American film director who has filmed the pseudo-documentary, Interview with the Assassin (2002), the period drama, The Illusionist, and the 2011 thriller Limitless. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Neil Burger, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/17329"}}, {tmdbId:"74647", properties:{bornIn:"Boston, Massachusetts", imdbId:"0298488", born:date('1965-10-17'), name:"Keith Fulton", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74647"}}, {tmdbId:"106537", properties:{imdbId:"0672492", born:date('1966-08-07'), name:" Louis Pepe", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/106537"}}, {tmdbId:"110351", properties:{imdbId:"1126861", name:"J.T.S. Moore", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nJ. T. S.  Moore is American film director and producer.  Along with an undergraduate degree in history from Stanford University, Moore also graduated from the University of Southern California's School of Cinematic Arts with a Master's degree in film production.  He's known primarily for Revolution OS (2001), a film about the origins of the Free Software and open-source movements.  He also wrote and directed the Civil War action-drama Shooting Creek in 1995...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/110351"}}, {tmdbId:"56937", properties:{bornIn:"Wien, Austria", imdbId:"0375267", born:date('1947-03-22'), name:"André Heller", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/phGnClIcYGzBy981ArudGBrq8PA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56937"}}, {tmdbId:"56938", properties:{imdbId:"0772761", name:" Othmar Schmiderer", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56938"}}, {tmdbId:"3290", properties:{bornIn:"Des Moines, Iowa, USA", imdbId:"0373282", born:date('1962-07-06'), name:"Peter Hedges", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nPeter Hedges (born July 6, 1962) is an American novelist, screenwriter, and film director. \n\nHedges grew up in West Des Moines, Iowa, and attended Valley High School, where he was involved in the theater department, including the improv group and the mime troupe, \"The Bakers Dozen\".  He later went to the North Carolina School of the Arts...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3290"}}, {tmdbId:"7313", properties:{bornIn:"Bristol, England", imdbId:"0101508", born:date('1967-01-23'), name:"Steve Box", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSteve Box (born 23 January 1967 in Bristol) is an Oscar-winning English animator and director who works for Aardman Animations...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4YQQdd2VMi3DOSbyojdcNBEnr6P.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7313"}}, {tmdbId:"111212", properties:{imdbId:"0302572", name:"Michael O. Gallant", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/111212"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"5133", properties:{bornIn:"Yardley, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0919514", born:date('1951-11-30'), name:"Bo Welch", bio:"Robert W.  \"Bo\" Welch III (born November 30, 1951) is an American production designer and director...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lYSuKR7b8aNYnZmzVQh4CPk5YMe.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5133"}}, {tmdbId:"67075", properties:{bornIn:" Toyokawa, Aichi, Japan", imdbId:"0814469", born:date('1961-12-20'), name:"Sion Sono", bio:"Sion Sono (園 子温 Sono Shion, born December 18, 1961) is a Japanese filmmaker, author and poet.  Best known on the festival circuit for the film Love Exposure (2008), he has been called \"the most subversive filmmaker working in Japanese cinema today\"...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/AfPlYmCrt0m1ff2JialRamOCYxK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67075"}}, {tmdbId:"73051", properties:{imdbId:"0540443", name:"Jim Malone", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/73051"}}, {tmdbId:"1409418", properties:{imdbId:"0970388", name:"Tuck Tucker", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1409418"}}, {tmdbId:"90", properties:{bornIn:"Sant Adrià de Besòs, Barcelona, Catalunya", imdbId:"0170043", born:date('1960-04-09'), name:"Isabel Coixet", bio:"Isabel Coixet Castillo is a Spanish film director.  She is one of the most prolific film directors of contemporary Spain, having directed twelve feature-length films since the beginning of her film career in 1988, in addition to documentary films, shorts and commercials. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Isabel Coixet, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/s2Hspn17nOf6LIuVrULvV3OOiX0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/90"}}, {tmdbId:"110464", properties:{imdbId:"0433225", name:"Paul Justman", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/110464"}}, {tmdbId:"71548", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York City", imdbId:"0813164", born:date('1976-01-01'), name:"Peter Sollett", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nPeter Sollett (born 1976) is an American film director and screenwriter known for his feature films Raising Victor Vargas (2002) and Nick and Norah's Infinite Playlist (2008). \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Peter Sollett licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71548"}}, {tmdbId:"7911", properties:{imdbId:"0710020", born:date('1960-03-13'), name:" Joe Ranft", died:date('2005-08-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/f1BoWC2JbCcfP1e5hKfGsxkHzVU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/7911"}}, {tmdbId:"8557", properties:{bornIn:"São Paulo, São Paulo, Brazil", imdbId:"0576987", born:date('1955-11-09'), name:"Fernando Meirelles", bio:"Fernando Meirelles (born November 9, 1955 in São Paulo, Brazil) is a Brazilian film director.  He was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Director in 2004 for his work in the Brazilian film City of God, released in 2002 in Brazil and in 2003 in the U. S.  by Miramax Films.  He was also nominated for the Golden Globe Best Director award in 2005 for The Constant Gardener...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/at0fRZl4fJwqaytXOfvgs1lOM9E.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8557"}}, {tmdbId:"8559", properties:{bornIn:"São Paulo, São Paulo, Brazil", imdbId:"0526199", born:date('1966-01-01'), name:" Kátia Lund", bio:"Kátia Lund (born 1966 in São Paulo) is an American-Brazilian film director and screenwriter.  Her most notable work was as co-director of the film City of God. \n\nLund's parents are Americans who emigrated to Brazil before she was born.  She graduated from Escola Maria Imaculada, an American Catholic school in São Paulo where she excelled in art.  She then attended Brown University where she became interested in filmmaking...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8jNK0JjXe6e47G9VgBtGutLadKK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/8559"}}, {tmdbId:"563341", properties:{bornIn:"Haifa, Israel", imdbId:"0074844", born:date('1969-08-08'), name:"Nir Bergman", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uU81AFHIpIp7TpccG4IgLEWHi0R.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/563341"}}, {tmdbId:"15344", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0009190", born:date('1966-06-27'), name:"J.J. Abrams", bio:"Jeffrey Jacob Abrams (born June 27, 1966) is an American filmmaker.  He is best known for his work in the genres of action, drama, and science fiction.  Abrams wrote or produced such films as Regarding Henry (1991), Forever Young (1992), Armageddon (1998), Cloverfield (2008), Star Trek (2009), Star Wars: The Force Awakens (2015), and Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker (2019)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ecNnEjzBApky2R7nBqp2iY3Zo1H.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15344"}}, {tmdbId:"107762", properties:{bornIn:"village Podorvikha, Irkutsk Region, RSFSR, USSR, (now Russia)", imdbId:"0812546", born:date('1951-06-14'), name:"Aleksandr Sokurov", bio:"Aleksandr Sokurov (born June 14, 1951)  is a Russian director of avant-garde and independent films that have won him international acclaim.  Described as a heir to Tarkovsky, spare, gloomy and contemplative, he often blurs lines between image and world.  His noticable trademark and style includes long, accurate shots of real painterly compositions, disorted field of view, zooms and use of wide angle lenses...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oNLxLidA1BOuZ7OyQcQXWKcl4E0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/107762"}}, {tmdbId:"41788", properties:{bornIn:"Nancy, France", imdbId:"0679928", born:date('1951-01-10'), name:"Nicolas Philibert", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia  \n\n  Nicolas Philibert (born 10 January 1951) is a French film director and actor.  He has directed nine films since 1978.  His film Être et avoir was screened out of competition at the 2002 Cannes Film Festival.   \n\n  Description above from the Wikipedia article Nicolas Philibert, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aodMGAb8kZzOFPT8Ems7vy37Kq4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41788"}}, {tmdbId:"52609", properties:{bornIn:"California,USA", imdbId:"0252135", born:date('1970-12-24'), name:"Breck Eisner", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMichael \"Breck\" Eisner (born December 24, 1970) is an American television and film director. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Breck Eisner, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/52609"}}, {tmdbId:"15602", properties:{bornIn:"Madrid, Spain", imdbId:"0508208", born:date('1968-05-26'), name:"Fernando León de Aranoa", bio:"Fernando León de Aranoa (May 26, 1968, Madrid) is an award-winning Spanish screenwriter and film director...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hscFcZHgyZ7BxPdOWnhmeMr6BQF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15602"}}, {tmdbId:"3950", properties:{bornIn:"Fremont, California, USA", imdbId:"0936482", born:date('1973-03-04'), name:"Len Wiseman", bio:"Len Ryan Wiseman (born March 4, 1973) is an American director and screenwriter who directed the Underworld series of vampire films and Live Free or Die Hard. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Len Wiseman, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3950"}}, {tmdbId:"62116", properties:{bornIn:"Denver, Colorado, United States", imdbId:"0937306", name:"Bille Woodruff", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nBille Woodruff is a music video and film director, noted for directing many videos for a number of R&B and hip-hop artists since the mid-1990s.  These artists include Joe, for whom Woodruff has directed nine music videos since 1994, and Toni Braxton, whom he has worked 6 times since 1996.  Woodruff directed the videos for some of Braxton's biggest singles, including \"Un-Break My Heart\"...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/62116"}}, {tmdbId:"56578", properties:{bornIn:"US", imdbId:"0871860", born:date('1966-09-04'), name:"Jeff Tremaine", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJeffery James \"Jeff\" Tremaine (born September 4, 1966) is an American film and television producer/director, and, along with Johnny Knoxville and Spike Jonze, one of the creators of MTV's Jackass.  He directed Jackass: The Movie, Jackass Number Two, Jackass 3D, and Jackass spinoff Wildboyz.  Tremaine is the former editor of Big Brother Magazine and a former art director of the influential BMX magazine GO as well as a former professional BMX rider...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hyoxbPPPRQESo96cjktGujXbLhL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56578"}}, {tmdbId:"74142", properties:{imdbId:"1246888", name:" Roger Gould", bio:"Roger Gould is known for his work on Up (2009), Brave (2012) and Monsters University (2013).  Formerly Head of the Animated Short Films Department at Pixar Animation Studios.  Now Creative Director of Pixar's Theme Parks group working on Pixar inspired attractions at Disney Theme Parks worldwide...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74142"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"1214860", properties:{imdbId:"0579318", name:"Linda Mendoza", bio:"Linda Mendoza is American film and television director.  Mendoza's directorial career began in 1992, directing promotional segments for Fox and MTV.  She then went on to direct sketches for the Nickelodeon sketch comedy series' Roundhouse and All That.  Her other television series credits include, The Chris Rock Show, The Brothers García, Unfabulous, Girlfriends, The Bernie Mac Show, MADtv, Scrubs, Gilmore Girls and among other series...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1214860"}}, {tmdbId:"69646", properties:{bornIn:"Molkom, Värmlands län, Sweden", imdbId:"0540297", born:date('1965-03-16'), name:"Ulf Malmros", bio:"Ulf Malmros is a Swedish screenwriter and film director...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/m24viAODeOG5Nzobaz5gGmyjOOt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/69646"}}, {tmdbId:"1081892", properties:{imdbId:"1195672", name:"Mark Moskowitz", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1081892"}}, {tmdbId:"29922", properties:{bornIn:"Frankfurt am Main, Hesse, West Germany", imdbId:"1197971", born:date('1963-05-26'), name:"Marcus Nispel", bio:"Marcus Nispel (born May 26, 1963) is a German feature film director as well as producer and a director of television commercials and music videos.  Many of his films have been remakes and contain extreme graphic violence...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gKvwpCr23UxQIuS4yJZhTvHLN0C.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/29922"}}, {tmdbId:"74152", properties:{bornIn:"Lower Hutt, Wellington, New Zealand", imdbId:"0420422", born:date('1963-01-29'), name:"Christine Jeffs", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nChristine Jeffs (born 1963) is a New Zealand born film director known for directing the British motion picture Sylvia, starring Gwyneth Paltrow and Daniel Craig, and the American independent film Sunshine Cleaning (2009), starring Amy Adams and Emily Blunt. \n\nJeffs is also the director and screenwriter of the New Zealand film Rain (2001). \n\nJeffs lives in Auckland with her partner John Toon, cinematographer of Sunshine Cleaning and her other films...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74152"}}, {tmdbId:"21905", properties:{bornIn:"Hong Kong, China", imdbId:"0659380", born:date('1965-01-01'), name:"Danny Pang", bio:"Danny Pang is a Chinese film director, writer and editor who often works with his twin brother Oxide Chun Pang...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/A7jZ7cjEdWufEwN5Eh7CiIknLX7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21905"}}, {tmdbId:"31033", properties:{bornIn:"Hong Kong, China", imdbId:"0161152", born:date('1965-11-11'), name:" Oxide Chun Pang", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nThe Pang Brothers are Danny Pang Fat and Oxide Pang Chun, twin-brother screenwriters and film directors, born in 1965 in Hong Kong.  Among their films is the hit Asian horror film, The Eye, which has spawned two sequels, as well as a Hollywood remake and a Hindi remake.  Besides working in Hong Kong, the pair frequently work in the Thai film industry, where they made their directorial debut as a team, Bangkok Dangerous...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31033"}}, {tmdbId:"52845", properties:{bornIn:"Monroe, Louisiane.", imdbId:"0456732", born:date('1964-12-14'), name:" Karey Kirkpatrick", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nKarey Kirkpatrick (born c.  1965) is a screenwriter.  His films include James and the Giant Peach, Chicken Run, The Spiderwick Chronicles, Charlotte's Web and The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy adaptation.  He directed Imagine That starring Eddie Murphy as well as Over the Hedge with Tim Johnson. \n\nKirkpatrick attended the University of Southern California School of Cinematic Arts, graduating in 1988...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/52845"}}, {tmdbId:"116805", properties:{bornIn:"Royal Oak, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"0270552", born:date('1962-09-17'), name:"Paul Feig", bio:"Paul S.  Feig is an American director, actor and author.  Feig is known for playing Mr.  Eugene Pool, Sabrina's science teacher, on the first season of Sabrina, the Teenage Witch.  Feig also created the critically acclaimed show, Freaks and Geeks and has directed a several episodes of The Office and Arrested Development; plus select episodes of 30 Rock, Parks and Recreation, Mad Men and other television series...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jQQr4Poxd5Lvs0mm8mPTJ98KMD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/116805"}}, {tmdbId:"592702", properties:{imdbId:"0876726", born:date('1960-07-01'), name:"Hannu Tuomainen", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/592702"}}, {tmdbId:"20023", properties:{bornIn:"Alexandria, Egypt", imdbId:"0149631", born:date('1926-01-25'), name:"Youssef Chahine", bio:"Youssef Chahine (Arabic: يوسف شاهين‎; 25 January 1926 – 27 July 2008) was an Egyptian film director, of Lebanese origin.  He was active in the Egyptian film industry from 1950 until his death.  A winner of the Cannes 50th Anniversary Award (for lifetime achievement), Chahine was credited with launching the career of actor Omar Sharif...", died:date('2008-07-27'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/eISYmf4YgY39B6ss0jbwwi2gJhz.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20023"}}, {tmdbId:"20024", properties:{bornIn:"Haifa, Israele", imdbId:"0321159", born:date('1950-10-11'), name:" Amos Gitai", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAmos Gitai (born 11 October 1950 in Haifa, Israel) is an Israeli film director. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Amos Gitai, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/rzeDnQ8JSnshvhmM9hzk955Wg9R.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20024"}}, {tmdbId:"223", properties:{bornIn:"Mexico City, Distrito Federal, Mexico", imdbId:"0327944", born:date('1963-08-15'), name:" Alejandro González Iñárritu", bio:"Alejandro González Iñárritu (American Spanish: [aleˈxandɾo gonˈsales iˈɲaritu]; credited since 2014 as Alejandro G.  Iñárritu; born August 15, 1963) is a Mexican film director, producer and screenwriter.  He is the first Mexican director to be nominated for the Academy Award for Best Director and the Directors Guild of America Award for Outstanding Directing, for Babel (2007)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qWrltG9e0ssM3Y9pF86EAgteKHu.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/223"}}, {tmdbId:"20025", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Tokyo Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"0408076", born:date('1926-09-15'), name:" Shôhei Imamura", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nShōhei Imamura (Tokyo, 15 September 1926 – 30 May 2006) was a Japanese film director.  Imamura was the first Japanese director to win two Palme d'Or awards, but was never Oscar nominated for any category. \n\nHis eldest son Daisuke Tengan is also a script writer and film director, and worked on the screenplays to Imamura's films The Eel (1997), Dr.  Akagi (1998), Warm Water Under a Red Bridge (2001) and 11'9\"01 September 11 (2002)...", died:date('2006-05-30'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/a5KwTfuni2tVdjed3ihfJKrci5d.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20025"}}, {tmdbId:"16862", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0500988", born:date('1937-10-30'), name:" Claude Lelouch", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nClaude Barruck Joseph Lelouch (born 30 October 1937) is a French film director, writer, cinematographer, actor and producer. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Claude Lelouch, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/d7s7Ifc2JS0Hzm31YAgVtK5vuKc.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16862"}}, {tmdbId:"20026", properties:{bornIn:"Téhéran, Iran", imdbId:"0538533", born:date('1980-02-15'), name:" Samira Makhmalbaf", bio:"Samira Makhmalbaf (born February 15, 1980) is an internationally acclaimed Iranian filmmaker and script writer.  She is the daughter of Mohsen Makhmalbaf, the film director and writer.  She is considered to be one of the most influential directors as part of the Iranian New Wave...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nsnrt6MU7yBrDOjVJRIyWjaYzuG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20026"}}, {tmdbId:"20027", properties:{bornIn:"Banfora, Upper Volta [now Burkina Faso]", imdbId:"0653458", born:date('1954-01-21'), name:" Idrissa Ouedraogo", bio:"Idrissa Ouédraogo was born in Banfora, Upper Volta (now Burkina Faso), in 1954.  He grew up in the town of Ouahigouya in the northern region of his homeland, and in 1976 he was awarded a Bachelor of Arts degree.  To ensure a better life his farmer parents sent him to Ouagadougou for further education, where he attended the African Institute for Cinema Studies (Institut Africain d’Etudes Cinématographiques) completing his studies in 1981 with a masters...", died:date('2018-05-01'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/p3qqjBuh1mzC1dgNoyPxS4bH3j.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20027"}}, {tmdbId:"56338", properties:{imdbId:"1002475", name:" Andrew R. Jones", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cyJNjj7zg0vgExOdeR8IQ50FTco.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56338"}}, {tmdbId:"56340", properties:{bornIn:"Kaminoyama, Prefettura di Yamagata, Giappone", imdbId:"1238086", born:date('1968-01-26'), name:" Takeshi Koike", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56340"}}, {tmdbId:"56341", properties:{bornIn:"Yonago, Tottori, Japan", imdbId:"0535340", born:date('1963-03-14'), name:" Mahiro Maeda", bio:"Mahiro Maeda (前田 真宏 Maeda Mahiro) born March 14, 1963 is one of the most prominent Japanese anime creators working today, having worked as director, character designer, and animator for many of Japan's top series.  Helen McCarthy in 500 Essential Anime Movies called him \"one of the most imaginative visualists in anime\".  He also worked on Concept Art and Design for Mad Max: Fury Road (2015), which won six Academy Awards...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56341"}}] AS row
