UNWIND [{tmdbId:"81809", properties:{imdbId:"0523276", name:"Declan Lowney", bio:"Declan Lowney (born 1960) is an Irish director, known for his work in television and film.  Among his work, he's directed shows by Penn & Teller, Father Ted, Alan Partridge: Alpha Papa, and Red Dwarf commercials for the AA...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81809"}}, {tmdbId:"2036", properties:{bornIn:"London, England", imdbId:"0307497", born:date('1970-05-26'), name:"Alex Garland", bio:"Alexander \"Alex\" Medawar Garland is an English novelist, screenwriter, producer and director, known for his work as the screenwriter of 28 Days Later (2002) and as the writer and director of Ex Machina (2014) and Annihilation (2018).  He also wrote and directed all eight episodes of his television debut, Devs (2019)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iMHWxkJf7n8GK9M8HUb0E7OUUvK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2036"}}, {tmdbId:"53216", properties:{imdbId:"1401752", name:"Dwayne Carey-Hill", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDwayne Carey-Hill is an American animation director, currently working on the Comedy Central series Drawn Together.  Prior to Drawn Together, he worked on Futurama, as Susie Dietter's assistant director and then promoted to a director and directed the episode \"Obsoletely Fabulous\".  He also worked for Sit Down, Shut Up, an animated remake of the 2003 Australian show of the same name...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53216"}}, {tmdbId:"114722", properties:{bornIn:"Kyoto Prefecture - Japan", imdbId:"0960025", born:date('1965-11-14'), name:"Kentarô Ohtani", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/j04gUgb797bmceqQZviO7Fvy0OU.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/114722"}}, {tmdbId:"53525", properties:{bornIn:"Toronto, Canada", imdbId:"0657372", name:"Mark Palansky", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53525"}}, {tmdbId:"53935", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"1996918", born:date('1965-07-26'), name:"Dito Montiel", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nDito Montiel, born as Orlandito Montiel, (July 26, 1965) is an American author, screenwriter, director and musician. \n\nBorn in New York City, he came into the public eye after the breakup of his hardcore punk band Major Conflict.  Later, Montiel would gain notoriety in 1989 when Geffen Records signed his newly formed outfit Gutterboy to a $1 million record deal – an unheard of sum at the time...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53935"}}, {tmdbId:"47786", properties:{bornIn:"Tbilisi, Georgia SSR, USSR", imdbId:"1201875", born:date('1979-01-01'), name:"Géla Babluani", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/j1ANdmAtoAwhBF0FEP7i1q2AAMx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/47786"}}, {tmdbId:"84618", properties:{imdbId:"1076716", name:"Tom Gustafson", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/84618"}}, {tmdbId:"61087", properties:{imdbId:"0946327", name:"Mennan Yapo", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/61087"}}, {tmdbId:"74272", properties:{bornIn:"Zagreb, Croatia", imdbId:"1058247", name:"Goran Dukic", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nGoran Dukić is a Croatian film director, screenwriter and actor best known for writing and directing the 2006 film Wristcutters: A Love Story. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Goran Dukić, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74272"}}, {tmdbId:"116803", properties:{imdbId:"0494938", born:date('1952-04-20'), name:"David Leaf", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDavid Leaf (born April 20, 1952) is an American writer, producer and director known for documentaries, music programs and pop culture retrospectives.  Among his best known documentaries are The Night James Brown Saved Boston (2008), The U. S.  vs.  John Lennon (2006) and Beautiful Dreamer: Brian Wilson and the Story of SMiLE (2004).  He also wrote the landmark Brian Wilson biography The Beach Boys and The California Myth (1978)...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/116803"}}, {tmdbId:"226095", properties:{imdbId:"0526794", name:"Lian Lunson", bio:"Lian Lunson is an Australian actress who became an award-winning documentary filmmaker.  She has also written a novel. \n\nShe was born in Ned Kelly Country in Australia.  She moved to Los Angeles in 1987 after working as an actress in Australia. \n\nHer production company is based in LA and is called Horse Pictures. \n\nShe made a documentary in 1997 about Willie Nelson for the TV channel PBS. \n\nShe also made a documentary about the poet and singer / songwriter Leonard Cohen, called...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bupjrp5xCzOOSyq2SgDnh97zlHs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/226095"}}, {tmdbId:"84110", properties:{bornIn:"Toronto, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0242757", name:"Sam Dunn", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Sam Dunn is a Canadian anthropologist and film-maker whose work focuses on the culture of heavy metal.  Together with Scot McFadyen, Dunn owns Toronto-based production company Banger Films, Inc. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Sam Dunn, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/84110"}}, {tmdbId:"84111", properties:{bornIn:"Toronto, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"1083864", name:" Scot McFadyen", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \"Scot McFadyen\" is a Canadian director, producer and music supervisor whose work focuses on the culture of heavy metal.  Together with Sam Dunn, McFadyen owns Toronto-based production company Banger Films, Inc. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Scot McFadyen, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/84111"}}, {tmdbId:"1172541", properties:{imdbId:"1737383", name:" Jessica Joy Wise", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1172541"}}, {tmdbId:"229182", properties:{imdbId:"1411980", name:"Andrew Leman", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/229182"}}, {tmdbId:"59362", properties:{imdbId:"1285750", name:" Andrew Jimenez", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/59362"}}, {tmdbId:"20193", properties:{bornIn:"Watertown, New York, USA", imdbId:"0004410", born:date('1973-05-11'), name:"Mark Neveldine", bio:"Mark Neveldine is an American film director, film producer, screenwriter and camera operator.  He is best known for frequently collaborating with Brian Taylor as Neveldine/Taylor...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20193"}}, {tmdbId:"31119", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"1234893", born:date('1971-12-21'), name:"Sylvain White", bio:"Sylvain White (born December 21, 1971) is a film and television director...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8n84QfPuQCvMaOPXNOOcK1ehhOC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31119"}}, {tmdbId:"94261", properties:{imdbId:"0549090", name:"Russell P. Marleau", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94261"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"68843", properties:{imdbId:"1375358", born:date('1977-11-15'), name:"Jon Hurwitz", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJonathan Benjamin \"Jon\" Hurwitz (born November 15, 1977) is an American screenwriter.  He is a graduate of the Wharton School at the University of Pennsylvania as well as an alumnus of Randolph High School. \n\nJon Hurwitz, with Hayden Schlossberg, wrote Harold &amp; Kumar Go to White Castle and wrote/directed Harold &amp; Kumar Escape from Guantanamo Bay...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/68843"}}, {tmdbId:"68844", properties:{bornIn:"Livingston, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"1376383", born:date('1978-06-09'), name:" Hayden Schlossberg", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nHayden Schlossberg (born June 9, 1978) is an American screenwriter/director/producer from Randolph, New Jersey who became well known for co-writing with Jon Hurwitz: Harold &amp; Kumar Go to White Castle, and for co-writing, co-directing, and co-producing with him \"Harold and Kumar Escape from Guantanamo Bay. \"\n\nHe is a 2000 honors graduate of the University of Chicago as well as a graduate of Randolph High School...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/68844"}}, {tmdbId:"51116", properties:{bornIn:"Tunisia", imdbId:"0759270", born:date('1964-11-08'), name:"Pierre Salvadori", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nPierre Salvadori (born 8 November 1964, Tunisia) is a French Corsican film director from Santo-Pietro-di-Venaco known for works on romantic comedies such as Hors de prix (2006). \n\nIn 1989 he wrote his first screenplay, which would then become the hit film Cible émouvante (Wild Target), which he directed in 1993...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/czK3ryuYG3ukbD3Ik58vmd1egc2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/51116"}}, {tmdbId:"68167", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0146049", name:"Gil Cates Jr.", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/68167"}}, {tmdbId:"83923", properties:{imdbId:"1159782", name:"Seiji Mizushima", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83923"}}, {tmdbId:"107490", properties:{bornIn:"Ixelles, Brabant, Belgium", imdbId:"0233757", born:date('1957-02-09'), name:"Jaco Van Dormael", bio:"Jaco Van Dormael was born on February 9, 1957 in Ixelles, Brabant, Belgium.  He is a director and writer...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/107490"}}, {tmdbId:"19003", properties:{imdbId:"1823216", name:"Heidi Ewing", bio:"Heidi Ewing is a director, producer, and writer of documentary films.  She and Rachel Grady founded Loki Films in 2001, and have collaborated on several documentaries together.  Detropia won two awards, Outstanding Direction and Outstanding Original Score, at the 2013 Cinema Eye Honors for Nonfiction Filmmaking. \n\nEwing is a native of Farmington Hills, Michigan, and is a graduate of Mercy High School and the Georgetown School of Foreign Service...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19003"}}, {tmdbId:"19006", properties:{imdbId:"1823227", name:" Rachel Grady", bio:"Rachel Grady is a film director involved in producing the documentary films Jesus Camp, Boys of Baraka, and 12th and Delaware.  She is the stepdaughter of James Grady. \n\nJesus Camp was coproduced and filmed by Grady in 2005 and debuted at the 2006 Tribeca Film Festival, it was nominated for Best Documentary Feature at the 79th Academy Awards.  She coproduced and filmed 12th & Delaware.  The film premiered on January 24, 2010 at the 2010 Sundance Film Festival in the U. S.  Documentary Competition...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19006"}}, {tmdbId:"59848", properties:{bornIn:"St Germain en Laye, France", imdbId:"1125131", born:date('1971-04-04'), name:"Jean-Baptiste Andrea", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJean-Baptiste Andrea grew up in Cannes, France.  He started making short films, and later moved to Paris.  He graduated from college with a degree in economics and political science, but funded most of his projects by translating books.  In Paris, he met Fabrice Canepa, and the two of them began writing films together.  Together, they wrote and directed Dead End...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ysCv5cEhg4r592pkrVfW318I7bl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/59848"}}, {tmdbId:"74623", properties:{imdbId:"1381100", born:date('1976-03-16'), name:"Kyle Newman", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74623"}}, {tmdbId:"77658", properties:{imdbId:"0403038", name:"Simon Hunter", bio:"Feature film and commercials director Simon Hunter grew up in  Scotland...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1z5Dy3g2Hh8H5U85mBrBVaISNGm.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77658"}}, {tmdbId:"1224522", properties:{imdbId:"0544055", name:"Henriette Mantel", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/l4je9YondpATFPTeE0Of2HSILCp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1224522"}}, {tmdbId:"116330", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0187091", born:date('1967-05-01'), name:"Patrick Creadon", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nPatrick Creadon (born May 1, 1967) is an American documentary filmmaker, best known for the documentary film Wordplay.  A profile of New York Times crossword editor Will Shortz, Wordplay premiered at the 2006 Sundance Film Festival and became the second-highest grossing documentary of that year.  His second film, I. O. U. S. A...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/116330"}}, {tmdbId:"112588", properties:{bornIn:"Phoenix, Arizona, U.S.", imdbId:"0225269", born:date('1952-08-23'), name:"Kirby Dick", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nKirby Dick (born August 23, 1952) is an American film director, producer, screenwriter, and editor.  He is best known for directing documentary films.  He received an Academy Award nomination for Best Documentary Feature for directing Twist of Faith (2005).  He has also received numerous awards from film festivals, including the Sundance Film Festival and Los Angeles Film Festival...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/112588"}}, {tmdbId:"65190", properties:{imdbId:"0041161", name:"Philip G. Atwell", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPhilip G.  Atwell (often misspelled Phillip G.  Atwell) is an American music video, television commercial and feature film director.  Starting out as a music video producer, he took up directing in 1999.  Often co-directing with Dr.  Dre, he has helmed many music videos for Eminem and other hip hop artists. \n\nIn 2000 Atwell directed and executive-produced the concert documentary The Up in Smoke Tour...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/65190"}}, {tmdbId:"80172", properties:{bornIn:"Cincinnati, Ohio, USA", imdbId:"0130549", name:"Marty Callner", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMarty Callner is a director.  His primary work is with music videos.  Marty has directed work from such popular artists as Cher, The Rolling Stones and Aerosmith and has work recorded back as far as 1977 and as recent as 2009.  He has been nominated for 7 Emmys, 3 DGAs, and 1 CableACE Award.  His son is writer/actor Dax Callner. Callner directed Bette Midler's HBO concert special Diva Las Vegas which first aired in 1997.  Diva Las Vegas is now available on DVD...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80172"}}, {tmdbId:"6037", properties:{bornIn:"Waukegan, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0833779", born:date('1976-11-08'), name:"Colin Strause", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nBrothers Greg and Colin Strause (self-titled as Brothers Strause) are a directing duo, most famous for directing Aliens vs.  Predator: Requiem and Skyline, and special effects artists who make movies and grew up in Waukegan, Illinois.  They are the founders of Hydraulx, a special effects company. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Brothers Strause , licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6037"}}, {tmdbId:"6038", properties:{bornIn:"Waukegan, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0833780", born:date('1975-01-16'), name:" Greg Strause", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nBrothers Greg and Colin Strause (self-titled as Brothers Strause) are a directing duo, most famous for directing Aliens vs.  Predator: Requiem and Skyline, and special effects artists who make movies and grew up in Waukegan, Illinois.  They are the founders of Hydraulx, a special effects company. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Brothers Strause , licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6038"}}, {tmdbId:"46366", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo, Japan", imdbId:"0437526", born:date('1955-06-08'), name:"Shûsuke Kaneko", bio:"Shusuke Kaneko (born June 8, 1955) is a Japanese filmmaker and screenwriter. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Shusuke Kaneko, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vKJ3GFuYBeVBFaNdSq42RPkDxWT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/46366"}}, {tmdbId:"566328", properties:{bornIn:"USA", imdbId:"1302591", born:date('1973-02-14'), name:"Michael Sucsy", bio:"After earning a Masters of Fine Arts in film from the prestigious Art Center College of Design, Sucsy began directing commercials exclusively through Los Angeles-based Palomar Pictures.  \n\nDubbed by Shoot! Magazine as one of the industry's crop of new directors to watch, he was subsequently nominated for the Young Director of the Year Award given in conjunction with the 2002 Cannes Lions International Advertising Festival...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xl0XLatHCU8gqzSFJdM8W8vLByV.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/566328"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"19983", properties:{bornIn:"Planegg, Germany", imdbId:"0304921", born:date('1948-02-13'), name:"Sam Garbarski", bio:"Sam Garbarski was born in 1948 in Planegg, Bavaria, Germany.  He is a director and writer, known for Vijay and I (2013), Quartier lointain (2010) and Irina Palm (2007)...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19983"}}, {tmdbId:"115893", properties:{bornIn:"New York, New York, USA", imdbId:"0625747", born:date('1955-07-07'), name:"Stanley Nelson", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/lRYyHCFY0U2RlMVJ7OpPYmkHMvA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/115893"}}, {tmdbId:"566275", properties:{imdbId:"1736575", name:"Aram Rappaport", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/566275"}}, {tmdbId:"3028", properties:{bornIn:"Long Beach, California, U.S.", imdbId:"0262597", born:date('1946-09-19'), name:"Bruce A. Evans", bio:"Bruce Anslie Evans (born September 19, 1946) is an American film director, producer and screenwriter best known for his work on Stand by Me (1986), Jungle 2 Jungle (1996) and Mr.  Brooks (2007)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/h1NsYkWwIbJ6VBfoR32bBESdn8K.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3028"}}, {tmdbId:"57274", properties:{bornIn:"Khon Kaen, Thailand", imdbId:"1437277", born:date('1961-02-17'), name:" Panna Rittikrai", bio:"Panna Rittikrai (Thai: พันนา ฤทธิไกร; RTGS: Phanna Ritthikrai) or birth name Krittiya Lardphanna (Thai: กฤติยา ลาดพันนา;[1] RTGS: Krittiya Latphanna, February 17, 1961 – July 20, 2014) was a Thai martial arts action choreographer, film director, screenwriter, and actor.  The head of the Muay Thai Stunt team (previously known as P. P. N...", died:date('2014-07-20'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ztvTI56VNksjMB0i9AM8us2NLE9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57274"}}, {tmdbId:"1152981", properties:{imdbId:"0030253", born:date('1970-06-01'), name:"Graham Annable", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1152981"}}, {tmdbId:"62854", properties:{bornIn:" Berkeley, California, United States", imdbId:"1676223", born:date('1977-12-01'), name:"Akiva Schaffer", bio:"An American writer for Saturday Night Live, a film director, songwriter, and a member of The Lonely Island, a sketch-comedy troupe that first found success on the Internet, which includes SNL cast member Andy Samberg and SNL writer Jorma Taccone.  He majored in film at University of California, Santa Cruz. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Akiva Schaffer licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iGbjkd0fpjdbdtXukpNk1tyBof4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/62854"}}, {tmdbId:"93419", properties:{bornIn:"New York City - New York - USA", imdbId:"0769135", born:date('1949-02-17'), name:"Don Scardino", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nDon Scardino (born 17 February 1948) is an American television director and producer and a former actor. \n\nBorn in New York City, Scardino began his career as an actor.  His first Broadway credit was as an understudy in The Playroom in 1965.  Additional Broadway acting credits include Johnny No-Trump, Godspell, and King of Hearts...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3yGJ8GcYZLURUweqmYhC77QyA1K.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/93419"}}, {tmdbId:"95143", properties:{imdbId:"0460031", name:"Dan Klores", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95143"}}, {tmdbId:"34110", properties:{bornIn:"Israel", imdbId:"0610219", born:date('1966-07-04'), name:"Oren Moverman", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nOren Moverman (born July 4, 1966) is an Israeli filmmaker, screenwriter, and former journalist based in New York City. \n\nMoverman was the screenwriter and associate producer of Jesus' Son, a 2000 Lion’s Gate/Alliance Release.  Directed by Alison Maclean, the film stars Billy Crudup, Samantha Morton, Jack Black, Holly Hunter &amp; Dennis Hopper. \n\nMoverman served as screenwriter of Face, starring Bai Ling, Treach and Kristy Wu...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34110"}}, {tmdbId:"54559", properties:{bornIn:"Germany", imdbId:"0023355", born:date('1974-05-28'), name:"Christian Alvart", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nChristian Alvart (born May 28, 1974) is a German filmmaker and screenwriter.  Prior to working in the film business Christian Alvart worked in various positions, most recently as a senior editor at Filmmagzin X-TRO.  In 1999 he made his debut as a film director with the thriller Curiosity &amp; the Cat, for which he also wrote the screenplay.  His next film was the thriller Antibodies.  Pandorum was Alvart's first Hollywood movie...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54559"}}, {tmdbId:"71068", properties:{bornIn:"Bristol, Avon, England, UK", imdbId:"1630273", born:date('1957-06-17'), name:"Phyllida Lloyd", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dVGeuomp4NAr9LtkMLD0EViHFdd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71068"}}, {tmdbId:"437833", properties:{bornIn:"Guadalajara, Messico", imdbId:"0726638", born:date('1970-06-02'), name:"Patricia Riggen", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/437833"}}, {tmdbId:"52934", properties:{bornIn:"London, England", imdbId:"0831557", born:date('1976-03-19'), name:"Nicholas Stoller", bio:"Nicholas Stoller is an English–American screenwriter and director.  He is known mainly for directing the 2008 comedy Forgetting Sarah Marshall, and its 2010 spin-off/sequel, Get Him to the Greek...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/247iI9VZHnKB9QteCIUheKAAZtI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/52934"}}, {tmdbId:"58260", properties:{bornIn:"Berlin - Germany", imdbId:"1170286", born:date('1966-03-27'), name:"Martin Weisz", bio:"Martin Weisz is a German music video and film director.  He has directed over 350 music videos and worked with artists such as Nickelback, Brandy, Puff Daddy, and LL Cool J.  He has also directed numerous commercials.  Martin Weisz won an MTV European Video Award for Best Dance Video and was nominated for Best Rock Video in 2000. \n\nHe made his debut as a film director with the controversial 2006 film Rohtenburg (called Grimm Love in the United States)...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/58260"}}, {tmdbId:"589006", properties:{imdbId:"2253934", name:"Derek Sieg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/589006"}}, {tmdbId:"84335", properties:{bornIn:"Long Island, New York, U.S.", imdbId:"1362570", born:date('1950-01-01'), name:"Joe Lynch", bio:"Joe Lynch is an American film director, producer, and actor. \n\nLynch began his career as a child actor, however he soon became obsessed in filmmaking.  His first two student shorts, mAHARBA & hiBeams, were selected to screen at many film festivals.  He was named \"Filmmaker of the Year\" in 1999 by the Long Island Voice. \n\nLynch has directed music videos for such groups as DVDA, Pete Yorn, Strapping Young Lad, 311 and Godhead.  He was also one of the creators of the television show Uranium for Fuse TV...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/maeIOyMqToTT0XuWxO0Fy40lNzR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/84335"}}, {tmdbId:"94222", properties:{bornIn:"Barcelona - Catalonia - Spain", imdbId:"0665041", born:date('1978-07-25'), name:"David Pastor", bio:"David Pastor (1978 in Barcelona) is a spanish writer, producer and director known for Carriers (2009), The Last Days (2013), Eternal (2015) and The Occupant (2020). \n\nHis younger brother, Alex Pastor, is director and producer.  Usually they work together...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bswaVitByWWca3ewtoZGSXUF1qT.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94222"}}, {tmdbId:"94220", properties:{bornIn:"Barcelona, Spain", imdbId:"1883612", born:date('1981-03-13'), name:" Àlex Pastor", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yiZbtm5A0wkmRaIslijH6kmEl8s.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94220"}}, {tmdbId:"85150", properties:{imdbId:"0509633", born:date('1967-09-14'), name:"Jens Lien", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJens Lien (born 14 September 1967) is a Norwegian film director.  He graduated from the London International Film School in 1993.  His graduation project was the short film \"Montana\", that was featured at the short film festival in Grimstad that year.  in 1995 he again participated in this festival, with the entry \"Mitt elektriske kjøkken\" (My Electrical Kitchen)...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/85150"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"15435", properties:{imdbId:"0051157", name:" Randall Balsmeyer", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/15435"}}, {tmdbId:"55785", properties:{bornIn:"Sendai, Prefettura di Miyagi, Giappone", imdbId:"0412517", born:date('1963-01-24'), name:" Shunji Iwai", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/iRz0WnbUKP9qwKRRho6ObmZEoGy.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55785"}}, {tmdbId:"20709", properties:{bornIn:"La Rochelle, Francia", imdbId:"1749112", born:date('1970-01-01'), name:"Vincent Paronnaud", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nORoAfK0JGLXQKJBNBMGRgexsfL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20709"}}, {tmdbId:"109293", properties:{bornIn:"Vaslui, Romania", imdbId:"1717949", born:date('1975-09-14'), name:"Corneliu Porumboiu", bio:"Corneliu Porumboiu, born in 1975, Vaslui, Romania, became known in 2006 for his first feature, 12:08 EAST OF BUCHAREST, which won the Camera d'Or award at the Cannes Film Festival where it was shown in Directors' Fortnight.  His subsequent films confirmed his talent as a storyteller and director...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1wtcDmz5Q9jubiWzcBdXcsGeGdj.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/109293"}}, {tmdbId:"133090", properties:{bornIn:"Barcelona, Barcelona, Catalonia, Spain", imdbId:"0346360", name:"José Luis Guerín", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJosé Luis Guerín (born 1960) is a Spanish filmmaker and educator, known for his meditative  and intellectually curious  work in both documentary and narrative filmmaking...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fh4KuzugYjfjnx6rePnlEfhL0cl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/133090"}}, {tmdbId:"71527", properties:{imdbId:"0773605", name:"Marco Schnabel", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71527"}}, {tmdbId:"76249", properties:{bornIn:"Belgium", imdbId:"0607831", born:date('1966-01-01'), name:"Koen Mortier", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/76249"}}, {tmdbId:"25873", properties:{bornIn:"Malta - Europe", imdbId:"0143984", born:date('1958-04-27'), name:"Jon Cassar", bio:"Jon Cassar was born on April 27, 1958 in Malta.  He is a producer and director...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/25873"}}, {tmdbId:"111686", properties:{bornIn:"United Kingdom", imdbId:"1637768", born:date('1979-02-20'), name:"Jim Field Smith", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJim Field Smith (born 20 February 1979) is a British film director, comedy writer, and actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jim Field Smith, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/111686"}}, {tmdbId:"126945", properties:{bornIn:"Liverpool, Merseyside, England, UK", imdbId:"1093053", born:date('1962-01-01'), name:"Brian Percival", bio:"Brian Percival is a British film director, known for his work on the British television series Downton Abbey and North & South, as well as the feature film The Book Thief...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zx4ZfHNPNF0h22UN8QMgBBAmcXW.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/126945"}}, {tmdbId:"71609", properties:{bornIn:"Copenhagen, Denmark", imdbId:"1258686", born:date('1974-09-30'), name:"Joachim Trier", bio:"Joachim Trier (born 1974) is a Norwegian film director raised in Oslo, Norway.  His father Jacob Trier was the sound technician of Pinchcliffe Grand Prix, a notable film produced in Norway.  He is a distant relative to Danish director Lars von Trier. \n\nAs a teenager, he was a top skateboarder who began shooting and producing his own skateboarding videos...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9N4tq2bIccxiQwPh1UGBv1OMlA6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71609"}}, {tmdbId:"112201", properties:{imdbId:"0276400", name:"Sophie Fiennes", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/112201"}}, {tmdbId:"3964", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0851281", name:"Patrick Tatopoulos", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nPatrick Tatopoulos is a French-Greek production designer, who lives and works in the United States.  His designs have appeared in numerous motion pictures, including Pitch Black, Underworld, I, Robot, The Chronicles of Riddick, Independence Day, Bram Stoker's Dracula, Stargate, Spawn, Godzilla, Stuart Little, I Am Legend, 10,000 BC, and Live Free or Die Hard...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6tkcPHANqVx7sXTXKR8knw87h06.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3964"}}, {tmdbId:"150975", properties:{bornIn:"Seoul, South Korea", imdbId:"0393254", born:date('1961-10-25'), name:"Sang-soo Hong", bio:"Hong Sang-soo (born October 25, 1961) is a South Korean film director and screenwriter...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cjZT9zhN5Yl65vTYAoyxCE02rm4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/150975"}}, {tmdbId:"62342", properties:{bornIn:"Cambridge, England", imdbId:"0556573", name:"Adam Mason", bio:"Adam Mason was born in Cambridge in 1975.  He graduated from the London Film School, and immediately began his film career.  He directed and produced more than 90 music videos over the next seven years, as well as several award winning short films...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hFmm3xC6EV70Lg7Lnm6UINwUm6R.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/62342"}}, {tmdbId:"937777", properties:{bornIn:"Hildesheim, Germany", imdbId:"1190799", born:date('1974-07-07'), name:"Ingo Rasper", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/937777"}}, {tmdbId:"65702", properties:{imdbId:"0022768", name:"Kent Alterman", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nKent Alterman is an American film director and producer.  He made his directorial debut in 2008 with Semi-Pro starring Will Ferrell. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Kent Alterman, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/65702"}}, {tmdbId:"113500", properties:{bornIn:"München, Germany", imdbId:"0836715", born:date('1967-01-01'), name:"Philipp Stölzl", bio:"Philipp Stölzl (born 1967 in Munich) is a German film director, opera director and screenwriter.  He began to direct music videos in the mid 1990s and directed his first feature film in 2002. \n\nPhilipp Stölzl was trained as a set and costume designer at the Münchner Kammerspielen where he graduated in 1988.  He worked in these professions in German theatres and began to work for films in 1996.  He debuted as director in 1998 with the music video for Rammstein's \"Du riechst so gut\"...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/113500"}}, {tmdbId:"107446", properties:{bornIn:"Miami, Florida, USA", imdbId:"0520488", born:date('1975-07-12'), name:"Phil Lord", bio:"Phil Lord was born on July 12, 1975 in Miami, Florida, USA as Philip A.  Lord.  He is a director, producer, and writer, known for Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse, The Lego Movie, and Clone High...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2MagibFHZxky3FmMubyABUnf4lw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/107446"}}, {tmdbId:"155267", properties:{bornIn:"Everett, Washington, USA", imdbId:"0588087", born:date('1975-09-23'), name:" Christopher Miller", bio:"Christopher Miller was born on September 23, 1975 in Everett, Washington, USA as Christopher Robert Miller.  He is a producer and writer, known for The Lego Movie, 22 Jump Street and Cloudy with a Chance of Meatballs.  He graduated from Dartmouth College...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yfAmZ1uMuzv2DFLl9kjAHDnDdR0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/155267"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"229931", properties:{bornIn:"Isfahan, Iran", imdbId:"1410815", born:date('1972-05-07'), name:"Asghar Farhadi", bio:"Asghar Farhadi (اصغر فرهادی) was born in 1972 in Iran.  He became interested in cinema in his teenage years and started his filmmaking education by joining the Youth Cinema Society of Esfahan in 1986 where he made 8mm and 16mm short films.  Asghar Farhadi received his Bachelors in Theater from University of Tehran's School of Dramatic Arts in 1998 and his Masters in Stage Direction from Tarbiat Modarres University a few years later...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3jdWTO8hmpEOiJkwBX310koOuf6.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/229931"}}, {tmdbId:"77656", properties:{imdbId:"1216753", name:"Gary Hustwit", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nGary Hustwit is an independent filmmaker based in New York and London.  He has produced and directed a number of documentaries including the 2007 film Helvetica. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article [****] , licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/e1TJL7v06wbCCxQXokvIgkGReYJ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77656"}}, {tmdbId:"1074311", properties:{imdbId:"2360225", name:"Diane Crespo", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1074311"}}, {tmdbId:"227945", properties:{imdbId:"1516290", name:" Stefan C. Schaefer", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/227945"}}, {tmdbId:"126855", properties:{bornIn:"Moscow, USSR (Russia)", imdbId:"0526732", born:date('1949-07-12'), name:"Pavel Lungin", bio:"Pavel Semyonovich Lungin is a Russian film director.  He is sometimes credited as Pavel Loungine...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/126855"}}, {tmdbId:"81044", properties:{bornIn:"Saint-Cloud, Francia", imdbId:"2376614", born:date('1975-08-10'), name:"Alexandre Bustillo", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJulien Maury and Alexandre Bustillo are French filmmakers.  The two are known for working on their projects together, with both men co-directing and Bustillo writing the script.  They list their influences as Dario Argento, Roman Polanski, Clive Barker and John Carpenter.   Their first film was Inside, a controversial horror film about a pregnant woman stalked by a madwoman who wants her child for herself...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81044"}}, {tmdbId:"81045", properties:{imdbId:"2377660", name:" Julien Maury", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJulien Maury and Alexandre Bustillo are French filmmakers.  The two are known for working on their projects together, with both men co-directing and Bustillo writing the script.  They list their influences as Dario Argento, Roman Polanski, Clive Barker and John Carpenter.   Their first film was Inside, a controversial horror film about a pregnant woman stalked by a madwoman who wants her child for herself...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81045"}}, {tmdbId:"80949", properties:{bornIn:"Montréal, Québec, Canada", imdbId:"0875056", born:date('1967-07-03'), name:"Aristomenis Tsirbas", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAristomenis Tsirbas (born 1967, Montreal, Canada) is a film director, producer, writer, animator and visual effects animator.  He is well known for directing the award winning short films The Freak and Terra which was adapted into the 2007 feature film of the same name produced by MeniThings Productions and Snoot Entertainment. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Aristomenis Tsirbas, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/80949"}}, {tmdbId:"19852", properties:{bornIn:"Columbia, South Carolina, USA", imdbId:"0842523", born:date('1952-10-23'), name:"Robin Swicord", bio:"Robin Swicord (born 1952) is an American screenwriter and film director.  She wrote the screenplay for the film Memoirs of a Geisha, based on the novel of the same name by Arthur Golden.  Her other screenplay credits include Little Women, Practical Magic, Matilda, The Perez Family, and Shag. \n\nHer directorial debut was with the 1993 short film The Red Coat, for which she also wrote the screenplay...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19852"}}, {tmdbId:"52528", properties:{imdbId:"0603758", name:"Paulo Morelli", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/52528"}}, {tmdbId:"14172", properties:{imdbId:"0567112", name:"Michael McCullers", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMichael McCullers (born 1971) is an American comedy film screenwriter. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Michael McCullers, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/azfbf4fdJV09J4WeiUjwl55cVrb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/14172"}}, {tmdbId:"74655", properties:{bornIn:"Alexandria, Virginia, Stati Uniti", imdbId:"1099918", born:date('1976-06-10'), name:"Jeremy Saulnier", bio:"Jeremy Saulnier is an American film director, cinematographer and screenwriter, known for his movies Blue Ruin (2013), Green Room (2015) and Hold the Dark (2018)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tTvAWJQFg0uMTCpIb3QphrQQMZA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74655"}}, {tmdbId:"93047", properties:{bornIn:"Schenectady, New York, USA", imdbId:"0781733", born:date('1968-07-17'), name:"Joshua Seftel", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJoshua Seftel (born July 17, 1968) is an American filmmaker.  Born in Schenectady, New York, Seftel graduated from Tufts University in the class of 1990 as a pre-med and French literature major.  He currently lives in New York City and is represented by Creative Artists Agency in Los Angeles, California.  Seftel directed the feature film comedy War, Inc...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/93047"}}, {tmdbId:"59027", properties:{imdbId:"1275670", name:"Jeremy Garelick", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/59027"}}, {tmdbId:"588044", properties:{imdbId:"1390496", name:"Jaffar Mahmood", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/588044"}}, {tmdbId:"96323", properties:{imdbId:"1306443", name:"Marcel Sarmiento", bio:"Marcel Sarmiento is a film director and writer who has created both comedy and horror films.  He wrote and directed the 2007 comedy Heavy Petting, and co-directed the 2008 horror film Deadgirl with Gadi Harel.   Sarmiento contributed the 'D is for Dogfight' segment of The ABCs of Death, an anthology horror film.   Marcel has also written some screenplays and adaptations and wrote a chapter of the book, The Modern Con Man: How to Get Something for Nothing...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96323"}}, {tmdbId:"96324", properties:{imdbId:"0362847", name:" Gadi Harel", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96324"}}, {tmdbId:"562918", properties:{bornIn:"Toronto, Canada", imdbId:"2326979", name:"Larysa Kondracki", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/562918"}}, {tmdbId:"131122", properties:{imdbId:"1077590", name:"Isidro Ortiz", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/131122"}}, {tmdbId:"88556", properties:{bornIn:"Ireland", imdbId:"1137264", name:"Glenn McQuaid", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/88556"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"46588", properties:{imdbId:"0688361", name:"Bill Pohlad", bio:"Bill Pohlad is a director and feature film producer.  In 2009 Pohland launched a new motion picture distribution company called Apparition.  Pohlad co-founded the firm with veteran independent movie producer Bob Berney.  \n\nPohlad also owns a movie production company, River Road Entertainment, which has offices in Los Angeles and Minneapolis.  It produced several notable movies, including Brokeback Mountain, A Prairie Home Companion and Into the Wild...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/46588"}}, {tmdbId:"1692687", properties:{bornIn:"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands", imdbId:"0374048", born:date('1965-07-26'), name:"Matthijs van Heijningen Jr.", bio:"Matthijs van Heijningen Jr.  is a Dutch filmmaker, mostly working on commercials for big international brands such as Toyota, Pepsi and Renault.  He is the son of film producer Matthijs van Heijningen...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gWPNvAVh0lQXpUE7ozEp1V2Qj6k.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1692687"}}, {tmdbId:"93468", properties:{imdbId:"0140617", name:"Gareth Carrivick", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/93468"}}, {tmdbId:"1230368", properties:{bornIn:"Toronto - Ontario - Canada", imdbId:"0528508", born:date('1959-05-19'), name:"Laurie Lynd", bio:"Laurie Lynd  is a director and writer...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1230368"}}, {tmdbId:"1242435", properties:{imdbId:"0033773", name:"Patrick Archibald", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1242435"}}, {tmdbId:"105643", properties:{imdbId:"0646515", name:" Jay Oliva", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJay Oliva is an American storyboard artist, a film producer and animated film director working for Warner Brothers Animation. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia Jay Oliva licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/y7EbnuoKFMvU7uZ4aD50jThyNoF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/105643"}}, {tmdbId:"35269", properties:{imdbId:"0780922", name:" Dick Sebast", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRichard \"Dick\" Sebast is an American story director, animator and television producer known for working at companies such as Disney, Hanna-Barbera, MGM and Universal. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Dick Sebast, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/35269"}}, {tmdbId:"72101", properties:{bornIn:"Ginevra, Svizzera", imdbId:"1236625", born:date('1977-07-06'), name:"Martin Gero", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/72101"}}, {tmdbId:"45627", properties:{imdbId:"1879589", name:"Nelson McCormick", bio:"Nelson McCormick is an American director and producer for film and television...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kP4UNE4NKEWmWgc6VmUkTCC5bz3.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/45627"}}, {tmdbId:"71506", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"1462495", born:date('1971-03-25'), name:"Rémi Bezançon", bio:"Rémi Bezançon (born 25 March 1971) is a French director and screenwriter. \n\nRémi Bezançon studied at the Ecole Supérieure de Réalisation Audiovisuelle (ESRA) in Paris and the École du Louvre.  In 2005 he released his first feature film Ma vie en l'air before meeting with success in 2008 with The First Day of the Rest of Your Life.  In 2011, he directed Un heureux événement, adapted from the novel by Eliette Abécassis, with Louise Bourgoin, Pio Marmaï and Josiane Balasko...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vQtEg8yRvtwIztfpW8PmoFAIgPf.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71506"}}, {tmdbId:"106677", properties:{imdbId:"0764275", name:"Steven J. Santos", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/106677"}}, {tmdbId:"63973", properties:{bornIn:"Rome, Italy", imdbId:"0308520", born:date('1968-10-15'), name:"Matteo Garrone", bio:"Born in Rome in 1968, Matteo Garrone graduated from the Liceo Artistico in 1986.  In 1996 he won the Sacher Festival with the short film Silhouette.  The following year, with his own production company Archimede, he made his first feature film, Terra di Mezzo (Land in Between).  In the same year his second feature film, Ospiti (Guests) was presented at the Venice Film Festival.  His third feature film, Estate Romana (Roman Summer), was also shown at the Venice Film Festival...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/4QfjC6ELaFP2f3Ixo3JWEpcznr.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/63973"}}, {tmdbId:"81963", properties:{imdbId:"0995691", name:"Jonah Markowitz", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81963"}}, {tmdbId:"27745", properties:{bornIn:"Toronto, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0178338", born:date('1968-10-14'), name:"Robert C. Cooper", bio:"Robert C.  Cooper is a Canadian writer and producer best known for his work in the Stargate franchise.  He was formerly an executive producer of Stargate SG-1 and Stargate Atlantis until both series conclusion and currently holds the same title on the third Stargate series Stargate Universe.  He also co-created both Stargate Atlantis and Stargate Universe with Brad Wright...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27745"}}, {tmdbId:"66856", properties:{imdbId:"0412247", name:"Guillaume Ivernel", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/66856"}}, {tmdbId:"66857", properties:{imdbId:"0704588", born:date('1961-12-25'), name:" Arthur Qwak", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nArthur Qwak is a comic book author and director of French animated series born December 25, 1961...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/66857"}}, {tmdbId:"73547", properties:{imdbId:"1419617", name:"Bård Breien", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/73547"}}, {tmdbId:"51470", properties:{bornIn:"Ghent, Belgium", imdbId:"0051206", born:date('1964-07-24'), name:"Nic Balthazar", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nNic Balthazar (born 24 July 1964, Ghent) is a Belgian film director and a TV/radio personality (presenter, reporter, producer). \n\nHis first movie is Ben X. \n\nIn Flanders he is well known as a movie critic and television presenter.  To some extent he is also known as a positive vegetarian activist. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Nic Balthazar, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/51470"}}, {tmdbId:"76439", properties:{imdbId:"0329223", name:"Rosser Goodman", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/76439"}}, {tmdbId:"73588", properties:{imdbId:"0774340", name:"Marc Schölermann", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/73588"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"10757", properties:{bornIn:"Wellington, New Zealand", imdbId:"0001005", born:date('1954-04-30'), name:" Jane Campion", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJane Campion (born 30 April 1954) is a film maker and screenwriter.  She is one of the most internationally successful New Zealand directors, although most of her work has been made in or financed by other countries, principally Australia – where she now lives – and the United States.  Campion is the second of five women ever nominated for the Academy Award for Best Director...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kMhbtZ63q0VfgzYPN60wix63zTK.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10757"}}, {tmdbId:"20640", properties:{bornIn:"Beijing, China", imdbId:"0155280", born:date('1952-08-12'), name:" Kaige Chen", bio:"Chen Kaige (born August 12, 1952) is a Chinese film director and a leading figure of the fifth generation of Chinese cinema.  His films are known for their visual flair and epic storytelling...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7Ap9bUjDKwKMqtoza8W0PEYXoli.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20640"}}, {tmdbId:"56209", properties:{bornIn:"Liège, Belgium", imdbId:"0201094", born:date('1951-04-21'), name:" Jean-Pierre Dardenne", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ahSgr4Jb1xJc5stE1h4sDYckVPN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56209"}}, {tmdbId:"56836", properties:{bornIn:"Villefranche-sur-Saône", imdbId:"0220019", born:date('1942-07-06'), name:" Raymond Depardon", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56836"}}, {tmdbId:"16767", properties:{bornIn:"Orimattila, Finland", imdbId:"0442454", born:date('1957-04-04'), name:" Aki Kaurismäki", bio:"Aki Kaurismäki is a Finnish film writer, director, actor and producer.  Together with his older brother, filmmaker Mika Kaurismäki, he founded the production and distribution company Villealfa.  He's a graduate in Media Studies from the University of Tampere, Finland...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/kiJErWEOv4Ew7aHOGKg4ljsmppZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/16767"}}, {tmdbId:"121585", properties:{bornIn:"Puerto Montt, Chile", imdbId:"0749914", born:date('1941-07-25'), name:" Raoul Ruiz", bio:"Raúl Ernesto Ruiz Pino was an experimental Chilean filmmaker, writer and teacher whose work is best known in France.  He directed more than 100 films.  Ruiz spent some years at the Catholic University of Santa Fe, Argentina's cinema school.  Back in Chile, he directed his first feature film Tres Tristes Tigres in the late 1960s, winning the Golden Leopard at the Locarno Film Festival...", died:date('2011-08-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gsJkcICbmk1GCi3EkDkxE6qZcpe.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/121585"}}, {tmdbId:"131685", properties:{bornIn:"Nazareth, Israel", imdbId:"0837839", born:date('1960-07-28'), name:" Elia Suleiman", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gIy5QcL9ShxnHecTpCY699nm92A.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/131685"}}, {tmdbId:"71174", properties:{bornIn:"Kuching", imdbId:"0874633", born:date('1957-10-27'), name:" Ming-liang Tsai", bio:"Tsai Ming-liang (Chinese: 蔡明亮; pinyin: Cài Míngliàng) (born 27 October 1957) is a Malaysian-Taiwanese filmmaker.  He has written and directed 10 feature films and has also directed many short films and television films.  Tsai is one of the most celebrated \"Second New Wave\" film directors of Taiwanese cinema.  His films have been acclaimed worldwide and have won numerous film festival awards...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7un9C6VGcjveENYXQIqLPeP7YZx.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/71174"}}, {tmdbId:"2303", properties:{bornIn:"Düsseldorf, North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany", imdbId:"0000694", born:date('1945-08-14'), name:" Wim Wenders", bio:"Ernst Wilhelm \"Wim\" Wenders is a German film director, playwright, author, photographer and producer...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/AbqrYglSgaMfetQAeqdHaqiPSof.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2303"}}, {tmdbId:"12453", properties:{bornIn:"Shanghai, China", imdbId:"0939182", born:date('1956-07-17'), name:" Kar-wai Wong", bio:"Wong Kar-wai is a Hong Kong Second Wave filmmaker, internationally renowned as an auteur for his visually unique, highly stylized films.  Wong's films frequently feature protagonists who yearn for romance in the midst of a knowingly brief life and scenes that can often be described as sketchy, digressive, exhilarating, and containing vivid imagery...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zLngBAag9DSKtSAOWcfsFtEU3i5.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/12453"}}, {tmdbId:"26971", properties:{imdbId:"0909022", name:"Andrew Waller", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/26971"}}, {tmdbId:"27977", properties:{bornIn:"Suresnes, Hauts-de-Seine, Île-de-France, France", imdbId:"0136021", born:date('1960-11-22'), name:" Leos Carax", bio:"Leos Carax (born 22 November 1960) is a French-born film director, critic, and writer.  Carax is noted for his poetic style and his tortured depictions of love.  His first major work was Boy Meets Girl (1984), and his notable works include Lovers on the Bridge (1991) and the controversial Pola X (1999).  His professional name is an anagram of his first and middle names...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/88XIIn3LGljoBghXnTAPe7WBkxI.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27977"}}, {tmdbId:"201", properties:{bornIn:"Versailles, France", imdbId:"0327273", born:date('1963-05-08'), name:" Michel Gondry", bio:"Michel Gondry (born May 8, 1963) is a French film, commercial, and music video director and a screenwriter.  He is noted for his inventive visual style and manipulation of mise en scène...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1IAnVsl8JgHpUirBXpsbLlWyS1y.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/201"}}, {tmdbId:"53120", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0218621", born:date('1969-10-12'), name:"James DeMonaco", bio:"American screenwriter, director, and producer.  He is best known for creating the Purge franchise, writing all four films in the series and directing the first three, The Purge (2013), The Purge: Anarchy (2014), and The Purge: Election Year (2016)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/nH0LS98m3ZiAgIqROLYrr9H5DnD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/53120"}}, {tmdbId:"62795", properties:{imdbId:"0215534", name:"Adam Del Deo", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/62795"}}, {tmdbId:"74091", properties:{bornIn:"Nagano Prefecture, Japan", imdbId:"1396121", born:date('1973-02-09'), name:"Makoto Shinkai", bio:"Makoto Shinkai (born as Makoto Niitsu) is a Japanese anime director and animator.  He traces his passion for creation to the manga, anime, and novels he was exposed to while in middle school.  He is married to Mika Shinohara...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/6QSL2u9mvVbNTLOx08NjpK4AFGC.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74091"}}, {tmdbId:"61847", properties:{imdbId:"0542450", name:"Ethan Maniquis", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/61847"}}, {tmdbId:"6047", properties:{bornIn:"USA", imdbId:"0618680", name:"Jeffrey Nachmanoff", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJeffrey Nachmanoff is an American screenwriter and director.  He wrote the screenplay for the 2004 blockbuster film The Day After Tomorrow.  He wrote and directed Traitor, which was released on August 27, 2008. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jeffrey Nachmanoff, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vUpyTkNbPH83kOclKsbINopEkJ2.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6047"}}, {tmdbId:"137787", properties:{bornIn:"Kuressaare", imdbId:"0704664", born:date('1968-05-21'), name:"Ilmar Raag", bio:"Estonian film director, screenwriter, media executive and columnist Ilmar Raag was born in Kuressaare, Estonia.  He grew up in Kuressaare and also graduated high school there.  In 1997 he graduated University of Tartu and in 1999 he received M. A.  degree in screen writing from Ohio University.  In 1997 Raag made his directorial debut an amateur film Tappev Tartu (1998).  After that he find himself working in TV management and in 2002-2005 he served as CEO of Estonian National Television (ETV)...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/137787"}}, {tmdbId:"1030914", properties:{bornIn:"Iksan, South Korea", imdbId:"1276328", born:date('1971-01-01'), name:"Hee-il Leesong", bio:"Leesong Hee-il is a South Korean film director whose first feature film No Regret is regarded as \"the first real Korean gay feature. \" The film won him Best Independent Film Director at the 2006 Director's Cut Awards.  Leesong is openly gay...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hY5C9atZTM9jIdnpv0yWuJ3ny7p.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1030914"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"1260119", properties:{imdbId:"1010896", name:" Bonni Cohen", bio:"Bonni Cohen is a producer and director, known for The Rape of Europa (2006), National Geographic Explorer (1985) and Audrie & Daisy (2016)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wjujeUIHiNxN5cWJANVlmJEOJ3d.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1260119"}}, {tmdbId:"1028821", properties:{imdbId:"1011820", name:" Nicole Newnham", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1028821"}}, {tmdbId:"237517", properties:{imdbId:"0640337", name:"Geoffrey O'Connor", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/237517"}}, {tmdbId:"38023", properties:{bornIn:"Scranton - Pennsylvania - USA", imdbId:"0455078", born:date('1954-09-14'), name:"Michael Patrick King", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nMichael Patrick King (born September 14, 1954) is an American director, writer and producer for television shows...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/38023"}}, {tmdbId:"84113", properties:{imdbId:"0138706", name:"Charles Robert Carner", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/84113"}}, {tmdbId:"6508", properties:{imdbId:"0849164", name:" Loveleen Tandan", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLoveleen Tandan ( is an Indian film director and casting director.  She is known as the \"co-director: India\" of the four time Golden Globe, seven time BAFTA Award and eight Academy Award winning (including best picture) Slumdog Millionaire (2008), for which she shared a New York Film Critics Online Award for Best Director with Danny Boyle...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/znzDJnK8OCrvK23IP6Lu2C8ePox.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/6508"}}, {tmdbId:"77147", properties:{bornIn:"St. Paul, Minnesota, United States", imdbId:"0235719", name:"John Erick Dowdle", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJohn Erick Dowdle (born December 1973) is a U. S.  director, producer, screenwriter, and editor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article John Erick Dowdle, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/aNj1zjorMNAwtsHSv3mSFGeL5FX.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/77147"}}, {tmdbId:"44263", properties:{bornIn:"A Coruña, A Coruña, Galicia, Spain", imdbId:"1618276", born:date('1977-02-19'), name:"Luis Piedrahita", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nLuis Piedrahita Cuesta (born 1977 in Coruña, Spain) is a Spanish stand-up comedian, magician, script writer, broadcaster and author.  He is known as \"El Rey de las Cosas Pequeñas\" (\"The King of Small Things\"), due to his monologues in which he critiques the lack of regard of everyday things such as toilet lids, carnivorous plants, etc...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/edYQfvVgqxbUwqNz5BThkNXYzLR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/44263"}}, {tmdbId:"44264", properties:{imdbId:"1924019", name:" Rodrigo Sopeña", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/44264"}}, {tmdbId:"98521", properties:{bornIn:"Pescara, Italy", imdbId:"0797455", born:date('1965-01-01'), name:"Floria Sigismondi", bio:"​Canadian photographer and director Floria Sigismondi started her career as a fashion photographer.  She is best known for writing and directing The Runaways.  She came to directing music videos when she was approached by the production company The Revolver Film Co. , and directed music videos for a number of Canadian bands.  \n\nIn October 2004 she gave birth to a daughter, Tosca Vera Sigismondi-Berlin...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1WDa5FXRdGXYxVmhx2J7bl7ErKg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/98521"}}, {tmdbId:"64140", properties:{bornIn:"Tangier - Morocco", imdbId:"1065402", name:"Sanaa Hamri", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nSanaa Hamri is a Moroccan American music video and film director.  She is one of the few prominent female film and music video directors of color...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/64140"}}, {tmdbId:"131321", properties:{imdbId:"0050988", name:"Thomas Balmès", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/131321"}}, {tmdbId:"56194", properties:{bornIn:"Naples, Campania, Italy", imdbId:"0815204", born:date('1970-05-31'), name:"Paolo Sorrentino", bio:"Paolo Sorrentino is an Italian film director and screenwriter.  His 2013 film The Great Beauty (La Grande Bellezza) won the Oscar for Best Foreign Language Film in the 2014 Academy Awards...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7vZePzIFzNpqA50tozjJG2i0LDH.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56194"}}, {tmdbId:"59611", properties:{bornIn:"France", imdbId:"1052791", born:date('1971-10-16'), name:"Pascal Laugier", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/so3HYrCTW3h9s6WPC78Yv1OuueZ.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/59611"}}, {tmdbId:"20657", properties:{bornIn:"Iasi, Romania", imdbId:"0612816", born:date('1968-04-27'), name:"Cristian Mungiu", bio:"Cristian Mungiu (b.  1968, Iaşi) is a Romanian filmmaker, winner of the Palme d'Or in 2007. \n\nAfter studying English literature at the University of Iaşi, he worked for a few years as a teacher and as a journalist.  After that, he enrolled at the University of Film in Bucharest to study film directing.  After graduating in 1998, Mungiu made several short films.  In 2002, he debuted with his first feature film, Occident...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3ECIvZzvUw4DOdQj797BsqH3bRb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/20657"}}, {tmdbId:"42412", properties:{imdbId:"0464115", name:"Eran Kolirin", bio:"Eran Kolirin is an Israeli screenwriter and film director.  His directorial debut is The Band's Visit (2007), winning eight Awards of the Israeli Film Academy and prizes at several international film festivals.  Kolirin himself won the Israeli Film Academy's awards for best director and best screenplay...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/jLDaQXWRrNOhNPIyLwd89Ow6cvl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/42412"}}, {tmdbId:"78725", properties:{imdbId:"0580982", name:"Agnès Merlet", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78725"}}, {tmdbId:"54525", properties:{bornIn:"Lleida, Lleida, Catalonia, Spain", imdbId:"0049371", born:date('1968-11-02'), name:"Jaume Balagueró", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJaume Balagueró i Bernat (born 2 November 1968 in Lleida, Spain), is a Catalan film director widely known for his horror films. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jaume Balagueró, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/l9kW5ftAXo7nuz8ArqMzeKJ453W.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54525"}}, {tmdbId:"56411", properties:{bornIn:"Stati Uniti d'America", imdbId:"0275629", born:date('1971-05-27'), name:"Glenn Ficarra", bio:"Glenn Ficarra is an American film and television writer, director and producer...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56411"}}, {tmdbId:"56412", properties:{bornIn:"Burien, Seattle, Washington, USA", imdbId:"0720135", born:date('1967-01-01'), name:" John Requa", bio:"John Requa is an American film and television writer, director and producer...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56412"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"114404", properties:{bornIn:"Hammersmith, London, England", imdbId:"0764601", born:date('1974-01-07'), name:"Miguel Sapochnik", bio:"Miguel Sapochnik is an English film and television director and former storyboard artist.  He is best known as the director of the feature Repo Men and HBO series Game of Thrones, as well as for his work on several other U. S.  television series (Awake, Fringe, House, Mind Games)...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/114404"}}, {tmdbId:"74052", properties:{imdbId:"0042796", name:"Peter Avanzino", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nPeter Avanzino is an American animation director.  He has directed several episodes of Futurama, and currently serves as supervising director on the 6th season of the series.  He has also directed episodes of Drawn Together, Duckman, The Wild Thornberrys, Sit Down, Shut Up, and The Ren and Stimpy Show.  He was also a storyboard artist on The Ren and Stimpy Show and the The Simpsons...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74052"}}, {tmdbId:"79272", properties:{imdbId:"0501281", born:date('1965-08-29'), name:"Ella Lemhagen", bio:"Ella Lemhagen studied directing at Dramatiska Institutet\n\n1989-92.  She made her debut as\n\na feature film director in 1996 with the highly praised Drömprinsen - filmen om\n\nEm/The Prince of Dreams, for which she also wrote the original screenplay.  Ella\n\nhas had great national and international success with her films.  Her 1999\n\nfeature Tsatsiki, morsan och polisen/Tsatsiki, Mum and the Policeman, is one of\n\nthe most popular contemporary Swedish children- and youth oriented films of all\n\ntime...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/79272"}}, {tmdbId:"17386", properties:{bornIn:"Melle, Deux-Sèvres, France", imdbId:"0134559", born:date('1961-06-15'), name:"Laurent Cantet", bio:"Laurent Cantet is a French director and writer.   In 2008 he won the Palm d'Or at the Cannes Film Festival for The Class...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/17386"}}, {tmdbId:"76936", properties:{bornIn:"Toyama, Japan", imdbId:"0847690", born:date('1955-12-04'), name:"Yôjirô Takita", bio:"Yōjirō Takita (滝田 洋二郎 Takita Yōjirō, born December 4, 1955) is a Japanese filmmaker. \n\nHis 2008 film Departures (おくりびと Okuribito) won the Best Foreign Language Film at the U. S.  81st Academy Awards, in an upset over the Israeli Animated documentary, Waltz with Bashir.  He also won the 2009 Japan Academy Prize for Director of the Year, among other accolades, for the film. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Yōjirō Takita, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/85Ask7tvPJkIPtihAUyS8yyZB6J.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/76936"}}, {tmdbId:"92743", properties:{imdbId:"1985821", name:"Jamin Winans", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/92743"}}, {tmdbId:"229962", properties:{imdbId:"0862211", name:" Mike Thurmeier", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/229962"}}, {tmdbId:"82511", properties:{bornIn:"New York, New York, USA", imdbId:"0323239", born:date('1978-01-01'), name:"Will Gluck", bio:"Will Gluck is an American film director, screenwriter and producer...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82511"}}, {tmdbId:"89154", properties:{bornIn:"Mysore, Karnataka, India", imdbId:"0222150", born:date('1973-04-03'), name:"Prabhudheva", bio:"Prabhu Deva is an Indian dance choreographer, film director, producer and actor, who has worked in Tamil, Telugu, Hindi, Malayalam and Kannada films.  In a career spanning twenty five years, he has performed and designed a wide range of dancing styles and has garnered two National Film Awards for Best Choreography...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/d6swsmuzdeWiwOHMQJjCudiuL0e.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89154"}}, {tmdbId:"57692", properties:{bornIn:"Brooklyn, New York, USA", imdbId:"0107366", name:"Neal Brennan", bio:"Neal Brennan (born 1973) is an American writer, stand-up comedian, director, and producer.  He is best known for co-creating the Comedy Central series Chappelle's Show. \n\nBrennan and Dave Chappelle met when both were aspiring stand-ups.  Through his older brother, an established stand up comedian and comedy writer Kevin Brennan, Brennan got a part-time job working as the doorman at Boston Comedy Club in New York City where Chappelle was a frequent performer...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mxhkJw0ZDdAIMsnljygMsLZ0dAS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57692"}}, {tmdbId:"10855", properties:{bornIn:"USA", imdbId:"0329755", born:date('1970-01-01'), name:"Chris Gorak", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nChris Gorak is a film director who started as an art director and production designer.  He has directed the 2006 film Right at Your Door and is directing the upcoming film The Darkest Hour. \n\nGorak attended Tulane University where he earned an architecture degree.  He changed his career to film and worked as art director for directors like David Fincher, the Coen brothers, and Terry Gilliam...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/10855"}}, {tmdbId:"130128", properties:{bornIn:"Copenhagen, Denmark", imdbId:"0255411", born:date('1966-03-14'), name:"Jonas Elmer", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJonas Elmer (born March 14, 1966 in Denmark) is a Danish film director, screenwriter and previously an actor.  In 1988 he was a production assistant at the set of Family Business, starring Sean Connery. \n\nElmer graduated in direction at the National Film School of Denmark in 1995.  His debut as a director came with the Danish film Let's Get Lost which won him a Robert and Bodil Award for Best Danish Film...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/130128"}}, {tmdbId:"134129", properties:{imdbId:"1534600", born:date('1971-07-22'), name:"Benny Boom", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nBenny Boom (born on July 22, 1971) is a music video director and current director of Gorilla Flix, Inc.  He trained at Temple University's School of Radio, Television, &amp; Film, and also served as a protégé of veteran director Little X and Hype Williams.  He has also directed music videos for Sean Paul, Nas, Amerie, Kelly Rowland, Monica, Keyshia Cole, Mario, Ciara, Cassidy, Lil' Kim, LL Cool J, Nelly, P.  Diddy, 50 Cent and many others...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/134129"}}, {tmdbId:"95407", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0484879", born:date('1969-09-24'), name:"Jeffery Scott Lando", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95407"}}, {tmdbId:"86270", properties:{bornIn:"USA", imdbId:"2676052", born:date('1974-05-03'), name:"Joseph Kosinski", bio:"Joseph Kosinski (born May 3, 1974) is an American television commercial and feature film director best known for his computer graphics and computer generated imagery work.  He made his big-screen directorial debut with the Disney Digital 3-D science fiction film Tron: Legacy, the sequel to the 1982 film Tron.  His previous work has primarily been with CGI related television commercials including the \"Starry Night\" commercial for Halo 3 and the award-winning \"Mad World\" commercial for Gears of War...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/8EIjP8ZP1BTXgZjn134luPlMWKN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/86270"}}, {tmdbId:"81159", properties:{imdbId:"0596668", name:"Christian Molina", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/87wy48vFbtjpT2Ifdu8T2rxreQb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/81159"}}, {tmdbId:"230339", properties:{bornIn:"Scarborough, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0840075", name:" Sudz Sutherland", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDavid \"Sudz\" Sutherland is a Canadian film director and screenwriter.  His credits include the films Doomstown, Love, Sex and Eating the Bones and Guns, as well as episodes of Da Kink in My Hair, Degrassi: The Next Generation, Wild Roses and Jozi-H.  He was one of the creators of the forthcoming Canadian television sitcom She's the Mayor, scheduled to debut in 2011...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/230339"}}, {tmdbId:"129097", properties:{bornIn:"Toronto, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0005616", name:" Aaron Woodley", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/129097"}}, {tmdbId:"76422", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, Stati Uniti", imdbId:"0006846", born:date('1968-02-20'), name:"Ric Roman Waugh", bio:"Ric Roman Waugh was born on February 20, 1968 in Los Angeles, California, USA.  He is known for his work on Felon (2008), Snitch (2013) and Shot Caller (2017)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/cu0MJd4exIgSLgaE0uwMDTFQcpA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/76422"}}, {tmdbId:"1048454", properties:{imdbId:"1182222", name:"Robert Barry Ptolemy", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1048454"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"139098", properties:{bornIn:"Lakewood, Colorado, USA", imdbId:"0161834", born:date('1974-01-23'), name:"Derek Cianfrance", bio:"Derek Cianfrance is an American film director, cinematographer, screenwriter and editor...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/o5V0NWEDBPAnKU4pDTZmd6KWW5f.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/139098"}}, {tmdbId:"107045", properties:{bornIn:"Obihiro, Japan", imdbId:"1622836", born:date('1967-09-01'), name:"Masahiro Andô", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/107045"}}, {tmdbId:"87257", properties:{bornIn:"Oakland, California, USA", imdbId:"1560977", born:date('1977-07-10'), name:"Cary Joji Fukunaga", bio:"Cary Joji Fukunaga is an American film director, writer, and cinematographer.  He is known for writing and directing the 2009 film \"Sin Nombre\", the 2011 film \"Jane Eyre\", and for directing and executive producing the first season of the HBO series \"True Detective\", for which he won the Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Directing for a Drama Series.  He has received acclaim for the 2015 war drama \"Beasts of No Nation\", in which Fukunaga was writer, director, producer, and cinematographer...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qhrtYCUM2NEaqVP3oB7vqkOTpx0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/87257"}}, {tmdbId:"108346", properties:{bornIn:"Tolosa, Francia", imdbId:"1754436", born:date('1974-01-01'), name:"Sophie Barthes", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/108346"}}, {tmdbId:"75035", properties:{bornIn:"Issy-les-Moulineaux,Hauts-de-Seine,France", imdbId:"0576298", born:date('1965-08-06'), name:"Olivier Megaton", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nOlivier Megaton (born Olivier Fontana 6 August 1965) is a French film director, writer, editor best known for directing the film The Red Siren, Transporter 3 from The Transporter series and the upcoming Luc Besson film Colombiana starring Zoe Saldana and Michael Vartan.  He also served as a second unit director for the film Hitman. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Olivier Megaton, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/75035"}}, {tmdbId:"19346", properties:{bornIn:"Denmark", imdbId:"0649117", born:date('1961-03-26'), name:"Niels Arden Oplev", bio:"Niels Arden Oplev is a writer-director from Denmark...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yGdxpPjMhIaeGaJL8TsVSpDuEbh.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19346"}}, {tmdbId:"2679", properties:{bornIn:" Toronto, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"0352524", born:date('1973-02-07'), name:"David Hackl", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nDavid Hackl (born 7 February 1973 in Toronto) is a Canadian film director and production designer. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article David Hackl, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2679"}}, {tmdbId:"82194", properties:{bornIn:"Johannesburg, South Africa", imdbId:"0088955", born:date('1979-09-17'), name:"Neill Blomkamp", bio:"Neill Blomkamp (born 17 September 1979) is a South African–Canadian film director, film producer, screenwriter, and animator.  Blomkamp employs a documentary-style, hand-held, cinéma vérité technique, blending naturalistic and photo-realistic computer-generated effects...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yj40QEEfjbRFnlwY0XunocNKdAe.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82194"}}, {tmdbId:"74396", properties:{bornIn:"Lidingö, Stockholms län, Sweden", imdbId:"0019247", born:date('1965-04-01'), name:"Tomas Alfredson", bio:"Tomas Alfredson is a Swedish film director, best known internationally for directing the 2008 vampire film Let the Right One In.  Alfredson has received the Guldbagge award for Best Direction twice; in 2005 for Four Shades of Brown, and in 2009 for Let the Right One In.  His future film work includes John Le Carré's Tinker, Tailor, Soldier, Spy followed by Philip Reeve's Larklight for the Warner Bros...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/5av7nZwWHgcYjJkO5P0gVMQy2Cg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/74396"}}, {tmdbId:"447616", properties:{imdbId:"1179906", name:"Carl Deal", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/447616"}}, {tmdbId:"408353", properties:{imdbId:"0504357", name:" Tia Lessin", bio:"Tia Lessin is an American film and television producer and director, especially for documentaries...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vQxmE79EHmWznywZ0xH3OpP4CPR.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/408353"}}, {tmdbId:"84061", properties:{imdbId:"1400426", name:"Daniel Barnz", bio:"Daniel Barnz (born 1970) is an American screenwriter and director.   Barnz made his debut in directing in the 2001 movie, The Cutting Room.   He also directed the 2009 movie, Phoebe in Wonderland, which received very positive reviews from critics.  Peter Travers wrote: \"Writer-director Daniel Barnz focuses the movie — his first, and it's a beauty. \"  He wrote and directed a movie adaption of the novel Beastly, a modern-day take on Beauty and the Beast...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/84061"}}, {tmdbId:"84852", properties:{bornIn:"Busan, South Korea", imdbId:"1082740", born:date('1969-05-14'), name:"JK Youn", bio:"JK Youn (윤제균) is a South Korean film producer, director and screenwriter...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vWFeFRf86mNs0TQS4JBCImBv2C8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/84852"}}, {tmdbId:"59229", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"1349040", born:date('1980-04-15'), name:"Damien Dante Wayans", bio:"Damien Dante Wayans is an American actor, writer, producer and director.  He is a member of the Wayans family...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/59229"}}, {tmdbId:"91268", properties:{bornIn:" Washington D.C., USA", imdbId:"0281508", born:date('1974-10-31'), name:"Ruben Fleischer", bio:"Ruben Samuel Fleischer (born October 31, 1974) is an American film director, film producer, television producer, music video director, and commercial director who lives in Los Angeles.  He is best known as the director of Zombieland, his first feature film.  He followed it by making the films 30 Minutes or Less, Gangster Squad and the 2018 film version of Venom which is based on the Marvel Comics character...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/3JLxOPFTLigSy8FjFjDyMwD9GIp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/91268"}}, {tmdbId:"313", properties:{bornIn:"New Jersey, USA ", imdbId:"0475578", born:date('1959-07-10'), name:"Ellen Kuras", bio:"Ellen Kuras ASC (born July 10, 1959 in New Jersey) is an American cinematographer and director.  She has collaborated several times with directors Michel Gondry and Spike Lee.  In 2013 she was a member of the jury at the 63rd Berlin International Film Festival. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Ellen Kuras, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/karbKVM0CPdRXbmLp4XX9oLQXSb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/313"}}, {tmdbId:"938835", properties:{imdbId:"0954912", name:"Marina Zenovich", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/e8yM9qyIVkTTq10gDGdkclK67xF.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/938835"}}, {tmdbId:"86523", properties:{bornIn:"Champaign, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"1315434", born:date('1968-05-03'), name:"Nina Paley", bio:"Nina Paley was born on May 3, 1968 in Champaign, Illinois, USA.  She is a director and writer, known for Sita Sings the Blues (2008), The Prophet (2014) and Fetch! (2002).  She was previously married to Liam...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/86523"}}, {tmdbId:"101542", properties:{bornIn:"Wilmington, Delaware, USA", imdbId:"1488800", born:date('1980-10-05'), name:"Ti West", bio:"Ti West (born October 5, 1980) is an American film director, best known for his work in horror films. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Ti West, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/qc7DRSS5CFDbNofjsyynYxOu5s.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101542"}}, {tmdbId:"558929", properties:{bornIn:"Clawson, Michigan, USA", imdbId:"1379002", born:date('1974-01-01'), name:"David Robert Mitchell", bio:"David Robert Mitchell is an American director mainly known for the breakout horror film ''It Follows'' which had its world premiere at the Cannes Film Festival in May 2014...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sBMvMf13HRdHFNydZvgPJrjtkai.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/558929"}}] AS row
