UNWIND [{tmdbId:"31621", properties:{bornIn:"Aurora, Ohio", imdbId:"0123009", name:"Jeff Burr", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nJeff Burr (born Aurora, Ohio in 1963) is an American film director, Writer and producer best known for his work in horror sequels, such as Stepfather II, The Texas Chainsaw Massacre III, Puppet Master 4 and 5, and Pumpkinhead II. \n\nBurr attended the University of Southern California (USC) with R.  A.  Mihailoff who played Leatherface in Leatherface: The Texas Chainsaw Massacre III...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31621"}}, {tmdbId:"1285810", properties:{name:"Jeffrey Radice", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1285810"}}, {tmdbId:"1285876", properties:{imdbId:"6195255", name:"Chapman Way", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1285876"}}, {tmdbId:"108258", properties:{imdbId:"0099474", born:date('1953-02-28'), name:"Chris Bould", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/108258"}}, {tmdbId:"1286930", properties:{imdbId:"0002416", name:"John O'Hagan", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/crC1T4NMwzi7afD8nQgLEce6xgY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1286930"}}, {tmdbId:"17278", properties:{bornIn:"Somerville, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0327064", born:date('1963-04-13'), name:"Nick Gomez", bio:"Nick Gomez (born April 13, 1963) is an American film director and actor.  He has directed for a number of television and film studios.  He has also acted in a few minor films.  In February 1998, Gomez and his film Illtown were given the Minami Toshiko Award at the 9th Yubari International Fantastic Film Festival...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/17278"}}, {tmdbId:"3451", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0835799", born:date('1928-09-02'), name:"Mel Stuart", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMel Stuart  (born September 2, 1928) is an American film director and producer. \n\nStuart directed the fantasy-musical Willy Wonka &amp; the Chocolate Factory (1971).  He has directed other features, including If It's Tuesday, This Must Be Belgium (1969), One Is a Lonely Number (1974) and Running on the Sun: The Badwater 135 (2000). \n\nStuart also directed feature documentaries including Four Days in November and Wattstax...", died:date('2012-08-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hOMTPvZtyjyGeH5q86YOlggm1kl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/3451"}}, {tmdbId:"93395", properties:{bornIn:"Chicago, Illinois, USA", imdbId:"0703954", born:date('1960-01-01'), name:"Paul Quinn", died:date('2015-09-02'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/93395"}}, {tmdbId:"83415", properties:{bornIn:"Toronto, Ontario, Canada", imdbId:"1313340", born:date('1966-04-14'), name:"Michael McGowan", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nMichael McGowan (born April 14, 1966 in Toronto, Ontario) is a Canadian filmmaker who wrote directed the feature films One Week and Saint Ralph.  After creating the stop-motion children's TV show, Henry's World, he wrote and directed Saint Ralph, which won the Outstanding Achievement in Direction award from the Director's Guild of Canada and the Writer's Guild of Canada award for Best Feature Film...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83415"}}, {tmdbId:"56717", properties:{bornIn:"Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0891114", born:date('1969-09-05'), name:"Tom Vaughan", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nTom Vaughan (born 5 September 1969) is a Scottish television and film director.  His work includes Cold Feet (1999) and He Knew He Was Right (2004) for television, and What Happens in Vegas (2008) and Extraordinary Measures (2010) for cinema. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Tom Vaughan (director), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56717"}}, {tmdbId:"11013", properties:{bornIn:"Kingston, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0003529", born:date('1979-08-29'), name:"Dan Harris", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/11013"}}, {tmdbId:"1290272", properties:{imdbId:"1552637", name:"Dennis Widmyer", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wZbN0JZd6kbGAHRglEH8u7CfGJ0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1290272"}}, {tmdbId:"2332", properties:{bornIn:"Hilden, Germany", imdbId:"0678857", born:date('1960-09-14'), name:"Christian Petzold", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nChristian Petzold (born 14 September 1960 in Hilden) is a German movie director. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Christian Petzold (director), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9XwFtjzPp9EaBnGDFo28t1PsKlg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/2332"}}, {tmdbId:"82714", properties:{bornIn:"Wallasey, Merseyside, England, UK", imdbId:"0164639", born:date('1935-10-28'), name:"Alan Clarke", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nAlan Clarke (28 October 1935 – 24 July 1990) was a television and film director, producer and writer, born in Wallasey, Merseyside, England. \n\nMost of Clarke's output was for television rather than cinema, including work for the famous play strands The Wednesday Play and Play for Today.  His subject matter tended towards social realism, especially with respect to deprived or oppressed communities...", died:date('1990-07-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/x6kTRGX18cgNJXscWkebNYomwPq.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/82714"}}, {tmdbId:"93911", properties:{bornIn:"Liverpool, England, UK", imdbId:"0203993", born:date('1945-11-10'), name:"Terence Davies", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nTerence Davies (born 10 November 1945) is an English screenwriter, film director, sometime novelist and actor.  As a filmmaker, Davies is noted for his recurring themes of emotional (and sometimes physical) endurance, the influence of memory on everyday life and the potentially crippling effects of dogmatic religiosity on the emotional life of individuals and societies...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uBbFee7ggk5vrCK4kcAcLOSYi0y.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/93911"}}, {tmdbId:"87183", properties:{imdbId:"1766424", name:"Mark Young", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/87183"}}, {tmdbId:"1255496", properties:{imdbId:"2126907", name:"Gabe Polsky", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1255496"}}, {tmdbId:"94155", properties:{bornIn:"London - England - UK", imdbId:"0777447", born:date('1963-05-01'), name:"Stefan Schwartz", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94155"}}, {tmdbId:"57870", properties:{imdbId:"0089176", name:"Jason Bloom", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nJason Bloom is a film director whose films include Bio-Dome starring Pauly Shore and Overnight Delivery starring Paul Rudd and Reese Witherspoon.  He also directed Viva Las Nowhere with James Caan and Daniel Stern and Irving with James Belushi. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jason Bloom, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/57870"}}, {tmdbId:"94169", properties:{bornIn:"The Bronx, New York, U.S", imdbId:"0077587", born:date('1917-09-06'), name:"John Berry", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nJohn Berry (September 6, 1917 – November 29, 1999) was an American film director, who went into self-exile in France when his career was interrupted by the Hollywood blacklist...", died:date('1999-11-29'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7R31d8lYcCRomWfnwf3b8p0Ae0F.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94169"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"102709", properties:{imdbId:"0002606", name:"David Price", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bEOU4dsyW0Oe2owVUI29gDEt6GL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/102709"}}, {tmdbId:"56746", properties:{imdbId:"0817770", name:"Greg Spence", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/56746"}}, {tmdbId:"94180", properties:{bornIn:"Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0718469", born:date('1887-03-14'), name:"Charles Reisner", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nCharles \"Chuck\" Reisner (14 March 1887 – 24 September 1962) was an American film director and actor of the 1920s and 1930s. \n\nHe directed over 60 films between 1920 and 1950 and acted in over 20 films between 1916 and 1929.  He starred alongside Charlie Chaplin in A Dog's Life in 1918 and The Kid in 1921. \n\nIn 1930 under MGM he directed the film Chasing Rainbows a musical which starred actors Bessie Love and Charles King...", died:date('1962-09-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/yk0s9H0WYWCwIESqm9yJ2O9oewt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94180"}}, {tmdbId:"950853", properties:{imdbId:"1711118", name:"Samantha Grant", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/950853"}}, {tmdbId:"544699", properties:{bornIn:"Brno, Moravia, AustriaHungary [now Brno, Czech Republic]", imdbId:"0460033", born:date('1910-01-26'), name:"Elmar Klos", died:date('1993-07-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/u7BTGFZAD0ny8uRl0QGPXPtvVe4.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/544699"}}, {tmdbId:"94918", properties:{imdbId:"2905562", name:"Daniel Barber", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nDaniel Barber is a British director who was nominated for an Academy Award in 2008 for his short film 'The Tonto Woman'.  Barber's wife Sandra was by his side throughout the Oscar ceremonies, despite her own struggle with cancer. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Daniel Barber (director), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94918"}}, {tmdbId:"18627", properties:{bornIn:"New York City, New York, USA", imdbId:"0607407", born:date('1938-02-23'), name:"Paul Morrissey", bio:"Paul Morrissey (born 23 February 1938, New York City) is an American film director, best-known for his association with Andy Warhol. \n\nMorrissey attended Ampleforth College, a private Roman Catholic boarding school and Fordham University, both Roman Catholic schools, and later served in the United States Army...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/zzyefFRWdOE1VQ41PnjeDGgUH7a.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/18627"}}, {tmdbId:"140617", properties:{bornIn:" Boston, Massachusetts, U.S.", imdbId:"1554601", born:date('1974-08-06'), name:"Ezra Edelman", bio:"Ezra Edelman is a director and producer.  He is the son of children's rights activist Marian Wright Edelman and Georgetown University law professor Peter B.  Edelman.  He has two brothers, Joshua, an educational administrator, and Jonah, co-founder and CEO of Stand for Children.  Edelman graduated from Sidwell Friends School in Washington D. C.  during July 1992, before going on to acquire his baccalaureate from Yale University...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/140617"}}, {tmdbId:"27444", properties:{imdbId:"0650561", name:"James Orr", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   James Orr is an Canadian writer, director and producer of motion pictures.  Orr's screenplay credits include Three Men and a Baby, Tough Guys and Sister Act 2: Back in the Habit, whilst his director credits include Mr.  Destiny and Man of the House. \n\nIn September 2010, wine critic James Suckling announced the launch of his new video-based website featuring content taped in locations across the world, created in collaboration with James Orr...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/27444"}}, {tmdbId:"26487", properties:{imdbId:"0720000", name:"Norman René", bio:"Norman René (1951 – May 24, 1996) was an American director.  He is known for his films Longtime Companion (1989), Prelude to a Kiss (1992), and Reckless (1995)...", died:date('1996-05-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/vVvWJesEWdxyBnATaU4wP98yn22.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/26487"}}, {tmdbId:"930791", properties:{bornIn:"Dublin, Ireland", imdbId:"0107543", born:date('1880-01-13'), name:"Herbert Brenon", died:date('1958-06-21'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/930791"}}, {tmdbId:"30422", properties:{bornIn:"Minneapolis, Minnesota, USA", imdbId:"0806915", born:date('1925-03-09'), name:"Jack Smight", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJack Smight (March 9, 1925 - September 1, 2003) was an American theatre and film director.  Smight was born in Minneapolis, Minnesota and went to school with future actor Peter Graves.  His film credits include The Traveling Executioner, Rabbit, Run, Loving Couples, Midway, Harper, Airport 1975, Damnation Alley and the Emmy Award-winning Eddie, as well as many episodes of television series such as The Twilight Zone and The Alfred Hitchcock Hour...", died:date('2003-09-01'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/30422"}}, {tmdbId:"95320", properties:{bornIn:"Pazos Hermos, Ourense, Galicia, Spain", imdbId:"0181579", born:date('1973-05-31'), name:"Rodrigo Cortés", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nRodrigo Cortés Giráldez (born May 31, 1973) is a Spanish film director, producer, screenwriter, editor, and occasional actor. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Rodrigo Cortés, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95320"}}, {tmdbId:"41041", properties:{bornIn:"Bristol, England, UK", imdbId:"1247462", born:date('1970-08-16'), name:"Christopher Smith", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nChristopher Smith, (born 16 August 1970 in Bristol, England, UK) is a British film director and screenwriter. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article  Christopher Smith, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7Un0sQeq7V9DgJw9n3OEzdo4vod.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41041"}}, {tmdbId:"119665", properties:{bornIn:"Harrington Park, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0414423", name:"Gregory Jacobs", bio:"Gregory \"Greg\" Jacobs is an American film director, assistant director, producer, and screenwriter.  He has frequently collaborated with several film directors, most notably Steven Soderbergh.  Jacobs has also been operating as a director himself, having overseen projects such as Criminal, Wind Chill and Magic Mike XXL...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/uJVO8ChqP6Exk7BwX1K3gi2Cd14.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/119665"}}, {tmdbId:"23964", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0002657", born:date('1956-11-03'), name:"Gary Ross", bio:"Gary Ross (born November 3, 1956) is an American film director, writer, and producer.  He is best known for directing The Hunger Games...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9EeuS6rCWPquj5uts6waw1y15Kp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/23964"}}, {tmdbId:"440124", properties:{imdbId:"2288328", name:"Drew Heriot", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/440124"}}, {tmdbId:"90657", properties:{imdbId:"0539950", name:"David Mallet", bio:"David Mallet is a British director particularly noted for his work on music videos, including David Bowie's innovative \"Ashes to Ashes\", Rush's \"Distant Early Warning, and Queen's \"Radio Ga Ga\" and \"I Want to Break Free\" videos.  He has also served as a producer on television programmes including \"The Kenny Everett Video Show\"...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/90657"}}, {tmdbId:"95462", properties:{bornIn:"Edinburgh, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0131910", born:date('1934-01-17'), name:"Donald Cammell", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nDonald Seaton Cammell (17 January 1934 – 24 April 1996) was a Scottish film director who enjoys a cult reputation thanks to his debut film Performance, which he co-directed with Nicolas Roeg. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article  Donald Cammell , licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", died:date('1996-04-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xIaAVsujonfsstCsYMXu9KCgbRg.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95462"}}, {tmdbId:"26850", properties:{bornIn:"Cuba", imdbId:"0844896", born:date('1968-12-20'), name:"Eduardo Sánchez", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nEduardo Miguel Sánchez-Quiros (born December 20, 1968) is a Cuban-born American director most famous for co-directing and writing the 1999 film The Blair Witch Project with Daniel Myrick...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/avKJyjTHky4OenGxepCjj1BYZYB.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/26850"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"95992", properties:{imdbId:"0779714", name:"Robert Scott", died:date('2006-01-05'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95992"}}, {tmdbId:"95066", properties:{imdbId:"0660886", born:date('1924-01-09'), name:"Sergei Parajanov", bio:"Sergei Parajanov (Armenian: Սերգեյ Փարաջանով;  Russian: Серге́й Ио́сифович Параджа́нов; Georgian: სერგო ფარაჯანოვი; Ukrainian: Сергій Йо́сипович Параджа́нов; sometimes spelled Paradzhanov or Paradjanov; January 9, 1924 – July 20, 1990) was a Soviet film director and artist of Armenian descent who made significant contributions to Soviet cinematography through Ukrainian, Georgian, and Armenian cinema...", died:date('1990-06-21'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/90Vpo4UtfYeckMRLesg9Fanqgcs.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95066"}}, {tmdbId:"132239", properties:{imdbId:"0619836", name:"Babak Najafi", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/132239"}}, {tmdbId:"96446", properties:{bornIn:"New York, USA", imdbId:"0706268", name:"Kevin Rafferty", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nKevin Rafferty is an American documentary film cinematographer, director, and producer, best known for his 1982 documentary The Atomic Cafe...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/96446"}}, {tmdbId:"187067", properties:{imdbId:"1084749", name:"David Allen", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/187067"}}, {tmdbId:"1214133", properties:{bornIn:"Stockton, California, USA", imdbId:"0425593", born:date('1922-09-30'), name:"Lamont Johnson", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nLamont Johnson (September 30, 1922 – October 24, 2010) was an American actor and film director who has appeared in and directed many television shows and movies.  He won two Emmy Awards. \n\nJohnson was born Ernest Lamont Johnson, Jr.  in Stockton, California, the son of Ruth Alice (née Fairchild) and Ernest Lamont Johnson, who was a realtor.  Johnson began his career in radio, playing the role of Tarzan in a popular syndicated series in 1951...", died:date('2010-10-24'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/oGqhGmjBntl4C0wVGDScr2u13Iw.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1214133"}}, {tmdbId:"59670", properties:{imdbId:"0026862", name:"Jane Anderson", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/59670"}}, {tmdbId:"124695", properties:{imdbId:"2175118", name:"David Jung", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/124695"}}, {tmdbId:"1326297", properties:{bornIn:"Los Alamos, New Mexico, USA", imdbId:"1783713", name:"Bradley King", bio:"Bradley Dean King is an American film director and screenwriter...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/xDcfdeIb19MJJnRym4jUs98Movi.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1326297"}}, {tmdbId:"565524", properties:{bornIn:"Bangkok, Thailand", imdbId:"0950841", born:date('1942-11-29'), name:"Chatrichalerm Yukol", bio:"His Serene Highness Prince Chatrichalerm Yukol is a Thai film director, screenwriter and film producer.  A prolific director since the 1970s, among his films is the 2001 historical epic, The Legend of Suriyothai.  A member of the Thai royal family, his official royal title is Mom Chao, or M. C. , the most junior title still considered royalty.  He is theoretically 19th in line for the Thai throne.  He is widely known by his nickname, Than Mui...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/565524"}}, {tmdbId:"583881", properties:{bornIn:"Handa, Aichi, Japan", imdbId:"0633729", born:date('1976-08-29'), name:"Nobuhiro Yamashita", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/583881"}}, {tmdbId:"97591", properties:{imdbId:"1757667", name:"Joel Anderson", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/97591"}}, {tmdbId:"24757", properties:{imdbId:"0845973", name:"Sylvio Tabet", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/24757"}}, {tmdbId:"98538", properties:{bornIn:"London", imdbId:"0658482", born:date('1941-08-29'), name:"Tony Palmer", bio:"Tony Palmer is a British film director and author.   His work includes over 100 films, ranging from early works with The Beatles, Cream, Jimi Hendrix and Frank Zappa (200 Motels), to his classical portraits which include profiles of Maria Callas, Margot Fonteyn, John Osborne, Igor Stravinsky, Richard Wagner, Yehudi Menuhin, Carl Orff, Benjamin Britten and Ralph Vaughan Williams.  He is also a stage director of theatre and opera...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/g9lFSxdyPL9w6KZT0FJZlFzhYIl.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/98538"}}, {tmdbId:"1331163", properties:{bornIn:"Hoboken, New Jersey, U.S.", imdbId:"1322753", born:date('1977-09-17'), name:"Sam Esmail", bio:"Sam Esmail is an Egyptian-American screenwriter, film and television director, and television producer.  He is best known as the creator of the television series Mr.  Robot (2015–present)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mej39wMtNDsOI5HklLb65QAiM6K.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1331163"}}, {tmdbId:"185995", properties:{imdbId:"0908037", name:"Michael Walker", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/185995"}}, {tmdbId:"1195866", properties:{imdbId:"0313569", name:"Peter George", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1195866"}}, {tmdbId:"33317", properties:{bornIn:"Cambridge, Cambridgeshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0500896", born:date('1947-04-20'), name:"David Leland", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nDavid Leland (born 20 April 1947 in Cambridge, England) is a director, screenwriter and actor who came to international fame with his directorial debut Wish You Were Here in 1987. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article David Leland, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/9nWtHb2usnfeGXScwLmVpbFq6S9.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33317"}}, {tmdbId:"1222374", properties:{imdbId:"0668350", name:"Jamie Payne", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1222374"}}, {tmdbId:"100616", properties:{bornIn:"Cambridge, Massachusetts, USA", imdbId:"0221265", born:date('1939-01-01'), name:"Tom DeSimone", bio:"Tom DeSimone (born 1939) is an American director, writer, producer and editor, perhaps best known for directing the cult films Chatterbox (1977), Hell Night (1981), and The Concrete Jungle (1982). \n\nDeSimone was born in Cambridge, Massachusetts, and earned a Bachelor of Arts degree from Emerson College.  He relocated to Los Angeles, California in the 1960s, and enrolled at the University of Southern California to earn a Master's degree in filmmaking...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/r402yi9RIPuItcMz8tDFvKhoe9o.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100616"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"100891", properties:{bornIn:"North Olmsted, Ohio", imdbId:"0597521", born:date('1971-08-13'), name:"David Monahan", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   \n\nDavid Harold Monahan (born August 13, 1971 in North Olmsted, Ohio) is an actor, best known for recurring roles on Crossing Jordan as Detective Matt Seely and Dawson's Creek as Tobey Barret.  He has also appeared in such films as The Last Supper (2000), The Mostly Unfabulous Social Life of Ethan Green (2005) and Something New (2006). \n\nA 1989 graduate of Bishop Denis J...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/2NzQDcARuhSn2CGS5IRPmeomIxt.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100891"}}, {tmdbId:"31310", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0384335", born:date('1933-01-28'), name:"Jack Hill", bio:"​From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nJack Hill (born January 28, 1933) is an U. S.  film director, noted for his work in the exploitation film genre.  Hill was born in Los Angeles.  His mother, Mildred (née Pannill), was a music teacher and his father, Roland Everett Hill, worked as a set builder for film studios and was an architect. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jack Hill, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/e2HQQCcGwCul8aPIXeb9fQpDqKS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/31310"}}, {tmdbId:"179609", properties:{bornIn:"Tenterden, GB", born:date('1949-08-01'), name:"Nigel Finch", died:date('1995-02-14'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/179609"}}, {tmdbId:"1368144", properties:{bornIn:"  United States", imdbId:"0629658", born:date('1973-12-09'), name:"Max Nichols", bio:"Born on December 9, 1973 in the USA.  He is a director and actor, known for Two Night Stand (2014), Heft and Day 5 (2016).  Has been married to Rachel Nichols since May 25, 2001...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/y9tgsQjrWmxj7xNCYAwD1RnyfFN.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1368144"}}, {tmdbId:"1352991", properties:{imdbId:"0519594", name:"Andrew Loo", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1352991"}}, {tmdbId:"89981", properties:{bornIn:"Budapest, Hungary", imdbId:"0070670", born:date('1905-03-05'), name:"László Benedek", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nLászló Benedek (Hungarian pronunciation: [ˈlaːsloː ˈbɛnɛdɛk]; March 5, 1905 – March 11, 1992; sometimes Laslo Benedek) was a Hungarian-born film director and cinematographer, most notable for directing The Wild One (1953). \n\nBorn in Budapest, he worked as a writer and editor in Hungarian cinema until World War II.  Louis B.  Mayer helped the Jewish Benedek escape and brought him to Hollywood where he directed his first film for MGM in 1944 as a stand-in...", died:date('1992-03-11'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/89981"}}, {tmdbId:"114629", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0602333", born:date('1949-01-01'), name:"Philippe Mora", bio:"Philippe Mora is an Australian film writer, director, actor and artist.  He was born in France to a German Jewish father and an Australian mother...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/114629"}}, {tmdbId:"101520", properties:{bornIn:"London, England, UK", imdbId:"0319241", born:date('1912-05-29'), name:"John Gilling", bio:"John Gilling (29 May 1912 – 22 November 1984) was an English film director and screenwriter, born in London.  He was chiefly known for his horror films, especially for Hammer Films, for whom he directed Shadow of the Cat (1961), The Plague of the Zombies (1966), The Reptile (1966) (the latter two filmed back to back in Cornwall) and The Mummy's Shroud, among others.  He is also renown for many low to mid budget detective films and teleplays with unexpected touches of comedy blended in...", died:date('1984-11-22'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101520"}}, {tmdbId:"1286323", properties:{bornIn:"Los Angeles, California, USA", imdbId:"0583275", born:date('1957-05-03'), name:"Michael Meyer", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ll3hpdhMK56s3yiyLCQliBY6xWA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1286323"}}, {tmdbId:"1019303", properties:{bornIn:"St. Louis, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"2122478", born:date('1979-03-20'), name:"Duke Johnson", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1019303"}}, {tmdbId:"104879", properties:{bornIn:"Asturias, Spain", imdbId:"0579466", born:date('1941-01-01'), name:"Ramón Menéndez", bio:"Luis Ramón Menéndez Velasco was an actor...", died:date('2007-01-01'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/104879"}}, {tmdbId:"54507", properties:{bornIn:"Palo Alto, California, USA", imdbId:"1163851", born:date('1979-11-02'), name:"Jon M. Chu", bio:"Jonathan Murray \"Jon\" Chu (born November 2, 1979) is an American film director and screenwriter best known for directing the movies Step Up 2: The Streets, Step Up 3D and Justin Bieber: Never Say Never.  Chu is an alumnus of the University of Southern California School of Cinema-Television...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7qzoszJh8PuI2rqgMceuCqq4vQG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54507"}}, {tmdbId:"94045", properties:{bornIn:"Toronto, Ontario,  Canada", imdbId:"0002573", born:date('1951-01-19'), name:"Bill Corcoran", bio:"Bill Corcoran is a Canadian film and television director...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wbp8xIJqdKDhQhWUpwAyIxoK0v0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/94045"}}, {tmdbId:"103344", properties:{bornIn:"Portland, Oregon, USA", imdbId:"0949597", born:date('1897-11-13'), name:"Harold Young", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nHarold Young (November 13, 1897 – March 3, 1972) was an American film director, editor, and occasional actor. \n\nBorn in Portland, Oregon, Young was active as a film editor from 1923-1934, working first on a series of George O'Hara short subjects under the director Malcolm St.  Clair. \n\nYoung's best-known early directoral assignment is probably The Scarlet Pimpernel (1934), starring Leslie Howard and Merle Oberon, one example of his occasional work in Britain...", died:date('1972-03-03'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/103344"}}, {tmdbId:"134102", properties:{bornIn:"Tokyo - Japan", imdbId:"0406722", born:date('1948-11-25'), name:"Jun Ichikawa", bio:"Jun Ichikawa was a Japanese film director and screenwriter.  He was first a director of television commercials before adding filmmaking to his creative activities.  His most famous film outside of Japan was Tony Takitani, an adaptation of a short story by Haruki Murakami.  He died of a cerebral hemorrhage after suddenly collapsing at a restaurant, shortly before his latest film, Buy a Suit, was to premier at the Tokyo International Film Festival...", died:date('2008-09-19'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dmRHGKPaNh0hoosSNzhr2jRQq2h.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/134102"}}, {tmdbId:"55252", properties:{bornIn:"Pasadena, California, USA", imdbId:"1783265", born:date('1964-10-10'), name:"Tim Miller", bio:"Timothy Miller is an American film director and visual effects artist.  He made his feature-film directing debut with Deadpool.  He was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Animated Short Film as co-story writer and executive producer of the short animated film Gopher Broke...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/dCyBYwhO76j5wA96HPb6k5xk2Le.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/55252"}}, {tmdbId:"67592", properties:{name:"Mark Linfield", bio:"Mark Linfield is a British writer, producer and director of nature documentaries for cinema and television.  He is best known for his work with the BBC Natural History Unit as a producer of two episodes of the television series Planet Earth (2006) and as writer and co-director of the associated feature film Earth (2007)...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/67592"}}, {tmdbId:"47333", properties:{imdbId:"0920274", born:date('1956-05-28'), name:"John Wells", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia  John Marcum Wells (born May 28, 1956) is an American theater and television producer, writer and director.  He is best known for his role as executive producer and show runner of the television series ER, Third Watch, and The West Wing.  His company, John Wells Productions, is currently based at Warner Bros.  studios in Burbank, California...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/47333"}}, {tmdbId:"83287", properties:{bornIn:"Glasgow, Strathclyde, Scotland, UK", imdbId:"0708903", born:date('1969-12-05'), name:"Lynne Ramsay", bio:"Lynne Ramsay (born 5 December 1969) is a Scottish film director, screenwriter, producer, and cinematographer, best known for the feature films Ratcatcher (1999), Morvern Callar (2002), We Need to Talk about Kevin (2011), and You Were Never Really Here (2017)...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/hmSR9lVV65ojYHyyOtzmNPbVjSY.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83287"}}, {tmdbId:"41795", properties:{bornIn:"Havanna, Cuba", imdbId:"0182873", born:date('1961-06-10'), name:"Manny Coto", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bcJeO8ZkEmgDK4AmNNyGyRtOSPG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/41795"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"1189125", properties:{name:"Yin Li", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1189125"}}, {tmdbId:"105287", properties:{imdbId:"0365311", name:"Scott Harris", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/105287"}}, {tmdbId:"34949", properties:{bornIn:"London, United Kingdom", imdbId:"1013671", born:date('1970-01-01'), name:"Lucy Walker", bio:"Lucy Walker (born in London, United Kingdom) is a film director, mostly of theatrical feature documentaries.  On January 25th, 2010 she was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Documentary Feature for Waste Land, which she directed...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/34949"}}, {tmdbId:"116832", properties:{imdbId:"0136603", name:"Patricia Cardoso", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/116832"}}, {tmdbId:"1223815", properties:{imdbId:"0804887", born:date('1957-03-04'), name:"Steve Skrovan", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1223815"}}, {tmdbId:"133502", properties:{bornIn:"London,  England", imdbId:"0193508", born:date('1960-03-11'), name:"Simon Curtis", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/mpMyd3Cc7WG2epXYCbdDmcMX2BD.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/133502"}}, {tmdbId:"100036", properties:{bornIn:"LaGrange, Kentucky, USA", imdbId:"0000428", born:date('1875-01-22'), name:"D. W. Griffith", bio:"David Llewelyn Wark Griffith was a premier pioneering American film director.  He is best known as the director of the controversial and groundbreaking 1915 film The Birth of a Nation and the subsequent film Intolerance (1916).  Griffith's film The Birth of a Nation made pioneering use of advanced camera and narrative techniques, and its immense popularity set the stage for the dominance of the feature-length film...", died:date('1948-07-23'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/7EanyqqLfQzS9PnKIBa6w1Rbbi8.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/100036"}}, {tmdbId:"21305", properties:{bornIn:"San Jose, California, USA", imdbId:"0045800", born:date('1889-12-04'), name:"Lloyd Bacon", bio:"Lloyd Bacon was an American stage and silent-era screen actor who is most remembered as a film director, making films in virtually all genres.  Among the 130 films he directed is the 1933 Warner Bros.  classic 42nd Street...", died:date('1955-11-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/gGQlsA8kdC6Uo9oIM7d0BLLIXwL.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/21305"}}, {tmdbId:"4410", properties:{bornIn:"Rome, Italy", imdbId:"0744023", born:date('1906-05-08'), name:"Roberto Rossellini", bio:"Roberto Rossellini (8 May 1906 – 3 June 1977) was an Italian film director and screenwriter.  Rossellini was one of the directors of the Italian neorealist cinema, contributing films such as Roma città aperta (Rome, Open City 1945) to the movement...", died:date('1977-06-03'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/c9SGpj5JFJjMplUnxp3r1vPf4WM.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4410"}}, {tmdbId:"118415", properties:{bornIn:"Summit, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0048918", born:date('1971-02-26'), name:"Sean Baker", bio:"Sean Baker is an American film/TV director and co-creator of Greg the Bunny. \n\nHe is best known for the independent feature films Tangerine, The Florida Project and Starlet...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/bz96USgFMwR3MhrPoGVv84e1R7K.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/118415"}}, {tmdbId:"83524", properties:{imdbId:"0944937", born:date('1967-05-30'), name:"Shinobu Yaguchi", bio:"Shinobu Yaguchi is a Japanese film director and screenwriter.  He specializes in feel-good \"zero to hero\" films, where a group of people take up an unlikely activity, face a number of obstacles, but finally succeed. [citation needed] His film Waterboys was particularly successful and led to a TV series which entered its third season in 2005.  He was awarded Best Screenplay at the 2005 Yokohama Film Festival for his film Swing Girls...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/1wwEJVpbCv1xtSB6PLUK3ye6MXo.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/83524"}}, {tmdbId:"1101410", properties:{bornIn:"USA", imdbId:"1757777", born:date('1983-01-01'), name:"Dave Green", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1101410"}}, {tmdbId:"107148", properties:{imdbId:"0875953", born:date('2018-05-01'), name:"Michael Tucker", bio:"Michael Tucker, an American documentary film director, was born in Honolulu, Hawaii.  He is currently best known for his recent documentary The Prisoner or: How I Planned to Kill Tony Blair.  He also directed a documentary in Iraq during the 2003 Iraqi War entitled Gunner Palace. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Michael Tucker(director), licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/107148"}}, {tmdbId:"95329", properties:{bornIn:"London, England", imdbId:"0175430", born:date('1937-09-24'), name:"Kevin Connor", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Kevin Connor is an English film and television director currently based in Hollywood.   Connor was born in London on the 24 of September 1937 and grew up during the 2nd World War.  Later, he became a member of the sound departments of several movies, then a cutter, editor, and finally a director...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/sQifjywTBDlLuPnTODHcWxIxwo0.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/95329"}}, {tmdbId:"1827779", properties:{imdbId:"2953454", name:"Shannon Hartman", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1827779"}}, {tmdbId:"1293994", properties:{bornIn:"Fountain, Colorado, United States", imdbId:"1218281", born:date('1981-06-28'), name:"Jon Watts", bio:"Jon Watts is an American film director, producer and screenwriter.  He directed the films Clown and Cop Car and episodes of the Onion News Network. \n\nWatts was born and raised in Fountain, Colorado.  He studied film at New York University. \n\nBefore directing movies, Watts directed commercials for production company Park Pictures.  When trying to get the job directing Spider-Man: Homecoming, Watts got a tattoo of Spider-Man on his chest to make himself \"stand out in the field\"...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fkXChMX6CUXY1yOxBehAzvaTCl7.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1293994"}}, {tmdbId:"78615", properties:{bornIn:"Fresno, California, USA", imdbId:"0738736", born:date('1930-12-21'), name:"Phil Roman", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/78615"}}, {tmdbId:"586002", properties:{bornIn:"Harrogate, Yorkshire, England, UK", imdbId:"0354091", born:date('1973-03-07'), name:"Andrew Haigh", bio:"Andrew Haigh (born 7 March 1973) is an English director, screenwriter and producer...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/pJAv105SAZiQ3lGY2wGURz4bENp.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/586002"}}, {tmdbId:"1213162", properties:{bornIn:"Kittanning, Pennsylvania, USA", imdbId:"0390844", born:date('1961-12-13'), name:"Todd Holland", bio:"Todd Holland (born December 13, 1961) is an American television and film director and producer...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1213162"}}, {tmdbId:"1402638", properties:{imdbId:"6406593", name:"Jim Weedon", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1402638"}}] AS row
CREATE (n:Person{tmdbId: row.tmdbId}) SET n += row.properties SET n:Director;
UNWIND [{tmdbId:"1137890", properties:{bornIn:" Paris, France", imdbId:"0179023", born:date('1976-04-11'), name:"Coralie", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1137890"}}, {tmdbId:"110834", properties:{imdbId:"0613981", name:"John Murlowski", bio:"John Murlowski is an American film director, producer and writer.  After graduating from Art Center College of Design in Pasadena, Murlowski spent five years directing commercials and educational films.  He is perhaps best know for the thriller Black Cadillac, a feature film based on a true road rage incident in which John and his friends were almost killed.  In 2004, Murlowski launched the production company Maple Island Films...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/tgTQjYtBou3IiJjpYgG17RNch9q.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/110834"}}, {tmdbId:"4586", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0685759", born:date('1957-07-04'), name:"Pitof", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.  \n\n \n\nJean-Christophe \"Pitof\" Comar (born 4 July 1957) is a French film and visual effects director notable for Vidocq and Catwoman. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Pitof, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/z7lKv1EscqXN6LjxEj45gE3D1jA.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/4586"}}, {tmdbId:"1361389", properties:{bornIn:"White Plains, New York, USA", imdbId:"3228270", born:date('1987-02-26'), name:"Dan Berk", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1361389"}}, {tmdbId:"356", properties:{bornIn:"San Francisco, California, USA", imdbId:"0005726", born:date('1946-11-18'), name:"Jack Green", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/356"}}, {tmdbId:"90375", properties:{bornIn:"St. Louis, Missouri, USA", imdbId:"0127511", born:date('1888-04-16'), name:"Christy Cabanne", bio:"William Christy Cabanne (April 16, 1888 – October 15, 1950) was an American film director, screenwriter and silent film actor...", died:date('1950-10-16'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ie0zr5ZBQzvpkUepozOJ0Hlw8OS.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/90375"}}, {tmdbId:"108106", properties:{bornIn:"York, Nebraska, USA", imdbId:"0629243", born:date('1874-01-06'), name:"Fred Niblo", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nFred Niblo (January 6, 1874 – November 11, 1948) was an American pioneer film actor, director and producer.   Niblo was born Frederick Liedtke (several sources give \"Frederico Nobile\", apparently erroneously) in York, Nebraska, to a French mother and a father who had served as a captain in the American Civil War and was wounded at the Battle of Gettysburg...", died:date('1948-11-11'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/108106"}}, {tmdbId:"33166", properties:{bornIn:"Paris, France", imdbId:"0163229", born:date('1898-11-11'), name:"René Clair", bio:"René Clair was a French filmmaker and writer.  He first established his reputation in the 1920s as a director of silent films in which comedy was often mingled with fantasy.  He went on to make some of the most innovative early sound films in France, before going abroad to work in the UK and USA for more than a decade...", died:date('1981-03-15'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/wUMa7OFmeYxmBsDlGHgHKuOtK3Y.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/33166"}}, {tmdbId:"84736", properties:{bornIn:"Prague, Czechoslovakia [now Czech Republic]", imdbId:"0664852", born:date('1933-07-10'), name:"Ivan Passer", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nIvan Passer (born July 10, 1933) is a Czech-born film director and screenwriter. \n\nA significant figure in the Czech New Wave of the mid-1960s, Passer worked closely with Miloš Forman on many of his films, and directed his first feature in 1965.  Following the Soviet invasion in 1968, Passer defected to the West, aided by Carlo Ponti and has been living and working in the United States since then...", died:date('2020-01-09'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/fCG4NeOJwpn36ToYozFjFlOHPEG.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/84736"}}, {tmdbId:"1379396", properties:{imdbId:"0236973", name:"Miller Drake", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1379396"}}, {tmdbId:"5446", properties:{bornIn:"Plainfield, New Jersey, USA", imdbId:"0359457", born:date('1900-01-23'), name:"David Hand", bio:"“I was born in the shadow of my father’s brick-yard at Plainfield, N.  J.  Visited Plainfield High School.  Tried lumber-jacking in the North Woods.  No soap! Studied cartooning under Orr and DeBeck at the Chicago Academy of Fine Arts in 1917-18, and while there located my future wife.  Started animating Andy Gump in Chicago 1919.  Fascinated by easy work and big money decided to stick...", died:date('1986-10-11'), poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/z6OfyPCRbDsT6qUGOjcsS39ZmBb.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/5446"}}, {tmdbId:"19656", properties:{bornIn:"Caracas, Venezuela", imdbId:"0349406", born:date('1974-09-10'), name:"Sebastián Gutiérrez", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia. \n\nSebastián Gutiérrez (born September 10, 1974) is an award-winning Venezuelan-American film director, screenwriter, film producer and occasional actor.  He won the Critics' Award at the Festival du Film Policier de Cognac for his directorial debut Judas Kiss. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Sebastián Gutiérrez, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/19656"}}, {tmdbId:"1335642", properties:{imdbId:"1271076", name:"Robert Gordon", poster:"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w440_and_h660_face/ga18g92FNpOoHsPGlPgXrlZtAcd.jpg", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1335642"}}, {tmdbId:"101238", properties:{imdbId:"0716262", born:date('1943-10-17'), name:"Michael Reeves", died:date('1969-02-11'), url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/101238"}}, {tmdbId:"108670", properties:{imdbId:"0445196", name:"John Keitel", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/108670"}}, {tmdbId:"60295", properties:{bornIn:"Montréal, Québec, Canada", imdbId:"0808807", born:date('1943-07-31'), name:"John N. Smith", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/60295"}}, {tmdbId:"54839", properties:{bornIn:"Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania", imdbId:"0714599", born:date('1961-02-16'), name:"Eric Red", bio:"From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia.   Eric Red (born Eric Joseph Durdaller; February 16, 1961) is an American screenwriter and director, best known for writing the horror classics The Hitcher and Near Dark. \n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Eric Red, licensed under CC-BY-SA,full list of contributors on Wikipedia...", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/54839"}}, {tmdbId:"116103", properties:{imdbId:"0184323", name:"Bill Couturié", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/116103"}}, {tmdbId:"1120414", properties:{imdbId:"0692332", name:"William Porter", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/1120414"}}, {tmdbId:"935279", properties:{imdbId:"0204720", name:"J. Davis", url:"https://themoviedb.org/person/935279"}}] AS row
